  <desc>SpookyWanderin1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1b385469-ed4b-4f73-9866-b6696aeb2af8</url>
  <urlname>Spooky Wanderings : S1 Kenwick Pioneer Cemetery by TeamBarritts</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99002489" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Spooky Wanderings : S1 Kenwick Pioneer Cemetery</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>TeamBarritts</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">TeamBarritts</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Spooky Wanderings&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Kenwick Pioneer Cemetery&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1b385469-ed4b-4f73-9866-b6696aeb2af8"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1b385469-ed4b-4f73-9866-b6696aeb2af8&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;At the given coordinates you will see some large rocks along the path - How many are there in total?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a284edc6-2b8a-4974-a3f3-ae6e9ead1305" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kenwick Pioneer Cemetery is located in Kenwick, adjacent to Albany Highway.  It is part of the 1.2 hectares (3 acres) of land donated by Wallace Bickley for a school for the children of the Canning in 1863.

In 1865 a rammed earth building with shingle roof was constructed by convicts. The school, with accommodation for a school teacher and police constable, served as school, courthouse, church, post office and social centre for many years. 

A church, St Michael and All Angels, was built on a site next to the school and served the district until the end of the century.

The school closed in 1896 and in 1900 the school and church were demolished. Only the cemetery remains. Over 200 people were buried at the cemetery during its use, however few grave stones remain. 
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d145caeb-98e9-4811-8d6d-8e37e1682ce8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Adventure Lab takes you on a short tour of some of the oldest and most interesting cemetery’s around East Perth and the Hills area's.  This Lab should take about 2 hours to complete and all sites should have good phone coverage. 

While you are visiting the various locations please take the opportunity to read a few of the headstones, finding about the area and the history of the people who are laid to rest there.  Sometimes it may give a hint as to what they did and where they originated from. 

Very importantly, please remember where you are and show the appropriate respect for the residents and people visiting them.

There is also an optional bonus mystery cache to find once you have finished.  You will need to collect the clues provided in the journals to solve the puzzle and get the cache coordinates.  

Good luck and have fun! 
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/cd3915b6-08ff-4489-a0ff-c706f0943106" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations, now onto the next one!!  The word you need is "housed"&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.04945" lon="115.98305">
