  <name>LBMybc-03</name>
  <desc>PTAPublicArtAr3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/PTA</url>
  <urlname>PTA Public Art (Armadale Line) : S3 Maddington Station by Granett</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-148" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>PTA Public Art (Armadale Line) : S3 Maddington Station</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Granett</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Granett</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;PTA Public Art (Armadale Line)&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Maddington Station&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/PTA"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/PTA&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many sculptures are there?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5b093d1e-fabf-4e37-9c05-eb59e987ff29" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Travel and Journeys through Country

Three free standing figure sculptures made of burnished aluminium with brightly coloured artwork ceramic tiles representing travel, time and the seasons and special tiles by community members. These works are designed to be bold and colourful and to make reference to ancient shapes and symbols. The symbols used in the designs are associated with Nyoongar ideas about travel,  camps and resting points on a journey, sources of water and food, traditional walk paths and the passing of time as represented by the six seasons.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/791572a5-4bd6-47e9-924f-496371c4f927" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Public Transport Authority Public Art

While the PTA is predominately about moving people from one place to another, they have commissioned some spectacular pieces of art which can be contemplated while you wait for your train to arrive.

This Adventure Lab takes you to some examples along the Armadale line. The geofences are fairly generous and you might be able do some stages while on the train. However a closer inspection of these works is highly recommended.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
