  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/MaddingtonHistory</url>
  <urlname>Stepping Back In Time - Maddington : S5 Maddington Centenary Hall and Gosnells Road Board by LAXA</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476910019" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Stepping Back In Time - Maddington : S5 Maddington Centenary Hall and Gosnells Road Board</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>LAXA</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">LAXA</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Stepping Back In Time - Maddington&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Maddington Centenary Hall and Gosnells Road Board&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/MaddingtonHistory"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/MaddingtonHistory&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Who officially opened the Maddington Centenary Hall (last name only)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d93e87e2-c386-47d4-bb93-841edf7a685b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This monument marks the spot of the Maddington Centenary Hall constructed in 1929, but it was also the location of the Gosnells Road Board from 1907 until destroyed by a fire, along with all the records they contained in 1928. New offices were built in Maddington and local administration for the area did not move to Gosnells until 1973 when the present offices were opened near the corner of Gosnells Road and the Albany Highway. 
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9fa098ca-9d15-4a5b-aff4-1176c9630a25" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to a short flashback to the origins of Gosnells and Maddington.
Follow the footsteps of the early settlers and learn about the agricultural beginnings of the Southern River and Canning River Area from the first settlement in 1829.
We recommend walking between the stages to immerse yourself in the history of this place.
Please take note of the bonus information given at each stage, helping you to find the bonus box (GC8ZGT8).
We hope you enjoy this little walk back in time with us.

Throughout this adventure, we have linked sound bites from the City of Gosnells relating to the stations where available. To listen to the sound bites, mark and open the links in each location.

Listen to a brief introduction here: https://www.gosnells.wa.gov.au/files/assets/public/audio_files/heritage/walk_trail/part_1_intro.mp3  


&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d2125a88-63b4-4e0e-82c7-cc69e9e2d821" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Your Bonus letter is: L

Use all bonus letter to make something typical for the Gosnells-Maddington area (hint: Lemonade)
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
