   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Icons of South Perth&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Pagoda Ballroom&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/360c5218-28a5-4aa0-a1dc-db2d4cd7c7b9"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/360c5218-28a5-4aa0-a1dc-db2d4cd7c7b9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What was the Pagoda Ballroom also known as?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/532ad2ef-82de-41ed-a15f-e03810efbda8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Pagoda Ballroom is part of the Como Heritage Trail. The ballroom was built around the skeleton of the 1922 Pagoda Ballroom, originally owned by Perth hotelier Harold C. Gordon. The ballroom was designed by architect Fred Zuideveld and was a popular venue for balls and functions. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/91a05639-9d06-4fe3-9f93-17c7b2e5bc4f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Adventure Lab will take you to a number of iconic structures in the City of South Perth - some in South Perth and some in Como. The tour can be driven, walked or cycled.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/dda35f5a-cde4-445a-96b9-8a5b93a545a4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.14915" lon="116.016967">
  <ele>67.0</ele>
  <time>2021-03-27T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBeRXX-03</name>
  <desc>MinnawarraMagi3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/01b71aab-dfad-48f3-913c-1b89eaedf5aa</url>
  <urlname>Minnawarra Magic : S3 Minnawarra Park Plaque by Team Red Roo</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-123" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Minnawarra Magic : S3 Minnawarra Park Plaque</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Team Red Roo</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Team Red Roo</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Minnawarra Magic&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Minnawarra Park Plaque&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/01b71aab-dfad-48f3-913c-1b89eaedf5aa"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/01b71aab-dfad-48f3-913c-1b89eaedf5aa&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year was the land for Minnawarra Park aquired?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4721312e-631b-469e-87af-c454c7740412" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This plaque is placed at the south end of the ornamental bridge. The bridge was constructed to be both beautiful and useful, and has served as the backdrop for many photos - of wedding groups as well as normal visitors.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0b76110c-6933-4a88-b4fb-6edf2e67327d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Adventure (as in the name) will take you for a short walk mainly around Minnawarra Park and the Armadale Civic and Cultural Precinct. You should be able to find all five points within about 15 minutes, unless of course you decide to stop to admire the beauty. Minnawarra Park is also used for various community events throughout the year.

The main feature of the park is the ornamental lake which has several fountains running to aerate the water and stop algae from forming. The lake also supports a large number of ducks and other birds all year round. It is fed from Sanctuary Lake on the other side of Armadale Road, which in turn is fed by  Neerigen Brook. Sanctuary Lake is a safe haven from predators for birds and allows for limited nest sites during breeding season. 

After answering the question for each waypoint correctly, you'll be able to work out the coordinates of the Bonus cache - GC983CR . The Bonus cache can be found at S 32 08.uvw  E 116 00.xyz&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Make a note of this number for the bonus cache: W = 4

The Bonus cache (GC983CR) can be found at S 32 08.uvw  E 116 00.xyz&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.149333" lon="116.016617">
