   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Minnawarra Magic&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Port Jackson Fig Tree&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/01b71aab-dfad-48f3-913c-1b89eaedf5aa"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/01b71aab-dfad-48f3-913c-1b89eaedf5aa&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the Tree number on the plaque under this tree?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/cf7b6caf-9dac-4b5a-8d09-525b9729b1b9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Coordinates for this tree are taken on the pathway in front of the tree, but the answer to the question is several meters away at the base of the tree. Trees like this one provide large shade areas used by both visitors and local bird life in summer. The birds here are not tame, but are semi used to people in their area. Armadale has a listing of 29 Heritage Trees and you can get a free copy from the Perth Hills Armadale Visitor Centre in Jull St.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0b76110c-6933-4a88-b4fb-6edf2e67327d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Adventure (as in the name) will take you for a short walk mainly around Minnawarra Park and the Armadale Civic and Cultural Precinct. You should be able to find all five points within about 15 minutes, unless of course you decide to stop to admire the beauty. Minnawarra Park is also used for various community events throughout the year.

The main feature of the park is the ornamental lake which has several fountains running to aerate the water and stop algae from forming. The lake also supports a large number of ducks and other birds all year round. It is fed from Sanctuary Lake on the other side of Armadale Road, which in turn is fed by  Neerigen Brook. Sanctuary Lake is a safe haven from predators for birds and allows for limited nest sites during breeding season. 

After answering the question for each waypoint correctly, you'll be able to work out the coordinates of the Bonus cache - GC983CR . The Bonus cache can be found at S 32 08.uvw  E 116 00.xyz&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Make a note of these numbers for the bonus cache: X = 8 , Y = 6. The Bonus cache (GC983CR) can be found at S 32 08.uvw  E 116 00.xyz&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
