 <wpt lat="-31.967933" lon="115.87665">
  <ele>14.0</ele>
  <time>2020-01-17T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBJj4A-09</name>
  <desc>CityIsWadjukC09</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/TCIWC</url>
  <urlname>This city is Wadjuk Country : S09 Matagarup by parkacruz</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-209" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>This city is Wadjuk Country : S09 Matagarup</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>parkacruz</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">parkacruz</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;This city is Wadjuk Country&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Matagarup &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/TCIWC"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/TCIWC&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What date was Yagan tragically killed? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6856cb72-28f9-4f9a-8a0e-df7d992208c3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Matagarup - which refers to the place where the river is only leg deep, was once a small chain of islands and surrounding mud flats. Where the island currently stands was a much smaller island known as Kakaroomup. This area was a main crossing point from one side of the river to the other, where Noongars could wade through the water.  

The area in which Heirisson Island is currently located is an important area for Noongar people. A statue of Wadjuk Noongar warrior Yagan was erected on the island to recognise Yagan’s strong leadership and resistance fighting during the early years of the Swan River Colony. Amidst the fighting a bounty was set upon his head, he was shot, his head was removed and sent to London where it was exhibited as an "anthropological curiosity". A museum in Liverpool kept it more than a century before burying it with other remains in an unmarked grave in 1964. Noongars asked for repatriation, 177 years later, his head was finally buried in a traditional ceremony in the Swan Valley.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/79cbb012-2a74-4686-afba-7d425fd49400" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The City of Perth is Wadjuk Boodjar (Country) covering the area between Gargatup, the place down by the hillside (in Kings Park), and Matagarup, the place of the leg holes (Heirisson Island), where Noongars would cross the river. This area, near the lowest and easiest crossing point on the Swan River (at Matagarup), was an important communication and trade centre between the coast and the islands. Whadjuck/Balardong custodian Tom Bennell referred to Perth as ”Beerit” meaning ”pathways” due to its importance for meetings, travel and trade.

This Adventure Lab Cache will take you on an approximate 12km journey around Wadjuk Boodjar  depending on the route you take, you may walk, ride, drive (parts) or use public transport to get around, we recommend you give yourself a good half of a day to complete the adventure. 

Photo credit: Parkacru

VIEWER ADVICE
Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander viewers are advised that the following Adventure Lab Cache may contain images of people who have died.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/de9be3ed-db5a-42da-ae05-fc1b56e94266" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations on completing this stage.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
