   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Minnawarra Magic&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Armadale Congregational Church&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/01b71aab-dfad-48f3-913c-1b89eaedf5aa"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/01b71aab-dfad-48f3-913c-1b89eaedf5aa&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year was this church first built?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/aa3f2872-b919-4193-b66f-925f7514117d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This church was the first built in Armadale and was originally built on the corner of Church Avenue and Third Rd but was saved and relocated to the border of Minnawarra Park and the Civic Precinct to preserve it for future generations. It is still in use today.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0b76110c-6933-4a88-b4fb-6edf2e67327d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Adventure (as in the name) will take you for a short walk mainly around Minnawarra Park and the Armadale Civic and Cultural Precinct. You should be able to find all five points within about 15 minutes, unless of course you decide to stop to admire the beauty. Minnawarra Park is also used for various community events throughout the year.

The main feature of the park is the ornamental lake which has several fountains running to aerate the water and stop algae from forming. The lake also supports a large number of ducks and other birds all year round. It is fed from Sanctuary Lake on the other side of Armadale Road, which in turn is fed by  Neerigen Brook. Sanctuary Lake is a safe haven from predators for birds and allows for limited nest sites during breeding season. 

After answering the question for each waypoint correctly, you'll be able to work out the coordinates of the Bonus cache - GC983CR . The Bonus cache can be found at S 32 08.uvw  E 116 00.xyz&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Make a note of this number for the bonus cache: Z = 0

The Bonus cache (GC983CR) can be found at S 32 08.uvw  E 116 00.xyz&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
