 <wpt lat="-31.951233" lon="115.891133">
  <ele>5.0</ele>
  <time>2020-01-17T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBJj4A-10</name>
  <desc>CityIsWadjukC10</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/TCIWC</url>
  <urlname>This city is Wadjuk Country : S10 The Arbour by parkacruz</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-210" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>This city is Wadjuk Country : S10 The Arbour</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>parkacruz</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">parkacruz</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;This city is Wadjuk Country&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Arbour&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/TCIWC"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/TCIWC&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;As you look up along the walkway what Indigenous tools do you think the artwork panels represent? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ff9222f0-477a-4bf3-82d9-85757de7cc9d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Located on the eastern shores of the Derbarl Yerrigan (Swan River) with scenic views over Matagarup Bridge and the Perth City skyline beyond is Optus Stadium and the surrounding Stadium Park. Acknowledging the site’s significant heritage with this being a burial site for the local indigenous people, the Wadjuk Noongar, and with guidance from the Wadjuk Working Party, it offers a real celebration of Western Australia’s Aboriginal culture in many forms of art and landscape. 

The Arbour, a 350m long architectural tensioned cable-net structure, supporting indigenous inspired artwork panels, crawling vines and plants and feature programmable LED lighting is a walk way that weaves and slithers representing a Waugal - rainbow serpent, around a portion of Stadium Park. 

Image credit: ABC Education Resources
Final photo credit: Parkacru

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/79cbb012-2a74-4686-afba-7d425fd49400" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The City of Perth is Wadjuk Boodjar (Country) covering the area between Gargatup, the place down by the hillside (in Kings Park), and Matagarup, the place of the leg holes (Heirisson Island), where Noongars would cross the river. This area, near the lowest and easiest crossing point on the Swan River (at Matagarup), was an important communication and trade centre between the coast and the islands. Whadjuck/Balardong custodian Tom Bennell referred to Perth as ”Beerit” meaning ”pathways” due to its importance for meetings, travel and trade.

This Adventure Lab Cache will take you on an approximate 12km journey around Wadjuk Boodjar  depending on the route you take, you may walk, ride, drive (parts) or use public transport to get around, we recommend you give yourself a good half of a day to complete the adventure. 

Photo credit: Parkacru

VIEWER ADVICE
Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander viewers are advised that the following Adventure Lab Cache may contain images of people who have died.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d8d68c50-0d46-48c7-a052-06be9da146b9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations on completing this stage. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
