That wasn't too far, you can feel the bridge move about, don't stress, it is meant to do that... I think.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0835811f-a20f-4814-b617-83e6edb3eb82" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is a quick little tour that will teach you not-a-lot about this and that. 

Matagarup Bridge is a suspension pedestrian bridge crossing over the Swan River in Perth, Western Australia. Situated approximately half-way between Heirisson Island and the Goongoongup Bridge, it provides pedestrian access between Burswood and East Perth.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0fbebcc9-bf05-464e-8de1-2a624ffef532" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Onwards to the next location!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
