   <groundspeak:name>Perth Red Cat Adventure : S08 West Australian Visitor Centre</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Bristag</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Bristag</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Perth Red Cat Adventure&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;West Australian Visitor Centre&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/RedTour"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/RedTour&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Face the entrance, now walk to the left of the building, how many steps are between the upper and lower level?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/65b3a7e5-3f14-4874-b0db-fb0ca2558bfa" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Red Cat stop 12 - Central Park

I had to highlight the Western Australian Visitor Centre, It is a one stop shop for travel information, souvenirs and offers free tours about the Perth CBD.
Stop in have break and plan some more adventures.

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2b086e18-1940-4fa8-ae54-650e6f68b64d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This adventure takes you on a tour in the Perth CBD.

This tour takes advantage of the free to ride Red Cat Bus route, there are historic buildings, side tours, museums and parkland to checkout along the way.

If you are driving to the CBD, the adventure can be completed in any order, so just park up and hop on the bus anywhere along the route.
However I recommend catching the train into Perth CBD and commencing the adventure at the Red Cat Bus stop 24 - Wellington St Perth Station. From this stop the first location is St Mary's Cathedral.
 &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;From here hop on the Red Cat at stop 12 - Central Park. The next location is Barracks Arch.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
