   <groundspeak:name>[L] It feels like home : S3 Beer o’clock</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>.K.B.</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">.K.B.</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;It feels like home&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Beer o’clock &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Home"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Home&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What were used for transporting barrels of beer from the brewery to other hotels?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/72c2e175-db72-457b-b81f-355001eb020a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;An iconic site. Childhood memories of driving from the south back home to the north are full of images of an illuminated brewery. Look for a plaque which outlines “Life at the Swan Brewery”.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c63dde21-8349-4b09-931a-400ae9f36155" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Inner Perth spans some picturesque river locations. This adventure lab is best done by bike. 

Since the final physical cache is hidden west of all the virtual locations, the order has been fixed to east to west. In addition, this will allow for those travelling by car to park since all parking is on the river side of Mounts Bay Road.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;You’re on a roll. Time to roll to another river side location.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.960917" lon="115.8449">
  <ele>54.0</ele>
  <time>2020-01-04T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBN7tp-01</name>
  <desc>KingsParkAdve01</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/kingspark</url>
  <urlname>Kings Park Adventure : S01 State War Memorial by jasenjanine</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909833" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Kings Park Adventure : S01 State War Memorial</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>jasenjanine</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">jasenjanine</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Kings Park Adventure&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;State War Memorial&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/kingspark"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/kingspark&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year is mentioned on the "ANZAC BLUFF" plaque?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/18da00fe-c955-4d1e-851c-5cd668694a55" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The State War Memorial Precinct is located in Kings Park overlooking Perth Water. It comprises the Cenotaph, Court of Contemplation, Flame of Remembrance and Pool of Reflection. 

The Cenotaph is an 18 metre granite obelisk honouring all Western Australians who gave their lives in the service of their country.

The Court of Contemplation is located at the western side of the precinct and commemorates the conflicts in which Western Australians have fallen, with the walls featuring the names of major battlefields.

The Flame of Remembrance within the Pool of Reflection burns continuously, symbolising the promise of all Western Australians.

"We will remember them"
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c4b5e2d1-4e09-477b-b926-93ab6865c238" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kings Park is one of the most popular visitor destinations in Western Australia, with spectacular views of the Perth Waterways and Darling Range. Spread over 990 acres, the park is a mixture of grassed parkland, botanical gardens and natural bushland on Mount Eliza. Two-thirds of the grounds are conserved as native bushland. 
Previously known as Perth Park, it officially opened in 1895.  Its name was changed to King's Park in 1901 (dropping the apostrophe in later years).  


This adventure lab cache will highlight some of the special places that Kings Park is famous for.  We hope you enjoy visiting the locations chosen.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/aa4d25e9-b9a2-4d99-a754-95a7580ff69e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well Done!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.021483" lon="115.809383">
  <ele>7.0</ele>
  <time>2020-05-17T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBrNtN-03</name>
  <desc>CaringForWater3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cherryorchard</url>
  <urlname>Caring for Waterbirds : S3 Swan Estuary Marine Park by fairwaydrivers</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-290" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Caring for Waterbirds : S3 Swan Estuary Marine Park</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>fairwaydrivers</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">fairwaydrivers</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Caring for Waterbirds&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Swan Estuary Marine Park&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cherryorchard"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cherryorchard&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Which waterbird mentioned on the information board has a long slightly downturned beak ?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2b356f4d-fbf6-479b-b9b8-efee297ad8c6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Located on the bike path with lots of information is a shelter. I hope you take the time to read this and learn more about caring for waterbirds. You will also find the answer to the question here.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f6292440-19d6-4fcb-a1bb-d28838755318" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Swan Estuary and its foreshore provide habitats for a diversity of waterbirds. The sedges, samphires and trees around this area are essential for maintaining the health of the estuary and the waterbirds.The seagrass meadows provide a nursery habitat for fish and crustaceans. Dead and decaying seagrass provides food for invertebrates that are food for waterbirds. The shallow mudflats are exposed during low tide which may only be for a few hours each day. These mudflats hide mussel deposits and are home to worms, aquatic snails, insects and other minute crustaceans sought after by waterbirds.Other waterbirds trap small fish in the open water.
This adventure is best done on a lovely bike ride which will give you beautiful views of the Swan River and the many waterbirds. See how many different species you can count!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done. We hope you learned a lot about waterbirds&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.951217" lon="115.8535">
  <ele>25.0</ele>
  <time>2020-01-23T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBnmX8-06</name>
  <desc>PerthsTheatreS6</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Theatre</url>
  <urlname>Perth’s Theatre Scene : S6 Comedy Lounge by familysteiner</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-236" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Perth’s Theatre Scene : S6 Comedy Lounge</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>familysteiner</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">familysteiner</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Perth’s Theatre Scene&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Comedy Lounge&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Theatre"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Theatre&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Facing the gate from the footpath, look at the metal Water Corp access cover in the pavement to the right. What six letter word is featured?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d7171c54-3614-492d-9494-7ade14b0d669" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Comedy Lounge is Perth’s first, and only, purpose-built venue for live comedy. Opening in 2004, it provides regular laughs to the people of Perth, and features interstate and international comedy talent alongside local comedians.

The coordinates will take you to the footpath side of the entrance gate.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3ac167c3-0dba-4363-bb05-0e8eac02c57a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
Since the time of Settlement, the Perth CBD has been home to a vibrant theatre scene and this short Adventure Lab will take you to some of this city’s key live performance locations, both historical and current. The seven locations are in close proximity and you should easily be able to complete the series within two hours. Take your time to appreciate some of the wonderful architecture of the contemporary theatres as well as the remnants of those lost to development. 

Given the building density within this area, the listed coordinates may not be as accurate as desired. However there should be sufficient information in each location’s description for you to find what you need once you have navigated to the general area. Enjoy!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/273a8a68-3338-4c29-84a9-85573376b4be" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;CORRECT!

Congratulations &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.9714" lon="115.8338">
  <ele>1.0</ele>
  <time>2020-07-13T08:00:00Z</time>
