   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Local Heroes - The Legends of Anzac &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Bassendean &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/LocalHeroes"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/LocalHeroes&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is written on all 3 plaques in the ground around the memorial? (6 words)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/562c47b4-fdc4-4a5d-9e10-5fc7dddddbe6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Located in the park behind the Shire, this memorial is the newest of the series. The memorial wall has spaces that I hope are never needed . &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8adb3a14-83ff-43a6-b9fa-7dc5c0472b8d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Having grown up in Western Australia, I have always been interested in the stories behind the people listed on the suburban war memorials. 
These are ordinary people, who stood up to be counted in extraordinary times and made the ultimate sacrifice.
This series is a roughly 10 km in length and encompasses a small number of memorials, large and small, old and new that were commissioned either by the people of the community in the area or the local branch of the R.S.L.  &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/76285f4a-b3da-43ab-be0a-eb38847cfbe4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Old Perth Road is nearby and is one of the oldest villages in Perth.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
