   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;The Oxford Strip&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The grandest of them all&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/369b029f-0e2d-4f72-8ffd-2de06a2a60c4"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/369b029f-0e2d-4f72-8ffd-2de06a2a60c4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Number of obvious birds flying? As a single numeral.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7a974aed-6da5-41d6-882f-f91ea4c8f008" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Unmistakeable in its size and the message it depicts. Best viewed from across the road, it’s a beauty to behold.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/483ff958-72c2-43a0-bd81-da6995831721" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Oxford Street runs from Mount Hawthorn at the northern end to Leederville at the southern end. The strip is most famous for its cafes. Quite literally, each block has at least one. As is customary for areas with cafe atmosphere, street art abounds. I’ve picked out 5 locations but there are many more to enjoy. A bike lane does run down the length of the strip on both the eastern and western sides; not the best of designs so use at your own peril.

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/463f8baa-b1bc-4215-a1b2-d913d7e2264f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done. Enjoy the area.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
