   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;The Oxford Strip&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Time to build&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/369b029f-0e2d-4f72-8ffd-2de06a2a60c4"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/369b029f-0e2d-4f72-8ffd-2de06a2a60c4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;A 3D object appears in the top left corner of the artwork. On what 2D shape is it based?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0d217cc6-7568-4500-813b-cfbc7c7bd823" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is not actually one of my favourites since I prefer brighter colour, but it’s iconic in its age and detail. The artwork depicts a town. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/483ff958-72c2-43a0-bd81-da6995831721" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Oxford Street runs from Mount Hawthorn at the northern end to Leederville at the southern end. The strip is most famous for its cafes. Quite literally, each block has at least one. As is customary for areas with cafe atmosphere, street art abounds. I’ve picked out 5 locations but there are many more to enjoy. A bike lane does run down the length of the strip on both the eastern and western sides; not the best of designs so use at your own peril.

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1bacd64e-2983-4120-96b1-a5c27bf05d85" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;You got it. One, two, three sides. One artwork to go.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
