  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d20f283a-60dc-489d-8931-e0d5ceced025</url>
  <urlname>[L] Midland Workshops : S5 Ambulance Post by neva2old</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99002487" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] Midland Workshops : S5 Ambulance Post</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>neva2old</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">neva2old</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Midland Workshops&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Ambulance Post&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d20f283a-60dc-489d-8931-e0d5ceced025"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d20f283a-60dc-489d-8931-e0d5ceced025&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What else was stored here? ( 2 words)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1830f8c9-e7a1-4c5e-a99b-090d116fad3a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;the Ambulance Post was the original Timekeepers Office, which was first built on the site of the Peace memorial and later relocated in 1924&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/202280b3-e399-46f4-a269-0b5a164c92e6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Midland Workshops.   Between 1902 and 1904 the Western Australian Government Railway Workshops were relocated to Midland.
The Midland Railway Workshops ran for close to a century on the Eastern fringe of Perth, Western Australia.

Large and multifaceted, the Workshops were vital to the development and maintenance of the West Australian rail system, and a crucial training ground for skilled tradespeople. Their closure in 1994 brought to an end not only a specific industrial complex but also a complex social community.

Despite the harsh, dirty and often dangerous working conditions, many thousands of former workers regretted the loss of the traditions, camaraderie and pride in workmanship that characterised their Midland working lives.

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ed9f0265-7660-4222-8d97-336f12cfb959" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done !!  Now go find the Railway workshop Bonus Cache GC9DTX9  its not far.
S31 53.715 E116 00.202&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
