   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Midland Workshops&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Block 2&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d20f283a-60dc-489d-8931-e0d5ceced025"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d20f283a-60dc-489d-8931-e0d5ceced025&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is a Dog Spike? ( 1 word)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b6173c40-5f0e-4bca-8818-6790f73274a5" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Block 2 housed the Blacksmiths and the boiler shops. Look up can you see the figurine of the Blacksmith&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/202280b3-e399-46f4-a269-0b5a164c92e6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Midland Workshops.   Between 1902 and 1904 the Western Australian Government Railway Workshops were relocated to Midland.
The Midland Railway Workshops ran for close to a century on the Eastern fringe of Perth, Western Australia.

Large and multifaceted, the Workshops were vital to the development and maintenance of the West Australian rail system, and a crucial training ground for skilled tradespeople. Their closure in 1994 brought to an end not only a specific industrial complex but also a complex social community.

Despite the harsh, dirty and often dangerous working conditions, many thousands of former workers regretted the loss of the traditions, camaraderie and pride in workmanship that characterised their Midland working lives.

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5b7b824e-8dd3-40bb-bbae-6149ee7ae347" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt; Well done, if you have time venture down the side streets and read the plaques along the way&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
