   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;The Dead Politicians of Karrakatta&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Sir James Mitchell&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/TheDeadPoliticians"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/TheDeadPoliticians&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Nearby to Sir James Mitchell's resting place is a plaque honouring a lady named Magdalen.  What was her middle name starting with P?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/272bda9d-bf33-44d7-8f39-abe7cb55fa94" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Sir James Mitchell, GCMG (27 April 1866 – 26 July 1951) was an Australian politician. He was the 13th Premier of Western Australia, serving on two occasions, the Lieutenant-Governor of Western Australia for 15 years, and the 22nd Governor of Western Australia from 1948 to 1951.

Use the camera on you phone to scan the QR code on the sign to read about the life of Sir James Mitchell&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b9e0ea1a-1329-4b63-a108-35203c6c0594" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Karrakatta Cemetery first opened for burials in 1899. This historic cemetery is the final resting place of many thousands of Western Australians. Monuments and headstones bear many famous names including those of university founders, writers and historians, state premiers and other historic individuals.

The cemetery is centrally located just seven kilometres west of Perth city centre and is easily accessible by car or train.

Stately stands of cypress trees – a hallmark of Karrakatta – flank the main driveway off Railway Road and preside over beautiful garden areas in the historic heart of the cemetery.

There are two walk trails that will lead you some of the resting places of people in our history that now call Karrakatta Cemetery home.  They can be located at this website:
https://www.mcb.wa.gov.au/our-cemeteries/karrakatta-cemetery/historical-walk-trails

This Adventure Lab will take you to the final resting place of 5 politicians who have left their mark on the State of Western Australia
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/29ef0f6c-95ec-4c22-9641-7f442d480cf4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;The Mitchell Freeway and Sir James Mitchell Park are 2 Perth features that have been named in honour of Sir James Mitchell.
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
