  <time>2020-04-08T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBRBas-03</name>
  <desc>ParanormalPert3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ParanormalPerth</url>
  <urlname>Paranormal Perth : S3 Karrakatta Cemetery by Barrikon</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909757" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Paranormal Perth : S3 Karrakatta Cemetery</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Barrikon</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Barrikon</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Paranormal Perth&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Karrakatta Cemetery&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ParanormalPerth"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ParanormalPerth&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Located within a gazebos is history of the cemetery. The first burial occurred in what month?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/20e0633b-48a8-4198-aeca-b4d79803cd9b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Karrakatta is Western Australia’s biggest cemetery and is the resting place of some of WA’s most influential and instrumental people.
Although not renowned for supernatural activity, it is home to the birth place of end.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8dc1ada0-08ea-4e7e-964c-57a7b3bf56ff" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Stories of lost souls, destitute apparitions, shadowy figures with unfinished business and ethereal beings providing protection, fill history books and live within myths across the world. Perth is no different. 

Tales of ghostly encounters can be found across the city and by partaking on this paranormal hunt you may experience your very own unexplained event.

Your adventure covers approximately 53kms and is available anytime however to fully experience possibilities of the afterlife, it is suggested you wait until darkness falls. A good torch will be needed if venturing out after dark.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3249fb3e-1f99-44a6-b8b5-cff67e2339e1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.922533" lon="115.84125">
  <ele>36.0</ele>
  <time>2021-01-31T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBEMaj-01</name>
  <desc>OxfordStripS1No</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/369b029f-0e2d-4f72-8ffd-2de06a2a60c4</url>
  <urlname>The Oxford Strip : S1 Northern strip by .K.B.</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909813" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>The Oxford Strip : S1 Northern strip</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>.K.B.</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">.K.B.</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;The Oxford Strip&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Northern strip&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/369b029f-0e2d-4f72-8ffd-2de06a2a60c4"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/369b029f-0e2d-4f72-8ffd-2de06a2a60c4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the symbol in the centre of the black and white artwork?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/eb8030be-50a1-49a5-8c30-dec8820cf417" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Plenty of art at this northern end. Axford Park war memorial is showcased at the end of the strip.

On the Telstra building is a colourful artwork. On a much smaller adjacent wall is a black and white artwork. It depicts a skateboard, rainbow, sun, fish and some letters. The centrepiece of the artwork is a symbol.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/483ff958-72c2-43a0-bd81-da6995831721" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Oxford Street runs from Mount Hawthorn at the northern end to Leederville at the southern end. The strip is most famous for its cafes. Quite literally, each block has at least one. As is customary for areas with cafe atmosphere, street art abounds. I’ve picked out 5 locations but there are many more to enjoy. A bike lane does run down the length of the strip on both the eastern and western sides; not the best of designs so use at your own peril.

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/86c757f0-dcc4-441d-a9d7-d4f7c0cd4620" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done. Grab a coffee and start exploring.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.091233" lon="115.769067">
  <ele>17.0</ele>
  <time>2020-09-09T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBre3h-04</name>
  <desc>ManningParkS4Az</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ManningPark</url>
  <urlname>Manning Park : S4 Azelia Ley Homestead Museum by Barnzy12</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99001481" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Manning Park : S4 Azelia Ley Homestead Museum</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Barnzy12</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Barnzy12</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Manning Park&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Azelia Ley Homestead Museum&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ManningPark"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ManningPark&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;There is a plaque on the right of the walkway infront of an Oak tree, what is the last word on the plaque?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8e43045b-0602-4996-bc79-4b0f265e67bd" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Azelia Ley (nee Manning) grew up on the nearby Davilak Estate, and in 1900 married John Ley, a customs officer. In 1915, her mother Florence divided her fathers estate into portions for each of their children, and 152 acres was transferred to Azelia.

She began buildings the Manning Tree House (now Azelia Ley Homestead Museum) in 1923, although she only moved into the property in 1927 after her husbands death. She lived on the property and managed her farm until her death in 1954.

In the Early 1980's the City of Cockburn along with some prominent residents decided to restore the residence and transform it into a musuem, which officially opened on 12th November 1983.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a0918eb8-1ba3-48fd-8f39-679fdc407ba2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Manning Park is named after the Manning family, who were prominent in the Cockburn area around the 19th century. The land was originally purchased by Charles Manning in 1860.

This adventure will take you to some prominent sights in Manning Park.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e4d51792-9bea-447d-8b28-a9f242e08e4d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.095667" lon="115.770283">
  <ele>14.0</ele>
