  <name>LBre3h-01</name>
  <desc>ManningParkS1Da</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ManningPark</url>
  <urlname>Manning Park : S1 Davilak Ruins by Barnzy12</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99001475" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Manning Park : S1 Davilak Ruins</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Barnzy12</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Barnzy12</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Manning Park&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Davilak Ruins&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ManningPark"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ManningPark&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the main building material remaining on-site? (9 letters, starting with L)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5aad3591-b382-4e96-8d94-c5dcb987054a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Davilak Ruins are the remains of several buildings constructed by the Manning family, the ruins consist of a large homestead and several outbuildings. 

The original heritage listed Davilak House was built around 1840 by the Manning family and was one of the first small farms in the colony complete with vineyards, limestone houses, a dairy and stables. A number of extensions and outbuildings were destroyed by fire in 1960, and the ruined structures that remain represent the buildings built with limestone.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a0918eb8-1ba3-48fd-8f39-679fdc407ba2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Manning Park is named after the Manning family, who were prominent in the Cockburn area around the 19th century. The land was originally purchased by Charles Manning in 1860.

This adventure will take you to some prominent sights in Manning Park.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7f84b01c-8004-437c-9017-7785804b518d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
