   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Manning Park&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Old Wagon House&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ManningPark"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ManningPark&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Nearby to the Wagon House is small outbuilding, what is the buildings name (2 words, 9 and 5 letters only, no punctuation)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/73964abe-6175-4be3-9fb4-e7289e6953bd" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Wagon House is located adjacent to the Azelia Ley Homestead. Built in 1985, it houses various wagons, trucks, carriages and farm machinery which have been donated to the musuem over time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a0918eb8-1ba3-48fd-8f39-679fdc407ba2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Manning Park is named after the Manning family, who were prominent in the Cockburn area around the 19th century. The land was originally purchased by Charles Manning in 1860.

This adventure will take you to some prominent sights in Manning Park.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9ae78c88-e70c-48e1-8e58-63178573b8c1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
