   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Manning Park&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Manning Park Lookout&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ManningPark"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ManningPark&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;At the top of the lookout there is a plaque in the ground, What is located 25km away? (2 words, 8 and 6 letters)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/fdc233e2-afbe-4304-8b40-65d7d72dafa6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Manning Park lookout is located on the Davilak Trail, which runs around the edge of the park and provides views over Cockburn Sound, Jervoise Bay and the Darling Scarp. A particular point of interest is the South Fremantle Power Station which is located to the west.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a0918eb8-1ba3-48fd-8f39-679fdc407ba2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Manning Park is named after the Manning family, who were prominent in the Cockburn area around the 19th century. The land was originally purchased by Charles Manning in 1860.

This adventure will take you to some prominent sights in Manning Park.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b1af4aac-5be9-4315-807e-6fda51ef38c9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
