   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.056067" lon="115.741383">
  <ele>10.0</ele>
  <time>2019-07-02T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBRXKy-01</name>
  <desc>LWestOzWander2S</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/WOZBlackSwan</url>
  <urlname>[L] West Oz Wander #2 : S01 The Round House by West Oz Geocaching</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-387" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] West Oz Wander #2 : S01 The Round House</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>West Oz Geocaching</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">West Oz Geocaching</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;West Oz Wander #2&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Round House&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/WOZBlackSwan"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/WOZBlackSwan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year was the bakery conserved by the City of Fremantle&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/211fcd17-7edb-4049-9593-aa1e35822c26" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Round House, on Arthur Head, is neither a house nor round. It is dodecagonal, having twelve sides, and was built as a jail in 1830-1 (twenty years before convicts arrived).

This makes it the oldest public building in the State. 

During 1966 the standard gauge railway was extended past the end of High Street and the original steps were partly demolished and rebuilt in their present form.

You are looking for an information plaque to the right side of the steps up to the main entrance to the Round House.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7ba2105b-269b-4f75-9d77-8a158e9cdf1e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Take a trip visiting the early European history of the Western Australia colony.

Indigenous Australians have been occupying Western Australia for around 40,000 to 60,000 years.

The first recorded European contact was in 1616 when Dutch explorer Dirk Hartog landed on the west coast but the first permanent settlement was not made until 1826 when a settlement was established at Albany to formally take possession of the western third of the continent of Australia for the British Crown.  The Swan River Colony was established in 1829 starting the official history of European settlement of Western Australia.

This set of lab caches explores the early buildings and places of the Swan River Colony.

&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.955267" lon="116.165167">
  <ele>138.0</ele>
  <time>2020-08-15T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBqEvG-04</name>
  <desc>MundaringWeirA4</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Mundaring</url>
  <urlname>Mundaring Weir Adventure Lab : S4 C Y O Connor Memorial by jasenjanine</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476910067" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Mundaring Weir Adventure Lab : S4 C Y O Connor Memorial</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>jasenjanine</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">jasenjanine</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Mundaring Weir Adventure Lab&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;C Y O Connor Memorial&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Mundaring"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Mundaring&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Where does Mundaring Weir supply water to?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a665f36e-cbe5-4f96-b3b7-5f6096f5f29e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Born in Ireland 1843, Charles Yearlton O'Connor immigrated to New Zealand in 1866.  He relocated to Western Australia in 1891 where he was responsible for the construction of the Fremantle Harbour &amp; the Goldfields Water Supply Scheme.  Sadly he died a tragic death in 1902 leaving behind his wife Susan to which they had 8 children.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8fd2b6fd-31f2-4a79-8e94-15d370f26e67" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Located in the Perth Hills, the Mundaring Weir is one of the world's greatest engineering projects.

Completed in 1903, the weir is the start of the water pipeline that pumps water to the Kalgoorlie goldfields some 700km away.

We have created this adventure lab to highlight some of the history &amp; beauty of the precinct.  

Mundaring Weir is a great spot to take the family &amp; the little ones will enjoy feeding the birds, enjoy!

**  Once you complete the adventure, use your journal entries to work out the Bonus Cache (GC8M58V). **&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/95968e65-0914-4975-ba55-328f6cc11ad1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;CY OCONNOR MEMORIAL:
East co-ordinates are EFGH minus 1530.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.955583" lon="116.1657">
  <ele>150.0</ele>
