  <name>LBqEvG-01</name>
  <desc>MundaringWeirA1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Mundaring</url>
  <urlname>Mundaring Weir Adventure Lab : S1 Viewing Platform by jasenjanine</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476910061" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Mundaring Weir Adventure Lab : S1 Viewing Platform</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>jasenjanine</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">jasenjanine</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Mundaring Weir Adventure Lab&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Viewing Platform&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Mundaring"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Mundaring&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;At your feet is a four word phrase.  What is the last word?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e4262e7f-0f7b-4375-910c-3845209c07a4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Thomas Crowley Hodgson recommended the site of the weir for what appeared to be foundations of solid granite, where a 100ft high concrete wall would be constructed.  He wrote in his recommendations that the hilly and rocky catchment would fill the reservoir each year.

This spot will take you to a fantastic viewing point of the weir wall iconic inner valve tower.  Don't forget your camera!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8fd2b6fd-31f2-4a79-8e94-15d370f26e67" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Located in the Perth Hills, the Mundaring Weir is one of the world's greatest engineering projects.

Completed in 1903, the weir is the start of the water pipeline that pumps water to the Kalgoorlie goldfields some 700km away.

We have created this adventure lab to highlight some of the history &amp; beauty of the precinct.  

Mundaring Weir is a great spot to take the family &amp; the little ones will enjoy feeding the birds, enjoy!

**  Once you complete the adventure, use your journal entries to work out the Bonus Cache (GC8M58V). **&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2fa0de2f-e89e-4a07-ac79-d1a810c5ae15" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;VIEWING PLATFORM:
South Coordinates are ABCD minus 1387.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
