 <wpt lat="-32.055167" lon="115.739467">
  <ele>5.0</ele>
  <time>2020-09-05T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBinUo-02</name>
  <desc>DefenceOfPerth2</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Defence</url>
  <urlname>The Defence of Perth : S2 Fremantle Maritime Museum by Meme28</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-359" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>The Defence of Perth : S2 Fremantle Maritime Museum</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Meme28</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Meme28</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;The Defence of Perth&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Fremantle Maritime Museum&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Defence"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Defence&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How long in feet is HMAS Ovens? (digits)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7126c134-d257-4aaf-98de-33d38be74a1d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Perched on the Indian Ocean's shore, the WA Maritime Museum is symbolic of Fremantle’s past, present and future as a coastal city and port.

The Museum houses several unique galleries that explore WA's maritime relationship. From leisure boats and handcrafted sailing boats to commercial pearl luggers, the Museum inspires visitors to discover WA’s affinity with the ocean.

To the left of the museum lies the 89 metre (295 feet) long Oberon class Submarine, HMAS Ovens. It is an authentic Cold War-era vessel situated on Fremantle's historic World War Two submarine slipway, part of the home base for an Allied submarine fleet, which was stationed here during the war.  Amongst controls, sensors, tactical equipment and torpedoes, 63 people lived and served aboard the vessel in extremely cramped conditions.

The HMAS Ovens exhibit serves as a living memorial to submariners and those who gave their lives while serving from Fremantle during World War Two.

Ref: http://museum.wa.gov.au/museums/maritime
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/58814ab7-66e9-4885-b1d4-1399d838349f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Western Australia has some significant military locations, which have played an important role in the country’s wartime history. There are many military museums from Albany in the South, Broome in the North, and Kalgoorlie in the East. 

This series looks at some of the local military sites in the Perth area, which includes World War II Tunnels, local Telecommunications, Spitfires, Tanks and Artillery. 

Most museums have restricted opening hours, however the WWII Tunnels and tours of HMAS Ovens are temporarily suspended due to Covid-19. 

Important: 
The WWII Tunnels location in Mosman Park will take some physical effort to reach the site, however there is a path for wheelchairs and people with walking aides. Please follow the Directional Signs from the Boundary Road Carpark to the Heritage Site - approximately 350 metres.




https://scoop.com.au/military-museums-to-visit-across-wa


&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0ab88948-6f85-4964-986b-fbe1cc841e0e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations! 
Fun Fact- 
HMAS Ovens was launched on the 4 December 1967, and decommissioned on 1 December 1995.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.940433" lon="115.776367">
