   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Mundaring Weir Adventure Lab&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Pleasure Garden&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Mundaring"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Mundaring&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Who is the artist that created the "Weir Worker"&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e094384e-aa18-4db1-9f4a-30ed67bfaea5" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The surrounding area was known as the Pleasure Garden &amp; was laid by Paddy Dawson, a former weir construction worker in the 1920's.  He &amp; his wife lived in this area in the old stationmasters house &amp; his wife sold tea &amp; flowers from the nearby rose garden to the hundreds of visitors that would visit the dam by train each weekend.

Today there is also a new playground as well as electric BBQs &amp; toilets, but the rose garden &amp; exotic gardens still stand.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8fd2b6fd-31f2-4a79-8e94-15d370f26e67" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Located in the Perth Hills, the Mundaring Weir is one of the world's greatest engineering projects.

Completed in 1903, the weir is the start of the water pipeline that pumps water to the Kalgoorlie goldfields some 700km away.

We have created this adventure lab to highlight some of the history &amp; beauty of the precinct.  

Mundaring Weir is a great spot to take the family &amp; the little ones will enjoy feeding the birds, enjoy!

**  Once you complete the adventure, use your journal entries to work out the Bonus Cache (GC8M58V). **&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d5c8f40b-ecc3-481c-b25a-bbddb53732a2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;PLEASURE GARDEN:  
Gather the clues from each journal entry.  Cache hint will be provided in the geochecker!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.940033" lon="115.77615">
  <ele>80.0</ele>
  <time>2020-09-01T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LB6jJL-03</name>
  <desc>BeBoldReabold33</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ReaboldHill</url>
  <urlname>Be bold : Reabold Hill at Bold Park : S3 3. Seasonal Surprises by m4yb</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476915799" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Be bold : Reabold Hill at Bold Park : S3 3. Seasonal Surprises</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>m4yb</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">m4yb</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Be bold : Reabold Hill at Bold Park&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;3. Seasonal Surprises&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ReaboldHill"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ReaboldHill&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the common name of the frog on the right hand sign&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/09a54f0e-1230-464a-aa2d-27624937e9b2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Here are informative signs about the biodiversity of Bold Park, and the large number of plant and animal species.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5277b505-cf56-43e9-9cf9-16b463375042" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Bold Park close to the Coast, North of the River, covers 437 hectares and is one of the largest remaining bushland remnants in the urban area ofthe Swan Coastal Plain.  It was declared an A Class Reserve in 1998, and has an impressive biodiversity despite its proximity to the CBD.
Reabold Hill took the names of local Council figures  of the early 1900’s, Frank Rea and William Bold. It is the highest natural point on the Coastal Plain, the path you will be on will reward you with amazing views of the City and the Indian Ocean.
Please note the carpark hours: 5.30 am to 7pm from 1 April to 31 October, and 5.30am to 8pm 1 November to 31 March.
There is a Bonus Box associated with this Adventure, GC8Z9C2.  Make sure to collect the clues . And have fun!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Correct. D for the Bonus Box is the number of macrofungi added together down to 1 digit.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
