   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Be bold : Reabold Hill at Bold Park&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;2. Reabold Hill Enhancement&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ReaboldHill"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ReaboldHill&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the full name ( first name and surname) of the Minister who officially opened the Enhanced Walkway on 11  May 2005.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/26e1f692-9f10-41a3-85f5-a8684c5d1d33" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;At this location is a plaque detailing the official opening of the walkway on 11 May 2005.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5277b505-cf56-43e9-9cf9-16b463375042" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Bold Park close to the Coast, North of the River, covers 437 hectares and is one of the largest remaining bushland remnants in the urban area ofthe Swan Coastal Plain.  It was declared an A Class Reserve in 1998, and has an impressive biodiversity despite its proximity to the CBD.
Reabold Hill took the names of local Council figures  of the early 1900’s, Frank Rea and William Bold. It is the highest natural point on the Coastal Plain, the path you will be on will reward you with amazing views of the City and the Indian Ocean.
Please note the carpark hours: 5.30 am to 7pm from 1 April to 31 October, and 5.30am to 8pm 1 November to 31 March.
There is a Bonus Box associated with this Adventure, GC8Z9C2.  Make sure to collect the clues . And have fun!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Correct! Nearby is a number of metal flowers. Number of flowers +1 is B for the bonus box.
C  is the number of letters in the MLA’s surname&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
