 <wpt lat="-31.914733" lon="115.799367">
  <ele>3.0</ele>
  <time>2021-04-26T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBByQh-02</name>
  <desc>HerdsmanLakePe2</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3f03b2b5-e8c7-4523-a788-f89320921b98</url>
  <urlname>Herdsman Lake, Perth : S2 Statue in the lake by J2V Travel</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-274" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Herdsman Lake, Perth : S2 Statue in the lake</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>J2V Travel</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">J2V Travel</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Herdsman Lake, Perth&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Statue in the lake&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3f03b2b5-e8c7-4523-a788-f89320921b98"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3f03b2b5-e8c7-4523-a788-f89320921b98&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many figures are depicted in the statue? Look carefully.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a9fb1dbe-ab0b-4508-abe0-0ca3ff996474" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The statute in the lake was created by Pietro Porcelli and sat on top of the AMP Chambers building, 140 St George’s Tce, Perth from 1914 to 1972.  The statue was saved when the original building was demolished and eventually found its way to the current location when the Floreat Waters housing estate was developed in the 1990s.


&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f31219a6-70d9-4285-8fe6-6a1f720a71e1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This adventure lab will take you on a 7km loop around Herdsman Lake. It is best enjoyed by cycling, running or walking on the paths around the lake. Collect answers at each location to calculate the final coordinates for a bonus traditional geocache.

The Herdsman Lake Regional Park consists of native bush, parklands, an inner wetland and a dredged outer moat consisting of four deep permanent water bodies joined by small channels. 

It is a popular spot for birdwatchers. The lake is a breeding site for at least 20 species of birds including black swans. Please take care around the grassy areas as there may be tiger snakes.

The adventure is designed to start and finish at the car park on the south-west side of the lake, and to go clockwise around the lake. However, you can visit the locations in any order.

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d132f963-5b0b-42d8-8970-1ef10e2407bf" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;B=8&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
