 <wpt lat="-31.876317" lon="116.108633">
  <ele>185.0</ele>
  <time>2020-06-12T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBrZEi-03</name>
  <desc>RailwayReserve3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/RRHT2020</url>
  <urlname>Railway Reserves Heritage Trail : S3 Hovea Station by TeamBarritts</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909749" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Railway Reserves Heritage Trail : S3 Hovea Station</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>TeamBarritts</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">TeamBarritts</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Railway Reserves Heritage Trail&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Hovea Station&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/RRHT2020"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/RRHT2020&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;At the given coordinates you will find a plaque, what does it say the station is named after?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7dae0159-26e9-479f-ae2b-d590c64d3a92" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Hovea Station was the first train station in the park and was built in 1912.  It also served the nearby farmers and workers who commuted to Midland.

The famous line of palms determine the old platform and the nearby pad is still visible where the Station Masters house stood.

The rail line ceased being used in 1966.

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/84cc0cf3-8d28-4e6d-88c4-bbebe35387d5" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Railway Reserves Heritage Trail follows the route of the old Eastern Railway and is unique in providing a 41 kilometer loop entirely on railway formations. This extensive trail passes through quaint hills communities including Darlington, Parkerville and Mundaring, and covers a wide range of terrains with scenic views and numerous points of historical and natural significance.

This adventure will take you to five different points along the trail and should only take a few hours to complete.  Most can be reached by driving to nearby parking areas with a short stroll to the required locations.  The longest walk is approximately 2 klm round trip between locations 1 and 2.  These trails are well kept and easily accessible to all ages and levels of fitness.

Mobile reception can be patchy along the trail in certain spots, so we have increased the geofence to ensure all relevant information and data is available to you.  Always wear appropriate footwear, hat, sunscreen and carry enough water.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/13da39fc-01f7-4c79-b6a3-7e871efd12b9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Great work, now to the next location!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.838517" lon="115.948433">
