  <time>2020-06-12T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBrZEi-05</name>
  <desc>RailwayReserve5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/RRHT2020</url>
  <urlname>Railway Reserves Heritage Trail : S5 Mundaring Station &amp; Signal Tower by TeamBarritts</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909753" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Railway Reserves Heritage Trail : S5 Mundaring Station &amp; Signal Tower</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>TeamBarritts</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">TeamBarritts</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Railway Reserves Heritage Trail&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Mundaring Station &amp; Signal Tower&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/RRHT2020"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/RRHT2020&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;At the given coordinates you will see a small metal box,what letters are written on it?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4ec085aa-7476-4494-a527-445bce081e50" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Our last destination is the old Mundaring Station and adjoining Sculptor Park.

The original Eastern Railway passed through Mundaring on its first route through to Chidlow, and Mundaring Station was known as the central point for the region.  It also played a significant role for the construction of the Mundaring Weir and associated rail lines.

Following the construction of the second route of the Eastern Railway, the Mundaring line served as an alternative to the second route at the time of accidents and derailments, until its closing to traffic in 1954. 

As with the other locations, there are several information boards near the given coordinates that look at all the different locations and attractions the area has to offer, such as Mundaring Weir, located south of Mundaring on Mundaring Weir Rd.

This is also a good place to finish the adventure with the park, play areas, picnic tables and BBQ’s.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/84cc0cf3-8d28-4e6d-88c4-bbebe35387d5" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Railway Reserves Heritage Trail follows the route of the old Eastern Railway and is unique in providing a 41 kilometer loop entirely on railway formations. This extensive trail passes through quaint hills communities including Darlington, Parkerville and Mundaring, and covers a wide range of terrains with scenic views and numerous points of historical and natural significance.

This adventure will take you to five different points along the trail and should only take a few hours to complete.  Most can be reached by driving to nearby parking areas with a short stroll to the required locations.  The longest walk is approximately 2 klm round trip between locations 1 and 2.  These trails are well kept and easily accessible to all ages and levels of fitness.

Mobile reception can be patchy along the trail in certain spots, so we have increased the geofence to ensure all relevant information and data is available to you.  Always wear appropriate footwear, hat, sunscreen and carry enough water.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/82f86664-c93e-45f0-8110-4070a8e8bd02" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations, you've completed the adventure!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.904133" lon="116.165417">
