  <name>LBhyXS-04</name>
  <desc>LetsExploreMun4</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ExploreMundaring</url>
  <urlname>Let's Explore Mundaring : S4 Munda Biddi Northern Terminus by arnott.family</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909977" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Let's Explore Mundaring : S4 Munda Biddi Northern Terminus</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>arnott.family</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">arnott.family</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Let's Explore Mundaring&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Munda Biddi Northern Terminus&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ExploreMundaring"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ExploreMundaring&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;At the info shelter are several rusty panels.  Find the panel with tracks and footprints on it.  How many horseshoes are there?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c84d7980-6186-487c-b751-ac84cc1a6f77" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Munda Biddi means 'path through the forest' in the Noongar Aboriginal language. The trail meanders through scenic river valleys and the magnificent eucalypt forests of WA's South West. There are few places left in the world where a 1000km track could be built through an undeveloped natural corridor.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e819f454-c863-4344-ba64-c0dc289f2626" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to Mundaring.  Mundaring is a pleasant town on the eastern edge of the Perth Hills. It's famous in Western Australia for the Mundaring Weir which, through the remarkable engineering achievements of Charles Yelverton O'Connor, has supplied water to towns in the wheatbelt and the gold towns of Kalgoorlie and Coolgardie. Since the dam was built people have come from Perth to marvel at this watery saviour of the Eastern Goldfields. 
In this adventure we'll explore a few locations of interest in the Mundaring townsite.  All waypoints are located in walking distance and can easily be completed in under an hour.  But be sure to take some time to enjoy all that this charming little town has to offer.
Please note that any answers requiring numbers shall be in written form.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done.. You've completed this stage!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.90385" lon="116.165317">
  <ele>303.0</ele>
  <time>2020-08-15T08:00:00Z</time>
