   <groundspeak:name>Mundaring LGA Heritage Pub Crawl : S2 Mundaring Hotel</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>fratra</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">fratra</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Mundaring LGA Heritage Pub Crawl&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Mundaring Hotel&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/hph"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/hph&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;When standing on Jacoby St, How many arched windows can you see (not including the door)? (digit)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/60d08c87-6054-4d27-b5f7-ec1268c0b157" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Mundaring Hotel was opened in 1899 in Mundaring, a hills suburb of Perth, Western Australia.

The Mundaring Hotel is positioned prominently in the old heart of Mundaring, opposite the Railway Reserves Heritage Trail and on the adjacent corner of the Mundaring Hall.

In 1997 the Mundaring Hotel was categorised as having exceptional significance on the Shire of Mundaring municipal inventory and in 2016 was listed on Western Australia’s Heritage Register for the contribution made by the place to Western Australia’s cultural heritage.

MHI site 39 - The Mundaring Hotel has very high aesthetic, social and historic significance for its two storey styling and landmark qualities; its associations with the old heart of Mundaring and prominent people involved with the development of the district.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5ed890c9-75a3-435c-b521-bf5e55a0aecf" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;

We invite you to visit some local Heritage Listed establishments within the Mundaring LGA - this adventure should take between 1 - 2 hours.  The required information is able to be accessed 24/7.



Municipal Heritage Inventory -
It is mandatory under the Heritage of Western Australia Act 1990 for each local government
to maintain a Municipal Heritage Inventory (MHI). The Shire of Mundaring MHI lists many
places that contribute to the history and character of the local area and classifies them
according to the degree of significance. Modification of places on the MHI may not always
require planning approval, although sympathetic design is still recommended to maintain the
character and heritage values. 


&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.9042" lon="116.166667">
