  <desc>LetsExploreMun3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ExploreMundaring</url>
  <urlname>Let's Explore Mundaring : S3 Old Post Office by arnott.family</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909975" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Let's Explore Mundaring : S3 Old Post Office</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>arnott.family</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">arnott.family</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Let's Explore Mundaring&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Old Post Office&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ExploreMundaring"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ExploreMundaring&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;To the right of the entrance are 3 concrete cubes.  What is written on the middle cube?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2b954a00-2d4e-4971-9335-63191baa3113" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The first post office in Mundaring operated from July 1898, to late 1925 in a weatherboard and iron building on the corner of Jacoby and Hodgson Streets. As well as posts and telegraphs, from sometime after 1912, the post office, in common with many others, operated as a Commonwealth Savings Bank Agency. The original post office is now used as a playgroup centre. In early 1926, in line with the shift of the commercial centre of Mundaring from the railway line side of town to the York Road (Great Eastern Highway), a new weatherboard and iron post office was opened on the corner of York Road and Nichol Street.  In June 1997, after some internal modifications, the former post office building re-opened as the Mundaring Art Gallery, which had previously operated from a converted service station in Great Eastern Highway Mahogany Creek.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e819f454-c863-4344-ba64-c0dc289f2626" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to Mundaring.  Mundaring is a pleasant town on the eastern edge of the Perth Hills. It's famous in Western Australia for the Mundaring Weir which, through the remarkable engineering achievements of Charles Yelverton O'Connor, has supplied water to towns in the wheatbelt and the gold towns of Kalgoorlie and Coolgardie. Since the dam was built people have come from Perth to marvel at this watery saviour of the Eastern Goldfields. 
In this adventure we'll explore a few locations of interest in the Mundaring townsite.  All waypoints are located in walking distance and can easily be completed in under an hour.  But be sure to take some time to enjoy all that this charming little town has to offer.
Please note that any answers requiring numbers shall be in written form.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;You're doing well.  Another location complete!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.86585" lon="116.120217">
  <ele>255.0</ele>
  <time>2021-02-12T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBTnrz-03</name>
  <desc>SpookyWanderin3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1b385469-ed4b-4f73-9866-b6696aeb2af8</url>
  <urlname>Spooky Wanderings : S3 Parkerville Children’s Home Bush Cemetery by TeamBarritts</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99002493" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Spooky Wanderings : S3 Parkerville Children’s Home Bush Cemetery</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>TeamBarritts</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">TeamBarritts</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Spooky Wanderings&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Parkerville Children’s Home Bush Cemetery&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1b385469-ed4b-4f73-9866-b6696aeb2af8"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1b385469-ed4b-4f73-9866-b6696aeb2af8&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;At the given coordinates you will find a plaque, what year did Ursula Fanning die?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1ed61369-0b37-4d2a-bc72-9bab0cd68c41" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Children’s Bush Cemetery was part of the Parkerville Children’s Home (now known as Parkerville Children and Youth Care), but originally called The League of Charity Home for Waifs and Stray Babies. The Home was founded in 1903 by the Sisters of the Anglican Church.  When a child died, the Sisters would carry the simple coffins by horse and cart along the small dirt track from the Home.

The Cemetery is located 3 kms west of the Home at the end of a gravel road (Wilson Rd). There are approximately 30 babies &amp; young children buried in the cemetery who died between 1903 and 1919, but the names of only 24 are known. They are listed on a plaque by the entrance gate.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d145caeb-98e9-4811-8d6d-8e37e1682ce8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Adventure Lab takes you on a short tour of some of the oldest and most interesting cemetery’s around East Perth and the Hills area's.  This Lab should take about 2 hours to complete and all sites should have good phone coverage. 

While you are visiting the various locations please take the opportunity to read a few of the headstones, finding about the area and the history of the people who are laid to rest there.  Sometimes it may give a hint as to what they did and where they originated from. 

Very importantly, please remember where you are and show the appropriate respect for the residents and people visiting them.

There is also an optional bonus mystery cache to find once you have finished.  You will need to collect the clues provided in the journals to solve the puzzle and get the cache coordinates.  

Good luck and have fun! 
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c7343bff-bf76-46f5-92c6-af11878e077b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations, now onto the next one!!  The word you need is "abandoning"&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.901667" lon="116.166633">
  <ele>304.0</ele>
  <time>2020-08-15T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBhyXS-02</name>
  <desc>LetsExploreMun2</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ExploreMundaring</url>
  <urlname>Let's Explore Mundaring : S2 Old School House by arnott.family</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
