   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Let's Explore Mundaring&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Old School House&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ExploreMundaring"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ExploreMundaring&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;At the waypoint you should see a bench.  To whom is the bench placed in honour of?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/23804f3b-1c73-47e8-8b0a-b3728414327c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The old Mundaring Primary School has very high social, historic and aesthetic significance on its site in the centre of the Mundaring townsite. Historically and socially, the building has served the community since 1908 and is one of the last remnants of original buildings in the town centre.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e819f454-c863-4344-ba64-c0dc289f2626" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to Mundaring.  Mundaring is a pleasant town on the eastern edge of the Perth Hills. It's famous in Western Australia for the Mundaring Weir which, through the remarkable engineering achievements of Charles Yelverton O'Connor, has supplied water to towns in the wheatbelt and the gold towns of Kalgoorlie and Coolgardie. Since the dam was built people have come from Perth to marvel at this watery saviour of the Eastern Goldfields. 
In this adventure we'll explore a few locations of interest in the Mundaring townsite.  All waypoints are located in walking distance and can easily be completed in under an hour.  But be sure to take some time to enjoy all that this charming little town has to offer.
Please note that any answers requiring numbers shall be in written form.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Another location is finished.  Way to go!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
