   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;"Its All About The Kids" - Playing!&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Mundaring - Pioneer Park&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/AATK"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/AATK&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many daisy's are there?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3ac90193-707c-446c-99ac-e26567ed3023" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Another well established park in the heart of Mundaring's shopping district.  It has a great playground with slides, tunnels, rope ladders, monkey bars and a large sandpit.  It also has undercover picnic tables and plenty of benches to sit at and watch all the activity going on around you.

You will also find toilets, fast food outlets and convenience stores close by. 

There is plenty of parking however can get busy at times.

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8228662f-9b6b-498f-ae3f-705b0234ef20" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to our Adventure Lab Cache designed by kids for kids!

We have always loved parks and playgrounds so we thought a perfect theme for our series would revolve around some in the Mundaring area.  

This series will only take about an hour to complete, depending if you can pry the kids away from the swings.

Each has plenty of parking, good phone reception and amenities close by.

Please Enjoy!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.902517" lon="116.180317">
  <ele>307.0</ele>
  <time>2021-02-12T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBTnrz-04</name>
  <desc>SpookyWanderin4</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1b385469-ed4b-4f73-9866-b6696aeb2af8</url>
  <urlname>Spooky Wanderings : S4 Mundaring Cemetery by TeamBarritts</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99002495" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Spooky Wanderings : S4 Mundaring Cemetery</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>TeamBarritts</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">TeamBarritts</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Spooky Wanderings&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Mundaring Cemetery&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1b385469-ed4b-4f73-9866-b6696aeb2af8"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1b385469-ed4b-4f73-9866-b6696aeb2af8&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;At the given coordinates there is a columbarium, how many walls form this structure (as marked)?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/db0cdae6-3232-4592-8e9a-5d9805db93ea" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Mundaring Cemetery is located at the intersection of Yarri Grove and Railway Terrace, Mundaring, Western Australia and was gazetted as a burial ground in 1906.  Before the creation of Mundaring Cemetery families travelled to Midland and Guildford for funerals.

The earliest burials took place in the Anglican section of the cemetery and the earliest headstone that survives is that of Albert Lemmey, who died at the age of three in 1916. The next recorded burial was that of Private Gordon Jacque of the 28th Battalion. Jacques had been gassed during World War I and returned home for care, dying shortly afterwards in January 1919. His brother carved the timber enclosure that surrounds the grave.
The Mundaring Cemetery is administered by the Shire of Mundaring and, since 2007, is no longer available for interments unless already reserved.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d145caeb-98e9-4811-8d6d-8e37e1682ce8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Adventure Lab takes you on a short tour of some of the oldest and most interesting cemetery’s around East Perth and the Hills area's.  This Lab should take about 2 hours to complete and all sites should have good phone coverage. 

While you are visiting the various locations please take the opportunity to read a few of the headstones, finding about the area and the history of the people who are laid to rest there.  Sometimes it may give a hint as to what they did and where they originated from. 

Very importantly, please remember where you are and show the appropriate respect for the residents and people visiting them.

There is also an optional bonus mystery cache to find once you have finished.  You will need to collect the clues provided in the journals to solve the puzzle and get the cache coordinates.  

Good luck and have fun! 
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/017531bc-3c7e-4db0-8be6-973842047dc9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations, now onto the next stage!!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.8969" lon="115.7565">
  <ele>22.0</ele>
  <time>2019-07-10T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBx2SP-01</name>
  <desc>WESTCOASTWANDE1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/WCW</url>
  <urlname>A WEST COAST WANDER : S1 Tom Hungerford by m4yb</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909901" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>A WEST COAST WANDER : S1 Tom Hungerford</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>m4yb</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">m4yb</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;A WEST COAST WANDER&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Tom Hungerford&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/WCW"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/WCW&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many seahorses are seen in the plaque?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/89b226d9-dda3-489d-9211-eda24b749ff9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;At this location is a plaque in the ground.  This plaque marks the location of a beach house used by WA writer Tom Hungerford (1915-2011).
Tom Hungerford is remembered for his novels The Ridge and the River, set in the islands of Papua New Guinea during World War II, and Sowers of the Wind: A Novel of the Occupation of Japan.
He also wrote autobiographical works, Stories From Suburban Road, Knockabout with a Slouch Hat and Red Rover All Over published in one book called Straightshooter by the Fremantle Arts Centre Press.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/48498caf-36fd-4cf3-a819-120b5c5f1b75" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A little wander along some of the beachside suburbs of Perth North of the River, checking out landmarks and historic spots. The distance from start to finish is 4.7 km, a pleasant drive, cycle or walk enjoying the ocean outlook.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.8957" lon="115.7554">
  <ele>6.0</ele>
  <time>2020-11-28T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LB7Yq4-03</name>
  <desc>SLSCCityBeachT3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/SLSCpapillon367</url>
  <urlname>SLSC - City Beach to Sorrento : S3 Scarboro SLSC by papillon367</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-345" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>SLSC - City Beach to Sorrento : S3 Scarboro SLSC</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>papillon367</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">papillon367</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;SLSC - City Beach to Sorrento&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Scarboro SLSC&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/SLSCpapillon367"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/SLSCpapillon367&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the third large word on the most western door south of the SLSC lookout?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4168b23c-fd95-4339-a676-5bcb602ee0f7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Founded in 1928, Scarboro SLSC is located on the Esplanade in Scarborough, within the City of Stirling. Scarborough Beach is located approximately 14kms from Perth CBD and is well served through high-frequency public transport making it easily accessible to the greater Perth metropolitan area. 
In 2018, the club marked its 90th anniversary and moved into new purpose built facilities as part of the Scarborough Foreshore Redevelopment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1b3833c7-e4ba-4779-a7a1-798e221e747d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Adventure Lab is a tribute to all the volunteers who keep our beaches safe. It will take you to the Surf Life Saving Clubs between City Beach and Sorrento. It can be done in any order but the Bonus cache is at the Northern end of the Adventure Lab locations.
Please enter all answers in lowercase.
Hope you enjoy this AL, and don't forget to collect the clues for the Bonus which can be found at:
South 31 47.ABC East 115 44.DBE
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4fb70a6d-46c5-4a70-9aa3-244391d089d2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done, you have entered the right answer!
The clue for the Bonus cache is: C = 5&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.894467" lon="115.756233">
  <ele>16.0</ele>
