  <name>LBx2SP-02</name>
  <desc>WESTCOASTWANDE2</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/WCW</url>
  <urlname>A WEST COAST WANDER : S2 Scarborough Clock Tower by m4yb</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909903" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>A WEST COAST WANDER : S2 Scarborough Clock Tower</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>m4yb</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">m4yb</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;A WEST COAST WANDER&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Scarborough Clock Tower&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/WCW"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/WCW&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Look for a plaque at the southern end of one of the benches.  Which district did Fred Marsh belong to?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0ab87326-3b70-484e-9f2b-5e6f4bb548da" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Scarborough Clock Tower was unveiled in 1979 to commemorate WA’s 150th anniversary of European settlement, as well as Rotary International's 75th Anniversary, whose members at the time put forward the idea of the clock.
The very 70's design of the Clock Tower means the time can be seen from many angles:  Rotarian David Taggart, who owned Scarborough Pharmacy for 50 years, said Scarborough parents wanted a clock so their children would never have an excuse to be late home from a day at the beach.  
In 2017, the Clock Tower was moved west 7 metres during the multi million dollar foreshore redevelopment and is no longer at the centre of the roundabout.
It is on the WA State Register of Historical places.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/48498caf-36fd-4cf3-a819-120b5c5f1b75" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A little wander along some of the beachside suburbs of Perth North of the River, checking out landmarks and historic spots. The distance from start to finish is 4.7 km, a pleasant drive, cycle or walk enjoying the ocean outlook.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
