   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;"Its All About The Kids" - Playing!&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Stoneville - Riley Road Dog Park &amp; Playground&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/AATK"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/AATK&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many Seahorses are there in the play area?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/45dd1c33-fd26-443b-bb0f-3dbf415feed0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is a small fully fenced park and playground that is also dog friendly.  It has benches, swings, slides, balancing and climbing equipment including a large sandpit!

Parking might be an issue, though there are a few spots you can pull off the road for a short stop.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8228662f-9b6b-498f-ae3f-705b0234ef20" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to our Adventure Lab Cache designed by kids for kids!

We have always loved parks and playgrounds so we thought a perfect theme for our series would revolve around some in the Mundaring area.  

This series will only take about an hour to complete, depending if you can pry the kids away from the swings.

Each has plenty of parking, good phone reception and amenities close by.

Please Enjoy!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.28945" lon="115.906933">
  <ele>11.0</ele>
  <time>2020-04-17T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBEh6J-02</name>
  <desc>CraftBeerWineT2</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/CBAWT</url>
  <urlname>Craft Beer &amp; Wine Trail : S2 King Road Brewing Co. by pommieparkin2</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-284" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Craft Beer &amp; Wine Trail : S2 King Road Brewing Co.</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>pommieparkin2</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">pommieparkin2</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Craft Beer &amp; Wine Trail&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;King Road Brewing Co.&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/CBAWT"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/CBAWT&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;When does the kitchen close? (5 words)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a49cf9e2-965b-43f9-a40b-d7799b02c5c9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This seems an unlikely spot for a craft brewery, being in the middle of nowhere, between Rockingham and Byford. It can get incredibly busy at the weekend on a nice sunny day. It boasts a selection of craft beers and ciders, a rustic restaurant and extensive grounds with a play area for the kids.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5f5ebda9-0d65-4e22-ba61-6bcbb26516e4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;If discovering quality, unique craft beers and wine is at the top of your geocaching 'to do' list, the Peel Region Craft Beer and Wine Trail makes it easy for you. We have included five of the locations in this Adventure. The trail provides an authentically local experience, to be enjoyed at your own pace. You will need to hop into the geomobile and go for a drive through some attractive countryside in the Peel Region. You do not have to enter the establishment......but then again.....Why not?
 VIEW ALL JOURNAL ENTRIES FOR DETAILS ABOUT A BONUS CACHE. CHEERS, Have fun.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6f4a48ca-dd75-42a8-a9f1-fed633383529" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;You will need to make a note of the letter H for the keyword in the checker for the bonus cache GC8PEJT&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
