   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;"Its All About The Kids" - Playing!&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Sawyers Valley - Football Oval &amp; Playground&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/AATK"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/AATK&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many silver music tubes are at the location?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7125f035-5ccd-4ed7-b990-c4a08d762862" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is a relatively new park in the area and is unknown by most residents.  

You will find toilets, BBQ facilities and some picnic tables.  Parking may become a problem when there are any sporting events on at the nearby oval.

The playground has swings, slides, ladders, sandpit and numerous other activities to keep the kids amused.

There is also a service station and hotel close by.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8228662f-9b6b-498f-ae3f-705b0234ef20" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to our Adventure Lab Cache designed by kids for kids!

We have always loved parks and playgrounds so we thought a perfect theme for our series would revolve around some in the Mundaring area.  

This series will only take about an hour to complete, depending if you can pry the kids away from the swings.

Each has plenty of parking, good phone reception and amenities close by.

Please Enjoy!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.903717" lon="116.2049">
  <ele>310.0</ele>
  <time>2020-04-10T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBHWnu-04</name>
  <desc>MundaringLGAHe4</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/hph</url>
  <urlname>Mundaring LGA Heritage Pub Crawl : S4 Sawyers Valley Tavern by fratra</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99000323" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Mundaring LGA Heritage Pub Crawl : S4 Sawyers Valley Tavern</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>fratra</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">fratra</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Mundaring LGA Heritage Pub Crawl&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Sawyers Valley Tavern&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/hph"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/hph&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many small green planter boxes are on the outside railings surrounding the tavern?  (digit)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f64e0a1e-0007-4f4a-9272-277f18d2e416" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Sawyers Valley Tavern was established in 1882 in Sawyers Valley, a hills suburb of Perth, Western Australia. It was originally called the Sawyers Valley Hotel before acquiring its current name.

In 2016 the Sawyers Valley Tavern was listed on Western Australia's Heritage Register for the contribution made by the place to Western Australia's cultural heritage

MHI site 230 - The Sawyers Valley Tavern has high aesthetic and social significance for the local community and the Shire of Mundaring. The aesthetic significance is highlighted by the building's Art Deco character that is unique in the Shire. The site also has historic significance as the location of Lot Leather's former store and hotel.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5ed890c9-75a3-435c-b521-bf5e55a0aecf" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;

We invite you to visit some local Heritage Listed establishments within the Mundaring LGA - this adventure should take between 1 - 2 hours.  The required information is able to be accessed 24/7.



Municipal Heritage Inventory -
It is mandatory under the Heritage of Western Australia Act 1990 for each local government
to maintain a Municipal Heritage Inventory (MHI). The Shire of Mundaring MHI lists many
places that contribute to the history and character of the local area and classifies them
according to the degree of significance. Modification of places on the MHI may not always
require planning approval, although sympathetic design is still recommended to maintain the
character and heritage values. 


&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.8777" lon="115.7528">
  <ele>13.0</ele>
  <time>2020-11-28T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LB7Yq4-04</name>
  <desc>SLSCCityBeachT4</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/SLSCpapillon367</url>
  <urlname>SLSC - City Beach to Sorrento : S4 Trigg Island SLSC by papillon367</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476910129" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>SLSC - City Beach to Sorrento : S4 Trigg Island SLSC</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>papillon367</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">papillon367</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;SLSC - City Beach to Sorrento&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Trigg Island SLSC&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/SLSCpapillon367"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/SLSCpapillon367&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Who funded the mural? (3 words, lowercase)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/fe63fa64-6979-4c5d-aa34-2e8d344c7600" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Trigg Island SLSC was formed in October 1953. Since its inception, the Club has had three premises, the latest being built in 1993. Trigg Island is renowned for its infamous Blue Hole, which has claimed many lives over the years, although its notoriety has diminished more recently due to changes in the structure of the metropolitan coastline. Nevertheless it is the Club’s proud boast to have never lost a life in patrolled areas, and that more than 50% of all rescues carried out in Western Australia are at Trigg beach.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1b3833c7-e4ba-4779-a7a1-798e221e747d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Adventure Lab is a tribute to all the volunteers who keep our beaches safe. It will take you to the Surf Life Saving Clubs between City Beach and Sorrento. It can be done in any order but the Bonus cache is at the Northern end of the Adventure Lab locations.
Please enter all answers in lowercase.
Hope you enjoy this AL, and don't forget to collect the clues for the Bonus which can be found at:
South 31 47.ABC East 115 44.DBE
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c3e3cf85-b32b-4efe-be3b-ac0868cac09c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done, you have entered the right answer!
The clue for the Bonus cache is: D = 0&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.876967" lon="115.752167">
  <ele>10.0</ele>
  <time>2019-07-10T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBx2SP-03</name>
  <desc>WESTCOASTWANDE3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/WCW</url>
  <urlname>A WEST COAST WANDER : S3 Trigg Island Surf Lifesaving Club by m4yb</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909905" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>A WEST COAST WANDER : S3 Trigg Island Surf Lifesaving Club</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>m4yb</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">m4yb</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;A WEST COAST WANDER&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Trigg Island Surf Lifesaving Club&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/WCW"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/WCW&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Near the given coordinates is a bench.  What is the surname of the person whose name is on the plaque (In capital letters)?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9154e35d-e3e6-4903-b593-e55a04af71b3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Trigg Island is a low wave-washed rocky islet that forms the northern boundary of the long Swanbourne to Trigg beaches. This northern part of the Perth coast was only developed in the 1950s, with the Trigg Island Surf Life Saving Club being established in 1954. In its first two years of operation it rescued 47 people from the more hazardous surf at this end of the beach.
The surf club patrols the northern 1.5 km of the beach including the infamous Blue Hole, a permanent rip that runs out on the south side of the island, and has been the scene of many rescues. Furthermore, like adjoining South Trigg and Scarborough beaches, waves are higher along Trigg Beach, and the continuous bar is more likely to be cut by rips and rip channels, making this one of the most hazardous beaches in the Perth region.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/48498caf-36fd-4cf3-a819-120b5c5f1b75" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A little wander along some of the beachside suburbs of Perth North of the River, checking out landmarks and historic spots. The distance from start to finish is 4.7 km, a pleasant drive, cycle or walk enjoying the ocean outlook.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.7956" lon="116.00375">
  <ele>16.0</ele>
  <time>2020-06-23T08:00:00Z</time>
