  <desc>LSSBS4LightHors</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/StarSwampBushland</url>
  <urlname>[L] Star Swamp Bushland : S4 Light-Horse Division by iluvtrekking</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909955" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] Star Swamp Bushland : S4 Light-Horse Division</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>iluvtrekking</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">iluvtrekking</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Star Swamp Bushland&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Light-Horse Division&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/StarSwampBushland"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/StarSwampBushland&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The City of Stirling is a City of what?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/34df81b5-de1e-4fa2-9ebf-2811b04fa068" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
During the Second World War, a platoon of Australian Army 10th Light Horse Division was stationed at Mt Flora (Not Mt Floreat as stated on the sign) on coast watch duties.

The division used the swamp and a nearby well on Hope Street as frequent watering stations for their horses. 

The horses were once kept at a long-gone yard, which is now the intersection of Hope and Hale Streets.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6848cb18-a6c8-41dd-bdb0-612e81a8caf9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Star Swamp Bushland is a 96-hectare Class-A reserve, vested in, and managed by the City of Stirling. It is located 15 km north of Perth and comprises four hectares of semi-permanent freshwater lake with paperbark trees and 92 hectares of banksia, tuart, jarrah and marri woodlands, and areas of low heath.

Star Swamp provides a breeding site and sanctuary for both waterbirds and other bushland bird species with over 65 species of birds have been recorded. The bushland is also an important habitat for species of reptiles, insects, and spiders.

The main flowering period is between August and October, although there are plants in flower all year round. Over a dozen species of orchids occur in the bushland and several hundred flora species have been listed.

Ref: https://www.bushlandperth.org.au/treasures/star-swamp-bushland-reserve/&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8ac966cf-1fa7-4c0e-878f-03fccec2909b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Can you imagine how noisy it must have been with all the soldiers and their horses camped here?
D=4
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.85675" lon="115.751467">
  <ele>11.0</ele>
  <time>2020-10-10T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBJffw-05</name>
  <desc>KayaWandjooS5Ka</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Kaya</url>
  <urlname>Kaya Wandjoo : S5 Karil (crab) by thornies</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99002545" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Kaya Wandjoo : S5 Karil (crab)</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>thornies</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">thornies</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Kaya Wandjoo&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Karil (crab)&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Kaya"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Kaya&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the minimum size in milimetres for a legal size Green mud crab?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/86ab2a94-b118-48e6-a4a2-4a9964f26e83" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is a favourite spot for fishing. You need to consult the legal size limit sticker.

Art Credit: MAAC Car Park - Creatures of Marmion Marine Park by Amok Island &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/dc7ad8d6-de30-4c45-8925-6dde0736d902" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kaya Wandjoo. These words are Hello and Welcome in Noongar language, the language of the Noongar Whadjuk  people. This beautiful coast is part of Whadjuk boodjar (country) and as you explore this adventure lab you will learn some other Noongar words and names.

This adventure lab is ideal to do on foot or bike and fills in the section of coastline between two other adventure labs. It can be started at any of the 5 locations.

I would like to acknowledge the Noongar Whadjuk  people, the Traditional Custodians of this land and pay my respects to their Elders past, present and emerging. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4e46bf41-6b53-4605-8322-8101b7d92df7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.879667" lon="116.208383">
  <ele>267.0</ele>
  <time>2020-04-10T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBHWnu-05</name>
  <desc>MundaringLGAHe5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/hph</url>
  <urlname>Mundaring LGA Heritage Pub Crawl : S5 Mount Helena Tavern by fratra</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99000325" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Mundaring LGA Heritage Pub Crawl : S5 Mount Helena Tavern</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>fratra</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">fratra</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Mundaring LGA Heritage Pub Crawl&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Mount Helena Tavern&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/hph"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/hph&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What word can you see on the arch as you enter the beer garden? (7 letters)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/92df5a62-8e96-49e9-8f16-e93f16382edf" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Mount Helena Tavern was opened in 1902 in Mount Helena, a hills suburb of Perth, Western Australia. It was originally called the Lion Mill Hotel, then the Mount Helena Hotel, before acquiring its current name. Locally it is referred to as The Mounties

In 2016 the Mount Helena Tavern was listed on Western Australia’s Heritage Register for the contribution made by the place to Western Australia’s social heritage.

MHI site 179 - The Mount Helena Tavern has very high aesthetic, social and historic significance for the Mount Helena community and the Shire of Mundaring.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5ed890c9-75a3-435c-b521-bf5e55a0aecf" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;

We invite you to visit some local Heritage Listed establishments within the Mundaring LGA - this adventure should take between 1 - 2 hours.  The required information is able to be accessed 24/7.



Municipal Heritage Inventory -
It is mandatory under the Heritage of Western Australia Act 1990 for each local government
to maintain a Municipal Heritage Inventory (MHI). The Shire of Mundaring MHI lists many
places that contribute to the history and character of the local area and classifies them
according to the degree of significance. Modification of places on the MHI may not always
require planning approval, although sympathetic design is still recommended to maintain the
character and heritage values. 


&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.878733" lon="116.21">
  <ele>270.0</ele>
  <time>2020-07-13T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBVbwm-01</name>
  <desc>ItsAllAboutThe1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/AATK</url>
  <urlname>"Its All About The Kids" - Playing! : S1 Mt Helena - Pioneer Park by BJA3</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909891" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>"Its All About The Kids" - Playing! : S1 Mt Helena - Pioneer Park</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>BJA3</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">BJA3</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;"Its All About The Kids" - Playing!&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Mt Helena - Pioneer Park&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/AATK"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/AATK&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many rungs on the light blue monkey bars?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/dfad4111-0d0a-4fec-864f-3828fa555ccd" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A well established park in the heart of Mt Helena with a great playground for all ages, BBQ facilities, toilets, hotel and convenience store close by. 

There is plenty of parking however can get busy on the weekends.

This is a great place to start our series.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8228662f-9b6b-498f-ae3f-705b0234ef20" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to our Adventure Lab Cache designed by kids for kids!

We have always loved parks and playgrounds so we thought a perfect theme for our series would revolve around some in the Mundaring area.  

This series will only take about an hour to complete, depending if you can pry the kids away from the swings.

Each has plenty of parking, good phone reception and amenities close by.

Please Enjoy!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.852033" lon="115.7512">
