  <name>LBJffw-04</name>
  <desc>KayaWandjooS4Ma</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Kaya</url>
  <urlname>Kaya Wandjoo : S4 Maambakoort (ocean) by thornies</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99002543" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Kaya Wandjoo : S4 Maambakoort (ocean)</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>thornies</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">thornies</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Kaya Wandjoo&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Maambakoort (ocean)&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Kaya"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Kaya&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What type of cliffs are there at this location?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b4dfeaf5-19a0-45ef-81b4-b7085de6eb7b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Enjoy the walk from the nearest car park through the coastal scrub until you end up behind the Indian Ocean Marine Research Centre. 

Art credits: Peter Ryan mural on the Sorrento Beach Shower block
Hayley Welsh artwork Splash of Colour on Water Corporation Asset
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/dc7ad8d6-de30-4c45-8925-6dde0736d902" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kaya Wandjoo. These words are Hello and Welcome in Noongar language, the language of the Noongar Whadjuk  people. This beautiful coast is part of Whadjuk boodjar (country) and as you explore this adventure lab you will learn some other Noongar words and names.

This adventure lab is ideal to do on foot or bike and fills in the section of coastline between two other adventure labs. It can be started at any of the 5 locations.

I would like to acknowledge the Noongar Whadjuk  people, the Traditional Custodians of this land and pay my respects to their Elders past, present and emerging. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/35af462a-2870-4529-b900-4bf1419be36a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations!

&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
