   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Kaya Wandjoo&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Boola Bindjel (many bubble)&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Kaya"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Kaya&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many air bubbles are depicted in the Creatures of Marmion Marine Park mural by Brenton See?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/919ab8ea-5248-4976-a2ac-2530188ed4cf" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is a fantastic spot for snorkelling, swimming, enjoying the view and public art. You are looking for the mural on the northern wall of the MAAC building.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/dc7ad8d6-de30-4c45-8925-6dde0736d902" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kaya Wandjoo. These words are Hello and Welcome in Noongar language, the language of the Noongar Whadjuk  people. This beautiful coast is part of Whadjuk boodjar (country) and as you explore this adventure lab you will learn some other Noongar words and names.

This adventure lab is ideal to do on foot or bike and fills in the section of coastline between two other adventure labs. It can be started at any of the 5 locations.

I would like to acknowledge the Noongar Whadjuk  people, the Traditional Custodians of this land and pay my respects to their Elders past, present and emerging. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d389d091-5067-4915-8304-654c0b840fab" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations! While you are here, enjoy the mural of Creatures of Marmion Marine Park by Amok Island.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
