 <wpt lat="-32.348717" lon="116.047933">
  <ele>208.0</ele>
  <time>2020-04-17T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBEh6J-01</name>
  <desc>CraftBeerWineT1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/CBAWT</url>
  <urlname>Craft Beer &amp; Wine Trail : S1 Millbrook Winnery by pommieparkin2</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-283" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Craft Beer &amp; Wine Trail : S1 Millbrook Winnery</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>pommieparkin2</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">pommieparkin2</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Craft Beer &amp; Wine Trail&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Millbrook Winnery&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/CBAWT"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/CBAWT&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many spokes are on the mill wheel on the gate? Enter the number, not the word.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/aaaa73c1-50a1-427e-8aa6-fd85b8195e23" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A stunning location in a tranquil setting. No need to go beyond the gates but it would be a pity to come all this way and not venture further.
Millbrook is a boutique winery and restaurant in the historic town of Jarrahdale in Western Australia, 50 minutes south-east of Perth. The winery is located at the picturesque Chestnut Farm, a property that backs on to the Serpentine River and is nestled among jarrah forests, with stunning vistas of the rolling landscape.

The origins of Chestnut Farm date back to the 19th century, when the original owner, Joseph Batt, planted an orchard and the first grapevines in 1865, providing fruit to the local timber-millers in Jarrahdale.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5f5ebda9-0d65-4e22-ba61-6bcbb26516e4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;If discovering quality, unique craft beers and wine is at the top of your geocaching 'to do' list, the Peel Region Craft Beer and Wine Trail makes it easy for you. We have included five of the locations in this Adventure. The trail provides an authentically local experience, to be enjoyed at your own pace. You will need to hop into the geomobile and go for a drive through some attractive countryside in the Peel Region. You do not have to enter the establishment......but then again.....Why not?
 VIEW ALL JOURNAL ENTRIES FOR DETAILS ABOUT A BONUS CACHE. CHEERS, Have fun.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/dc762787-bc82-4c16-9a4c-6e319956e665" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;You will need to make a note of the letter C for the keyword in the checker for the bonus cache&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
