 <wpt lat="-32.339117" lon="115.8201">
  <ele>13.0</ele>
  <time>2020-04-25T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LB7EhB-01</name>
  <desc>BaldivisDogPar1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/BDP</url>
  <urlname>Baldivis Dog Park : S1 Tuart by Kyzabra</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476910123" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Baldivis Dog Park : S1 Tuart</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Kyzabra</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Kyzabra</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Baldivis Dog Park&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Tuart&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/BDP"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/BDP&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;At the base of this tuart, is a plaque. What year was Tuart Ridge Estate opened?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0c168874-91dd-45ff-86d8-e9c45667de95" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Eucalyptus gomphocephala, known as Tuart, is a species of tree, one of the six forest giants of Southwest Australia. Tuart forest was common on the Swan coastal plain, until the valuable trees were felled for export and displaced by the urban development around Perth.

A 350year old Tuart is not far from here amongst the trees in the Settlers Walk. It is in a park off Rankin Meander and has a circumference of 7.70 metres&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/604a7b92-e3c2-46b2-b593-9bcb4266a413" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Take a short stroll from the Baldivis Dog Park, and down along the creek.
There are some interesting artworks along this short adventure lab series.
Park at the dog park, start your wander, then turn around and come back to give your 4 legged friends a real run.

At each location, there will be a clue once you answer the question. Grab the 5 letters (one in each answer), which will reveal a key word. You will need this keyword for a nearby mystery cache.

Keep a note of the clues for the bonus at https://coord.info/GC8PQ4H 
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done. But dont forget you need a clue.

The letter you need is "G"&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.339867" lon="115.8208">
