  <desc>WelcomeToRottn5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a20eeaee-4f8d-4a77-9351-3ce8f4f7d0a3</url>
  <urlname>Welcome to Rottnest : S5 Island Heritage by Barco</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-446" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Welcome to Rottnest : S5 Island Heritage</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Barco</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Barco</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Welcome to Rottnest&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Island Heritage&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a20eeaee-4f8d-4a77-9351-3ce8f4f7d0a3"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a20eeaee-4f8d-4a77-9351-3ce8f4f7d0a3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;By what name was Lomas Cottage commonly known?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2dfffcbc-2956-4523-8ca3-f4e4f7944070" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A number of wonderful heritage buildings exist on the island and are open to the public, including Holy Trinity Church, the Salt Store, the Chapel and the Museum. There are also extensive military buildings and infrastructure including Kingstown Barracks &amp; parade ground (operational until 1984) and the Oliver Hill gun battery (WWII fortifications).

And while Rottnest today is a place of joyful memories, sadly that has not always been the case. Established in 1839 as a British penal facility, around 4000 Aboriginal prisoners were incarcerated on the island with around 370 dying during captivity. The island was also used as an internment camp in both WWI and WWII, and more recently was a secure quarantine facility for Covid-19.

This grassed area is Heritage Common where you will find a number of heritage buildings and information boards. Please take the time to reflect on the past.

Also located here is Lomas Cottage, now an exhibition space. An information board is outside.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6be0f959-3fcc-482b-823b-da42db56d643" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Situated 18kms offshore in the sparkling Indian Ocean, Rottnest Island is Perth's playground - with over 500,000 visitors each year coming to enjoy this A Class protected reserve.

Known as Wadjemup to the local Nyoongar people, 'Rotto' is absolutely packed with incredible experiences, breathtaking scenery, fantastic beaches, amazing wildlife and a huge array of things to see &amp; do. Whether you flew here, sailed over, caught a ferry or even swam here (yes, people do!), you'll quickly discover why Rotto is much-loved by locals and visitors alike.

It's a destination like no other. This Adventure will highlight a few locations to compliment your visit and can easily be completed on foot during a day trip - giving you heaps of time to explore and enjoy the rest of the island!

Note: All visitors are required to pay an admission fee to the island (Government levy to help fund conservation). Accordingly, this Adventure has been approved for publication by Geocaching HQ.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7adea259-0b85-4a90-922a-8e8d97a2b872" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done.

A person without knowledge of the past is like a tree without roots.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.98935" lon="115.540583">
  <ele>6.0</ele>
  <time>2020-12-30T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBB6HK-04</name>
  <desc>WelcomeToRottn4</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a20eeaee-4f8d-4a77-9351-3ce8f4f7d0a3</url>
  <urlname>Welcome to Rottnest : S4 Lighthouses &amp; Shipwrecks by Barco</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476919018" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Welcome to Rottnest : S4 Lighthouses &amp; Shipwrecks</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Barco</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Barco</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Welcome to Rottnest&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Lighthouses &amp; Shipwrecks&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a20eeaee-4f8d-4a77-9351-3ce8f4f7d0a3"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a20eeaee-4f8d-4a77-9351-3ce8f4f7d0a3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;In what year was the Leeman Monument unveiled?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4c7f8059-db4c-41d3-a7c9-833ce39c8d8a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Opening in 1900, the Bathurst Lighthouse was built in response to the City of York being wrecked on the reef a year earlier with the tragic loss of 11 lives. Recognising that one lighthouse in the centre of the island was insufficient, this additional lighthouse was constructed at half the height of the main lighthouse at Wadjemup Hill, and provides an additional reference point for seafarers navigating into Fremantle.

Offering fantastic views across the iconic Pinky Beach the lighthouse beam is visible for 14 nautical miles. Bathurst Lighthouse is closed to the public, however guided tours are available at Wadjemup Lighthouse. With a number of wrecks around the coastal waters and its limestone reef terrain, Rottnest offers world-class diving opportunities. In fact, one such event led directly to the first known European to land on Rottnest: Abraham Leeman in 1658. 

The commemorative Leeman Monument is nearby.

Note: the beach stage can be reached via the signed 'Eagle' coastal path along Pinky Beach.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6be0f959-3fcc-482b-823b-da42db56d643" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Situated 18kms offshore in the sparkling Indian Ocean, Rottnest Island is Perth's playground - with over 500,000 visitors each year coming to enjoy this A Class protected reserve.

Known as Wadjemup to the local Nyoongar people, 'Rotto' is absolutely packed with incredible experiences, breathtaking scenery, fantastic beaches, amazing wildlife and a huge array of things to see &amp; do. Whether you flew here, sailed over, caught a ferry or even swam here (yes, people do!), you'll quickly discover why Rotto is much-loved by locals and visitors alike.

It's a destination like no other. This Adventure will highlight a few locations to compliment your visit and can easily be completed on foot during a day trip - giving you heaps of time to explore and enjoy the rest of the island!

Note: All visitors are required to pay an admission fee to the island (Government levy to help fund conservation). Accordingly, this Adventure has been approved for publication by Geocaching HQ.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c06c066a-2c87-4623-8f4a-14817bdc5116" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done.

Bonus fact: built in 1896 the Wadjemup Lighthouse was Australia's first rotating beam lighthouse.
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.989517" lon="115.5356">
  <ele>7.0</ele>
  <time>2020-12-30T08:00:00Z</time>
