  <desc>WelcomeToRottn3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a20eeaee-4f8d-4a77-9351-3ce8f4f7d0a3</url>
  <urlname>Welcome to Rottnest : S3 Beaches &amp; Bays by Barco</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476919016" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Welcome to Rottnest : S3 Beaches &amp; Bays</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Barco</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Barco</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Welcome to Rottnest&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Beaches &amp; Bays&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a20eeaee-4f8d-4a77-9351-3ce8f4f7d0a3"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a20eeaee-4f8d-4a77-9351-3ce8f4f7d0a3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What was the name of Willem de Vlamingh’s ship that anchored here in 1696?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/704b81f5-c5eb-44ac-9251-4e4e948e5332" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A beach-lovers paradise, with over 63 secluded beaches and 20 bays to sit and relax you will be spoilt for choice on Rottnest. With incredible scenery at every turn, Rottnest boasts some of the finest beaches in the world.

One which regularly tops traveller recommendation lists is The Basin, famed for its crystal clear shallow waters and fantastic snorkelling. Situated only a 10 minute walk from the main settlement, The Basin's pristine waters offer a safe environment for the whole family.

With swimming, surfing, fishing, snorkelling, diving and boating opportunities all around the island this A Class Reserve provides a magical marine environment.

When enjoying the beaches please stay safe and remember the beach code:

Take nothing but photographs
Keep nothing but memories
Leave nothing but footprints

Looking out over the beach is the Willem de Vlamingh Commemorative Plaque.

Note: the lighthouse stage can be reached via the signed 'Eagle' coastal path along the beach.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6be0f959-3fcc-482b-823b-da42db56d643" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Situated 18kms offshore in the sparkling Indian Ocean, Rottnest Island is Perth's playground - with over 500,000 visitors each year coming to enjoy this A Class protected reserve.

Known as Wadjemup to the local Nyoongar people, 'Rotto' is absolutely packed with incredible experiences, breathtaking scenery, fantastic beaches, amazing wildlife and a huge array of things to see &amp; do. Whether you flew here, sailed over, caught a ferry or even swam here (yes, people do!), you'll quickly discover why Rotto is much-loved by locals and visitors alike.

It's a destination like no other. This Adventure will highlight a few locations to compliment your visit and can easily be completed on foot during a day trip - giving you heaps of time to explore and enjoy the rest of the island!

Note: All visitors are required to pay an admission fee to the island (Government levy to help fund conservation). Accordingly, this Adventure has been approved for publication by Geocaching HQ.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/426d81e1-8afb-42a0-881b-cef7474fe31f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done.

I hope you enjoyed your dip in the ocean. Did you find Nemo?&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
