   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;A Stroll Around Larkhill&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Homestead&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cf94e8cd-426b-4e6c-9005-bff09749c2b7"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cf94e8cd-426b-4e6c-9005-bff09749c2b7&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What name appears on the vane&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0d5c181c-bc9a-41f1-84be-d60a3613b5e6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This structure is not the actual site of the original 1800s homestead. If you look back towards the sports fields that is down the hill a little way. The only remains are a few fence posts and a broken gate. When we first visited this site about 7 years ago there were information boards giving the history of the site but they have disappeared too. I am currently researching it and will update this page when I am able.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/22ef9791-6c1e-4af1-b457-febcac1c1ff0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;We have enjoyed all of the adventure Lab Caches that we have tried so far but must admit that we did most of them by car or public transport. With the festive season over it has been decided that I need a little more exercise! So this one is designed to take you on a walk or bike ride, starting and finishing in Larkhill Sports Complex and meandering on bush walks up to the Old Homestead which boasts a panoramic view of the whole complex.
Venture to the boardwalks for amazing viewing of nature such as the 600+ year old grass trees. The viewing platforms will highlight other special features of interest. Make time to stop and read the nature signage along the trails that highlight and explain the flora and fauna of the area. The wetland is a Federally recognised Threatened Ecological Community (TEC).
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a1440e10-3151-46d8-b0a3-b7d8cc019fe8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations. The letter P will come in useful later.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.384783" lon="115.76515">
