   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;A Stroll Around Larkhill&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Summit&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cf94e8cd-426b-4e6c-9005-bff09749c2b7"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cf94e8cd-426b-4e6c-9005-bff09749c2b7&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How tall is this slender shrub? (no gaps between entries)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/93b1d4f0-5df4-46fe-b712-4ecf3cce6faa" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;You have a clear view of the surrounding area from up here, including the Lark Hill Thoroughbred Training Facility which is where Horse Racing trainers come to work their champions on a grass and sand surfaced track.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/22ef9791-6c1e-4af1-b457-febcac1c1ff0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;We have enjoyed all of the adventure Lab Caches that we have tried so far but must admit that we did most of them by car or public transport. With the festive season over it has been decided that I need a little more exercise! So this one is designed to take you on a walk or bike ride, starting and finishing in Larkhill Sports Complex and meandering on bush walks up to the Old Homestead which boasts a panoramic view of the whole complex.
Venture to the boardwalks for amazing viewing of nature such as the 600+ year old grass trees. The viewing platforms will highlight other special features of interest. Make time to stop and read the nature signage along the trails that highlight and explain the flora and fauna of the area. The wetland is a Federally recognised Threatened Ecological Community (TEC).
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/178d6158-757e-4feb-88ad-0ee461e38018" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;To find the bonus cache you will need to remove the blinkers &amp; make a note of the letter S&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
