 <wpt lat="-32.386667" lon="115.762917">
  <ele>3.0</ele>
  <time>2021-02-19T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBhjdt-01</name>
  <desc>StrollAroundLa1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cf94e8cd-426b-4e6c-9005-bff09749c2b7</url>
  <urlname>A Stroll Around Larkhill : S1 An Entrance to the Reserve by pommieparkin2</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476910043" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>A Stroll Around Larkhill : S1 An Entrance to the Reserve</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>pommieparkin2</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">pommieparkin2</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;A Stroll Around Larkhill&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;An Entrance to the Reserve&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cf94e8cd-426b-4e6c-9005-bff09749c2b7"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cf94e8cd-426b-4e6c-9005-bff09749c2b7&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many safety signs must be observed(letters)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ada61dc8-1ede-4f6b-9205-b27eed2742ac" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The reserve is located in an area known as the Becher Plain, which has been formed through the accumulation of Holocene sediments over a period of around 7000 years. This unique environment contains 21 threatened ecological community damp lands and is an important scientific research area for the study of the holocene dune swales.
The Lark Hill Nature Reserve takes in a linear, north-south oriented swale with constructed walking tracks around the swale, and two elevated walkways that cross the swale, providing good visitor viewing access.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/22ef9791-6c1e-4af1-b457-febcac1c1ff0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;We have enjoyed all of the adventure Lab Caches that we have tried so far but must admit that we did most of them by car or public transport. With the festive season over it has been decided that I need a little more exercise! So this one is designed to take you on a walk or bike ride, starting and finishing in Larkhill Sports Complex and meandering on bush walks up to the Old Homestead which boasts a panoramic view of the whole complex.
Venture to the boardwalks for amazing viewing of nature such as the 600+ year old grass trees. The viewing platforms will highlight other special features of interest. Make time to stop and read the nature signage along the trails that highlight and explain the flora and fauna of the area. The wetland is a Federally recognised Threatened Ecological Community (TEC).
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/57b33604-a1ab-4df2-acb4-77fc5ce9cf65" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done, you got it. Make a note of the letter R&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.387917" lon="115.765583">
  <ele>5.0</ele>
