  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476910049" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>A Stroll Around Larkhill : S4 A Bridge Too Far?</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>pommieparkin2</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">pommieparkin2</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;A Stroll Around Larkhill&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;A Bridge Too Far?&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cf94e8cd-426b-4e6c-9005-bff09749c2b7"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cf94e8cd-426b-4e6c-9005-bff09749c2b7&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year is the reference&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9d0f2cb3-397c-4bdf-a59c-aca9e638ae88" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A nice covered area to get out of the sun and take the weight off your feet while reading the interesting signage.
The Southern Brown Bandicoot or Quenda is one of WA's most endearing mammals. Often not much bigger than a brown rat, they can grow as big as rabbits. They only inhabit areas with dense vegetation so this area should be ideal for them but unfortunately, as they are nocturnal you probably will not catch sight of them, unless of course you are one of those intrepid night cachers!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/22ef9791-6c1e-4af1-b457-febcac1c1ff0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;We have enjoyed all of the adventure Lab Caches that we have tried so far but must admit that we did most of them by car or public transport. With the festive season over it has been decided that I need a little more exercise! So this one is designed to take you on a walk or bike ride, starting and finishing in Larkhill Sports Complex and meandering on bush walks up to the Old Homestead which boasts a panoramic view of the whole complex.
Venture to the boardwalks for amazing viewing of nature such as the 600+ year old grass trees. The viewing platforms will highlight other special features of interest. Make time to stop and read the nature signage along the trails that highlight and explain the flora and fauna of the area. The wetland is a Federally recognised Threatened Ecological Community (TEC).
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a6c1d0a5-6b14-495c-bc42-133e9c43a5b5" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;This little fella has just uncovered the letter O&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.392217" lon="115.761717">
  <ele>9.0</ele>
