   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Craft Beer &amp; Wine Trail&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Peel Ridge Winery&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/CBAWT"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/CBAWT&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What two letters appear in the shield?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/112909c1-f2ad-4874-95bc-f2e0ff0fe69c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Situated in Karnup close to the towns of Rockingham, Mandurah and Baldavis in perfect tranquillity set amongst the Kangaroos, Kookaburras, Blue Jays and other native wildlife.

Known for their speciality Nebbiolo and Tempranillo wines but also produce Shiraz, Cabernet Sauvignon and Fortified Shiraz. The whiterange includes Chenin Blanc, Verdelho and Sparkling. The team believe that ‘quality wines begin in the vineyard’ and that their use of time intensive traditional methods enables meticulous care and expert craftsmanship to be infused into every bottle.

Art in the Vines events are held regularly in the grounds and cellar door tastings are open weekends and during the week by appointment.
Once completed VIEW ALL JOURNAL ENTRIES FOR DETAILS ABOUT A BONUS CACHE&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5f5ebda9-0d65-4e22-ba61-6bcbb26516e4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;If discovering quality, unique craft beers and wine is at the top of your geocaching 'to do' list, the Peel Region Craft Beer and Wine Trail makes it easy for you. We have included five of the locations in this Adventure. The trail provides an authentically local experience, to be enjoyed at your own pace. You will need to hop into the geomobile and go for a drive through some attractive countryside in the Peel Region. You do not have to enter the establishment......but then again.....Why not?
 VIEW ALL JOURNAL ENTRIES FOR DETAILS ABOUT A BONUS CACHE. CHEERS, Have fun.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/42c191a0-43d7-4ceb-b697-21fac13b9fd3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;The last letter you need for the key word in the bonus cache checker is S&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.4107" lon="115.784117">
  <ele>11.0</ele>
  <time>2020-04-17T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBEh6J-04</name>
  <desc>CraftBeerWineT4</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/CBAWT</url>
  <urlname>Craft Beer &amp; Wine Trail : S4 Peel Estate Wines by pommieparkin2</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-286" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Craft Beer &amp; Wine Trail : S4 Peel Estate Wines</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>pommieparkin2</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">pommieparkin2</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Craft Beer &amp; Wine Trail&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Peel Estate Wines&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/CBAWT"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/CBAWT&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many arrows are on the sign? Enter the number, not the word.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/87ed2cd0-7f4d-4b7e-b4bc-172c4ead1ad3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Peel Estate Wines has been an integral part of the Peel Region for over 40 years. In 1973 the first Shiraz vines were planted, followed by Chenin Blanc and Zinfandel in 1976, and Cabernet Sauvignon in 1979. Other varieties such as Chardonnay, Verdelho, Cabernet Franc and the traditional Portuguese Port Varieties were planted in 1980.

The Peel region with its close proximity to the Indian Ocean is the ideal location to grow wine grapes as it combines unique coastal limestone soils and a Mediterranean climate, ensuring wines with fruit intensity along with specific regional characteristics.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5f5ebda9-0d65-4e22-ba61-6bcbb26516e4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;If discovering quality, unique craft beers and wine is at the top of your geocaching 'to do' list, the Peel Region Craft Beer and Wine Trail makes it easy for you. We have included five of the locations in this Adventure. The trail provides an authentically local experience, to be enjoyed at your own pace. You will need to hop into the geomobile and go for a drive through some attractive countryside in the Peel Region. You do not have to enter the establishment......but then again.....Why not?
 VIEW ALL JOURNAL ENTRIES FOR DETAILS ABOUT A BONUS CACHE. CHEERS, Have fun.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8896631d-68cb-4a63-8fad-c4c3755c2c74" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;A double E will come in useful for GC8PEJT&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.691333" lon="115.702467">
  <ele>7.0</ele>
  <time>2020-08-25T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBDfgq-01</name>
  <desc>MindarieWander1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/MINDARIE</url>
  <urlname>Mindarie Wanderer : S1 Watering Hole - The Marina by olthomas</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-353" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Mindarie Wanderer : S1 Watering Hole - The Marina</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>olthomas</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">olthomas</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Mindarie Wanderer&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Watering Hole - The Marina&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/MINDARIE"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/MINDARIE&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;On the wall is a sign discussing the conditions of entry to The Marina. What is the 6th word of the 3rd condition?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d77dcc7d-e540-41f9-ad94-d6e4e8f87205" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Here at Mindarie Marina you will find many places to have a drink, some food or even a hair cut! This is the social centre of Mindarie.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1bf20d88-6171-4dfb-aa59-a47d56937de8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The purpose of this adventure lab is to get you out for a walk or bike ride along our stunning coastline. The series can be done in either direction with ample parking and watering holes at either end to aid the weary cacher! 

It is approximately 3km from one end to the other with a suggested route attached to the Bonus Box - GC8YQKG. This route keeps it fairly flat and gives you a nosey at the posh houses. NB There is a section of steps but there is a flat paved section to roll your bike up or down.

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Cheers!

Your code letter for the Bonus Box is X&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
