   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Mindarie Wanderer&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Entrance&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/MINDARIE"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/MINDARIE&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;At this location is a red Entry marker for boat traffic. What does the black and white three character sign read at the top. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1c061243-38d8-4a8f-bf73-226d149a82d1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Many days you can spot people fishing off this sea wall and other days its just watching the boats come and go.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1bf20d88-6171-4dfb-aa59-a47d56937de8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The purpose of this adventure lab is to get you out for a walk or bike ride along our stunning coastline. The series can be done in either direction with ample parking and watering holes at either end to aid the weary cacher! 

It is approximately 3km from one end to the other with a suggested route attached to the Bonus Box - GC8YQKG. This route keeps it fairly flat and gives you a nosey at the posh houses. NB There is a section of steps but there is a flat paved section to roll your bike up or down.

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Good work!

The code you need to collect here is F&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
