   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Mindarie Wanderer&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Osprey Nesting&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/MINDARIE"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/MINDARIE&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;There is a marker post here numbered '3' - what is the second to last word in the main paragraph?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e6277682-d617-433f-82ef-a9faa75e681f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Breeding season for Osprey is June/July and they like to create their nests (or stacks) on rocky ledges or high vantage points. You can see a man-made helping hand from this location but rest assured the Osprey are responsible for making it a home. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1bf20d88-6171-4dfb-aa59-a47d56937de8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The purpose of this adventure lab is to get you out for a walk or bike ride along our stunning coastline. The series can be done in either direction with ample parking and watering holes at either end to aid the weary cacher! 

It is approximately 3km from one end to the other with a suggested route attached to the Bonus Box - GC8YQKG. This route keeps it fairly flat and gives you a nosey at the posh houses. NB There is a section of steps but there is a flat paved section to roll your bike up or down.

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Good Quandong spotting !

Your letter for the bonus box here is M&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.678383" lon="115.695167">
  <ele>10.0</ele>
