   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Mindarie Wanderer&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Sentinel by Simon Gilby&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/MINDARIE"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/MINDARIE&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt; Spin around and look at the Quinns Beach sign - what is the second last word of paragraph 2?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/373bd623-9f45-49a8-bc01-fee72cb6acf2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;I've always wanted to place a traditional cache on this sculpture but never felt quite that mean! This is the start or end point of this series with local parking and a local watering hole.

While the sculpture is lovely, the associated info is to easy for any armchair cacher to find so lets make it a little harder.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1bf20d88-6171-4dfb-aa59-a47d56937de8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The purpose of this adventure lab is to get you out for a walk or bike ride along our stunning coastline. The series can be done in either direction with ample parking and watering holes at either end to aid the weary cacher! 

It is approximately 3km from one end to the other with a suggested route attached to the Bonus Box - GC8YQKG. This route keeps it fairly flat and gives you a nosey at the posh houses. NB There is a section of steps but there is a flat paved section to roll your bike up or down.

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations for getting out and grabbing some fresh air!

Your reward for the bonus box is H&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
