   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;End of the Line&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Butler Station&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/EOTL"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/EOTL&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Although not being an end of the line station Butler is the start and end point for what northern suburbs train line? ( _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ )&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5061fc48-f1e6-4370-ae21-a3d322f3f28f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Butler station is currently the northernmost terminus on the Perth Rail Network.

It is located 40.7km to the north of Perth and was opened on Septermber 21st 2014.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b725a41a-cce1-431d-909c-cab48dd07c51" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Please be aware the locations for this Adventure Lab are quite a distance from the map marker, make sure you check your nearest Lab point before commencing.

The metropolitan Perth rail network is comprised of five major lines connecting the four Metropolitan Development Corridors and Fremantle to the Perth CBD.

Over the coming years the network is set to expand even further to accomade travelers from Ellenbrook, Forrestfield and extending lines past Armadale to Byford and continuing north to Yanchep.

This Adventure Lab will take you on a tour of the various lines of the Perth Rail Network. You are more than welcome to catch the trains to the stops (it can be done in a single day) if you wish but this is not a requirement, in fact all information can be gained and answered without entering the stations themselves.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7caf1eea-a012-4b3d-832e-baf2be3f7b19" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;The clue you need for the bonus final is:
 P&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.519333" lon="115.7512">
  <ele>17.0</ele>
  <time>2020-08-31T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBj1Vq-05</name>
  <desc>LMandurahsMari5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f6ad5266-a886-4c2e-ae97-fbd8d73a9b99</url>
  <urlname>[L] Mandurah's Marine Life + Puzzles Adventure Lab : S5 Mandurah Scoop by Mistraluna</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476919010" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] Mandurah's Marine Life + Puzzles Adventure Lab : S5 Mandurah Scoop</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Mistraluna</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Mistraluna</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Mandurah's Marine Life + Puzzles Adventure Lab&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Mandurah Scoop&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f6ad5266-a886-4c2e-ae97-fbd8d73a9b99"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f6ad5266-a886-4c2e-ae97-fbd8d73a9b99&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;At the last location, you were given another puzzle to solve. Where in WA are they found? (5 words, upper case, no spaces)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a3ecc023-6611-457b-b066-46ba27fa7a37" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This seemingly abstract artwork by Anne Neil, situated on the roundabout at the start of Manjoogoordap Road, which provides access to the Kwinana Freeway, was inspired by the region's long established water based activities and attractions, the abundance of marine life, especially the blue manna crab and the now famous annual Mandurah Crab Festival.

The design is representational of a fishing net, changing as it moves through the water. The Scoop is made up of five central posts or 'ribs', which are offset in an arched shape. It is constructed of marine grade aluminum, is approximately 10.5m high and sits within a 25 metre circular space within the roundabout. The whole structure is lit up at night, with the colours helping you to visualize the movement of the scoop through the water. It really is quite stunning to see!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0918047e-dc18-4811-b483-7502cd0f9637" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Adventure Lab cache is designed to get people out and about exploring Mandurah and the marine environment it has long been renowned for. The downtown tourist precinct seems to be forever evolving with new things to be discovered each time you wander around. Fortunately there are lots of places to stop, grab a bite to eat or something to drink before continuing on your way.

Please be prepared to spend a little bit of time on these ones with three of them having a fairly simple puzzle of some sort for you to solve. Hopefully, you will bring a pen and paper with you, your thinking caps and of course your cameras, for all the photo opportunities along the way.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/decebcb5-ab4d-4cee-a53a-bdd3db4b6ea8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations! That completes the Adventure Lab cache. Hope you had fun with it along the way and that you have a safe journey home. Bye!!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.607767" lon="115.658317">
  <ele>13.0</ele>
  <time>2019-07-08T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBnWWY-01</name>
  <desc>PerthNorthernB1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/PNBM</url>
  <urlname>Perth Northern Beaches Meander : S1 The Wreck of the Alkimos by megawat60</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99001483" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Perth Northern Beaches Meander : S1 The Wreck of the Alkimos</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>megawat60</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">megawat60</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Perth Northern Beaches Meander&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Wreck of the Alkimos&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/PNBM"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/PNBM&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the last word in the sixth line of the second paragraph&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8e8bae21-40b8-4b44-b9c5-f2d16f348e8e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;At the waypoint you will find a plaque describing the wreck and the details of its demise, it has been a much talked about and written about wreck with one great book by a local, to Perth, Jack Wong Sue.

A lot of talk about the wreck being haunted and the book is a fascinating read indeed.  Certainly some other great videos worth a look at if this history interests you, it certainly did me.  And I have very fond memories of 4 X 4 driving through the area back in the 1980's and 90's when the wreck was a lot lot more visible than it is today.

Hope you have enjoyed stage 1 of this Adventure Lab.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8c216064-ccd7-4b93-bb4c-d9523e5b22a4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A meander from the Wreck of the Alkimos to Leeman's Landing in Two Rocks, with some scenic outlooks and plenty of spots of historical significance on the way. 

This can easily be completed within a day or you could rush and do it in a few hours, however I recommend you take your time and explore the area and take in some of Western Australia's early history.  Some parts might have you thinking about the early European passengers who thought they were heading to Batavia (Jakarta) but ended up being shipwrecked on what is now the beautiful northern beaches of Perth.

It is best completed from south to north, however it can be completed in any order you like, parking is readily available at all points or for the fitter geocachers a bicycle ride is quite doable.

Keep a close eye on your answers at each stage, because there might be a "Bonus Box" (GC8ANQJ) published.
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
