   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Mandurah's Marine Life + Puzzles Adventure Lab&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Yaburgurt Memorial&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f6ad5266-a886-4c2e-ae97-fbd8d73a9b99"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f6ad5266-a886-4c2e-ae97-fbd8d73a9b99&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Not too difficult a question to answer here. How many crabs (whole crabs or parts of) can you see on the panels? (spell answer, lower case)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/019c76c2-56be-43b2-a5fb-9af9b2fa0051" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This artwork is located on Mandjar Square and was placed here to celebrate and commemorate the life of the Aboriginal leader Yaburgurt. His father (Winjan) and grandfather (Mogum) were leaders in the area. Yaburgurt was born  in Koolyininap (Halls Head) in 1824, a survivor of the Pinjarra Massacre he  became a significant  influential Noongar leader in the  region. Settlers gave him the name ‘George’ Winjan.

Yaburgurt saw much change and left a legacy that includes his wisdom, his knowledge of culture, his understanding and relationship of the land and the leadership of his people.  There is a  thread of cooperation and tolerance through his personal story as he found his way to work with the early colonising communities to great effect becoming one of the first Aboriginal people in the region to embrace reconciliation.

A hint for the next puzzle: you have in your hand the tool you need to solve it.

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0918047e-dc18-4811-b483-7502cd0f9637" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Adventure Lab cache is designed to get people out and about exploring Mandurah and the marine environment it has long been renowned for. The downtown tourist precinct seems to be forever evolving with new things to be discovered each time you wander around. Fortunately there are lots of places to stop, grab a bite to eat or something to drink before continuing on your way.

Please be prepared to spend a little bit of time on these ones with three of them having a fairly simple puzzle of some sort for you to solve. Hopefully, you will bring a pen and paper with you, your thinking caps and of course your cameras, for all the photo opportunities along the way.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/683825af-d149-4fc5-84c8-23ce3d2c7d5c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Awesome! Now you have new image showing a puzzle. Use your pen and paper to solve the puzzle before heading off to the next location.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.528483" lon="115.720367">
  <ele>4.0</ele>
  <time>2020-08-31T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBj1Vq-01</name>
  <desc>LMandurahsMar13</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f6ad5266-a886-4c2e-ae97-fbd8d73a9b99</url>
  <urlname>[L] Mandurah's Marine Life + Puzzles Adventure Lab : S1 3D Pavement Artwork by Mistraluna</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909807" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] Mandurah's Marine Life + Puzzles Adventure Lab : S1 3D Pavement Artwork</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Mistraluna</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Mistraluna</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Mandurah's Marine Life + Puzzles Adventure Lab&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;3D Pavement Artwork&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f6ad5266-a886-4c2e-ae97-fbd8d73a9b99"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f6ad5266-a886-4c2e-ae97-fbd8d73a9b99&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The Mandurah Estuary is how big? (6 words, 5-3-4-2-6-7, no spaces, all lower case)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9c854a6b-2da6-44e6-b4ab-79b6f87bc394" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Various locations around Mandurah have been transformed into tourism drawcards, aimed at creating additional photo opportunities for visitors and locals alike.

The pavement outside the Mandurah Visitor Centre on Mandurah Terrace boasts a remarkable depiction of the Peel-Harvey Estuary. Visit Mandurah commissioned Australia’s most highly awarded pavement artist, Jenny McCracken, to create this impressive 3D illusion for people to pose with.

If you stand at the spot from where the featured photo was taken, you can find the information you need to log this location's Adventure Lab cache.

PS Another of Jenny McCracken's artworks can be viewed and enjoyed at the Eastern End of the New Mandurah Traffic Bridge where the initial adventure lab icon is indicating, so you might like to go and check it out before leaving town.

PPS There is a hint on the image for the first puzzle, but here is another: M = V&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0918047e-dc18-4811-b483-7502cd0f9637" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Adventure Lab cache is designed to get people out and about exploring Mandurah and the marine environment it has long been renowned for. The downtown tourist precinct seems to be forever evolving with new things to be discovered each time you wander around. Fortunately there are lots of places to stop, grab a bite to eat or something to drink before continuing on your way.

Please be prepared to spend a little bit of time on these ones with three of them having a fairly simple puzzle of some sort for you to solve. Hopefully, you will bring a pen and paper with you, your thinking caps and of course your cameras, for all the photo opportunities along the way.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f16b1be1-bf69-46b3-ac13-448e0f87fe41" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done! Now you have new image showing a simple cipher with hint. Use pen and paper to solve it before heading off to the next location.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
