  <urlname>Yaberoo Budjara Heritage Trail : S5 Modern Communications! by megawat60</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-342" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Yaberoo Budjara Heritage Trail : S5 Modern Communications!</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>megawat60</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">megawat60</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Yaberoo Budjara Heritage Trail&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Modern Communications!&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/YBHT"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/YBHT&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;AT GZ, look NW at a bearing of 313 degrees and what is the main man made item you see? Two words 13-5&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/86c7c176-2ce2-40d0-aaa8-926e29bde7ec" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;If you walk a few more hundred metres you will come across a major junction where the firefighters came up from Wanneroo Rd and stopped the spread of the fire any further south.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c2f2c5b7-befb-464d-a211-5baf96d6e98f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This 28 kilometre one way trail is based on the movement of Yellagonga and his people between Lake Joondalup and Yanchep.

Welcome to a small section of this trail.  This section runs approximately 1.5 Kilometres South from Yanchep Beach Road and follows about 8 of my Traditional caches towards the end of this section of the trail at Lacey Rd.  You can start anywhere along the trail but worth doing with the traditional's along that route, if you haven't already done it!

There is a "Bonus Cache" so you will need to take notes of the clues as you progress.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9f0a8812-bbb8-4d39-980c-101abee6b7a8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;You know have the co-ords for the Bonus Box, so go get it at South 31 32.581 East 115 41.296&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
