   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Yaberoo Budjara Heritage Trail&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;More directional signs&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/YBHT"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/YBHT&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Looking south, how many triangular signs do you see?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0afa4c29-bbd6-4972-b569-1238483c4f42" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;On the western side of the trail you will find a burnt banksia tree, not quite the same location as the photo but this photo shows the start fo the regeneration growth.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c2f2c5b7-befb-464d-a211-5baf96d6e98f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This 28 kilometre one way trail is based on the movement of Yellagonga and his people between Lake Joondalup and Yanchep.

Welcome to a small section of this trail.  This section runs approximately 1.5 Kilometres South from Yanchep Beach Road and follows about 8 of my Traditional caches towards the end of this section of the trail at Lacey Rd.  You can start anywhere along the trail but worth doing with the traditional's along that route, if you haven't already done it!

There is a "Bonus Cache" so you will need to take notes of the clues as you progress.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c205f8eb-1c22-4b57-a48b-0d5c080f202a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Multiply the answer by 2 for the D co-ordinate.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
