   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Yaberoo Budjara Heritage Trail&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Meeting Place&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/YBHT"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/YBHT&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;There are more than ? caves&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/39e5856b-ad76-402a-9bd6-63429308b5c0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Inside the main area of the park is a great place to see many of the Western Grey kangaroos grazing on the lawns and around the golf course.  If you're lucky you may catch a flock of the endangered Carnaby black-cockatoos and in the late winter early spring some great blooms of wild flowers.  Keep your eyes open!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c2f2c5b7-befb-464d-a211-5baf96d6e98f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This 28 kilometre one way trail is based on the movement of Yellagonga and his people between Lake Joondalup and Yanchep.

Welcome to a small section of this trail.  This section runs approximately 1.5 Kilometres South from Yanchep Beach Road and follows about 8 of my Traditional caches towards the end of this section of the trail at Lacey Rd.  You can start anywhere along the trail but worth doing with the traditional's along that route, if you haven't already done it!

There is a "Bonus Cache" so you will need to take notes of the clues as you progress.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/42b2916d-2efb-40d1-9982-f7ef454ea396" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Clue 2 for the bonus location!  How many letters in the first word on the third line in the second paragraph?&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
