   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Yaberoo Budjara Heritage Trail&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;A good place to start&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/YBHT"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/YBHT&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What are not allowed on this trail.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/62357ce0-1553-4112-a0df-6ed3343ca234" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The start of the trail from Yanchep Beach Road, this photo was taken on the 19th December 2019 just after the road had been opened after the horrendous bush fires of that year.  Note the amount of re-growth that has started after the winter rains&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c2f2c5b7-befb-464d-a211-5baf96d6e98f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This 28 kilometre one way trail is based on the movement of Yellagonga and his people between Lake Joondalup and Yanchep.

Welcome to a small section of this trail.  This section runs approximately 1.5 Kilometres South from Yanchep Beach Road and follows about 8 of my Traditional caches towards the end of this section of the trail at Lacey Rd.  You can start anywhere along the trail but worth doing with the traditional's along that route, if you haven't already done it!

There is a "Bonus Cache" so you will need to take notes of the clues as you progress.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4c990ce2-11b4-4d06-9d2f-d804d2ebc248" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;How many letters in the last word of the second paragraph?&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
