  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-302" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] Dwellingup Trails : S5 Jarrah Log</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>ullyssia</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">ullyssia</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Dwellingup Trails&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Jarrah Log&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/10bd7e37-07f9-4517-acdf-c44b86bcbfce"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/10bd7e37-07f9-4517-acdf-c44b86bcbfce&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Approximately how many years old is this jarrah log?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/bbc4cda9-3839-414a-9e3d-631423e55708" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The last stop on the tour of Dwellingup.  

Here you will find an actual log and whim.  If you are interested in finding out more about the forrest, the Forest Heritage Centre is a 5-10 minute walk north (follow the emu footprints!).  There is an interpretive centre, a treetop walk, and a range of nature, forestry and indigenous based tours.

Just across the road from where you are standing is the Dwellingup Hotel.  It was built by Mr Hugh McNeil in 1911 and is the oldest building remaining in the town, having survived the 1961 fire.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b61a24aa-07de-4f97-90fa-3a81d9a0e69e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Adventure will take you on a small tour of the town of Dwellingup.  

At the end of the Adventure, you will receive the coordinates for a Bonus Cache located a short drive away: Dwellingup Trails AL Bonus Box (GC940X8).

Seeing as you have driven all the way here, I recommend you park at the visitor centre and take the opportunity to stretch the legs and walk to the various locations. It won't take longer than half an hour.

It is worth taking the time to check out the visitor centre either before or after your walk.  And if you have even more time to spend in the area, there is a lot to explore.  Take a ride on the Hotham Valley Railway, go camping or adventuring at Lane Pool Reserve, there are heaps of trails to explore by foot, bike, horse or 4WD - and this is is one of the few places the Bibbulmun and the Munda Biddi tracks intersect.

Or if too much adventure is not your thing, just spend time in town checking out some of the unique attractions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations!  When you have finished exploring Dwellingup, head to S 32° 42.967 E 116° 04.141 for the Bonus Box.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
