  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909883" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Getting Giddy in Beverley : S2 The chicken and the ..... ?</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Morgo the geo</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Morgo the geo</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Getting Giddy in Beverley&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The chicken and the ..... ?&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Giddy2017"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Giddy2017&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the other animal painted here, other than the chicken?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/bcce9d13-f601-4507-a18d-cb172f04e6de" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;At this location you will see two of the six animals painted as murals along Vincent Street. 

Lean against the wall and admire the view.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0e20e958-6f1b-41ca-83c5-9c9952122eb5" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Beverley is a wheatbelt town 130km east of Perth on the Avon River. Founded in 1838, Beverley is one of Western Australia’s oldest settlements.

The town is lucky to play host to well known artist James Giddy who visited in June 2017. He painted animals throughout the town centre, in a medium known as ‘en plain air’, simply translated to painting ‘in open air’.

This adventure lab takes you on a journey of his brilliant murals leaving a lasting mark on Vincent Street.

Stop and have a coffee at one of the cafes and explore the railway station art gallery. The skate park and playground should be a hit for the kids.

You will collect a letter from four of the locations and a suffix containing 5 characters at another. This clue will be the code required for the bonus box.  The BB is a short walk to the east of the murals. I would start the adventure at the fountain.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c26cbcdd-3ec3-44f5-85f5-059752df4b68" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done. The letter you require for the bonus box is ‘I’&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
