Giddy’s use of bold, painterly brushstrokes compliment the natural subjects and bring attention to his chosen medium. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0e20e958-6f1b-41ca-83c5-9c9952122eb5" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Beverley is a wheatbelt town 130km east of Perth on the Avon River. Founded in 1838, Beverley is one of Western Australia’s oldest settlements.

The town is lucky to play host to well known artist James Giddy who visited in June 2017. He painted animals throughout the town centre, in a medium known as ‘en plain air’, simply translated to painting ‘in open air’.

This adventure lab takes you on a journey of his brilliant murals leaving a lasting mark on Vincent Street.

Stop and have a coffee at one of the cafes and explore the railway station art gallery. The skate park and playground should be a hit for the kids.

You will collect a letter from four of the locations and a suffix containing 5 characters at another. This clue will be the code required for the bonus box.  The BB is a short walk to the east of the murals. I would start the adventure at the fountain.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e9c82d47-cafa-43be-a9f8-e943359f29c9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Awesome work. Write down the letter ‘D’.

Make sure you visit the Vampire aircraft too.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
