  <desc>LMNNS1StJosephs</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/newnorcia</url>
  <urlname>[L] Monkeying about in New Norcia : S1 St Joseph's Orphanage &amp; Old Convent by atCatpacity</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99000072" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] Monkeying about in New Norcia : S1 St Joseph's Orphanage &amp; Old Convent</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>atCatpacity</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">atCatpacity</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Monkeying about in New Norcia&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;St Joseph's Orphanage &amp; Old Convent&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/newnorcia"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/newnorcia&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many white pillars are outside the entrance to the visitors centre? (one digit) &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5731ba74-e792-4526-a9ca-6ffcfacf3a45" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;St Joseph's orphanage for girls was one of the two homes for indigenous children. The other being St Mary's boys home at the northern end of town. Though called an orphanage, many of the children may have had parents living in town or nearby and some may have been removed from their parents care. 
The old convent included a chapel, an infirmary, workrooms, and quarters for the sisters. 

This building now serves as the tourism hub for New Norcia. Inside is the visitors centre and gift shop as well as an art gallery/museum. Take a moment to look at the big map outside and get your bearings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2fa8714d-7bbf-457d-a958-153ce7f66b93" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;New Norcia is Australia's only monastic town. Founded in 1847 by Spanish Benedictine Monks, the catholic mission quickly grew into a small self-sufficient town. The town’s focus has changed over the years. From missionary work, to monastic and pastoral duties, to education, and now tourism.

A gem in the bush and a place of deep serenity, New Norcia is a place of beautiful historic buildings and spectacular landscapes. 

We would like to take you on a quick tour of the township. There’s much more to see than the five locations we have chosen. The route will take you past some other places where you might like to stop and explore. 

The waypoints will need to be collected in sequential order. This is so that we can deliver coordinates for our “Bonus Box” (GC91G24) when you have visited the final waypoint.

So, take your time and enjoy the peace and beauty of this truly unique place.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ac89e3a9-aa4f-4d35-af2e-3baa1d5b1819" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;It's worth noting that there is only one place in town to buy hot food. The Salvado Roadhouse Cafe is to the south of here on the main road.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-30.971383" lon="116.2156">
  <ele>215.0</ele>
  <time>2020-10-23T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBKWv5-05</name>
  <desc>LMNNS5MissionCo</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/newnorcia</url>
  <urlname>[L] Monkeying about in New Norcia : S5 Mission Cottages &amp; Marian Shrine by atCatpacity</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99000080" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] Monkeying about in New Norcia : S5 Mission Cottages &amp; Marian Shrine</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>atCatpacity</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">atCatpacity</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Monkeying about in New Norcia&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Mission Cottages &amp; Marian Shrine&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/newnorcia"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/newnorcia&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Go inside the interpretation centre. How many coloured glass windows are there? (one digit) &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d2bf05ad-6c21-4d21-9bac-542b06bc1cb0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The mostly empty field south of the Abbey Church was once the site of a small village of cottages. These houses were home to aboriginal families. New Norcia's original purpose was as a mission. The idea being to convert the Yued people - the traditional owners of this area - to Catholicism.

By the early 1900's, some of the indigenous people had left New Norcia and a few of the cottages were occupied by european families. The last of the cottages were demolished in 1950 and now only a few foundations remain.

The nearby heptagonal building was built around 1983 to commemorate a fire which threatened to burn down the newly founded mission in 1847. The brothers believed that they were saved by a painting of the Virgin Mary. More detail about this story can be found on the eastern side of the building. 

Today the Marian shrine is used as an interpretation centre for the mission cottages. There is information inside about the lives of aboriginal people on the mission. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2fa8714d-7bbf-457d-a958-153ce7f66b93" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;New Norcia is Australia's only monastic town. Founded in 1847 by Spanish Benedictine Monks, the catholic mission quickly grew into a small self-sufficient town. The town’s focus has changed over the years. From missionary work, to monastic and pastoral duties, to education, and now tourism.

A gem in the bush and a place of deep serenity, New Norcia is a place of beautiful historic buildings and spectacular landscapes. 

We would like to take you on a quick tour of the township. There’s much more to see than the five locations we have chosen. The route will take you past some other places where you might like to stop and explore. 

The waypoints will need to be collected in sequential order. This is so that we can deliver coordinates for our “Bonus Box” (GC91G24) when you have visited the final waypoint.

So, take your time and enjoy the peace and beauty of this truly unique place.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8a04cb37-a659-4d0e-97bd-7448646067bb" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations!

You will find the Bonus Box cache GC91G24 at:

S 30° 58.482
E 116° 12.815&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-30.970433" lon="116.216133">
  <ele>215.0</ele>
  <time>2020-10-23T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBKWv5-04</name>
  <desc>LMNNS4AbbeyChur</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/newnorcia</url>
  <urlname>[L] Monkeying about in New Norcia : S4 Abbey Church &amp; Monastery by atCatpacity</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99000078" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] Monkeying about in New Norcia : S4 Abbey Church &amp; Monastery</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>atCatpacity</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">atCatpacity</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Monkeying about in New Norcia&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Abbey Church &amp; Monastery &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/newnorcia"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/newnorcia&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What shape is depicted in the glass above the church door?  (one word) &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7ec0f3f8-5a57-402a-8f8d-7eb69ce3bdc0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Abbey Church is at least the fourth church built in New Norcia since the original mission house in 1847. The current building was completed in 1863, with the belfry added in 1908. Bishop Salvado (the founding bishop of New Norcia) is entombed inside. 

The church is still in use today. If the door is open, feel free to have a look inside. There is some impressive artwork and a large organ. 

Directly opposite the church are the gates to the monastery cloister. The monastery building as we see it today was built around the original mission house, with sections and wings being added over several decades. The Benedictines have lived and worked on this site for more than 170 years. 

The street between these two buildings was the original main road of New Norcia. The current main road was constructed in the 1920's, moving traffic away from the monastery. In 2017, Main Roads completed the Great Northern Highway bypass of New Norcia, which has surely made meditation even easier. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2fa8714d-7bbf-457d-a958-153ce7f66b93" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;New Norcia is Australia's only monastic town. Founded in 1847 by Spanish Benedictine Monks, the catholic mission quickly grew into a small self-sufficient town. The town’s focus has changed over the years. From missionary work, to monastic and pastoral duties, to education, and now tourism.

A gem in the bush and a place of deep serenity, New Norcia is a place of beautiful historic buildings and spectacular landscapes. 

We would like to take you on a quick tour of the township. There’s much more to see than the five locations we have chosen. The route will take you past some other places where you might like to stop and explore. 

The waypoints will need to be collected in sequential order. This is so that we can deliver coordinates for our “Bonus Box” (GC91G24) when you have visited the final waypoint.

So, take your time and enjoy the peace and beauty of this truly unique place.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b9a34497-d006-4d59-ba81-2c500a47d190" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;You can join the monks for one of the seven daily prayer sessions in the Monastery chapel, and on Saturdays it is possible to meet a monk. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-30.969367" lon="116.21385">
  <ele>225.0</ele>
  <time>2020-10-23T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBKWv5-03</name>
  <desc>LMNNS3Cemetery</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/newnorcia</url>
  <urlname>[L] Monkeying about in New Norcia : S3 Cemetery by atCatpacity</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99000076" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] Monkeying about in New Norcia : S3 Cemetery</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>atCatpacity</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">atCatpacity</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Monkeying about in New Norcia&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Cemetery&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/newnorcia"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/newnorcia&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Find Angelina Taylor. What was her husband's first name? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f749c566-6e8d-4b67-b71f-60f20f319763" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The town's cemetery is located between the girls and boys boarding schools, St Gertrude's and St Ildephonsus'. These days the school buildings are used as accommodation for school and music camps.

The simple white crosses mark graves of indigenous people. You might notice a few prominent family names that made up this small community on the headstones. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2fa8714d-7bbf-457d-a958-153ce7f66b93" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;New Norcia is Australia's only monastic town. Founded in 1847 by Spanish Benedictine Monks, the catholic mission quickly grew into a small self-sufficient town. The town’s focus has changed over the years. From missionary work, to monastic and pastoral duties, to education, and now tourism.

A gem in the bush and a place of deep serenity, New Norcia is a place of beautiful historic buildings and spectacular landscapes. 

We would like to take you on a quick tour of the township. There’s much more to see than the five locations we have chosen. The route will take you past some other places where you might like to stop and explore. 

The waypoints will need to be collected in sequential order. This is so that we can deliver coordinates for our “Bonus Box” (GC91G24) when you have visited the final waypoint.

So, take your time and enjoy the peace and beauty of this truly unique place.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2fb5af06-8794-4530-b285-d340badfc352" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Some of the town's landmarks are laid out in the shape of a cross with the cemetery at the top and the monastery at the bottom. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
