 <wpt lat="-32.78125" lon="117.499317">
  <ele>346.0</ele>
  <time>2020-12-09T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBgmKQ-01</name>
  <desc>WheatbeltMuseu1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/98bb97f2-6ba9-4cd3-b363-4a194e301275</url>
  <urlname>Wheatbelt Museums : S1 Wheatbelt Museums - Albert Facey's Homestead by burns345</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99000062" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Wheatbelt Museums : S1 Wheatbelt Museums - Albert Facey's Homestead</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>burns345</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">burns345</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Wheatbelt Museums&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Wheatbelt Museums - Albert Facey's Homestead&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/98bb97f2-6ba9-4cd3-b363-4a194e301275"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/98bb97f2-6ba9-4cd3-b363-4a194e301275&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the Surname of the Minister for Tourism who Officially opened the Albert Facey Homestead on 15 October 2000.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ed6079f7-3aef-4b33-9c84-fbd8a066967c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to Alberts Facey's Homestead. 

Albert Facey built this homestead on his farm at Norman's Lake in 1924.

Albert's homestead has been lovingly conserved and was relocated to this position in 2000 as testament to Albert's connection to to Shire of Wickepin's past.

The interior has been fitted out to reflect what life was like back in the early days.

Whilst here you can complete the 80 kilometre self drive Albert Facey Heritage Trail in and around the Wheatbelt town of Wickepin.

Take some time to explore the Albert Facey Homestead, and see where Facey spent much of his life, before travelling on to see the Wickepin Boarding House and the Wickepin Hotel.
Drive past the various farms where Facey worked including the Miekles, the Phillips, the Morans and the Bibbys farm. 

The trail also gives an insight into some of the general history of the area visiting Tarling Well, Tarling Hall and the Inkiepinkie School.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8d9e6215-e093-4b60-b38b-ca79e7ab1af1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the start of 5 wheatbelt museums around Kulin and surrounding Shires

You can do them in any order and whenever you are in the area. However you do not have to go into the museums to answer any of the questions. Check on the internet as to opening times as they may vary month to month. 

Volunteers play an important roll in keeping the museums open for the public to enjoy so respect what they are doing.

The museums are:-
Alberts Facey's homestead – Wickepin
Pioneer Museum – Corrigin
Butlers Museum – Kulin
Australiam Inland Mission Hospital Museum – Lake Grace
Bluebird Discovery Centre – Dumbleyung

Now start on your journey into some of Western Australias history in this area.

CONGRATULATIONS ebenie for being the first to complete this Adventure Lab.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations you have completed the Albert Facey's Homestead part of Adventure Lab Wheatbelt Museums.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
