   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Kellerberrin Heritage Trail II&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Kellerberrin Post Office&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c0adc565-c80b-43d6-9247-8373a2b7ec6e"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c0adc565-c80b-43d6-9247-8373a2b7ec6e&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year was Post Office built?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/aa9f9a78-baa8-4066-8ae0-70f737e8718a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Kellerberrin Post Office is a large two storey building of brick construction laid in a stretcher pattern. The place has a dutch gable tile roof with a separate semi-circular roof to the double storey entry porch, which is a dominant feature of the building. The entry porch is supported on Romanesque style white columns to both levels and bares the name of the building with the year of construction in black lettering.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d8907103-93bd-4f2e-a169-2556ad0bfef3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kellerberrin Heritage Trail II shows you rest of the POI all over town.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
