   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Lets get Arty&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Equinox &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Arty"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Arty&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the number on the bow of the ship named Bulwarra&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/eec775a8-5725-48b6-876f-7e9c6df7bfaa" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is a large mural surrounded by many smaller ones. The history of Busselton can yet again be seen in this mural . Another Jack Bromell piece. Painted in 2016 , this painting took 8weeks and over 60 paint pens to complete it is 28 metres long. It depics the intriguing  history of the Busselton jetty ,the longest wooden piled jetty in the Southern Hemisphere&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ebbf7a33-3277-4aa9-8ee0-d02b2d0335bd" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to Busselton learn about our town thru murals , the past and the present.
Cover mural by Sam Allen&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Hope you enjoyed finding all the little stories within this picture.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
