   <groundspeak:owner id="">Falcon351</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Lets not Forget&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Ocean views&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Notforget"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Notforget&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;In what year did Troy Buswell officially open the place of refection.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a950a5c7-6931-4f07-8633-768684d7bb0d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;THE CIRCLE OF LIFE is a memorial to Busselton community members who have died in tragedy 
Busselton is the only place who lost a member of our community in both  Bali bombings.
Busselton high school teacher Carol Johnson in 2002 bombing and
A student Bredan Fitzgerald 16 in another bombing in Bali in 2005
202 people lost their lives in the 2002 bombing.
Please take a seat and look out at the ocean ,depending on the day will depend on the emotions you will feel. Beautiful view.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9465ec12-45bd-49d8-b0a1-78eab4aa0fcb" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;My adventure is unique because it gives you time to reflect and give thanks for what we have today because of the sacrifice of our ancestors. This adventure will have you wandering thru cemetaries,a memorial and a cemotaph. Please be respectful of your surrounding.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done. You have complete a completed this adventure and seen some history of Busselton . Some old and some not so old . Congratulation. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-33.6463" lon="115.33995">
  <ele>8.0</ele>
  <time>2020-02-29T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LB8aBw-02</name>
  <desc>ByTheBayS2Circl</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ByTheBay</url>
  <urlname>By The Bay : S2 Circle of Life Memorial by pood</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-472" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>By The Bay : S2 Circle of Life Memorial</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>pood</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">pood</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;By The Bay&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Circle of Life Memorial&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ByTheBay"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ByTheBay&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many plaques are on the straight limestone blocks on the Eastern side of the short path?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0664f714-1b2f-4f49-a0fb-14ebe78952d1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The 'Circle of Life' is well known throughout the World, here parts of the Busselton Jetty have been recycled and incorporated to create a memorial monument overlooking the seas.

A committee set about the task to create the beautiful mosaic, encompassing the plaque of the World.
As a place of Reflection and Remembrance for the Busselton residents who have died in tragic circumstances.

To remember those lost in tragedy.
A place to reflect and remember.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/902ea194-af46-4e38-93cb-054668520576" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A Meander from the Iconic Busselton Jetty, along the scenic Foreshore, down through the Cultural Centre of town towards some Local Historical Buildings.

Geographe Bay was named in May 1801 by the French Explorer Nicolas Baudin, he named the Bay after his ship, the 'Geographe'.
Busselton was settled in the early 1830's by the Bussell family, George Layman and the Chapman Brothers.

This Adventure Lab can easily be completed within a day, however I would recommend you take your time and explore the area and take in some of Busselton's Cultural and Early Historical Locations. 

There are plenty of stories to read along the way, depicting the Early Farming Settlements, the Pioneers and their Livelihoods from the Pioneering Days.

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b7e8a9b1-37bc-483b-bcef-6959f00a34e7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-33.64735" lon="115.343667">
  <ele>6.0</ele>
  <time>2020-02-29T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LB8aBw-03</name>
  <desc>ByTheBayS3Busse</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ByTheBay</url>
  <urlname>By The Bay : S3 Busselton Settlement Art Project by pood</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-473" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>By The Bay : S3 Busselton Settlement Art Project</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>pood</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">pood</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;By The Bay&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Busselton Settlement Art Project&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ByTheBay"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ByTheBay&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the book John is reading?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3cebf094-7e38-4bb7-81eb-31d9a603850a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;At the Cultural and Heritage Complex, a community driven project celebrating the History of Busselton has been created.
This features six life sized bronze sculptures acknowledging the life of the Aboriginal people as the traditional owners of the land, through to the early pioneers and industries that established the area as a successful outpost from Perth.
Here is one of the sculptures, John Garret Bussell, born in Portsea Hampshire, England, on August 16th, 1803. 
Following his gratuation from Oxford, John and his brothers set sail for Western Australia in 1829.
With Governor Stirling's encouragement they made their way to take up land at August. The land proved difficult to clear and cultivate.
On April 14th, 1834, John and his brothers arrived in Geographe Bay from Augusta on the ship 'Ellen' to begin the new settlement.
In 1835 the fledgling settlement was named Busselton in recognition of the achievements of John Bussell and his brothers.
Hats off to John Bussell and the early Pioneers&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/902ea194-af46-4e38-93cb-054668520576" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A Meander from the Iconic Busselton Jetty, along the scenic Foreshore, down through the Cultural Centre of town towards some Local Historical Buildings.

Geographe Bay was named in May 1801 by the French Explorer Nicolas Baudin, he named the Bay after his ship, the 'Geographe'.
Busselton was settled in the early 1830's by the Bussell family, George Layman and the Chapman Brothers.

This Adventure Lab can easily be completed within a day, however I would recommend you take your time and explore the area and take in some of Busselton's Cultural and Early Historical Locations. 

There are plenty of stories to read along the way, depicting the Early Farming Settlements, the Pioneers and their Livelihoods from the Pioneering Days.

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/df52ad4e-dc84-4884-97b0-9adc7e57dada" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
