   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Lets get Arty&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Hello possum&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Arty"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Arty&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;In what year was the mural completed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/633631a9-2189-4ef8-887f-f36192626a63" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This mural was painted by Jerome Davenport this mural is painted on the side of the Geocatch building its titled Our Catchment in Colour ,it was commissioned by Geocatch and depicts the catchment area of Geographe bay. Look for the animals that are native to our area. The Ringtail possum is a threatened species it  only lives in the South west of Western Australia. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ebbf7a33-3277-4aa9-8ee0-d02b2d0335bd" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to Busselton learn about our town thru murals , the past and the present.
Cover mural by Sam Allen&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;What other animals did you find that are local to our area?&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
