  <desc>ByTheBayS5TheBu</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ByTheBay</url>
  <urlname>By The Bay : S5 The Butter Factory - Busselton Museum by pood</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-475" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>By The Bay : S5 The Butter Factory - Busselton Museum</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>pood</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">pood</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;By The Bay&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Butter Factory - Busselton Museum&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ByTheBay"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ByTheBay&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the location on the Telephone Exchange Building?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c3003751-dfaf-49ba-a231-2b83f49b0e96" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Heritage Butter Factory and Busselton Museum has ten display rooms packed with photographs, equipment and memorabillia which trace the family, social, civic, commercial and maritime history of Busselton.
Everything from agriculture to whaling, wedding dresses, kitchenware, musical, a blacksmith shed, travel and transport.
The one hectare site is situated on the grassy banks of the Vasse River with group settlement huts and a school building even with the old chalk and slate boards for your notes.
The Old Butter Factory was subject to fire in 2018, whilst not extensive, the upper floor has experienced a loss of fabric and artifacts.  
The City of Busselton has engaged Project Managers for the repairs to the affected areas.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/902ea194-af46-4e38-93cb-054668520576" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A Meander from the Iconic Busselton Jetty, along the scenic Foreshore, down through the Cultural Centre of town towards some Local Historical Buildings.

Geographe Bay was named in May 1801 by the French Explorer Nicolas Baudin, he named the Bay after his ship, the 'Geographe'.
Busselton was settled in the early 1830's by the Bussell family, George Layman and the Chapman Brothers.

This Adventure Lab can easily be completed within a day, however I would recommend you take your time and explore the area and take in some of Busselton's Cultural and Early Historical Locations. 

There are plenty of stories to read along the way, depicting the Early Farming Settlements, the Pioneers and their Livelihoods from the Pioneering Days.

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/426e5b61-efa2-4d18-9b1d-db168e7791b3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations on finding all the locations for the Adventure Lab 'By The Bay'.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
