   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Dunsborough Travels&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Walks and Falls&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/379e47bd-a4d6-483d-b017-abb87b4090a7"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/379e47bd-a4d6-483d-b017-abb87b4090a7&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the biggggest obstacle on your way back . Hint it was fun coming down it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d9c94fe6-f93d-4d66-a697-a68c82ed788b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This beautiful natural phenomena is culturally significant  to the Wadandi people . It is a ceremonial  place . Please be respectful of the boodja(country)
Please take your memories of their gnwirri booja ( beautiful country) and leave only djinnas (footprints) Please make sure you have sunscreen on and plenty of water. 
Parking can be had off Moses rock road&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1ce9e081-814b-4a64-be6a-1a5bc01f3a7c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is a unique adventure because it involves visiting locations that have outstanding beauty and includes places that have piqued our geocaching adventures&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f6f5053e-0fc9-43cc-9aa4-d0767bbd3dce" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;The views are amazing hope you enjoyed them well done.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
