 <wpt lat="-33.95725" lon="116.137433">
  <ele>157.0</ele>
  <time>2021-04-04T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBwmJk-01</name>
  <desc>BridgetownHeri1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/91d23bcf-074c-446a-9f3c-7db52232c85a</url>
  <urlname>Bridgetown Heritage Walk : S1 Old police station and goal by I C Nothing</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-466" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Bridgetown Heritage Walk : S1 Old police station and goal</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>I C Nothing</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">I C Nothing</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Bridgetown Heritage Walk&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Old police station and goal&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/91d23bcf-074c-446a-9f3c-7db52232c85a"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/91d23bcf-074c-446a-9f3c-7db52232c85a&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Commemoration of the restoration of the old police station and goal occurred on what date? (Write as per plaque)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c2b160d5-8c7a-47b5-8b02-9329c30351a0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The old goal was constructed in 1889 by James Gibbs with the police quarters being constructed in 1907.
The original building consisted of two cells, a storeroom, kitchen, exercise yard, office, two lobbies and two police living rooms. The goal was used until 10th April 1970.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b75b5e86-e468-46d3-adfd-677451772790" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to Bridgetown, I C Nothing’s second home located on the Blackwood River.
The town was surveyed in April 1868 by Thomas Carey who proposed the name Bridgetown for two reasons.
1. As it is at a bridge
2. Bridgetown was the first ship that transported wool from this district.

Bridgetown is a timber and agricultural  town producing sheep, cattle, dairy products, fruit , nuts and timber.

Bridgetown has many heritage buildings from when timber was in high demand during the building boom of 1890’s. This lab will take you on a walk to explore some of these heritage buildings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8e28e716-784e-4ccd-a284-2d86337da1db" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done, if you are completing the lab stage on Saturday take the time to have a look inside.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-33.95805" lon="116.1374">
