  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99001495" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Bridgetown Heritage Walk : S2 Town Hall</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>I C Nothing</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">I C Nothing</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Bridgetown Heritage Walk&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Town Hall&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/91d23bcf-074c-446a-9f3c-7db52232c85a"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/91d23bcf-074c-446a-9f3c-7db52232c85a&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year was the foundation stone laid in?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b7ea0284-7506-43c5-a145-e1e5f020c22d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Bridgetown Hall was constructed in 1936 but prior to this on this site was the Mechanics Institute built in 1877.
This was the site where locals would come to watch movies from 1904 to 1932. In 1932 the building was demolished to make way for the Town Hall Which continued screening movies until 1997.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b75b5e86-e468-46d3-adfd-677451772790" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to Bridgetown, I C Nothing’s second home located on the Blackwood River.
The town was surveyed in April 1868 by Thomas Carey who proposed the name Bridgetown for two reasons.
1. As it is at a bridge
2. Bridgetown was the first ship that transported wool from this district.

Bridgetown is a timber and agricultural  town producing sheep, cattle, dairy products, fruit , nuts and timber.

Bridgetown has many heritage buildings from when timber was in high demand during the building boom of 1890’s. This lab will take you on a walk to explore some of these heritage buildings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f08884af-b7df-4b23-bbe4-e19cfc38dcbc" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done on finishing stage 2. Why not continue walking down Main Street and explore the shops and local cafes whilst completing this lab.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-33.959217" lon="116.13695">
