  <urlname>Bridgetown Heritage Walk : S5 Blackwood Pharmacy by I C Nothing</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99001501" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Bridgetown Heritage Walk : S5 Blackwood Pharmacy</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>I C Nothing</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">I C Nothing</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Bridgetown Heritage Walk&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Blackwood Pharmacy&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/91d23bcf-074c-446a-9f3c-7db52232c85a"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/91d23bcf-074c-446a-9f3c-7db52232c85a&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year was this building constructed?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4d109a31-9eff-4323-8ff8-9b42adeda6d6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Blackwood Pharmacy was opened by Francis H Ick.
The building later became Capricorn Tearooms in the 1980’s with an addition put on the southern side of the building for a private residences.
Blackwood pharmacy is an example of a typical early nineteenth century shop with many original features still present.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b75b5e86-e468-46d3-adfd-677451772790" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to Bridgetown, I C Nothing’s second home located on the Blackwood River.
The town was surveyed in April 1868 by Thomas Carey who proposed the name Bridgetown for two reasons.
1. As it is at a bridge
2. Bridgetown was the first ship that transported wool from this district.

Bridgetown is a timber and agricultural  town producing sheep, cattle, dairy products, fruit , nuts and timber.

Bridgetown has many heritage buildings from when timber was in high demand during the building boom of 1890’s. This lab will take you on a walk to explore some of these heritage buildings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3c7bd186-5f56-4438-92ee-58624c4e517c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done on completing this stage, make sure you take the time discover the hidden treasures Bridgetown has to offer.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
