   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Bridgetown Heritage Walk&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;St Paul’s Anglican Church&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/91d23bcf-074c-446a-9f3c-7db52232c85a"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/91d23bcf-074c-446a-9f3c-7db52232c85a&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The church was constructed in ?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6be9525f-fe55-4a96-8b62-869db6989541" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;St Paul’s Anglican Church was constructed to replace an earlier timber church.
The church was built from local stone in a gothic federation design.
The church contains a range of ecclesiastical pieces in brass, copper and silver art made by local artist Herbert Augustus Gordon Holdsworth (1886 -1965).
The lynch gate and wall were constructed In 1920 with further additions added in 1950.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b75b5e86-e468-46d3-adfd-677451772790" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to Bridgetown, I C Nothing’s second home located on the Blackwood River.
The town was surveyed in April 1868 by Thomas Carey who proposed the name Bridgetown for two reasons.
1. As it is at a bridge
2. Bridgetown was the first ship that transported wool from this district.

Bridgetown is a timber and agricultural  town producing sheep, cattle, dairy products, fruit , nuts and timber.

Bridgetown has many heritage buildings from when timber was in high demand during the building boom of 1890’s. This lab will take you on a walk to explore some of these heritage buildings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/aed7d39e-0206-4e1e-ba60-1aaf90786a31" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations you have completed stage 4.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
