  <name>LBVT1c-01</name>
  <desc>CKS1KulinMemori</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Kulin</url>
  <urlname>Country Kulin : S1 Kulin Memorial Hall by burns345</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909871" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Country Kulin : S1 Kulin Memorial Hall</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>burns345</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">burns345</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Country Kulin&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Kulin Memorial Hall&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Kulin"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Kulin&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What was the builders surname?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/12fab4c1-a25d-41fa-9763-818644a98be0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kulin Memorial Hall, a single storey brick and iron building designed in the Inter-War Free Classical style, is of cultural heritage significance.
The foundation stone is dedicated to the First World War. 

The hall was the venue for many dances and social events in Kulin through the depression years and into the Second World War with wartime farewells and welcome homes, and the annual Anzac Day service. 
The Volunteer Air Defence Corps, formed in 1942, used the Gentleman's social rooms as an observation post. 
The hall was available for free rent to local fundraising bodies during the war. Many fundraising dances were held, as well as many balls such as the Debutante’s Ball and the Grand Ball, and school concerts..
Currently serves numerous community functions.
Since its construction in 1928, the place has been associated with a number of community organisations. The importance of the place is demonstrated by the efforts of the community, n&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3d18e99b-8568-4fc5-97bd-e30941c1da45" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
Welcome to Kulin which is located in the heart of the WA Wheatbelt
The town of Kulin developed after the railway connected from Narrogin in 1915.
100 years on and Kulin remains one of the most productive districts in the WA Wheatbelt.

The Kulin Region community prides itself on being progressive, proactive, safe and friendly. As a community, they have achieved some incredible things:
Their famous Kulin Bush Races are an award winning, 100% voluntarily coordinated and run event
They have the biggest Waterslide in Regional WA.
The Tin Horse Highway is recognised as the Wheatbelt’s most popular tourist drive.
The state-of-the-art Freebairn Recreation Centre is the hub of community life.
Kulin opened the very first Bendigo Community Bank Branch in WA. 
They were the first town to build a combined FESA and Emergency Services building.

There is a bonus cache at the end so don't forget to collect all the information from each Adventure Lab.
CONGRATULATIONS ebenie first to complete this Adventure Lab&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations and welcome to Kulin Memorial Hall.
Bonus Cache hint A = 4&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.669367" lon="118.155717">
