 <wpt lat="-32.667817" lon="118.157083">
  <ele>308.0</ele>
  <time>2020-12-09T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBgmKQ-03</name>
  <desc>WheatbeltMuseu3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/98bb97f2-6ba9-4cd3-b363-4a194e301275</url>
  <urlname>Wheatbelt Museums : S3 Wheatbelt Museums - Butlers Museum by burns345</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99000066" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Wheatbelt Museums : S3 Wheatbelt Museums - Butlers Museum</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>burns345</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">burns345</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Wheatbelt Museums&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Wheatbelt Museums - Butlers Museum&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/98bb97f2-6ba9-4cd3-b363-4a194e301275"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/98bb97f2-6ba9-4cd3-b363-4a194e301275&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year did the Butler's Garage open?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9be54ec4-a389-4119-b532-33bfeb3f6737" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Butlers Garage is a significant piece of Kulin’s Heritage, particularly that’s associated with the development of the agricultural industry and thus the identity of the region.
The architecture of the building is a fine example of construction during the Depression years. 

During the mid 1920's WM Butler &amp; Co of Wickepin established a machinery agency business in Kulin. 

In the late 1920's WH (Bill) Butler (WM's son) established in Kulin and took over the agency, developing it further with the construction of the garage on this site. 

The agencies functioned continuously right up until 1994. 

The garage has been restored and houses the Kulin Museum. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8d9e6215-e093-4b60-b38b-ca79e7ab1af1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the start of 5 wheatbelt museums around Kulin and surrounding Shires

You can do them in any order and whenever you are in the area. However you do not have to go into the museums to answer any of the questions. Check on the internet as to opening times as they may vary month to month. 

Volunteers play an important roll in keeping the museums open for the public to enjoy so respect what they are doing.

The museums are:-
Alberts Facey's homestead – Wickepin
Pioneer Museum – Corrigin
Butlers Museum – Kulin
Australiam Inland Mission Hospital Museum – Lake Grace
Bluebird Discovery Centre – Dumbleyung

Now start on your journey into some of Western Australias history in this area.

CONGRATULATIONS ebenie for being the first to complete this Adventure Lab.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c502684e-b9bb-439a-9919-60bbab30d9b3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations you have completed the Butlers Museum part of Adventure Lab Wheatbelt Museums&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.668517" lon="118.159117">
