  <urlname>Country Kulin : S4 Kulin Water Slide by burns345</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909877" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Country Kulin : S4 Kulin Water Slide</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>burns345</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">burns345</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Country Kulin&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Kulin Water Slide&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Kulin"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Kulin&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;In emergency dial ???&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6fec3317-6816-4de0-b49f-8f3035af2061" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Kulin Waterslide is the biggest in regional Western Australia  and is 182 metres long and 18 metres high, 

What a great place to stop during those hot summer months to fully refresh your family.

There’s plenty more to do at the redeveloped Kulin Aquatic Centre.

Note:

The Kulin Aquatic centre is opening 2nd November 2021 at the beginning of the season. The water slide is opening on the weekend of 6th and 7th November 2021.

Please check the Facebook page for opening times and any special events.

Kulin Aquatic Centre Facebook Page  - https://www.facebook.com/shireofkulin/
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3d18e99b-8568-4fc5-97bd-e30941c1da45" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
Welcome to Kulin which is located in the heart of the WA Wheatbelt
The town of Kulin developed after the railway connected from Narrogin in 1915.
100 years on and Kulin remains one of the most productive districts in the WA Wheatbelt.

The Kulin Region community prides itself on being progressive, proactive, safe and friendly. As a community, they have achieved some incredible things:
Their famous Kulin Bush Races are an award winning, 100% voluntarily coordinated and run event
They have the biggest Waterslide in Regional WA.
The Tin Horse Highway is recognised as the Wheatbelt’s most popular tourist drive.
The state-of-the-art Freebairn Recreation Centre is the hub of community life.
Kulin opened the very first Bendigo Community Bank Branch in WA. 
They were the first town to build a combined FESA and Emergency Services building.

There is a bonus cache at the end so don't forget to collect all the information from each Adventure Lab.
CONGRATULATIONS ebenie first to complete this Adventure Lab&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations and welcome to Kulin Water Slide which is open during summer months.
Bonus cache hint is  D = 8&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.669067" lon="118.160217">
  <ele>309.0</ele>
  <time>2020-10-29T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBVT1c-05</name>
  <desc>CKS5TinHorseHig</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Kulin</url>
  <urlname>Country Kulin : S5 Tin Horse Highway by burns345</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909879" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Country Kulin : S5 Tin Horse Highway</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>burns345</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">burns345</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Country Kulin&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Tin Horse Highway&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Kulin"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Kulin&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What should you do carefully?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/29854709-1f18-4a63-b792-55361d842488" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Tin Horse Highway stretches from Kulin to Jilakin Rock where on the first weekend of October the Kulin Bush Races are held.
A must see as the locals keep them updated and maintained with many new additions being added each year.
They are made out of scrap recycled materials from the farms.
This is a country road used by heavy trucks and can be busy at times so be careful and keep a look out for your kids so they don't wander onto the road.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3d18e99b-8568-4fc5-97bd-e30941c1da45" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
Welcome to Kulin which is located in the heart of the WA Wheatbelt
The town of Kulin developed after the railway connected from Narrogin in 1915.
100 years on and Kulin remains one of the most productive districts in the WA Wheatbelt.

The Kulin Region community prides itself on being progressive, proactive, safe and friendly. As a community, they have achieved some incredible things:
Their famous Kulin Bush Races are an award winning, 100% voluntarily coordinated and run event
They have the biggest Waterslide in Regional WA.
The Tin Horse Highway is recognised as the Wheatbelt’s most popular tourist drive.
The state-of-the-art Freebairn Recreation Centre is the hub of community life.
Kulin opened the very first Bendigo Community Bank Branch in WA. 
They were the first town to build a combined FESA and Emergency Services building.

There is a bonus cache at the end so don't forget to collect all the information from each Adventure Lab.
CONGRATULATIONS ebenie first to complete this Adventure Lab&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations and welcome to the Start of Tin Horse Highway - enjoy the next 10 kms.
Bonus cache hint is  E = 6&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
