   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Merredin&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Railway Dam&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d96b4b9c-0cc2-4033-8a39-641e7d60871b"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d96b4b9c-0cc2-4033-8a39-641e7d60871b&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year was the Rocky Start Map dated by Albert Calvert? (use digits)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1a168fef-223a-4017-bf05-8bb2eb27d88b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Originally this Dam was built to store water run off from the rock for the steam trains. It is now a favourite picnic spot surrounded by the sound of birds, tall trees and wild flowers (during season) The Peak (Rock) is also a nice walk. Legend has it there is a giant Carp living in the dam - Ive never seen it myself - let me know if you do!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3abdc620-6d7d-4535-914b-0d3179db3fb4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to Merredin 'The Heart of The Wheatbelt'. Place of my birth and childhood memories. I hope you enjoy a small insight to the place I call home.

 The town’s name is derived from the Aboriginal word “merrit-in” the place of the merrit tree, a eucalypt used to make spears.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/fddf6bf5-da99-4c07-b6a2-fb5db7113c4b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
