  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-7" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Merredin : S2 Millitary Hospital</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>geotrakka</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">geotrakka</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Merredin&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Millitary Hospital&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d96b4b9c-0cc2-4033-8a39-641e7d60871b"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d96b4b9c-0cc2-4033-8a39-641e7d60871b&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What was this exact area of the ruins used as during World War ll?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a4f36b75-9cb3-4ef8-947e-002c22980992" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This military hospital was built in 1942. Patients were transported to Merredin by special ambulance trains. Merredin was located well inland making it a less likely bombing target. It was a rail junction which meant that casualties could arrive from various directions and it had an independent water supply in the form of the railway dam which would allow it to continue operating even if the enemy destroyed the Goldfields Water Supply pipeline. Water from the railway dam was pumped to a tank at the top of Merredin Peak from where it gravitated down to the hospital. 
You can either walk or drive around the well sign posted track to learn more about the ruins.
Near here is where the original land owners Njakinjaki (Nyaki Nyaki Noongar) camped in the bushland. Some of my childhood friends had Grandparents and Great Grandparents who would talk about their time here. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3abdc620-6d7d-4535-914b-0d3179db3fb4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to Merredin 'The Heart of The Wheatbelt'. Place of my birth and childhood memories. I hope you enjoy a small insight to the place I call home.

 The town’s name is derived from the Aboriginal word “merrit-in” the place of the merrit tree, a eucalypt used to make spears.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/092c158e-0791-4e85-b3d9-cc662df6427c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-33.102117" lon="118.452417">
  <ele>290.0</ele>
  <time>2020-12-09T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBgmKQ-04</name>
  <desc>WheatbeltMuseu4</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/98bb97f2-6ba9-4cd3-b363-4a194e301275</url>
  <urlname>Wheatbelt Museums : S4 Wheatbelt Museums -  AIM Hospital Museum by burns345</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99000068" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Wheatbelt Museums : S4 Wheatbelt Museums -  AIM Hospital Museum</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>burns345</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">burns345</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Wheatbelt Museums&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Wheatbelt Museums -  AIM Hospital Museum&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/98bb97f2-6ba9-4cd3-b363-4a194e301275"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/98bb97f2-6ba9-4cd3-b363-4a194e301275&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many pickets on front gate?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/edda50ee-4c15-431b-a356-5727a62eb51f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Australiam Inland Mission Hospital Museum . 

Originally opened in 1926 however ceased operation as a hospital in 1952.

It was then used as nurses quartes and storeroom for the new hospital until 1984.

Restoration then followed until 1992 when it was opened as Inland Mission Hospital Museum (Heritage Listed)

The Lake Grace Australian Inland Mission hospital was the only one in Western Australia and one of only three remaining in Australia.

Visitors are able to experience this early twentieth century rural hospital that, in its time, serviced approximately 16,000 km2.

The Lake Grace Aim Hospital Museum contains the old-style wards, duty room, kitchen and laundry.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8d9e6215-e093-4b60-b38b-ca79e7ab1af1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the start of 5 wheatbelt museums around Kulin and surrounding Shires

You can do them in any order and whenever you are in the area. However you do not have to go into the museums to answer any of the questions. Check on the internet as to opening times as they may vary month to month. 

Volunteers play an important roll in keeping the museums open for the public to enjoy so respect what they are doing.

The museums are:-
Alberts Facey's homestead – Wickepin
Pioneer Museum – Corrigin
Butlers Museum – Kulin
Australiam Inland Mission Hospital Museum – Lake Grace
Bluebird Discovery Centre – Dumbleyung

Now start on your journey into some of Western Australias history in this area.

CONGRATULATIONS ebenie for being the first to complete this Adventure Lab.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/57c7d908-1631-4f1a-bfaf-e8444de8c36c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations you have completed the Australian Inland Mission Hospital Museum part of Adventure Lab Wheatbelt Museums&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-34.32445" lon="115.1684">
