 <wpt lat="-34.3688" lon="115.135533">
  <ele>6.0</ele>
  <time>2021-01-02T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBV6eq-04</name>
  <desc>MeanderThruThe4</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/337f3b26-6e4a-43ce-8fa9-ced5bb30a17b</url>
  <urlname>Meander thru the ages : S4 Stone wheel by ringtailposs</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-499" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Meander thru the ages : S4 Stone wheel</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>ringtailposs</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">ringtailposs</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Meander thru the ages&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Stone wheel&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/337f3b26-6e4a-43ce-8fa9-ced5bb30a17b"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/337f3b26-6e4a-43ce-8fa9-ced5bb30a17b&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the wheel encrusted in?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/787cd55e-412d-42c9-9df3-430b3bee7ba8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This wheel was built in 1895. It was to bring water to the lighthouse for the builders and then later the keepers cottages. The wheel delivered about a litre of water for evert stroke of the pump that was activated by the wheel spinning. The water came from a spring in the wetland. This wheel has been like this since i was a kid and over the years has slowly but surely become more and more encrusted.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8ee60e45-60cf-4613-8de0-fa9bb99ee003" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;I have started this lab in an area that there are no others and to emphasis the uniqueness of the Southwest. From old to new and tourist places to points of interest that we found intriguing. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/982cf7d9-775e-4475-b836-b28da30a3daa" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done now before leaving the area you may like to wander a bit further up the road and have a look at the Augusta Lighthouse &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-34.686367" lon="117.931417">
  <ele>296.0</ele>
  <time>2021-02-04T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBiEoA-01</name>
  <desc>LCastleRockAdv1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/pipeline</url>
  <urlname>[L] Castle Rock Adventure : S1 Castle Rock Day Use Area by jasenjanine</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909991" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] Castle Rock Adventure : S1 Castle Rock Day Use Area</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>jasenjanine</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">jasenjanine</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Castle Rock Adventure&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Castle Rock Day Use Area&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/pipeline"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/pipeline&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the bird on the "Scuplting the Porongurups" sign?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7c719b1d-07a3-46d9-aa06-154c77695feb" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Granite Skywalk day-use area is a easily accessed by a 2WD car and has plenty of sealed parking bays. There are numerous sheltered picnic tables, barbeques, toilets and is partially accessible for people with disabilities. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/00614976-5195-4ffd-bade-1a0ce855a2b4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The massive ancient granite domes of Porongurup National Park rise 670 metres, giving exhilarating views of the landscape, especially from the Granite Skywalk suspended from Castle Rock.

A marvel of engineering, the two lookouts give spectacular views across the park and undulating farmland to Albany on the south coast, Mt Gardner and Mt Manypeaks to the south-east and the Stirling Range to the north.

The two kilometre walk up from the Castle Rock picnic area passes through jarrah, marri and karri forest and by Balancing Rock to reach the base of Castle Rock and the lower lookout. Reaching the upper lookout requires scrambling through and over rocks and climbing a 7 metre ladder. 

** You will need a reasonable amount of fitness (and an aptitude for heights), to be able to complete this Adventure Lab.

We hope you enjoy :)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1d42563e-d489-4f10-902a-a470d2ea909d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well Done!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
