 <wpt lat="-28.902633" lon="114.892833">
  <ele>210.0</ele>
  <time>2019-04-06T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBdqJo-09</name>
  <desc>GreatWestOzRo09</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/WOZ2019</url>
  <urlname>The Great West Oz Road Trip : S09 Geraldton by West Oz Geocaching</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-199" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>The Great West Oz Road Trip : S09 Geraldton</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>West Oz Geocaching</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">West Oz Geocaching</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;The Great West Oz Road Trip&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Geraldton&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/WOZ2019"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/WOZ2019&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the date of the opening? (Enter it as it appears on the plaque.)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c89a9ec5-2f91-401c-8296-1ea79e8e87ea" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;414.6km by road from Perth

The largest city in Western Australia north of Perth. The city is located on Champion Bay, discovered by Commander D Dring in the colonial schooner "Champion" in January 1840. The bay was named by the Royal Navy hydrographic surveyor, J L Stokes, who surveyed it later in 1840.

The Geraldton area was first explored by George Grey in 1839. In 1848 copper and lead were discovered on the Murchison River. The first exports of ore from the Murchison mines was made from Champion Bay in 1849, and soon after in 1850 surveyor Augustus Gregory was instructed to survey a townsite at this place. 

On June 3 1851 the townsite of Geraldton was declared. The name was most probably given by Surveyor-General J.S. Roe, and honours the colony's Governor at that time, Captain Charles Fitzgerald.

Nearby to the city is the Mumbida Wind Farm.  Find the plaque dedicated to the opening of the wind farm.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/02bfc544-156d-4cad-a499-2bcc61ab7736" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the West Oz Geocaching Road Trip adventure taking you to some interesting locations in Western Australia.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-35.026633" lon="117.875317">
  <ele>26.0</ele>
  <time>2020-12-01T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBn83k-05</name>
  <desc>LALBANYAWalkTh5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7f45afac-7547-410b-9415-d06f2bccd73b</url>
  <urlname>[L] ALBANY  -  'A Walk Through Time' : S5 Vancouver Cottage Hospital by allinaday</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909805" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] ALBANY  -  'A Walk Through Time' : S5 Vancouver Cottage Hospital</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>allinaday</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">allinaday</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;ALBANY  -  'A Walk Through Time'&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Vancouver Cottage Hospital&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7f45afac-7547-410b-9415-d06f2bccd73b"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7f45afac-7547-410b-9415-d06f2bccd73b&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;This mosaic is one of ? regional artworks placed throughout Western Australia (Numeral)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/14360acc-ef56-4008-b6aa-b300d7da7d7f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Albany Cottage Hospital is the heritage site of a former hospital in Albany. 
The buildings and grounds are situated on a site that overlooks the Princess Royal Harbour. The main building is constructed from local limestone, with a roof of split jarrah shingles. The hospital was completed in 1897, from the 1886 design of George Temple-Poole, and continued to operate until 1962. 
The site is also named the Vancouver Arts Centre Group for its later use as a community arts centre.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9c50156b-3164-4347-857c-cc54aa19afa1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Albany is the oldest colonial settlement in Western Australia.

It was founded on the 26th of December 1826 as a military outpost of New South Wales.

There are a number of Heritage buildings in Albany, and this Adventure will take you to just  few of these buildings, which are beautifully preserved. 
There are many more old buildings around our pretty town, so if you have some time, wander around, soak in the history and ponder life from a bygone era.

A bonus cache has been placed.  You will find the co-ordinates for this cache after the last journal entry.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/602f8f5a-240a-4b3d-aea6-a0d2a6d76150" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;You can find the bonus cache at: 

                              S35 01. 603
                              E117 52.467&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-35.023683" lon="117.883567">
  <ele>26.0</ele>
  <time>2020-12-01T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBn83k-01</name>
  <desc>LALBANYAWalkTh1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7f45afac-7547-410b-9415-d06f2bccd73b</url>
  <urlname>[L] ALBANY  -  'A Walk Through Time' : S1 Town Hall by allinaday</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-432" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] ALBANY  -  'A Walk Through Time' : S1 Town Hall</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>allinaday</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">allinaday</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;ALBANY  -  'A Walk Through Time'&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Town Hall&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7f45afac-7547-410b-9415-d06f2bccd73b"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7f45afac-7547-410b-9415-d06f2bccd73b&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Where was Lancel Victor de Hamel born and what year?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d5e5abaa-6c7a-43ce-8346-3b2038c4d738" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Completed in 1888, the Town hall is constructed of locally quarried granite, finished with stucco ornamentation.
Originally the building housed municipal and commercial offices on the ground floor with the public hall on the first floor. The hall provided a venue for cultural and community events such as theatre, cinema, meetings and dances.

The building was listed on the State Register of Heritage Places in 1996.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9c50156b-3164-4347-857c-cc54aa19afa1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Albany is the oldest colonial settlement in Western Australia.

It was founded on the 26th of December 1826 as a military outpost of New South Wales.

There are a number of Heritage buildings in Albany, and this Adventure will take you to just  few of these buildings, which are beautifully preserved. 
There are many more old buildings around our pretty town, so if you have some time, wander around, soak in the history and ponder life from a bygone era.

A bonus cache has been placed.  You will find the co-ordinates for this cache after the last journal entry.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/19243750-b793-4a6d-8466-32e509bf205b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-35.02555" lon="117.8835">
  <ele>20.0</ele>
