  <name>LBn83k-02</name>
  <desc>LALBANYAWalkTh2</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7f45afac-7547-410b-9415-d06f2bccd73b</url>
  <urlname>[L] ALBANY  -  'A Walk Through Time' : S2 St John's Church by allinaday</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909799" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] ALBANY  -  'A Walk Through Time' : S2 St John's Church</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>allinaday</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">allinaday</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;ALBANY  -  'A Walk Through Time'&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;St John's Church&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7f45afac-7547-410b-9415-d06f2bccd73b"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7f45afac-7547-410b-9415-d06f2bccd73b&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Who is the altar window dedicated to?  (Use I as in EYE in your numeral answer)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7f69cedd-25a3-4490-8f07-f726fcce5b18" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The church, completed in 1844,  is a stone building with gabled roofs covered in shingles. The aisle of the church is made from 22-centimetre (9 in) thick blocks that had been made in England. The stone walls are 540 millimeters (21 in) thick and the building also has stone foundations; the stone was thought to be quarried from nearby Mount Melville and Mount Clarence. The walls are so thick that no buttresses are required. The original building is now the nave of the present church, with the gallery behind built in 1852. The tower and porch were completed in 1853. The tower is topped with battlements on the parapet.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9c50156b-3164-4347-857c-cc54aa19afa1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Albany is the oldest colonial settlement in Western Australia.

It was founded on the 26th of December 1826 as a military outpost of New South Wales.

There are a number of Heritage buildings in Albany, and this Adventure will take you to just  few of these buildings, which are beautifully preserved. 
There are many more old buildings around our pretty town, so if you have some time, wander around, soak in the history and ponder life from a bygone era.

A bonus cache has been placed.  You will find the co-ordinates for this cache after the last journal entry.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/de41d976-3503-4b74-afd0-d2cfde494bbc" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-35.026883" lon="117.880817">
  <ele>13.0</ele>
