  <desc>LALBANYAWalkTh4</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7f45afac-7547-410b-9415-d06f2bccd73b</url>
  <urlname>[L] ALBANY  -  'A Walk Through Time' : S4 Patrick Taylor Cottage by allinaday</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909803" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] ALBANY  -  'A Walk Through Time' : S4 Patrick Taylor Cottage</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>allinaday</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">allinaday</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;ALBANY  -  'A Walk Through Time'&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Patrick Taylor Cottage&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7f45afac-7547-410b-9415-d06f2bccd73b"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7f45afac-7547-410b-9415-d06f2bccd73b&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Name the three British mariners etched on this monument.  (Last names only,  in clockwise direction)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/cd63dc21-1d2a-4e61-b239-a0a835c92f30" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Patrick Taylor Cottage is the oldest surviving dwelling in Western Australia.

The Building was constructed by the Morley brothers in 1832.  John Lawrence Morley had served as a former sailor with the East India Company and was one of the first settlers in the area.  The cottage was originally set on a 240 acre block. The building was sold to Patrick Taylor in 1835 by the Morleys, on a much smaller block.  It stayed in the Taylor family until the 1950's.

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9c50156b-3164-4347-857c-cc54aa19afa1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Albany is the oldest colonial settlement in Western Australia.

It was founded on the 26th of December 1826 as a military outpost of New South Wales.

There are a number of Heritage buildings in Albany, and this Adventure will take you to just  few of these buildings, which are beautifully preserved. 
There are many more old buildings around our pretty town, so if you have some time, wander around, soak in the history and ponder life from a bygone era.

A bonus cache has been placed.  You will find the co-ordinates for this cache after the last journal entry.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
