   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Great Southern Museum Precinct&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Amity&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ba0492be-c901-4482-b9b5-a6099405f5d7"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ba0492be-c901-4482-b9b5-a6099405f5d7&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;There is a plaque on a piece of granite, what is the four letter word before "of Albany"&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/075d03d3-13e8-436a-aefd-35a83a9b4d9a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The ship on display here is a replica of the Brig Amity, which brought the first European settlers to the West Coast of Australia&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ff8b4c43-765a-4a44-88fb-4d991c3f1415" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Great Southern Museum Precinct, a group of closely located Albany landmarks and a location that is often driven past and admired, but not so often visited.

These locations are all in very close proximity and can be done in any order.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
