  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ba0492be-c901-4482-b9b5-a6099405f5d7</url>
  <urlname>Great Southern Museum Precinct : S5 Albany Residency Museum by Barnzy12</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476919036" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Great Southern Museum Precinct : S5 Albany Residency Museum</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Barnzy12</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Barnzy12</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Great Southern Museum Precinct&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Albany Residency Museum&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ba0492be-c901-4482-b9b5-a6099405f5d7"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ba0492be-c901-4482-b9b5-a6099405f5d7&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;There is a small plaque on the wall "The Albany Residency Museum", what is the last name of the Architect?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9119f901-7730-41ef-af08-81671f181383" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Residency Museum was originally built in 1850 as a store and office for the nearby convict-hiring depot. In 1872 when the depot closed, more rooms were added.  From 1873 to 1953 it was the centre of the town’s social events, when it became home to the local government administrator, known as the Government Resident and later the Resident Magistrate (thus becoming known as ‘The Residency’)

After renovations, the building re-opened in 1975 as The Albany Residency Museum, the first branch of the WA Museum outside the metropolitan area.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ff8b4c43-765a-4a44-88fb-4d991c3f1415" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Great Southern Museum Precinct, a group of closely located Albany landmarks and a location that is often driven past and admired, but not so often visited.

These locations are all in very close proximity and can be done in any order.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
