   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Great Southern Museum Precinct&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;British Settlement on the West Coast&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ba0492be-c901-4482-b9b5-a6099405f5d7"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ba0492be-c901-4482-b9b5-a6099405f5d7&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year was the monument erected?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b459cbe8-2772-4295-bf9e-b8eeb0be99a9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The monument at this location recognises the First British Settlement on the Western side of Australia by Major Edmund Lockyer who landed here from the Brig Amity on 26th December 1826.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ff8b4c43-765a-4a44-88fb-4d991c3f1415" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Great Southern Museum Precinct, a group of closely located Albany landmarks and a location that is often driven past and admired, but not so often visited.

These locations are all in very close proximity and can be done in any order.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
