 <wpt lat="-35.029167" lon="117.880633">
  <ele>7.0</ele>
  <time>2021-05-29T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBcZyG-02</name>
  <desc>GreatSouthernM2</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ba0492be-c901-4482-b9b5-a6099405f5d7</url>
  <urlname>Great Southern Museum Precinct : S2 Group Settlement by Barnzy12</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476915747" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Great Southern Museum Precinct : S2 Group Settlement</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Barnzy12</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Barnzy12</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Great Southern Museum Precinct&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Group Settlement&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ba0492be-c901-4482-b9b5-a6099405f5d7"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ba0492be-c901-4482-b9b5-a6099405f5d7&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;According to the "Group Settlement and Beyond sign", many migrants landed in Albany en route to land allocations between Manjimup and ......&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/503568ec-3220-4b77-88b4-db10413d86bc" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;To help speed up Albanys growth which had been slowed by the Great War, Premier Sir James Mitchell proposed the Group Settlements Scheme in the 1920's. The scheme allowed an allocation of land to groups of 20-30 families.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ff8b4c43-765a-4a44-88fb-4d991c3f1415" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Great Southern Museum Precinct, a group of closely located Albany landmarks and a location that is often driven past and admired, but not so often visited.

These locations are all in very close proximity and can be done in any order.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-35.029883" lon="117.881367">
  <ele>6.0</ele>
  <time>2020-05-21T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBvKeK-01</name>
  <desc>LANZACS1PierOfR</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/AAH</url>
  <urlname>[L] Albany ANZAC History : S1 Pier of Remembrance by allinaday</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99001513" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] Albany ANZAC History : S1 Pier of Remembrance</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>allinaday</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">allinaday</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Albany ANZAC History&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Pier of Remembrance&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/AAH"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/AAH&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the ship on the plaque in front of you?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e8e4efe8-f3e0-4f51-98dd-2d84ba86721d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Peace Park was opened in 2010 and it is designed to commemorate the departure to the war front of soldiers who served in the Australian and New Zealand Army Corps (ANZAC) during WW1.

The features of the park include: a memorial wall, pier of remembrance, interpretive signage, lighting, landscaping, pathways and seating.  
A small area of the garden has been planted with Aleppo Pines, the same tree as found on Lone Pine Ridge in Gallipoli, providing a living connection between Albany and Gallipoli.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/380447a7-65e2-438a-a9e2-a791f67c8161" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;On the 1st of November 1914, Albany was the final departure point for the first and second convoys of ANZAC troops on their way to the battlefields of the First World War.  For many, Albany was the last image Australian soldiers had of their homeland.
Most thought they were on a great adventure.  Instead, they were fighting a conflict that many would not return from.
This Adventure will take you to a number of locations around our beautiful city which pay tribute to those who fought for our freedom. 'As the sun rises and goes down, we will remember them'.  Take your time to enjoy and explore the various locations you will visit.  This can take anything from a few hours to a day.

At each location, there will be a clue once you answer the question. The 5 letters (one in each answer will reveal a key word that you will require for a bonus mystery cache.

Please Note:  No full stops are required when you enter your answers.


&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-35.027467" lon="117.887133">
  <ele>14.0</ele>
  <time>2020-12-01T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBn83k-03</name>
  <desc>LALBANYAWalkTh3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7f45afac-7547-410b-9415-d06f2bccd73b</url>
  <urlname>[L] ALBANY  -  'A Walk Through Time' : S3 The Old Post Office by allinaday</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909801" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] ALBANY  -  'A Walk Through Time' : S3 The Old Post Office</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>allinaday</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">allinaday</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;ALBANY  -  'A Walk Through Time'&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Old Post Office&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7f45afac-7547-410b-9415-d06f2bccd73b"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7f45afac-7547-410b-9415-d06f2bccd73b&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;On what date was the message received in Perth following completion of the telegraph line?  (Dont add the 'th')&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/14cf27c4-a910-44fe-adfe-34a3ebbe5f16" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Built in two stages between 1869 and 1895, The Old Post Office has cultural heritage significance.  It was the base station of the intercolonial telegraph of 1875, linking Western Australia with Adelaide, thence with the rest of the world. It is one of Albany's most interesting buildings architecturally and historically. It was originally used as customs house, post office, telegraph office, sometimes for local government meetings, theatrical performances, debates, lectures, concerts, socials and even church services. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9c50156b-3164-4347-857c-cc54aa19afa1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Albany is the oldest colonial settlement in Western Australia.

It was founded on the 26th of December 1826 as a military outpost of New South Wales.

There are a number of Heritage buildings in Albany, and this Adventure will take you to just  few of these buildings, which are beautifully preserved. 
There are many more old buildings around our pretty town, so if you have some time, wander around, soak in the history and ponder life from a bygone era.

A bonus cache has been placed.  You will find the co-ordinates for this cache after the last journal entry.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ca65437e-4249-49e0-8df1-14abfbbd7cbd" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
