  <desc>LANZACS3DesertM</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/AAH</url>
  <urlname>[L] Albany ANZAC History : S3 Desert Mounted Corps Memorial by allinaday</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99001517" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] Albany ANZAC History : S3 Desert Mounted Corps Memorial</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>allinaday</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">allinaday</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Albany ANZAC History&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Desert Mounted Corps Memorial&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/AAH"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/AAH&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What Regiment is this seat dedicated to?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8ad4deb3-ea74-41d6-a6ee-87e27578468a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The ANZAC Desert Mounted Corps Memorial is a duplicate of the original statue erected in Suez in the 1930's.  The original was irreparably damaged during the Suez crisis in 1956.  The masonry was salvaged and brought to Australia for re-erection on this site which for many troops who sailed from King George Sound in 1914 was their last glimpse of Australian soil.
The walk to the summit, lined with native bushland and memorials, begins at the carpark.
Behind the memorial, you will find the Padre White Lookout.  This is dedicated to the Albany priest credited with introducing the dawn service tradition to Australia.
You will need to locate a granite bench to answer the question. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/380447a7-65e2-438a-a9e2-a791f67c8161" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;On the 1st of November 1914, Albany was the final departure point for the first and second convoys of ANZAC troops on their way to the battlefields of the First World War.  For many, Albany was the last image Australian soldiers had of their homeland.
Most thought they were on a great adventure.  Instead, they were fighting a conflict that many would not return from.
This Adventure will take you to a number of locations around our beautiful city which pay tribute to those who fought for our freedom. 'As the sun rises and goes down, we will remember them'.  Take your time to enjoy and explore the various locations you will visit.  This can take anything from a few hours to a day.

At each location, there will be a clue once you answer the question. The 5 letters (one in each answer will reveal a key word that you will require for a bonus mystery cache.

Please Note:  No full stops are required when you enter your answers.


&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Z&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
