  <desc>LANZACS2AvenueO</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/AAH</url>
  <urlname>[L] Albany ANZAC History : S2 Avenue Of Honour by allinaday</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99001515" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] Albany ANZAC History : S2 Avenue Of Honour</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>allinaday</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">allinaday</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Albany ANZAC History&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Avenue Of Honour&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/AAH"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/AAH&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Name of person this tree is dedicated to, starting with rank.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ac982742-0dbb-457c-8255-c074fea077d0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Avenue of Honour was planted in 1955 - 1956 and replaced the original avenue planted along Middleton Road.  It honours those who died in service or were killed in action in WW1, WW2 and the Korean War.
The trees are Swamp Mahogany and each tree has a plaque dedicated to a service person.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/380447a7-65e2-438a-a9e2-a791f67c8161" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;On the 1st of November 1914, Albany was the final departure point for the first and second convoys of ANZAC troops on their way to the battlefields of the First World War.  For many, Albany was the last image Australian soldiers had of their homeland.
Most thought they were on a great adventure.  Instead, they were fighting a conflict that many would not return from.
This Adventure will take you to a number of locations around our beautiful city which pay tribute to those who fought for our freedom. 'As the sun rises and goes down, we will remember them'.  Take your time to enjoy and explore the various locations you will visit.  This can take anything from a few hours to a day.

At each location, there will be a clue once you answer the question. The 5 letters (one in each answer will reveal a key word that you will require for a bonus mystery cache.

Please Note:  No full stops are required when you enter your answers.


&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;N&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
