   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Coastal Defences&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Historic Survey Marker&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/dda786c5-f9e5-4cec-823d-fcd84f0279d7"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/dda786c5-f9e5-4cec-823d-fcd84f0279d7&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the four digit number in the small circle?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2fec54f6-f56c-4dcd-b418-198a5bfd651f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This historic survey marker was established by the Institution of Engineering and Mining Surveyors Australia to locate the point determined by Major F Rainsford Hannay for John Blackbourn to set out the Princess Royal Battery. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f48495ea-03a7-4c1c-a082-8e2dd40aa4a2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;During the nineteenth century, the loss of the strategic port of Albany to any enemy squadron was recognised as a potential threat to the security of Australia. 

All of the Australian colonies agreed to pay for a fort with the Imperial British Government to supply the funs. The fort was opened in 1893, the first federal  defence Australia - known today as Princess Royal Fortress.

This adventure lab will take you to some of these coastal defences.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;well done&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-35.02995" lon="117.914833">
