   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Coastal Defences&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Underground Magazine&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/dda786c5-f9e5-4cec-823d-fcd84f0279d7"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/dda786c5-f9e5-4cec-823d-fcd84f0279d7&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;According to the plaque, how many shells could the magazine store?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/af938f73-9779-4c49-8c0e-7d7d70aa8af1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This two chambered concrete magazine was built in 1893 and shells and cartridges. The original storage rooms were surrounded by a lamp chamber comprised of lamp enclosures covered with thick glass protected by wire. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f48495ea-03a7-4c1c-a082-8e2dd40aa4a2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;During the nineteenth century, the loss of the strategic port of Albany to any enemy squadron was recognised as a potential threat to the security of Australia. 

All of the Australian colonies agreed to pay for a fort with the Imperial British Government to supply the funs. The fort was opened in 1893, the first federal  defence Australia - known today as Princess Royal Fortress.

This adventure lab will take you to some of these coastal defences.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;well done&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
