  <desc>CoastalDefence3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/dda786c5-f9e5-4cec-823d-fcd84f0279d7</url>
  <urlname>Coastal Defences : S3 Gun Fortifications by WebblyWA</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99001507" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Coastal Defences : S3 Gun Fortifications</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>WebblyWA</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">WebblyWA</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Coastal Defences&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Gun Fortifications&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/dda786c5-f9e5-4cec-823d-fcd84f0279d7"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/dda786c5-f9e5-4cec-823d-fcd84f0279d7&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;You will find an info board in the trenches. when the guns were test fired, what effective range did they demonstrate (yards - no commas) &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a5e4e51d-d383-445d-a22e-966c3d65bc7b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The two gun emplacements on the upper Fortress were positioned to provide maximum protection to the entrance of Princess Royal Harbour.

Construction of the emplacements was completed in February 1893. The guns were eventually replaced in 1938 and again in 1945 and were abandoned in 1956.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f48495ea-03a7-4c1c-a082-8e2dd40aa4a2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;During the nineteenth century, the loss of the strategic port of Albany to any enemy squadron was recognised as a potential threat to the security of Australia. 

All of the Australian colonies agreed to pay for a fort with the Imperial British Government to supply the funs. The fort was opened in 1893, the first federal  defence Australia - known today as Princess Royal Fortress.

This adventure lab will take you to some of these coastal defences.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;well done&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-35.031183" lon="117.9129">
