 <wpt lat="-28.782617" lon="114.579267">
  <ele>8.0</ele>
  <time>2020-12-22T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBF71d-04</name>
  <desc>CoastalLightin4</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/CLWA</url>
  <urlname>Coastal Lighting WA  : S4 Point Moore Lighthouse by parkacruz</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99000010" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Coastal Lighting WA  : S4 Point Moore Lighthouse</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>parkacruz</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">parkacruz</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Coastal Lighting WA &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Point Moore Lighthouse&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/CLWA"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/CLWA&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Who was the light keeper in c.1886?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d4c04049-04d0-400b-90f7-d597a93c58ef" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Moore Point Lighthouse was the first all steel tower built on the mainland of Australia.
It is also the oldest surviving Western Australia lighthouse under Federal control. The foundation were originally laid for the Moore Point Lighthouse in 1877, but were found to be in the wrong place. Following this discovery they were relocated to the current site 5 kilometres from the centre of Geraldton. The tower was a prefabricated steel tower by Chance Bros. of Birmingham, and brought to Australia in segments from England aboard the ‘Lady Louisa’. It was bolted together on the new foundations. The light was first exhibited in 1878. The original original kerosene wick lamp was replaced by an incandescent-mantle lamp in 1911. A further conversion to electricity was undertaken in 1958. The light was significantly upgraded in power in 1962 when the candelas was raised from 90,000 to 320,000, the light was further upgraded in 1985. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9a1f8750-e3dc-47b8-b391-e919b7d37e5d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Western Australia has the longest coastline of any state or territory in Australia, at 12,889 km (20,781 km including islands). It is a significant portion of the coastline of Australia, which is 35,877 km (59,736 km including islands). 

The earliest full charting of the coastline occurred during exploration in the late eighteenth and early nineteenth centuries.

The coastline has some features or organisms that are found on the entire length, while some others are specific to particular coastal regions. 

Western Australia has some of the most remote and harsh coastline in the world.  The coast sweeps in a great semicircle, facing south on the Southern Ocean, west and northwest on the Indian Ocean, and north on the Timor Sea. It was one of the last states to be lit, with most lights dating from the turn of the 20th Century. 

This lab cache highlights some of the lighthouses along Western Australia’s coastline, the history and the importance of navigating our dangerous coastline.

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ccdc643b-b84e-47b6-a0d1-d086c353b17d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations on completing this stage, we hope you enjoy Coastal Lighting WA.

You will need to keep note of this...... SHINE&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
