   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Discover Esperance&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Pink Lake&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c775d289-15a5-42a2-b6c2-7df6d95f5899"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c775d289-15a5-42a2-b6c2-7df6d95f5899&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What was the name of Edward John Eyre's companion?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/368ae3ce-c64c-4458-be4e-f2aeabac004b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Pink Lake is just one in a chain of wetlands that circle Esperance. These wetlands are recognised internationally for their importance as a habitat that regularly supports 20,000 water birds, including several threatened species. 

Historically, the lake has been pink due to salt concentrations. However, it has not been pink for many years, but could well turn pink again as conditions change.

On 18th June 1841, Edward John Eyer and his companion passed this way on during their 1500 km journey from Fowlers Bay to Albany.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/20f64421-e983-4547-9b94-aa514213cb1c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Esperance is a town in the Goldfields Esperance region of Western Australia, on the Southern Ocean coastline approximately 720 kilometres east-southeast of Perth.  Its major industries are tourism, agriculture, and fishing. 

A beach and nature lover's dream, Esperance is blessed with squeaky-clean white sand, turquoise waters, untouched islands and colour-filled wildflower country. 

This AdventureLab will take to just 5 of the many wonderful places to visit while in Esperance. 
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d139051f-b2d2-49d8-b268-b2c4c3889504" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
