</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.638867" lon="129.001917">
  <ele>95.0</ele>
  <time>2020-09-13T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBY64B-03</name>
  <desc>NullarborLinks3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Nullarbor</url>
  <urlname>Nullarbor Links ~ The Aussie Way : S3 Border Links by pood</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918622" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Nullarbor Links ~ The Aussie Way : S3 Border Links</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>pood</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">pood</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>South Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Nullarbor Links ~ The Aussie Way&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Border Links&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Nullarbor"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Nullarbor&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the date on the GPS Checkpoint placed here?  month and year&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/70d57321-d2a8-42f4-aaad-d53b18e60334" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Border - At Border Village there is a Line marking the Border between Western Australia and South Australia, as it crosses the Highway at 60 degress.
Eucla is 87 m above sea level and located just 11 km from the South Australian border on the eastern edge of Western Australia. It is 1429 km east of Perth via the Great Western and Eyre Highways;  710 km east of Norseman; 491 km west of Ceduna and 1265 km west of Adelaide.
The old Telegraph Station at Eucla is one of the iconic and lonely images of the Nullarbor. 
It is now nothing more than a few old stone walls slowly disappearing under huge white sand dunes on the edge of the Great Australian Bight. 
A reminder of the isolated nature of this harsh environment and the way nature will always win against humans. Today, apart from the Telegraph Station there are the ruins of the old jetty on the coastline.
The Time - it will be different when you cross the Border.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2a334634-b43a-447d-8767-e1cd05cd766f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Nullarbor Plain
As you travel across it’s windblown, barren surface you might feel more like you have left earth and are traversing the surface of another planet. 
Crossing this huge plain is a quintessential Australian road trip experience and the incredible vast landscapes will make you feel in awe of the wonderful Country we are traveling across.
The name Nullarbor comes from the Latin word “nullus” meaning “nothing” and the word “arbor” meaning “tree”.
Wombats, emus and kangaroos call the Nullarbor home.
Can you imagine driving for 146.6km in a completely straight line, without a single bend or turn in the road? The Eyre Highway is where you will find this curve-free road, stretching between Caiguna and Balladonia.
As you drive across the Nullarbor Plain, you could play 18 holes of golf along the world’s longest golf course – the Nullarbor Links.
Now as you drive across the Nullarbor Plain, you can add Australia's longest Adventure Lab the 'Nullarbor Links ~ The Aussie Way', to your journey.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6085903f-708a-446b-93b3-1d5a85cf8256" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations on crossing the Border&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
