   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>South Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Nullarbor Links ~ The Aussie Way&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Nullarbor Links&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Nullarbor"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Nullarbor&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the person driving the tractor, at the Opening of the Nullarbor Golf Links on 9/11/1991?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/32505ee3-1564-43d4-bc19-ebfbbf352d72" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The isolation and unique location means there is nowhere else in the world like the Nullarbor.

The Nullarbor Plain is a place where you can watch whales up close, explore historic limestone caves, get views of surreal cliff faces, play a hole on the world’s longest golf course or just relax and watch the beautiful sunset over the Nullarbor Plain.
There is quite a bit of history inside the Old Nullarbor Road House, some interesting photos, the old fashioned cash register, the old fashioned fridges, even the old fuel pump out the front is an icon.

As you travel across the Nullarbor you can now add 'The Nullarbor Links ~ The Aussie Way' to your Journey.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2a334634-b43a-447d-8767-e1cd05cd766f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Nullarbor Plain
As you travel across it’s windblown, barren surface you might feel more like you have left earth and are traversing the surface of another planet. 
Crossing this huge plain is a quintessential Australian road trip experience and the incredible vast landscapes will make you feel in awe of the wonderful Country we are traveling across.
The name Nullarbor comes from the Latin word “nullus” meaning “nothing” and the word “arbor” meaning “tree”.
Wombats, emus and kangaroos call the Nullarbor home.
Can you imagine driving for 146.6km in a completely straight line, without a single bend or turn in the road? The Eyre Highway is where you will find this curve-free road, stretching between Caiguna and Balladonia.
As you drive across the Nullarbor Plain, you could play 18 holes of golf along the world’s longest golf course – the Nullarbor Links.
Now as you drive across the Nullarbor Plain, you can add Australia's longest Adventure Lab the 'Nullarbor Links ~ The Aussie Way', to your journey.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d676e6b1-a1e4-4f14-a903-132c78e41789" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations on arriving at the Nullarbor.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
