   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Broome - It's a pearler!&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;China Town&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Broome"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Broome&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The total number of counting beads in the abacus ? (2 digits)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1a98182d-8d58-4142-a19a-d5c194f97f0f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Broome boasts a multicultural population lured by the promise of finding their fortunes. Indonesian, Malay, Chinese, Japanese, European and Indigenous cultures have all blended to create a welcoming and colourful 
personality that is the heart and soul of Broome.
Many Chinese families established businesses in town and today the China Town area thrives with a variety of enterprises and the streetscape highlights traditional Chinese features.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d2ad1127-ffe2-4a9c-a2f7-84653d30f0bf" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The first recorded European to land on Broome shores was explorer William Dampier aboard his ship the HMS Roebuck.
The town was founded in 1883 as a port for the pearling industry and was named after the then Governor of WA – Sir Frederick Broome. 
Although today, Broome is famous for it's beautiful pearls, originally Broome made it's name from the shells - not the pearls. From the 1880's, mother of pearl (the shell) was used to make buttons, cutlery handles, inlays and other ornate objects but with the introduction of plastic in the 1900's, mother of pearl became too expensive to use. The local economy collapsed and it would take until the mid 1950's before the pearl industry was revitalised and since has developed into the booming industry it has become.
This historic pearling town in now one of the most favourite holiday destinations in the country.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations you have correctly answered this question!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
