   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Broome - It's a pearler!&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Sun Picture House&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Broome"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/Broome&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;From the sign above the entry door - What is the name of the first 'talkie' movie screened in 1933?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/288e34b2-6889-42f2-bb33-f0d1c6089e57" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Sun Pictures building in Broome's China town, was constructed in 1905 by the Yamasaki family. Initially the structure served as an Asian Emporium with a portion of the building devoted to a traditional Japanese Noh theatre. 
In 1913, Master Pearler Ted Hunter purchased the building and converted it into a 500 seat outdoor picture theatre, opening with a silent movie in December 1916.
Over the years Sun Pictures has had a succession of owners and is significant as the world's oldest outdoor picture garden.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d2ad1127-ffe2-4a9c-a2f7-84653d30f0bf" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The first recorded European to land on Broome shores was explorer William Dampier aboard his ship the HMS Roebuck.
The town was founded in 1883 as a port for the pearling industry and was named after the then Governor of WA – Sir Frederick Broome. 
Although today, Broome is famous for it's beautiful pearls, originally Broome made it's name from the shells - not the pearls. From the 1880's, mother of pearl (the shell) was used to make buttons, cutlery handles, inlays and other ornate objects but with the introduction of plastic in the 1900's, mother of pearl became too expensive to use. The local economy collapsed and it would take until the mid 1950's before the pearl industry was revitalised and since has developed into the booming industry it has become.
This historic pearling town in now one of the most favourite holiday destinations in the country.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations on answering correctly!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
