 <wpt lat="-16.394667" lon="122.9281">
  <ele>33.0</ele>
  <time>2020-12-22T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBF71d-03</name>
  <desc>CoastalLightin3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/CLWA</url>
  <urlname>Coastal Lighting WA  : S3 Cape Leveque Lighthouse by parkacruz</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99000008" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Coastal Lighting WA  : S3 Cape Leveque Lighthouse</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>parkacruz</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">parkacruz</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Coastal Lighting WA &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Cape Leveque Lighthouse&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/CLWA"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/CLWA&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the Safari Tent near you beginning with N? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/582fa5b5-8e2c-44e5-ac6a-7fb0524e5b77" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Cape Leveque Lighthouse is a significant landmark on the isolated coast, and continues to operate today. The tower is 13.1m high. Cape Leveque lighthouse was commissioned on 9 August 1911, and was one of ten lighthouses built on the West Australian coast between 1900 and 1913, most of them on the North West coast. 

Cape Leveque lighthouse tower was manufactured in Perth. Construction of the lighthouse and associated quarters cost £9,219. The lighthouse was fitted with a third order, dioptric triple flashing white light, which was visible for 18 nautical miles in fine weather. The light was fuelled by kerosene and the lighthouse was manned by two light keepers. The tower is the only prefabricated cast iron lighthouse designed by the Public Works Department and manufactured locally by Bela Makutz .

The RAAF had a base near the lighthouse during World War Two, and an airstrip was built nearby in 1955. The lighthouse was modernised in 1965/66 with a new light and a non-directional radio beacon.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9a1f8750-e3dc-47b8-b391-e919b7d37e5d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Western Australia has the longest coastline of any state or territory in Australia, at 12,889 km (20,781 km including islands). It is a significant portion of the coastline of Australia, which is 35,877 km (59,736 km including islands). 

The earliest full charting of the coastline occurred during exploration in the late eighteenth and early nineteenth centuries.

The coastline has some features or organisms that are found on the entire length, while some others are specific to particular coastal regions. 

Western Australia has some of the most remote and harsh coastline in the world.  The coast sweeps in a great semicircle, facing south on the Southern Ocean, west and northwest on the Indian Ocean, and north on the Timor Sea. It was one of the last states to be lit, with most lights dating from the turn of the 20th Century. 

This lab cache highlights some of the lighthouses along Western Australia’s coastline, the history and the importance of navigating our dangerous coastline.

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4f2284e8-d557-47c8-a70d-999743e49aa2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations on completing this stage, we hope you enjoy Coastal Lighting WA.

You will need to keep note of this...... LIGHT&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.9475" lon="115.778783">
  <ele>17.0</ele>
  <time>2021-08-24T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBdNDN-01</name>
  <desc>ZamiaTrailS1Cam</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9e4dfea9-9f32-4add-bd82-780ea404cb82</url>
  <urlname>Zamia Trail : S1 Camel Lake trail by J2V Travel</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-303" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Zamia Trail : S1 Camel Lake trail</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>J2V Travel</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">J2V Travel</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Zamia Trail&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Camel Lake trail&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9e4dfea9-9f32-4add-bd82-780ea404cb82"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9e4dfea9-9f32-4add-bd82-780ea404cb82&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What was Mr Bold's middle name?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f5f32a47-7552-48ff-a90e-11fb44cdb45b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Walk into the park and take the first right on to Camel Lake trail. This takes you through a wooded section parallel with Perry Lakes Drive. The first stop is in front of where Camel Lake used to be. In 1875 Ernest Giles rested his camels here after his historic trek from Port Augusta to Perth. In 1890s it became a temporary quarantine station for camels imported for transportation to and from the Goldfields. The first question is about the person Bold Park is named after.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/50e7e046-d21e-4d63-a9d3-b4977538d3a5" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;On this adventure lab, enjoy a challenging 6-7km walk/run on limestone paths through Bold Park. The Park is one of the largest remaining bushland remnants in the Perth urban area with Xamia palms, Tuart and Banksia trees. Along the way there are views of the Indian Ocean, Perth city and the suburbs of Floreat and City Beach. 

The adventure lab is designed to start and finish at the Camel Lake car park, near the corner of Stephenson Ave and Perry Lakes Drive (S 31 56.880, E 115 46.830). There are five stops along the way to answer questions and receive clues to a bonus cache in Perry Lakes.

Allow one to two hours to complete the 6-7km loop along Camel Lake Trail, Zamia Trail and Yoorn Walk. There are some steep uphill and downhill sections. It requires a moderate level of fitness.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7d8a5fa4-c659-4b85-9dc7-90eba82d91be" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;William Ernest Bold as Town Clerk of the City of Perth from 1901 to 1945. Record this coordinate for the bonus cache, E = 8.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.949983" lon="115.775717">
  <ele>36.0</ele>
  <time>2021-08-24T08:00:00Z</time>
