   <groundspeak:owner id="">J2V Travel</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Zamia Trail&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Pine plantation&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9e4dfea9-9f32-4add-bd82-780ea404cb82"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9e4dfea9-9f32-4add-bd82-780ea404cb82&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the danger shown on the sign? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/048033cf-777b-40d9-b192-243c354103c3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Continue walking on Zamia Trail and around the pine plantation. The pines were planted some time after 1917 when Perth City Council bought the land and started to create a park. After a steep downhill you will arrive at the fifth and final station.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/50e7e046-d21e-4d63-a9d3-b4977538d3a5" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;On this adventure lab, enjoy a challenging 6-7km walk/run on limestone paths through Bold Park. The Park is one of the largest remaining bushland remnants in the Perth urban area with Xamia palms, Tuart and Banksia trees. Along the way there are views of the Indian Ocean, Perth city and the suburbs of Floreat and City Beach. 

The adventure lab is designed to start and finish at the Camel Lake car park, near the corner of Stephenson Ave and Perry Lakes Drive (S 31 56.880, E 115 46.830). There are five stops along the way to answer questions and receive clues to a bonus cache in Perry Lakes.

Allow one to two hours to complete the 6-7km loop along Camel Lake Trail, Zamia Trail and Yoorn Walk. There are some steep uphill and downhill sections. It requires a moderate level of fitness.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5d94e32e-0935-40f5-bee2-a276da5f3d3f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;One more hill to go. Then turn right on Yoorn Walk, return to the car park and go find the bonus cache. A = 9.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
