   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Zamia Trail&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Climb to Reabold Hill&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9e4dfea9-9f32-4add-bd82-780ea404cb82"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9e4dfea9-9f32-4add-bd82-780ea404cb82&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Who is the bird on this sign named after?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8cc225d4-c3ea-465d-b8d7-bf44fa09011f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;On this leg you'll pass a sign about the Zamia palm. When you get to a four-way intersection on the path, continue straight ahead. This section is uphill with a stop in the middle to answer a question. There are large Tuart trees on the slope.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/50e7e046-d21e-4d63-a9d3-b4977538d3a5" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;On this adventure lab, enjoy a challenging 6-7km walk/run on limestone paths through Bold Park. The Park is one of the largest remaining bushland remnants in the Perth urban area with Xamia palms, Tuart and Banksia trees. Along the way there are views of the Indian Ocean, Perth city and the suburbs of Floreat and City Beach. 

The adventure lab is designed to start and finish at the Camel Lake car park, near the corner of Stephenson Ave and Perry Lakes Drive (S 31 56.880, E 115 46.830). There are five stops along the way to answer questions and receive clues to a bonus cache in Perry Lakes.

Allow one to two hours to complete the 6-7km loop along Camel Lake Trail, Zamia Trail and Yoorn Walk. There are some steep uphill and downhill sections. It requires a moderate level of fitness.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a4826b19-5986-40f1-96c0-d3e666c8eea3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;You have completed the second stage. Keep going, it gets easier after the next hill. Record this coordinate for the bonus cache, D = 3.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
