  <name>LBxF7Q-05</name>
  <desc>ItsAllAboutThen</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/6089bbb5-94cb-4157-87fb-7ae4730256b1</url>
  <urlname>"Its All About The Kids" in Toodyay! : S5 Pelham Lookout &amp; Reserve by BJA3</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476915777" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>"Its All About The Kids" in Toodyay! : S5 Pelham Lookout &amp; Reserve</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>BJA3</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">BJA3</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;"Its All About The Kids" in Toodyay!&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Pelham Lookout &amp; Reserve&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/6089bbb5-94cb-4157-87fb-7ae4730256b1"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/6089bbb5-94cb-4157-87fb-7ae4730256b1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the height above sea level?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ed2405e5-397a-417b-a356-21dcfe6484be" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Rising up the slopes, overlooking town is Pelham Reserve &amp; Lookout.   It covers over 50 hectares of bushland adjoining the southern part of the town area. It allows easily accessible opportunities to traverse some 6 kilometres of signposted walk tracks.

In spring the slopes of Pelham Reserve are carpeted in pink Everlasting flowers.

Pelham Reserve also contains many World War II features of interest and the dam and spillway associated with Toodyay’s original water supply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d1cf63b7-1ba3-4492-abb7-e5c152160efe" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to our Adventure Lab Cache #2, designed by kids for kids!

Toodyay is a town on the Avon River in the Wheatbelt region of WA, 85 kilometres north-east of Perth.

The name Toodyay is believed to be derived from an Aboriginal word 'Duidgee' which means 'place of plenty', referring to the richness and fertility of the area and was where the first European settlement occurred in 1836. 

This AL will take you on a small tour of some of sights around the town that the kids will want to see with a bonus cache to find at the end.

Please enjoy! 
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f7d70e65-44a9-4fb7-b8a0-6aad91d7966e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Nearly done, now off to the bonus cache!  You will need F=7&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
