  <desc>ItsAllAboutThes</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/6089bbb5-94cb-4157-87fb-7ae4730256b1</url>
  <urlname>"Its All About The Kids" in Toodyay! : S3 The Cola Café and Museum by BJA3</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476915773" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>"Its All About The Kids" in Toodyay! : S3 The Cola Café and Museum</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>BJA3</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">BJA3</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;"Its All About The Kids" in Toodyay!&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Cola Café and Museum&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/6089bbb5-94cb-4157-87fb-7ae4730256b1"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/6089bbb5-94cb-4157-87fb-7ae4730256b1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the buildings number?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d5121a1d-134b-4b69-bea7-c5d3305ddcad" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Cola Café and Museum is a 1950’s style Café serving retro tucker, foot-tapping music and features a unique collection of Coca-Cola memorabilia collected over a 45 year period.

It is finely decked out in red, white and black. Wherever you sit you’re surrounded by Brian Dawes’ Coke obsession; everything from the conservative to the quaint to the quirky. Many items have a story - like the Coca- Cola sign that once advertised a Louis Armstrong Concert or the red plastic chairs for the café’s al fresco diners, snapped up from the Sydney 2000 Olympics. There’s a model-T open delivery truck; coca-cola transistors; a miniature vending machine; clocks; bottle and can collections; and a lot more besides."&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d1cf63b7-1ba3-4492-abb7-e5c152160efe" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to our Adventure Lab Cache #2, designed by kids for kids!

Toodyay is a town on the Avon River in the Wheatbelt region of WA, 85 kilometres north-east of Perth.

The name Toodyay is believed to be derived from an Aboriginal word 'Duidgee' which means 'place of plenty', referring to the richness and fertility of the area and was where the first European settlement occurred in 1836. 

This AL will take you on a small tour of some of sights around the town that the kids will want to see with a bonus cache to find at the end.

Please enjoy! 
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f84c1c56-bf58-4bde-a935-d3a174d48c22" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Nice work!  You will need C=8 &amp; D=4&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
