   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;"Its All About The Kids" in Toodyay!&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Christmas 360&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/6089bbb5-94cb-4157-87fb-7ae4730256b1"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/6089bbb5-94cb-4157-87fb-7ae4730256b1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What shape is on the main doors?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/71e381ac-21d9-4f56-a37c-6afd3a72a7e2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Christmas 360 is a wonderland of everything Christmas. It is Christmas all year round at this shop.  It brings you the latest lighting trends and Christmas decorations, from around the globe, each and every year.

This is a must-visit shop when you are in Toodyay and it is jammed packed with Christmas goodies. It’s a highly recommended destination for any visitor to this part of town.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d1cf63b7-1ba3-4492-abb7-e5c152160efe" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to our Adventure Lab Cache #2, designed by kids for kids!

Toodyay is a town on the Avon River in the Wheatbelt region of WA, 85 kilometres north-east of Perth.

The name Toodyay is believed to be derived from an Aboriginal word 'Duidgee' which means 'place of plenty', referring to the richness and fertility of the area and was where the first European settlement occurred in 1836. 

This AL will take you on a small tour of some of sights around the town that the kids will want to see with a bonus cache to find at the end.

Please enjoy! 
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0a465bce-28f6-446d-bce8-21a4c708d765" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Great work!  You will need E=2&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
