  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3a6ea64c-dcfc-44cd-867d-3d24b2f94bb8</url>
  <urlname>Exploring Jandakot Airport : S4 TAFE Aerospace Training Centre by fratra</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909829" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Exploring Jandakot Airport : S4 TAFE Aerospace Training Centre</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>fratra</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">fratra</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Exploring Jandakot Airport&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;TAFE Aerospace Training Centre&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3a6ea64c-dcfc-44cd-867d-3d24b2f94bb8"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3a6ea64c-dcfc-44cd-867d-3d24b2f94bb8&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year was the Aerospace Training Centre opened?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c0a8196a-e6ea-41b7-80ec-880e6d6d5291" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Jandakot campus houses the AeroSpace Training Centre which is comprised of two distinct facilities, the hangar on Compass Road and the annex on Eagle Drive.
The main campus building includes a 1,500 square metre hangar facility that houses a variety of aircraft including SM TAFE's very own Boeing 737. Our Boeing 737 is maintained in a fully serviceable condition and used as a non-flying static training facility for students across an array of training courses, from pilot studies, to cabin crew, to aircraft maintenance, and even safety and ground handling.
Other facilities and training devices available for students include additional fixed wing and rotorcraft static trainers, a learning resource centre with computer and wireless internet resources, computer-based training modules and a flight simulator.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a095ea7a-8514-43c0-84f7-f59bbf954654" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Opened in 1963, Jandakot Airport is the major General Aviation airport in Western Australia, and is one of the busiest airfields and largest aviation training bases in Australia.
It accommodates the aircraft of service organisations, including the Royal Flying Doctor Service, CALM Forest and Bushfire Patrol, and the WA Police Air Support. Jandakot airport is also a major training base for international airline pilots.

It should take 30 - 45 minutes to complete this Lab and there is a bonus box to pick up at the end - GC9FYFF.

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations!
Now, record the letter P to assist you in finding the bonus box.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.093333" lon="115.878767">
