  <desc>ExploringJanda3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3a6ea64c-dcfc-44cd-867d-3d24b2f94bb8</url>
  <urlname>Exploring Jandakot Airport : S3 The Sugar Bird Lady by fratra</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909827" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Exploring Jandakot Airport : S3 The Sugar Bird Lady</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>fratra</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">fratra</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Exploring Jandakot Airport&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Sugar Bird Lady&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3a6ea64c-dcfc-44cd-867d-3d24b2f94bb8"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3a6ea64c-dcfc-44cd-867d-3d24b2f94bb8&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the Aircraft registration on Sugar Bird Lady?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c142c51e-877d-41bc-ba9b-45f1f0331328" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Robin Miller Dicks - The Sugar Bird Lady
Her mother was the writer Dame Mary Durack and her father was an aviator, Captain Horrie Miller.
After obtaining a private pilot licence and a commercial flying licence while training as a nurse, she approached the Western Australian Department of Health to ask permission to fly to northern Western Australia in order to carry out a vaccination programme.
Permission granted, she borrowed money for a Cessna 182 Skylane and set out on her first flight on 22 May 1967. Travelling to remote communities, she would treat children with the Sabin vaccine in sugar lumps. She later flew with the Royal Flying Doctor Service of Australia (RFDS).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a095ea7a-8514-43c0-84f7-f59bbf954654" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Opened in 1963, Jandakot Airport is the major General Aviation airport in Western Australia, and is one of the busiest airfields and largest aviation training bases in Australia.
It accommodates the aircraft of service organisations, including the Royal Flying Doctor Service, CALM Forest and Bushfire Patrol, and the WA Police Air Support. Jandakot airport is also a major training base for international airline pilots.

It should take 30 - 45 minutes to complete this Lab and there is a bonus box to pick up at the end - GC9FYFF.

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations!
Now, record the letter L to assist you in finding the bonus box.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
