  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-44" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] The Lake Dumbleyung : S4 Terry Ward</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Everlasting</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Everlasting</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;The Lake Dumbleyung&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Terry Ward&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3f82a051-bc52-498a-95dc-4792dca9fa60"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3f82a051-bc52-498a-95dc-4792dca9fa60&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Terry Ward's Plaque: What is the sentence in the last line ? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/dd469054-424d-49fe-9a77-6ca640f223a5" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Dumbleyung Short Stories book

September 1986 – Terry Ward caught two bream in lake with nets.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f140b888-9374-4a3f-86bb-f5b3cc3ad612" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;One Year, Two World Records
 
On December 31st 1964, after breaking the world land speed record in Lake Eyre, South Australia and with only hours to spare, Campbell broke the world water speed record on Lake Dumbleyung in his jet propelled hydroplane boat, Bluebird. This gave him him the two world records in the same year – a feat that has never been achieved before or since.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/52c78787-0f0e-4796-bc0e-55797e03e37f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations on completing this stage.

E117 38.020 &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
