   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-33.3159" lon="117.6334">
  <ele>300.0</ele>
  <time>2021-09-05T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LB1TrP-05</name>
  <desc>LTheLakeDumble5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3f82a051-bc52-498a-95dc-4792dca9fa60</url>
  <urlname>[L] The Lake Dumbleyung : S5 Donald Campbell by Everlasting</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-45" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] The Lake Dumbleyung : S5 Donald Campbell</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Everlasting</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Everlasting</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;The Lake Dumbleyung&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Donald Campbell&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3f82a051-bc52-498a-95dc-4792dca9fa60"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3f82a051-bc52-498a-95dc-4792dca9fa60&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Can you spot the small circular plaque on the rock plaque - what it is engraving ? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/789efca9-e0c3-4724-8893-cb454ff61646" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Between them, Campbell and his father had set 11 speed records on water and 10 on land.

Campbell decided a massive jump in speed was called for following his successful 1964 land speed record attempt in Bluebird CN7. His vision was of a supersonic rocket car with a potential maximum speed of 840 mph (1,350 km/h). ... We can have the car on the track within three years."

Died: 4 January 1967 (aged 45)
Occupation: Speed record breaker
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f140b888-9374-4a3f-86bb-f5b3cc3ad612" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;One Year, Two World Records
 
On December 31st 1964, after breaking the world land speed record in Lake Eyre, South Australia and with only hours to spare, Campbell broke the world water speed record on Lake Dumbleyung in his jet propelled hydroplane boat, Bluebird. This gave him him the two world records in the same year – a feat that has never been achieved before or since.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/72b75185-559d-4e38-ab54-d6f10a8bb2b5" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations on completing this stage.

GC9G00X - Bonus: S33 18.947 E117 38.020 &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
