   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;The Lake Dumbleyung&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Campbells are coming!&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3f82a051-bc52-498a-95dc-4792dca9fa60"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3f82a051-bc52-498a-95dc-4792dca9fa60&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;In the middle sign board: How many people work on bluebird in the photo?  &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9ceec526-3d22-4d02-b746-41e14ad07cae" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It sits near Lake Dumbleyung as a tribute to Mr Campbell, who died aged 45 while attempting a new water speed record in England.

Dumbleyung Shire president Gordon Davidson said the town received significant rainfall but those concerned were also excited by the lake’s condition.

“Initially the flooding ruined stock feed, caused erosion and damaged fences,” he said.

“But as the rain continued and the filling of Lake Dumbleyung begun, we realised this was a rain that could change our community.”&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f140b888-9374-4a3f-86bb-f5b3cc3ad612" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;One Year, Two World Records
 
On December 31st 1964, after breaking the world land speed record in Lake Eyre, South Australia and with only hours to spare, Campbell broke the world water speed record on Lake Dumbleyung in his jet propelled hydroplane boat, Bluebird. This gave him him the two world records in the same year – a feat that has never been achieved before or since.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e9b46fca-d447-4b9d-8ac3-1704d4d1638a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations on completing this stage.

Bonus Cache at  E117 38.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
