   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;The Lake Dumbleyung&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Pussycat Hill Lookout&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3f82a051-bc52-498a-95dc-4792dca9fa60"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3f82a051-bc52-498a-95dc-4792dca9fa60&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Last paragraph: how many words ?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0822b116-9b58-41e1-9b5d-e9c9f33bea21" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Acknowledgement and Thank you 
Terry Ward
for his generous donation of the land to the Shire of Dumbleyung in 1984 to permit the public access to Pussycat Hill Lookout and the Dumbleyung Lake Yacht Club&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f140b888-9374-4a3f-86bb-f5b3cc3ad612" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;One Year, Two World Records
 
On December 31st 1964, after breaking the world land speed record in Lake Eyre, South Australia and with only hours to spare, Campbell broke the world water speed record on Lake Dumbleyung in his jet propelled hydroplane boat, Bluebird. This gave him him the two world records in the same year – a feat that has never been achieved before or since.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2ba2ebf4-d8b6-4c05-b5d3-18a1b3976f41" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations on completing this stage.

