 <wpt lat="-31.90165" lon="116.166817">
  <ele>301.0</ele>
  <time>2021-09-12T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBCTGN-01</name>
  <desc>ExploringTheHi1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/23699a08-d5b1-44cf-b01c-663a7140dadf</url>
  <urlname>Exploring the Hills : S1 Mundaring Visitors Centre by TeamBarritts</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99000318" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Exploring the Hills : S1 Mundaring Visitors Centre</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>TeamBarritts</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">TeamBarritts</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Exploring the Hills&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Mundaring Visitors Centre&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/23699a08-d5b1-44cf-b01c-663a7140dadf"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/23699a08-d5b1-44cf-b01c-663a7140dadf&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the year for the official opening of the second classroom? (Hint: Sign)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/619bfefb-8431-4847-a053-ba0a174a5d0b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Perth Hills Mundaring Visitor Centre is a National Tourism Accredited Visitor Centre located in the old school house in the heart of Mundaring and is the ideal first port of call to seek information on local attractions, trails, activities, wineries, dining and accommodation options. They also manage campsite bookings and general enquiries for Lake Leschenaultia.

The Centre houses the district museum, so it is well worth a visit to learn more about the history of the area, as well as a retail section stocked with a selection of souvenirs, local produce, walk and cycle trails, including the long distance Bibbulmun Track and Munda Biddi Trail, regional maps and general information.

Perth Hills Mundaring Visitor Centre is open seven days; from 9.30am to 4pm Monday to Saturday and 10am to 2.30pm on Sundays and most public holidays (closed Ch&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/21959691-17ba-4c36-b7c3-8273019465a6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;We all like exploring new areas and geocaching does this by taking us to spots where we would not have known about or ever thought to go.  Another way would be to visit the Visitor Centre's at those locations which will have some great advice and can showcase local attractions.

This Lab takes you on a tour of the Visitor Centre's around the Perth Hills area and nearby satellite towns.

You will need to allow an afternoon to take a leisurely drive throughout the district to complete this adventure lab and claim the bonus at the end.  It is recommended that you start at Mundaring and follow through to Toodyay, Northam, York and finally Beverley - however you can do them in any order you choose.

Good Luck and enjoy!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d0225b79-41cc-48ae-89d0-05e0028423b3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Good job!  You will need A=5&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.55055" lon="116.46545">
