  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/23699a08-d5b1-44cf-b01c-663a7140dadf</url>
  <urlname>Exploring the Hills : S4 Toodyay Visitors Centre by TeamBarritts</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99000324" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Exploring the Hills : S4 Toodyay Visitors Centre</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>TeamBarritts</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">TeamBarritts</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Exploring the Hills&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Toodyay Visitors Centre&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/23699a08-d5b1-44cf-b01c-663a7140dadf"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/23699a08-d5b1-44cf-b01c-663a7140dadf&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What date is written on the plaque at the given coordinates?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/61357782-146a-4556-acb3-51553fe6bf31" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Learning about Toodyay is easy at the visitor centre as they stock a huge range of brochures covering not only Toodyay - but the Avon Valley and Wheatbelt districts. Their local staff have many combined years of experience and are always passionate about passing on their knowledge. The centre is famous for providing local products as well as maps, souvenirs, information on local flora and fauna, picture books, history books, guides and information brochures.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/21959691-17ba-4c36-b7c3-8273019465a6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;We all like exploring new areas and geocaching does this by taking us to spots where we would not have known about or ever thought to go.  Another way would be to visit the Visitor Centre's at those locations which will have some great advice and can showcase local attractions.

This Lab takes you on a tour of the Visitor Centre's around the Perth Hills area and nearby satellite towns.

You will need to allow an afternoon to take a leisurely drive throughout the district to complete this adventure lab and claim the bonus at the end.  It is recommended that you start at Mundaring and follow through to Toodyay, Northam, York and finally Beverley - however you can do them in any order you choose.

Good Luck and enjoy!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3abfb9b9-9cb3-448a-8364-c974109635e3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Awesome work!  You will need E=0&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
