   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Exploring the Hills&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;York Visitors Centre&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/23699a08-d5b1-44cf-b01c-663a7140dadf"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/23699a08-d5b1-44cf-b01c-663a7140dadf&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the month and year displayed on the plaque at the given coordinates?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/bd406d1a-1a96-43c2-b3ef-9d7bd736d7da" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The York Visitor Centre, located inside the York Town Hall is a nationally-accredited tourism business which provides a full range of visitor services including: Local knowledge and expertise; York attractions and eatery information; Accommodation information; Town and regional maps; Free WiFi; Festival and Event information; Heritage and nature walk brochures; and Wildflower and Canola information.

York was the first inland settlement in Western Australia and the town has many historic, heritage-listed Victorian and Federation buildings.  An abundance of local activities and facilities make it an attractive destination and a fantastic place to live.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/21959691-17ba-4c36-b7c3-8273019465a6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;We all like exploring new areas and geocaching does this by taking us to spots where we would not have known about or ever thought to go.  Another way would be to visit the Visitor Centre's at those locations which will have some great advice and can showcase local attractions.

This Lab takes you on a tour of the Visitor Centre's around the Perth Hills area and nearby satellite towns.

You will need to allow an afternoon to take a leisurely drive throughout the district to complete this adventure lab and claim the bonus at the end.  It is recommended that you start at Mundaring and follow through to Toodyay, Northam, York and finally Beverley - however you can do them in any order you choose.

Good Luck and enjoy!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/89cdbe28-774d-4c7b-abc9-2b475704463f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done!  You will need B=7 &amp; C=5&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.652233" lon="116.671767">
