  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99000326" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Exploring the Hills : S5 Northam Visitors Centre</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>TeamBarritts</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">TeamBarritts</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Exploring the Hills&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Northam Visitors Centre&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/23699a08-d5b1-44cf-b01c-663a7140dadf"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/23699a08-d5b1-44cf-b01c-663a7140dadf&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year did James Michell pass away?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/05e0b7fe-da34-4eb7-a7b6-7d1511a546d3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Northam Visitor Centre is located at 2 Grey Street in Northam on the banks of the Avon River. 

The friendly staff at the Visitor Centre will be able to offer advice on places to see, stay and eat while you are in the area, information on heritage sites and the places of interest that you may enjoy during your stay. 

The Centre includes an interpretive space featuring the “Sense of Place” Migrant Exhibition, Northam’s First People Exhibition, and environmental displays. While you are at the Centre you will also have the opportunity to browse through a wide range of local produce and artwork, and a great selection of souvenirs and gifts to remember your time in Northam. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/21959691-17ba-4c36-b7c3-8273019465a6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;We all like exploring new areas and geocaching does this by taking us to spots where we would not have known about or ever thought to go.  Another way would be to visit the Visitor Centre's at those locations which will have some great advice and can showcase local attractions.

This Lab takes you on a tour of the Visitor Centre's around the Perth Hills area and nearby satellite towns.

You will need to allow an afternoon to take a leisurely drive throughout the district to complete this adventure lab and claim the bonus at the end.  It is recommended that you start at Mundaring and follow through to Toodyay, Northam, York and finally Beverley - however you can do them in any order you choose.

Good Luck and enjoy!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/90fb4cf2-cd2b-4cca-bba6-9da42688d5ea" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Great work, now for the bonus!  You will need F=6&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
