 <wpt lat="-23.34485" lon="119.746233">
  <ele>548.0</ele>
  <time>2021-09-18T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBhnxU-04</name>
  <desc>NewmanTownS4Sta</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9e8c0bf3-9acd-41cb-b1e7-cac0bfacf6aa</url>
  <urlname>Newman Town : S4 Stan &amp; Ella by chickenhawk07</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99000314" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Newman Town : S4 Stan &amp; Ella</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>chickenhawk07</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">chickenhawk07</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Newman Town&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Stan &amp; Ella&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9e8c0bf3-9acd-41cb-b1e7-cac0bfacf6aa"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9e8c0bf3-9acd-41cb-b1e7-cac0bfacf6aa&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;On the base of the statue is a plaque. What are the three letters after the CEO's name ?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f0d52633-ea5a-42fd-a9c4-216698591e95" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;If you are driving on the Great Northern Highway into Newman you will notice a metal statue of a couple overlooking Mount Whaleback.

The sculpture is of veteran prospector Stan Hilditch and his wife Ella.

The couple accidently discovered the largest iron ore deposit in the world in 1957.

But despite the amazing find, the couple wasn't allowed to tell anyone about it for four years. Read the story on the information boards at Haul Pack 793B&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/fd5fe89f-02fa-430f-9eff-318d9e0eb70e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Newman is the largest inland town in the Pilbara and provides accomodation and infrastructure for many surrounding minesites.
The Eastern Pilbara is one of the most isolated and inhospitable regions in Australia. Temperatures in summer time hover around 40°C and the hot winds blow in off the Great Sandy Desert. 
This adventure lab will take you to 5 locations around town. Phone reception is strong so you shouldnt have any issues here.
I would like to acknowledge the Nyiyaparli Traditional Owners, on whose ancestral land this Adventure Lab plays. I would like to pay my respect to their Elders past and present and extend that respect to all Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples today.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7554d304-8b9e-4107-bf70-8ad7359bb656" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Correct&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-22.7179" lon="117.764683">
  <ele>1116.0</ele>
  <time>2021-09-18T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBGt2v-02</name>
  <desc>TomPriceTownS2M</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9ab9b64a-5eed-48aa-9f6f-e24b67670e07</url>
  <urlname>Tom Price Town : S2 Mount Nameless/Jarndunmunha by Kyzabra</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99000272" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Tom Price Town : S2 Mount Nameless/Jarndunmunha</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Kyzabra</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Kyzabra</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Tom Price Town&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Mount Nameless/Jarndunmunha&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9ab9b64a-5eed-48aa-9f6f-e24b67670e07"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9ab9b64a-5eed-48aa-9f6f-e24b67670e07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;According to the plaque, what is the distance to Perth in kms ? (number only)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/22932e14-338a-405e-bc04-e29c440ab1a9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The peak of Mount Nameless/Jarndunmunha stands 1128 metres above sea level, and from the lookout there are sweeping views across the Hammersley Ranges, the town of Tom Price and the iron ore mining operations.
It’s the second highest accessible mountain by four wheel drive in Western Australia and offers all of the rewards of a spectacular mountain view without the hike! When driving to the summit, low range 4WD is required. 
Look for the plaque near the lookout for the answer.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/15b35e88-697f-4870-ab7e-e92802e672f4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Tom Price, situated in the Pilbara region of Western Australia, is a mining town. The town is located inland, at the edge of the Hamersley Range. Tom Price is the highest town above sea level (747 metres (2,451 ft)) in Western Australia, and is consequently dubbed "Top Town in WA".
This Adventure Lab will take you around town, as well as a 4WD trek up Mt Nameless. 
Just a warning, the Mt Nameless location will require a 4WD to take the driven route, or a 3 hour return hike.
I would like to acknowledge the Nyiyaparli Traditional Owners, on whose ancestral land this Adventure Lab plays. I would like to pay my respect to their Elders past and present and extend that respect to all Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples today.


&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/15efaec3-a163-4a66-93f8-36fd810a939c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;What a view. Even better at sunrise&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-22.697983" lon="117.78695">
  <ele>724.0</ele>
  <time>2021-09-18T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBGt2v-05</name>
  <desc>TomPriceTownS5L</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9ab9b64a-5eed-48aa-9f6f-e24b67670e07</url>
  <urlname>Tom Price Town : S5 Lectra Haul by Kyzabra</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99000268" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Tom Price Town : S5 Lectra Haul</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Kyzabra</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Kyzabra</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Tom Price Town&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Lectra Haul&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9ab9b64a-5eed-48aa-9f6f-e24b67670e07"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9ab9b64a-5eed-48aa-9f6f-e24b67670e07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;On the data plate on the the side of the cart, there is a Model number. What is it ? (2 digits and a letter)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/00d7c1a4-53a7-4f97-82ee-3d3b4ab95616" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is the final resting spot of one of the mine haul packs.
You cant climb on it but can use the nearby rest area to sit and relax. A new area has been built here.
Near the table and chair is a rockershovel. 

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/15b35e88-697f-4870-ab7e-e92802e672f4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Tom Price, situated in the Pilbara region of Western Australia, is a mining town. The town is located inland, at the edge of the Hamersley Range. Tom Price is the highest town above sea level (747 metres (2,451 ft)) in Western Australia, and is consequently dubbed "Top Town in WA".
This Adventure Lab will take you around town, as well as a 4WD trek up Mt Nameless. 
Just a warning, the Mt Nameless location will require a 4WD to take the driven route, or a 3 hour return hike.
I would like to acknowledge the Nyiyaparli Traditional Owners, on whose ancestral land this Adventure Lab plays. I would like to pay my respect to their Elders past and present and extend that respect to all Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples today.


&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0c1d3299-d144-4eb0-a336-91aee8f4cb4c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Correct&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
