  <desc>LThePerthfectR1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9b87cb29-5ac7-47f6-97d7-e40a62c42976</url>
  <urlname>[L] The Perth-fect Race : S1 Perth Airport by Cirrus_WA</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99000328" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] The Perth-fect Race : S1 Perth Airport</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Cirrus_WA</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Cirrus_WA</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;The Perth-fect Race&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Perth Airport&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9b87cb29-5ac7-47f6-97d7-e40a62c42976"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9b87cb29-5ac7-47f6-97d7-e40a62c42976&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What aircrafts first flight was 17 September 2013? (Full model description at top of information)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c345057e-0cb7-4fd1-a425-095cd357c67f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Route Info: This is the basic form of information given to teams, it may be given to them by the host at the start of a leg, in a clue box at a new location or once a challenge has been completed.


As with all international arrivals into Western Australia, Perth Airport is where the final day of competition began.
Teams arrived in Perth from Singapore, where they had already completed a number of tasks. Make your way to the airport viewing platform to start your Perth-fect Race Adventure.


Please be aware of the opening times for this location:
October-March 06:30-19:00
April-September 07:30-17:30
Check perthairport.com.au for closures.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/59ba51eb-26ca-4ea3-b29a-9d8f9fb679a9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Amazing Race is a reality television program that started in the US in 2001.

It sees teams race against each other around the world, completing challenges along the way to get the next piece of information needed to continue on the race.

The first season of The Amazing Race Australia was in 2011. It saw 11 teams race around the world going to 10 countries and covering over 50 000km. The series culminated in the final three teams racing around Perth completing challenges attempting to arrive at the check-in point first and claim a $250 000 prize.

In this recreation of the final leg you will have to make your way along the same route that the teams did to claim your final prize, not cash but a cache (GC9G7E2).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e7977f5c-c253-444b-b377-fe011dbbb16a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Caution: Detour Ahead&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
