   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;The Perth-fect Race&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Heirisson Island&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9b87cb29-5ac7-47f6-97d7-e40a62c42976"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9b87cb29-5ac7-47f6-97d7-e40a62c42976&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the colour of the diamond on the sign?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/540892ac-9429-4ced-a87e-eae45c4e6984" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The final journey of the season had the teams making their way back to the city to find the final pitstop with eliminated teams cheering on the winners at Heirisson Island.

The Island is in the area known to the local Noongar people as Matagarup and was a significant river crossing with no other crossings possible downstream until Fremantle.
Originally a number of islands were surrounded by mud flats. Reclaimation and dredging around the area over the years produced the 0.3km2 island you see today.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/59ba51eb-26ca-4ea3-b29a-9d8f9fb679a9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Amazing Race is a reality television program that started in the US in 2001.

It sees teams race against each other around the world, completing challenges along the way to get the next piece of information needed to continue on the race.

The first season of The Amazing Race Australia was in 2011. It saw 11 teams race around the world going to 10 countries and covering over 50 000km. The series culminated in the final three teams racing around Perth completing challenges attempting to arrive at the check-in point first and claim a $250 000 prize.

In this recreation of the final leg you will have to make your way along the same route that the teams did to claim your final prize, not cash but a cache (GC9G7E2).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c597f199-ace6-4e0e-8b69-dd651bbb9817" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Five Stops, 117km, congratulations on completing your Perth-fect Race. 

The bonus cache can be found at 

S31 57.944 E115 53.095&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
