  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99000330" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] The Perth-fect Race : S2 Kings Park</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Cirrus_WA</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Cirrus_WA</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;The Perth-fect Race&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Kings Park&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9b87cb29-5ac7-47f6-97d7-e40a62c42976"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9b87cb29-5ac7-47f6-97d7-e40a62c42976&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the number?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/12962967-30f5-40e1-891a-a4cec986fbc4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A detour is a choice between two options, each with its own pros and cons. Teams must choose which task they believe best suits their skills.

Here you have a choice between Count &amp; Calculate.

Count: Head to the Kaarta Gar-up Lookout (S31 57.549 E115 50.659) and count the number of vertical poles along the lookouts fencing. Enter this number to unlock the next lab location.

Calculate: Head to the Wishing Well (S31 57.577 E115 50.654) and calculate the following L3W3 Word Value + Teeth on Gear = A
A x Spokes in Gear = B
B - L4W5 Word Value = Answer, enter this number to unlock the next lab location.


Once the teams arrived in Perth they made their way to Kings Park where a clue box was waiting for them to give them information about where to head to next. 
During the filming of the episode the clue box was set up between the State War Memorial and Eternal Flame. A slight adjustment for your race today will bring you to one of the best views of Perth City the park has to offer.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/59ba51eb-26ca-4ea3-b29a-9d8f9fb679a9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Amazing Race is a reality television program that started in the US in 2001.

It sees teams race against each other around the world, completing challenges along the way to get the next piece of information needed to continue on the race.

The first season of The Amazing Race Australia was in 2011. It saw 11 teams race around the world going to 10 countries and covering over 50 000km. The series culminated in the final three teams racing around Perth completing challenges attempting to arrive at the check-in point first and claim a $250 000 prize.

In this recreation of the final leg you will have to make your way along the same route that the teams did to claim your final prize, not cash but a cache (GC9G7E2).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1ba07e0b-4330-4d11-9242-64a840ea8c3f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
