   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;The Perth-fect Race&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Fremantle Prison&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9b87cb29-5ac7-47f6-97d7-e40a62c42976"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9b87cb29-5ac7-47f6-97d7-e40a62c42976&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many window are there on the towers of the gate house? ( _ _ )&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/fba942b2-9c7a-4238-a521-ace0dd30ee3d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;When the teams arrived here they found the clue box waiting for them in courtyard of the prison.

Their challenge at the prison was to take a set of 12 keys and search the convict towers for the cell that one of their keys would open. On a hot day for filming, temperatures in towers reached the high 30's and teams struggled to complete the assigned task.

Luckily for you there is an easier task awaiting for you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/59ba51eb-26ca-4ea3-b29a-9d8f9fb679a9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Amazing Race is a reality television program that started in the US in 2001.

It sees teams race against each other around the world, completing challenges along the way to get the next piece of information needed to continue on the race.

The first season of The Amazing Race Australia was in 2011. It saw 11 teams race around the world going to 10 countries and covering over 50 000km. The series culminated in the final three teams racing around Perth completing challenges attempting to arrive at the check-in point first and claim a $250 000 prize.

In this recreation of the final leg you will have to make your way along the same route that the teams did to claim your final prize, not cash but a cache (GC9G7E2).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/84e9dc6a-793f-40fc-8bd8-29891296fd7a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
