   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;The Perth-fect Race&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Point Peron&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9b87cb29-5ac7-47f6-97d7-e40a62c42976"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9b87cb29-5ac7-47f6-97d7-e40a62c42976&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the ammunition size and model of the relica cannon installed here?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9a134aa3-5602-4f61-8936-ea12589efc10" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The location of the final roadblock of the series took place at Point Peron.

A roadblock only allows one team member to complete the task. Here the contestants found a barrel full of flags on the beach and had to arrange them in the order of the countries that they had visited on the race.

Since then there has been development and refurbishment occurring around the point. A replica cannon has been erected at one of the former battery positions on the point, make your way there to complete your final challenge before the finish line.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/59ba51eb-26ca-4ea3-b29a-9d8f9fb679a9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Amazing Race is a reality television program that started in the US in 2001.

It sees teams race against each other around the world, completing challenges along the way to get the next piece of information needed to continue on the race.

The first season of The Amazing Race Australia was in 2011. It saw 11 teams race around the world going to 10 countries and covering over 50 000km. The series culminated in the final three teams racing around Perth completing challenges attempting to arrive at the check-in point first and claim a $250 000 prize.

In this recreation of the final leg you will have to make your way along the same route that the teams did to claim your final prize, not cash but a cache (GC9G7E2).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a417e768-889e-4e29-ac00-658d5a96b101" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;The finish line awaits.
Go, go, go.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.952383" lon="115.881367">
  <ele>13.0</ele>
  <time>2021-10-05T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBUWQ2-02</name>
  <desc>ViewsFromVicto2</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9e9751cb-08fc-4aa6-a067-95ffb7755852</url>
  <urlname>Views from Victoria Gardens : S2 Charnock Woman Mosaic by Paskersfind</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99000420" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Views from Victoria Gardens : S2 Charnock Woman Mosaic</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Paskersfind</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Paskersfind</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Views from Victoria Gardens&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Charnock Woman Mosaic&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9e9751cb-08fc-4aa6-a067-95ffb7755852"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9e9751cb-08fc-4aa6-a067-95ffb7755852&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many "coolbardies" are depicted within the mosaic?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/cb914ab5-5fbd-4e2a-92e3-70f00dffdb2a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This colourful mosaic tells the Noongar Dreaming story of a giant evil spirit who stole children. The complete story can be found on the plaque attached to the nearby wall and makes for interesting reading. There are some stunning views to checkout from this location.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/54f60d21-1384-489d-b0f3-125fb31b97b6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Now just might be a great time to visit beautiful Victoria Gardens in East Perth. Located on an elevated peninsula above Claisebrook Cove, these gardens were one of the earliest public parks in Perth and offer stunning views of the Swan River and its surrounds together with a variety of artworks that celebrate Indigenous history and the early culture of this area.  All five locations can be found within the immediate vicinity and can be done in any order as you stroll to  all corners of the park. 
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a9e5c1f9-e97d-4049-82a9-2ac6acdf2197" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Hope you are enjoying the stunning views and making note of the answer to the question if you are after the bonus.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.951933" lon="115.882117">
