   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Views from Victoria Gardens&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Niche Wall Mural&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9e9751cb-08fc-4aa6-a067-95ffb7755852"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9e9751cb-08fc-4aa6-a067-95ffb7755852&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The length of this mural is&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7f75d96f-1728-43fd-b1d3-a4b71423041a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This impressive mural is an allegory for the history and development of this part of East Perth.  Marvel at the colours, textures and sheer size of this unique piece of artwork.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/54f60d21-1384-489d-b0f3-125fb31b97b6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Now just might be a great time to visit beautiful Victoria Gardens in East Perth. Located on an elevated peninsula above Claisebrook Cove, these gardens were one of the earliest public parks in Perth and offer stunning views of the Swan River and its surrounds together with a variety of artworks that celebrate Indigenous history and the early culture of this area.  All five locations can be found within the immediate vicinity and can be done in any order as you stroll to  all corners of the park. 
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b5a3cf1b-d513-453e-9c4c-36f849ce4685" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;A "not so little" hidden gem! And another number to add to the bonus cache tally.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-21.198533" lon="119.7146">
  <ele>200.0</ele>
  <time>2021-10-04T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBentd-05</name>
  <desc>WhenIsMarbleNo5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0bac773d-b432-4ef7-ae47-b7abc45234bf</url>
  <urlname>When is Marble not Marble? : S5 Flying Comet Lookout by pommieparkin2</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99000416" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>When is Marble not Marble? : S5 Flying Comet Lookout</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>pommieparkin2</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">pommieparkin2</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;When is Marble not Marble?&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Flying Comet Lookout&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0bac773d-b432-4ef7-ae47-b7abc45234bf"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0bac773d-b432-4ef7-ae47-b7abc45234bf&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year did the tragedy occur that is commemorated on the plaque?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/785c937c-af21-45e8-a0e6-825fcade9619" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;5km down Comet Mine Road is the Flying Fox Lookout that’s an ideal spot to watch the sunset or have a picnic lunch and look at the panoramic view. This was used to run the depth gauge when the river was running.
The location gives a great view over the Coongan River and is a fantastic photo opportunity.
Easily accessible by 2WD vehicles &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d9516bbc-31e7-4aa7-9c2d-cb381945d5c0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Marble Bar has earned the reputation as Australia's hottest town by experiencing consistently high temperatures during summer months when the mercury climbs to over 38 degrees for days on end.
The record is 160 consecutive days over 38.7 degrees recorded in the sweltering summer of 1923-24.
An extraordinary colourfully Jasper Bar crosses the Coongan River. Unfortunately this Bar was mistakenly identified as Marble giving rise to the town's name. Somehow Jasper Bar just doesn't have the same ring to it!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Great answers. I hope you enjoyed Marble Bar as much as we did.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-21.176283" lon="119.7433">
  <ele>207.0</ele>
  <time>2021-10-04T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBentd-02</name>
  <desc>WhenIsMarbleNo2</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0bac773d-b432-4ef7-ae47-b7abc45234bf</url>
  <urlname>When is Marble not Marble? : S2 Tank Hill by pommieparkin2</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99000410" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>When is Marble not Marble? : S2 Tank Hill</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>pommieparkin2</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">pommieparkin2</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;When is Marble not Marble?&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Tank Hill&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0bac773d-b432-4ef7-ae47-b7abc45234bf"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0bac773d-b432-4ef7-ae47-b7abc45234bf&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What date was the plaque unveiled?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/da3d7030-c7c0-4ef3-b917-ae26528b5846" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Watet Tank Hill makes an ideal lookout over the town for sightseeing and photographs.  
You can drive right to the top.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d9516bbc-31e7-4aa7-9c2d-cb381945d5c0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Marble Bar has earned the reputation as Australia's hottest town by experiencing consistently high temperatures during summer months when the mercury climbs to over 38 degrees for days on end.
The record is 160 consecutive days over 38.7 degrees recorded in the sweltering summer of 1923-24.
An extraordinary colourfully Jasper Bar crosses the Coongan River. Unfortunately this Bar was mistakenly identified as Marble giving rise to the town's name. Somehow Jasper Bar just doesn't have the same ring to it!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done, that's correct &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-21.1716" lon="119.742783">
  <ele>178.0</ele>
