  <name>LBentd-04</name>
  <desc>WhenIsMarbleNo4</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0bac773d-b432-4ef7-ae47-b7abc45234bf</url>
  <urlname>When is Marble not Marble? : S4 Government Buildings by pommieparkin2</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99000414" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>When is Marble not Marble? : S4 Government Buildings</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>pommieparkin2</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">pommieparkin2</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;When is Marble not Marble?&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Government Buildings&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0bac773d-b432-4ef7-ae47-b7abc45234bf"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0bac773d-b432-4ef7-ae47-b7abc45234bf&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the manufacturers serial number?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/44e52217-3e22-4043-a522-daab31fefdf6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Government Building is possibly the most impressive architecture in Marble Bar. Built of local stone in 1895, it still provides accommodation for Government Departments.
Amongst these are the Police Station, Mines Department and the Courthouse.
We thoroughly enjoyed our visit to the Museum which is run by a very knowledgeable local lady. It's well worth the visit and is open from 8am to 2pm. Monday to Saturday &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d9516bbc-31e7-4aa7-9c2d-cb381945d5c0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Marble Bar has earned the reputation as Australia's hottest town by experiencing consistently high temperatures during summer months when the mercury climbs to over 38 degrees for days on end.
The record is 160 consecutive days over 38.7 degrees recorded in the sweltering summer of 1923-24.
An extraordinary colourfully Jasper Bar crosses the Coongan River. Unfortunately this Bar was mistakenly identified as Marble giving rise to the town's name. Somehow Jasper Bar just doesn't have the same ring to it!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done. That's another one completed&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-21.171483" lon="119.744583">
  <ele>178.0</ele>
