  <name>LBentd-03</name>
  <desc>WhenIsMarbleNo3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0bac773d-b432-4ef7-ae47-b7abc45234bf</url>
  <urlname>When is Marble not Marble? : S3 Ironclad Hotel by pommieparkin2</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99000412" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>When is Marble not Marble? : S3 Ironclad Hotel</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>pommieparkin2</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">pommieparkin2</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;When is Marble not Marble?&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Ironclad Hotel&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0bac773d-b432-4ef7-ae47-b7abc45234bf"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0bac773d-b432-4ef7-ae47-b7abc45234bf&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How much was a 7oz glass of beer during WWII.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e515cd8e-bbb7-48ff-8f86-c4311e5a9461" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Ironclad Hotel has been part of the Marble Bar social life since 1893. The name Ironclad is likely named after the Ironclad lease granted in 1891, and was the richest claim in the area at that time. Completed in 1892, the Ironclad Hotel had two rooms and a bar. Over the next decade the Ironclad continued to expand and change proprietors.
In 1914 new proprietors constructed a new building which was considered to be the most modern bar in the North West. 
During WWII the Ironclad was a rare but welcome change for RAAF troops based at Corunna Downs.
It was under the same owner for 60 years until it was sold by George Miles in 1966.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d9516bbc-31e7-4aa7-9c2d-cb381945d5c0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Marble Bar has earned the reputation as Australia's hottest town by experiencing consistently high temperatures during summer months when the mercury climbs to over 38 degrees for days on end.
The record is 160 consecutive days over 38.7 degrees recorded in the sweltering summer of 1923-24.
An extraordinary colourfully Jasper Bar crosses the Coongan River. Unfortunately this Bar was mistakenly identified as Marble giving rise to the town's name. Somehow Jasper Bar just doesn't have the same ring to it!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Another correct answer. You are doing a great job?&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
