   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;When is Marble not Marble?&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Silhouettes &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0bac773d-b432-4ef7-ae47-b7abc45234bf"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0bac773d-b432-4ef7-ae47-b7abc45234bf&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is hanging off the wheelbarrow &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c824ddd3-b975-4d80-9891-86869ed151a5" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Not too shabby an entry statement is it? Well we like it!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d9516bbc-31e7-4aa7-9c2d-cb381945d5c0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Marble Bar has earned the reputation as Australia's hottest town by experiencing consistently high temperatures during summer months when the mercury climbs to over 38 degrees for days on end.
The record is 160 consecutive days over 38.7 degrees recorded in the sweltering summer of 1923-24.
An extraordinary colourfully Jasper Bar crosses the Coongan River. Unfortunately this Bar was mistakenly identified as Marble giving rise to the town's name. Somehow Jasper Bar just doesn't have the same ring to it!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations that's correct&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
