 <wpt lat="-33.31825" lon="115.635983">
  <ele>24.0</ele>
  <time>2021-10-10T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBBq4i-01</name>
  <desc>RSHPS1MarlstonH</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/91e60a96-a610-4881-8d81-0500d6c563b5</url>
  <urlname>[L] Roundabouts, Sculptures, and high points : S1 Marlston Hill Lookout by LAXA</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918628" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] Roundabouts, Sculptures, and high points : S1 Marlston Hill Lookout</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>LAXA</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">LAXA</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Roundabouts, Sculptures, and high points&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Marlston Hill Lookout &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/91e60a96-a610-4881-8d81-0500d6c563b5"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/91e60a96-a610-4881-8d81-0500d6c563b5&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Look for the plaque at the bottom of the stairs.  This  Tower was officially opened by ?????? ????? M.L.A. B.E.d.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/063b083d-020a-4084-8cee-ccf752e44058" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Marlston Hill Lookout is one of the best locations to enjoy sweeping views of the City of Bunbury. From the top, you can enjoy a 360-degree outlook of the City of Three Waters including Bunbury Harbour and Koombana Bay.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/61bb6502-37b6-4311-96ed-7401fe9c8920" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to Bunbury's first Adventure labcache.

This little tour of a little under 2 km will take you to some interesting artwork and spectacular views. 
Please note: there is no bonus cache as we are too far to maintain one.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/eaf7907d-94d1-4dc4-a187-418554915501" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done. Now go to the top and enjoy the view&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-33.32325" lon="115.637017">
  <ele>17.0</ele>
  <time>2021-10-10T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBBq4i-02</name>
  <desc>RSHPS2GatewaySc</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/91e60a96-a610-4881-8d81-0500d6c563b5</url>
  <urlname>[L] Roundabouts, Sculptures, and high points : S2 Gateway sculpture by LAXA</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918630" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] Roundabouts, Sculptures, and high points : S2 Gateway sculpture</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>LAXA</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">LAXA</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Roundabouts, Sculptures, and high points&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Gateway sculpture&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/91e60a96-a610-4881-8d81-0500d6c563b5"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/91e60a96-a610-4881-8d81-0500d6c563b5&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the sculptor (plaque on the sculpture)?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d9ee551d-6d02-492a-9f2d-f0b4820cd8f3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Bunbury is a medium sized coastal town approximately 175kms south of the State capital of Perth. In the town center, on a traffic roundabout, you will find this abstract sculpture.
It represents a boat and waves, and was constructed to commemorate the memory of a Bunbury resident.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/61bb6502-37b6-4311-96ed-7401fe9c8920" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to Bunbury's first Adventure labcache.

This little tour of a little under 2 km will take you to some interesting artwork and spectacular views. 
Please note: there is no bonus cache as we are too far to maintain one.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6d1f8ee5-5f85-475c-a17c-b8da23212273" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done, watch out for the cars&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-33.324333" lon="115.63695">
  <ele>9.0</ele>
  <time>2021-10-10T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBBq4i-03</name>
  <desc>RSHPS3BrotherSi</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/91e60a96-a610-4881-8d81-0500d6c563b5</url>
  <urlname>[L] Roundabouts, Sculptures, and high points : S3 Brother &amp; Sister Sculpture by LAXA</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918632" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] Roundabouts, Sculptures, and high points : S3 Brother &amp; Sister Sculpture</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>LAXA</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">LAXA</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Roundabouts, Sculptures, and high points&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Brother &amp; Sister Sculpture&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/91e60a96-a610-4881-8d81-0500d6c563b5"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/91e60a96-a610-4881-8d81-0500d6c563b5&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What animal can you find between 'Brother &amp; Sister'?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/980f2ab6-2d0c-4377-9eb9-806558c9fbf1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Two sandstone figures sunning themselves on a concrete base in the middle of the main street of Bunbury. The two figures seem blissfully unaware that they are naked amongst the shoppers and holiday makers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/61bb6502-37b6-4311-96ed-7401fe9c8920" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to Bunbury's first Adventure labcache.

This little tour of a little under 2 km will take you to some interesting artwork and spectacular views. 
Please note: there is no bonus cache as we are too far to maintain one.
