 <wpt lat="-33.95055" lon="115.0716">
  <ele>98.0</ele>
  <time>2021-10-17T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBRDhz-01</name>
  <desc>MargS1OldHospit</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/aa57e288-e927-4359-addb-d35433e3c51e</url>
  <urlname>European settlement in Margaret River : S1 Old Hospital by papillon367</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99000457" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>European settlement in Margaret River : S1 Old Hospital</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>papillon367</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">papillon367</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;European settlement in Margaret River&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Old Hospital&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/aa57e288-e927-4359-addb-d35433e3c51e"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/aa57e288-e927-4359-addb-d35433e3c51e&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What implement is attached to the Soup Kitchen board next to the bowl? (1 word)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8a96f81b-4db0-4c87-9ca3-3a8a5a91ecf0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The influx of Group Settlers to the Margaret River region in the 1920s created a need for medical services as at the time the nearest medical assistance was in Busselton.
Settlers were asked to contribute one shilling a week towards a medical scheme to help fund provision of a doctor. Dr Rigby arrived in 1923 and plans were started for a weatherboard cottage hospital.
The hospital was built by May 1924. In 1929, extra nurses’ accommodation and the Margaret Cecil Rest House were built and the 1930s saw a new dining room, extra nurses’ bathroom, operating theatre and sterilising facilities added.
In the 1960s, the need for a new hospital was recognised and the Hospital Amenities Committee, community groups and the Shire Council began lobbying the government in a process that would take almost 30 years. Building started on the new hospital in 1989. The old hospital is now being used as a Community Centre.

The coordinates are taking you to the "Soup Kitchen".&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7e6fef59-0fbc-4337-9fb8-20eeee93f9ed" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Wadandi Noongar people are the traditional landowners of this part of the South West region of WA. A group of white settlers established the town of Augusta near Cape Leeuwin in the 1830s and the Margaret River was named in the late 1830s after early settler John Bussell’s step-second-cousin Margaret Whicher.
It wasn’t until 1912 that Margaret River started to be built, with three houses constructed in what is today regarded as the town site. 
This Adventure Lab will take you to some of the European settlement sites in and around Margaret River. Most of the information for this AL was sourced from the website of the Margaret River &amp; Districts Historical Society. 
There is more to discover in the area so please visit their website for further information: https://mrdhs.com.au/locations-margaret-river
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/12fb3a01-30be-4c44-9d10-f24281a865c7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done, now onto the next location!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-33.952583" lon="115.070067">
  <ele>100.0</ele>
  <time>2021-10-17T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBRDhz-05</name>
  <desc>MargS5HomeOfMCD</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/aa57e288-e927-4359-addb-d35433e3c51e</url>
  <urlname>European settlement in Margaret River : S5 Home of M.C. Davies by papillon367</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99000465" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>European settlement in Margaret River : S5 Home of M.C. Davies</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>papillon367</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">papillon367</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;European settlement in Margaret River&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Home of M.C. Davies&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/aa57e288-e927-4359-addb-d35433e3c51e"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/aa57e288-e927-4359-addb-d35433e3c51e&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;In what year was the current business established?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/55c90863-f542-4ee8-90a5-edbfe2699217" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This home was built in 1885 by timber king Maurice Coleman Davies at Karridale and relocated to Margaret River in the 1950s.
Not only did MC Davies bring roads, rail and safe ports to the region, he exported five of his six sons to open trading offices on each continent (the sixth remained as manager).
Global demand for Margaret River hardwood was booming in the 1880s and Davies, who’d made his money supplying building materials during the gold rush while in South Australia, had the means to get it to market where others had tried and failed. So revered was jarrah that it was used to pave the streets of London and Paris!
The building had quite a journey in its 134-year history. In the 1950s the front section was moved to Farrelly St in Margaret River as a convent school and later sold privately. There it remains today as the main building of the Margaret River Motel.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7e6fef59-0fbc-4337-9fb8-20eeee93f9ed" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Wadandi Noongar people are the traditional landowners of this part of the South West region of WA. A group of white settlers established the town of Augusta near Cape Leeuwin in the 1830s and the Margaret River was named in the late 1830s after early settler John Bussell’s step-second-cousin Margaret Whicher.
It wasn’t until 1912 that Margaret River started to be built, with three houses constructed in what is today regarded as the town site. 
This Adventure Lab will take you to some of the European settlement sites in and around Margaret River. Most of the information for this AL was sourced from the website of the Margaret River &amp; Districts Historical Society. 
There is more to discover in the area so please visit their website for further information: https://mrdhs.com.au/locations-margaret-river
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/32e9d1ce-75c6-4752-92e4-46678ab8df23" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done, now onto the next location!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
