   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;European settlement in Margaret River&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;St Margaret's Anglican Church&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/aa57e288-e927-4359-addb-d35433e3c51e"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/aa57e288-e927-4359-addb-d35433e3c51e&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many tall windows are there on the Southern wall of the church? (number)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0c72a8c1-8b8a-43fe-a3e3-21ab797bcb52" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The church, rectory and parish hall were built by local craftsmen Arthur and Leslie Mann in 1926. It was dedicated to Saint Margaret of Scotland by Bishop Wilson on 30th January, 1927. St Margaret is the Patron Saint of wives. Queen of Scotland, she died in 1093 and was canonized in 1250.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7e6fef59-0fbc-4337-9fb8-20eeee93f9ed" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Wadandi Noongar people are the traditional landowners of this part of the South West region of WA. A group of white settlers established the town of Augusta near Cape Leeuwin in the 1830s and the Margaret River was named in the late 1830s after early settler John Bussell’s step-second-cousin Margaret Whicher.
It wasn’t until 1912 that Margaret River started to be built, with three houses constructed in what is today regarded as the town site. 
This Adventure Lab will take you to some of the European settlement sites in and around Margaret River. Most of the information for this AL was sourced from the website of the Margaret River &amp; Districts Historical Society. 
There is more to discover in the area so please visit their website for further information: https://mrdhs.com.au/locations-margaret-river
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/97a6df6f-a12a-435d-9e39-1a75dd9f626e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done, now onto the next location!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
