  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476910057" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Margaret River Adventure : S4 Western Grey Kangaroos of Kevill Road</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>PilotJen</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">PilotJen</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Margaret River Adventure&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Western Grey Kangaroos of Kevill Road&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9aeac2a1-be3c-4a3f-aa80-fdf1eb57926d"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9aeac2a1-be3c-4a3f-aa80-fdf1eb57926d&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What are the first 2 digits of the Western Power pole number after the letter S?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e24b2008-4eda-4196-abe7-d15f7bc3b611" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Grey Kangaroos are sometimes hard to see in Margaret River but on this this special road they are a plenty. PLEASE DRIVE SLOWLY as they are often just relaxing near the side of the road. Several large properties have made their land Kangaroo friendly. I have never driven down this road and not seen a Grey Kangaroo. Please respect the owners and do not trespass onto their property. You can see plenty of roos from the road. Enjoy this special place. 

The western grey kangaroo is not found in the north or the far southeast of Australia, and the eastern grey does not extend beyond the New South Wales–South Australia border, but the two species are both common in the Murray–Darling basin area. They never interbreed in the wild, although it has proved possible to produce hybrids between eastern grey females and western grey males in captivity. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/cf9f9c76-bdd7-4cbc-9cf6-1dafe9694e41" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This lab will take you to well known areas of Margaret River and areas that tourists rarely notice or visit. You will see kangaroos and a small waterfall at the end of this lab if you start at the visitor centre. 

This lab is not a long one, but it will be fun. Enjoy! &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-33.649867" lon="115.331083">
  <ele>8.0</ele>
  <time>2021-10-29T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBZDMB-05</name>
  <desc>SpookyNightsAN5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0361894f-c546-409c-bcfe-ba493ba0c7db</url>
  <urlname>Spooky Nights - A NIGHT ADVENTURE LAB : S5 Meet the Ghost of the Old York Hospital by pood</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99000466" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Spooky Nights - A NIGHT ADVENTURE LAB : S5 Meet the Ghost of the Old York Hospital</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>pood</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">pood</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Spooky Nights - A NIGHT ADVENTURE LAB&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Meet the Ghost of the Old York Hospital&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0361894f-c546-409c-bcfe-ba493ba0c7db"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0361894f-c546-409c-bcfe-ba493ba0c7db&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What direction is the reflector pointing?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/34075222-ce79-463a-bff6-e52a24ac563c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;I am the Ghost of the Old York Hospital, no-one knows my name.
I am a shadowy figure who will make you feel uneasy if you enter my domain.
It is said, many paranormal activites occur within the walls of the old York hospital.
The Matron was right to say there were hauntings here.
The Nurses, when they were on duty, only went upstairs to the Wards in pairs, 
they never went alone.
The building was later used as a camp hostel, on occasions the camp supervisors have said they saw jugs levitating and move across the hall, it fell, crashed and broke into many pieces. 
I held the door handle, I turned the door knob, the door slammed shut.
If someone could find out my name, I might Rest In Peace.
Stand at this waypoint, and shine your torch around.

After you have answered the question, you might like to sit and reflect 
on what my name may have been. 
Maybe even suggest a ghostly name for me in your log.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9df66400-852a-4297-98be-99c72d2b8f83" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Western Australia has a number of Haunted Buildings.
Do you belive in the paranormal? 
Maybe this Adventure Lab will change your thoughts.
Unusual sightings, cold pockets of air, or sudden movements of objects for no apparent reason, unusual noises such as knocking or footsteps. 
There have been many reports at a few known locations around Western Australia.
Busselton hasn't been known as one of the famous haunted locations.
Have you experienced any activity or what is your theory, please include these in your logs.
This Adventure is from the Ghosts Point of View,
now it is time to get into the Spirit of things and meet your first Ghost.

This is a NIGHT TIME Adventure Lab.
It is a short walk around Lou Western Oval, 
and you WILL NEED a TORCH to find the answers to the questions.
ENSURE YOU ARE WITHIN 10 METRES OF THE WAYPOINTS TO FIND THE REFLECTORS.
ENJOY.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congrats on finding the lonley old ghost, who is in spirit at York.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-33.650967" lon="115.330167">
