  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99000458" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Spooky Nights - A NIGHT ADVENTURE LAB : S1 Meet Timothy from Vasse</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>pood</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">pood</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Spooky Nights - A NIGHT ADVENTURE LAB&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Meet Timothy from Vasse&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0361894f-c546-409c-bcfe-ba493ba0c7db"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0361894f-c546-409c-bcfe-ba493ba0c7db&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;I lost my bearing when I fell from my ship into the surf. What is the bearing? (numbers only)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6079132b-a330-4238-a88f-14d78a3dbcd2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;I am Timothy Thomas Vasse, I was a French Sailor who was lost in the surf at Wonnerup. Some stories say I had not drowned, I survived and was looked after kindly by the 
local Wardandi People. 
The local Wardandi People left on a hunting trip, upon their return, they found my remains on the beach.
You may visit the site my ship pulled up to at Wonnerup and see where I was lost in the surf.
During the calm Summer days, there are plenty of people enjoying the surf where I was lost overboard.
I have been remembered by the Vasse River and the new township of Vasse.
I hope you get to see my statue out in the new town of Vasse.
Stand at the waypoint, and shine your torch around to find the reflector, here you will find the answer.

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9df66400-852a-4297-98be-99c72d2b8f83" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Western Australia has a number of Haunted Buildings.
Do you belive in the paranormal? 
Maybe this Adventure Lab will change your thoughts.
Unusual sightings, cold pockets of air, or sudden movements of objects for no apparent reason, unusual noises such as knocking or footsteps. 
There have been many reports at a few known locations around Western Australia.
Busselton hasn't been known as one of the famous haunted locations.
Have you experienced any activity or what is your theory, please include these in your logs.
This Adventure is from the Ghosts Point of View,
now it is time to get into the Spirit of things and meet your first Ghost.

This is a NIGHT TIME Adventure Lab.
It is a short walk around Lou Western Oval, 
and you WILL NEED a TORCH to find the answers to the questions.
ENSURE YOU ARE WITHIN 10 METRES OF THE WAYPOINTS TO FIND THE REFLECTORS.
ENJOY.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congrats on Finding Timothy&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
