  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99000462" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Spooky Nights - A NIGHT ADVENTURE LAB : S3 Meet Maria at the Abbey in New Norcia</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>pood</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">pood</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Spooky Nights - A NIGHT ADVENTURE LAB&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Meet Maria at the Abbey in New Norcia&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0361894f-c546-409c-bcfe-ba493ba0c7db"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0361894f-c546-409c-bcfe-ba493ba0c7db&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Possums are nocturnal, they live in the Peppi Trees, native to Australia. What 3 trees can you see, are from the Northern Hemisphere?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/05f7a44c-9fd1-4154-ae7b-463f049d63e7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;I am a 26 year old Benedictine Missionary Sister from Spain, in the Northern Hemisphere.
My name is Sister Maria, I am one of the most influential women on staff, and spent 17 years living and teaching traditional Catholicism before becoming gravely ill with cancer.
I wore a blue habit, and my ghost wanders around the clock tower every night at midnight; keeping an eye on the community I cherished for almost two decades.
As Australia’s only monastic town, New Norcia has its fair share of haunted stories, are you coming to visit me?
Stand at this waypoint, shine your torch around to find the reflector, then look for your answer, shining your torch south FROM the reflector, you will see your answer.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9df66400-852a-4297-98be-99c72d2b8f83" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Western Australia has a number of Haunted Buildings.
Do you belive in the paranormal? 
Maybe this Adventure Lab will change your thoughts.
Unusual sightings, cold pockets of air, or sudden movements of objects for no apparent reason, unusual noises such as knocking or footsteps. 
There have been many reports at a few known locations around Western Australia.
Busselton hasn't been known as one of the famous haunted locations.
Have you experienced any activity or what is your theory, please include these in your logs.
This Adventure is from the Ghosts Point of View,
now it is time to get into the Spirit of things and meet your first Ghost.

This is a NIGHT TIME Adventure Lab.
It is a short walk around Lou Western Oval, 
and you WILL NEED a TORCH to find the answers to the questions.
ENSURE YOU ARE WITHIN 10 METRES OF THE WAYPOINTS TO FIND THE REFLECTORS.
ENJOY.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations on finding Sister Maria.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
