   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Hamilton Hill Memorial Hall&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Commemorating the fallen&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/97b81221-05fe-445d-8561-f7a22dbe3ee3"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/97b81221-05fe-445d-8561-f7a22dbe3ee3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;At GZ you will find a sign, who headed the committee? (3 names)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/01f9b7e9-f9c1-4950-8b43-f2b55e1c9514" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Hamilton Hill Association was a highly persuasive committee which was a driving force in fundraising for the halls construction. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/86ff71f5-e2da-4200-9929-9cdcd34ffb91" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Hamilton Hill Memorial Hall was completed and officially opened on 19th July 1925. 

At the end of the 1914-1918 war memorial centographs were being built throughout the state, but the newly formed Hamilton Hill Association looked to built a hall in memory of those who lost their lives. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/516f0c9f-a1c8-40da-99d4-161ca26a7ec4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
