   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Hamilton Hill Memorial Hall&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;War Memorial&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/97b81221-05fe-445d-8561-f7a22dbe3ee3"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/97b81221-05fe-445d-8561-f7a22dbe3ee3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;On the memorial, fill in the blank: The …… dead&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b150fa2d-4a63-4485-9650-e5bb3de84451" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The memorial at the front of the Hamilton Hill Memorial Hall was erected by the residents of Spearwood in 1922. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/86ff71f5-e2da-4200-9929-9cdcd34ffb91" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Hamilton Hill Memorial Hall was completed and officially opened on 19th July 1925. 

At the end of the 1914-1918 war memorial centographs were being built throughout the state, but the newly formed Hamilton Hill Association looked to built a hall in memory of those who lost their lives. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8f209515-f4bf-483a-950d-d4473f5598a2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
