   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Hamilton Hill Memorial Hall&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Lest We Forget&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/97b81221-05fe-445d-8561-f7a22dbe3ee3"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/97b81221-05fe-445d-8561-f7a22dbe3ee3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;On the plaque fill in the missing word: Honour the ……. Living &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4251e0ec-a1a7-4d83-9a84-fd753ee71398" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;At the front of the Hamilton Hill Memorial Hall is stone laid by Mrs W.M. Winfield in honour of those who took part in the Great War 1914-1918&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/86ff71f5-e2da-4200-9929-9cdcd34ffb91" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Hamilton Hill Memorial Hall was completed and officially opened on 19th July 1925. 

At the end of the 1914-1918 war memorial centographs were being built throughout the state, but the newly formed Hamilton Hill Association looked to built a hall in memory of those who lost their lives. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1da0e163-c82e-454b-8b37-eac38feb5eaf" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
