   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Discover Pemberton&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Pemberton Hotel&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/91b9475f-dbd0-439d-b7bd-883bc8bfa5a9"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/91b9475f-dbd0-439d-b7bd-883bc8bfa5a9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name on the Pemberton Hotel Fascade (look up)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0f15f295-ce5a-4383-9080-74d8546fbdf4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Pemberton Hotel was originally built in Greenbushes in the early 1900's and known as the Courthouse Hotel.   In February 1926 an application was granted for the transfer of the license from Greenbushes to Pemberton.  The Pemberton Hotel was opened in April 1926 re-built from materials transported from the former Courthouse Hotel site in Greenbushes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4595632c-5318-4829-ae8b-01b558120734" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Pemberton is known for it's tall karri trees. There are a couple of fire lookout trees in the region you can still climb - Gloucester Tree and Dave Evans Bicentennial Tree. The area has some beautiful landscapes and popular for photographers. Having been a regular visitor to the town for 40 years - I encourage you to discover it for yourself.

Please note: There is paid entry to Gloucester Tree.
$15 National Parks Day Pass - per car
$8 Concession (or Motorbike) National Park Day Pass&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
