   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Sculpture by the Sea&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Converse&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0cc4a3da-595a-41a3-be90-0042addb0066"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0cc4a3da-595a-41a3-be90-0042addb0066&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What are the names of the two artists?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/80bdfdc4-3e4c-48fb-9cf0-095538aab3cc" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;An interactive piece to encourage you to consider your relationship with nature.

Even though the area is often very busy with people sitting around on the grass you can usually find this seat free. Nice shady spot too :)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/abb4eb2a-8ff8-4016-883e-b279e2019ff2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Sculpture by the Sea started in Bondi in 1997 and quickly grew to become one of Sydney's most popular annual events. The popularity of the Bondi event led to the creation of a Cottesloe event in 2005 - which is now enjoyed by around 250,000 visitors annually.

The event is free and each event showcases around 70 sculptures. The exhibition is featured from the sea wall all the way along the sand towards North Cottesloe and on the surrounding grassed areas creating a beautiful sculpture park.

The 18th Annual Cottesloe Exhibition is scheduled for 4-21 March 2022.

The public can commission and buy sculptures, and since the first Cottesloe exhibition the Town of Cottesloe has also regularly purchased sculptures for ongoing public display.

This Adventure Lab takes you to a few of the permanent sculptures along a 2km stretch of coast - perfect for a nice walk, cycle, drive, skateboard, scooter or hoverboard.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done.

The tree sitting here will have a bird's eye view of any future Indiana redevelopments!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
