   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Sculpture by the Sea&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Centrefold&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0cc4a3da-595a-41a3-be90-0042addb0066"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0cc4a3da-595a-41a3-be90-0042addb0066&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;When was this sculpture purchased?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/debe1b9f-3adb-4718-890e-827c847a0967" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The circular nature of this sculpture lends to some great photo framing opportunities.

Made from aluminium and black oxide.

The inaugural sculpture purchased (entitled 'Four Pots') can be found in the grounds of the nearby Civic Centre. Feel free to divert there along Napier Street if time allows however please note the gates to the grounds close at 5pm daily (hence not included in this AL trail).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/abb4eb2a-8ff8-4016-883e-b279e2019ff2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Sculpture by the Sea started in Bondi in 1997 and quickly grew to become one of Sydney's most popular annual events. The popularity of the Bondi event led to the creation of a Cottesloe event in 2005 - which is now enjoyed by around 250,000 visitors annually.

The event is free and each event showcases around 70 sculptures. The exhibition is featured from the sea wall all the way along the sand towards North Cottesloe and on the surrounding grassed areas creating a beautiful sculpture park.

The 18th Annual Cottesloe Exhibition is scheduled for 4-21 March 2022.

The public can commission and buy sculptures, and since the first Cottesloe exhibition the Town of Cottesloe has also regularly purchased sculptures for ongoing public display.

This Adventure Lab takes you to a few of the permanent sculptures along a 2km stretch of coast - perfect for a nice walk, cycle, drive, skateboard, scooter or hoverboard.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done.

A reminder if you're considering a diversion to the Civic Centre - gates close at 5pm daily.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
