 <wpt lat="-31.986" lon="115.752867">
  <ele>13.0</ele>
  <time>2021-12-30T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBtL9j-01</name>
  <desc>SculptureByThe1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0cc4a3da-595a-41a3-be90-0042addb0066</url>
  <urlname>Sculpture by the Sea : S1 Untitled Free Form by Barco</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99001486" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Sculpture by the Sea : S1 Untitled Free Form</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Barco</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Barco</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Sculpture by the Sea&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Untitled Free Form&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0cc4a3da-595a-41a3-be90-0042addb0066"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0cc4a3da-595a-41a3-be90-0042addb0066&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The artist comes from which country?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8032f66f-d0c0-4e1c-b3a0-5e1f8bf4abe8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Sculpture (and art is general) is a very personal thing - some will love and others hate the very same piece.

I like this one as the steel free form reminds me of the way I used to try and bend my Scalextric as a kid!

This sculpture was donated to the Town by the Bernadt Family. Maybe they had a Scalextric set too :)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/abb4eb2a-8ff8-4016-883e-b279e2019ff2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Sculpture by the Sea started in Bondi in 1997 and quickly grew to become one of Sydney's most popular annual events. The popularity of the Bondi event led to the creation of a Cottesloe event in 2005 - which is now enjoyed by around 250,000 visitors annually.

The event is free and each event showcases around 70 sculptures. The exhibition is featured from the sea wall all the way along the sand towards North Cottesloe and on the surrounding grassed areas creating a beautiful sculpture park.

The 18th Annual Cottesloe Exhibition is scheduled for 4-21 March 2022.

The public can commission and buy sculptures, and since the first Cottesloe exhibition the Town of Cottesloe has also regularly purchased sculptures for ongoing public display.

This Adventure Lab takes you to a few of the permanent sculptures along a 2km stretch of coast - perfect for a nice walk, cycle, drive, skateboard, scooter or hoverboard.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done. 

Look out for some other sculptures in the area, including one at the entrance to Grant Marine Park opposite.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.304267" lon="115.701817">
  <ele>2.0</ele>
  <time>2021-12-30T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBKZyP-01</name>
  <desc>PenguinIslandE1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/aba5d9c4-6600-4b5c-aa21-a410b5bb18bc</url>
  <urlname>Penguin Island Exploration : S1 Penguin Island ferry by KatieAndLucy</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99001496" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Penguin Island Exploration : S1 Penguin Island ferry</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>KatieAndLucy</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">KatieAndLucy</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Penguin Island Exploration&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Penguin Island ferry&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/aba5d9c4-6600-4b5c-aa21-a410b5bb18bc"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/aba5d9c4-6600-4b5c-aa21-a410b5bb18bc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many silver bench-chairs are here for waiting ferry passengers? (numeral)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8deca33e-ae4c-4864-be63-30f51dbdfe8c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Begin your exploration of the island by boarding the ferry. Tickets can be bought online https://www.penguinisland.com.au/ or by visiting the booking kiosk. Depending on the tide, some locals like to walk across the exposed sandbar to the island. While you might avoid the ferry and park fees this way, it can be extremely dangerous with steep drop offs and quick-changing conditions. Walking the sandbar is --not recommended--. People have come to unfortunate ends doing so. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/162d10de-e12d-41ef-b117-3f138b8d85f1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Located in the Shoalwater Islands Marine Park, Penguin Island is home to colonies of pelicans, terns, gulls, and of course Little Penguins. Over the years, the penguin population has been hit hard by human activity such as hunting, as well as introduced animals such as dogs and rabbits, and only a few hundred now remain. Today, Penguin Island's penguins are protected from these threats by the park's rules, appropriate facilities, and conservation work. However, they are still under threat from the broader problems of climate change and habitat damage, as well as human activity such as fishing and boating. To complete this AL, you will be heading to the island on the ferry. The ferry prices and park fees can be found at https://www.penguinisland.com.au/&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done! Don't forget to look out for dolphins on your ride over to the island!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.304167" lon="115.6906">
  <ele>3.0</ele>
  <time>2021-12-30T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBKZyP-03</name>
  <desc>PenguinIslandE3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/aba5d9c4-6600-4b5c-aa21-a410b5bb18bc</url>
  <urlname>Penguin Island Exploration : S3 Beach hangouts by KatieAndLucy</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99001500" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Penguin Island Exploration : S3 Beach hangouts</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>KatieAndLucy</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">KatieAndLucy</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Penguin Island Exploration&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Beach hangouts&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/aba5d9c4-6600-4b5c-aa21-a410b5bb18bc"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/aba5d9c4-6600-4b5c-aa21-a410b5bb18bc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the brand of the item pictured on the 'McKenzie's Well' board?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b04881dd-19fb-4343-8a1b-70e0db21f058" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;There are lots of gorgeous spots to spend some time paddling in the water and relaxing on the beach. Look carefully (from a distance) in some of the caves - you might spot some of the wild penguins hanging out in the shade. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/162d10de-e12d-41ef-b117-3f138b8d85f1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Located in the Shoalwater Islands Marine Park, Penguin Island is home to colonies of pelicans, terns, gulls, and of course Little Penguins. Over the years, the penguin population has been hit hard by human activity such as hunting, as well as introduced animals such as dogs and rabbits, and only a few hundred now remain. Today, Penguin Island's penguins are protected from these threats by the park's rules, appropriate facilities, and conservation work. However, they are still under threat from the broader problems of climate change and habitat damage, as well as human activity such as fishing and boating. To complete this AL, you will be heading to the island on the ferry. The ferry prices and park fees can be found at https://www.penguinisland.com.au/&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3ff23956-86ee-44c0-9695-d32eb8e7f91d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Good job! Take your time, there's no rush. It's so nice to lay on the beach or paddle in the clear waters here!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.3055" lon="115.691817">
  <ele>4.0</ele>
