  <name>LBKZyP-02</name>
  <desc>PenguinIslandE2</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/aba5d9c4-6600-4b5c-aa21-a410b5bb18bc</url>
  <urlname>Penguin Island Exploration : S2 Discovery Centre by KatieAndLucy</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99001498" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Penguin Island Exploration : S2 Discovery Centre</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>KatieAndLucy</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">KatieAndLucy</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Penguin Island Exploration&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Discovery Centre&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/aba5d9c4-6600-4b5c-aa21-a410b5bb18bc"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/aba5d9c4-6600-4b5c-aa21-a410b5bb18bc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Looking at the board titled 'For the Birds', which bird is pictured with eggs?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e1f3828d-afa2-4e39-832b-a651cffb69cb" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Here at the Discovery Centre, you can visit the 10 Little Penguins which have been rescued over the years but which are not suitable for release. Jerry the penguin was rescued 25 years ago. After being blinded in one eye by a fishing hook, she wouldn't have survived in the wild. Now she and the other rescued penguins act as ambassadors for the island, and conservation in general. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/162d10de-e12d-41ef-b117-3f138b8d85f1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Located in the Shoalwater Islands Marine Park, Penguin Island is home to colonies of pelicans, terns, gulls, and of course Little Penguins. Over the years, the penguin population has been hit hard by human activity such as hunting, as well as introduced animals such as dogs and rabbits, and only a few hundred now remain. Today, Penguin Island's penguins are protected from these threats by the park's rules, appropriate facilities, and conservation work. However, they are still under threat from the broader problems of climate change and habitat damage, as well as human activity such as fishing and boating. To complete this AL, you will be heading to the island on the ferry. The ferry prices and park fees can be found at https://www.penguinisland.com.au/&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/57a64e39-5956-4f59-a8a6-15e3f48a2d18" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Nice one! Maybe you'll be able to spot some of these birds as you walk around the island. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
