  <desc>GERALDTONFORES5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/fc29b1a0-e5af-4d53-94aa-2463ff375afc</url>
  <urlname>GERALDTON FORESHORE WANDERING  : S5 Geraldton museum by OOH YEH</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-584" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>GERALDTON FORESHORE WANDERING  : S5 Geraldton museum</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>OOH YEH</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">OOH YEH</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;GERALDTON FORESHORE WANDERING &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Geraldton museum &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/fc29b1a0-e5af-4d53-94aa-2463ff375afc"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/fc29b1a0-e5af-4d53-94aa-2463ff375afc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year was the propeller raised&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8cba74ae-4973-4102-832f-cb483a3b5603" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Overlooking the Indian Ocean, the Museum of Geraldton celebrates the rich heritage of the land, sea and people of the Mid West region.
Discover ancient landforms, Yamaji history and culture, and the region’s unique natural landscapes and marine environment.
The archaeological riches from four Dutch shipwrecks - Batavia, Gilt Dragon, Zuytdorp, and Zeewijk, are revealed in the Shipwrecks Gallery. Visitors can join a guided highlights tour available daily at 11.30am.
Witness the wrecks of HMAS Sydney (II) and HSK Kormoran
as they currently lie, 2,500 metres deep on the ocean floor,
in From Great Depths, a moving exhibit and 3D film. 
Hint

You need to find a very large propeller outside &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0b1ae1a8-e434-452a-a142-a01c2a4c5571" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to Geraldton foreshore.
Here you can find many activities for the young and old . I recommend you start at one end and work your way to the other . There is plenty of parking along the way . 
In 2007, the Geraldton foreshore area, previously an abandoned railway marshalling yard, was redeveloped and today hosts a playground with water activities, public green spaces, public beaches, picnic areas, basketball court and shaded play areas. The project was completed in 2008.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/be0dd6c9-7777-4c09-bf9e-8497f3586053" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
