 <wpt lat="-32.042883" lon="115.755267">
  <ele>13.0</ele>
  <time>2022-01-21T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBRvmA-01</name>
  <desc>FremantleStree1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/4a778b59-dd0e-4287-b03f-ae3763290ff9</url>
  <urlname>Fremantle Street Art : S1 The Kraken by Gumnut6160</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99001504" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Fremantle Street Art : S1 The Kraken</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Gumnut6160</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Gumnut6160</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Fremantle Street Art&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Kraken&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/4a778b59-dd0e-4287-b03f-ae3763290ff9"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/4a778b59-dd0e-4287-b03f-ae3763290ff9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;In front of the mural is a traffic light controller box. What is the 3 digit number located on the box?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7a9f410e-da3d-421a-8a8e-d5a21df63829" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Painted by world renowned British artist Phlegm in 2015, the kraken is spray painted onto the side of the old Fremantle navy store building.
Phlegm, known for his black and white characters, typically targets and transforms run down urban spaces or factories. He feels that rather than being an awkward canvas in an art gallery, the art becomes part of the city’s architecture.
Unfortunately the artwork has been vandalised but it is one of my favourites and worthy of inclusion.

Parking can be a little difficult along here, so you may find it easier to park at Tuckfield Oval on Tuckfield Street, then walk down.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f4f7d8b4-9fc3-421c-b406-e9655e744eb8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fremantle has long been renowned for it’s art culture.
In 2013 Fremantle Council took the unorthodox approach of rewriting it’s blanket ban policy on graffiti for one which preserves artistic work that contributes to the culture and vibrancy of the city. 
The result has been the making of a vibrant, edgy city with a surprise around every corner. 
This Adventure Lab will take you to 5 different street art locations in central Fremantle, some well known, some not so well known.

Don’t forget to collect the clues after each stage to claim the bonus cache at the end 'Fremantle Street Art Bonus Cache' GC9MAQ2.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/958ce6e7-09d3-4a59-b9c6-894b08bf251c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done!
Now, make note of the letter A, you will need this if you are going to find the bonus cache.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.057133" lon="115.74925">
  <ele>8.0</ele>
  <time>2022-01-21T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBRvmA-02</name>
  <desc>FremantleStree2</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/4a778b59-dd0e-4287-b03f-ae3763290ff9</url>
  <urlname>Fremantle Street Art : S2 The Norfolk by Gumnut6160</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99001506" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Fremantle Street Art : S2 The Norfolk</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Gumnut6160</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Gumnut6160</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Fremantle Street Art&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Norfolk &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/4a778b59-dd0e-4287-b03f-ae3763290ff9"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/4a778b59-dd0e-4287-b03f-ae3763290ff9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;On the wall there is a plaque. What is the 3rd word on the plaque? (8 letters)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a3b8e2f9-b1c9-42a7-90c6-c4100940e2d7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Created by Vhils, a Portugese artist, the artwork was commissioned by Fremantle Council in 2013 as part of the Fremantle Street Art Festival.
The artwork, a relief portrait etched into the side of The Norfolk Hotel, features Dame Dorothy Tangney, an Australian personality, a Fremantle resident and first female member of the Australian senate.
Vihls' work often depicts the faces of individuals often unknown within the community.
He creates his artworks by breaking his portraits into 3 colours, then uses these colours to provide depth. He is best known for his use of etching using acid, pneumonic drills, bleach and even explosives.
If you stand at the base of the wall you can see in some areas the initial rough outline in spray paint used to sketch his first design. Pneumonic drill marks are also visible into the plaster and brick which he used to develop the depth needed in the portrait.
Vihls' believes that destruction is a form of construction.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f4f7d8b4-9fc3-421c-b406-e9655e744eb8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fremantle has long been renowned for it’s art culture.
In 2013 Fremantle Council took the unorthodox approach of rewriting it’s blanket ban policy on graffiti for one which preserves artistic work that contributes to the culture and vibrancy of the city. 
The result has been the making of a vibrant, edgy city with a surprise around every corner. 
This Adventure Lab will take you to 5 different street art locations in central Fremantle, some well known, some not so well known.

Don’t forget to collect the clues after each stage to claim the bonus cache at the end 'Fremantle Street Art Bonus Cache' GC9MAQ2.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f6da37fd-f654-4894-80be-132a8c6200ab" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done!
Now, note down the letter M, this will help you if you wish to find the bonus cache at the end.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
