  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/4a778b59-dd0e-4287-b03f-ae3763290ff9</url>
  <urlname>Fremantle Street Art : S4 Numbat by Gumnut6160</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99001510" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Fremantle Street Art : S4 Numbat</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Gumnut6160</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Gumnut6160</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Fremantle Street Art&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Numbat&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/4a778b59-dd0e-4287-b03f-ae3763290ff9"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/4a778b59-dd0e-4287-b03f-ae3763290ff9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;There is a lane opposite the mural. What is it called? (sign on wall, 2 words)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0ac269e2-0827-4127-a208-235f34ab2f6a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Painted in 2012 by Belgian artist ROA, the mural features a numbat, an Australian marsupial.
ROA is known for his strong obsession with animals and rodents and will often paint animals which are endangered or once inhabited the location in which it was painted.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f4f7d8b4-9fc3-421c-b406-e9655e744eb8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fremantle has long been renowned for it’s art culture.
In 2013 Fremantle Council took the unorthodox approach of rewriting it’s blanket ban policy on graffiti for one which preserves artistic work that contributes to the culture and vibrancy of the city. 
The result has been the making of a vibrant, edgy city with a surprise around every corner. 
This Adventure Lab will take you to 5 different street art locations in central Fremantle, some well known, some not so well known.

Don’t forget to collect the clues after each stage to claim the bonus cache at the end 'Fremantle Street Art Bonus Cache' GC9MAQ2.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6e47387b-3aa4-4c67-bb1e-8a88b2972f54" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Great! 
Now jot down the letter L, you will need it if you wish to find the bonus cache at the end.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
