   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Fremantle Street Art&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Horatio's Wall&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/4a778b59-dd0e-4287-b03f-ae3763290ff9"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/4a778b59-dd0e-4287-b03f-ae3763290ff9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the quote written on Horatio's wall? (5 words, above the words 'Horatio's Wall')&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4dbfeae3-104c-4c04-9269-5abb8d6a04c8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Horatio's Wall is an ongoing art work by Fremantle personality Horatio.T. Birdbath who can often be found here making additions to his work.
He has many other mini artworks around the city including the planter boxes and bollards around Market Street and near the wall.
Horatio, a quirky and loveable character started the wall in 2002 and has gradually added to it over the many years and is made using mostly acrylic markers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f4f7d8b4-9fc3-421c-b406-e9655e744eb8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fremantle has long been renowned for it’s art culture.
In 2013 Fremantle Council took the unorthodox approach of rewriting it’s blanket ban policy on graffiti for one which preserves artistic work that contributes to the culture and vibrancy of the city. 
The result has been the making of a vibrant, edgy city with a surprise around every corner. 
This Adventure Lab will take you to 5 different street art locations in central Fremantle, some well known, some not so well known.

Don’t forget to collect the clues after each stage to claim the bonus cache at the end 'Fremantle Street Art Bonus Cache' GC9MAQ2.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8249f77c-b05d-47b4-836d-702425adc3e4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Brilliant!
The letter you will need to find the bonus cache is the letter U.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.057917" lon="115.7429">
