  <name>LBRvmA-03</name>
  <desc>FremantleStree3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/4a778b59-dd0e-4287-b03f-ae3763290ff9</url>
  <urlname>Fremantle Street Art : S3 Too Much Colour by Gumnut6160</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99001508" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Fremantle Street Art : S3 Too Much Colour</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Gumnut6160</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Gumnut6160</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Fremantle Street Art&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Too Much Colour&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/4a778b59-dd0e-4287-b03f-ae3763290ff9"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/4a778b59-dd0e-4287-b03f-ae3763290ff9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is written on the characters arm? (3 words)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d0131858-0d78-45a8-baec-8ab67e08443a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;TMC or Too Much Colour consists of 3 artists who are based here in Perth, Western Australia.
Their artworks can be seen all around Perth and are typically bright and punchy.
This one was created as part of PUBLIC 2015, an art project which saw 45 artists from around the world transform spaces and walls around Perth into an urban canvas.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f4f7d8b4-9fc3-421c-b406-e9655e744eb8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fremantle has long been renowned for it’s art culture.
In 2013 Fremantle Council took the unorthodox approach of rewriting it’s blanket ban policy on graffiti for one which preserves artistic work that contributes to the culture and vibrancy of the city. 
The result has been the making of a vibrant, edgy city with a surprise around every corner. 
This Adventure Lab will take you to 5 different street art locations in central Fremantle, some well known, some not so well known.

Don’t forget to collect the clues after each stage to claim the bonus cache at the end 'Fremantle Street Art Bonus Cache' GC9MAQ2.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ff5f144d-dbaf-4804-bb27-1a89b9e5af43" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;You got it!
Now, note down the letter R. You will need this if you wish to find the bonus cache at the end.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-33.6308" lon="115.338817">
  <ele>-2.0</ele>
  <time>2022-01-27T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBwRvM-05</name>
  <desc>WalkingBusselt5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9ff0b9a3-5e97-4816-aaed-59191a057716</url>
  <urlname>Walking Busselton Jetty : S5 The End .......almost by SVKR_WA</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99001531" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Walking Busselton Jetty : S5 The End .......almost</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>SVKR_WA</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">SVKR_WA</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Walking Busselton Jetty&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The End .......almost&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9ff0b9a3-5e97-4816-aaed-59191a057716"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9ff0b9a3-5e97-4816-aaed-59191a057716&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;On the sign at the top of the ramp, how many lines is a person fishing allowed to operate?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/98c58e21-789f-425c-bf53-c7540ee1c69a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Well, Congratulations, you have reached the end of the jetty, almost.  

If the observatory is open, there will be a little further to walk to be able to claim you truly walked to the end of the jetty, all 1841m.

Look for the ramp leading down to the water.  Is there anyone fishing today?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/414b92a0-1c04-466f-97d0-642f5c5840e8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Busselton Jetty is the longest timber piled jetty in the Southern Hemisphere at 1841m long.  Construction Commenced in 1864 and the first section opened in 1865,  The jetty has been extended numerous times until the 1960s when it reached its current length.

The jetty has survived Cyclone Alby in 1978, insect borers, several fires, extreme weather and the threat of demolition, to now become a major tourist attraction.

The jetty features a railway line along its length and an underwater observatory at the end.

Walking the Jetty has become a "right of passage" for locals, and tourists alike.  There are many fishing spots and places to jump into the water on a hot day. 

There is a small cost to enter the jetty.  Pop into the visitors centre first to book a ticket on the train, or for the observatory.  

You will need to walk at least one way to complete this Adventure Lab&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6df4bb81-ec70-41b2-8e8c-43bb09809157" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Walk to the end of the jetty if you can, marvel at how far you are from the shore.  

Enjoy the trip back......&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
