  <name>LBdWKr-01</name>
  <desc>RavensthorpeHo1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1d7914d0-193b-4a7d-b1fb-c384319741d7</url>
  <urlname>Ravensthorpe Hopetoun  Welcomes You : S1 Ravensthorpe Silo by burns345</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-31" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Ravensthorpe Hopetoun  Welcomes You : S1 Ravensthorpe Silo</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>burns345</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">burns345</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Ravensthorpe Hopetoun  Welcomes You&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Ravensthorpe Silo &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1d7914d0-193b-4a7d-b1fb-c384319741d7"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1d7914d0-193b-4a7d-b1fb-c384319741d7&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many litres of paint was used?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6c372224-4a99-4d70-9dda-cb3b55097dae" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Ravensthorpe silo mural and enjoy the start of this southern Adventure Lab.
Created by Dutch born artist Amok Island who created the six stages of Banksia baxteri along with a New Holland Honeyeater and Honey Possum who are the main pollinators of this banksia species.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/49b5cea4-10b3-4a1e-80ae-1ef79bb21fa4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ravensthorpe is located on Highway 1 (the South Coast Highway) half way between Albany and Esperance
The area was first surveyed by the Western Australia Surveyor General John Septimus Roe in 1848 and he named the local range, the Ravensthorpe Range. Roe named Mount Short after the Bishop Augustus Short of South and Western Australia. 
Hopetoun is a town on the south coast of Western Australia.
Mary Ann Harbour was named in November 1865 by the sealer James Sale on the cutter Mary Ann. 
Hopetoun was established in 1900 as the port servicing the Phillips River goldfield, named after the first Governor-General of Australia, John Hope, 7th Earl of Hopetoun. The townsite was gazetted on 9 February 1901.
The town became a shipping port for the mining industry, with a jetty built in 1901. The railway line between Hopetoun and Ravensthorpe operated from 1909 to 1935. 
Fitzgerald River National Park covers 297,244 ha of coastline between Bremer Bay and Hopetoun. Please visit for the coastline and wildflowers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2d470975-2164-4dfd-8dd9-aea6f81eb3be" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations and welcome to this fantastic area of Western Australia&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
