   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Ravensthorpe Hopetoun  Welcomes You&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Port Hotel&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1d7914d0-193b-4a7d-b1fb-c384319741d7"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1d7914d0-193b-4a7d-b1fb-c384319741d7&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the Cafe - 3 words&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e330faa9-4c98-4561-a5fe-f5269468e20b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Port Hotel Hopetoun was established in 1901 on the esplanade boasting spectacular views of the southern ocean.
It is on Veal Street which was named in honour of Thomas and Sarah Veal.
They were on the way from South Australia to South Africa when the then Government asked them to stay in Hopetoun and operate the local Post Office and General Store.
They had two daughters Hilda Bertha Veal was my grandmother.
Hilda Parsons married George Parsons and had a daughter Sarah Kathleen Sylvia who later married Bevly John Furniss Burns.
The rest is history and the start of my life and family.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/49b5cea4-10b3-4a1e-80ae-1ef79bb21fa4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ravensthorpe is located on Highway 1 (the South Coast Highway) half way between Albany and Esperance
The area was first surveyed by the Western Australia Surveyor General John Septimus Roe in 1848 and he named the local range, the Ravensthorpe Range. Roe named Mount Short after the Bishop Augustus Short of South and Western Australia. 
Hopetoun is a town on the south coast of Western Australia.
Mary Ann Harbour was named in November 1865 by the sealer James Sale on the cutter Mary Ann. 
Hopetoun was established in 1900 as the port servicing the Phillips River goldfield, named after the first Governor-General of Australia, John Hope, 7th Earl of Hopetoun. The townsite was gazetted on 9 February 1901.
The town became a shipping port for the mining industry, with a jetty built in 1901. The railway line between Hopetoun and Ravensthorpe operated from 1909 to 1935. 
Fitzgerald River National Park covers 297,244 ha of coastline between Bremer Bay and Hopetoun. Please visit for the coastline and wildflowers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/25f4d18a-df35-4633-a298-e5550816c6e1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations - This is an old photo of the hotel. Now enjoy the rest of the Add Lab.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
