  <urlname>[L] Australind Bunbury Tourist Drive 260 : S10 Belvidere by West Oz Geocaching</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99002525" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] Australind Bunbury Tourist Drive 260 : S10 Belvidere</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>West Oz Geocaching</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">West Oz Geocaching</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Australind Bunbury Tourist Drive 260&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Belvidere&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0b629cdd-df49-49a1-b896-4727eef727e4"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0b629cdd-df49-49a1-b896-4727eef727e4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the date of the journal of Lt. Henry William St Pierre Bunbury (As written on the information board minus the comma.)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/371564b7-5350-4740-9100-cb08b24344d1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Belvidere has a rich and varied past. Many people have sought food and shelter here including Nyoongars, early settlers, Indian labourers and alternative lifestylers. All these people have shared the ability to be resourceful and inventive to enable them to live in this challenging environment.
Belvidere was one of the first farms established in the South-West. Thomas Little and his labourers began establishing the horse and cattle farm here in 1840 on behalf of their employer, Charles Robert Prinsep of Calcutta.  Little name the homestead and property Belvidere after Charles Prinsep's house in Calcutta.

Learn more about the people of Belvidere here at the infomation shelter and along the nearby walk trail.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9efba563-718e-4429-b417-f748ede82572" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Australind Bunbury Tourist Drive, designated as Tourist Drive 260, is a 14-kilometre-long  historic route from Bunbury to Leschenault via Australind.

There are numerous places of interest along the way and this Adventure Lab will take you to some of them.

Note the numeric answers to some of the questions as they will allow you to find a bonus geocache after completing all stages of this Adventure Lab.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b3d6dba8-ce3f-446d-a8c6-c69b7a89ce8c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations on completing this stage of the bonus cache.

For the bonus cache record the year. (WXYZ)&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
