  <urlname>[L] Australind Bunbury Tourist Drive 260 : S08 Australind Memorial Seat by West Oz Geocaching</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99002521" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] Australind Bunbury Tourist Drive 260 : S08 Australind Memorial Seat</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>West Oz Geocaching</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">West Oz Geocaching</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Australind Bunbury Tourist Drive 260&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Australind Memorial Seat&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0b629cdd-df49-49a1-b896-4727eef727e4"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0b629cdd-df49-49a1-b896-4727eef727e4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the Observatory?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4b197d70-493e-46c6-8940-c43fefe39d3a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Australind Settlement (on Wakefield Principles) was formed in 1841 on the eastern side of Leschenault Inlet by the Western Australian Company.

A town site of 1000 acres was surveyed and the division of 100,000 acres into small farms was planned through causes beyond the control of settlers and despite the labours of the Chief Commissioner Marshall Waller Clifton, F.R.S the achievement fell short of the vision.

This memorial recalls the vision, commemorated those hardy pioneers who continued to labour here in face of great difficulty and records the benefit Western Australia received from the coming of settlers and official in the ships

Island Queen..........December 1840
Parkfield.........................March 1841
Diadem.............................April 1842
Trusty.......................December 1842

The answer to the question can be found on the plaque located on the west side of the memorial seat.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9efba563-718e-4429-b417-f748ede82572" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Australind Bunbury Tourist Drive, designated as Tourist Drive 260, is a 14-kilometre-long  historic route from Bunbury to Leschenault via Australind.

There are numerous places of interest along the way and this Adventure Lab will take you to some of them.

Note the numeric answers to some of the questions as they will allow you to find a bonus geocache after completing all stages of this Adventure Lab.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ce9ad18c-c389-4f13-811b-4be9b1afc734" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations on completing this stage of the adventure lab.

There are no clues for bonus cache at this location.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
