  <urlname>[L] Australind Bunbury Tourist Drive 260 : S03 Dolphin Discovery Centre by West Oz Geocaching</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99001528" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] Australind Bunbury Tourist Drive 260 : S03 Dolphin Discovery Centre</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>West Oz Geocaching</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">West Oz Geocaching</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Australind Bunbury Tourist Drive 260&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Dolphin Discovery Centre&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0b629cdd-df49-49a1-b896-4727eef727e4"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0b629cdd-df49-49a1-b896-4727eef727e4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What colour is the triangles in the blue parts of the sculpture?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c5975212-db60-4179-bb27-48ff40590253" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Dolphin Discovery Centre is a not for profit organisation and eco-tourism venue located on Koombana Bay Bunbury.

The Bay is home to over 100 wild bottlenose dolphins who often visit the Dolphin Discovery Centre's beach in knee-high water. The centre runs year-round eco cruises out into the bay where you will see the dolphins in their natural habitat. In summer their "Swim with Dolphin" tour operates where you can swim with wild dolphins.

On the way to the entrance from the public car park you will find a themed sculpture that will allow you to answer the question.

They provide educational activities and field-based learning in marine and environmental studies. These activities include both incursions and excursions and the content within each has been designed to be interactive, entertaining and educational.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9efba563-718e-4429-b417-f748ede82572" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Australind Bunbury Tourist Drive, designated as Tourist Drive 260, is a 14-kilometre-long  historic route from Bunbury to Leschenault via Australind.

There are numerous places of interest along the way and this Adventure Lab will take you to some of them.

Note the numeric answers to some of the questions as they will allow you to find a bonus geocache after completing all stages of this Adventure Lab.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d5ed46fa-6d12-4960-b9c9-3bedb3caa6ca" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations on completing this stage of the Adventure Lab.

There are no clues for the bonus cache at this location.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
