   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;CircleRoute Series&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Oats Street Station&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/4ac5a720-33bf-41f4-95c9-17e316ac338d"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/4ac5a720-33bf-41f4-95c9-17e316ac338d&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;At Oats Street Station, which of the following destinations starting with 'K' can you catch a direct bus to?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/72883649-752d-42e0-9e88-7e5be6636b95" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Oats Street Station is where the CircleRoute crosses the Armadale Line and Thornlie Line.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/cb291dd4-26b3-46f5-bbf7-1fd98a3a4cd5" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This cache is part of the CircleRoute series. The series follows the CircleRoute bus service, one of Perth's high frequency family of bus services. The CircleRoute bus service operates with up to 1228 weekly services.

There are 5 lab locations, one at each station where the CircleRoute crosses a train line. A bonus final cache is located in Fremantle, the start and end point of the CircleRoute.

Make sure you also pick up the 17 traditional caches located at each timing point along the CircleRoute. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Make sure to note the following clues, in order to locate the final bonus cache:
D = 8
G = 4&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
