   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;DENHAM DISCOVERY TRAIL&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;THE OLD PEARLER&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/24dcde1e-9304-47a6-83d2-f3ed31191e10"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/24dcde1e-9304-47a6-83d2-f3ed31191e10&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;On the plaque nearby is a quote by a brick cutter. Name, 2 words.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/efa1888c-2116-4e83-9ce8-a939be3efa58" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Probably the only restaurant built of shell blocks!
The Hamelin Cockle Shells have over the centuries cemented together to form a soft rock named coquina, and blocks of this rock were used to build The Old Pearler as well as the Denham’s Anglican Church.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9c278d7b-88d6-493b-bb72-fcbd399c9e1e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is a short, walkable Adventure through the town of Denham in Shark Bay. 
Shark Bay is traditional country of the Malgana, Nhamda and Yingkarta people who have inhabited the area as early as 30,000 years ago. The Malgana name for Shark Bay is Gutharraguda, which means “two bays” or “ “two waters “
Denham is situated 8.5 hours’ drive north of Perth in the UNESCO Shark Bay  World Heritage Area. Captain Henry Mangles Denham charted the area in 1858 and gave the town his name. It was once a pearling port but now gives visitors a wide range of experiences from boating, diving, and swimming, as well as natural wonders like the dolphins of Monkey Mia, the stromatolites of Hamelin Pool, Shell Beach, and further afield François Peron National Park and Dirk Hartog Island.
This Adventure Lab can be done on foot in a short time, all being accessed from  Denham’s main street, Knight Street.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Another one, off you go!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
