   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;DENHAM DISCOVERY TRAIL&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;DENHAM DISCOVERY &amp; VISITOR CENTRE&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/24dcde1e-9304-47a6-83d2-f3ed31191e10"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/24dcde1e-9304-47a6-83d2-f3ed31191e10&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;On the compass rose on the ground, what is the distance in kms to where HMAS Sydney Ii  lies?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/19ff8769-1d95-4ab4-9ac4-6dcbb69b7495" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is just the place for information and maps on Shark Bay!
The Living Place, the Mapping Place and the Experiencing Place are great displays to tell you about this wonderful area.
Outside, you will see a Memorial to the crew of HMAS Sydney II who went down with their ship in 1941, a fishing boat the Velsheda and a compass rose set in the ground.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9c278d7b-88d6-493b-bb72-fcbd399c9e1e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is a short, walkable Adventure through the town of Denham in Shark Bay. 
Shark Bay is traditional country of the Malgana, Nhamda and Yingkarta people who have inhabited the area as early as 30,000 years ago. The Malgana name for Shark Bay is Gutharraguda, which means “two bays” or “ “two waters “
Denham is situated 8.5 hours’ drive north of Perth in the UNESCO Shark Bay  World Heritage Area. Captain Henry Mangles Denham charted the area in 1858 and gave the town his name. It was once a pearling port but now gives visitors a wide range of experiences from boating, diving, and swimming, as well as natural wonders like the dolphins of Monkey Mia, the stromatolites of Hamelin Pool, Shell Beach, and further afield François Peron National Park and Dirk Hartog Island.
This Adventure Lab can be done on foot in a short time, all being accessed from  Denham’s main street, Knight Street.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done, onto the next one!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
