   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;1962 Perth Commonwealth Games&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Beatty Park Aquatic Centre&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d6a4004a-4017-4fc5-86e3-9325f6693059"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d6a4004a-4017-4fc5-86e3-9325f6693059&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What was the name of the company that built the aquatic centre (7 letters no full stops or spaces)? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/032ad79d-05c6-40de-82cc-a55721351582" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Swimming and diving events were held at the Beatty Park Aquatic Centre. Australian swimming legends Dawn Fraser and Murray Rose both won four gold medals. The original pool and grandstands are still in use today. 

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/90fe87fe-9fc1-41a1-9679-0e959d6be564" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The 1962 British Empire and Commonwealth Games were held in Perth from 22 November to 1 December 1962. 863 athletes from 35 countries participated in nine sports – athletics, bowls, boxing, cycling, fencing, rowing, swimming, weightlifting and wrestling.

53,000 people attended the opening ceremony at Perry Lake Stadium on a stinking hot 40 degree day.

The games were a huge success, putting Perth on the international map and spurring development of the city.

This adventure lab takes you to four of the sites used for the games. Collect a clue at each site to solve the coordinates for the bonus cache. It is recommended to start at Beatty Park.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f6067d97-2f75-4f84-a5fd-d40887c0b0ff" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;For the games, Beatty Park Pool had two 50-yard pools and a diving pool.  Record this coordinate for the bonus cache, A = 5.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.9278" lon="115.834">
