  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d6a4004a-4017-4fc5-86e3-9325f6693059</url>
  <urlname>1962 Perth Commonwealth Games : S2 Lake Monger Velodrome by J2V</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99002480" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>1962 Perth Commonwealth Games : S2 Lake Monger Velodrome</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>J2V</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">J2V</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;1962 Perth Commonwealth Games&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Lake Monger Velodrome&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d6a4004a-4017-4fc5-86e3-9325f6693059"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d6a4004a-4017-4fc5-86e3-9325f6693059&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;There are no interpretative signs about the games around the venue today. What is the name of the stadium (last name only)?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/262a3799-011b-4aad-8972-ec0134ec09da" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Track cycling events were held at the Lake Monger Velodrome. 
The concrete velodrome was covered with grassy banks in the 1980’s and the ground become the home of the Floreat Athena Football Club.
At the posted coordinates you’ll be standing on the tunnel that goes under the concrete track. 
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/90fe87fe-9fc1-41a1-9679-0e959d6be564" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The 1962 British Empire and Commonwealth Games were held in Perth from 22 November to 1 December 1962. 863 athletes from 35 countries participated in nine sports – athletics, bowls, boxing, cycling, fencing, rowing, swimming, weightlifting and wrestling.

53,000 people attended the opening ceremony at Perry Lake Stadium on a stinking hot 40 degree day.

The games were a huge success, putting Perth on the international map and spurring development of the city.

This adventure lab takes you to four of the sites used for the games. Collect a clue at each site to solve the coordinates for the bonus cache. It is recommended to start at Beatty Park.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7233859d-98b1-47af-886c-cc0a20e01ff6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;At the games there were only four cycling events (all for men) on a concrete track. How times have changed! C = 7.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.946717" lon="115.790117">
