  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d6a4004a-4017-4fc5-86e3-9325f6693059</url>
  <urlname>1962 Perth Commonwealth Games : S4 Perry Lakes Stadium 2 by J2V</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99002484" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>1962 Perth Commonwealth Games : S4 Perry Lakes Stadium 2</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>J2V</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">J2V</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;1962 Perth Commonwealth Games&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Perry Lakes Stadium 2&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d6a4004a-4017-4fc5-86e3-9325f6693059"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d6a4004a-4017-4fc5-86e3-9325f6693059&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt; Find the sign that mentions the dual women’s gold medalist. What was her last name?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4a70ee4a-dfe7-45f4-aa00-4dc9bf18712c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The second stop at the old Perry Lake Stadium is where field events were held, inside the running track. There are interpretative signs on the board walk. Timber used for grandstand seating, and signs from around the venue, were recycled and used in landscaping around the redeveloped site.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/90fe87fe-9fc1-41a1-9679-0e959d6be564" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The 1962 British Empire and Commonwealth Games were held in Perth from 22 November to 1 December 1962. 863 athletes from 35 countries participated in nine sports – athletics, bowls, boxing, cycling, fencing, rowing, swimming, weightlifting and wrestling.

53,000 people attended the opening ceremony at Perry Lake Stadium on a stinking hot 40 degree day.

The games were a huge success, putting Perth on the international map and spurring development of the city.

This adventure lab takes you to four of the sites used for the games. Collect a clue at each site to solve the coordinates for the bonus cache. It is recommended to start at Beatty Park.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/03116ab1-8fac-4c2f-9649-568f79a1e0e4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Older geocachers may remember attending interschool athletic carnivals here. Walk around the corner to see the original scoreboard. B = 0&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
