  <name>LBQ3oX-03</name>
  <desc>1962PerthCommoe</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d6a4004a-4017-4fc5-86e3-9325f6693059</url>
  <urlname>1962 Perth Commonwealth Games : S3 Perry Lakes Stadium 1 by J2V</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99002482" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>1962 Perth Commonwealth Games : S3 Perry Lakes Stadium 1</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>J2V</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">J2V</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;1962 Perth Commonwealth Games&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Perry Lakes Stadium 1&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d6a4004a-4017-4fc5-86e3-9325f6693059"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d6a4004a-4017-4fc5-86e3-9325f6693059&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;A pavilion was built adjacent to the main stadium for broadcasting during the games. Who was it named after (last name)?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0b0237c4-72e4-4c5c-b3d7-e286bff246fa" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;There are two stops at the old Perry Lakes Stadium site. The first is near the entrance where the athletes marched in for the opening ceremony. Today you can retrace the steps along Athletes Parade, down the main straight where the grandstand was and around to the scoreboard that has been persevered. The stadium was demolished in 2012 and replaced with a housing estate.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/90fe87fe-9fc1-41a1-9679-0e959d6be564" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The 1962 British Empire and Commonwealth Games were held in Perth from 22 November to 1 December 1962. 863 athletes from 35 countries participated in nine sports – athletics, bowls, boxing, cycling, fencing, rowing, swimming, weightlifting and wrestling.

53,000 people attended the opening ceremony at Perry Lake Stadium on a stinking hot 40 degree day.

The games were a huge success, putting Perth on the international map and spurring development of the city.

This adventure lab takes you to four of the sites used for the games. Collect a clue at each site to solve the coordinates for the bonus cache. It is recommended to start at Beatty Park.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/885c931d-4b75-4a2c-bdc8-b2081af466d9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Walk down Athletes Parade to the next stop. Coordinate for the bonus cache, E = 5.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
