 <wpt lat="-31.9259" lon="115.767133">
  <ele>43.0</ele>
  <time>2022-03-17T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBQ3oX-05</name>
  <desc>1962PerthCommol</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d6a4004a-4017-4fc5-86e3-9325f6693059</url>
  <urlname>1962 Perth Commonwealth Games : S5 Games Village, City Beach by J2V</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99002486" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>1962 Perth Commonwealth Games : S5 Games Village, City Beach</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>J2V</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">J2V</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;1962 Perth Commonwealth Games&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Games Village, City Beach&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d6a4004a-4017-4fc5-86e3-9325f6693059"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d6a4004a-4017-4fc5-86e3-9325f6693059&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Search the veranda (inside and outside) to find the photo of the marathoner. What was his last name?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/542835d5-87bb-47f2-90e2-f3e4f98cb8ad" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;150 new houses were built for the Games Village, around what is now called Beecroft Park. The site included a recreation hall, dining hall, shops and an administration building. 

It has been said that the Games Village was the most enduring legacy of the games because of the influence that the subdivision and building design had on the subsequent development of Perth suburbs.

A shopping centre, on the site of the old dining hall, burnt down in 2014. The shopping centre was rebuilt and named Empire Village, drawing on the history of the site.

There are a lot of interpretative signs about the 1962 Commonwealth Games on the north side of the car park, and inside and outside the verandas.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/90fe87fe-9fc1-41a1-9679-0e959d6be564" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The 1962 British Empire and Commonwealth Games were held in Perth from 22 November to 1 December 1962. 863 athletes from 35 countries participated in nine sports – athletics, bowls, boxing, cycling, fencing, rowing, swimming, weightlifting and wrestling.

53,000 people attended the opening ceremony at Perry Lake Stadium on a stinking hot 40 degree day.

The games were a huge success, putting Perth on the international map and spurring development of the city.

This adventure lab takes you to four of the sites used for the games. Collect a clue at each site to solve the coordinates for the bonus cache. It is recommended to start at Beatty Park.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/51a6157f-088a-4f22-8454-30cf3bc3b46b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations you have completed the Commonwealth Games adventure lab. Find the bonus cache nearby. D = 7.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.9869" lon="115.821167">
  <ele>5.0</ele>
  <time>2022-03-24T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBRsVm-01</name>
  <desc>AklugerLovesLa1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/da0e4e8c-a102-4cde-9c74-7ac9cc3465ff</url>
  <urlname>____akluger loves labs : S1 ____akluger loves Katamburdup by ____akluger</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99002500" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>____akluger loves labs : S1 ____akluger loves Katamburdup</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>____akluger</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">____akluger</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;____akluger loves labs&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;____akluger loves Katamburdup&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/da0e4e8c-a102-4cde-9c74-7ac9cc3465ff"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/da0e4e8c-a102-4cde-9c74-7ac9cc3465ff&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What bird is described on the sign as having a "turned down beak"?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/05cc7304-1eee-4a56-a5ff-2b9162415496" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Katamburdup, meaning "place of high importance", has a rather new refurbishment. While here, also check out my friend _DaughtersofEve_'s cache called, "Take a seat".

You will need the second info board.

Picture of the bird by wikimedia user Alan Schmierer, used with permission.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/56089b91-8ea1-43a9-8349-50c0a495fdc4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;I am honored that I was chosen as one of 300 people that received an Adventure Lab credit!

After each stage, you will receive 2 letters. When in the right order, they will form the name of another thing I really like.

Enjoy the river!

Congratulations to cravo10 on FTF on this AL!
The Adventure Lab® logo is a registered trademark of Groundspeak, Inc. DBA Geocaching. Used with permission. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/50288715-9366-4e22-8582-1dd793d61b0f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;GE&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.990467" lon="115.817167">
  <ele>-1.0</ele>
  <time>2022-03-24T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBRsVm-03</name>
  <desc>AklugerLovesLa3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/da0e4e8c-a102-4cde-9c74-7ac9cc3465ff</url>
  <urlname>____akluger loves labs : S3 ____akluger loves highland cattle by ____akluger</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99002504" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>____akluger loves labs : S3 ____akluger loves highland cattle</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>____akluger</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">____akluger</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;____akluger loves labs&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;____akluger loves highland cattle&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/da0e4e8c-a102-4cde-9c74-7ac9cc3465ff"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/da0e4e8c-a102-4cde-9c74-7ac9cc3465ff&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Who wrote the poem that is on the plaque on this bench?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a419d571-d180-4670-8f6b-c791cd768a78" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A plaque on a bench.

This station has nothing really to do with the title, it's just a reference to the poem. 

Picture by wikimedia user Gordon Legget, used under permission.

Location completion image by wikimedia user Aconcagua&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/56089b91-8ea1-43a9-8349-50c0a495fdc4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;I am honored that I was chosen as one of 300 people that received an Adventure Lab credit!

After each stage, you will receive 2 letters. When in the right order, they will form the name of another thing I really like.

Enjoy the river!

Congratulations to cravo10 on FTF on this AL!
The Adventure Lab® logo is a registered trademark of Groundspeak, Inc. DBA Geocaching. Used with permission. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b1efd919-4d4c-4785-9982-2c81411b85e3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;AC&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
