  <name>LBNUdU-04</name>
  <desc>LLostKatanning4</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/161e044d-28db-4eca-b062-3e56529ce60c</url>
  <urlname>[L] Lost Katanning : S4 Pioneer Women’s Clock and Heritage Rose Garden by Boyzrule5</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909771" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] Lost Katanning : S4 Pioneer Women’s Clock and Heritage Rose Garden</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Boyzrule5</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Boyzrule5</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Lost Katanning&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Pioneer Women’s Clock and Heritage Rose Garden &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/161e044d-28db-4eca-b062-3e56529ce60c"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/161e044d-28db-4eca-b062-3e56529ce60c&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the date on the plaque of the memorial? (As written)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e579f2f1-4d85-4af7-9030-a4016504d634" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The clock is one of two of its kind in the public realm; the other is located in Parliament House in Perth.
The clock was built to commemorate the pioneering women of Katanning, and was unveiled in 1956 by Sister Elizabeth Grover after a year’s construction. Sister Grover was the oldest surviving daughter of William Grover, one of the first settlers in the Shire. According to the Heritage Council of Western Australia, the clock cost the town 1458 pounds, nine shillings and eight pence to build. A local jeweller and watchmaker, a Mr LFW Quartermaine, won the contract of maintaining and supervising the clock in 1955, for which he was paid 10 pounds a year.
   
Heritage Rose Garden
This delightful garden is located opposite the Town Hall and incorporates a Noongar Time Walk, Malay Mosaic, the Pioneer Women’s Clock and roses dating back to 1830. There is also a memorial wall with plaques remembering the pioneers of the district.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/31f0a8f3-8c80-4869-ba26-d196fce31e3a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Katanning, situated 362km from Perth and 185km from Albany. Katanning is thought to come from an Aboriginal word ‘Kartannin’ meaning ‘big meeting place’ and it still holds true to this meaning in the 21st century, as the largest town in the Upper Great Southern servicing many surrounding towns. 
Midway between Eticup and Yowangup was a clear pool of sweet water, named by the local peoples  “Kartanup”, and from this pool, which is in the bed of the creek passing through the Katanning Park, now filled with sand and serving as a playground in the summer for the children of the present generation, did the town of Katanning receive its name.
Official recognition was given to the settlement to the east of the Perth-Albany road in 1861, when Sergeant McKenna, with his wife and family, was appointed the first trooper to the district. The police camp was set up at the waterhole now known as the Police Pools.
Katanning was declared a town on June 10, 1898.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2ee80295-3a53-40af-be13-4c6aaf85fc5d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Good work, almost there.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
