  <name>LBrRz2-01</name>
  <desc>LLakeCliftonTh1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5c5358bc-a875-4a5f-9337-09d697d0a131</url>
  <urlname>[L] Lake Clifton Thrombolites  : S1 Walking at Lake Clifton by fratra</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99002518" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] Lake Clifton Thrombolites  : S1 Walking at Lake Clifton</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>fratra</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">fratra</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Lake Clifton Thrombolites &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Walking at Lake Clifton&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5c5358bc-a875-4a5f-9337-09d697d0a131"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5c5358bc-a875-4a5f-9337-09d697d0a131&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How far is the return journey along the boardwalk? XXXm (answer format)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d9ed13c5-af88-4367-9611-b6eab28d0725" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Walk along the boardwalk that ventures through the lakeside reeds and out onto Lake Clifton.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/42da0919-1cde-4023-8be6-df1cf24359fd" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Somethings clearly get better with age! 

Located at Yalgorup National Park, south of Mandurah, the thrombolite reef at Lake Clifton offers you a glimpse of what life was like when the earth began.

These rock-like formations are found in only a few places in the world and scientists believe that thrombolites are one of the first life forms on earth, dating back approximately 570 million years, producing oxygen that made all subsequent life possible.

The Lake Clifton thrombolites are approximately 2,000 years old and the largest in the southern hemisphere. You can view them from above on a boardwalk over the lake with January to May being the best time to see them when the water levels are low.

Collect the letters  at each stage to allow you to locate  the bonus cache GC9QZXB&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b2820c1b-65c2-4c51-8dc8-61cc28996f05" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Make a note of the letters L and A to find the Bonus cache&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
