   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;HMAS Sydney II Memorial&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Stele&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/890d2d1b-386c-4e34-9b99-05a9ede1de0c"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/890d2d1b-386c-4e34-9b99-05a9ede1de0c&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;There is a plaque on the wall a few meters from the Stele, what depth in meters was the ship found?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8a2bc8f7-c0d6-4190-b21c-ea0fcae80421" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Based on the historical symbolism of standing stones as grave markers this vertical element expresses the prow of the HMAS Sydney II, metraphorically, in a single dramatic gesture, while providing a major focal point visible for many miles. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7e5bfe44-2aab-4337-8a32-4fcfa5eb4147" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The HMAS Sydney II Memorial comprises many symbolic elements expressing the tragic loss of 645 lives on board the HMAS Sydney II.

There is a bonus box to this lab - GC9R0XT&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/abdce38a-c176-4356-a266-99f9a4c97c77" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
