   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Kings Park - Playgrounds&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Arthur Fairall Playground&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/73002670-5c7c-4420-aa34-a7f76a879bab"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/73002670-5c7c-4420-aa34-a7f76a879bab&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Which era is noted on this plaque?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4f06bc0d-4e25-4a7c-9f1e-20fdc37aaf5c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Arthur Fairall playground The Synergy Parkland in Kings Park and Botanic Garden is the first environmental playground and community area of its kind in Australia. It has been given a new lease of life. What was once a much-loved but worn-out playground that had entertained Perth children for more than three decades, has been revamped into an exciting and challenging area for children to explore, discover, play and simply enjoy being outdoors. It features a 75m-long elevated walkway and two-tiered island fort suitable for children over six years. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/20f44e6d-6c71-4002-8a92-d0d8a3839ae2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This one is for the kids! We packed a picnic and spent the day exploring the playgrounds. Alternatively, two of the locations have cafe's. 

Kings Park is one of the world’s largest and most beautiful inner city parks. It is rich in Aboriginal and European history, contemporary culture and offers innovative design, displays and services. Kings Park has an international reputation for scientific research, leading horticulture, conservation and public education.
Kings Park is home to the spectacular Western Australian Botanic Garden, which displays over 3,000 species of the State’s unique flora. Two thirds of the 400 hectare park is protected as bushland and provides a haven for native biological diversity.
Visitors can enjoy sweeping views of the Swan and Canning Rivers, the city skyline and the Darling Ranges to the east. Bushland walk trails, immaculate gardens and parklands and a variety of children’s discovery play areas can all be found in Kings Park. 
Ref: https://www.bgpa.wa.gov.au/kings-park&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f11ba8c6-612a-43f0-9a81-aefa9b1a8b94" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Way to go! Did you see the Pterosaurs in the metal on the walkway?&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
