  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99002554" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Lighthouse Park - A night time lab : S4 Lighthouse Park West</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>olthomas</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">olthomas</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Lighthouse Park - A night time lab&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Lighthouse Park West&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/98e52a77-ac64-4e6c-9992-9d159339430d"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/98e52a77-ac64-4e6c-9992-9d159339430d&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Can you spot the reflector? What shape is it?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a69bc83f-470c-47d2-a8b2-a946a762c833" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Shine your torch around and see what you can spot.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a407ffa9-44c3-47e7-9766-3ce77e29b828" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;When is the best time to view a working lighthouse? Well in the dark of course! So this adventure is all about the dark. Grab your torch and your device and off you go. Bonus cache available. https://coord.info/GC9RFYH&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Miaow! Your bonus letter is H&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-34.977967" lon="116.8918">
  <ele>163.0</ele>
  <time>2022-04-22T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBNRio-04</name>
  <desc>ValleyOfTheGia4</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/4fd4bfaa-5fba-4494-8c3c-c7e9053c07a1</url>
  <urlname>Valley of the Giants Ancient Empire Walk : S4 King Tingle by allinaday</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-608" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Valley of the Giants Ancient Empire Walk : S4 King Tingle</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>allinaday</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">allinaday</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Valley of the Giants Ancient Empire Walk&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;King Tingle&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/4fd4bfaa-5fba-4494-8c3c-c7e9053c07a1"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/4fd4bfaa-5fba-4494-8c3c-c7e9053c07a1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How frequently does the King Tingle flower?  (Numeral only)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/364a0ec1-fb62-4d57-adaa-e991afd1510c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Named for his majestic appearance, this red tingle grows straight and tall among his gnarled neighbours.  Unlike other ancient tingles in this forest, he hasn't been burnt outside his base although you can see evidence of past fires on his bark. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b76a4c59-ced9-4d9f-97db-80f346fe9bf0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;  The Valley of the Giants is a family friendly, nature based attraction with guided walks, educational programs and a discovery centre.

The park is open every day of the year from 9am to 5pm.  If you wish to complete the Tree Top Walk, there is a fee.  The Ancient Empire Walk is free of charge.  Phone coverage may be a bit patchy.

 It is home to the famous Tree Top Walk which spans approx 600 metres and reaches a height of 40 metres above the forest floor.  

The Ancient Empire is an interpretive trail that meanders across the forest floor in between 400 year old tingle trees.   Much of the plant life in this forest is unique to the south west of Western Australia.  Trees such as the tingle only occur in this small area and provide a window to the past.

As you wander and marvel at this amazing area, you will come across a number of interpretive plaques which have the answers you seek to complete this adventure.

Bonus cache has been placed in the area.  Coordinates revealed at completion of AL.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/17bc0996-c146-42fa-bd8d-ee56e3ea67f3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
