   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Valley of the Giants Ancient Empire Walk&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Red Tingle&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/4fd4bfaa-5fba-4494-8c3c-c7e9053c07a1"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/4fd4bfaa-5fba-4494-8c3c-c7e9053c07a1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the botanical name of the Red Tingle Tree?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/cf93ae51-525d-45a2-87e6-70f66e40efad" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Growing up to 75m tall and up to 20m in girth, you can recognise red tingles by their large, often hollowed out bases.  These hollows are created by a combination of fungal and insect attack and then fire burning out the dead wood from the centre of the tree.
Red Tingles only grow in a small area around Walpole and Nornalup and need over a metre of rain every year to survive.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b76a4c59-ced9-4d9f-97db-80f346fe9bf0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;  The Valley of the Giants is a family friendly, nature based attraction with guided walks, educational programs and a discovery centre.

The park is open every day of the year from 9am to 5pm.  If you wish to complete the Tree Top Walk, there is a fee.  The Ancient Empire Walk is free of charge.  Phone coverage may be a bit patchy.

 It is home to the famous Tree Top Walk which spans approx 600 metres and reaches a height of 40 metres above the forest floor.  

The Ancient Empire is an interpretive trail that meanders across the forest floor in between 400 year old tingle trees.   Much of the plant life in this forest is unique to the south west of Western Australia.  Trees such as the tingle only occur in this small area and provide a window to the past.

As you wander and marvel at this amazing area, you will come across a number of interpretive plaques which have the answers you seek to complete this adventure.

Bonus cache has been placed in the area.  Coordinates revealed at completion of AL.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1ea66923-b6b9-4ec3-88c5-b12cac34c7b6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
