   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Valley of the Giants Ancient Empire Walk&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Grandma Tingle&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/4fd4bfaa-5fba-4494-8c3c-c7e9053c07a1"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/4fd4bfaa-5fba-4494-8c3c-c7e9053c07a1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How old is she?  (Numerals only)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/639c332e-6422-4f2c-a272-0f48b38a5f6d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Grandma Tingle was so named because of her gnarled and wrinkled appearance and her distinct 'face' which gives her an almost human character.  In the past she was called the Gatekeeper as though she was keeping watch over the forest.  &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b76a4c59-ced9-4d9f-97db-80f346fe9bf0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;  The Valley of the Giants is a family friendly, nature based attraction with guided walks, educational programs and a discovery centre.

The park is open every day of the year from 9am to 5pm.  If you wish to complete the Tree Top Walk, there is a fee.  The Ancient Empire Walk is free of charge.  Phone coverage may be a bit patchy.

 It is home to the famous Tree Top Walk which spans approx 600 metres and reaches a height of 40 metres above the forest floor.  

The Ancient Empire is an interpretive trail that meanders across the forest floor in between 400 year old tingle trees.   Much of the plant life in this forest is unique to the south west of Western Australia.  Trees such as the tingle only occur in this small area and provide a window to the past.

As you wander and marvel at this amazing area, you will come across a number of interpretive plaques which have the answers you seek to complete this adventure.

Bonus cache has been placed in the area.  Coordinates revealed at completion of AL.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1ed57e95-be36-4d65-a7e1-1b5f96b1ff98" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
