 <wpt lat="-32.070533" lon="116.00165">
  <ele>19.0</ele>
  <time>2022-04-30T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBN6xf-03</name>
  <desc>HiddenSuburban3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7152a471-7de7-4efc-8e35-b2905d5f4cae</url>
  <urlname>Hidden Suburban Art  : S3 Local Flora and Fauna by LAXA</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99002532" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Hidden Suburban Art  : S3 Local Flora and Fauna</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>LAXA</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">LAXA</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Hidden Suburban Art &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Local Flora and Fauna&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7152a471-7de7-4efc-8e35-b2905d5f4cae"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7152a471-7de7-4efc-8e35-b2905d5f4cae&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Face South - West, at the middle level of the stairs. Which animal is depicted in bottom right hand corner, (use its Noongar name)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/aa4df526-11ea-4f3c-a72c-0bc1345f3b24" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;At the Town Square, Mark Datodi's installation of aluminium fish highlight and celebrate the marine life found in nearby river systems - the Canning River, Ellis Brook and the Southern River. Besides the impressive water feature, paintings of local plants and wildlife described with their English and Noongar names inform you about the abundance and biodiversity of native plants and animals in and around the area. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/979c4783-24fa-4cc7-abaa-9609b17fa833" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This little tour will take you around the heart of Gosnells to some obvious and some less obvious examples of suburban street art, celebrating culture, heritage and diversity in the City.
You can park your car at the first location (the Railway markets in Gosnells), the tour will loop you back here, should you choose to do them in order. We can recommend a stop at the nearby pub as a reward. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9d96ee10-9353-47ed-9bc2-bc542f917c4e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.071633" lon="116.00135">
  <ele>19.0</ele>
  <time>2022-04-30T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBN6xf-05</name>
  <desc>HiddenSuburban5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7152a471-7de7-4efc-8e35-b2905d5f4cae</url>
  <urlname>Hidden Suburban Art  : S5 The Foundation of a City by LAXA</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99002536" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Hidden Suburban Art  : S5 The Foundation of a City</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>LAXA</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">LAXA</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Hidden Suburban Art &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Foundation of a City&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7152a471-7de7-4efc-8e35-b2905d5f4cae"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7152a471-7de7-4efc-8e35-b2905d5f4cae&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;You will find the depiction of the ship on which the very early settlers arrived in WA. What is the name of the ship?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6246b295-a274-4f30-ad1a-f5fa5163e55a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Painted by Trish Bygott and Nathan Crotty, this laneway mural depicts the early foundational history of the City of Gosnells. The artist drew inspiration for this mural from iconic pioneering descriptions of Gosnells including orchards, ploughing of the fields, ladies on the lawn, the brick factory and market gardens to create this mural. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/979c4783-24fa-4cc7-abaa-9609b17fa833" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This little tour will take you around the heart of Gosnells to some obvious and some less obvious examples of suburban street art, celebrating culture, heritage and diversity in the City.
You can park your car at the first location (the Railway markets in Gosnells), the tour will loop you back here, should you choose to do them in order. We can recommend a stop at the nearby pub as a reward. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f524e2aa-49aa-4fa6-8c55-17be38fb00fb" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.072267" lon="116.004117">
  <ele>21.0</ele>
  <time>2022-04-30T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBN6xf-04</name>
  <desc>HiddenSuburban4</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7152a471-7de7-4efc-8e35-b2905d5f4cae</url>
  <urlname>Hidden Suburban Art  : S4 Early Settlers by LAXA</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99002534" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Hidden Suburban Art  : S4 Early Settlers</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>LAXA</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">LAXA</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Hidden Suburban Art &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Early Settlers&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7152a471-7de7-4efc-8e35-b2905d5f4cae"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7152a471-7de7-4efc-8e35-b2905d5f4cae&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year is Andy Pages Truck ?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/961d9a1a-7965-483e-be29-4fda7243df5f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Framing the walkway in this little park is a mural by David &amp; Leslie Arandle, depicting aspects of the life of the Pages brothers. Michael and Fermina Pages left Spain in 1904 with their six children and arrived in Western Australia. Michael worked on farms in Darlington before selecting a block in Martin which they developed into a successful farm. Andres Pages established a store and in the 1920s with the rapid uptake of motor vehicles, installed a petrol bowser out the front of the store which developed into a garage. The Pages garage was very successful and other family members worked as carriers until the 1950s. This site of the park was a former residence which was cleared in the late 1960s. The mature trees on the site were evident within the former garden. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/979c4783-24fa-4cc7-abaa-9609b17fa833" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This little tour will take you around the heart of Gosnells to some obvious and some less obvious examples of suburban street art, celebrating culture, heritage and diversity in the City.
You can park your car at the first location (the Railway markets in Gosnells), the tour will loop you back here, should you choose to do them in order. We can recommend a stop at the nearby pub as a reward. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/90a9557e-63cc-4ef3-a0c2-cdfdf04bcf76" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-33.358467" lon="116.1491">
  <ele>197.0</ele>
  <time>2022-04-30T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBkyf7-05</name>
  <desc>VisitCollieS5Co</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7daca72b-534f-405b-9d53-da4e5e1b0d19</url>
  <urlname>Visit Collie : S5 Coal Mining by WebblyWA</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476912232" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Visit Collie : S5 Coal Mining</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>WebblyWA</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">WebblyWA</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Visit Collie&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Coal Mining&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7daca72b-534f-405b-9d53-da4e5e1b0d19"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7daca72b-534f-405b-9d53-da4e5e1b0d19&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;There is a yellow sign in front of the machine, what year was the machine donated to the Collie Community?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5cef482e-9e5d-4eba-b103-1692098f92f6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The 54RB mechanical shovel was purchased by Griffin Coal in 1961 and worked in excess of 38,000 hours in the coal fields around Collie during which time it moved ~9 million tonnes of coal. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/800f5ebc-30b3-461c-b444-c75ba469f54b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Collie Visitors Centre. This adventure lab will take you around the visitors centre precinct. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/382f5f4a-16ac-46f3-b4a6-010ef17fde2d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-33.35855" lon="116.149133">
  <ele>197.0</ele>
  <time>2022-04-30T08:00:00Z</time>
