   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;The (old) Road to Bunbury&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Harvey&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c8032bc6-fa86-4ce5-9234-a06129c1e8fc"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c8032bc6-fa86-4ce5-9234-a06129c1e8fc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Where are you?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/83cb610c-85e1-4f7a-a131-5dabbf6738f1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Harvey Western Australia – Smile. Boasts a 2 metre round disc of 2 cows for photo props. Step up to the plate and put your face through the holes to have a magical photo for you memories of the Beautiful Harvey icon.

The design was a mixture of ideas put forward by the art departments of Harvey and Australind Senior High Schools. A design competition, which was won by a group of Harvey students.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3de6cb8d-13fc-4aec-90e3-a2dd257ecc2d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Before the Forrest Hwy was opened in 2009 one of the main routes to Bunbury was along the South Western Hwy. The old road to Bunbury passes through several towns which this Adventure Lab will cause you to visit. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6502ce8e-e857-4da7-8cf0-472626bac27c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
