   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Lesmurdie Falls Adventure Lab&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Shoulder Lookout Trail Junction&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ddf93f00-840a-4a2a-b88d-36ace2986019"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ddf93f00-840a-4a2a-b88d-36ace2986019&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;From this junction point, how many metres would you need to travel to reach Shoulder Lookout?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5fd62d3b-d279-484e-924a-37a1a67b7f43" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A leisurely stroll down the valley along Lesmurdie Brook trail is a chance to connect with the unique beauty of the Perth hills, The directional sign in front of you provides useful information for visitors and a chance to decide if the walk to the Shoulder Lookout would be worth it. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/07c74bad-d79f-46c9-82d9-3dcb1dce29c3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Lesmurdie Falls Adventure Lab. Lesmurdie Falls is the spectacular point where Lesmurdie Brook plummets 40 metres over the granite edge of the Darling Scarp into the lush valley below. 
Located within the Mundy Regional Park, the area around the falls offers stunning views over the Swan Coastal Plain as well as access to lookouts and relatively short and easy hiking trails ranging from the short 300m Cascades Walk to the 3km Valley Loop Trail.
This adlab extends from the Cascades down to the Lesmurdie Falls lookouts, a distance of less than 1km.
At the starting point, there is a large carpark, picnic tables and toilet facilities. Please note there is no potable drinking water available, dogs are permitted on a leash and there is an optional mystery bonus cache available.
[We respectfully acknowledge the Beeloo people, the traditional owners and the first people of these lands.]&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/53501c2b-763c-421c-b359-3528920c73a5" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;60% complete with the best to come (especially if there have been recent rains). Another bonus cache clue: I am a granite inselberg.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
