   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Lesmurdie Falls Adventure Lab&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Start: Lesmurdie Falls Picnic area&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ddf93f00-840a-4a2a-b88d-36ace2986019"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ddf93f00-840a-4a2a-b88d-36ace2986019&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the small bird depicted on the information board? [2 words]&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9558c522-689f-4f82-a5e5-de5adc0ec789" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This area provides picnic tables with shade, toilet facilities and rubbish bins. Disabled access is available to the toilets and picnic tables. From the car park, make your way down the steps and get your bearings from the large information board in front of you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/07c74bad-d79f-46c9-82d9-3dcb1dce29c3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Lesmurdie Falls Adventure Lab. Lesmurdie Falls is the spectacular point where Lesmurdie Brook plummets 40 metres over the granite edge of the Darling Scarp into the lush valley below. 
Located within the Mundy Regional Park, the area around the falls offers stunning views over the Swan Coastal Plain as well as access to lookouts and relatively short and easy hiking trails ranging from the short 300m Cascades Walk to the 3km Valley Loop Trail.
This adlab extends from the Cascades down to the Lesmurdie Falls lookouts, a distance of less than 1km.
At the starting point, there is a large carpark, picnic tables and toilet facilities. Please note there is no potable drinking water available, dogs are permitted on a leash and there is an optional mystery bonus cache available.
[We respectfully acknowledge the Beeloo people, the traditional owners and the first people of these lands.]&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5009517b-436b-4e8d-a376-98b12d277d16" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;20% done, 80% to go unless you are after the mystery bonus cache. Clue 1: I am a well known  Australian landform feature!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
