   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Lesmurdie Falls Adventure Lab&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Cascades&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ddf93f00-840a-4a2a-b88d-36ace2986019"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ddf93f00-840a-4a2a-b88d-36ace2986019&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is this trail 'perfect for viewing' in spring? [1 word ]&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e4ff3c2e-9c0b-4c30-8d53-898de43bb792" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A short 300m walk up the valley brings you to the series of small waterfalls known as the cascades. There is a small signage board located near the bridge across the brook that makes for interesting reading.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/07c74bad-d79f-46c9-82d9-3dcb1dce29c3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Lesmurdie Falls Adventure Lab. Lesmurdie Falls is the spectacular point where Lesmurdie Brook plummets 40 metres over the granite edge of the Darling Scarp into the lush valley below. 
Located within the Mundy Regional Park, the area around the falls offers stunning views over the Swan Coastal Plain as well as access to lookouts and relatively short and easy hiking trails ranging from the short 300m Cascades Walk to the 3km Valley Loop Trail.
This adlab extends from the Cascades down to the Lesmurdie Falls lookouts, a distance of less than 1km.
At the starting point, there is a large carpark, picnic tables and toilet facilities. Please note there is no potable drinking water available, dogs are permitted on a leash and there is an optional mystery bonus cache available.
[We respectfully acknowledge the Beeloo people, the traditional owners and the first people of these lands.]&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/caf8bddb-1f58-4aec-9f6b-4427ac4a6391" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;40% down and your mystery bonus clue is: I am located in Western Australia!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
