   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Things to see and do&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;For duck sake&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/62fc7104-bf0d-40b7-9a6b-1aa6e2e84cae"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/62fc7104-bf0d-40b7-9a6b-1aa6e2e84cae&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What school assisted with project&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/22f82b3a-0c83-4a21-ad49-316ddb662b71" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is such a beautiful place you have the beautiful walk around the lake and a wonderful playground with bbq facilities and toilets and playground equipment for children with disabilities just across the road. And if you wish the wildlife park. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/fe8e5989-1a22-4111-8295-2e62d8a74e6f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Wagb is coming up and we would like to put out to participants a see and do lab things for all ages to aee and do&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4e3dbb3a-b518-48c4-8ddc-f2cfe1b72b05" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulation on your caching ability and i hope your having fun&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.8505" lon="116.252167">
  <ele>255.0</ele>
  <time>2022-05-18T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBQ9bu-03</name>
  <desc>WelcomeToChidl3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/78383dcb-c760-475c-84ed-ce088db462f2</url>
  <urlname>Welcome to Chidlow : S3 Lake Leschenaultia by GeoNut5</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909750" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Welcome to Chidlow : S3 Lake Leschenaultia</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>GeoNut5</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">GeoNut5</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Welcome to Chidlow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Lake Leschenaultia&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/78383dcb-c760-475c-84ed-ce088db462f2"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/78383dcb-c760-475c-84ed-ce088db462f2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What day/s is the cafe not open?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b9f6941c-ef26-4cc7-ab9f-f0c3ca3b8aef" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Lake Leschenaultia is a man-made lake constructed in 1897 as key infrastructure for the Western Australian Government Railways and holds approximately 520 million litres of water.  

It is the largest reservoir constructed on the Eastern Railway line and supplied water to steam trains for almost 50 years. Since 1949 it has been used as a recreation area for both locals, interstate and overseas visitors. Many locals learned to swim at the Lake, especially before the 1960s when there were no public swimming pools available locally. 

In 2005, Lake Leschenaultia gained a heritage listing based on the railway history, recreational significance and other factors. In 2006, the 40m timber jetty (constructed in 1971) was removed due to safety issues and has since been replaced with a pontoon.

The name "Leschenaultia" comes from the lake colour's resemblance to the Blue Leschenaultia flower.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/42fd9276-62a9-4347-b77e-082b8ff999d6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Having just moved back to WA and being located in the Chidlow area, I thought what better than to show off some of the local features and sites of this great little town.

I have also added a Bonus Cache to find after finishing the adventure.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/03935ba7-9e75-45aa-9c5b-83c03303cef8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Great work and well done.

You will need the code word "SAYS"&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.862733" lon="116.267017">
  <ele>298.0</ele>
  <time>2022-05-18T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBQ9bu-05</name>
  <desc>WelcomeToChidl5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/78383dcb-c760-475c-84ed-ce088db462f2</url>
  <urlname>Welcome to Chidlow : S5 Railway Reserve and Park by GeoNut5</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909754" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Welcome to Chidlow : S5 Railway Reserve and Park</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>GeoNut5</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">GeoNut5</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Welcome to Chidlow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Railway Reserve and Park&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/78383dcb-c760-475c-84ed-ce088db462f2"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/78383dcb-c760-475c-84ed-ce088db462f2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;When year was the second section of railway completed?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/030909da-de88-459c-9877-d7dcc74f21f9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Chidlow Well Railway Station was completed in 1884 and was listed as a refreshment stop on the timetable. It was also an important stop for watering of the trains from the well and the huge water towers in the station.  These demands on Chidlow's Well led to Lake Leschenaultia being created in 1898 as a railway reservoir, where water was pumped by steam-powered pumps into the station yard water towers. The railway made the forest area more accessible and by 1898 there more than 14 licensed sleeper cutters working from the Chidlow area.  

Many of the sleepers from Chidlow were used in goldfields railways and mine shafts.  Orchardists were the next generation of workers to populate the area as the soil was found to be extremely productive.  

Chidlow was a major factor in the rapid growth of fruit exports from WA between 1907 – 1914, and the success of the fruit growing industry reflected in the growth of the township after the turn of the century.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/42fd9276-62a9-4347-b77e-082b8ff999d6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Having just moved back to WA and being located in the Chidlow area, I thought what better than to show off some of the local features and sites of this great little town.

I have also added a Bonus Cache to find after finishing the adventure.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c3c544ba-e349-4960-b3f2-993e634c7e9f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Great work and well done.

You will need the code word "CHIDLOW"&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.8624" lon="116.268067">
