  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/78383dcb-c760-475c-84ed-ce088db462f2</url>
  <urlname>Welcome to Chidlow : S2 Chidlow Tavern by GeoNut5</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909748" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Welcome to Chidlow : S2 Chidlow Tavern</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>GeoNut5</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">GeoNut5</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Welcome to Chidlow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Chidlow Tavern&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/78383dcb-c760-475c-84ed-ce088db462f2"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/78383dcb-c760-475c-84ed-ce088db462f2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is written in LARGE letters on the boards above the entrance?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e551d56f-8b5f-4c2c-bc29-0ec76c35e976" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Chidlow Tavern was opened in 1884 and was originally called The Oxford Inn before assuming its current name in 1973.

It sits right on the footpath in Thomas Street Chidlow, opposite the Railway Reserve Heritage Trail where Chidlow's Wells Station once stood. The building is single-storey brick, with simple timber detailing to the front veranda, doors and windows. The roof is of corrugated iron with a hipped form that continues down to form the veranda without any break in pitch. Projecting rooms to the front and side also have hipped roofs extending out from the main roof structure. The main entry into the hotel is from a door on the veranda with stained glass panels and sidelights.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/42fd9276-62a9-4347-b77e-082b8ff999d6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Having just moved back to WA and being located in the Chidlow area, I thought what better than to show off some of the local features and sites of this great little town.

I have also added a Bonus Cache to find after finishing the adventure.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5c7fcd7b-2150-404c-b0b1-933523d6f6b4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Awesome and well done!!!

You will need the code word "RULES"&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.862167" lon="116.269117">
  <ele>307.0</ele>
  <time>2022-05-18T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBQ9bu-01</name>
  <desc>WelcomeToChidl1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/78383dcb-c760-475c-84ed-ce088db462f2</url>
  <urlname>Welcome to Chidlow : S1 Chidlow Well by GeoNut5</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909746" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Welcome to Chidlow : S1 Chidlow Well</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>GeoNut5</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">GeoNut5</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Welcome to Chidlow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Chidlow Well&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/78383dcb-c760-475c-84ed-ce088db462f2"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/78383dcb-c760-475c-84ed-ce088db462f2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What date is written on the plaque at the given coordinates?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ab408de6-f022-46ec-8bd0-a13a65d64d0d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The well commemorates pioneer, William Chidlow. 

The Chidlow townsite was originally named Chidlow's Well after a small waterhole near the old Northam road. The watering place had been known to travellers for many years and was named after a pioneer family of Northam. Settlement began in 1883 when it became known that Chidlow's Well was to be the terminus of the second section of the Eastern Railway. The railway station and townsite were changed from Chidlow's well to Chidlow in 1920.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/42fd9276-62a9-4347-b77e-082b8ff999d6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Having just moved back to WA and being located in the Chidlow area, I thought what better than to show off some of the local features and sites of this great little town.

I have also added a Bonus Cache to find after finishing the adventure.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c3174f6b-5d53-4b8f-8411-601da9d3753b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Great work and well done.

You will need the code word "GEONUT"&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.82015" lon="116.256067">
  <ele>264.0</ele>
  <time>2022-05-18T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBQ9bu-04</name>
  <desc>WelcomeToChidl4</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/78383dcb-c760-475c-84ed-ce088db462f2</url>
  <urlname>Welcome to Chidlow : S4 Karakamia Sanctuary by GeoNut5</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909752" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Welcome to Chidlow : S4 Karakamia Sanctuary</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>GeoNut5</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">GeoNut5</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Welcome to Chidlow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Karakamia Sanctuary&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/78383dcb-c760-475c-84ed-ce088db462f2"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/78383dcb-c760-475c-84ed-ce088db462f2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What isn't permitted?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d78459c9-4913-43eb-ae47-fdd8eb141d60" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Karakamia Sanctuary is a 2.75 km² nature reserve within the Jarrah forest of the Darling Scarp and is owned and managed by the Australian Wildlife Conservancy.

A visit to Karakamia Wildlife Sanctuary is like going back in time to experience the bush as it was 200 years ago, before the arrival of feral animals.  The sanctuary is 268 ha surrounded by a vermin-proof fence: feral animals have been eradicated providing a safe haven where many threatened mammals can now thrive.

Here you can observe critically endangered mammals such as Woylies and Western Ringtail Possums and also catch a glimpse of Quenda, and Tammar Wallabies, foraging together on the forest floor under towering Jarrah and Marri trees. Listen to the Red-tailed Black Cockatoos chortle in chorus as the sun goes down, then try to catch a glimpse of tiny microbats darting and dashing along the bush tracks as they chase a tasty mosquito or other morsel.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/42fd9276-62a9-4347-b77e-082b8ff999d6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Having just moved back to WA and being located in the Chidlow area, I thought what better than to show off some of the local features and sites of this great little town.

I have also added a Bonus Cache to find after finishing the adventure.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9f140018-d809-4ca9-baea-58a1ab3e6559" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Great work and well done.

You will need the code word "FIVE"&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-33.319417" lon="115.632983">
  <ele>18.0</ele>
  <time>2022-05-28T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBZDbm-05</name>
  <desc>BeachesOfBunbu5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f57c3292-16fb-45e9-87e1-7b463235590f</url>
  <urlname>Beaches of Bunbury : S5 Lighthouse Beach by SVKR_WA</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99003619" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Beaches of Bunbury : S5 Lighthouse Beach</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>SVKR_WA</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">SVKR_WA</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Beaches of Bunbury&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Lighthouse Beach&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f57c3292-16fb-45e9-87e1-7b463235590f"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f57c3292-16fb-45e9-87e1-7b463235590f&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;On the directional sign, how far how far is it to Point Casuarina? (numbers only)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4237b612-c638-4bad-a5c9-480a26dc5bfe" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This part of the beach is a little less popular.  However, there is still often people walking along the beach and the paths.  Nearby is the iconic Bunbury Lighthouse that the beach is named after.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/bcbff0d4-3ac0-4509-80e1-a912db6dacca" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to Bunbury.  One of my favourite parts of this city is Ocean Drive.  Ocean Drive takes you past some fabulous beaches.  Whether you like to swim, surf, cycle, walk or just sit and contemplate life, you'll find a perfect spot at one of the beaches along Ocean Drive.

So drive, walk cycle or even grab one of the many e-scooters available for hire along this stretch.  You will pass a number of traditional geocaches, earthcaches, cafes, a pub, plus many spots to access the beaches, or to sit and watch the water.

Maybe you'll spot a whale, or some ships lining up to enter the port.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/87121ef8-23d6-44d1-afe5-cb3fba67326f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done.  Take a walk up to the lighthouse.  Don't forget the geocache nearby.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-33.322167" lon="115.631317">
  <ele>7.0</ele>
  <time>2022-05-28T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBZDbm-04</name>
  <desc>BeachesOfBunbu4</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f57c3292-16fb-45e9-87e1-7b463235590f</url>
  <urlname>Beaches of Bunbury : S4 Wyalup - Rocky Point by SVKR_WA</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99003617" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Beaches of Bunbury : S4 Wyalup - Rocky Point</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>SVKR_WA</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">SVKR_WA</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Beaches of Bunbury&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Wyalup - Rocky Point&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f57c3292-16fb-45e9-87e1-7b463235590f"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f57c3292-16fb-45e9-87e1-7b463235590f&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;On the Beach side of this structure is a small plaque.  Who is it "In Loving Memory" of?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d0f3839f-4f4a-42ae-8d55-0be31ad338ed" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Wyalup Rocky Point is a place of Indigenous significance. Wyalup means a ‘place of mourning’ as in the past the area was a Noongar burial ground. The waves plummet over these ancient and rare rock formations. Sunset time is the best, where the light creeps down over the evening landscape, providing a dramatic backdrop.

With plenty of facilities, this park and beach is a great family spot.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/bcbff0d4-3ac0-4509-80e1-a912db6dacca" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to Bunbury.  One of my favourite parts of this city is Ocean Drive.  Ocean Drive takes you past some fabulous beaches.  Whether you like to swim, surf, cycle, walk or just sit and contemplate life, you'll find a perfect spot at one of the beaches along Ocean Drive.

So drive, walk cycle or even grab one of the many e-scooters available for hire along this stretch.  You will pass a number of traditional geocaches, earthcaches, cafes, a pub, plus many spots to access the beaches, or to sit and watch the water.

Maybe you'll spot a whale, or some ships lining up to enter the port.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/29234a96-5ad1-4748-aaa8-37173207762f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Nice work.  Take a seat here and look out at the ocean.  

Don't forget to grab the Earthcache and Whereigo caches nearby.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
