   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Gnarojin Park&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;FIRST ANZAC SERVICE &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3ceca63a-26c5-46da-b133-8ce72c89dd30"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3ceca63a-26c5-46da-b133-8ce72c89dd30&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What Year was on the tile?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7e9dd0b7-fd01-4fbd-bed6-1316c45a7ada" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Narrogin's first observance of Anzac Day was held in ----.
It took the form of a service conducted by the combined
Protestant churches in the town hall, with an impassioned
address by the mayor Dr Mackie.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ce526394-5db9-405a-b1f4-b5edb31147b3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Newton House Barbecue stands on the site of the original Newton family home, build in the early 1900's. It recreates the elements of a pioneer home - the stone chimney matters stove. water tank and kitchen table - representing comfort and shelter. surrounding the  house is an old fashioned country garden. 
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4ab81afa-ccbe-4787-a051-c53c7385b1de" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations on completing this stage. - well done.
Please check the bonus cache at GC9VXC4&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
