   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Welcome to Narrogin&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Migrant Camp&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/06cef230-1579-45bf-80d4-a688189fdcae"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/06cef230-1579-45bf-80d4-a688189fdcae&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many nationalities are listed on the board&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/39ed8d3d-ee1f-4b7c-8683-7da208c1585f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This site near here was tent camp of many migrants who worked or the WAGR nearby.
Prior to the migrants - nearby at Popanyinning there was a prisoner of war camp which also supplied workers to the Railways before the migrants came.  There are a lot of names still here within the town.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7da06754-2acf-4ffe-822b-df860ab943ce" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A bit of the history of our town 
Of days gone by.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6cc45891-fecd-4c0d-9bbf-e68416a468b6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations.   Bonus cache coming up!!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
