   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Welcome to Narrogin&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Brickworks&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/06cef230-1579-45bf-80d4-a688189fdcae"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/06cef230-1579-45bf-80d4-a688189fdcae&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The full name of the Overseer buried here somewhere&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f3a957b9-1d60-4c10-95dd-8a1c7870c676" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The existing brickwork are built on the site of the originals brickworks established about 1900.
Here Charles Quartermaine, one of the earliest residents in Narrogin his block here in 1872.  It was used as the exchange depot between York and Katanning.   There is a grave listed here, but unfortunately nothing remains now.  He was one of Quatermaine's overseers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7da06754-2acf-4ffe-822b-df860ab943ce" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A bit of the history of our town 
Of days gone by.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6fc6979d-31a7-4034-ade2-4149742fabca" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Congratulations.  Coordinates for - Narrogin Love the Life Bonus Cache -
S32 56.756 E117 11.458
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
