   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Arthur River&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;A Vital Link&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/05ae21a4-6bc6-41d8-8732-111e6342d805"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/05ae21a4-6bc6-41d8-8732-111e6342d805&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Arthur River Facts - Third Dot form - what are the  two Last words?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5b4799b4-24d7-4e81-baf3-d8275ad3ba31" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The towns post office originally operated out of the inn. Mary Ann Spratt was appointed as the post mistress in 1866. The post office itself was not gazetted until 1892 which was the same year that the telegraph line was connected. The first telephone subscriber service commenced in 1913.

Please look at the sign - "Arthur River Facts"&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6140f09d-8a22-4c9b-ad16-0f430e06d102" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The towns post office originally operated out of the inn. Mary Ann Spratt was appointed as the post mistress in 1866. The post office itself was not gazetted until 1892 which was the same year that the telegraph line was connected. The first telephone subscriber service commenced in 1913.

When the Great Southern Railway opened in 1889, much of the existing trade moved to new railway towns further east and many of the centres along the old "Coach Road" closed.

A bridge over the Arthur River was built in 1907 at Nobles Crossing.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/130fc456-00ae-4aae-aaad-cbbf5d8ce350" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well Done!.

Bonus S33 20. ___&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
