  <desc>ArthurRiverS2AR</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/05ae21a4-6bc6-41d8-8732-111e6342d805</url>
  <urlname>Arthur River : S2 A Rendezvous for farmers by skyejam</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99003693" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Arthur River : S2 A Rendezvous for farmers</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>skyejam</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">skyejam</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Arthur River&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;A Rendezvous for farmers &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/05ae21a4-6bc6-41d8-8732-111e6342d805"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/05ae21a4-6bc6-41d8-8732-111e6342d805&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Arthur River Facts - First dot form - John Cronin arrived in the colony in 1855 aged  __ ?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0664a965-0cd2-437a-b918-cf2857a1d39f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The legacy
The Trimming family demolished the Inn building in 1934 and the stones were used to build the Arthur River Hall. The Kitchen still stands and is one of the oldest buildings on the Albany Highway. It was built separate from the main Inn building to reduce the chance of accidental fire damage. There was no running water when the Inn was built so water had to be drawn from the well which can still be seen today. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6140f09d-8a22-4c9b-ad16-0f430e06d102" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The towns post office originally operated out of the inn. Mary Ann Spratt was appointed as the post mistress in 1866. The post office itself was not gazetted until 1892 which was the same year that the telegraph line was connected. The first telephone subscriber service commenced in 1913.

When the Great Southern Railway opened in 1889, much of the existing trade moved to new railway towns further east and many of the centres along the old "Coach Road" closed.

A bridge over the Arthur River was built in 1907 at Nobles Crossing.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4143e1a3-4002-4ed4-9f17-7866c18864a7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well Done!

Bonus :- E117 02. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
