 <wpt lat="-33.346467" lon="117.03745">
  <ele>320.0</ele>
  <time>2022-06-13T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBXyjR-05</name>
  <desc>ArthurRiverS5On</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/05ae21a4-6bc6-41d8-8732-111e6342d805</url>
  <urlname>Arthur River : S5 On the back of sheep by skyejam</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99003699" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Arthur River : S5 On the back of sheep</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>skyejam</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">skyejam</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Arthur River&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;On the back of sheep&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/05ae21a4-6bc6-41d8-8732-111e6342d805"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/05ae21a4-6bc6-41d8-8732-111e6342d805&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What the year - cricket pitch built ? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/fb314052-724b-43c9-a29a-546a05409f90" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Wandering Shepherds
Like many parts of regional Western Australia sheep were a vital Part of the local economy. One of the mayor issues facing the pastoralists in the area was ensuring that their herds were kept safe and away from areas of poison. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6140f09d-8a22-4c9b-ad16-0f430e06d102" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The towns post office originally operated out of the inn. Mary Ann Spratt was appointed as the post mistress in 1866. The post office itself was not gazetted until 1892 which was the same year that the telegraph line was connected. The first telephone subscriber service commenced in 1913.

When the Great Southern Railway opened in 1889, much of the existing trade moved to new railway towns further east and many of the centres along the old "Coach Road" closed.

A bridge over the Arthur River was built in 1907 at Nobles Crossing.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/eeee235f-243f-40f9-8461-53891d79b77c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well Done!

&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-33.306833" lon="117.329967">
  <ele>272.0</ele>
  <time>2022-06-11T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBbv7K-01</name>
  <desc>LWaginS1TheWagi</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e9339261-b5e0-4d77-8ae1-b118dcf1261a</url>
  <urlname>[L] Wagin : S1 The Wagin War Memorial by sevabo</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99003711" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] Wagin : S1 The Wagin War Memorial</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>sevabo</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">sevabo</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Wagin&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Wagin War Memorial &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e9339261-b5e0-4d77-8ae1-b118dcf1261a"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e9339261-b5e0-4d77-8ae1-b118dcf1261a&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;In 1949 a further "__" were added. (what number)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/349c3d69-ccdc-4b87-bd4d-774210f03010" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The monument commemorates those who died in service or were killed in action in World Wars One and Two. It was moved to its present position when the Wagin Swimming Pool was constructed in 1967.
The Wagin War Memorial was unveiled in Piesse Park by the Governor Sir Willam Campion on the 29th March 1925 and paid tribute to 64 fallen heroes. The memorial was dedicated by the Reverend W.E. Moorhouse .
The West Australian (Perth), 31st March 1925.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a530fa34-ca3e-4af9-a540-53a6a466367e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The name of the town is derived from Wagin Lake, a usually dry salt lake south of the town. The lake's name is of Noongar origin, and was first recorded by a surveyor in 1869–72. It means "place of emus", or "site of the foot tracks from when the emu sat down".
The town itself came into existence after the construction of the Great Southern Railway which was completed in 1889 with the town originally called Wagin Lake.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8cb68f1b-1bac-4f4e-afc9-d8deaac477a6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well Done !&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
