   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Waterfalls and Rapids&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Lesmurdie Falls&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7f15a1f3-fda5-4858-b478-c635f52f22ee"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7f15a1f3-fda5-4858-b478-c635f52f22ee&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What structure can you see at the top of the falls?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/271fc08a-f33a-46ee-b77b-4d849563dd2c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Being arguably the best waterfall Perth has to offer, this popular hike is a must do for those looking for a quick escape from the city. You can start at either car park on the top or bottom, depending on how you want to walk it. There is a defined path which will take you up or down the side of the falls, giving you stunning views the entire way. At the top are multiple trails which take you to vantage points of Perth below and you can even walk to Lions Lookout nearby! As with all of these waterfalls, it is even more spectacular after heavy rainfall.

Distance: Numerous trails starting at 1km
Recommended for: Beginners&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/38a3bbf1-4aa8-494d-97b9-f8694299312b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;If you’ve found yourself a clear day after a heavy downpour, the best thing you can do is hop in your car and get yourself to one of these waterfall hikes as soon as possible! Perth has a good collection of waterfalls within its hills, snuggled up against the scarp, some higher than others but all set in beautiful natural bushlands.
Pack a picnic, your hiking boots, walking poles and don't forget your camera. 

*Please note: all but one of these locations will require a short hike, sometimes over rough ground.*
Source: https://perthisok.com/best-of-wa/the-best-waterfall-hikes-in-perth/&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/fb7b602c-b363-44f9-a3b6-17e5b3e04799" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;The falls are beautiful after rain. Have you done the Lesmurdie Falls Adventure Lab created by Paskersfind? It is really close by!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.976883" lon="116.024617">
  <ele>75.0</ele>
  <time>2022-06-24T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBSg4d-03</name>
  <desc>WaterfallsAndR3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7f15a1f3-fda5-4858-b478-c635f52f22ee</url>
  <urlname>Waterfalls and Rapids : S3 Whistlepipe Gully by Boyzrule5</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909760" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Waterfalls and Rapids : S3 Whistlepipe Gully</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Boyzrule5</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Boyzrule5</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Waterfalls and Rapids&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Whistlepipe Gully&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7f15a1f3-fda5-4858-b478-c635f52f22ee"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7f15a1f3-fda5-4858-b478-c635f52f22ee&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is depicted on the pink square&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/346c4db1-5fb9-4d6e-8832-b5204e5b3ca2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Situated in Lesmurdie, this walk follows the stream most of the way until you reach a small waterfall at the end with stunning views of the Swan Coastal Plain and city. You will be treated with smaller waterfalls along the route and can return along the other side allowing for a change of scenery and a beautiful overgrown wonderland at the very end. Interestingly, will see the remains of a once existing Japanese styled cottage.

Distance: 3.5km return walk
Recommended for: Beginners&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/38a3bbf1-4aa8-494d-97b9-f8694299312b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;If you’ve found yourself a clear day after a heavy downpour, the best thing you can do is hop in your car and get yourself to one of these waterfall hikes as soon as possible! Perth has a good collection of waterfalls within its hills, snuggled up against the scarp, some higher than others but all set in beautiful natural bushlands.
Pack a picnic, your hiking boots, walking poles and don't forget your camera. 

*Please note: all but one of these locations will require a short hike, sometimes over rough ground.*
Source: https://perthisok.com/best-of-wa/the-best-waterfall-hikes-in-perth/&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1b3887a0-3b42-4a6e-a18c-28362e3eb0f2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Great work; it's a nice easy walk with the sound of the water falling nearby.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.95185" lon="115.847683">
  <ele>40.0</ele>
  <time>2022-06-26T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBe1XU-01</name>
  <desc>ParliamentaryP1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/391865c9-d460-4d93-9ca7-961ff6c6be0a</url>
  <urlname>Parliamentary Precinct : S1 Parliament House by familysteiner</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-363" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Parliamentary Precinct : S1 Parliament House</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>familysteiner</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">familysteiner</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Parliamentary Precinct&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Parliament House&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/391865c9-d460-4d93-9ca7-961ff6c6be0a"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/391865c9-d460-4d93-9ca7-961ff6c6be0a&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Who was the Leader of the Opposition at the time of the Complex completion? (3 words)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/eacd85b3-c8bf-4384-b82a-963b7edf1f4a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Parliament House is the home of the Parliament of Western Australia, including the Legislative Council (upper house) and Legislative Assembly (lower house). The original building features Greek Revival architecture elements, and was built between 1902 and 1094. Extensions have been added over subsequent years. 

This Ad Lab waypoint will take you to the terrace outside the front steps of Parliament House, where you will find a plaque on the wall commemorating the completion of the Complex in 1971.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9a06c184-2795-46b2-9e9c-7d7307bfab89" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Adventure Lab will take you to some key locations within the Parliamentary Precinct. As well as being home to WA State Government buildings, it boasts lovely gardens and grassed areas, as well as views over the CBD. Take your time to explore this heritage-rich precinct&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/155852d6-68cc-4540-a477-2296cea5b52a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;CORRECT! 
Congratulations. Did you know that visitors to Parliament can also
take tours of the House?&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.951683" lon="115.84615">
  <ele>48.0</ele>
  <time>2022-06-26T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBe1XU-02</name>
  <desc>ParliamentaryP2</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/391865c9-d460-4d93-9ca7-961ff6c6be0a</url>
  <urlname>Parliamentary Precinct : S2 Solidarity Park by familysteiner</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-364" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Parliamentary Precinct : S2 Solidarity Park</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>familysteiner</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">familysteiner</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Parliamentary Precinct&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Solidarity Park&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/391865c9-d460-4d93-9ca7-961ff6c6be0a"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/391865c9-d460-4d93-9ca7-961ff6c6be0a&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What single word is written on the third last line of Mark Allen's poem?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f11e2860-6d36-4d0c-bd90-64925e675746" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Solidarity Park is located opposite Parliament House. In 1997 a "Workers Embassy" was set up on some vacant land opposite the Parliament House during union protests of the Court Government's "third wave" legislation for industrial relations. What began with a caravan and portable barbecue soon transformed into a landscaped shelter with a monument to the trade union workers who have died during their work.

At this waypoint, you will find a memorial to Mark F. Allen, Trade Union Organiser for the BLF/CFMEU who lost his life in 1996 trying to protect the safety of workers. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9a06c184-2795-46b2-9e9c-7d7307bfab89" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Adventure Lab will take you to some key locations within the Parliamentary Precinct. As well as being home to WA State Government buildings, it boasts lovely gardens and grassed areas, as well as views over the CBD. Take your time to explore this heritage-rich precinct&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ac81d9de-00b3-4f66-b82a-db45a235cc87" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;CORRECT!
Congratulations. Take time to look at the Memorial Wall, built on 21 June 1997, which commemorates all killed and injured workers.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.953317" lon="115.84435">
  <ele>91.0</ele>
  <time>2022-06-26T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBe1XU-05</name>
  <desc>ParliamentaryP5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/391865c9-d460-4d93-9ca7-961ff6c6be0a</url>
  <urlname>Parliamentary Precinct : S5 Dumas House by familysteiner</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-367" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Parliamentary Precinct : S5 Dumas House</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>familysteiner</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">familysteiner</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Parliamentary Precinct&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Dumas House&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/391865c9-d460-4d93-9ca7-961ff6c6be0a"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/391865c9-d460-4d93-9ca7-961ff6c6be0a&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;From which floor of Dumas House was this plaque relocated? (Two digits)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3f18ef94-f9f2-4162-aaca-09008617bcac" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Dumas House is a fourteen-storey public office building opened in 1965. Constructed in the Post-War International style, it was built by the State Government and has been occupied by various Government departments since opening. In 1978, Government Building was named Dumas House in honour of Sir Russell Dumas (1887-1975), former Public Works Department Director of Works and Buildings.

After 50 years the building was showing signs of deterioration and from 2014 a four year process commenced to remediate the deterioration and to conserve the building. In the 2019 Architecture Awards, the project was awarded a commendation for conservation of a significant 20th century heritage building.

At this waypoint, you will find a plaque mounted on a pedestal. 
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9a06c184-2795-46b2-9e9c-7d7307bfab89" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Adventure Lab will take you to some key locations within the Parliamentary Precinct. As well as being home to WA State Government buildings, it boasts lovely gardens and grassed areas, as well as views over the CBD. Take your time to explore this heritage-rich precinct&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f4b4414b-10f1-40d9-9571-b17159398e48" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;CORRECT!
Congratulations. Did you know that the 14th floor once had a promenade deck (Legacy Lookout) which became a tourist attraction?&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.951817" lon="115.845617">
  <ele>57.0</ele>
  <time>2022-06-26T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBe1XU-03</name>
  <desc>ParliamentaryP3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/391865c9-d460-4d93-9ca7-961ff6c6be0a</url>
  <urlname>Parliamentary Precinct : S3 Hale House by familysteiner</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-365" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Parliamentary Precinct : S3 Hale House</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>familysteiner</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">familysteiner</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Parliamentary Precinct&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Hale House&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/391865c9-d460-4d93-9ca7-961ff6c6be0a"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/391865c9-d460-4d93-9ca7-961ff6c6be0a&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What did Mr F. C. Faulkner state were "quite as essential as a good mind"? (2 words)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1e517d87-e1d9-46a5-9999-f301d3abb2e0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; Hale House was originally home to Western Australia's first secondary education facility and boarding house, Hale School, opening in 1914. The site had always been considered small from the beginning, and with student numbers continuing to grow, a location for a new and large school complex was secured in Wembley Downs in 1938. However due to the outbreak of WW2, work on the new site was delayed. Hale School remained at West Perth until 1958 when the new school was finally completed and the students were relocated.

At this waypoint you will find several interpretive signs surrounding Hale House which provide details of the building's history and an insight into boarding house life.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9a06c184-2795-46b2-9e9c-7d7307bfab89" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Adventure Lab will take you to some key locations within the Parliamentary Precinct. As well as being home to WA State Government buildings, it boasts lovely gardens and grassed areas, as well as views over the CBD. Take your time to explore this heritage-rich precinct&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1815aec0-f818-4134-bbc8-bee5928a5809" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;CORRECT!
Congratulations. Take the time to examine the scholastic style of architecture presented here, rarely found in WA.

&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.952667" lon="115.844467">
  <ele>61.0</ele>
  <time>2022-06-26T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBe1XU-04</name>
  <desc>ParliamentaryP4</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/391865c9-d460-4d93-9ca7-961ff6c6be0a</url>
  <urlname>Parliamentary Precinct : S4 The original Perth Observatory by familysteiner</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-366" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Parliamentary Precinct : S4 The original Perth Observatory</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>familysteiner</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">familysteiner</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Parliamentary Precinct&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The original Perth Observatory&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/391865c9-d460-4d93-9ca7-961ff6c6be0a"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/391865c9-d460-4d93-9ca7-961ff6c6be0a&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the Architect who designed the Government Astronomer's Residence &amp; Offices? (3 words)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/87817460-a353-470a-a008-f5ade0e7d48b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The original Perth Observatory was constructed in 1896 and was officially opened in 1900 by John Forrest, the first premier of Western Australia. Its chief roles were keeping Standard Time for Western Australia and meteorological data collection. The observatory dome was demolished in the 1960s to make way for Dumas House, after the Observatory of the city was relocated to Bickley in 1965. The house of the chief astronomer of the old observatory remains today, the current tenant is the National Trust

At this waypoint, you will find a plaque explaining the history of the buildings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9a06c184-2795-46b2-9e9c-7d7307bfab89" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Adventure Lab will take you to some key locations within the Parliamentary Precinct. As well as being home to WA State Government buildings, it boasts lovely gardens and grassed areas, as well as views over the CBD. Take your time to explore this heritage-rich precinct&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/13dde25a-7b3c-40cc-9bf9-eb5ff6e3dc8b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;CORRECT!
Congratulations.  Did you know that a cannon was fired here at 1pm every day to help keep people's clocks accurate? &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.771967" lon="116.062767">
  <ele>21.0</ele>
  <time>2022-06-24T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBSg4d-05</name>
  <desc>WaterfallsAndR5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7f15a1f3-fda5-4858-b478-c635f52f22ee</url>
  <urlname>Waterfalls and Rapids : S5 Bells Rapids by Boyzrule5</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909764" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Waterfalls and Rapids : S5 Bells Rapids</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Boyzrule5</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Boyzrule5</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Waterfalls and Rapids&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Bells Rapids&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7f15a1f3-fda5-4858-b478-c635f52f22ee"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7f15a1f3-fda5-4858-b478-c635f52f22ee&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The river walk is how many meters uphill? (Numeric)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/973aa561-f531-4e23-9d84-6bc5782ec754" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A walk bridge spanning the Swan River over the white water rapids make this an exciting viewing spot during the Avon Descent. Perfect for a picnic and bushwalk or that special day out.

There are two unique Bell's Rapid circuit walk trails - the 2.5km River walk and the 3km Goat walk. The site is noted for providing fantastic vantage points for the annual Avon Descent. Walkers can enjoy scenic views of Bells Rapids, the countryside and coastal plains, with beautiful grey kangaroos at certain times of the year.

Distance: About 1km
Recommended for: The adventurous
Source: www.swanvalley.com.au&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/38a3bbf1-4aa8-494d-97b9-f8694299312b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;If you’ve found yourself a clear day after a heavy downpour, the best thing you can do is hop in your car and get yourself to one of these waterfall hikes as soon as possible! Perth has a good collection of waterfalls within its hills, snuggled up against the scarp, some higher than others but all set in beautiful natural bushlands.
Pack a picnic, your hiking boots, walking poles and don't forget your camera. 

*Please note: all but one of these locations will require a short hike, sometimes over rough ground.*
Source: https://perthisok.com/best-of-wa/the-best-waterfall-hikes-in-perth/&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d28e25f6-005d-4646-94d8-c40ad019d135" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Fantastic work; did you know the 'A swing through Swan' Adventure Lab created by Sir Fancy is not too far away.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.368917" lon="116.001183">
