  <urlname>Waterfalls and Rapids : S1 Serpentine Falls by Boyzrule5</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909756" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Waterfalls and Rapids : S1 Serpentine Falls</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Boyzrule5</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Boyzrule5</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Waterfalls and Rapids&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Serpentine Falls&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7f15a1f3-fda5-4858-b478-c635f52f22ee"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7f15a1f3-fda5-4858-b478-c635f52f22ee&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What number do you dial before you dig? (numeric)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/90d38ef2-fda3-4a90-9359-e1f5ac6a35c3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Situated just over 50 minutes from Perth is this hidden oasis. You can choose from one of three walks in the area. A short paved trail will take you from the carpark to the falls, but if you have the time, the Baldwin’s Bluff is highly recommended. It is quite a steep track, but that being said, it is a beautiful hike and worth it for the stunning views over the falls at the end. 
Serpentine is the only one on this list with an entry fee, but it is definitely worth it for the sights and well maintained facilities including toilets and a barbecue area to make the trip worthwhile.
*No dogs (or other pets) allowed.*

Distance: 100m (car park walk) to 6km return (Baldwin’s Bluff)
Recommended for: All&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/38a3bbf1-4aa8-494d-97b9-f8694299312b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;If you’ve found yourself a clear day after a heavy downpour, the best thing you can do is hop in your car and get yourself to one of these waterfall hikes as soon as possible! Perth has a good collection of waterfalls within its hills, snuggled up against the scarp, some higher than others but all set in beautiful natural bushlands.
Pack a picnic, your hiking boots, walking poles and don't forget your camera. 

*Please note: all but one of these locations will require a short hike, sometimes over rough ground.*
Source: https://perthisok.com/best-of-wa/the-best-waterfall-hikes-in-perth/&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f8b76021-0f08-4986-b301-fed75e5aa7a5" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Well done, you can pay the entry and enjoy the surrounds or move on to the next location.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
