   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Millie’s Slides&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Kyilla Park&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9da10ede-8d03-484c-bcbb-395d52ac9410"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9da10ede-8d03-484c-bcbb-395d52ac9410&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What colour is the slide?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7528ba7e-1d63-4cf8-97aa-e81c6b46bc10" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;By far our closest park to home. When Millie is older we will be able to watch her from our second storey. Hugely busy on a Saturday morning as the park hosts a weekly farmer’s market. Busy at school breaks too since it’s dual use with school and community use.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/bcde3c90-f3de-49f8-b198-e0fa1b3e3acc" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are blessed to have plenty of parks within walking distance of home. We thought we would share some with you.

Family friendly. To enable those without children to visit each location, it is possible to walk on a paved, public path to answer each question. 

There is no need to enter any playground area, although you’re encouraged to do so. If your bum fits, slide I say.

&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
