   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Millie’s Slides&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Yokine Reserve&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9da10ede-8d03-484c-bcbb-395d52ac9410"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9da10ede-8d03-484c-bcbb-395d52ac9410&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What colour is the slide?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/bfd4cdeb-3dbc-4917-86fb-ea3b6f7b47cb" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The grandest reserve in the area. Far more extensive play areas are further west. This is also the start and finish of the Yokine Parkrun.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/bcde3c90-f3de-49f8-b198-e0fa1b3e3acc" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are blessed to have plenty of parks within walking distance of home. We thought we would share some with you.

Family friendly. To enable those without children to visit each location, it is possible to walk on a paved, public path to answer each question. 

There is no need to enter any playground area, although you’re encouraged to do so. If your bum fits, slide I say.

&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
