 <wpt lat="-32.9262" lon="117.078233">
  <ele>333.0</ele>
  <time>2022-06-28T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBaGH9-01</name>
  <desc>NGNMMRSS1Narrog</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/aa155a58-7237-492e-a955-664960fb5b19</url>
  <urlname>NGN MMRS : S1 Narrogin Gliding Club by Cirrus_WA</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909766" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>NGN MMRS : S1 Narrogin Gliding Club</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Cirrus_WA</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Cirrus_WA</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;NGN MMRS&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Narrogin Gliding Club&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/aa155a58-7237-492e-a955-664960fb5b19"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/aa155a58-7237-492e-a955-664960fb5b19&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the workshop at the NGC?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5fd7dde3-175a-4b86-84dd-025687a02184" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Gliding Club was formed in the 1960's however my family association started in 1983 when my parents having returned to Western Australia started calling the clubs and Narrogin answered the phone.

Over the years of attending the club my fondest memories are of sitting around the fire on winter nights, driving cars back to the clubhouse after long days at the far ends of the airfield (at age 8) and setting up cubby houses. Washing down the gliders at the start of each day and the long lines of aircraft waiting on the edge of the runway during the state championships.

It was here that I learned to ride a bike and fly planes; although lots has changed over the years, everything is still familiar.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/bf292e1c-19f3-4fc5-9d54-d65eeedbb258" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;BE AWARE: The airfield can be busy, especially on weekends, make sure you drive slowly and are aware of aircraft when walking around.

My childhood and youth are filled with memories of Friday afternoons piling into the car and heading down to Narrogin to spend the weekend at the gliding club. On occasions, summer holidays were spent in the town and its surrounds.

So many great stories were had here and in the town and this lab aims to share those memories with you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;To find the bonus cache you will need the following information:

V _ - _ _ _&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.926467" lon="117.079433">
  <ele>328.0</ele>
  <time>2022-06-28T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBaGH9-02</name>
  <desc>NGNMMRSS2Narrog</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/aa155a58-7237-492e-a955-664960fb5b19</url>
  <urlname>NGN MMRS : S2 Narrogin Aero Club by Cirrus_WA</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909768" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>NGN MMRS : S2 Narrogin Aero Club</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Cirrus_WA</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Cirrus_WA</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;NGN MMRS&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Narrogin Aero Club&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/aa155a58-7237-492e-a955-664960fb5b19"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/aa155a58-7237-492e-a955-664960fb5b19&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many bricks tall is the chimney of the bbq?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9608251a-8704-439a-8b10-84ee257d027d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Although I can't remember the year my lasting memory of the powered aircraft side of the airfield is from the mid-90s.

Flight operations for the afternoon were suspended when a call came over the radio that an Army plan was approaching the area on a training exercise.
15 minutes later the roar of 2 C-130 aircraft came along runway 36 depositing a number of jeeps along behind them on their passes.
Once the exercise was over the planes lined up with the jeeps and while we were given permission to explore the equipment the army cooked up a big feed for everyone on the bbq.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/bf292e1c-19f3-4fc5-9d54-d65eeedbb258" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;BE AWARE: The airfield can be busy, especially on weekends, make sure you drive slowly and are aware of aircraft when walking around.

My childhood and youth are filled with memories of Friday afternoons piling into the car and heading down to Narrogin to spend the weekend at the gliding club. On occasions, summer holidays were spent in the town and its surrounds.

So many great stories were had here and in the town and this lab aims to share those memories with you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Info for Bonus

_ H - _ _ _&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.930233" lon="117.17325">
  <ele>353.0</ele>
  <time>2022-06-28T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBaGH9-03</name>
  <desc>NGNMMRSS3Narrog</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/aa155a58-7237-492e-a955-664960fb5b19</url>
  <urlname>NGN MMRS : S3 Narrogin Swimming Pool by Cirrus_WA</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909770" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>NGN MMRS : S3 Narrogin Swimming Pool</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Cirrus_WA</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Cirrus_WA</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;NGN MMRS&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Narrogin Swimming Pool&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/aa155a58-7237-492e-a955-664960fb5b19"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/aa155a58-7237-492e-a955-664960fb5b19&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Who was the mayor of Narrogin when the recreation centre was opened on 23rd April 1983? (Full line no punctuation)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8dc8b924-509c-41e0-b1e7-23b76c681539" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Summer holidays were made better with afternoon trips to the pool in the afternoon heat.

The manager of the pools for years was Alby Timleris, I was always a little frightened of the large man at the front gate but Alby cared for everyone who entered his pools and made sure everyone was safe.
I remember one afternoon I finally garnered up the courage to go for a bombie off the high diving board, unfortunately, I didn't realise that bombie time was over and I was called over to the grass next to the office for 5 minutes time out.

Swimming was always made better when just before heading back to the club by purchasing some lollies or icecreams from the canteen.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/bf292e1c-19f3-4fc5-9d54-d65eeedbb258" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;BE AWARE: The airfield can be busy, especially on weekends, make sure you drive slowly and are aware of aircraft when walking around.

My childhood and youth are filled with memories of Friday afternoons piling into the car and heading down to Narrogin to spend the weekend at the gliding club. On occasions, summer holidays were spent in the town and its surrounds.

So many great stories were had here and in the town and this lab aims to share those memories with you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Info for Bonus

_ _ - T _ _&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.935983" lon="117.169517">
  <ele>375.0</ele>
