   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;NGN MMRS&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Narrogin Croissants&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/aa155a58-7237-492e-a955-664960fb5b19"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/aa155a58-7237-492e-a955-664960fb5b19&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year was the market established?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f3b8d91c-2ebc-4b19-83a8-30a7d37c9a18" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;One of the best things about a weekend in Narrogin was coming into town early on a Sunday morning with dad and heading here to collect tray fulls of croissants fresh out of the oven.

It got to the point where orders were prepared Friday night to ensure that there would be enough for everyone.

I had thought this place had closed as I was looking in the wrong part of town, after a conversation with the family discovered my error and was pleased to see it was still here.
I had a chat with the original owner and although he is retiring at the end of 2022 his daughter and son-in-law will be continuing the tradition into the future.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/bf292e1c-19f3-4fc5-9d54-d65eeedbb258" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;BE AWARE: The airfield can be busy, especially on weekends, make sure you drive slowly and are aware of aircraft when walking around.

My childhood and youth are filled with memories of Friday afternoons piling into the car and heading down to Narrogin to spend the weekend at the gliding club. On occasions, summer holidays were spent in the town and its surrounds.

So many great stories were had here and in the town and this lab aims to share those memories with you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Award Information&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;Award Message:&lt;br /&gt;Info for Bonus

_ _ - _ _ G&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
