 <wpt lat="-31.9497" lon="115.860667">
  <ele>26.0</ele>
  <time>2022-07-02T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LB1Nwy-04</name>
  <desc>NorthbridgeSte4</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f6d45c18-5aa4-4bd4-8d1e-55260ce64c18</url>
  <urlname>Northbridge Step Back in Time : S4 PICA- Perth Institute of Contemporary Arts by Meme28</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909927" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Northbridge Step Back in Time : S4 PICA- Perth Institute of Contemporary Arts</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Meme28</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Meme28</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Northbridge Step Back in Time&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;PICA- Perth Institute of Contemporary Arts&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f6d45c18-5aa4-4bd4-8d1e-55260ce64c18"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f6d45c18-5aa4-4bd4-8d1e-55260ce64c18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Look up- Who made the clock? If you cannot see it, the answer is in the description.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/743912ee-b249-464e-9914-7e30e7c2ee7c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The PICA building was designed in the Federation Free Classical style.

The building dates from 1896, and for 40 years was the Perth Boys' and Girls' School (one of several schools known collectively as Perth Central School). 

PICA began operating from the James Street building in 1988 with the main aim of promoting contemporary art (visual, performing or mixed) in Western Australia. It operates a year-round program of exhibitions, performances, and screenings, and offers a public education program. The Benson London clock remains as one of the original features.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d7d0fc34-4849-4953-b6c3-03e1c73d9263" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Like my last AdLab - Colonial Northbridge, I love the history of the area including how the buildings all have a story. Once you answer the question an older photo will pop up.
It was hard to cull my list, but I hope you enjoy wandering around the area...

30 minutes should be enough time for this walk...&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.9495" lon="115.860367">
  <ele>30.0</ele>
  <time>2022-07-02T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LB1Nwy-03</name>
  <desc>NorthbridgeSte3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f6d45c18-5aa4-4bd4-8d1e-55260ce64c18</url>
  <urlname>Northbridge Step Back in Time : S3 The West Australian Museum by Meme28</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909925" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Northbridge Step Back in Time : S3 The West Australian Museum</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Meme28</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Meme28</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Northbridge Step Back in Time&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The West Australian Museum&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f6d45c18-5aa4-4bd4-8d1e-55260ce64c18"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f6d45c18-5aa4-4bd4-8d1e-55260ce64c18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;From where you are standing, looking towards the museum, how many stairs are in front of you? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/15595532-3128-4d3f-9840-4b71d7b87e1a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Western Australian Museum has been in existence for over 120 years. 
Today, the Museum has seven public locations across our State – plus a Collection and Research Centre that houses more than eight million objects.

After a massive renovation, the WA Museum 'Boola Bardip' opened on Saturday 21 November 2020 with nine-days of celebration.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d7d0fc34-4849-4953-b6c3-03e1c73d9263" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Like my last AdLab - Colonial Northbridge, I love the history of the area including how the buildings all have a story. Once you answer the question an older photo will pop up.
It was hard to cull my list, but I hope you enjoy wandering around the area...

30 minutes should be enough time for this walk...&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
