   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Northbridge Step Back in Time&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Brass Monkey&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f6d45c18-5aa4-4bd4-8d1e-55260ce64c18"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f6d45c18-5aa4-4bd4-8d1e-55260ce64c18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Look up- How many floors (balconies) are there?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/230f6c3f-0d2a-43f4-8e29-c48e27894ab0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Federation Filigree Style building was constructed in 1896.

The three-storey hotel with its distinctive verandahs was deliberately located to capitalise on the ever-increasing trade coming through Perth Railway Station. After the Fremantle to Guildford line had been completed in 1881, activity moved away from the Swan River and into town next to the station.

https://heritageperth.com.au/properties
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d7d0fc34-4849-4953-b6c3-03e1c73d9263" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Like my last AdLab - Colonial Northbridge, I love the history of the area including how the buildings all have a story. Once you answer the question an older photo will pop up.
It was hard to cull my list, but I hope you enjoy wandering around the area...

30 minutes should be enough time for this walk...&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.946167" lon="115.86105">
  <ele>21.0</ele>
  <time>2022-07-02T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LB1Nwy-05</name>
  <desc>NorthbridgeSte5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f6d45c18-5aa4-4bd4-8d1e-55260ce64c18</url>
  <urlname>Northbridge Step Back in Time : S5 Perth Tramway Network by Meme28</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909929" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Northbridge Step Back in Time : S5 Perth Tramway Network</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Meme28</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Meme28</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Northbridge Step Back in Time&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Perth Tramway Network&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f6d45c18-5aa4-4bd4-8d1e-55260ce64c18"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f6d45c18-5aa4-4bd4-8d1e-55260ce64c18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Look up- How many clocks can you see on the corner?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/09d6f9e5-f1b2-48e4-be50-1088b977c7b3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Erected in 1935 in the Art Deco style, this building was originally the Midland Bus Co. depot and offices. 

The Perth tramway network served Perth, from 1899 until 1958. 

The network was initially run by a private company but was taken over by the state government in 1913. From a single line along Hay Street, the network expanded north as far as Osborne Park, east as far as Welshpool, south as far as Como, and west as far as Claremont. The tramways were gradually replaced by buses after World War II.


&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d7d0fc34-4849-4953-b6c3-03e1c73d9263" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Like my last AdLab - Colonial Northbridge, I love the history of the area including how the buildings all have a story. Once you answer the question an older photo will pop up.
It was hard to cull my list, but I hope you enjoy wandering around the area...

30 minutes should be enough time for this walk...&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.94795" lon="115.856833">
