   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Samuel's Ramble Around Wireless Hill&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Calling the world&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5949f316-1cb7-4105-b294-ca15e07aff7e"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5949f316-1cb7-4105-b294-ca15e07aff7e&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the 4th 'word' in this Morse Code?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7b899882-e997-45a6-ba30-2fedc839b5e3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The longer the words in a message the longer the message is to transmit so some common words and procedures were shortened for convenience.

This bench has an example of one kind of shortened morse code transmission. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3450fb1f-8d22-4efe-9c6e-36fa300036ab" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;At a recent geocaching event at Wireless Hill it was noticed that various tables and seats had symbols embedded on them that once translated detail information relating to the original European purpose of Wireless Hill.

This Adventure takes you around 5 of the seats.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
