   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Byford Sculptures Trail 1&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Child Health Sister &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d79447ae-a2be-4b70-96c8-517d6adbecf2"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d79447ae-a2be-4b70-96c8-517d6adbecf2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the child.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f5f2afdc-8a23-4621-9f06-12ae193ac011" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Sister Wossley looked after Byford's little ones from the  Byford hall in the 1940s.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ea1c5b33-6d18-4392-9ed4-f3a15cc60267" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Drive, walk or ride through Byford while taking in sculptures from internationally renowned WA artist Len Zuks.

Mr Zuks has had paintings exhibited at the Louvre in Paris, the Venice Biennale and the London Olympics art exhibition.

In 2009 he won the People’s Choice award at Sculptures by the Sea. After wide public consultation, he created Byford’s sculptures of historical figures from ideas put forward by Byford residents.

The works were commissioned by the Byford Progress Association with support from the Shire of Serpentine Jarrahdale.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
