  <desc>HistoryOfGingi3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e684a1d6-cdb0-44ff-acf5-64143cb90d72</url>
  <urlname>History of Gingin : S3 Gingin Post Office by Lachlan1.77</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909866" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>History of Gingin : S3 Gingin Post Office</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Lachlan1.77</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Lachlan1.77</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;History of Gingin&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Gingin Post Office&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e684a1d6-cdb0-44ff-acf5-64143cb90d72"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e684a1d6-cdb0-44ff-acf5-64143cb90d72&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year was the Post and Telegraph Office officially opened? (yyyy)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1144be24-485c-4449-92dd-82668952c6b1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Gingin Post Office is significant as a rare example of the Colonial Government's post office building program and is the oldest extant purpose built post office in Western Australia. It represents the vigorous lobbying by the Gingin community for its construction and the associated connection to the telegraph line from Perth to Geraldton. It represents the complementary association between police and postal service in the early development of public facilities. The residence demonstrates the role and lifestyle of the postmaster at the time.

You will find information to answer the question on the brown information sign to the south east of the post office building.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3a69ce78-35ff-45b8-b9af-e3631375a519" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Gingin is one of the oldest towns in the State, with explorers and pioneers arriving in 1831, just two years after the Swan River Colony was proclaimed. To this day Gingin retains some important remnants of its pioneering days dating back to the 1850s. Join us on a short tour of Gingin and some of its sites near Granville Park.

This Adventure Lab has bonus final cache located at another historical site in Gingin. Please refer to GC9V9CA (https://coord.info/GC9V9CA) for more information.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
