   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;History of Gingin&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Gingin Road Board&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e684a1d6-cdb0-44ff-acf5-64143cb90d72"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e684a1d6-cdb0-44ff-acf5-64143cb90d72&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year was the election to form the first Road Board held? (yyyy)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f264566c-b74b-4ada-a5d3-cac415e0f894" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Gingin Road Board Office (fmr) is significant in representing the development of the local government in 1911 and of continued development when it was vacated in 1968 for new premises. It has a social and civic significance for the associations with staff and elected members throughout that period.

You will find information to answer the question on the brown information sign in front of the building.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3a69ce78-35ff-45b8-b9af-e3631375a519" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Gingin is one of the oldest towns in the State, with explorers and pioneers arriving in 1831, just two years after the Swan River Colony was proclaimed. To this day Gingin retains some important remnants of its pioneering days dating back to the 1850s. Join us on a short tour of Gingin and some of its sites near Granville Park.

This Adventure Lab has bonus final cache located at another historical site in Gingin. Please refer to GC9V9CA (https://coord.info/GC9V9CA) for more information.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.579933" lon="117.85465">
  <ele>292.0</ele>
