  <name>LBzwHD-01</name>
  <desc>GoldenPipelinek</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/04f53c66-c21a-4ce4-9e36-f30669bde873</url>
  <urlname>Golden Pipeline Trail: Old Doodlakine : S1 Old Doodlakine Town by Cirrus_WA</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909882" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Golden Pipeline Trail: Old Doodlakine : S1 Old Doodlakine Town</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Cirrus_WA</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Cirrus_WA</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Golden Pipeline Trail: Old Doodlakine&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Old Doodlakine Town&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/04f53c66-c21a-4ce4-9e36-f30669bde873"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/04f53c66-c21a-4ce4-9e36-f30669bde873&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;On what date was Doodlakine declared a township?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a669005e-5e23-46fd-955a-2248fc362598" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The original town of Doodlakine was located near this spot where a well was sunk to provide water for travellers heading east from Perth.

With the rail line being surveyed to the south the town slowly moved to service the train line and no buildings remain at this spot.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e1350396-295f-4287-9d1c-63a8e853cbb6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Golden Pipeline Heritage Trail follows the water pipeline conceived by C.Y. O'Conner to supply the goldfields of Western Australia with much needed fresh water.

The Golden Pipeline Trail aims to use adventure labs to highlight some of the historic places and towns along the journey.

------

Old Doodlakine
The town sprung up due to the well sunk not far from here, it's demise came due to the running of the trainline.
Although today there are no buildings left at the original Doodlakine townsite there is still lots to see.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
