   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Golden Pipeline Trail: Old Doodlakine&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Centenary of Doodlakine&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/04f53c66-c21a-4ce4-9e36-f30669bde873"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/04f53c66-c21a-4ce4-9e36-f30669bde873&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Who unveiled the plaque? (First and Last Name only)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2443270c-61aa-49b9-915c-5fd6dd03da58" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A commemorative stone of the Centenary of the old townsite of Doodlakine&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e1350396-295f-4287-9d1c-63a8e853cbb6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Golden Pipeline Heritage Trail follows the water pipeline conceived by C.Y. O'Conner to supply the goldfields of Western Australia with much needed fresh water.

The Golden Pipeline Trail aims to use adventure labs to highlight some of the historic places and towns along the journey.

------

Old Doodlakine
The town sprung up due to the well sunk not far from here, it's demise came due to the running of the trainline.
Although today there are no buildings left at the original Doodlakine townsite there is still lots to see.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
