   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Golden Pipeline Trail - Cunderdin&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;O’Connor Park&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b1e3dd37-36af-43f3-8eaf-8d0902ff5b3e"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b1e3dd37-36af-43f3-8eaf-8d0902ff5b3e&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;At the pipe segment, there is a small plaque - fill in the blank “commemorate the X of water flowing”&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/647b46ee-49de-4606-b13d-0e787647f0e2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;O’Connor park located adjacent to the museum was opened in 2001 and is named in honour of CY O’Connor. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b626109c-17b0-45bd-9a8a-eb2278c7a229" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Golden Pipeline Heritage Trail follows the water pipeline conceived by C.Y. O'Conner to supply the goldfields of Western Australia with much needed fresh water.

The Golden Pipeline Trail aims to use adventure labs to highlight some of the historic places and towns along the journey.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
