   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Golden pipeline trail: Totadgin Rock&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Filled to overflowing&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/6d9c7e65-2605-4d47-8c3d-b0ad39e2328b"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/6d9c7e65-2605-4d47-8c3d-b0ad39e2328b&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the common name of barbula calycina? (word right under this one)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e7ec2684-699a-492d-bfb5-6a7081d429ba" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;SIGN.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/17da6696-490f-4402-8fa6-52d4f227163f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Totadgin Rock, a large granite outcrop incorporating a small “wave rock” located 14 km south of Merredin, is worth a side-trip from Great Eastern Highway. This Lab follows some of the signposted walk across the dome of the rock to see the wave formation and read about the theory behind its creation.

You dont need to walk to the top of the dome for this lab but for a great view it is recomended.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
