   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Golden pipeline trail: Mount Charlotte&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Liquid Gold&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3ced8d1b-dba1-44d7-8c3d-aa4b5c466a3b"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3ced8d1b-dba1-44d7-8c3d-aa4b5c466a3b&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;what building used to stand here?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c7f928d3-da07-4c76-b46e-377223f31d39" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;information on the sign with the same title.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c9d2667d-b30f-49e1-abbc-339ef102c6c3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Mount Charlotte is both the beginning and the end of the Heritage Trail story. It was near here that Paddy Hannan discovered gold, sparking the rush which led to the need for water. And it was here that the water finally arrived in 1903, at the end of its 560 km journey from Mundaring.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
