   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Campus Caper&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Boodjar (Wadjuk Nyungar land)&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c6b50eaf-377b-4463-86e1-8d540a96d6eb"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c6b50eaf-377b-4463-86e1-8d540a96d6eb&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Which is Ant Season?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b93262af-ba0c-4ea9-bad5-e4ce2ff64d72" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A purpose-built Centre for Aboriginal Studies opened at Curtin in 1994.

CAS (building 211) is an Indigenous-managed research and education centre that contributes to positive social change for Aboriginal Australians.

Unlike most other buildings at Curtin, the centre is circular in design to represent unity and equality.
Inside is the Midgegoroo Meeting Place, used to hold exhibitions, functions and special ceremonies.

At this waypoint (between Building 211 and 209) is a representation of the 6 Noongar seasons.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3f1633b2-956e-4800-b926-07d872ff1164" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;There's more than meets the eye at Curtin University's Bentley campus. 

Curtin is the largest of Western Australia's universities. It's main campus at Bentley, situated on a former pine plantation, stretches over 116 hectares. 
  
Around campus you will find award winning architecture, hidden gardens, urban art and secret tidbitz at every turn - this adventure will take you to just a few favourites - be sure to explore a little more and see what treasures you uncover!

PLEASE NOTE WELL:
Parking is paid. There are 5 different colour coded zones. Rates and access vary. Please take note and park accordingly. Inspectors are are often swift and fines can be hefty. 

Consider arriving via an alternative method. Getting to Curtin is fairly easy, with good transperth bus connections and free local shuttles (from Waterford, Bentley, Vic Park and South Perth).&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
