  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c6b50eaf-377b-4463-86e1-8d540a96d6eb</url>
  <urlname>Campus Caper : S1 An Institute of Technology: History &amp; Architecture by FreeRangeKelly</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-326" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Campus Caper : S1 An Institute of Technology: History &amp; Architecture</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>FreeRangeKelly</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">FreeRangeKelly</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Campus Caper&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;An Institute of Technology: History &amp; Architecture&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c6b50eaf-377b-4463-86e1-8d540a96d6eb"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c6b50eaf-377b-4463-86e1-8d540a96d6eb&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the sculpture at the front entrance? (Answer format - one word)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/32935b3f-e2da-41c9-b407-ee9ea1a91671" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Originally the Perth Tecnical College, a bushfire at the Collier Pine Plantation paved the way for the Bentley campus, with the Western Australia Institute of Technology officially opening in 1966.

The first buildings for WAIT took a utilitarian ‘brutalist’ style of brick and off-form concrete that reflected the practical and egalitarian nature of the institution. These buildings are now a celebrated example of modernist architecture of this era.

In 1987 the institute became Curtn University of Technology, Australia's first university of technology. The "of Technology" suffix was eventually dropped in 2010, from then on operating as "Curtin University".

At this location - Building 201 - you can see some of the original features and brutalist architecture of WAIT.
Designed with a street market in mind, inside you will find a central atrium, open air staircases and Juliette balconies.

Currently operating as 'Library 201' this building is open weekdays 8am  to 10pm and weekends 10am to 6pm.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3f1633b2-956e-4800-b926-07d872ff1164" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;There's more than meets the eye at Curtin University's Bentley campus. 

Curtin is the largest of Western Australia's universities. It's main campus at Bentley, situated on a former pine plantation, stretches over 116 hectares. 
  
Around campus you will find award winning architecture, hidden gardens, urban art and secret tidbitz at every turn - this adventure will take you to just a few favourites - be sure to explore a little more and see what treasures you uncover!

PLEASE NOTE WELL:
Parking is paid. There are 5 different colour coded zones. Rates and access vary. Please take note and park accordingly. Inspectors are are often swift and fines can be hefty. 

Consider arriving via an alternative method. Getting to Curtin is fairly easy, with good transperth bus connections and free local shuttles (from Waterford, Bentley, Vic Park and South Perth).&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
