   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Campus Caper&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Secret Gardens&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c6b50eaf-377b-4463-86e1-8d540a96d6eb"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c6b50eaf-377b-4463-86e1-8d540a96d6eb&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the lecture theatre in this building called?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/70ffd813-0eea-49ad-878c-bd95d625eef2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Curtin is home to some amazing gardens, many with a specific theme and atmosphere. 

The Japanese Garden in the courtyard of Building 401 is a quiet place where you will find water features, even koi!

As you explore, you might want to also check out:
* Sculpture Garden - Opposite the Guild Building (106F)
* Spiritual Garden - Between Buildings 307 and 308
* Malaysian Garden - Outside Buildings 101 and 109
* Mediterranean Garden - in the courtyard of 
Building 202
* edible Garden - Outside Curtin Connect (between buildings 102 and 103)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3f1633b2-956e-4800-b926-07d872ff1164" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;There's more than meets the eye at Curtin University's Bentley campus. 

Curtin is the largest of Western Australia's universities. It's main campus at Bentley, situated on a former pine plantation, stretches over 116 hectares. 
  
Around campus you will find award winning architecture, hidden gardens, urban art and secret tidbitz at every turn - this adventure will take you to just a few favourites - be sure to explore a little more and see what treasures you uncover!

PLEASE NOTE WELL:
Parking is paid. There are 5 different colour coded zones. Rates and access vary. Please take note and park accordingly. Inspectors are are often swift and fines can be hefty. 

Consider arriving via an alternative method. Getting to Curtin is fairly easy, with good transperth bus connections and free local shuttles (from Waterford, Bentley, Vic Park and South Perth).&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
