  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c6b50eaf-377b-4463-86e1-8d540a96d6eb</url>
  <urlname>Campus Caper : S2 Look Ever Forward by FreeRangeKelly</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-327" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Campus Caper : S2 Look Ever Forward</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>FreeRangeKelly</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">FreeRangeKelly</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Campus Caper&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Look Ever Forward&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c6b50eaf-377b-4463-86e1-8d540a96d6eb"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c6b50eaf-377b-4463-86e1-8d540a96d6eb&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is Curtin HIVE the hub for?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/71272756-d2cf-498a-b35d-bb814674ec57" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The words “look ever forward”, taken from the writings of John Curtin in 1932 about the role of universities, became the University's motto in 1996.

The John Curtin Centre was developed in the mid-1990s, and houses the John Curtin Gallery &amp; John Curtin Prime Ministerial Library.

The Gallery is one of WA’s major public art galleries, and is also one of the largest and best equipped university galleries in the country.

The Library was Australia's first Prime Ministerial Library. It houses personal records, photos and objects and more related to John Curtin and is available for research use. The library also hosts notable academic and political figures for events. 
*please note, the JCPML and reading room are currently open by appointment only&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3f1633b2-956e-4800-b926-07d872ff1164" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;There's more than meets the eye at Curtin University's Bentley campus. 

Curtin is the largest of Western Australia's universities. It's main campus at Bentley, situated on a former pine plantation, stretches over 116 hectares. 
  
Around campus you will find award winning architecture, hidden gardens, urban art and secret tidbitz at every turn - this adventure will take you to just a few favourites - be sure to explore a little more and see what treasures you uncover!

PLEASE NOTE WELL:
Parking is paid. There are 5 different colour coded zones. Rates and access vary. Please take note and park accordingly. Inspectors are are often swift and fines can be hefty. 

Consider arriving via an alternative method. Getting to Curtin is fairly easy, with good transperth bus connections and free local shuttles (from Waterford, Bentley, Vic Park and South Perth).&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
