   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Nannup&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Nannup Tiger&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7cfc124c-a89a-424d-8193-1c89188ea088"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7cfc124c-a89a-424d-8193-1c89188ea088&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;At head height on the sculpture is a small plaque. Who was the artist who created the sculpture?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7b86919c-af66-4b07-9629-99b00deb5269" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The area around Nannup is famous for its unconfirmed sightings of the “Nannup Tiger”. 

This stage will take you to a sculpture of the Nannup Tiger. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0a489c51-54c0-4178-8048-3ca36723ce95" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Nannup is a small town located in the South West of Western Australia, 280 kilometres from Perth. 

This adventure lab will take you on a small tour of some historic sights down the Main Street. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
