   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;QEIIMC&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Harry Perkins Institute&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a5013315-2abd-439f-b217-41c6e1b4e636"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a5013315-2abd-439f-b217-41c6e1b4e636&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Which artist created this piece outside PathWest? (two words)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/53810b09-e52a-482c-ba24-c295aebe8470" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Charles Henry "Harry" Perkins was an Australian farmer, businessman, and philanthropist who was best known as the chairman of Wesfarmers from 1986 to 2002. He also served as chancellor of Curtin University and helped establish the Western Australian Institute for Medical Research, which was later renamed the Harry Perkins Institute of Medical Research in his honour. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/efa3aa84-d9c9-4abf-88de-3d6b51046d7e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Queen Elizabeth II Medical Centre, home to the largest medical centre in the southern hemisphere, hosting globally recognised major medical, research and education tenants.

Back in the 1950s the first hospital to be housed on the site was the Perth Chest Hospital (currently A Block), built to look after mainly tuberculosis patients. In 1963 the expanding hospital became known as Sir Charles Gairdner Hospital after the then current Governor of Western Australia.

Photographs taken from A Fair Sized Town, Sir Charles Gairdner Hospital and its history 1958-1988 - Carolyn Polizzotto.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.967233" lon="115.814267">
