  <desc>QEIIMCS2PerthCh</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a5013315-2abd-439f-b217-41c6e1b4e636</url>
  <urlname>QEIIMC : S2 Perth Chest Hospital - A Block by olthomas</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909920" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>QEIIMC : S2 Perth Chest Hospital - A Block</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>olthomas</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">olthomas</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;QEIIMC&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Perth Chest Hospital - A Block&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a5013315-2abd-439f-b217-41c6e1b4e636"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a5013315-2abd-439f-b217-41c6e1b4e636&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The trees grown here were grown from cuttings of which tree? (one word)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c8d60d9b-ee98-4fd2-92d4-b75079764cd3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The original hospital on this site was the Perth Chest Hospital designed to treat tuberculosis patients. Patients began to be admitted here in August 1958. 

It now holds many departments including the inpatient pharmacy and physiotherapy and I can assure you, as it is my main department.... it looks like the pharmacy department was designed in 1958! 

The garden in which you now stand is known as the Rose Garden. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/efa3aa84-d9c9-4abf-88de-3d6b51046d7e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Queen Elizabeth II Medical Centre, home to the largest medical centre in the southern hemisphere, hosting globally recognised major medical, research and education tenants.

Back in the 1950s the first hospital to be housed on the site was the Perth Chest Hospital (currently A Block), built to look after mainly tuberculosis patients. In 1963 the expanding hospital became known as Sir Charles Gairdner Hospital after the then current Governor of Western Australia.

Photographs taken from A Fair Sized Town, Sir Charles Gairdner Hospital and its history 1958-1988 - Carolyn Polizzotto.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
