   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;QEIIMC&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Browne's Paddock&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a5013315-2abd-439f-b217-41c6e1b4e636"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a5013315-2abd-439f-b217-41c6e1b4e636&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;In 1875 the area was granted to whom? (two words)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a91f0e81-b12f-4421-ada8-1e7e38631476" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Prior to UWA leasing the site from the WA Government in 1922, Edward Browne began his dairy business grazing just one cow here in 1892. As his herd grew he supplied milk to Perth and its growing suburbs before he moved his growing business to Bayswater in 1896.  &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/efa3aa84-d9c9-4abf-88de-3d6b51046d7e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Queen Elizabeth II Medical Centre, home to the largest medical centre in the southern hemisphere, hosting globally recognised major medical, research and education tenants.

Back in the 1950s the first hospital to be housed on the site was the Perth Chest Hospital (currently A Block), built to look after mainly tuberculosis patients. In 1963 the expanding hospital became known as Sir Charles Gairdner Hospital after the then current Governor of Western Australia.

Photographs taken from A Fair Sized Town, Sir Charles Gairdner Hospital and its history 1958-1988 - Carolyn Polizzotto.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.599267" lon="116.072683">
