 <wpt lat="-24.907433" lon="113.6743">
  <ele>7.0</ele>
  <time>2022-08-14T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBnSKC-05</name>
  <desc>CarnarvonATast5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/11a58238-cd9d-47a8-92d7-346526564700</url>
  <urlname>Carnarvon   A taste of a good life : S5 Carnarvon Race Club by ebenie</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99004842" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Carnarvon   A taste of a good life : S5 Carnarvon Race Club</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>ebenie</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">ebenie</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Carnarvon   A taste of a good life&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Carnarvon Race Club&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/11a58238-cd9d-47a8-92d7-346526564700"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/11a58238-cd9d-47a8-92d7-346526564700&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the mounting yard called....... ....... ....... ........&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6d25c1fc-b247-4138-ae95-f4bde5b35bec" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Race Club commenced 12th December 1883 making it one of the oldest clubs in Western Australia.  There is a book "Tales of dust and glory"
The club was formed in the very early years of the Carnarvon township, before the town was officially gazetted.  The club relocated twice in 1924 to what is now the current airport site and again in 1944 to the current location of Massey Bay.  In 1974 the well known North West Institution became the Carnarvon Race Club.
Billy Mitchell was a life member of the race club.  This honour is not past out very often. He was Clerk off Course, ex jockey and general handyman.   His name was Lawrence William Mitchell.  His family owned and trained horses, they came ins from the stations and driving trucks in the early days.
All his family were "hands on" around the a Gascoyne area.  Some brothers were Reggie, Johnny, Jimmy and Boyo and their was a few girls in the mix.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5d64ffda-7dd8-4b44-8760-a705492fea80" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Carnarvon is my home town.  I still enjoy coming home to family &amp; friends
Seafood to die for especially when cooked for you
Beautiful weather (98% off the time). what more could you ask for
I hope you enjoy your stay here too
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
