 <wpt lat="-24.883217" lon="113.664017">
  <ele>8.0</ele>
  <time>2022-08-14T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBnSKC-03</name>
  <desc>CarnarvonATast3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/11a58238-cd9d-47a8-92d7-346526564700</url>
  <urlname>Carnarvon   A taste of a good life : S3 Carnarvon Airport by ebenie</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99004836" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Carnarvon   A taste of a good life : S3 Carnarvon Airport</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>ebenie</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">ebenie</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Carnarvon   A taste of a good life&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Carnarvon Airport&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/11a58238-cd9d-47a8-92d7-346526564700"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/11a58238-cd9d-47a8-92d7-346526564700&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the number plate on the MMA passenger coach on the mural&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/deae7013-eb92-4bc3-82ee-02fc76d3c383" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Carnarvon Airport is owned and operated by the Shire of Carnarvon and is located to the townsite with only a 2 min drive to CBD
Carnarvon Airport was originally built as a WW11 airstrip and first opened for passenger travel when it was transferred to the Department of Civil Aviation in 1947 and the original terminal was constructed in 1947.  A new terminal has now been erected but is a minimal facility servicing single airlines.
The airport contains 3 runways.
In 1993 the Commonwealth of Transport and Communication transferred the control to the Shire of Carnarvon.
Also a memory of me. My mother was the cleaner at the airport for the many years we were here.  On the drive across the entry to the airport, when it was gravel and every time the floods came through snd flooded passengers and works had to wait for a truck to drive across to ferry them backwards and forwards to the waters subsided 
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5d64ffda-7dd8-4b44-8760-a705492fea80" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Carnarvon is my home town.  I still enjoy coming home to family &amp; friends
Seafood to die for especially when cooked for you
Beautiful weather (98% off the time). what more could you ask for
I hope you enjoy your stay here too
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-24.885133" lon="113.655483">
