  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99004838" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Carnarvon   A taste of a good life : S4 HMAS Sydney Memorial</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>ebenie</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">ebenie</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Carnarvon   A taste of a good life&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;HMAS Sydney Memorial&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/11a58238-cd9d-47a8-92d7-346526564700"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/11a58238-cd9d-47a8-92d7-346526564700&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the date on the anchor&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/03f2a0e8-c667-44ae-8bdf-06ca4311e008" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A memorial for the Sydney Memorial is now located here in honour of the 645 officers and crew that lost there lives in a battle with the Kormoran .
On 19th November 1941 was in battle with the German cruiser Cormorant
  On Nov 24th the Sydney fail to return and was eventually found 16th March 2008 
207 kms from the west coast (Seep Point). all persons on board went down with the ship.
A memorial drive was a grant given to put Carnarvon another entry or exit from town.   Unfortunately this drive fell into despair so the monument was erected on Oliva Tce.
The is a small statement of the Kormoran nearby.  There is a memorial to the Kormoran at the Quobba and 70 germans and 2 Chinese we spotted off of Carnarvon and the ship Koolinda brought them to Carnarvon.  
The men were then place aboard the Centaur cargo hold and transported to Perth
There is more information on the net &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5d64ffda-7dd8-4b44-8760-a705492fea80" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Carnarvon is my home town.  I still enjoy coming home to family &amp; friends
Seafood to die for especially when cooked for you
Beautiful weather (98% off the time). what more could you ask for
I hope you enjoy your stay here too
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
