   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Carnarvon   catch a taste o the great life&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Memorial Park&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/8bad94c6-4dd3-49d7-8325-b33c81a3f089"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/8bad94c6-4dd3-49d7-8325-b33c81a3f089&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;When was the Vietnam war &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/948d8f54-bab2-4d33-b7e4-3b96eacad345" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The monument which is of Donnybrook freestone, and standing at the intersection and commanding the best position of the main streets, Robinson and Francis Streets.
It was originally erected to commemorate the soldiers of the Gascoyne District who served in WW1 but now commemorates all battles.
It was opened officially by Mrs Foss on 11th November 1923&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/53c062ac-ed42-407e-85e1-aa62a4b26dfd" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Carnarvon is my home town and I still enjoy coming home to see family and friends
 home you will enjoy your visit whilst your here too.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
