   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Rockingham Mural Meander&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Rockingham Foreshore - Mooriburdup Mural&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/81a5109e-b9bb-46eb-abd6-34c8a0e01059"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/81a5109e-b9bb-46eb-abd6-34c8a0e01059&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many birds are located on both side of the mural? (Numeral)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/26937ffe-aa11-4563-b8d8-171e8f558984" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Designed and installed in 2019 as part of an extensive redevelopment of the Rockingham Foreshore.

Painted by Western Australian artists Justin Martin, Biara Martin and Cheryl Martin it wraps around the lookout over Cockburn Sound. The lookout doubles as a stage and is used for community events throughout the year.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/365aa659-cb71-49bb-a2cb-42af0a723e82" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Over the last few years the City of Rockingham has partnered with local and state based artists to create murals around the city.

This adventure will take you to some of these murals and talk about the stories of how they have been developed.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
