   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Rockingham Mural Meander&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;McLarty Hall - Re[Frame]: Find What Works For You&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/81a5109e-b9bb-46eb-abd6-34c8a0e01059"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/81a5109e-b9bb-46eb-abd6-34c8a0e01059&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the artist that completed the mural?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8a57eb5e-8a92-4707-b40d-686a75d5c51f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Re[Frame] Project brought together local people with a lived experience of mental illness to explore their recovery strategies the final art work was inspired by these reflections.

For more information about the project I have linked to a City of Rockingham youtube video about the project.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/365aa659-cb71-49bb-a2cb-42af0a723e82" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Over the last few years the City of Rockingham has partnered with local and state based artists to create murals around the city.

This adventure will take you to some of these murals and talk about the stories of how they have been developed.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
