   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Murals of Mount Barker&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Plantagenet District Hall&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e30528ba-ef5d-4d95-8618-ecf7a587acae"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e30528ba-ef5d-4d95-8618-ecf7a587acae&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What was the event that the ticket was issued? (2 words)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e9204687-25cd-4b5c-889b-fd7cbd79017f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The first Plantagenet Hall was opened on 23rd September 1893.
The present hall was opened on this site in 1927. Movies were screened from that time up until 1963. It has also served as a dance venue and location for community meetings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c99cdff7-04ff-4c99-8b0b-981410b6464b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The locations of the murals have been placed to bring tourists into town by creating an exploration trail through the heart of town.
The murals were painted by visiting international artists during the 2019 Mountains and Murals Festival.
Remember to take note of your answers because you will need them to log a find on the bonus cache!
Enjoy your walk through town.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-34.6266" lon="117.661883">
