   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Murals of Mount Barker&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;West Australia Airways&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e30528ba-ef5d-4d95-8618-ecf7a587acae"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e30528ba-ef5d-4d95-8618-ecf7a587acae&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What was the passenger capacity of the plane? (word)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/839be3a2-7789-4a22-bd3b-a059cf53cc9f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;West Australia Airways flew from Perth to Mount Barker in a specially modified De Haviland DH.50A with a top speed of 180 km/h.
It went into service on the 1st December 1926 and crashed on 1st May 1929 at Mayland Airfield - without casualties.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c99cdff7-04ff-4c99-8b0b-981410b6464b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The locations of the murals have been placed to bring tourists into town by creating an exploration trail through the heart of town.
The murals were painted by visiting international artists during the 2019 Mountains and Murals Festival.
Remember to take note of your answers because you will need them to log a find on the bonus cache!
Enjoy your walk through town.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
