   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Murals of Mount Barker&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Founding of Mount Barker&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e30528ba-ef5d-4d95-8618-ecf7a587acae"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e30528ba-ef5d-4d95-8618-ecf7a587acae&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What was the name of the Noongar guide who accompanied Wilson?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c3c7e945-b960-4cb9-ab49-47bb54b1b23c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In December 1829, Dr. Thomas Braidwood Wilson named Mount Barker after Capt. Collet Barker - a surgeon of the Royal Navy.
Wilson explored this area in company with a Noongar guide who was an elder of the Menang people.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c99cdff7-04ff-4c99-8b0b-981410b6464b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The locations of the murals have been placed to bring tourists into town by creating an exploration trail through the heart of town.
The murals were painted by visiting international artists during the 2019 Mountains and Murals Festival.
Remember to take note of your answers because you will need them to log a find on the bonus cache!
Enjoy your walk through town.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-34.628383" lon="117.6623">
