 <wpt lat="-20.670733" lon="116.709417">
  <ele>38.0</ele>
  <time>2022-08-17T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBKsNP-02</name>
  <desc>ScenicDampierS2</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ab4fdcbc-6e03-46b4-af9e-9f0408cc77c3</url>
  <urlname>Scenic Dampier : S2 Dampier Lookout by dimor</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99005234" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Scenic Dampier : S2 Dampier Lookout</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>dimor</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">dimor</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Scenic Dampier&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Dampier Lookout&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ab4fdcbc-6e03-46b4-af9e-9f0408cc77c3"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ab4fdcbc-6e03-46b4-af9e-9f0408cc77c3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What two words are written in the top left hand corner of the map&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/85dbb9e3-de55-4826-aa11-0f21c9f24640" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;At this location you get a good view over Rio Tinto’s Dampier Salt Dampier operations and some of the islands.

In one of the gazebos you will find a map on a concrete pillar, this will help you with your answer&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/dddf275f-9ca1-4ea2-9275-813beac4b7c1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to Dampier, a small coastal port town in the Pilbara region of Western Australia.
Dampier is rich in history, Indigenous culture, mineral, marine and natural resources.
Dampier was constructed in 1965 as a port and processing centre for Hamersley Iron’s inland Pilbara iron ore mines. The port was opened when the first iron ore from Mount Tom Price was transported by Hamersley railway to Parker Point for shipment in 1966.
Five decades later Dampier Port is the second largest bulk export port in the world, shipping iron ore, liquefied gas, salt and anhydrous ammonia and also other cargo.
There are 42 islands off the coast of Dampier as well as outcrops and islets that make up the Dampier Archipelago and is home to several endangered species.
The Dampier region has over 3,700 hours of annual sunshine making it one of the sunniest places in Australia.

I ?? this town for it’s beautiful raw scenery, the sunshine, warm water and there is plenty to see and do around the area. What’s not to love
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
