   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Scenic Dampier&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Dampier Palm Foreshore&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ab4fdcbc-6e03-46b4-af9e-9f0408cc77c3"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ab4fdcbc-6e03-46b4-af9e-9f0408cc77c3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What marine animal does the artwork represent?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c91f360a-9a36-4f22-94e2-84d0227aaa18" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This location is a beautiful spot to sit under the palms with a book and let the day pass by, you can also swim here or let the kids enjoy the playground.
This is an area I love ?? and have spent many many (probably too many  ) hours here.

Down near the wall you will find some artwork to help with your answer&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/dddf275f-9ca1-4ea2-9275-813beac4b7c1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to Dampier, a small coastal port town in the Pilbara region of Western Australia.
Dampier is rich in history, Indigenous culture, mineral, marine and natural resources.
Dampier was constructed in 1965 as a port and processing centre for Hamersley Iron’s inland Pilbara iron ore mines. The port was opened when the first iron ore from Mount Tom Price was transported by Hamersley railway to Parker Point for shipment in 1966.
Five decades later Dampier Port is the second largest bulk export port in the world, shipping iron ore, liquefied gas, salt and anhydrous ammonia and also other cargo.
There are 42 islands off the coast of Dampier as well as outcrops and islets that make up the Dampier Archipelago and is home to several endangered species.
The Dampier region has over 3,700 hours of annual sunshine making it one of the sunniest places in Australia.

I ?? this town for it’s beautiful raw scenery, the sunshine, warm water and there is plenty to see and do around the area. What’s not to love
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
