  <desc>ScenicDampierS1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ab4fdcbc-6e03-46b4-af9e-9f0408cc77c3</url>
  <urlname>Scenic Dampier : S1 The Pilbara Wanderer by dimor</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99005232" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Scenic Dampier : S1 The Pilbara Wanderer</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>dimor</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">dimor</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Scenic Dampier&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Pilbara Wanderer&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ab4fdcbc-6e03-46b4-af9e-9f0408cc77c3"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ab4fdcbc-6e03-46b4-af9e-9f0408cc77c3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is Red Dog’s death date &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e8d644cf-aefe-4b70-9018-a7c020319288" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Here you will find the memorial statue of WA’s most famous dog, Red Dog, the Pilbara Wanderer.
It is believed Red Dog was born in Paraburdoo in 1971 and named “Tally Ho” by his first owner Col Cummings. 
Col moved to Dampier and soon after Tally took off to fend for himself, spending most of his time at Hamersley Iron transport section in Dampier meeting John the bus driver.
And as they say the rest is history but for us there have been two movies made and the story of our beloved Red Dog is now world famous.

At the bottom of the memorial stone you will find some plaques. One of these will help you with the answer you need&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/dddf275f-9ca1-4ea2-9275-813beac4b7c1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to Dampier, a small coastal port town in the Pilbara region of Western Australia.
Dampier is rich in history, Indigenous culture, mineral, marine and natural resources.
Dampier was constructed in 1965 as a port and processing centre for Hamersley Iron’s inland Pilbara iron ore mines. The port was opened when the first iron ore from Mount Tom Price was transported by Hamersley railway to Parker Point for shipment in 1966.
Five decades later Dampier Port is the second largest bulk export port in the world, shipping iron ore, liquefied gas, salt and anhydrous ammonia and also other cargo.
There are 42 islands off the coast of Dampier as well as outcrops and islets that make up the Dampier Archipelago and is home to several endangered species.
The Dampier region has over 3,700 hours of annual sunshine making it one of the sunniest places in Australia.

I ?? this town for it’s beautiful raw scenery, the sunshine, warm water and there is plenty to see and do around the area. What’s not to love
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
