   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Scenic Dampier&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;North West Shelf Gas Project&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ab4fdcbc-6e03-46b4-af9e-9f0408cc77c3"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ab4fdcbc-6e03-46b4-af9e-9f0408cc77c3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Whom was Mount Burrup named after?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b985078e-f01a-4749-9929-186281fec5a8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;At this location you get a view of the gas plant that supplies some towns and cities in WA with our household gas via a very long pipeline.
As well as producing liquefied natural gas (LNG), the North West Shelf Venture also produces liquefied petroleum gas (LPG), oil and condensate - a crude oil - for international energy markets.
The visitors centre is not always open but there is information about the project outside that is very interesting to read.

After the extensive reading of all the gas information make your way to the left of the visitors centre and find a plaque to get your answer&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/dddf275f-9ca1-4ea2-9275-813beac4b7c1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to Dampier, a small coastal port town in the Pilbara region of Western Australia.
Dampier is rich in history, Indigenous culture, mineral, marine and natural resources.
Dampier was constructed in 1965 as a port and processing centre for Hamersley Iron’s inland Pilbara iron ore mines. The port was opened when the first iron ore from Mount Tom Price was transported by Hamersley railway to Parker Point for shipment in 1966.
Five decades later Dampier Port is the second largest bulk export port in the world, shipping iron ore, liquefied gas, salt and anhydrous ammonia and also other cargo.
There are 42 islands off the coast of Dampier as well as outcrops and islets that make up the Dampier Archipelago and is home to several endangered species.
The Dampier region has over 3,700 hours of annual sunshine making it one of the sunniest places in Australia.

I ?? this town for it’s beautiful raw scenery, the sunshine, warm water and there is plenty to see and do around the area. What’s not to love
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.977733" lon="115.933967">
  <ele>14.0</ele>
  <time>2022-08-24T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBNCn5-03</name>
  <desc>TomatoLakeWalk3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/4d2d2149-79c1-455f-9e8b-7a72c1fa25b6</url>
  <urlname>Tomato Lake Walk Trail  : S3 Jida Bidi Trail by Paskersfind</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909960" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Tomato Lake Walk Trail  : S3 Jida Bidi Trail</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Paskersfind</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Paskersfind</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Tomato Lake Walk Trail &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Jida Bidi Trail&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/4d2d2149-79c1-455f-9e8b-7a72c1fa25b6"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/4d2d2149-79c1-455f-9e8b-7a72c1fa25b6&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many square metres of irrigated turf were removed as part of this project?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/edde91f9-b215-444d-a23a-d13709f19d14" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Why not take a quick detour around the Tomato Lake Interpretive Bushland Trail? The aim of this project was to extend the remnant bushland here in order to enhance the biodiversity and provide habitat for local fauna. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/93a6c83f-60dc-401c-8fbe-8dda4ed5cf10" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Tomato Lake Walk Trail winds its way among shady trees around the perimeter of this peaceful urban oasis in Kewdale. The dual-use pathway provides a safe walk-friendly environment for people of all ages as well as an opportunity to be awed by the abundance of birdlife on and around the lake.

Enjoy a short walk around (half) the lake and marvel at the breeding colony of Australian White ibises as you cross the boardwalk bridge. 

There is a mystery bonus cache for those interested in such things.







&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
