   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Kids' Bridge&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Under the bridge&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/649b8218-82d2-4dc1-a7b0-180e38d7829d"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/649b8218-82d2-4dc1-a7b0-180e38d7829d&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Who is the artist of the Djinang "Look"? ( 3 words)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5dd61058-ed60-4ae1-ac86-bcc4512c1ed5" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;You should be stood underneath the Kids' bridge for this answer&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1d9a47a0-7f75-4a8e-a0af-b47e4401c608" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Kids' Bridge, also named Koolangka Bridge meaning 'children' in Noongar, officially opened on 4 August 2021.

