   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Exploring Historic Cue&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Wardens Court and Police Station&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/abe1abf0-4cfe-4053-9ff7-38eb89ead689"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/abe1abf0-4cfe-4053-9ff7-38eb89ead689&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;When was the Cue Police Station opened?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/00f04e3b-5e09-4fa4-bb66-aa2bd12bb31f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This building was made of locally quarried limestone slabs and were designed to house the offices of a number of Government Departments.  
This building is still being used for Government purposes, including the local police station.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8b2e090c-0e7a-4a63-8ab3-64b44f62170f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Shire of Cue is 120kms south of Meekatharra and 80kms north of Mt Magnet, right in the middle of the beautiful outback. As you make your way into town you are struck by the heritage of the gold rush town lying in every building along the main street.
Cue was named after Tom Cue, an early prospector who became a major figure in the town's development. 
There is much to explore around Cue and this Adventure Lab will only give you a small snippet into the town's very rich goldmining history.  
If you have some time, travel out to Day Dawn and Big Bell both of whom were once thriving gold mining towns close to Cue. Sadly, now only ghost towns to explore.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-27.42165" lon="117.899233">
