  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/abe1abf0-4cfe-4053-9ff7-38eb89ead689</url>
  <urlname>Exploring Historic Cue : S1 Old Goal by allinaday</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476909992" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Exploring Historic Cue : S1 Old Goal</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>allinaday</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">allinaday</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Exploring Historic Cue&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Old Goal&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/abe1abf0-4cfe-4053-9ff7-38eb89ead689"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/abe1abf0-4cfe-4053-9ff7-38eb89ead689&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;When was the Old Goal officially opened?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/32d7cef1-d0a0-4b88-b3e0-d3002b000c21" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; The Old Goal has a central open yard surrounded by cells, and is considered unusual as it is not attached to the Police Station.  It was officially closed in 1914, but was used as a lock-up until the early 1930's.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8b2e090c-0e7a-4a63-8ab3-64b44f62170f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Shire of Cue is 120kms south of Meekatharra and 80kms north of Mt Magnet, right in the middle of the beautiful outback. As you make your way into town you are struck by the heritage of the gold rush town lying in every building along the main street.
Cue was named after Tom Cue, an early prospector who became a major figure in the town's development. 
There is much to explore around Cue and this Adventure Lab will only give you a small snippet into the town's very rich goldmining history.  
If you have some time, travel out to Day Dawn and Big Bell both of whom were once thriving gold mining towns close to Cue. Sadly, now only ghost towns to explore.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-20.748267" lon="116.8329">
  <ele>119.0</ele>
  <time>2022-09-16T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBK5rB-03</name>
  <desc>LookoutKarrath3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/31366525-e535-483c-bff9-04cb6292b290</url>
  <urlname>Lookout Karratha   : S3 Yaburara Heritage Trail Lookout by dimor</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99005742" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Lookout Karratha   : S3 Yaburara Heritage Trail Lookout</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>dimor</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">dimor</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Lookout Karratha  &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Yaburara Heritage Trail Lookout&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/31366525-e535-483c-bff9-04cb6292b290"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/31366525-e535-483c-bff9-04cb6292b290&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Fourth panel from the left&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/346a2ae8-9f2f-439e-9a51-59489c4b8fd4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;**4wd required if driving to this lookout, otherwise you can walk up via the Yaburara Heritage Walk Trail

This lookout give you views over the Leisureplex, Nickol, Pegs Creek, Millars Well, Tambrey and Baynton.
Behind the panels gives you distant views over the LIA area.


One of the panels will give you the answer you require&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a7c5ec97-d391-4056-b621-7d689224b2df" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Adventure Lab will take you to five (5) lookouts around Karratha.
I hope you enjoy the views like I do each time I’m here

Welcome to Karratha, the first city in the North West region of Western Australia.
Karratha was named after a pastoral station in the area and was established in 1968 to accommodate the processing and exploration workforce of the Hamersley Iron mining company and, in the 1980s the petroleum and liquified natural gas operations of the North West Shelf Venture.

On the first of July 2014 Karratha became a city. It covers an area of fifteen thousand square kilometres and has a population of around 20,000.
Karratha has the expected facilities of a major regional area with shopping centres, health campus and medical services, both public and private schools, airport, restaurants and cafes, hotels/motels and an arts precinct.

The weather here is divine most of the year except when cyclones come through. Plenty of warm sunny weather to enjoy with the laid back lifestyle ?? &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
