   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Lookout Karratha  &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Tank Hill Lookout&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/31366525-e535-483c-bff9-04cb6292b290"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/31366525-e535-483c-bff9-04cb6292b290&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;This lookout is how many metres above sea level&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5978b5d1-9fa1-444c-a797-859e363acf8d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This location gives you a good view over the town area and Nickol Bay.
You will need to locate a rock with a plaque to find your answer&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a7c5ec97-d391-4056-b621-7d689224b2df" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Adventure Lab will take you to five (5) lookouts around Karratha.
I hope you enjoy the views like I do each time I’m here

Welcome to Karratha, the first city in the North West region of Western Australia.
Karratha was named after a pastoral station in the area and was established in 1968 to accommodate the processing and exploration workforce of the Hamersley Iron mining company and, in the 1980s the petroleum and liquified natural gas operations of the North West Shelf Venture.

On the first of July 2014 Karratha became a city. It covers an area of fifteen thousand square kilometres and has a population of around 20,000.
Karratha has the expected facilities of a major regional area with shopping centres, health campus and medical services, both public and private schools, airport, restaurants and cafes, hotels/motels and an arts precinct.

The weather here is divine most of the year except when cyclones come through. Plenty of warm sunny weather to enjoy with the laid back lifestyle ?? &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
