   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Lookout Karratha  &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Dampier Salt Lookout&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/31366525-e535-483c-bff9-04cb6292b290"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/31366525-e535-483c-bff9-04cb6292b290&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;DSL proudly supports community based projects. Which one is named ?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6165b1a9-d41b-430e-909c-6a3c246da354" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This lookout is not far from the airport.  Here you will overlook the salt ponds.

Dampier Salt Limited (DSL) is a member of the Rio Tinto group of companies.  They are the world’s largest exporter of reliable, high quality (bulk) solar salt. DSL exports to Japan    , China   , Korea    , Indonesia    , Philippines    , Taiwan   , USA   , Africa and Europe

One of the panels up in the lookout will give you your answer (note: there are a few panels)
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a7c5ec97-d391-4056-b621-7d689224b2df" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Adventure Lab will take you to five (5) lookouts around Karratha.
I hope you enjoy the views like I do each time I’m here

Welcome to Karratha, the first city in the North West region of Western Australia.
Karratha was named after a pastoral station in the area and was established in 1968 to accommodate the processing and exploration workforce of the Hamersley Iron mining company and, in the 1980s the petroleum and liquified natural gas operations of the North West Shelf Venture.

On the first of July 2014 Karratha became a city. It covers an area of fifteen thousand square kilometres and has a population of around 20,000.
Karratha has the expected facilities of a major regional area with shopping centres, health campus and medical services, both public and private schools, airport, restaurants and cafes, hotels/motels and an arts precinct.

The weather here is divine most of the year except when cyclones come through. Plenty of warm sunny weather to enjoy with the laid back lifestyle ?? &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
