   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;The Three Springs LAB&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Information Bay&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a1450509-9868-41c7-8e5d-3eb6b63a07ca"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a1450509-9868-41c7-8e5d-3eb6b63a07ca&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What number is the first word of this town - e.g. 2&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9be7fe25-5de2-400c-acb9-5279d23b7193" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The information Bay is an ideal spot for a break if you're traveling either north or south. There is plenty of room for a car or 4wd and caravan so take the time for a break and to get some local information.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8443c525-557a-4048-818b-e4c4084eaee0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Lab Cache can be done in any order and has been placed to introduce you to some of the more interesting points in &amp; around Three Springs. The town has a reserve area between the railway line and the main road - and much of it allows for parking of cars &amp; caravans. 

The Midlands Road passes through the center of town and also holds most of the commercial businesses (Hotel, Post Office, Shops, Shire Offices etc). Other roads service towns to the west and east. All points of this Lab are caravan friendly - so if you're towing you can stay hitched. 

IIRC - the Midlands Road used to be called The Great Northern Highway, but lost that title when the Brand Highway was opened. Up until then it was the main road between Perth and Geraldton. 
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
