   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;The Three Springs LAB&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;North Midlands Medical Service&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a1450509-9868-41c7-8e5d-3eb6b63a07ca"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a1450509-9868-41c7-8e5d-3eb6b63a07ca&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;This town is named after Three what?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f66af219-896b-4886-8846-5b4b6ec35a85" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Hospital has been here for many years - I remember bringing a patient here many years ago after a collision with a road grader. 
Driving out of town on this road will take you towards Eneabba, Brand Highway and other points.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8443c525-557a-4048-818b-e4c4084eaee0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Lab Cache can be done in any order and has been placed to introduce you to some of the more interesting points in &amp; around Three Springs. The town has a reserve area between the railway line and the main road - and much of it allows for parking of cars &amp; caravans. 

The Midlands Road passes through the center of town and also holds most of the commercial businesses (Hotel, Post Office, Shops, Shire Offices etc). Other roads service towns to the west and east. All points of this Lab are caravan friendly - so if you're towing you can stay hitched. 

IIRC - the Midlands Road used to be called The Great Northern Highway, but lost that title when the Brand Highway was opened. Up until then it was the main road between Perth and Geraldton. 
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
