   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;The Three Springs LAB&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Wheat Silos&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a1450509-9868-41c7-8e5d-3eb6b63a07ca"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a1450509-9868-41c7-8e5d-3eb6b63a07ca&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many silos can you see?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/13c807b0-3129-4e09-8e9b-142d686783d9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Look while you can - because of cracks in the silo structure, the silos may be unstable and it is rumored that they may be demolished. This is pretty much the center of town. The side of the road that the Silos are situated on has quite a few bays that you can drive into and all will take a car/4wd and caravan.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8443c525-557a-4048-818b-e4c4084eaee0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Lab Cache can be done in any order and has been placed to introduce you to some of the more interesting points in &amp; around Three Springs. The town has a reserve area between the railway line and the main road - and much of it allows for parking of cars &amp; caravans. 

The Midlands Road passes through the center of town and also holds most of the commercial businesses (Hotel, Post Office, Shops, Shire Offices etc). Other roads service towns to the west and east. All points of this Lab are caravan friendly - so if you're towing you can stay hitched. 

IIRC - the Midlands Road used to be called The Great Northern Highway, but lost that title when the Brand Highway was opened. Up until then it was the main road between Perth and Geraldton. 
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
