   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Golden Pipeline Trail - Northam&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Dog In a ute&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/231715c2-fe5d-4c55-a871-4681e643642a"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/231715c2-fe5d-4c55-a871-4681e643642a&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year did the Withnell brothers arrive in Northam?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7ab952d9-d51a-4e94-8077-2e8b776934d3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Withnell brothers were jack of all trades in town. There are still decendants of Horace and Herbert living in Northam today.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/21130ac3-43db-452d-81dc-093d6b83da95" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This adventure lab is part of the Golden Pipeline Trail from Mundaring to Kalgoorlie.
Northam townsite was set aside in November 1830. Northam achieved prominence with the extension of railway to the Goldfields in 1894. It became an important centre for the provision of public services such as railways, roads, and water supplies.
In 1949 after the 2nd World War - Northams Millitary Hospital and Army Camp became the  Commonwealth  Immigration Accommodation Centre accommodating
 thousands of refugees.  With the refugees later settling in Northam it gave the town a population mix quite different to most other rural towns. A number of them worked on the water supply scheme.
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
