   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Golden Pipeline Trail - Northam&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;St Johns &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/231715c2-fe5d-4c55-a871-4681e643642a"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/231715c2-fe5d-4c55-a871-4681e643642a&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt; What is the Bishops Sir name?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e37d1259-0ec2-4f88-bc0c-149815a97862" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;St John the Evangelist Church in Northam is a picturesque Gothic style historical church built at the end of the 19th century using locally quarried stone. The stained glass windows which have been constructed using glass from St Georges Cathedral in Perth and Old St James, which was Northam’s first church. Look out for the large cracks that were the result of an earthquake in the late 1960s.
You are looking for a stone plaque laid by a Perth Bishop in 1889.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/21130ac3-43db-452d-81dc-093d6b83da95" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This adventure lab is part of the Golden Pipeline Trail from Mundaring to Kalgoorlie.
Northam townsite was set aside in November 1830. Northam achieved prominence with the extension of railway to the Goldfields in 1894. It became an important centre for the provision of public services such as railways, roads, and water supplies.
In 1949 after the 2nd World War - Northams Millitary Hospital and Army Camp became the  Commonwealth  Immigration Accommodation Centre accommodating
 thousands of refugees.  With the refugees later settling in Northam it gave the town a population mix quite different to most other rural towns. A number of them worked on the water supply scheme.
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.62765" lon="116.992383">
  <ele>208.0</ele>
