   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Golden Pipeline Trail - Meckering&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Big Camera&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/944ff8d0-ccde-4143-8931-2e6fa251610c"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/944ff8d0-ccde-4143-8931-2e6fa251610c&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is this giant camera structure used as? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2dbb9e1d-ed84-4c8c-ac5d-55ce80e6d4d7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;You've heard of the giant banana, giant ram, giant crayfish ... well Meckering has its own claim to fame with its giant Camera.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2607e740-9581-4825-8507-65fe73ace4d1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Golden Pipeline Heritage Trail follows the water pipeline conceived by C.Y.O'Connor to supply the Goldfields of Western Australia with much needed fresh water.
Meckering - a town along the way, benefited from the pipeline and still does today. Once a thriving country town, the devastation of an earthquake in 1968 flattened the town and it has never fully recovered.
This Adventure Lab will take you on a trip into the history of this little town.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
