   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Golden Pipeline Trail - Meckering&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Pioneer Cemetery that once was&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/944ff8d0-ccde-4143-8931-2e6fa251610c"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/944ff8d0-ccde-4143-8931-2e6fa251610c&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Vincent Selby worked on the pipeline for a period of how many years? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a141af57-f767-48b5-8a31-b80e766945bf" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This cemetery was closed in 1913 due to shallow rock. All burial records were destroyed by fire in 1927.  In 1966 its11 acres were cleared to allow for an expansion of the Meckering golf links.Sadly this one grave and the headstones are all that remains. You are looking for the one grave.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2607e740-9581-4825-8507-65fe73ace4d1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Golden Pipeline Heritage Trail follows the water pipeline conceived by C.Y.O'Connor to supply the Goldfields of Western Australia with much needed fresh water.
Meckering - a town along the way, benefited from the pipeline and still does today. Once a thriving country town, the devastation of an earthquake in 1968 flattened the town and it has never fully recovered.
This Adventure Lab will take you on a trip into the history of this little town.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
