   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Horseyard Hill Part 2 &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Tingle all over &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/314ecaff-f545-40de-89c3-b6f9d81cb10f"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/314ecaff-f545-40de-89c3-b6f9d81cb10f&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The yellow tingle has tiny cups for what? one word &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a6d31743-dfac-4fed-b26f-641da0545f75" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The yellow tingle is only found in the Walpole area and can grow to 40 metres, it usually flowers in December-January.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/94926b8f-8b87-4bbf-ac53-c20bb16178e9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Continue your walk around the trail and find the second part of this adventure. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
