   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Horseyard Hill Trail &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Cheap glue? &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/2f5cf0f1-e9ab-40c3-b039-b34d6c9c4514"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/2f5cf0f1-e9ab-40c3-b039-b34d6c9c4514&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Kangaroo droppings mixed with .. makes glue? one word &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/797fb87b-46c2-41c7-bf93-51b04319e77a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This walks gives interesting uses for the trees and shrubs that surround you. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a374ffc7-ce3e-4a95-9a01-c63f81f00edd" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to a hidden gem in Walpole. Located behind the visitor centre, Horseyard Hill is a 2.5 kilometre walk through beautiful bush. In Spring there is a variety of wildflowers to see and lots of birds to look out for. I suggest turning right at the end of the bridge to ensure downhill at the end :) Allow an hour. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
