   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Golden Pipeline Trail: Ghooli &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Stacked Up &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/707c666c-a724-4ee6-a2df-2550cc44b397"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/707c666c-a724-4ee6-a2df-2550cc44b397&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What's the name of the man pictured painting the stack? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7a275197-2aa7-48a5-bfcb-7d65b5fd9ffb" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A steel chimney 1.2m in diameter and 27m high set in a cast iron foot. the structure is supported with three wired guys. Chimney is lined with curved firebricks. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/69e3d017-c07f-4f84-8a3e-ae62ccb93bcb" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ghooli, Pump Station Number 6 on the Golden Pipeline Trail. 
Located 10km East of Southern Cross just off the main highway. 
A number of abandoned buildings here closed off to the public and containing asbestos so please follow the signage and warning signs. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
