  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-525" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Kings Park - Fraser Ave : S3 Historic Drinking Fountain</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Leg5</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Leg5</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Kings Park - Fraser Ave&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Historic Drinking Fountain&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5863f379-5bdb-42ee-b18b-906281c33058"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5863f379-5bdb-42ee-b18b-906281c33058&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;On the plaque, who was the Managing Director of the Water Authority (Surname only)?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3971e6d2-9870-43a6-9e7a-5e9dbfa82d29" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The fountain commemorates the centenary of Perth's Water Supply. Not far behind you is the Mt Eliza Reservoir is where the water is stored.

Right next to the fountain is the Tea Rooms Shelter. In 1899 the Terrace Tearooms was officially opened but down on the Swan River at Terrace Gardens. But in 1919 the Tea Room was moved to this location as a public Shelter, and there was 3 of these buildings in Kings Park - this is the last remaining.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e1fa713b-0775-4ace-ad00-6eff90846441" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to King Park, Fraser Ave has a few lesser known monuments and statues of WA’s history.
Ready for the 20 year Memorial of the Bali Bombing in Kuta.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
