   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Kings Park - Fraser Ave&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;10th Light Horse Regiment&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5863f379-5bdb-42ee-b18b-906281c33058"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5863f379-5bdb-42ee-b18b-906281c33058&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Alphabetically, who is the last name on the plaques?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4c4d6f74-e143-4425-bb5e-05133b05b609" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The monument was erected to perpetuate the Memory of those of the 10th Light Horse Regiment who fell in the Great War.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e1fa713b-0775-4ace-ad00-6eff90846441" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to King Park, Fraser Ave has a few lesser known monuments and statues of WA’s history.
Ready for the 20 year Memorial of the Bali Bombing in Kuta.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
