   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Peace Memorial Rose Garden&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Wishing Well&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f188fa14-b315-4023-b01c-80de265b2cf9"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f188fa14-b315-4023-b01c-80de265b2cf9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Which Club erected the wishing well?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ef0dfa6e-82ac-45cc-8c97-24eaa2ea021c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The plaque on the well will provide you with the answer to the following question.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/264b0418-c476-4227-9fb3-afed73ef57a7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A commemorative rose garden comprising formal rose plantings, hard and soft landscape elements, that was built over a period of years from 1948 to the early 1960s to the design of architect W.G. Bennett, and later modified in the 1970s and 1980s, has cultural heritage significance for the following reasons: 
