   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Swarbrick Wander &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Halo&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/930cdbde-8d95-45a5-b26f-b66ac0295e80"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/930cdbde-8d95-45a5-b26f-b66ac0295e80&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the halo called? Golden ?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d11c103e-e549-4f54-bc74-6103ef917d7e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Look up into the trees, a golden halo swings in the breeze. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1879aeaf-cd93-481d-927c-e415d1cb8813" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to Swarbrick part of the Walpole Wilderness. Enjoy your walk through the bush and admire the amazing mirrored wall. This area was logged in the late 90s and there was wide spread protesting at the logging of native trees that included Yellow Tingle, a tree only found in a 50k radius of Walpole. Now we are lucky to have a beautiful, peaceful walk where you can see wildflowers and listen to the birds. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
