   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Swarbrick Wander &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Light as a feather&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/930cdbde-8d95-45a5-b26f-b66ac0295e80"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/930cdbde-8d95-45a5-b26f-b66ac0295e80&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What 5 letter word is before feather?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/673e9f96-9493-47ed-8d5b-5ebfe1524c54" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Light as a feather, but not this one. This piece is by Lorenna Grant and Alan Clark and symbolises the endangered species and the loss of habitat. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1879aeaf-cd93-481d-927c-e415d1cb8813" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to Swarbrick part of the Walpole Wilderness. Enjoy your walk through the bush and admire the amazing mirrored wall. This area was logged in the late 90s and there was wide spread protesting at the logging of native trees that included Yellow Tingle, a tree only found in a 50k radius of Walpole. Now we are lucky to have a beautiful, peaceful walk where you can see wildflowers and listen to the birds. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
