 <wpt lat="-32.065117" lon="115.99985">
  <ele>21.0</ele>
  <time>2022-10-29T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBTyT3-01</name>
  <desc>HuntForTheHidd1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9900c07b-6b0f-4d06-b21c-9ccf18eff6ec</url>
  <urlname>The Hunt for the Hidden Valley Cache : S1 The Entrance to Hidden Valley by Paskersfind</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476910072" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>The Hunt for the Hidden Valley Cache : S1 The Entrance to Hidden Valley</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Paskersfind</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Paskersfind</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;The Hunt for the Hidden Valley Cache&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Entrance to Hidden Valley&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9900c07b-6b0f-4d06-b21c-9ccf18eff6ec"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9900c07b-6b0f-4d06-b21c-9ccf18eff6ec&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;One of the numbers required for the code is exactly half the total number of silver statues.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/bdd73eab-56b8-453d-a0e8-7dbf5aa036ba" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The map showed a small red star located in the top  corner. This is probably the best point through which to enter the valley. At this location, there is a statuary of tall, silver, strangely shaped creatures guarding the entrance. Luckily, they appear to be frozen in time and pose no threat.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/39eb6d61-865b-4f07-97b6-2812f4c685f9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The MAP showed features of a secluded river valley nestled right in the middle of suburbia. We had been rummaging around in the garage and found it under a drawer lining in an old desk.  Although it was a roughly drawn mud map, it clearly showed five locations within the valley where details could be found that would lead to a well-hidden secret cache. Such caches are highly sought after by adventure-seeking, outdoorsy types. The location of the secret cache is protected with a five digit code. The task is simple: visit all five locations, gather the necessary numbers and use them to work out the code.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.06575" lon="115.999933">
  <ele>21.0</ele>
  <time>2022-10-29T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBTyT3-02</name>
  <desc>HuntForTheHidd2</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9900c07b-6b0f-4d06-b21c-9ccf18eff6ec</url>
  <urlname>The Hunt for the Hidden Valley Cache : S2 The Lookout by Paskersfind</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476910074" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>The Hunt for the Hidden Valley Cache : S2 The Lookout</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Paskersfind</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Paskersfind</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;The Hunt for the Hidden Valley Cache&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Lookout&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9900c07b-6b0f-4d06-b21c-9ccf18eff6ec"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9900c07b-6b0f-4d06-b21c-9ccf18eff6ec&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Another number required for the code is the total number of flagpoles visible from this location.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/81003e89-bee1-40e3-8ef1-bf01940f5dbe" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Once past the bizarre statues, move towards the furthest reach of the lookout overhang marked with a red cross on the map. This vantage point provides splendid panoramic views across the valley and down to the the winding river at the bottom. As you take in the view, you can't help but notice a number of tall wooden or metal uprights, some with banners fluttering in the breeze.









&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/39eb6d61-865b-4f07-97b6-2812f4c685f9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The MAP showed features of a secluded river valley nestled right in the middle of suburbia. We had been rummaging around in the garage and found it under a drawer lining in an old desk.  Although it was a roughly drawn mud map, it clearly showed five locations within the valley where details could be found that would lead to a well-hidden secret cache. Such caches are highly sought after by adventure-seeking, outdoorsy types. The location of the secret cache is protected with a five digit code. The task is simple: visit all five locations, gather the necessary numbers and use them to work out the code.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.066183" lon="116.000167">
  <ele>11.0</ele>
  <time>2022-10-29T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBTyT3-03</name>
  <desc>HuntForTheHidd3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9900c07b-6b0f-4d06-b21c-9ccf18eff6ec</url>
  <urlname>The Hunt for the Hidden Valley Cache : S3 The Silent Beacons by Paskersfind</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476910076" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>The Hunt for the Hidden Valley Cache : S3 The Silent Beacons</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Paskersfind</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Paskersfind</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;The Hunt for the Hidden Valley Cache&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Silent Beacons&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9900c07b-6b0f-4d06-b21c-9ccf18eff6ec"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9900c07b-6b0f-4d06-b21c-9ccf18eff6ec&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many of these park benches can you see from this location?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4bfc7634-9b0e-4602-a282-09e76d330355" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It's time to enter the enter valley and have a look around. The map takes you to the junction of two pathways (as shown on the map with a red circle) where two rigid beacons stand guard. From this central location in the heart of the valley, take a 360 degree panorama and take note of the number of wooden-planked resting benches (of the type made with metal frames)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/39eb6d61-865b-4f07-97b6-2812f4c685f9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The MAP showed features of a secluded river valley nestled right in the middle of suburbia. We had been rummaging around in the garage and found it under a drawer lining in an old desk.  Although it was a roughly drawn mud map, it clearly showed five locations within the valley where details could be found that would lead to a well-hidden secret cache. Such caches are highly sought after by adventure-seeking, outdoorsy types. The location of the secret cache is protected with a five digit code. The task is simple: visit all five locations, gather the necessary numbers and use them to work out the code.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.06645" lon="116">
  <ele>7.0</ele>
  <time>2022-10-29T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBTyT3-04</name>
  <desc>HuntForTheHidd4</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9900c07b-6b0f-4d06-b21c-9ccf18eff6ec</url>
  <urlname>The Hunt for the Hidden Valley Cache : S4 The Solitary Obelisk by Paskersfind</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476910078" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>The Hunt for the Hidden Valley Cache : S4 The Solitary Obelisk</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Paskersfind</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Paskersfind</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;The Hunt for the Hidden Valley Cache&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Solitary Obelisk&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9900c07b-6b0f-4d06-b21c-9ccf18eff6ec"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9900c07b-6b0f-4d06-b21c-9ccf18eff6ec&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many lights make exactly half a Bank?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f2f3c636-f053-4e4c-854c-0830034a1543" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Take a walk up the garden path towards the Egyptian style obelisk positioned in this place of honour and guarded by rows of thorny shrubbery. This solitary monument stands defiantly as a tribute to those local heroes who made the ultimate sacrifice in years gone by. Take note of the BANK of caged illuminators placed to keep this memorial lit up when darkness descends.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/39eb6d61-865b-4f07-97b6-2812f4c685f9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The MAP showed features of a secluded river valley nestled right in the middle of suburbia. We had been rummaging around in the garage and found it under a drawer lining in an old desk.  Although it was a roughly drawn mud map, it clearly showed five locations within the valley where details could be found that would lead to a well-hidden secret cache. Such caches are highly sought after by adventure-seeking, outdoorsy types. The location of the secret cache is protected with a five digit code. The task is simple: visit all five locations, gather the necessary numbers and use them to work out the code.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.066317" lon="116.000683">
  <ele>10.0</ele>
  <time>2022-10-29T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBTyT3-05</name>
  <desc>HuntForTheHidd5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9900c07b-6b0f-4d06-b21c-9ccf18eff6ec</url>
  <urlname>The Hunt for the Hidden Valley Cache : S5 View to a Fountain by Paskersfind</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476910080" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>The Hunt for the Hidden Valley Cache : S5 View to a Fountain</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Paskersfind</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Paskersfind</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;The Hunt for the Hidden Valley Cache&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;View to a Fountain&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9900c07b-6b0f-4d06-b21c-9ccf18eff6ec"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9900c07b-6b0f-4d06-b21c-9ccf18eff6ec&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many horizontal planks make up exactly fifty percent of the platform?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7705ab84-f207-43b4-bd22-8d806d33ce34" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Following the map trail to the other side of the Hidden Valley, you arrive at a viewing platform (shown as a red square on the map) providing unobstructed views  across the lake to a prominent stone fountain. Water lilies cover much of this water feature and a small bridge on the opposite side provides access to the river beyond. This viewing platform is made up of a number of solid, horizontal planks at its base.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/39eb6d61-865b-4f07-97b6-2812f4c685f9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The MAP showed features of a secluded river valley nestled right in the middle of suburbia. We had been rummaging around in the garage and found it under a drawer lining in an old desk.  Although it was a roughly drawn mud map, it clearly showed five locations within the valley where details could be found that would lead to a well-hidden secret cache. Such caches are highly sought after by adventure-seeking, outdoorsy types. The location of the secret cache is protected with a five digit code. The task is simple: visit all five locations, gather the necessary numbers and use them to work out the code.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-33.5655" lon="115.084017">
  <ele>7.0</ele>
  <time>2022-11-05T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LB7o32-02</name>
  <desc>EagleBayToDuns2</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a54c0df8-64b7-4bfb-a777-7e4c38979501</url>
  <urlname>Eagle Bay to Dunsborough coastal trail : S2 Point Picquet whale lookout by J2V</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476910093" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Eagle Bay to Dunsborough coastal trail : S2 Point Picquet whale lookout</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>J2V</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">J2V</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Eagle Bay to Dunsborough coastal trail&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Point Picquet whale lookout&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a54c0df8-64b7-4bfb-a777-7e4c38979501"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a54c0df8-64b7-4bfb-a777-7e4c38979501&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What do southern right whales have over their heads (two words)?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/58a06fb7-4921-4cbd-adf4-7487e7052253" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;From September to November humpback, southern right and blue whales come close to shore as part of their annual southern migration. Read the 'whales of the cape' sign to answer the next question.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/bd32bbf8-f562-41c9-8be7-396cd98bec60" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Start at Eagle Bay and walk or run 8-9 kms on marked trails to Dunsborough boat ramp. Learn some local history, spot a whale (at the right time of year) and enjoy stunning coastal scenery. The trail is mainly flat, with some rocky and narrow sections. Wear sturdy shoes. The AdLab can be completed by car.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-33.560833" lon="115.069667">
  <ele>11.0</ele>
  <time>2022-11-05T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LB7o32-01</name>
  <desc>EagleBayToDuns1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a54c0df8-64b7-4bfb-a777-7e4c38979501</url>
  <urlname>Eagle Bay to Dunsborough coastal trail : S1 Baudin monument by J2V</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476910091" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Eagle Bay to Dunsborough coastal trail : S1 Baudin monument</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>J2V</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">J2V</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Eagle Bay to Dunsborough coastal trail&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Baudin monument&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a54c0df8-64b7-4bfb-a777-7e4c38979501"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a54c0df8-64b7-4bfb-a777-7e4c38979501&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the first word in the Aboriginal greeting on the nearby sign about salmon fishing?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/fc85c9ec-395a-4825-a017-0628f8f0f0eb" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;On 31 May 1801 Henri de Freycinet and men from a French scientific expedition landed a small boat from the ships Geographe and Naturaliste searching for water. It was the first known European landing in South West Australia. Nicholas Baudin was the captain of the expedition.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/bd32bbf8-f562-41c9-8be7-396cd98bec60" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Start at Eagle Bay and walk or run 8-9 kms on marked trails to Dunsborough boat ramp. Learn some local history, spot a whale (at the right time of year) and enjoy stunning coastal scenery. The trail is mainly flat, with some rocky and narrow sections. Wear sturdy shoes. The AdLab can be completed by car.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-33.572667" lon="115.086683">
