   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Mandurah’s Western Foreshore&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Fishing anyone? &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a5faf733-574a-4f1c-953b-b4d30e2a09f1"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a5faf733-574a-4f1c-953b-b4d30e2a09f1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the Maximum legal size in centimetres for Barramundi? (Enter the 2-digit number not the word) &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/394e5683-ac56-4676-9aa6-8f3ad53843b2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Mandurah is renowned for recreational fishing and crabbing. Common fish caught in the Estuary include herring, sand whiting, bream, cobbler, tailor and garfish. In season you can fish for salmon and tailor on the beach, and the Dawesville Cut is the best place to catch King George whiting.
Wherever you choose to cast your line, it is important to adhere to local fishing guidelines and legal size limits. 

In this location you will find an information ruler outlining the legal size limits for a variety of fish species. Examine this to answer the following question. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/03e30169-31d8-442d-bc07-e652a663c4cf" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Mandurah’s Western Foreshore has recently undergone a transformation with the inclusion of a play space that is a hub for families and friends to meet, play and rest. 

Designed for people of all ages and abilities, the new play space will be full of fun and activity year-round. It is a place for people to gather, celebrate and explore in the beauty of Mandurah’s Western Foreshore.

The play space design is inspired by Mandurah’s heritage, character and world-renowned natural environment. It connects the land and water by featuring elements from Mandurah’s iconic waterways including boating and estuary themed sculptural play.

This recreation precinct also includes a skate and activity space, 
large picnic tables, drinking fountains, a seating deck and new toilet facilities. 

With so much on offer here, I invite you to spend a little while exploring the area. Enjoy! 

**There is a bonus cache to find once the adventure is complete so remember to note down the clues after each completed location. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
