   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Mandurah’s Western Foreshore&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Meeting Place&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a5faf733-574a-4f1c-953b-b4d30e2a09f1"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a5faf733-574a-4f1c-953b-b4d30e2a09f1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Complete this sentence found on the plaque on top of one of the cut logs. ‘In honour of the new bridge, a new place to _____ __ _____’ (3 words)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/bbbde500-4982-451d-9a79-5bd62b25ae8b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Artist Chris Nixon’s concept for ‘Meeting Place’ was inspired by elemental forces of the Peel-Harvey Estuary and acts as an intersection of time and forces. It is a meeting place of the developed and natural.

The artwork entices viewers to explore and interact with it. Viewers experience unique angles from all perspectives as the artwork constantly changes and moves with the viewer. 

By day the artwork moves with the viewer, whereas at night the motion is driven by the animated lighting pulsing and dancing across the façade.

The nightly show further enhances the impact and iconic nature of the artwork. It appears as a floating illuminated helix responding to natural forces in real time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/03e30169-31d8-442d-bc07-e652a663c4cf" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Mandurah’s Western Foreshore has recently undergone a transformation with the inclusion of a play space that is a hub for families and friends to meet, play and rest. 

Designed for people of all ages and abilities, the new play space will be full of fun and activity year-round. It is a place for people to gather, celebrate and explore in the beauty of Mandurah’s Western Foreshore.

The play space design is inspired by Mandurah’s heritage, character and world-renowned natural environment. It connects the land and water by featuring elements from Mandurah’s iconic waterways including boating and estuary themed sculptural play.

This recreation precinct also includes a skate and activity space, 
large picnic tables, drinking fountains, a seating deck and new toilet facilities. 

With so much on offer here, I invite you to spend a little while exploring the area. Enjoy! 

**There is a bonus cache to find once the adventure is complete so remember to note down the clues after each completed location. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
