   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Mount Barker Police Station Museum&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Historical Precinct&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/2e0c764c-20a7-4cb3-8573-eeae1ad096a8"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/2e0c764c-20a7-4cb3-8573-eeae1ad096a8&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;From the information listed on the sign, what three words relate to the years 1868 - 1957?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/327c5af8-322e-420e-9087-889ff9f8ac98" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Museum is managed by volunteers. This signage lists all the features and usage of the location and well maintained buildings and gardens.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ffd33a9e-f987-492f-81f5-ae0bb5dfc8cf" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The original Old Police Station built was by convict labour in 1868. The mid 1880s saw the horse stables divided off as a lockup and a Court House office was added in 1919.Surrounded by magnificent lawns and gardens, the Plantagenet Historical Society opened the Cottage as a museum in 1968, furnishing it with artefacts donated by residents of the Shire.
The Old Police Station was occupied until 1908 when a new police station was constructed next door.
Other buildings include a Pioneer Room, Cottage, Stables, School House and a reconstructed 1870s house built of hand split wooden slabs and a complete apple picking shed has been assembled in honour of that industry's historical contribution and his and her "thunder boxes".

&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-34.618183" lon="117.660983">
  <ele>246.0</ele>
  <time>2022-11-24T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBdesy-02</name>
  <desc>MountBarkerPol2</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/2e0c764c-20a7-4cb3-8573-eeae1ad096a8</url>
  <urlname>Mount Barker Police Station Museum : S2 Police Station by richlink</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918640" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Mount Barker Police Station Museum : S2 Police Station</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>richlink</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">richlink</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Mount Barker Police Station Museum&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Police Station&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/2e0c764c-20a7-4cb3-8573-eeae1ad096a8"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/2e0c764c-20a7-4cb3-8573-eeae1ad096a8&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What other 'station' was established here in 1871? (one word)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/dad4d48c-1973-47c6-b6f7-f7215a561d0a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Police duties included not only law and enforcement but also having a change of horses ready for the mail coach which operated from Albany to Perth. They also patrolled as far as Esperance on horseback and other duties included census, weather reporting and mail deliveries.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ffd33a9e-f987-492f-81f5-ae0bb5dfc8cf" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The original Old Police Station built was by convict labour in 1868. The mid 1880s saw the horse stables divided off as a lockup and a Court House office was added in 1919.Surrounded by magnificent lawns and gardens, the Plantagenet Historical Society opened the Cottage as a museum in 1968, furnishing it with artefacts donated by residents of the Shire.
The Old Police Station was occupied until 1908 when a new police station was constructed next door.
Other buildings include a Pioneer Room, Cottage, Stables, School House and a reconstructed 1870s house built of hand split wooden slabs and a complete apple picking shed has been assembled in honour of that industry's historical contribution and his and her "thunder boxes".

&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-35.030117" lon="117.913517">
  <ele>112.0</ele>
