   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Convoy Walk&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Longing, Memory, Sight&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/4e032777-9aa9-46e8-9ac2-eaeef28a5b6c"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/4e032777-9aa9-46e8-9ac2-eaeef28a5b6c&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;At the base of the sculpture there is a metal plaque - aluminium, bronze and …….&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4f0cd3c8-e277-4f19-b8a3-f154015a0591" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;An artwork titled Longing, Memory, Sight -by Arif Satar and Audrey Fernandes-Satar marks the beginning of Convoy Walk. 

Inspired by a fragment of a letter a soldier sent to his loved one, it consists of an aluminium sculpture placed on top of a granite plinth. The plinth contains inscribed text obtained from original letters and postcards sent by Australian soldiers who departed in the 1914 Albany convoy to their loved ones during their deployment in First World War.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1e12e854-31da-4051-ac06-61d3cb90eb9b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Situated in the Albany Heritage Park, The Convoy Walk and lookout on Mount Adelaide was officially opened on 1 November 2014. The Convoy Walk leads to the Convoy Lookout with a view over King George Sound where troops gathered on ships before departing for the First World War. The walk contains 21 markers containing information about the ships in the First and Second Convoys, including the names and images of the troopships and escorts, and where they embarked troops. The lookout includes a shelter and interpretive material relating to the vessels in the convoy.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
