   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;The Mystery of the Stolen Painting&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Four Pots&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/40b41820-3bbd-48f9-9811-6830a152bd2f"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/40b41820-3bbd-48f9-9811-6830a152bd2f&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;A certain letter on the plaque underneath the sculpture is a different colour. The suspect whose surname begins with that letter is innocent&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/21a6a0e3-f2eb-46fe-9877-0019bc86780f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Not all people would trust a teenager as a witness, but you know James Kelly is a very honest, clever and also eagle-eyed boy. So when you spot him in the Civic Center, you ask him if he was here at the time of the robbery. "I sure was!", he replies and gives you some valuable information.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/09cbec68-fe11-474d-b178-d59b8171b7c6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Somebody has stolen the priceless painting "The Lady and the Geocache" by Geonardo DaVinci from the Akluger Art Gallery in the Cottesloe Civic Center! Police have identified six possible suspects. But now they need a witty and clever detective to find out who dunnit! That's where you come in. You have been asked by the police and the Akluger Art Gallery to ask witnesses and in this way discover the culprit.
These are the suspects:
Kevin Brown
Desiree McCabe
Richard Lesser
Lara Williams
Kira Orwell
Sam Bennet&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
