Here you will find many walk trails and parks .
Homestead ridge has a long history . The Wellard hospital was constructed in 1926 to service the settlement in the area . It was dismounted in 1930 and moved to Esperance. There is a plaque where the hospital stood on shipwright street. 
There are many native animals roaming in the parks and bush land . We have see kangaroo’s to bandicoots snakes and many different types of lizards so be careful. All the paths and trails are suitable for all ages .&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
