   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;OOH YEH’s BACKYARD&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Crossroads B&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/2dccdb2d-049c-4432-a102-7f62954051ad"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/2dccdb2d-049c-4432-a102-7f62954051ad&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the  26th letter&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9112b1f8-ef96-41ff-bda3-793d73e19f02" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Here you are looking for a sign of the Galah . There are many types of Galahs in the area most common one is the pink and grey . &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d05409b3-25f7-42f4-bf9c-4316a779cc2e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to our play ground . 
Here you will find many walk trails and parks .
Homestead ridge has a long history . The Wellard hospital was constructed in 1926 to service the settlement in the area . It was dismounted in 1930 and moved to Esperance. There is a plaque where the hospital stood on shipwright street. 
There are many native animals roaming in the parks and bush land . We have see kangaroo’s to bandicoots snakes and many different types of lizards so be careful. All the paths and trails are suitable for all ages .&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
