   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Masons Landing Park&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;A Bustling Timber Town&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ffd6034a-ad02-46a3-ae76-5b0684e8b293"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ffd6034a-ad02-46a3-ae76-5b0684e8b293&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Stables were built for how many horses?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b08253fc-5d65-41b2-90ed-0cdd08d71620" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A small town sprung up on the banks of the river to support Mason and Bird's timber operations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/683085f4-1abc-49e6-b3ac-47888691d176" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Masons Landing Park is on the banks of the Canning River.
It is a great spot for a family fun day out as there is a playground, bbqs, toilets and a gazebo.
It is a perfect place to launch a canoe and explore the river.
Take a stroll around the park and learn about the local environment and history.

There is information on each journal page that will help you locate bonus cache GCA2KT0 when it is published.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
