   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Masons Landing Park&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Original 'Canning Highway'&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ffd6034a-ad02-46a3-ae76-5b0684e8b293"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ffd6034a-ad02-46a3-ae76-5b0684e8b293&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Where was the timber milled? (two words)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b293c354-e502-487e-ad98-74e2e7c74958" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Canning River played a major role in the growth of Perth,  In the absence of roads, it was the major 'highway' linking people in outlying settlements to the main colony on the bank of the Swan River.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/683085f4-1abc-49e6-b3ac-47888691d176" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Masons Landing Park is on the banks of the Canning River.
It is a great spot for a family fun day out as there is a playground, bbqs, toilets and a gazebo.
It is a perfect place to launch a canoe and explore the river.
Take a stroll around the park and learn about the local environment and history.

There is information on each journal page that will help you locate bonus cache GCA2KT0 when it is published.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
