  <desc>MasonsLandingP5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ffd6034a-ad02-46a3-ae76-5b0684e8b293</url>
  <urlname>Masons Landing Park : S5 Woodloes Homestead by fratra</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-375" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Masons Landing Park : S5 Woodloes Homestead</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>fratra</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">fratra</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Masons Landing Park&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Woodloes Homestead&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ffd6034a-ad02-46a3-ae76-5b0684e8b293"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ffd6034a-ad02-46a3-ae76-5b0684e8b293&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How long is the trail to Woodloes Homestead in metres?  (digits only required)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8c84918a-0d09-4c0b-b52b-247b71bd48b5" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Woodloes Homestead was built in 1871 by architect Francis Bird. 
The homestead is situated on the banks of the Canning River in Cannington. 
Bird was partner in the Mason-Bird Timber Company, cut timber in the Darling Range and transported it via a horse-drawn railway to Mason's Landing, near Woodloes Homstead.  Woodloes Homstead was classified by the National Trust in 1988, nominated to the Register of The National Estate in 1991 and permanently added to Western Australian State Heritage register on 21 January 1997.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/683085f4-1abc-49e6-b3ac-47888691d176" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Masons Landing Park is on the banks of the Canning River.
It is a great spot for a family fun day out as there is a playground, bbqs, toilets and a gazebo.
It is a perfect place to launch a canoe and explore the river.
Take a stroll around the park and learn about the local environment and history.

There is information on each journal page that will help you locate bonus cache GCA2KT0 when it is published.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.025067" lon="115.936033">
  <ele>3.0</ele>
  <time>2022-12-04T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBsgxk-04</name>
  <desc>MasonsLandingP4</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ffd6034a-ad02-46a3-ae76-5b0684e8b293</url>
  <urlname>Masons Landing Park : S4 Oxygenation by fratra</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-374" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Masons Landing Park : S4 Oxygenation</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>fratra</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">fratra</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Masons Landing Park&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Oxygenation&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ffd6034a-ad02-46a3-ae76-5b0684e8b293"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ffd6034a-ad02-46a3-ae76-5b0684e8b293&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many oxygenation plants are now in place?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ec564dc7-7aeb-4e27-9f70-754160130a14" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The first oxygenation plant in Western Australia was constructed on the Canning River in the summer of 1998. It was part of a trial to investigate the feasibility of artificial oxygenation to improve water quality in the river and reduce phytoplankton blooms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/683085f4-1abc-49e6-b3ac-47888691d176" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Masons Landing Park is on the banks of the Canning River.
It is a great spot for a family fun day out as there is a playground, bbqs, toilets and a gazebo.
It is a perfect place to launch a canoe and explore the river.
Take a stroll around the park and learn about the local environment and history.

There is information on each journal page that will help you locate bonus cache GCA2KT0 when it is published.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
