   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Centenary Park&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Homecoming&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/80116ab4-5884-4d7f-9c67-a189511315fe"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/80116ab4-5884-4d7f-9c67-a189511315fe&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the soldier who is pictured bottom left of the plaque?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b6cf700c-9399-41ea-90c5-047bc183628b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Returned soldiers were able to spend time together at the Soldiers' Memorial Club, erected in memory of fallen soldiers, which opened on Anzac Day in 1921. The lead lights of the club show the colours of all the W.A units of the Australian Imperial Force (A.I.F).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3cdf6088-e8c2-4881-860e-0246555679c5" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Centenary park is located on Albany Highway at the junction of Memorial Avenue, opposite the Plantagenet District Hall.  It encompasses the War Memorial and the We Remember Them Walk.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
