   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Golden Pipeline Trail - No 2 Pump Station&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Suction Tank&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e789e21f-dc4b-4b60-8b75-80ff7a615248"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e789e21f-dc4b-4b60-8b75-80ff7a615248&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many bolt holes are in the end of the suction pipe? (Numerals)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c25a65cd-92f5-44ae-803c-fcabc4382c6d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;At this location you will find the remains of what was once the main suction tank for the pump station.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c9825c1b-a32a-4c53-9918-e67288a5d7e5" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The golden Pipeline Heritage Trail follows the water pipeline conceived by C.Y. O'Connor to supply the Goldfields of Western Australia with much needed fresh water.

The site of No 2 Pump Station was agonised over, probably because of the hilly terrain and the clayey soil. But a decision had to be made because two pumping stations were required to lift the water over the Darling Range.

In the end the hilly site chosen was fairly constricted so the suction tank and station were placed in line rather than the tank to one side of the station building as in other stations, which was more desirable in engineering terms.  No 2 Pump Station, completed in 1902, was probably situated in the most picturesque place of all the pumping station sites on the Goldfields Water Supply Scheme.

This Lab will take you to the original site where you will be required to answer some questions to proceed through the adventure and get the clues to find the bonus cache.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
