 <wpt lat="-31.450183" lon="130.896683">
  <ele>64.0</ele>
  <time>2022-12-28T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LB7VhG-03</name>
  <desc>NullarborLinksA</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/745abbe8-55ee-4581-a365-a77eaa22f810</url>
  <urlname>Nullarbor Links ~ The Aussie Way ~ Number Two : S3 Nullabor Road House ~ We're Back by pood</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99009148" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Nullarbor Links ~ The Aussie Way ~ Number Two : S3 Nullabor Road House ~ We're Back</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>pood</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">pood</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>South Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Nullarbor Links ~ The Aussie Way ~ Number Two&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Nullabor Road House ~ We're Back&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/745abbe8-55ee-4581-a365-a77eaa22f810"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/745abbe8-55ee-4581-a365-a77eaa22f810&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;There are 3 animals on this iconic Australian sign, what is the middle animal?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/900bd091-477a-4bf4-b36a-43190b47cc39" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Nullarbor Plain is one of Australia’s ultimate road trips. This colossal drive, which makes up a big chunk of the trip from Adelaide to Perth, requires an fair amount of preparation to complete successfully. Plenty of extra water is needed to last the distance as water is sometimes hard to get on the Nullabor. There is plenty of free camping sites and a few Roadhouses with accomodation and meals available along the way.

If you have ample time, there is plenty to see when conquering the Nullarbor Plain.
Using the Nullabor Roadhouse as a base, you can visit the Murrawijinie Caves to the north, 
see the old Nullabor Homestead Well and windmill, Gilgerabbie Hut to the south, the Nullabor Golf Links, the Old gravel Nullabor Highway to the east, out to the Ivy Tanks, the Great Australian Bight with the whales and their calves during the optimum months.

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1299bda9-577a-4113-b5cd-8b570e06f78c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;As we travel across The Nullarbor Plain we are finding so much more to explore.
Caves,Cliffs,Geological sites and Homesteads - all the more for another Adventure Lab.
Crossing this huge plain is a quintessential Australian road trip experience and the incredible vast landscapes will make you feel in awe of the wonderful Country we are traveling across.
The name Nullarbor comes from the Latin word “nullus” meaning “nothing” and the word “arbor” meaning “tree”.
Wombats, emus and kangaroos call the Nullarbor home.
Can you imagine driving for 146.6km in a completely straight line, without a single bend or turn in the road? The Eyre Highway is where you will find this curve-free road, stretching between Caiguna and Balladonia.
As you drive across the Nullarbor Plain, you could play 18 holes of golf along the world’s longest golf course – the Nullarbor Links.
Now as you cross the Nullarbor Plain, you can add Australia's longest Adventure Lab the 'Nullarbor Links ~ The Aussie Way II', to your journey.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
