   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Nullarbor Links ~ The Aussie Way ~ Number Two&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Ceduna ~ The Oyster Capital of Australia&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/745abbe8-55ee-4581-a365-a77eaa22f810"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/745abbe8-55ee-4581-a365-a77eaa22f810&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;A breath of fresh _ _ _ _ !&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2aa52002-7dd8-4b98-b98d-448ae239ee40" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ceduna is home to a Giangantic Oyster and a robust oyster industry, with various leases from Denial Bay and Smoky Bay that supply almost half of South Australia’s Oysters. 
Ceduna has earned itself the title of ‘Oyster Capital of Australia’, which is celebrated at the Ceduna Oysterfest during the SA Labour Day long weekend in October each year.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1299bda9-577a-4113-b5cd-8b570e06f78c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;As we travel across The Nullarbor Plain we are finding so much more to explore.
Caves,Cliffs,Geological sites and Homesteads - all the more for another Adventure Lab.
Crossing this huge plain is a quintessential Australian road trip experience and the incredible vast landscapes will make you feel in awe of the wonderful Country we are traveling across.
The name Nullarbor comes from the Latin word “nullus” meaning “nothing” and the word “arbor” meaning “tree”.
Wombats, emus and kangaroos call the Nullarbor home.
Can you imagine driving for 146.6km in a completely straight line, without a single bend or turn in the road? The Eyre Highway is where you will find this curve-free road, stretching between Caiguna and Balladonia.
As you drive across the Nullarbor Plain, you could play 18 holes of golf along the world’s longest golf course – the Nullarbor Links.
Now as you cross the Nullarbor Plain, you can add Australia's longest Adventure Lab the 'Nullarbor Links ~ The Aussie Way II', to your journey.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
