   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Melville Places 2&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Fragment&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/dcccaf8c-0325-41cd-a347-209ffd5579d2"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/dcccaf8c-0325-41cd-a347-209ffd5579d2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year did the City of Melville acquire the sculpture?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/dff4024c-ae91-41f1-86e7-c9f1e4f59222" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fragment evokes memories and responses that relate to the coastal and agricultural environments of Western Australia and the fragile top soil that covers much of the Southern
Coastal regions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5bae889d-e961-46d5-be77-5328134fb8ab" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Public Art can improve the connectivity of a precinct and its interrelationship with the rest of the area. Good public art can contribute to a sense of place, enhancing public spaces and celebrating cultural identity and community aspirations. (Source Melville City Council)

Like many local governments around the Perth Metropolitan area the City of Melville have brought and commissioned many pieces of art that now dot the various public parks and pathways around the local government area.  They also have constructed various viewing platforms and memorials at significant locations with the city boundaries.

Image: Coming of the colours (Source: Melville City council website)&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
