   <groundspeak:placed_by>.tbh</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">.tbh</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Melville Places 2&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Weather Figure&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/dcccaf8c-0325-41cd-a347-209ffd5579d2"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/dcccaf8c-0325-41cd-a347-209ffd5579d2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many triangles are there?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6250aceb-d50e-41cc-94ee-6d35a8dbaea1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Weather Figure reminds us of past occupants of the area and connects us with the weather in the most basic and elemental way; through seeing and learning. The sculpture has two kinetic
components; a wind vane and a wind speed indicator.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5bae889d-e961-46d5-be77-5328134fb8ab" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Public Art can improve the connectivity of a precinct and its interrelationship with the rest of the area. Good public art can contribute to a sense of place, enhancing public spaces and celebrating cultural identity and community aspirations. (Source Melville City Council)

Like many local governments around the Perth Metropolitan area the City of Melville have brought and commissioned many pieces of art that now dot the various public parks and pathways around the local government area.  They also have constructed various viewing platforms and memorials at significant locations with the city boundaries.

Image: Coming of the colours (Source: Melville City council website)&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
