   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Melville Places 2&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Heath Ledger Memorial&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/dcccaf8c-0325-41cd-a347-209ffd5579d2"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/dcccaf8c-0325-41cd-a347-209ffd5579d2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Who is the quote on the commemorative plaque attributed to? (2 words.)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7b558d91-0732-49d1-97a3-ec3d6a7a2fd9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The monument commemorates the Australian actor Heath Andrew Ledger who died from an accidental drug overdose on January 22, 2008.

It consists of three pieces with chess boards incorporated into them, a centrepiece with a yin and yang design reflecting Heath’s spiritual beliefs, and a commemorative plaque.

Heath was born in Perth and after several small roles In Australia he went to America to further his career. After several roles in films Heath achieved success with his role in Brokeback Mountain for which he was nominated for an Oscar and a BAFTA.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5bae889d-e961-46d5-be77-5328134fb8ab" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Public Art can improve the connectivity of a precinct and its interrelationship with the rest of the area. Good public art can contribute to a sense of place, enhancing public spaces and celebrating cultural identity and community aspirations. (Source Melville City Council)

Like many local governments around the Perth Metropolitan area the City of Melville have brought and commissioned many pieces of art that now dot the various public parks and pathways around the local government area.  They also have constructed various viewing platforms and memorials at significant locations with the city boundaries.

Image: Coming of the colours (Source: Melville City council website)&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
