   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Dongara - Port Denison &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Russ Cottage&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/8694e4a2-a497-41e0-9a7a-9fd9c8338d37"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/8694e4a2-a497-41e0-9a7a-9fd9c8338d37&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;There are flood markers on the front door of the cottage. What year was the highest flood to date? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f6e558d1-49a3-4e0d-924c-8b5dd72ba335" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Titus Russ squatted and built this cottage1868-1870 on land owned by Edward Hamersley. 
He is reputed to have carried the limestone blocks in a wheelbarrow from a quarry half a kilometer away. Its estimated the quantity of stone is over 50 tonnes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0e6a9297-3ef2-4999-864c-087122dedbce" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Situated 360 kilometres north of Perth the twin towns of Dongara and Port Denison boast true coastal village charm, with the Irwin River creating a scenic landmark as it meanders between the two towns. Beautiful beaches provide ideal conditions for sailing, surfing, fishing, windsurfing, kite surfing and swimming. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
