   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Boyanup Heritage Trail #1&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Post Office + Remembering the Fallen &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b64184ab-7642-4f5b-9fc6-b0227f84ea7e"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b64184ab-7642-4f5b-9fc6-b0227f84ea7e&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Year Mr Walton began + Year War Memorial was relocated &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ea733a53-56b9-4de7-80ed-d67c568f79e6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Here you will find two (2) plaques, you will need a two (2) part answer.
The Original Post Office + Remembering the Fallen

Remember to put a + between your answers&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/55eed3e4-1613-48e8-8211-e7c2f27cd83a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Boyanup is a town on the South Western Highway in the South West agricultural region of Western Australia, 195 km south of Perth and 18 km south-east of Bunbury, The town is located on the Preston River.
The townsite was gazetted in 1894.

Boyanup is a Noongar name, said to mean "a place of quartz" as "Boya" means "rock" or "stone".

The first European in the area was Lieutenant Henry William Bunbury, who in December 1836 explored the route from Pinjarra to Busselton and thought it to be ideal for farming.

A lovely little town away from ‘the rat race’ that has your basic small town amenities.

There are a couple of locations that have more than one (1) plaque so you will require more than one answer.
Enjoy your walk around town reading the plaques to find the answers you need.

There will be Boyanup Heritage Trail #2 coming soon


&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
