 <wpt lat="-33.483267" lon="115.72795">
  <ele>40.0</ele>
  <time>2023-01-08T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBTG94-03</name>
  <desc>BoyanupHeritagr</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b64184ab-7642-4f5b-9fc6-b0227f84ea7e</url>
  <urlname>Boyanup Heritage Trail #1 : S3 Hitching’s Garage by dimor</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476910096" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Boyanup Heritage Trail #1 : S3 Hitching’s Garage</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>dimor</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">dimor</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Boyanup Heritage Trail #1&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Hitching’s Garage&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b64184ab-7642-4f5b-9fc6-b0227f84ea7e"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b64184ab-7642-4f5b-9fc6-b0227f84ea7e&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Who drove (‘piloted’) the Big Six Studebaker&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/cdc64226-2d49-45ba-8236-283a1169f3d4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Another part of Boyanup’s history that was part of this little town. Sadly no more a garage but still standing.

Arthur Hitchings peddled around to the farms with his toolbox   on his pushbike, working on early cars, trucks and tractors. Back in days gone by&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/55eed3e4-1613-48e8-8211-e7c2f27cd83a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Boyanup is a town on the South Western Highway in the South West agricultural region of Western Australia, 195 km south of Perth and 18 km south-east of Bunbury, The town is located on the Preston River.
The townsite was gazetted in 1894.

Boyanup is a Noongar name, said to mean "a place of quartz" as "Boya" means "rock" or "stone".

The first European in the area was Lieutenant Henry William Bunbury, who in December 1836 explored the route from Pinjarra to Busselton and thought it to be ideal for farming.

A lovely little town away from ‘the rat race’ that has your basic small town amenities.

There are a couple of locations that have more than one (1) plaque so you will require more than one answer.
Enjoy your walk around town reading the plaques to find the answers you need.

There will be Boyanup Heritage Trail #2 coming soon


&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
