   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Boyanup Heritage Trail #1&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The CWA Rooms&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b64184ab-7642-4f5b-9fc6-b0227f84ea7e"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b64184ab-7642-4f5b-9fc6-b0227f84ea7e&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year was a “Younger Set” formed&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/199ddce7-8808-4689-b160-907f1525df5f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;*Note: The CWA building is now a private residence

The CWA is the pillar of any regional town, they are more than cups of tea, scones, jam and cream for which they are famous for.
Though cups of tea and cake would have seen them help so many people, acting as counsellors, cooking for families in times of need, and the list goes on.
The CWA Ladies here in Boyanup fund raised to get the money to build their meeting rooms.

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/55eed3e4-1613-48e8-8211-e7c2f27cd83a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Boyanup is a town on the South Western Highway in the South West agricultural region of Western Australia, 195 km south of Perth and 18 km south-east of Bunbury, The town is located on the Preston River.
The townsite was gazetted in 1894.

Boyanup is a Noongar name, said to mean "a place of quartz" as "Boya" means "rock" or "stone".

The first European in the area was Lieutenant Henry William Bunbury, who in December 1836 explored the route from Pinjarra to Busselton and thought it to be ideal for farming.

A lovely little town away from ‘the rat race’ that has your basic small town amenities.

There are a couple of locations that have more than one (1) plaque so you will require more than one answer.
Enjoy your walk around town reading the plaques to find the answers you need.

There will be Boyanup Heritage Trail #2 coming soon


&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
