   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Thornlie Line (Transperth)&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Queens Park Station&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f1cda1c9-0338-41a6-b26a-89e488331950"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f1cda1c9-0338-41a6-b26a-89e488331950&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the stop number for platform 1? (5 numbers)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f13be4bf-afa1-46c0-ac88-bfe80b09e9ed" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Queens Park Station opened in 1899 as Woodlupine, being renamed Queens Park in 1912. It was then rebuilt in 1997 and also refurbished in 2012. To Answer this question get off at this station and walk to the huts on the platform there you will see the answer.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1090b8f2-0079-422e-a018-f7649d4ef074" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Thornlie Line is one of the many Train Lines that are in Perth. It is my favourite line and I think Trains in Perth are really interesting. There are many facts about this line so I thought it would be a good idea to showcase them to others in the form of an Adventure Lab. Hope you enjoy! (Please note that during the Whole Line shutdown that lasts from Late 2023 to 2025 this Adventure Lab will not be available)&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
