   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Thornlie Line (Transperth)&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Victoria Park Station&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f1cda1c9-0338-41a6-b26a-89e488331950"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f1cda1c9-0338-41a6-b26a-89e488331950&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;When was this Station Rebuilt?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/37844a31-8b1a-4045-8255-00345219da4f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The original Victoria Park station opened in 1898. As part of upgrades the new station opened in 2008. The station is one of the upgraded stations on the line and looks rather nice compared to the other hut stations. To answer this question make sure you read the Location description carefully!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1090b8f2-0079-422e-a018-f7649d4ef074" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Thornlie Line is one of the many Train Lines that are in Perth. It is my favourite line and I think Trains in Perth are really interesting. There are many facts about this line so I thought it would be a good idea to showcase them to others in the form of an Adventure Lab. Hope you enjoy! (Please note that during the Whole Line shutdown that lasts from Late 2023 to 2025 this Adventure Lab will not be available)&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
