 <wpt lat="-32.070733" lon="115.847717">
  <ele>30.0</ele>
  <time>2023-02-28T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBGj7b-05</name>
  <desc>FionaStanleyS5M</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a381a328-bdf6-4fa3-b440-2f958e9bb713</url>
  <urlname>Fiona Stanley : S5 Metal flowers by .K.B.</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-646" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Fiona Stanley : S5 Metal flowers</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>.K.B.</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">.K.B.</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Fiona Stanley&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Metal flowers&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a381a328-bdf6-4fa3-b440-2f958e9bb713"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a381a328-bdf6-4fa3-b440-2f958e9bb713&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many metal flowers? Do not include the bench.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7d53fc29-3a60-4c09-930c-2d3febe97686" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A little detour to enjoy another artwork.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b5d21867-435f-48b4-a5f7-32f1f647fb40" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;If I lived a hundred years, I could identify the Fiona Stanley room call bell from a million different sounds. I’ve heard it ring continuously for over 600 cumulative hours so far in my life. I hear it for hours after I leave. It’s a futile call system since the central bell system is supposed to alert staff to a patient wanting assistance. But it never ever stops on my current ward, 6C. Poor staff literally never clear all calls simultaneously, even through the night, it rings constantly. It’s something to put on the feedback form.

From Wikipedia, Fiona Stanley Hospital (FSH) is a state government hospital and teaching facility in Murdoch, Western Australia. Completed in December 2013,[2] the hospital is the largest building project ever undertaken for the Government of Western Australia. It is immediately adjacent to the private non-profit St John of God Murdoch Hospital, with the distance between the entrances to the emergency departments of these two hospitals being approximately 390 metres (430 yd).
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
