   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Fiona Stanley&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Welcome to the park&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a381a328-bdf6-4fa3-b440-2f958e9bb713"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a381a328-bdf6-4fa3-b440-2f958e9bb713&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Name the park as shown on the sign on the fence. One word only.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ef1ab377-56f2-4609-b519-24ba7579c159" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;I hope you enjoyed the walk lakeside. This is my current view. I prefer the rooms on the other side since you see sunset.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b5d21867-435f-48b4-a5f7-32f1f647fb40" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;If I lived a hundred years, I could identify the Fiona Stanley room call bell from a million different sounds. I’ve heard it ring continuously for over 600 cumulative hours so far in my life. I hear it for hours after I leave. It’s a futile call system since the central bell system is supposed to alert staff to a patient wanting assistance. But it never ever stops on my current ward, 6C. Poor staff literally never clear all calls simultaneously, even through the night, it rings constantly. It’s something to put on the feedback form.

From Wikipedia, Fiona Stanley Hospital (FSH) is a state government hospital and teaching facility in Murdoch, Western Australia. Completed in December 2013,[2] the hospital is the largest building project ever undertaken for the Government of Western Australia. It is immediately adjacent to the private non-profit St John of God Murdoch Hospital, with the distance between the entrances to the emergency departments of these two hospitals being approximately 390 metres (430 yd).
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
