   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Fiona Stanley&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Over the road to enjoy the lake&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a381a328-bdf6-4fa3-b440-2f958e9bb713"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a381a328-bdf6-4fa3-b440-2f958e9bb713&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What colour is the zig zag sculpture?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e2a2622d-feb0-44d8-accc-983eecf39a40" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Cross carefully and enjoy the ambience. Imagine ringing bells for 600 hours if you will.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b5d21867-435f-48b4-a5f7-32f1f647fb40" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;If I lived a hundred years, I could identify the Fiona Stanley room call bell from a million different sounds. I’ve heard it ring continuously for over 600 cumulative hours so far in my life. I hear it for hours after I leave. It’s a futile call system since the central bell system is supposed to alert staff to a patient wanting assistance. But it never ever stops on my current ward, 6C. Poor staff literally never clear all calls simultaneously, even through the night, it rings constantly. It’s something to put on the feedback form.

