   <groundspeak:placed_by>.K.B.</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">.K.B.</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Fiona Stanley 2&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The boat garden&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9a6fc962-495b-4d16-9ec8-3642121f9a11"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9a6fc962-495b-4d16-9ec8-3642121f9a11&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;In the ground around the rusty coloured bow section of the “boat” are lights. How many lights as a number?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1816616a-6766-45fa-92a1-e2dc68051beb" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;There are many sunken garden areas both in and around the hospital. This one at the entrance looks like a boat to me. The bow is formed by rust coloured panels. The hand rail of the glass section illuminates at night.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c55cbd18-ac91-409a-a63c-82303d4f90fc" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Take a stroll around part of the grounds of Fiona Stanley hospital.

Fiona is a remarkable woman who contributed immensely to the medical field.

On the ground floor of the hospital is a stunning portrait of Professor Stanley. 70 small canvases depicting some of her life surround the portrait. 

Wikipedia:
Fiona Juliet Stanley AC FAA FASSA (born 1 August 1946) is an Australian epidemiologist noted for her public health work, her research into child and maternal health as well as birth disorders such as cerebral palsy. Stanley is the patron of the Telethon Kids Institute and a distinguished professorial fellow in the School of Paediatrics and Child Health at the University of Western Australia. From 1990 to December 2011 she was the founding director of Telethon Kids.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
