   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Foxes Lair Narrogin&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Railway Dam Picnic Area&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/406d90b7-7686-42c8-b23a-88f92fe26270"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/406d90b7-7686-42c8-b23a-88f92fe26270&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the number painted on the railway wheels - nnnn&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ea1ff189-d610-42c2-b0f3-1cd7a6348ca7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Railway Dam by 1910 with its two tanks and connecting overflow area was supplying water to an increasing number of steam locomotives on the wheatbelts Great Southern Railway Line.
This is a Recreation Vehicle Free Stay Area in Narrogin.
Also you will find The Commonage Parklands mountain bike trails - information boards give locations and degree of difficulty.
Information boards and QR Codes give you valuable information about Foxes Lair and its attractions.
Visit Doug Sawkins website https://www.foxeslair.org/ for more 
