   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Fremantle Hospital Surrounds&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Dos and don’ts&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f4464cd6-a45e-4e30-9cdc-91c39978f83d"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f4464cd6-a45e-4e30-9cdc-91c39978f83d&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What bird appears on the welcome sign?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ae4bca39-2ac5-48d3-bb92-21de1f503933" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A basic welcome sign to the Fremantle hospital appears in various forms and locations. It includes a sage reminder to not smoke. The sign depicts some well known things. One is a lighthouse.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/53f42483-7bb6-416f-bc28-d94b3afe9c7d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;An old but functional concrete jungle amongst typical bustling Freo street life. Sweeping views across the harbour are available from many rooms.

Fremantle Hospital is an Australian public hospital situated on South Terrace in central Fremantle, southwest of Perth, Western Australia.
It was formerly the major hospital in its region; however, with the opening of Fiona Stanley Hospital in Murdoch on 3 February 2015, it was substantially downsized, with the closure of its emergency department and a range of other services being relocated to the new hospital.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
