 <wpt lat="-32.347483" lon="115.796867">
  <ele>10.0</ele>
  <time>2023-03-19T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBuKVh-01</name>
  <desc>KayaWandjooBal1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7fd44f71-ab8d-4a31-829a-e04367f9f18c</url>
  <urlname>Kaya Wandjoo Baldivis : S1 Birak by Kyzabra</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-916" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Kaya Wandjoo Baldivis : S1 Birak</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Kyzabra</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Kyzabra</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Kaya Wandjoo Baldivis&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Birak&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7fd44f71-ab8d-4a31-829a-e04367f9f18c"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7fd44f71-ab8d-4a31-829a-e04367f9f18c&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What Animal is drawn on the Birak side ?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3520863d-c85e-4391-a1d5-fbd9062e24b1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;BIRAK DECEMBER — JANUARY
Season of the Young
Birak marks the hot and dry season, when the warm days are cooled by the afternoon sea breezes. An abundance of food sources still remain including mammals, birds, reptiles, and yonga. The start of the season sees the vibrant flowering of Nuytsia Floribunda, also known as the Western Australian Christmas Tree.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/61181880-0c83-449e-9572-495e418d435e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the new Baldivis Sporting complex
The new home for the Baldivis Brumbies and White Knights.
This lab centres around the artwork here.
Titled “Karrikins Dirdong” the distinctive sculpture by artists Jason Hirst and Peter Farmer is both aesthetically pleasing and educational, depicting the six Nyoongar seasons within the design.

There a five stages, all at the same location so not much walking needed.

At the three stages Birak, Boonaroo and Kambarang you will need to keep the answers to find the bonus cache 
https://coord.info/GCA64DN&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.347483" lon="115.796867">
  <ele>10.0</ele>
  <time>2023-03-19T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBuKVh-02</name>
  <desc>KayaWandjooBal2</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7fd44f71-ab8d-4a31-829a-e04367f9f18c</url>
  <urlname>Kaya Wandjoo Baldivis : S2 Boonaroo by Kyzabra</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-917" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Kaya Wandjoo Baldivis : S2 Boonaroo</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Kyzabra</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Kyzabra</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Kaya Wandjoo Baldivis&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Boonaroo&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7fd44f71-ab8d-4a31-829a-e04367f9f18c"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7fd44f71-ab8d-4a31-829a-e04367f9f18c&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What Animal is shown below the word ?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/464369ea-2b51-4fb3-840b-e4b25b7a1352" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;BOONAROO FEBRUARY — MARCH
Season of the Adolescence
Boonaroo marks the hottest part of the year, when there is little to no rain. Jarrah and Marri trees are in full bloom, along with Zamia pods. Fish, crab and mussels are the main portion of the diet in this season, with tailer and mullet trapped in the shallow waters and easily caught, as well as marron and gilgies collected from the wetlands. Wattle, banksia blossom and various roots are popular food sources at this time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/61181880-0c83-449e-9572-495e418d435e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the new Baldivis Sporting complex
The new home for the Baldivis Brumbies and White Knights.
This lab centres around the artwork here.
Titled “Karrikins Dirdong” the distinctive sculpture by artists Jason Hirst and Peter Farmer is both aesthetically pleasing and educational, depicting the six Nyoongar seasons within the design.

There a five stages, all at the same location so not much walking needed.

At the three stages Birak, Boonaroo and Kambarang you will need to keep the answers to find the bonus cache 
https://coord.info/GCA64DN&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
