Answer the question by reading the plaque and obtaining the relevant information.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/50c4be9c-dfcd-4b2c-890e-b43341fe1080" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Narrogin's Heritage Walk Trail is a fascinating and pleasant 1,250 metre circuit which includes many of the town's historic buildings. It offers a wealth of knowledge about the early settlers and events in the development of the town.

The trail route is designed in a clockwise direction and marked with black-on-silver triangles affixed to the footpath at regular intervals.

There are twenty-five silver information signs along the trail, which detail stories and history of the town.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
