   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Narrogin Heritage Walk Trail (Part 1)&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Stop 5: Party On&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b72a7e6c-c960-4e7d-b0d3-900b8698f1d3"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b72a7e6c-c960-4e7d-b0d3-900b8698f1d3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;In 1910, the Council held a special meeting to permit what activity at the Hall?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/99ece63b-5c79-499e-8f45-934d64fa95dc" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The sign for this stage is located on the footpath near to the pedestrian crossing.

You will need to be within 20 metres of the location to unlock the geofence.

Answer the question by reading the plaque and obtaining the relevant information.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/91805d80-1cec-450a-887c-5348b90e12d5" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Narrogin's Heritage Walk Trail is a fascinating and pleasant 1,250 metre circuit which includes many of the town's historic buildings. It offers a wealth of knowledge about the early settlers and events in the development of the town.

The trail route is designed in a clockwise direction and marked with black-on-silver triangles affixed to the footpath at regular intervals.

There are twenty-five silver information signs along the trail, which detail stories and history of the town.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
