 <wpt lat="-31.9297" lon="115.80435">
  <ele>11.0</ele>
  <time>2022-12-05T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBawbC-03</name>
  <desc>LRunningAround3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e445ea2f-aeb7-4eaf-a842-cf298c32c969</url>
  <urlname>[L] Running Around Herdies : S3 Halfway by ChrisRG</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-679" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] Running Around Herdies : S3 Halfway</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>ChrisRG</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">ChrisRG</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Running Around Herdies&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Halfway&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e445ea2f-aeb7-4eaf-a842-cf298c32c969"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e445ea2f-aeb7-4eaf-a842-cf298c32c969&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the title of the information plaque?  _ _ _ _ _    _ _ _    _ _ _ _&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3d85182e-0c20-4481-a022-7735c74272f6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The participants are now about halfway around the course and can decide if they are able to take it easy on the second half or if they need to go a bit faster to make it back before the cut-off.


&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2b7c2ed5-2006-40d2-932b-5c8bf3f02a94" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Every year an ultra-marathon takes place around Herdsmans Lake but it is an ultra marathon with a difference. There is no finish line, no required distance to run and all except 1 runner will fail to finish the event.
The run is a backyard ultra where the runners are required to run a 6.71km lap (referred to as a yard) every hour on the hour and they keep going until there is only 1 person left and that person can only run 1 more lap that the second last person. 
On the 21st June 2023 Philip Gore set a new world record in Queensland of 102 laps, that's running 6.71km every hour on the hour for 102 hours. The total distance covered in that time is 684km.

Collect the info for the bonus cache GCAA8W0&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.91485" lon="115.811833">
  <ele>17.0</ele>
  <time>2022-12-05T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBawbC-04</name>
  <desc>LRunningAround4</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e445ea2f-aeb7-4eaf-a842-cf298c32c969</url>
  <urlname>[L] Running Around Herdies : S4 The Bridge by ChrisRG</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-680" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] Running Around Herdies : S4 The Bridge</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>ChrisRG</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">ChrisRG</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Running Around Herdies&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Bridge&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e445ea2f-aeb7-4eaf-a842-cf298c32c969"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e445ea2f-aeb7-4eaf-a842-cf298c32c969&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many bridges do the participants cross in one lap?  _   Hint (Gur nafjre vf va bar bs gur qrfpevcgvbaf)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f163a699-766d-48e0-b927-9ddaa51ee1f0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;They have just crossed the last bridge and have just over 1km to go. This is one of the more scenic sections of the course but by the second day not too many can appreciate it. The occasional tiger snake can sometimes be spotted around here but they have never been seen during the event.
How many bridges do the participants cross in one lap?
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2b7c2ed5-2006-40d2-932b-5c8bf3f02a94" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Every year an ultra-marathon takes place around Herdsmans Lake but it is an ultra marathon with a difference. There is no finish line, no required distance to run and all except 1 runner will fail to finish the event.
The run is a backyard ultra where the runners are required to run a 6.71km lap (referred to as a yard) every hour on the hour and they keep going until there is only 1 person left and that person can only run 1 more lap that the second last person. 
On the 21st June 2023 Philip Gore set a new world record in Queensland of 102 laps, that's running 6.71km every hour on the hour for 102 hours. The total distance covered in that time is 684km.

Collect the info for the bonus cache GCAA8W0&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.919167" lon="115.796183">
  <ele>11.0</ele>
