   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Running Around Herdies&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The West Side&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e445ea2f-aeb7-4eaf-a842-cf298c32c969"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e445ea2f-aeb7-4eaf-a842-cf298c32c969&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How far in Kilometres is it to Popeys Lake Park?    #.#&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/62ae0f3c-f363-4321-9e14-afbf68a7a021" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is where the runners cross the second of five bridges and are about to enter the dreaded limestone section where during the daytime temperatures can reach up to 30° and the sunlight is reflected off the white surface. The dust stirred up when there is a large number together also finds it’s way into shoes and this can rub and cause blisters. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2b7c2ed5-2006-40d2-932b-5c8bf3f02a94" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Every year an ultra-marathon takes place around Herdsmans Lake but it is an ultra marathon with a difference. There is no finish line, no required distance to run and all except 1 runner will fail to finish the event.
The run is a backyard ultra where the runners are required to run a 6.71km lap (referred to as a yard) every hour on the hour and they keep going until there is only 1 person left and that person can only run 1 more lap that the second last person. 
On the 21st June 2023 Philip Gore set a new world record in Queensland of 102 laps, that's running 6.71km every hour on the hour for 102 hours. The total distance covered in that time is 684km.

Collect the info for the bonus cache GCAA8W0&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.910367" lon="115.806017">
  <ele>16.0</ele>
  <time>2022-12-05T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBawbC-05</name>
  <desc>LRunningAround5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e445ea2f-aeb7-4eaf-a842-cf298c32c969</url>
  <urlname>[L] Running Around Herdies : S5 The End by ChrisRG</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-681" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] Running Around Herdies : S5 The End</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>ChrisRG</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">ChrisRG</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Running Around Herdies&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The End&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e445ea2f-aeb7-4eaf-a842-cf298c32c969"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e445ea2f-aeb7-4eaf-a842-cf298c32c969&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Including the corner post and the gate post, how many posts are between the corner and the gate?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b3cd0cf7-6a4e-4289-8d65-7c5e74c81ed6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is where the finish line is. When the participants reach here they then make their way to their base to get some fluids, food and rest before heading out and doing it all again. The faster they can complete the 6.71km lap the more time they have to rest.
This is also where the celebrations begin when the winner finally crosses the line after running for a couple of days.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2b7c2ed5-2006-40d2-932b-5c8bf3f02a94" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Every year an ultra-marathon takes place around Herdsmans Lake but it is an ultra marathon with a difference. There is no finish line, no required distance to run and all except 1 runner will fail to finish the event.
The run is a backyard ultra where the runners are required to run a 6.71km lap (referred to as a yard) every hour on the hour and they keep going until there is only 1 person left and that person can only run 1 more lap that the second last person. 
On the 21st June 2023 Philip Gore set a new world record in Queensland of 102 laps, that's running 6.71km every hour on the hour for 102 hours. The total distance covered in that time is 684km.

Collect the info for the bonus cache GCAA8W0&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.909633" lon="115.804233">
