   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Who Are The People In Your Neighborhood?&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Smoko&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/6dce6964-de36-492d-9cd1-8c6628373796"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/6dce6964-de36-492d-9cd1-8c6628373796&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the artist?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/56275490-7874-4f95-b510-f13c00ccadce" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;What is smoko? Macquarie Dictionary defines smoko as (1) a break in the work of the morning or of the afternoon, originally to allow time for workers to smoke tobacco; (2) food or drink consumed at that time&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a037284e-4393-41c6-8d6b-aee787df3fa1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;On this adventure we will meet some interesting characters scattered around Midland.  The Midland Railway Workshops Sculptures commemorates those who have a connection with the Midland Railway Workshops.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.4914" lon="118.242">
  <ele>306.0</ele>
  <time>2023-07-18T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBv7g8-01</name>
  <desc>GoldenIeline902</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/251ea690-3bc7-4c84-a8f2-33887f1a50d3</url>
  <urlname>Golden Pipeline Trail: No. 4 Pump Station : S1 No. 4 Pump Station - 1902 by Boyzrule5</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476910134" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Golden Pipeline Trail: No. 4 Pump Station : S1 No. 4 Pump Station - 1902</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Boyzrule5</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Boyzrule5</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Golden Pipeline Trail: No. 4 Pump Station&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;No. 4 Pump Station - 1902&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/251ea690-3bc7-4c84-a8f2-33887f1a50d3"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/251ea690-3bc7-4c84-a8f2-33887f1a50d3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Looking just under the roofline, there are decorative ends to the rafters; how many rafters support the roof? (Numeric)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a15ac058-b0ea-4c0c-aa9f-81b10502ff14" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The 1st of the Merredin pump stations was completed in April 1902 and was the last in line of the larger pump stations housing three pumps and boilers. Standardisation was a guiding principle in designing the machinery for the pump stations so that parts could be interchangeable, the same cannot be said for the pump stations themselves. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7e5e4354-7e40-4ca2-8eae-71ddffaeea79" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Although fenced off due to asbestos issues, three generations of pump stations can be seen at this location. The original steam pump station, constructed at the turn of the century, is still an imposing landmark although it has not been used for more than 50 years. 
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.4924" lon="118.242383">
  <ele>306.0</ele>
  <time>2023-07-18T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBv7g8-03</name>
  <desc>GoldenIeline950</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/251ea690-3bc7-4c84-a8f2-33887f1a50d3</url>
  <urlname>Golden Pipeline Trail: No. 4 Pump Station : S3 No 4. Pump Station - 1950’s by Boyzrule5</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476910138" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Golden Pipeline Trail: No. 4 Pump Station : S3 No 4. Pump Station - 1950’s</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Boyzrule5</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Boyzrule5</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Golden Pipeline Trail: No. 4 Pump Station&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;No 4. Pump Station - 1950’s&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/251ea690-3bc7-4c84-a8f2-33887f1a50d3"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/251ea690-3bc7-4c84-a8f2-33887f1a50d3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many sets of 3 windows are there down the side of the building?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9ae6aaa0-740a-4ee1-9f11-5d6a8c7861e7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In the 1950’s the larger “three pump” stations, including No. 4, were replaced by electric pump stations. The original pump station building was given to the local council who sold the contents for scrap. The steel chimney was removed in 1964.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7e5e4354-7e40-4ca2-8eae-71ddffaeea79" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Although fenced off due to asbestos issues, three generations of pump stations can be seen at this location. The original steam pump station, constructed at the turn of the century, is still an imposing landmark although it has not been used for more than 50 years. 
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.491917" lon="118.242333">
  <ele>306.0</ele>
  <time>2023-07-18T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBv7g8-02</name>
  <desc>GoldenIeline424</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/251ea690-3bc7-4c84-a8f2-33887f1a50d3</url>
  <urlname>Golden Pipeline Trail: No. 4 Pump Station : S2 No 4. Pump Station - Receiving Tank by Boyzrule5</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476910136" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Golden Pipeline Trail: No. 4 Pump Station : S2 No 4. Pump Station - Receiving Tank</groundspeak:name>
