 <wpt lat="-28.042533" lon="114.67375">
  <ele>261.0</ele>
  <time>2023-08-08T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LB7k7G-01</name>
  <desc>ABTAjanaBinnuT1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/76a12e9f-9aa4-4561-96cc-4c3028b91d05</url>
  <urlname>(ABT) Ajana Binnu Trail : S1 Binnu by Team-Ruphace</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1262" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>(ABT) Ajana Binnu Trail : S1 Binnu</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Team-Ruphace</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Team-Ruphace</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;(ABT) Ajana Binnu Trail&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Binnu&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/76a12e9f-9aa4-4561-96cc-4c3028b91d05"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/76a12e9f-9aa4-4561-96cc-4c3028b91d05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;According to the plaque when did the Shelter shed and out of shed burn down &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0d56c8b2-7516-414f-9b10-44c630e8b7b3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to Binnu

Established around Early 1914 and originally named No4 Siding later changed to "Binnu" mid 1914.

Binnu consisted of a Main and Loop line, with stock yards, wheat bins and a 100ft platform.

General freight, grain wool, mail, machinery parts  and passengers were dispatched and received from the Siding.

The rail line was later closed in 1957.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/db46a561-313b-4307-bdb4-591ef4daa02e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the historical Rail towns of Ajana and Binnu

The towns of Ajana and Binnu were originally a rail Sidings used to get materials, equipment, people, and other resources to and from the nearby Lead Mines, with the main rail track going from Northampton to Geraldton then later being extended to Ajana 1913/14

Most of Ajana was abandoned and left for ruin after the rail system was closed in 1957 and unfortunately the rest was destroyed by Cyclone Seroja however a few reminants still remain.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
