   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;(ABT) Ajana Binnu Trail&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Water Tank&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/76a12e9f-9aa4-4561-96cc-4c3028b91d05"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/76a12e9f-9aa4-4561-96cc-4c3028b91d05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;According to the plaque what kind of steam engine was used to drive water to the tank&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/19316bcc-ee43-4604-b97a-b31f92d8ecb7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Ajana Water Tank

Established late 1913

The Ajana Tank is a 10,000 gallon round tank on a 30ft wooden stand built with a pump house near the dam where water was sourced.

The rail line was closed in 1957

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/db46a561-313b-4307-bdb4-591ef4daa02e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the historical Rail towns of Ajana and Binnu

The towns of Ajana and Binnu were originally a rail Sidings used to get materials, equipment, people, and other resources to and from the nearby Lead Mines, with the main rail track going from Northampton to Geraldton then later being extended to Ajana 1913/14

Most of Ajana was abandoned and left for ruin after the rail system was closed in 1957 and unfortunately the rest was destroyed by Cyclone Seroja however a few reminants still remain.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-27.991783" lon="114.624417">
  <ele>221.0</ele>
  <time>2023-08-08T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LB7k7G-03</name>
  <desc>ABTAjanaBinnuT3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/76a12e9f-9aa4-4561-96cc-4c3028b91d05</url>
  <urlname>(ABT) Ajana Binnu Trail : S3 Ajana Dam &amp; Catchment system by Team-Ruphace</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1264" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>(ABT) Ajana Binnu Trail : S3 Ajana Dam &amp; Catchment system</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Team-Ruphace</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Team-Ruphace</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;(ABT) Ajana Binnu Trail&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Ajana Dam &amp; Catchment system&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/76a12e9f-9aa4-4561-96cc-4c3028b91d05"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/76a12e9f-9aa4-4561-96cc-4c3028b91d05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The nearby concrete drainage system was constructed with what join&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7f194f04-9530-41b0-a5ea-644b4428241a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Ajana Dam was established around 1913 with the purpose of servicing the steam trains via the nearby water tank.

The dam is 150ft long by 100ft wide with a measured depth of 14ft when full.

The nearby drain / catchment system constructed on the west side of the dam were used to funnel water to the dam.

The rail system was closed in 1957&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/db46a561-313b-4307-bdb4-591ef4daa02e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the historical Rail towns of Ajana and Binnu

The towns of Ajana and Binnu were originally a rail Sidings used to get materials, equipment, people, and other resources to and from the nearby Lead Mines, with the main rail track going from Northampton to Geraldton then later being extended to Ajana 1913/14

Most of Ajana was abandoned and left for ruin after the rail system was closed in 1957 and unfortunately the rest was destroyed by Cyclone Seroja however a few reminants still remain.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-27.952617" lon="114.6421">
  <ele>207.0</ele>
  <time>2023-08-08T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LB7k7G-05</name>
  <desc>ABTAjanaBinnuT5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/76a12e9f-9aa4-4561-96cc-4c3028b91d05</url>
  <urlname>(ABT) Ajana Binnu Trail : S5 Ajana by Team-Ruphace</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1266" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>(ABT) Ajana Binnu Trail : S5 Ajana</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Team-Ruphace</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Team-Ruphace</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;(ABT) Ajana Binnu Trail&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Ajana&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/76a12e9f-9aa4-4561-96cc-4c3028b91d05"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/76a12e9f-9aa4-4561-96cc-4c3028b91d05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the town was probably derived from ?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b938723a-82dc-4179-a6aa-7cdb67cdc5f3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to Ajana

The work on the Ajana extension of the Northampton - Geraldton railway line began in 1911, it was approximately 33 miles long and was opened to rail traffic in 1913.

The railway line was primarily used to transport Lead to the port of Geraldton, however it was responsible for successfully opening up land to the North-East of Northampton.

A small town site called Ajana emerged at the head of the rail line and included a school, town hall, tennis courts, several residences, CGI sheds.

The name of Ajana is probably derived from 'Ajano' the Aboriginal name for Barrel Well and the nearby Aboriginal community.

With the closure of the railway in 1957 came the steady decline in Ajana's population, and with cyclone Seroja most of the buildings and infrastructure have all but been demolished.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/db46a561-313b-4307-bdb4-591ef4daa02e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the historical Rail towns of Ajana and Binnu

The towns of Ajana and Binnu were originally a rail Sidings used to get materials, equipment, people, and other resources to and from the nearby Lead Mines, with the main rail track going from Northampton to Geraldton then later being extended to Ajana 1913/14

Most of Ajana was abandoned and left for ruin after the rail system was closed in 1957 and unfortunately the rest was destroyed by Cyclone Seroja however a few reminants still remain.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-27.952283" lon="114.637717">
  <ele>209.0</ele>
  <time>2023-08-08T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LB7k7G-04</name>
  <desc>ABTAjanaBinnuT4</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/76a12e9f-9aa4-4561-96cc-4c3028b91d05</url>
  <urlname>(ABT) Ajana Binnu Trail : S4 Ajana Railhead by Team-Ruphace</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1265" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>(ABT) Ajana Binnu Trail : S4 Ajana Railhead</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Team-Ruphace</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Team-Ruphace</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;(ABT) Ajana Binnu Trail&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Ajana Railhead&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/76a12e9f-9aa4-4561-96cc-4c3028b91d05"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/76a12e9f-9aa4-4561-96cc-4c3028b91d05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;According to the plaque how far is it in miles to Geraldton&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0c7746c9-da95-4598-bf4f-adb0aaaccfd1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Ajana Railhead was established in 1913/14 with 3 rail lines, 1 main line and 2 loop lines.

Passengers, produce, general freight, machinery parts, stock were dispatched and recieved from the station.

There was a loading ramp, stock loading ramp and stockyards removed and re-erected from Northampton, 51ft turntable removed in1957, and a 2ft gauge tramway to Surprise Lead Mine completed in 1920 and removed in 1944.

The rail system was closed in 1957&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/db46a561-313b-4307-bdb4-591ef4daa02e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the historical Rail towns of Ajana and Binnu

The towns of Ajana and Binnu were originally a rail Sidings used to get materials, equipment, people, and other resources to and from the nearby Lead Mines, with the main rail track going from Northampton to Geraldton then later being extended to Ajana 1913/14

Most of Ajana was abandoned and left for ruin after the rail system was closed in 1957 and unfortunately the rest was destroyed by Cyclone Seroja however a few reminants still remain.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-34.2382" lon="116.1448">
