 <wpt lat="-32.000383" lon="115.958767">
  <ele>11.0</ele>
  <time>2023-09-23T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBeJG1-05</name>
  <desc>LFootballsNewH5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c0d5964b-75d1-4e91-bba0-03cfe08ab58b</url>
  <urlname>[L] Football's New Home  : S5 The Start of Football (Red/Orange) by LAXA</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476910150" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] Football's New Home  : S5 The Start of Football (Red/Orange)</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>LAXA</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">LAXA</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Football's New Home &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Start of Football (Red/Orange) &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c0d5964b-75d1-4e91-bba0-03cfe08ab58b"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c0d5964b-75d1-4e91-bba0-03cfe08ab58b&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;"Just not Cricket". What was the score of the first game (as written)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/47adb047-e814-4deb-aace-393f849b3380" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;the red/orange Artwork

Just not Cricket
 
The first game played by a Western Australian State representative side was at Fremantle oval on 24 March 1902, against a Maclaren English Test Cricket XL. In front of a crowd of 5000the visitors won ...
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/778cb6fc-5beb-4b81-b991-8af1839ac881" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is a quick 5 stage adventure lab cache at the newly build State Football Centre in Queens Park.

The artwork at the centre by Peter Farmer and Jason Hirst is called Koodjal Koodjal Four/4.

Joy, a sense of playfulness and the value of communities coming together are what artists Peter Farmer and Jason Hirst hope to convey with their series of four artworks for the State Football Centre. 

Although seemingly simple in form, the artworks are layered with meaning. As a Noongar artist, it was essential for Peter that he embed the sculptures with cultural symbols. Signifying the equality of women and men in the sport, the elongated and slightly squared oval shape of each work is composed from the symbols of a man and a woman sitting now fused together as one. The bright, happy colours were selected from Western Australian wildflowers.


After completing the last stage, you'll receive a codeword you may want to use to find:

https://coord.info/GCAEFCB
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
