Joy, a sense of playfulness and the value of communities coming together are what artists Peter Farmer and Jason Hirst hope to convey with their series of four artworks for the State Football Centre. 

Although seemingly simple in form, the artworks are layered with meaning. As a Noongar artist, it was essential for Peter that he embed the sculptures with cultural symbols. Signifying the equality of women and men in the sport, the elongated and slightly squared oval shape of each work is composed from the symbols of a man and a woman sitting now fused together as one. The bright, happy colours were selected from Western Australian wildflowers.


