   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Nickel in the heart of Kambalda&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Rail Bogger&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/004b018b-48f0-457f-802d-165f4d9952ce"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/004b018b-48f0-457f-802d-165f4d9952ce&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;On side of the bogger is a white button. What are the two words above this button?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5d616a40-eef4-4034-959c-eafaa3488c0c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This rail bogger would’ve had a hard life underground. Now, bloggers have rubber tyres and very mobile. Walk down the fence line and spot the white button. There are two words (painted over) that you need to answer the question. Check the photo for more help.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/526ba332-58f6-474a-ad46-88b1cf3c1708" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Originally a small artisanal gold mining camp in the 1900’s, is wasn’t until January 1966 that Western Mining Corporation struck massive nickel ore in their first drill hole KD1 that transformed the region. Within 18 months, a town sprung up and nickel was being mined. This Adventure Lab will take you to a few spots which looks at the history of Kambalda.

There is a bonus cache on Red Hill, so keep a lookout for the coordinates.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
