   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Nickel in the heart of Kambalda&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Land Sailing &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/004b018b-48f0-457f-802d-165f4d9952ce"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/004b018b-48f0-457f-802d-165f4d9952ce&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many land yachts are located here (digit)?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b690b859-03bc-47c0-b07a-99b688159c25" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Land sailing was a very popular past time on Lake Lefroy. With the discovery of significant gold mines under the lake, the club had to be moved to the western edge of the lake. Can you imagine ripping around on one of these?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/526ba332-58f6-474a-ad46-88b1cf3c1708" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Originally a small artisanal gold mining camp in the 1900’s, is wasn’t until January 1966 that Western Mining Corporation struck massive nickel ore in their first drill hole KD1 that transformed the region. Within 18 months, a town sprung up and nickel was being mined. This Adventure Lab will take you to a few spots which looks at the history of Kambalda.

There is a bonus cache on Red Hill, so keep a lookout for the coordinates.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.210383" lon="121.67295">
  <ele>388.0</ele>
  <time>2023-09-27T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBuWKt-02</name>
  <desc>NickelInTheHea2</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/004b018b-48f0-457f-802d-165f4d9952ce</url>
  <urlname>Nickel in the heart of Kambalda : S2 Red Hill Lookout by Morgo the geo</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-17" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Nickel in the heart of Kambalda : S2 Red Hill Lookout</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Morgo the geo</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Morgo the geo</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Nickel in the heart of Kambalda&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Red Hill Lookout&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/004b018b-48f0-457f-802d-165f4d9952ce"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/004b018b-48f0-457f-802d-165f4d9952ce&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many platforms are on the tower looking down the path to the lake?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c3a90b37-087e-4f56-8150-9a8d2cf4a0bc" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The best place to watch sunrise, sunset or a passing storm. This hill is formed by the oldest rocks in Kambalda. The second tower was used to drill a hole, one mile deep to see what was under the old rock. They found the same rock!!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/526ba332-58f6-474a-ad46-88b1cf3c1708" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Originally a small artisanal gold mining camp in the 1900’s, is wasn’t until January 1966 that Western Mining Corporation struck massive nickel ore in their first drill hole KD1 that transformed the region. Within 18 months, a town sprung up and nickel was being mined. This Adventure Lab will take you to a few spots which looks at the history of Kambalda.

There is a bonus cache on Red Hill, so keep a lookout for the coordinates.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.3922" lon="115.763083">
