   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Historical Buildings of York&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Imperial Homestead Hotel&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/210b90f7-9f08-4918-bace-bbcd0fe8fbcb"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/210b90f7-9f08-4918-bace-bbcd0fe8fbcb&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The verandah was restored after the Meckering earthquake -it was officially reopened by Hon  - first and last name needed&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3f5bbb9b-1d82-4bd8-a6ea-be2a0f49433e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;York is the oldest inland town in Western Australia, situated on the Avon River, 97 kilometres east of Perth in the Wheatbelt, on Ballardong Nyoongar land, and is the seat of the Shire of York. 

Avon Terrace it is the main street of the town of York, Western Australia, and is lined with heritage buildings.

The Imperial Homestead Hotel was built in 1886 to service travelers on the newly extended railway, the Imperial Homestead is living its best life after a full restoration.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/94280119-1063-4deb-b9db-c357eafa6346" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;York is the oldest inland town in Western Australia, situated on the Avon River, 97 kilometres east of Perth in the Wheatbelt, on Ballardong Nyoongar land, and is the seat of the Shire of York.  

Avon Terrace it is the main street of the town of York, Western Australia, and is lined with heritage buildings.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
