   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Historical Buildings of York&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Central Buildings&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/210b90f7-9f08-4918-bace-bbcd0fe8fbcb"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/210b90f7-9f08-4918-bace-bbcd0fe8fbcb&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the lane down the left hand side of the central Buildings&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6e3c0406-6a3d-4b70-a7e2-ada5c0e74cc5" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;York is the oldest inland town in Western Australia, situated on the Avon River, 97 kilometres east of Perth in the Wheatbelt, on Ballardong Nyoongar land, and is the seat of the Shire of York.

Avon Terrace it is the main street of the town of York, Western Australia, and is lined with heritage buildings.

Central Buildings comprise a range of single storey shops built up to the pavement over the period 1892 to 1907.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/94280119-1063-4deb-b9db-c357eafa6346" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;York is the oldest inland town in Western Australia, situated on the Avon River, 97 kilometres east of Perth in the Wheatbelt, on Ballardong Nyoongar land, and is the seat of the Shire of York.  

Avon Terrace it is the main street of the town of York, Western Australia, and is lined with heritage buildings.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
