  <name>LBeEBU-04</name>
  <desc>IndianPacificS4</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/17454ed2-3cc1-443e-ac4b-ca55aae81add</url>
  <urlname>Indian-Pacific  : S4 Perth by sandyofthesea</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476911143" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Indian-Pacific  : S4 Perth</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>sandyofthesea</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">sandyofthesea</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Indian-Pacific &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Perth&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/17454ed2-3cc1-443e-ac4b-ca55aae81add"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/17454ed2-3cc1-443e-ac4b-ca55aae81add&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of this train?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/728f655d-c8aa-4fd0-963c-c7a17c9ab71e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Australia’s only Western capital city is far different from its eastern counterparts. Boasting a laid-back culture with almost constant blue skies, Perth is a youthful city filled with natural wonders, a thriving art scene, exceptional food and wine, stimulating entertainment and fascinating local history. Each day brings you the opportunity to try a new trendy café, Perth, Western Australia discover the secrets of generations past, soak in the sun at a picturesque beach, stroll through lush gardens, and dine with a view before enjoying the evening’s entertainment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2e2bdae4-01e6-42ac-abcb-4e1abdcc1d60" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Don’t Dream It - Live It: this is how they describe these great Australian rail journeys.

There is no better way to travel across this vast country than by train. 

This adventure takes you on a journey on the Indian-Pacific from Adelaide to Perth. The stages relate to the planned stops along the way.

Enjoy the journey!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-30.74615" lon="121.466833">
  <ele>378.0</ele>
  <time>2023-09-27T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBeEBU-01</name>
  <desc>IndianPacificS1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/17454ed2-3cc1-443e-ac4b-ca55aae81add</url>
  <urlname>Indian-Pacific  : S1 Kalgoorlie - a city built from gold by sandyofthesea</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476911137" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Indian-Pacific  : S1 Kalgoorlie - a city built from gold</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>sandyofthesea</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">sandyofthesea</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Indian-Pacific &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Kalgoorlie - a city built from gold&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/17454ed2-3cc1-443e-ac4b-ca55aae81add"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/17454ed2-3cc1-443e-ac4b-ca55aae81add&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Welcome to Kalgoorlie! What is the city built on?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/afacb08f-8289-4b95-b0ce-2a63fc350888" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In June 1893, Patrick Hannan and Thomas Flanagan were travelling with a large group of men heading to the new gold prospect now known as Kalgoorlie. They discovered the first alluvial gold on the slopes of Mt Charlotte about 10 June 1893.
The two men, now in company with Dan Shea, searched for more gold - uncovering 100oz in a short period of time.
A Reward Claim was pegged out and Paddy Hannan rode the 30 miles back to Coolgardie, arriving at the Wardens Office (also the police station at the time) on the night of June 17th, 1893.
This started a gold rush which would eventually lead to the discovery of the richest gold find in Australian history - the Golden Mile.
Today, 130 years later, that find is still one of the world's biggest producers of gold - the KCGM Super Pit.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2e2bdae4-01e6-42ac-abcb-4e1abdcc1d60" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Don’t Dream It - Live It: this is how they describe these great Australian rail journeys.

There is no better way to travel across this vast country than by train. 

This adventure takes you on a journey on the Indian-Pacific from Adelaide to Perth. The stages relate to the planned stops along the way.

Enjoy the journey!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.008633" lon="125.332267">
  <ele>181.0</ele>
  <time>2023-09-27T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBeEBU-02</name>
  <desc>IndianPacificS2</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/17454ed2-3cc1-443e-ac4b-ca55aae81add</url>
  <urlname>Indian-Pacific  : S2 Rawlinna by sandyofthesea</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476911139" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Indian-Pacific  : S2 Rawlinna</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>sandyofthesea</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">sandyofthesea</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Indian-Pacific &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Rawlinna&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/17454ed2-3cc1-443e-ac4b-ca55aae81add"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/17454ed2-3cc1-443e-ac4b-ca55aae81add&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Where you stop for a meal is in front of a building. What was this building (two words)?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d6d8ae5a-8a6e-4e8a-a364-ed58963fa1c5" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Rawlinna is a small former railway town now better known as Australia’s largest sheep station. Exclusive to the Indian Pacific journey, guests are given the unique opportunity to disembark and enjoy a luxurious dining experience with drinks and canapes under the stars.

It’s an easy enough drive here from  Kalgoorlie but from Cook it is 3 tough days.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2e2bdae4-01e6-42ac-abcb-4e1abdcc1d60" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Don’t Dream It - Live It: this is how they describe these great Australian rail journeys.

There is no better way to travel across this vast country than by train. 

This adventure takes you on a journey on the Indian-Pacific from Adelaide to Perth. The stages relate to the planned stops along the way.

Enjoy the journey!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-30.613183" lon="130.4134">
  <ele>124.0</ele>
  <time>2023-09-27T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBeEBU-03</name>
  <desc>IndianPacificS3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/17454ed2-3cc1-443e-ac4b-ca55aae81add</url>
  <urlname>Indian-Pacific  : S3 Cook by sandyofthesea</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476911141" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Indian-Pacific  : S3 Cook</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>sandyofthesea</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">sandyofthesea</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>South Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Indian-Pacific &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Cook&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/17454ed2-3cc1-443e-ac4b-ca55aae81add"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/17454ed2-3cc1-443e-ac4b-ca55aae81add&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Find the galvanised iron fence with a sign. What year did the lines link up?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2a0a3468-0ac5-43ca-8bea-8551303d1151" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Officially, you are in ‘The Middle of Nowhere’. Welcome to Cook. Have a walk around and soak up the history of the Nullabour.

Cook is an old, abandoned railway town, with only a handful of permanent residents. Today it acts as a swap over town for train crews working for Pacific National, the freight company who owns the Trans-Tasman Rail Line. Westbound guests on board the Indian Pacific have some time to explore the old town with a map as your guide, while eastbound guests are treated to an Aussie outback lunch.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2e2bdae4-01e6-42ac-abcb-4e1abdcc1d60" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Don’t Dream It - Live It: this is how they describe these great Australian rail journeys.

There is no better way to travel across this vast country than by train. 

This adventure takes you on a journey on the Indian-Pacific from Adelaide to Perth. The stages relate to the planned stops along the way.

Enjoy the journey!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-34.938033" lon="138.581133">
  <ele>34.0</ele>
  <time>2023-09-27T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBeEBU-05</name>
  <desc>IndianPacificS5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/17454ed2-3cc1-443e-ac4b-ca55aae81add</url>
  <urlname>Indian-Pacific  : S5 Adelaide by sandyofthesea</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476911145" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Indian-Pacific  : S5 Adelaide</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>sandyofthesea</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">sandyofthesea</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>South Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Indian-Pacific &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Adelaide &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/17454ed2-3cc1-443e-ac4b-ca55aae81add"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/17454ed2-3cc1-443e-ac4b-ca55aae81add&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;There is a sculpture of a bird in the station. What is this bird (5 letters)?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0f6c6534-332f-4f76-a234-767b3ecaf4a2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This adventure starts in Adelaide and finishes in Perth (or vice-versa)  following the planned stops on the Indian-Pacific rail journey.

World-class food and wine, exceptional entertainment, picturesque beaches and a thriving arts culture; Adelaide has it all. Foodies will easily get lost in the thriving restaurant and bar scene and the award-winning wineries located in the Barossa and Adelaide Hills wine regions, located just outside the city. Adelaide Central Market also provides an exceptional journey for your tastebuds, showcasing a range of authentic Asian cuisine and artisan produce from various regions of South Australia

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2e2bdae4-01e6-42ac-abcb-4e1abdcc1d60" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Don’t Dream It - Live It: this is how they describe these great Australian rail journeys.

There is no better way to travel across this vast country than by train. 

This adventure takes you on a journey on the Indian-Pacific from Adelaide to Perth. The stages relate to the planned stops along the way.

Enjoy the journey!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.942583" lon="115.833183">
