   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Fremantle Line (Transperth)&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Cottesloe Station &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/2dd70f6e-870c-43ef-acc6-582fe8369255"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/2dd70f6e-870c-43ef-acc6-582fe8369255&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What famous sculpture event occurs at the beach every year? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1ceefeec-db7e-4e75-9afc-d6c09f8ad84d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Cottesloe station is served by Transperth Fremantle line services from Fremantle to Perth that continue through to Midland via the Midland line.

Cottesloe station saw 261,865 passengers in the 2013–14 financial year. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9167c011-5506-4743-8851-7bc3196b5250" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Fremantle Line is one of Perth's suburban rail lines running from Perth Station to Fremantle Station. The Line originally opened on the 1st March 1881 and since then it has undergone major changes like the electrification of the line which took place in the early 1990's. It is now one of Perth's busiest rail lines carrying around 5 million passengers per year. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
