 <wpt lat="-31.973733" lon="115.907467">
  <ele>22.0</ele>
  <time>2023-11-14T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBdswv-05</name>
  <desc>WhereInTheWAF25</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bdcb8216-d991-4482-b13b-62f202f3488d</url>
  <urlname>Where in the WAFL 2? : S5 West Coast Eagles Football Club by Kapelula</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-540" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Where in the WAFL 2? : S5 West Coast Eagles Football Club</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Kapelula</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Kapelula</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Where in the WAFL 2?&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;West Coast Eagles Football Club&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bdcb8216-d991-4482-b13b-62f202f3488d"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bdcb8216-d991-4482-b13b-62f202f3488d&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the Foundation?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/959f1dee-0b99-4ca1-98af-f6eb3166777b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The West Coast Eagles WAFL team came into the competition in the 2019 season after various arrangements for the AFL players to compete in the WAFL since their inaugural season in 1987.

Although initially proving to be successful finishing 4th in their first stand-alone season with a 9-9 win loss record qualifying for finals and reaching a semi-final against Claremont.

It has not been the same since. 2020 saw the team step back from the competition due to COVID protocols and since coming back in 2021 have only accrued 5 wins and a draw finishing last each season.

Club Colours: Royal Blue and Gold
Uniform: Gold Guernsey with royal blue wings and gold eagles logo, royal blue shorts, royal blue socks with gold hoop at the top
Premierships: 0&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c6251a1b-263c-4b09-904a-c25686be6c4a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Western Australian Football League or WAFL (pronounced locally as "waffle") is the premier Australian football competition in Western Australia.

The Western Australian Football Association was founded in 1885.  The name was the changed to the West Australian Football League (WAFL) in 1931 and had some name changes in 1990 and 1997-2000.

Before the introduction of the national Australian Football League (AFL) the WAFL was one of the big three leagues in the country along with the SANFL (South Australia) &amp; VFL (Victoria) however the increased professionalism of the AFL has seen a decline in popularity and the WAFL is now seen as a feeder league to the national competition.

The WAFL consists of several competitions- League (top tier), Reserves, Colts (under 19) &amp; Womens however not all teams compete in all competitions.

Currently there are 10 teams in the league, however over the years there have been a many as 21 teams playing in the competition.
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.972433" lon="115.906183">
