  <desc>WhereInTheWAF12</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b1490ac0-51f4-40e2-8ac5-57d33ea64dc3</url>
  <urlname>Where In The WAFL 1? : S2 Perth Football Club by monkeywand</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476911159" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Where In The WAFL 1? : S2 Perth Football Club</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>monkeywand</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">monkeywand</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Where In The WAFL 1?&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Perth Football Club&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b1490ac0-51f4-40e2-8ac5-57d33ea64dc3"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b1490ac0-51f4-40e2-8ac5-57d33ea64dc3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What are the names on the stand? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b23eef3f-bb9b-400e-86f4-72da301d5054" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Perth Football Club, nicknamed in Demons, is based in Lathlain. Formed in 1899, Perth is the fourth oldest of the WAFL clubs. The club song is sung to the tune of the anthem of the United States Marine Corps. 

Winning its first premiership in 1907, Perth did not win its second until 1955, with only 7 wins in total. Perth is statistically one of the least successful teams and has not played in a grand final since 1978. 
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2f0576fb-f31b-4f07-86da-fb5e57e03a7a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Western Australian Football League or WAFL (pronounced waffle) is the premier Australian football competition on Western Australia. 

The WAFL was founded in 1885 as the Western Australian Football Association changing to the current name in 1931. With some name changes in 1990 and 1997-2000.

Before the introduction of the national Australian Football League (AFL) the WAFL was one of the big three leagues in the country along with the SANFL (South Australia) &amp; VFL (Victoria) however the increased professionalism of the AFL has seen a decline in popularity and the WAFL is now seen as a feeder league to the national competition.

The WAFL consists of several competitions- League (top tier), Reserves, Colts (under 19) &amp; Womens however not all teams compete in all competitions.

Over the years there have been 21 teams play in the competition however currently there are 10 teams in the league.

Visit the origins of the WAFL home grounds, and discover the history of football. 

&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
