   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Where in the WAFL 2?&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;East Perth Football Club&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bdcb8216-d991-4482-b13b-62f202f3488d"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bdcb8216-d991-4482-b13b-62f202f3488d&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;It is now known as Perth Oval.  What was it known as originally?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ba7333a7-3530-4173-8f1f-729ec6f5f607" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The East Perth Football Club, nicknamed the Royals, is based in Leederville.  

The club was originally formed in 1902 as the Union Football Club.  

The club joined the WAFL in 1906 and changed its name to East Perth.in accordance with the WAFL's policy of having each club represent a district in Perth.

Club colours: Blue and Black
Uniform: Blue guernsey with black "V", blue shorts, blue and black hooped socks
Premierships: 17

*Information current as at November 2023*
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c6251a1b-263c-4b09-904a-c25686be6c4a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Western Australian Football League or WAFL (pronounced locally as "waffle") is the premier Australian football competition in Western Australia.

The Western Australian Football Association was founded in 1885.  The name was the changed to the West Australian Football League (WAFL) in 1931 and had some name changes in 1990 and 1997-2000.

Before the introduction of the national Australian Football League (AFL) the WAFL was one of the big three leagues in the country along with the SANFL (South Australia) &amp; VFL (Victoria) however the increased professionalism of the AFL has seen a decline in popularity and the WAFL is now seen as a feeder league to the national competition.

The WAFL consists of several competitions- League (top tier), Reserves, Colts (under 19) &amp; Womens however not all teams compete in all competitions.

Currently there are 10 teams in the league, however over the years there have been a many as 21 teams playing in the competition.
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
