  <name>LB1NvH-04</name>
  <desc>HydeParkS4Histo</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7dcd9777-de42-4a20-958b-80a66fce6fab</url>
  <urlname>Hyde Park : S4 History by col117</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476911153" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Hyde Park : S4 History</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>col117</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">col117</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Hyde Park&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;History &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7dcd9777-de42-4a20-958b-80a66fce6fab"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7dcd9777-de42-4a20-958b-80a66fce6fab&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;In what year was the planting of the grove of Jacarandas in the south east corner of the park?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a61b837e-6663-497e-915c-d52886d0a8da" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;For tens of thousands of years before the settlement of the swan river colony, this area was home to the native inhabitants of Australia. Originally known as Boodjamooling, the Hyde Park site was a campsite and meeting place for local Noongar people before European settlement. During the 1800s, the area was known as Third Swamp Reserve, with First and Second Swamps being located further South East (these natural lakes were drained in the 1800s).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/77de82bc-2d73-4b23-a99d-61b65334f158" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Hyde Park (formerly Third Swamp Reserve) is an inner-city park in Perth, the state capital of Western Australia. It is located in the north-east corner of the suburb of Perth – 2 km (1.2 mi) north of the central business district – surrounded by Vincent, William, Glendower and Throssell Streets.

Facilities include: public toilets, playground equipment, barbecues, drinking fountains, pavilion, stage area, fitness equipment and a sealed walking path of around 800 m (870 yd) in length ringing the lake. Electricity is available, which is used, for example, to power temporary fairground rides. A splash pad is particularly popular during warmer weather. A cafe is available adjacent to the main playground.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
