   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Hyde Park&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Araucaria bidwillii (Bunya Pine)&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7dcd9777-de42-4a20-958b-80a66fce6fab"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7dcd9777-de42-4a20-958b-80a66fce6fab&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Multiple warning signs around the park mention what adjective of seed pod which may fall from trees?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0c8552d6-d128-4fb8-99b8-c293915a3ca6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Hyde Park is synonymous for jacaranda trees, Moreton Bay figs and pine trees.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/77de82bc-2d73-4b23-a99d-61b65334f158" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Hyde Park (formerly Third Swamp Reserve) is an inner-city park in Perth, the state capital of Western Australia. It is located in the north-east corner of the suburb of Perth – 2 km (1.2 mi) north of the central business district – surrounded by Vincent, William, Glendower and Throssell Streets.

Facilities include: public toilets, playground equipment, barbecues, drinking fountains, pavilion, stage area, fitness equipment and a sealed walking path of around 800 m (870 yd) in length ringing the lake. Electricity is available, which is used, for example, to power temporary fairground rides. A splash pad is particularly popular during warmer weather. A cafe is available adjacent to the main playground.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
