   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Hyde Park&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Splash pad&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7dcd9777-de42-4a20-958b-80a66fce6fab"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7dcd9777-de42-4a20-958b-80a66fce6fab&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Who was Mayor as shown on the bottom right corner of the bronze plaque?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c4354e68-c364-4f35-ad08-a257ac5865b1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The splash pad has been refurbished multiple times over the years. Two mosaic murals no longer provide water. Near one of the murals is an information plaque which explains which schools designed the mosaics and when they were opened. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/77de82bc-2d73-4b23-a99d-61b65334f158" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Hyde Park (formerly Third Swamp Reserve) is an inner-city park in Perth, the state capital of Western Australia. It is located in the north-east corner of the suburb of Perth – 2 km (1.2 mi) north of the central business district – surrounded by Vincent, William, Glendower and Throssell Streets.

Facilities include: public toilets, playground equipment, barbecues, drinking fountains, pavilion, stage area, fitness equipment and a sealed walking path of around 800 m (870 yd) in length ringing the lake. Electricity is available, which is used, for example, to power temporary fairground rides. A splash pad is particularly popular during warmer weather. A cafe is available adjacent to the main playground.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
