  <name>LB5PNi-05</name>
  <desc>WhereInTheWAF15</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b1490ac0-51f4-40e2-8ac5-57d33ea64dc3</url>
  <urlname>Where In The WAFL 1? : S5 Swan Districts Football Club by monkeywand</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-610" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Where In The WAFL 1? : S5 Swan Districts Football Club</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>monkeywand</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">monkeywand</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Where In The WAFL 1?&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Swan Districts Football Club&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b1490ac0-51f4-40e2-8ac5-57d33ea64dc3"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b1490ac0-51f4-40e2-8ac5-57d33ea64dc3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name on the stand inside the fence line to the fence to the left as you look at the oval?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/befc5228-5065-4056-a8a7-e7fc74c92e07" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Swan Districts Football Club, nicknamed the Swans, was formed in 1933 and joined the then-Western Australian National Football League (WANFL) the following year. Swan Districts were a foundation member of the WAFL Women’s competition in 2019. 

Winning their first premiership in 1961, the Swans have won 8 premierships in total. 

The club song is to the tune of the 1926 song Baby Face, with its lyrics written by John Watts.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2f0576fb-f31b-4f07-86da-fb5e57e03a7a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Western Australian Football League or WAFL (pronounced waffle) is the premier Australian football competition on Western Australia. 

The WAFL was founded in 1885 as the Western Australian Football Association changing to the current name in 1931. With some name changes in 1990 and 1997-2000.

Before the introduction of the national Australian Football League (AFL) the WAFL was one of the big three leagues in the country along with the SANFL (South Australia) &amp; VFL (Victoria) however the increased professionalism of the AFL has seen a decline in popularity and the WAFL is now seen as a feeder league to the national competition.

The WAFL consists of several competitions- League (top tier), Reserves, Colts (under 19) &amp; Womens however not all teams compete in all competitions.

Over the years there have been 21 teams play in the competition however currently there are 10 teams in the league.

Visit the origins of the WAFL home grounds, and discover the history of football. 

&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
