   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Where In The WAFL 1?&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The West Perth Football Club &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b1490ac0-51f4-40e2-8ac5-57d33ea64dc3"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b1490ac0-51f4-40e2-8ac5-57d33ea64dc3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Who are the gates named after?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3103fec4-432b-4f00-aa13-d44fceecf56e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The West Perth Football Club, originally nicknamed the Cardinals but now known as the Falcons, is the oldest existing AFL club in Western Australia. Originally located at Leederville Oval, the team was relocated in 1994 to Arena Joondalup. The team’s club song is “It’s A Grand Old Flag” and its traditional rivals are East Perth. 

In 2022, the club became the seventh active club to participate in the Women’s WAFL (WAFLW). 

With 20 Premiership wins, beginning in 1987, to the most recent in 2022. 
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2f0576fb-f31b-4f07-86da-fb5e57e03a7a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Western Australian Football League or WAFL (pronounced waffle) is the premier Australian football competition on Western Australia. 

The WAFL was founded in 1885 as the Western Australian Football Association changing to the current name in 1931. With some name changes in 1990 and 1997-2000.

Before the introduction of the national Australian Football League (AFL) the WAFL was one of the big three leagues in the country along with the SANFL (South Australia) &amp; VFL (Victoria) however the increased professionalism of the AFL has seen a decline in popularity and the WAFL is now seen as a feeder league to the national competition.

The WAFL consists of several competitions- League (top tier), Reserves, Colts (under 19) &amp; Womens however not all teams compete in all competitions.

Over the years there have been 21 teams play in the competition however currently there are 10 teams in the league.

Visit the origins of the WAFL home grounds, and discover the history of football. 

&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
