   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Where in the WAFL 2?&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Subiaco Football Club&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bdcb8216-d991-4482-b13b-62f202f3488d"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bdcb8216-d991-4482-b13b-62f202f3488d&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Who’s jubilee was the entrance building erected to commemorate? (Full Title)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a4ef6b70-62b6-41f8-99a5-4cc98c95e2bc" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Subiaco Football Club, nicknamed the Lions, is now based at Leederville Oval, having previously played here at Subiaco Oval.

Before 1973 the club was known as the Maroons. 

The club was founded in 1896, and was admitted to the WAFL in 1901, along with North Fremantle. 

Club colours: Maroon and Gold
Uniform: Maroon guernsey with gold"V", maroon shorts, maroon socks
Premierships: 16

*Information current as at November 2023*&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c6251a1b-263c-4b09-904a-c25686be6c4a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Western Australian Football League or WAFL (pronounced locally as "waffle") is the premier Australian football competition in Western Australia.

The Western Australian Football Association was founded in 1885.  The name was the changed to the West Australian Football League (WAFL) in 1931 and had some name changes in 1990 and 1997-2000.

Before the introduction of the national Australian Football League (AFL) the WAFL was one of the big three leagues in the country along with the SANFL (South Australia) &amp; VFL (Victoria) however the increased professionalism of the AFL has seen a decline in popularity and the WAFL is now seen as a feeder league to the national competition.

The WAFL consists of several competitions- League (top tier), Reserves, Colts (under 19) &amp; Womens however not all teams compete in all competitions.

Currently there are 10 teams in the league, however over the years there have been a many as 21 teams playing in the competition.
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
