  <desc>WhereInTheWAF23</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bdcb8216-d991-4482-b13b-62f202f3488d</url>
  <urlname>Where in the WAFL 2? : S3 South Fremantle Football Club by Kapelula</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-538" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Where in the WAFL 2? : S3 South Fremantle Football Club</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Kapelula</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Kapelula</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Where in the WAFL 2?&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;South Fremantle Football Club&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bdcb8216-d991-4482-b13b-62f202f3488d"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bdcb8216-d991-4482-b13b-62f202f3488d&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year John Gerovich take the mark of the century?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/19423e13-289d-4a39-8a9c-3b8233d5c772" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;South Fremantle Football Club is based in Fremantle and has played here since its inception.

The club is commonly known by the nickname the Bulldogs.

South Fremantle Football Club was founded in 1900 and is one of the most supported clubs in the WAFL.  

The club is also recognised for its significant contribution of players who hail from Indigenous Australian, Italian and Croatian heritage.

Club colours: Red and White
Uniform: White guernsey with red"V", red shorts, red and white hooped socks
Premierships: 14

*Information current as at November 2023*&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c6251a1b-263c-4b09-904a-c25686be6c4a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Western Australian Football League or WAFL (pronounced locally as "waffle") is the premier Australian football competition in Western Australia.

The Western Australian Football Association was founded in 1885.  The name was the changed to the West Australian Football League (WAFL) in 1931 and had some name changes in 1990 and 1997-2000.

Before the introduction of the national Australian Football League (AFL) the WAFL was one of the big three leagues in the country along with the SANFL (South Australia) &amp; VFL (Victoria) however the increased professionalism of the AFL has seen a decline in popularity and the WAFL is now seen as a feeder league to the national competition.

The WAFL consists of several competitions- League (top tier), Reserves, Colts (under 19) &amp; Womens however not all teams compete in all competitions.

Currently there are 10 teams in the league, however over the years there have been a many as 21 teams playing in the competition.
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
