  <urlname>Perth Invaders : S1 PRT24 - Mends Street Jetty by Barrikon</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476912197" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Perth Invaders : S1 PRT24 - Mends Street Jetty</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Barrikon</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Barrikon</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Perth Invaders&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;PRT24 - Mends Street Jetty&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/880d17e3-4880-481f-92a2-a4b1fd510091"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/880d17e3-4880-481f-92a2-a4b1fd510091&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Besides vehicles, what else is not permitted on the jetty (according to the sign above the Invader)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d13968da-edce-46b7-a637-4e8c92669f45" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Mends Street Jetty has been around since 1898.

Various transport options have operated from this jetty over the years however today its main use is ferrying tourists from Perth's CBD to the Perth Zoo. 

Little do most know, this was an Invasion site with an Invader hiding in plain sight.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0d8aff3c-6013-4299-9141-34e0ba109c95" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In 2001 a French street artist with the pseudonym, INVADER, began a street art project which spanned the world. Tiles with Space Invaders emblazoned on them, adorned city buildings and infrastructure from Eilat in Israel to Sao Paulo in Brazil. There is even one on the International Space Station! 

Included in the Invasion was the humble city of Perth, Western Australia. 

26 INVADER tiles found themselves installed across Perth, each with a points system attached to them. When installed you were given a rudimentary map to find them all and 400 points to collect. 

Sadly, only 6 tiles remain. And this is where your adventure begins. 

Travel Perth to discover the 5 remaining tiles and maybe find the Bonus 6th.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
