   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Perth Invaders&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;PRT09 - Cultural Centre&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/880d17e3-4880-481f-92a2-a4b1fd510091"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/880d17e3-4880-481f-92a2-a4b1fd510091&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Immediately behind you is what building?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/082f036a-4dbf-4122-8f13-0dbf39bcbc63" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Perth Cultural Centre is made up of the Art Gallery of WA, WA Museum Boola Bardip, State Library of WA, The Blue Room, PICA (Perth Institute of Contemporary Arts) and the State Theatre Centre of WA.

Two Invaders where originally placed in this area but only one remains.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0d8aff3c-6013-4299-9141-34e0ba109c95" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In 2001 a French street artist with the pseudonym, INVADER, began a street art project which spanned the world. Tiles with Space Invaders emblazoned on them, adorned city buildings and infrastructure from Eilat in Israel to Sao Paulo in Brazil. There is even one on the International Space Station! 

Included in the Invasion was the humble city of Perth, Western Australia. 

26 INVADER tiles found themselves installed across Perth, each with a points system attached to them. When installed you were given a rudimentary map to find them all and 400 points to collect. 

Sadly, only 6 tiles remain. And this is where your adventure begins. 

Travel Perth to discover the 5 remaining tiles and maybe find the Bonus 6th.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
