A cultural hub. 

There are artworks from everyone and they are everywhere.  

There is a cache dedicated to this one tile...check out GC4TYD0.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0d8aff3c-6013-4299-9141-34e0ba109c95" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In 2001 a French street artist with the pseudonym, INVADER, began a street art project which spanned the world. Tiles with Space Invaders emblazoned on them, adorned city buildings and infrastructure from Eilat in Israel to Sao Paulo in Brazil. There is even one on the International Space Station! 

Included in the Invasion was the humble city of Perth, Western Australia. 

26 INVADER tiles found themselves installed across Perth, each with a points system attached to them. When installed you were given a rudimentary map to find them all and 400 points to collect. 

Sadly, only 6 tiles remain. And this is where your adventure begins. 

Travel Perth to discover the 5 remaining tiles and maybe find the Bonus 6th.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
