  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f67c51e2-3901-46e8-b008-211340b5e52f</url>
  <urlname>Charles Riley Wander : S1 Charles Riley by Barco</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-807" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Charles Riley Wander : S1 Charles Riley</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Barco</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Barco</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Charles Riley Wander&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Charles Riley&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f67c51e2-3901-46e8-b008-211340b5e52f"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f67c51e2-3901-46e8-b008-211340b5e52f&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many girls was Charles trying to rescue? (word)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4d337e56-9ac6-4087-875a-1c98c82e1dd3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;You are looking for a memorial plaque on the ground of the upper tier.

Used extensively in winter by North Beach Football Club and in summer by North Beach Cricket Club this clubhouse forms part of the larger multi-use Stirling Community Centre.

This plaque commemorates the tragic drowning of Charles Owen Riley, a trooper in the 2/3rd Australian Commando Squadron in WWII. Charles Owen Riley was the son of Charles Lawrence Riley, Bishop of Bendigo, and the grandson of Charles Owen Leaver Riley, the first Archbishop of Perth.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/27df700e-0cc6-4076-bcd7-8df556ca7d0b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A short wander around the Charles Riley Memorial Reserve. The journal entries will also lead you to a bonus cache (GCAJW8T).

Covering 8ha of sporting fields and recreation space, the Charles Riley reserve includes an impressive array of facilities, including:

Multiple sports clubs
Cricket nets
Stirling Community Centre
North Beach War Memorial
North Beach RSL Sub-branch
Two community play areas
BBQs &amp; picnic shelters
Fenced dog park
North Beach Toy Library
Accessible paths and amenities&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.861717" lon="115.758917">
  <ele>16.0</ele>
  <time>2024-01-30T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBwiHC-05</name>
  <desc>CharlesRileyWa5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f67c51e2-3901-46e8-b008-211340b5e52f</url>
  <urlname>Charles Riley Wander : S5 War Memorial by Barco</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-811" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Charles Riley Wander : S5 War Memorial</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Barco</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Barco</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Charles Riley Wander&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;War Memorial&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f67c51e2-3901-46e8-b008-211340b5e52f"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f67c51e2-3901-46e8-b008-211340b5e52f&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the missing word from the quote on the right-hand plaque? "Don't Forget Me, ..."&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/377b0a94-71f1-48cd-8783-a8b99f51a2d6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Look for the plaques on the nearby wall.

The monument commemorates those who have died in service or been killed in action in the various conflicts in which Australia has been involved.  It was dedicated in 1989 and moved to its current location in 2015 when the RSL Memorial Precinct was rededicated to the memory of Charles Owen Riley, trooper 2/3rd Australian Commando Squadron, WWII.

Additional plaques were added in 2018 to mark the centenary of the end of the Great War.

Lest we Forget.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/27df700e-0cc6-4076-bcd7-8df556ca7d0b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A short wander around the Charles Riley Memorial Reserve. The journal entries will also lead you to a bonus cache (GCAJW8T).

Covering 8ha of sporting fields and recreation space, the Charles Riley reserve includes an impressive array of facilities, including:

Multiple sports clubs
Cricket nets
Stirling Community Centre
North Beach War Memorial
North Beach RSL Sub-branch
Two community play areas
BBQs &amp; picnic shelters
Fenced dog park
North Beach Toy Library
Accessible paths and amenities&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
