   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Blackwall Reach Walk&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Parking Hut&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/fad35fc7-d21b-4994-ad7a-f3aa25ea3afc"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/fad35fc7-d21b-4994-ad7a-f3aa25ea3afc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the scientific name for the Blue-Banded Bee? (Two words)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4c8888ae-a102-4af0-b700-a5f495d0dd76" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;There is a small shelter at the parking area near here that gives information about the trails and history of the area.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/71b922bb-700f-4503-a735-e9289f83d73a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Blackwall Reach Reserve located in Bicton is a thin strip of bushland that runs along the Swan River.

There are a number of trails throughout the reserve ranging from paved to gravel to beaches.

There are numerous lookouts along the cliff tops and plenty of opportunities to spot wildlife, go fishing or find a place to swim.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
