   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Blackwall Reach Walk&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Our Beautiful Foreshore: Weeds&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/fad35fc7-d21b-4994-ad7a-f3aa25ea3afc"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/fad35fc7-d21b-4994-ad7a-f3aa25ea3afc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What type of grass is not mentioned on the sign?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c68dbcc1-dee9-400a-a996-9a9b01949d22" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;There are a number of signs along the paths that inform about the natural environment.

This sign talks of the weeds that can be found in the area.

Weeds overtake the native plant species and has larger impacts for the entire ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/71b922bb-700f-4503-a735-e9289f83d73a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Blackwall Reach Reserve located in Bicton is a thin strip of bushland that runs along the Swan River.

There are a number of trails throughout the reserve ranging from paved to gravel to beaches.

There are numerous lookouts along the cliff tops and plenty of opportunities to spot wildlife, go fishing or find a place to swim.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
