   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;An Excursion around Perth's Queens Gardens&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Heritage Shed&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/40268012-7f44-4352-96e2-ae97c70ea9c8"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/40268012-7f44-4352-96e2-ae97c70ea9c8&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;For how many years did James Brittain own and operate the East Perth Clayfields Reserve brickworks? (digit)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/92d16811-eee1-4e2e-b91e-cfb7e04cea6a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Located adjacent to the series of lakes that form the middle of these gardens is an old wood and tile shed that is part of the East Perth Heritage Trail. The informative noticeboard attached to the wall is well worth a read.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d7a1242f-8256-4530-8a9c-46853d484f20" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The beautifully manicured gardens and lakes of Perth's Queens Gardens can be found nestled among the sporting venues and office buildings of the East Perth precinct and provide a quiet and relaxed escape from the noise and bustle of the nearby city centre. 

You are invited to take a peaceful stroll around the gardens and locate the five stages of this Adventure Lab including one at Sir George Frampton's delightful replica statue of Peter Pan. Correct answers to the questions will enable access to the journal information necessary to solve the mystery bonus cache puzzle which uses five of the characters of the story of Peter Pan as clues.

From the city, you can take the free Red Cat bus and get off just a stone's throw from the entrance to  the gardens.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
