   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;An Excursion around Perth's Queens Gardens&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Peter Pan Statue&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/40268012-7f44-4352-96e2-ae97c70ea9c8"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/40268012-7f44-4352-96e2-ae97c70ea9c8&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;This statue was presented to the children of Western Australia by members and friends of which Perth club? (1 word)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6a2cb206-cfa8-416c-88f8-82d642dc9e88" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Close to the entry gate you will find Sir George Frampton's autographed, replica statue of Barrie's Peter Pan. Embedded in the crazy paving at the foot of the statue is a plaque providing the relevant information pertaining to this artwork. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d7a1242f-8256-4530-8a9c-46853d484f20" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The beautifully manicured gardens and lakes of Perth's Queens Gardens can be found nestled among the sporting venues and office buildings of the East Perth precinct and provide a quiet and relaxed escape from the noise and bustle of the nearby city centre. 

You are invited to take a peaceful stroll around the gardens and locate the five stages of this Adventure Lab including one at Sir George Frampton's delightful replica statue of Peter Pan. Correct answers to the questions will enable access to the journal information necessary to solve the mystery bonus cache puzzle which uses five of the characters of the story of Peter Pan as clues.

From the city, you can take the free Red Cat bus and get off just a stone's throw from the entrance to  the gardens.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
