 <wpt lat="-31.959417" lon="115.875433">
  <ele>15.0</ele>
  <time>2024-03-27T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBpn88-01</name>
  <desc>AnExcursionAro1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/40268012-7f44-4352-96e2-ae97c70ea9c8</url>
  <urlname>An Excursion around Perth's Queens Gardens : S1  The Gateway Entrance by Paskersfind</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476912225" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>An Excursion around Perth's Queens Gardens : S1  The Gateway Entrance</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Paskersfind</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Paskersfind</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;An Excursion around Perth's Queens Gardens&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt; The Gateway Entrance&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/40268012-7f44-4352-96e2-ae97c70ea9c8"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/40268012-7f44-4352-96e2-ae97c70ea9c8&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;According to the map legend, how many "Monuments" are located within these gardens? (digit)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/cc176f7b-ecf8-43a8-bf4c-cd528ace1ff6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;One of the entrances to Queens Gardens is located in the SW corner of the gardens. There is a double-sided notice board located just beyond the gates, the reverse side of which provides detailed and interesting information about the origins of these lakes and gardens. However, it is the side containing the colourful map of the gardens that you need to scrutinize carefully. 
 &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d7a1242f-8256-4530-8a9c-46853d484f20" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The beautifully manicured gardens and lakes of Perth's Queens Gardens can be found nestled among the sporting venues and office buildings of the East Perth precinct and provide a quiet and relaxed escape from the noise and bustle of the nearby city centre. 

You are invited to take a peaceful stroll around the gardens and locate the five stages of this Adventure Lab including one at Sir George Frampton's delightful replica statue of Peter Pan. Correct answers to the questions will enable access to the journal information necessary to solve the mystery bonus cache puzzle which uses five of the characters of the story of Peter Pan as clues.

From the city, you can take the free Red Cat bus and get off just a stone's throw from the entrance to  the gardens.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-34.3151" lon="115.162133">
