 <wpt lat="-31.97425" lon="115.85285">
  <ele>7.0</ele>
  <time>2024-04-01T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBmrQP-01</name>
  <desc>MeetTheBabyAni1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a68d2a9e-fa80-488c-b43c-5b37623e452a</url>
  <urlname>Meet The Baby Animals : S1 Aldo by Barrikon</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-672" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Meet The Baby Animals : S1 Aldo</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Barrikon</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Barrikon</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Meet The Baby Animals&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Aldo&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a68d2a9e-fa80-488c-b43c-5b37623e452a"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a68d2a9e-fa80-488c-b43c-5b37623e452a&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What does Aldo do with his trunk?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9d7e273d-e85f-4d69-a93e-93b1a3d5da01" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;What a silly and fun little creature
So adorable he just wants to greet you
With his long trunk and floppy ears
But when he grows up, one to fear
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6a480da4-bbbf-4e3d-a091-f4b4c069694e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Perth Zoo hosts many animals. For a fee you can see them, learn about them and even get hands on with some of the not-so-bitey ones.

In order to be big animal, you first need to be a small animal. 

21 baby animals figures are found around Perth. 14 within the zoo and 7 outside. 

'Jaylen' the baby Zebra and 'Arturo' the Brown Bear are near the entrance to the zoo.  
'Maya' the tiny Hippo is hidden at Elizabeth Quay and 'Joy' the cute Rock Wallaby is in Yagan Square.

This quest will have you finding the remaining 5 in Windsor Park. 

And for a bonus - there is also a Giant Gorilla at the zoo entrance. Why not take a picture with it!?

Visit perthzoo.wa.gov.au/wildaboutbabies for more information &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
