 <wpt lat="-32.15105" lon="116.122917">
  <ele>146.0</ele>
  <time>2024-03-29T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBiSMo-03</name>
  <desc>CanningDamS3Can</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/60056ec3-576f-4b34-983c-c845005ebb5d</url>
  <urlname>Canning Dam : S3 Canning Tunnel Outlet Main at Turtle Brook by familysteiner</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476912237" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Canning Dam : S3 Canning Tunnel Outlet Main at Turtle Brook</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>familysteiner</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">familysteiner</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Canning Dam&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Canning Tunnel Outlet Main at Turtle Brook&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/60056ec3-576f-4b34-983c-c845005ebb5d"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/60056ec3-576f-4b34-983c-c845005ebb5d&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year was this work completed? (4 digits)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0d631244-7771-4ba2-b972-ebf145a2b06e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Turtle Brook is a lovely spot to have a BBQ or a picnic whilst exploring the area. The Canning Tunnel was blasted through solid granite from Canning Dam to Roleystone to boost water flow from the dam. The outlet main pipe runs past the playground, and you can follow it to the tunnel portal near the road.  Walk to the beginning section of the pipe where it emerges from the ground, and look for a worker's hand-written inscription scratched into the concrete marking the completion of work on the Canning Tunnel. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b1548666-1f50-44b4-91c4-265cd28ab9fd" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Canning Dam is a benchmark site in the history of the provision of Perth’s water supply and in the history of concrete gravity dam construction in Western Australia. The dam was completed in 1940 at a cost of AU£1.1 million. Engineer Russell Dumas designed the dam and directed most of its construction. Its innovative structure and hydraulic design are considered to be at the forefront of concrete gravity dam design at the period. 

The construction of Canning Dam solved the problem of Perth’s water supply and it was the main source of water from 1940 to 1961, and remains essential to the city’s water supply service today.

This Adventure Lab will take you to some of the historical features and markers around the dam and reservoir. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.149817" lon="116.128783">
  <ele>212.0</ele>
  <time>2024-03-29T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBiSMo-01</name>
  <desc>CanningDamS1Can</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/60056ec3-576f-4b34-983c-c845005ebb5d</url>
  <urlname>Canning Dam : S1 Canning Dam Reservoir Lookout 1 by familysteiner</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-346" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Canning Dam : S1 Canning Dam Reservoir Lookout 1</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>familysteiner</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">familysteiner</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Canning Dam&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Canning Dam Reservoir Lookout 1&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/60056ec3-576f-4b34-983c-c845005ebb5d"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/60056ec3-576f-4b34-983c-c845005ebb5d&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Look at the signage at GZ. What is the SLWA catalogue number associated with the photo? (6 numbers, 2 letters)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6a9a0cf2-d408-4120-8803-eae6019cc108" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Canning Dam was built between 1934 and 1940. Little evidence now remains of the intricate system of tower cranes, guy ropes, cables, hoists, chutes and shutters that were needed to place concrete on such a large scale.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b1548666-1f50-44b4-91c4-265cd28ab9fd" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Canning Dam is a benchmark site in the history of the provision of Perth’s water supply and in the history of concrete gravity dam construction in Western Australia. The dam was completed in 1940 at a cost of AU£1.1 million. Engineer Russell Dumas designed the dam and directed most of its construction. Its innovative structure and hydraulic design are considered to be at the forefront of concrete gravity dam design at the period. 

The construction of Canning Dam solved the problem of Perth’s water supply and it was the main source of water from 1940 to 1961, and remains essential to the city’s water supply service today.

This Adventure Lab will take you to some of the historical features and markers around the dam and reservoir. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.155017" lon="116.125167">
  <ele>202.0</ele>
  <time>2024-03-29T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBiSMo-02</name>
  <desc>CanningDamS2Can</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/60056ec3-576f-4b34-983c-c845005ebb5d</url>
  <urlname>Canning Dam : S2 Canning Dam Quarry by familysteiner</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-347" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Canning Dam : S2 Canning Dam Quarry</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>familysteiner</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">familysteiner</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Canning Dam&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Canning Dam Quarry&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/60056ec3-576f-4b34-983c-c845005ebb5d"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/60056ec3-576f-4b34-983c-c845005ebb5d&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What were the bins pushed 200m along? (3 words)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ce50fef0-c274-4a74-9f37-58532375e379" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Canning Dam was built between 1934 and 1940 using rock from this quarry. Primary blasting detached the rock and secondary blasting reduced the boulders to a size small enough to be hand worked with pneumatic drills.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b1548666-1f50-44b4-91c4-265cd28ab9fd" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Canning Dam is a benchmark site in the history of the provision of Perth’s water supply and in the history of concrete gravity dam construction in Western Australia. The dam was completed in 1940 at a cost of AU£1.1 million. Engineer Russell Dumas designed the dam and directed most of its construction. Its innovative structure and hydraulic design are considered to be at the forefront of concrete gravity dam design at the period. 

The construction of Canning Dam solved the problem of Perth’s water supply and it was the main source of water from 1940 to 1961, and remains essential to the city’s water supply service today.

This Adventure Lab will take you to some of the historical features and markers around the dam and reservoir. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
