   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Canning Dam&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Canning Dam Old Township Buildings&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/60056ec3-576f-4b34-983c-c845005ebb5d"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/60056ec3-576f-4b34-983c-c845005ebb5d&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The silver plaque in the front garden refers to "Kwobodak Ngargagin" meaning "___?___ place of water"&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/84288c66-ead7-451f-b4fc-4a4138e952db" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;By 1934 a small township had been constructed to house the majority of the workmen and their families. As this work was carried out at the tail end of the depression these workmen were employed under ‘sustenance conditions’ which fixed the term of employment to the employee’s number of dependants. Initially the accommodation was in tents but later wooden huts were built. The small town grew to include a general store, butchers shop, and recreation hall to cater for the social life of the community. The school was built in March 1934. The only thing missing from a typical bush town was a hotel.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b1548666-1f50-44b4-91c4-265cd28ab9fd" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Canning Dam is a benchmark site in the history of the provision of Perth’s water supply and in the history of concrete gravity dam construction in Western Australia. The dam was completed in 1940 at a cost of AU£1.1 million. Engineer Russell Dumas designed the dam and directed most of its construction. Its innovative structure and hydraulic design are considered to be at the forefront of concrete gravity dam design at the period. 

The construction of Canning Dam solved the problem of Perth’s water supply and it was the main source of water from 1940 to 1961, and remains essential to the city’s water supply service today.

This Adventure Lab will take you to some of the historical features and markers around the dam and reservoir. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.154383" lon="116.127767">
  <ele>213.0</ele>
  <time>2024-03-29T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBiSMo-04</name>
  <desc>CanningDamS4Can</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/60056ec3-576f-4b34-983c-c845005ebb5d</url>
  <urlname>Canning Dam : S4 Canning Dam Wall by familysteiner</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476912239" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Canning Dam : S4 Canning Dam Wall</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>familysteiner</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">familysteiner</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Canning Dam&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Canning Dam Wall &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/60056ec3-576f-4b34-983c-c845005ebb5d"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/60056ec3-576f-4b34-983c-c845005ebb5d&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Look for the plaque on the upstream-side pillar. The Hon. H. Millington MLA was the then-minister for what? (5 words)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c9f02791-dd2e-48c6-9ed1-349d7823239e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The construction of Canning Dam ended a long period during which Perth's water supply was generally unsatisfactory in quality (either due to salinity or bacterial pollution or both) and in quantity. The project, the biggest public works program of the decade, stimulated significant growth in the local economy and provided desperately needed work for around five hundred men. Several innovative design concepts and construction methods which were new to Australia were introduced on the project. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b1548666-1f50-44b4-91c4-265cd28ab9fd" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Canning Dam is a benchmark site in the history of the provision of Perth’s water supply and in the history of concrete gravity dam construction in Western Australia. The dam was completed in 1940 at a cost of AU£1.1 million. Engineer Russell Dumas designed the dam and directed most of its construction. Its innovative structure and hydraulic design are considered to be at the forefront of concrete gravity dam design at the period. 

The construction of Canning Dam solved the problem of Perth’s water supply and it was the main source of water from 1940 to 1961, and remains essential to the city’s water supply service today.

This Adventure Lab will take you to some of the historical features and markers around the dam and reservoir. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
