   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Lap of the lake&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The old carparks&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/58a964fe-b088-4d71-a644-b7f58f7b28d2"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/58a964fe-b088-4d71-a644-b7f58f7b28d2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The sign is called “LAKE MONGER EXTERNAL ___________ LOCATIONS”.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/61da2acd-2926-415f-bf58-edb907733155" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Up until 2023, there were three “main” carparks along the southern side of the lake bordering Lake Monger Drive. These have been replaced with two larger carparks at the south eastern and south western corners of the park near the two of the playground area. 

Of the three “old” carparks, two have been filled in and one remains blocked. Edit, now closed!

There are frequent signs (every few hundred metres) outlining an important feature that occurs at three points around the lake.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e7fb639e-44e2-4f4c-8c2c-f6ed5669c08c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Lake Monger Reserve is a major Perth tourist and local community destination offering a mix of passive recreation areas, shared use paths, nature trails, shaded playgrounds, picnic and barbecue facilities and some sporting facilities for recreation use.

Please note that fishing or water activities such as boating and kayaking are not permitted at Lake Monger.

The middle of the park is taken up with Lake Monger, a habitat for an abundance of local flora and fauna making it a popular location to observe a wide selection of WA's beautiful birdlife.

Boardwalks and lookouts are provided around the lake from where you can take in the lake's natural beauty, with a lookout on the north side of the lake enjoying views to the Perth city skyline.

Features include:
Basketball
Barbecue
Dog Exercise Area - On Leash
Drinking Fountain
Exercise Equipment
Gazebo / Shelter
Lighting
Parking
Parking - Accessible
Picnic Table
Play Equipment
Public Toilet&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
