   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Lap of the lake&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Donor Honour Board&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/58a964fe-b088-4d71-a644-b7f58f7b28d2"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/58a964fe-b088-4d71-a644-b7f58f7b28d2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;At the bottom of one of the lists on the northern wall is Nathan STUBBERFIELD. Shown in speech marks, what was Nathan’s nickname?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f7ca736e-84aa-468d-82a3-795d5704121d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This significant location provides a tribute to organ tissue donors, who in death, gave life and wellbeing to others. Please be sure to show this location the respect it deserves.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e7fb639e-44e2-4f4c-8c2c-f6ed5669c08c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Lake Monger Reserve is a major Perth tourist and local community destination offering a mix of passive recreation areas, shared use paths, nature trails, shaded playgrounds, picnic and barbecue facilities and some sporting facilities for recreation use.

Please note that fishing or water activities such as boating and kayaking are not permitted at Lake Monger.

The middle of the park is taken up with Lake Monger, a habitat for an abundance of local flora and fauna making it a popular location to observe a wide selection of WA's beautiful birdlife.

Boardwalks and lookouts are provided around the lake from where you can take in the lake's natural beauty, with a lookout on the north side of the lake enjoying views to the Perth city skyline.

Features include:
