   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Waugal Monoliths&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Matriarch &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ff3e9407-ecb1-4294-a979-4751b084c64e"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ff3e9407-ecb1-4294-a979-4751b084c64e&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is growing in the statue?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0539b5ab-670f-48e3-9e3a-d505a26b9d70" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Beginning of life &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/37805915-85f9-426a-b548-f1735823922d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waugal Monolith Legend 
“Cold be hand &amp; heart &amp; bone &amp; cold be sleep under stone”
“Never to wake on stone bed never till the sun falls &amp; the moon is dead”
“In the black wind the stars shall die and still on gold here let them lie”
“Buried deep, never to sleep the Waugal trapped in time”
“Beware the winged serpent reborn within the lime”
Waugal legend - spirits with supernatural powers living in the Yanchep waters treated with fear and awe by locals. Victims were dragged down to the depths and imprisoned forever. 
Mark Lebuse was the sculptor.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
