   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Fremantle Hotels&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Orient Hotel&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/14be8ef5-980a-486f-9d2f-5298a641fbd8"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/14be8ef5-980a-486f-9d2f-5298a641fbd8&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Looking up from the corner of High and Henry Streets, what are the two words high up on the building?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/392b51fb-0b84-468b-a7cd-e908d0099edd" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This hotel has been formerly known as the Commercial Hotel, the Emerald Isle Hotel, Moloney's Hotel and Club Hotel.
The present building was constructed between 1902 and 1903 following the influx of people and money from the gold rush days of the 1890's.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b2366708-2100-41fe-afd3-ed6e32096f35" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Adventure Lab will take you to some of the existing and former hotels dotted around Freo. 
Please note that parking fees may apply in some areas.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
