  <desc>FremantleHotel2</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/14be8ef5-980a-486f-9d2f-5298a641fbd8</url>
  <urlname>Fremantle Hotels : S2 Cleopatra Hotel by jinta29</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1016" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Fremantle Hotels : S2 Cleopatra Hotel</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>jinta29</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">jinta29</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Fremantle Hotels&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Cleopatra Hotel&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/14be8ef5-980a-486f-9d2f-5298a641fbd8"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/14be8ef5-980a-486f-9d2f-5298a641fbd8&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Look up. What is the word directly below the triangle feature?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4796d006-4cf3-4e69-aa1f-0c725edda85f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Originally called the Crown and Thistle, the property was renovated in 1881 and named after the Cleopatra, a ship owned by Captain Fothergill. 
It had an attractive garden and tile paved path and a sign showing the ship Cleopatra in full sail. Captain Fothergill remained proprietor until 1896. 
The original building was demolished in 1906, with the new Cleopatra Hotel built on the site of the original. Work was completed in August 1907. 
The site was renovated in 1985 and the hotel was renamed ‘The Auld Mug Tavern’. The name has since reverted to Cleopatra.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b2366708-2100-41fe-afd3-ed6e32096f35" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Adventure Lab will take you to some of the existing and former hotels dotted around Freo. 
Please note that parking fees may apply in some areas.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
