   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Getting Around in Gidgegannup&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Gidgegannup Bakery&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/becda599-1c24-4fb0-a674-0579489487b1"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/becda599-1c24-4fb0-a674-0579489487b1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year was the bakery established?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ef66e509-4e5d-4497-8db6-c46370af1e56" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Established in 2005, the Gidgegannup Bakery stands as a beloved cornerstone in the heart of the quaint town of Gidgegannup, Western Australia. Stepping into this cozy establishment is like entering a haven of warmth and tantalizing aromas. The air is filled with the irresistible scent of freshly baked goods, drawing locals and visitors alike to indulge in a delightful array of treats. From traditional meat pies boasting flaky, golden crusts to artisanal bread loaves baked to perfection, every offering at the Gidgegannup Bakery is crafted with care and passion. The friendly faces behind the counter greet patrons with a smile as they browse through a tempting selection of sweet and savory delights. Whether it's a quick bite on the go or a leisurely morning spent savoring a cup of coffee and a warm pastry, the Gidgegannup Bakery holds a special place in the hearts and taste buds of all who enter its welcoming doors.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0c70ac52-daa1-459c-8cb9-2eee965e3cb7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Please note that all the answers can be found in the description of each location.

Come along on this adventure as we explore some highlights around Gidgegannup.

Gidgegannup is a township 40 kilometres northeast of Perth, Western Australia. The name Gidgegannup comes from a Noongar word meaning "Place where spears are made", and was first recorded by passing surveyors in 1852.

The townsite is situated on Toodyay Road. The locality is drained by the north flowing Wooroloo and Gidgegannup Brooks. Due to low density development, considerable amounts of natural vegetation remain in the area - and the roads to the north of Toodyay Road (O'Brien, Clenton and Berry, and Reen Roads) have been designated Wildflower Scenic Drive.

&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
