   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Getting Around in Gidgegannup&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Gidgegannup Showgrounds&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/becda599-1c24-4fb0-a674-0579489487b1"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/becda599-1c24-4fb0-a674-0579489487b1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Other than the Gidgegannup Show, what other event is held at the showgrounds?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/82ab498d-dd9c-4cc2-b446-a47fdc2f2ade" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Gidgegannup Showground is home to the Gidgegannup Agricultural Society show. The show features live entertainment, craft and animal exhibits, rides and food and drink outlets. The showground also hosts the Small Farm Field Days. There is also an agricultural hall and play space. The children's play area features a climbing wall, spining net and cubby with slide. The skate park is situated next to the play space. The hall and showgrounds can be booked through the City of Swan.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0c70ac52-daa1-459c-8cb9-2eee965e3cb7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Please note that all the answers can be found in the description of each location.

Come along on this adventure as we explore some highlights around Gidgegannup.

Gidgegannup is a township 40 kilometres northeast of Perth, Western Australia. The name Gidgegannup comes from a Noongar word meaning "Place where spears are made", and was first recorded by passing surveyors in 1852.

The townsite is situated on Toodyay Road. The locality is drained by the north flowing Wooroloo and Gidgegannup Brooks. Due to low density development, considerable amounts of natural vegetation remain in the area - and the roads to the north of Toodyay Road (O'Brien, Clenton and Berry, and Reen Roads) have been designated Wildflower Scenic Drive.

&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
