   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Getting Around in Gidgegannup&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Berry Reserve&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/becda599-1c24-4fb0-a674-0579489487b1"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/becda599-1c24-4fb0-a674-0579489487b1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the brook that flows through the reserve? (one word)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/247252b9-e947-40a9-9c56-d0da6876b69c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This beautiful reserve is tucked away at the back of Gidgegannup on Wooroloo Brook.
F.R. Berry Reserve is becoming an increasingly popular hotspot because of its unspoiled forests and native fauna.  It’s a top spot in WA for of the best wildflower displays of yellow wattles, rich blue leschenaultia and rare varieties that occur nowhere else on Earth.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0c70ac52-daa1-459c-8cb9-2eee965e3cb7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Please note that all the answers can be found in the description of each location.

Come along on this adventure as we explore some highlights around Gidgegannup.

Gidgegannup is a township 40 kilometres northeast of Perth, Western Australia. The name Gidgegannup comes from a Noongar word meaning "Place where spears are made", and was first recorded by passing surveyors in 1852.

The townsite is situated on Toodyay Road. The locality is drained by the north flowing Wooroloo and Gidgegannup Brooks. Due to low density development, considerable amounts of natural vegetation remain in the area - and the roads to the north of Toodyay Road (O'Brien, Clenton and Berry, and Reen Roads) have been designated Wildflower Scenic Drive.

&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
