   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Getting Around in Gidgegannup&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Noble Falls&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/becda599-1c24-4fb0-a674-0579489487b1"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/becda599-1c24-4fb0-a674-0579489487b1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How long is the walk trail?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f10850ad-a7bd-4d62-95ad-71794799156a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Noble Falls, nestled in the picturesque landscape of Gidgegannup, Western Australia, is a serene haven where nature's beauty reigns supreme. As the waters of the Wooroloo Brook cascade gracefully over ancient granite rocks, they create a mesmerizing spectacle that captivates visitors with its tranquility and charm. Surrounded by lush bushland, the falls offer a serene escape from the bustle of urban life, inviting visitors to immerse themselves in the soothing melodies of cascading water and the symphony of birdcalls echoing through the trees. Whether it's a leisurely stroll along the scenic walking trails, a peaceful picnic by the water's edge, or simply a moment of quiet reflection amidst nature's splendor, Noble Falls exudes an undeniable aura of tranquility and rejuvenation.
This lovely 3.5 kilometre walk along the Wooroloo Brook is attractive at all times of the year. The wildflowers are in bloom in the spring and the waterfall is stunning in winter. The walk adjoins a reserve, which is home to many birds and other wildlife.


&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0c70ac52-daa1-459c-8cb9-2eee965e3cb7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Please note that all the answers can be found in the description of each location.

Come along on this adventure as we explore some highlights around Gidgegannup.

Gidgegannup is a township 40 kilometres northeast of Perth, Western Australia. The name Gidgegannup comes from a Noongar word meaning "Place where spears are made", and was first recorded by passing surveyors in 1852.

The townsite is situated on Toodyay Road. The locality is drained by the north flowing Wooroloo and Gidgegannup Brooks. Due to low density development, considerable amounts of natural vegetation remain in the area - and the roads to the north of Toodyay Road (O'Brien, Clenton and Berry, and Reen Roads) have been designated Wildflower Scenic Drive.

&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
