   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Pelham Reserve Lookout&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Birds of Pelham&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/322954f3-f5f0-42b9-8d0b-e50a16f6b21d"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/322954f3-f5f0-42b9-8d0b-e50a16f6b21d&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many birds are listed on the information board?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/56a55ba2-1315-458c-8f38-87d67b08b635" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Pelham Reserve is home to many native animals such as kangaroos and euros.  In spring there is an impressive display of pink everlasting on the Everlasting Loop trail. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/eb7daa58-1c64-4ffd-8265-9399959a97fe" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Adventure Lab is a based at the Pelham Reserve Lookout, with views across the town of Toodyay. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
