   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;New Road&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Post Office&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/13736dfe-5639-413f-9ac8-5d9579a46cd9"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/13736dfe-5639-413f-9ac8-5d9579a46cd9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;On the bin, fill in the blank: "an XXXXXXXX as well as a convenience to our town."&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/aa115564-7aa5-4ac2-aed5-6b2f0b4afa6d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;For early Newcastle (eventually known as Toodyay), the Post Office was often the only link the townsfolk had with the rest of the colony. The Toodyay Post Office was erected in 1897 from a design by Government architect George Temple Poole.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/14bf330f-4024-419b-8e59-a62fa9c3738e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Stirling Terrace was originally known as the 'New Road,' surveyed in 1852 and cleared by convict labour.

During this time, the main street was nothing more than a dirt track, dusty in summer and bogged or flooded in winter. Pedestrians had to deal with open cesspits and livestock wandering the street, leading one local to complain whether: "something will be done to prevent pigs, goats and stray stock from patrolling the streets, at their own sweet will”

This adventure will take you to some historic sights along Stirling Terrace. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
