  <name>LBL2dK-04</name>
  <desc>OldOnslowTowns4</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7191bc3e-900f-497c-b130-4c7b14e773e6</url>
  <urlname>Old Onslow Townsite : S4 Mechanics Institute Hall by 80degrees</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476915732" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Old Onslow Townsite : S4 Mechanics Institute Hall</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>80degrees</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">80degrees</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Old Onslow Townsite&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Mechanics Institute Hall&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7191bc3e-900f-497c-b130-4c7b14e773e6"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7191bc3e-900f-497c-b130-4c7b14e773e6&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How long after the Hall was moved before it was reassembled&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/96d6419f-f979-4fe1-8479-183956e2f63a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Mechanics Institute Hall opened with a  calico costume ball in February 1912.  It replaced the Church Hall which was destroyed by a cyclone in 1909 and  became the centre of social activities and worship.  The hall included a library and reading room and after opening was used as a school.  It was one of the last buildings to move when the town relocated in 1926.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/535f7654-4696-4a79-8aa6-df6fa87aa727" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Adventure will take you for a journey through the original Onslow Township.  Onslow was established in 1883 to supply the surrounding sheep and cattle stations as well as the gold mines and pearling industry.  The town was gazetted in 1885 and it became important in the North West for the export of all of the above.
However with a rapidly silting river, large ships could no longer dock to load or unload goods.  In 1925 a new jetty opened at nearby Beardon Point ( now Onslow).  Onslow's people and many of its buildings relocated leaving behind the ghost town of today.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-21.711967" lon="114.94805">
  <ele>7.0</ele>
  <time>2024-07-22T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBL2dK-03</name>
  <desc>OldOnslowTowns3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7191bc3e-900f-497c-b130-4c7b14e773e6</url>
  <urlname>Old Onslow Townsite : S3 Law and Order by 80degrees</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476915730" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Old Onslow Townsite : S3 Law and Order</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>80degrees</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">80degrees</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Old Onslow Townsite&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Law and Order&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7191bc3e-900f-497c-b130-4c7b14e773e6"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7191bc3e-900f-497c-b130-4c7b14e773e6&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;On the Heritage Place Plaque what is the Place No.?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c25e1405-440a-4fc2-85df-dc2766e023df" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The police station comprised an office, courthouse, lockup and living quarters.  The lockup was extended in 1906 and served as a gaol for mostly Aboriginal prisoners detained under  the Masters and Servants Act.  The iron rings used to shackle inmates throughout the day are still visible.  An unroofed exercise yard allowed prisoners to move freely within but walls  topped with large pieces of broken bottles deterred escape.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/535f7654-4696-4a79-8aa6-df6fa87aa727" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Adventure will take you for a journey through the original Onslow Township.  Onslow was established in 1883 to supply the surrounding sheep and cattle stations as well as the gold mines and pearling industry.  The town was gazetted in 1885 and it became important in the North West for the export of all of the above.
However with a rapidly silting river, large ships could no longer dock to load or unload goods.  In 1925 a new jetty opened at nearby Beardon Point ( now Onslow).  Onslow's people and many of its buildings relocated leaving behind the ghost town of today.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-21.710967" lon="114.945533">
  <ele>6.0</ele>
  <time>2024-07-22T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBL2dK-05</name>
  <desc>OldOnslowTowns5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7191bc3e-900f-497c-b130-4c7b14e773e6</url>
  <urlname>Old Onslow Townsite : S5 The Ashburton Hotel and Hope's Store by 80degrees</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476915734" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Old Onslow Townsite : S5 The Ashburton Hotel and Hope's Store</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>80degrees</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">80degrees</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Old Onslow Townsite&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Ashburton Hotel and Hope's Store&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7191bc3e-900f-497c-b130-4c7b14e773e6"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7191bc3e-900f-497c-b130-4c7b14e773e6&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Who managed the hotel after 1919?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4e36a553-b1db-417b-b90e-6a49d8c7747d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Robert F Hope arrived in Onslow in 1892 to establish a store to service the goldfields.  The goldrush was almost over by that time but he established a strong business and later added the neighbouring hotel which he managed until 1919.
When Onslow moved, Hope refused the offer of land at the new town in exchange for lots in Old Onslow.  The hotel closed and the contents, goods and chattels were auctioned in 1926.  Built of stone and brick the hotel structure remained but the rest of the  materials were sold to the Hooley Brothers who carted them to their station, Diomenor, in 1929.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/535f7654-4696-4a79-8aa6-df6fa87aa727" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Adventure will take you for a journey through the original Onslow Township.  Onslow was established in 1883 to supply the surrounding sheep and cattle stations as well as the gold mines and pearling industry.  The town was gazetted in 1885 and it became important in the North West for the export of all of the above.
However with a rapidly silting river, large ships could no longer dock to load or unload goods.  In 1925 a new jetty opened at nearby Beardon Point ( now Onslow).  Onslow's people and many of its buildings relocated leaving behind the ghost town of today.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-21.70935" lon="114.944467">
