  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476915728" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Old Onslow Townsite : S2 Pearl Divers</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>80degrees</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">80degrees</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Old Onslow Townsite&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Pearl Divers&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7191bc3e-900f-497c-b130-4c7b14e773e6"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7191bc3e-900f-497c-b130-4c7b14e773e6&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The Asian Pearl divers lived in an area of town known as? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b2798292-2c5a-4309-adc0-fc9c1c3ea310" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The early pearling industry relied on cheap and expendable labour to meet the demand for pearls and pearl shells.  Pearl diving was incredibly dangerous resulting in the deaths of many divers.  Until 1885 all divers in the North West were Aboriginal but Asian divers gradually replaced them.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/535f7654-4696-4a79-8aa6-df6fa87aa727" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Adventure will take you for a journey through the original Onslow Township.  Onslow was established in 1883 to supply the surrounding sheep and cattle stations as well as the gold mines and pearling industry.  The town was gazetted in 1885 and it became important in the North West for the export of all of the above.
However with a rapidly silting river, large ships could no longer dock to load or unload goods.  In 1925 a new jetty opened at nearby Beardon Point ( now Onslow).  Onslow's people and many of its buildings relocated leaving behind the ghost town of today.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-21.70805" lon="114.959483">
  <ele>4.0</ele>
