 <wpt lat="-32.454617" lon="123.944567">
  <ele>149.0</ele>
  <time>2024-08-14T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBeXFi-05</name>
  <desc>NullarborPlain5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/fb8b50bf-d40f-47c6-b53e-29ecf52727ae</url>
  <urlname>Nullarbor Plain ~ Travel Trivia : S5 Theme: Wildlife by Ms Maddy</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476915762" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Nullarbor Plain ~ Travel Trivia : S5 Theme: Wildlife</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Ms Maddy</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Ms Maddy</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Nullarbor Plain ~ Travel Trivia&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Theme: Wildlife&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/fb8b50bf-d40f-47c6-b53e-29ecf52727ae"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/fb8b50bf-d40f-47c6-b53e-29ecf52727ae&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Dingoes are known to steal what from tourists? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/01d70ecc-68db-465b-b159-9087fa60be38" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Nullarbor is a wild sanctuary for wildlife of all kinds. One-humped camels roam in packs, kangaroos, wombats, emus and bandicoots forage in the scrub. A rich array of bird life lives out here including the (cute) green 28 parrots with yellow collars, wedge-tailed eagles and kookaburras. The blind cave spider lives underground in water known as stygofauna - and was named Australian Cave Animal of the Year 2024. Dingoes are likely to be spotted near the roadhouses looking for free snacks. Heaps of parking at the Whale Centre where you can view whales from May to October. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/44f55e29-0048-415c-82ff-0c5d3cb4ba1c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Nullarbor (Latin for no trees) trivia game. 

The aim is to break up your drive across the 90 mile straight. Australia’s longest straight road at 146.6km. This stretch of Eyre Highway runs from Caiguna (east) to Balladonia (west).

The Nullarbor Plain is a flat, treeless, expanse of limestone. ‘Tho unlikely you’ll see much (if any) wildlife during the day - I had to slow for a dingo early one morning as it padded across the highway. At the Head of Bight whales bask close to the spectacular Bunda Cliffs. 

All questions have multiple choice answers. You can log the waypoints in any order and either direction of travel.

Edward John Eyre (1841) described the Nullarbor Plain as “a hideous anomaly, a blot on the face of nature, the sort of place one gets into in bad dreams.” 

My view - It is one of the most extraordinary and peaceful places on Earth! 

Happy trails! 
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
