 <wpt lat="-34.314417" lon="115.155333">
  <ele>41.0</ele>
  <time>2024-09-05T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBZKEd-05</name>
  <desc>WAGOESBIGS5W024</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7161a18e-8eea-4635-af7f-d0cd0f32ea74</url>
  <urlname>WA GOES BIG : S5 WA Goes BIG in 2024 Augusta by pood</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918722" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WA GOES BIG : S5 WA Goes BIG in 2024 Augusta</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>pood</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">pood</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WA GOES BIG&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;WA Goes BIG in 2024 Augusta&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7161a18e-8eea-4635-af7f-d0cd0f32ea74"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7161a18e-8eea-4635-af7f-d0cd0f32ea74&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt; The Cape Leeuwin Lighthouse is the __________ on the Australian Mainland?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/50db1792-f247-48c9-b629-98f0da9873b7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;GCAGV8Y

It's our 11th annual WA Goes BIG Event, and you're invited! Pencil in your calendar and keep it free, you'll be joining us in Augusta for an action packed weekend of geocaching fun.

WAGB is an annual festival of Geocaching held at different locations around Western Australia. We put on a range of free activites for the community suitable for beginners through to more experienced geocachers that will keep you entertained and the best bit is that it's free to attend!

The weekend will kick off on Friday 20 September with our sundowner event, and the fun will continue right through to our farewell brekky on Monday 23 September.

If it's your first time, we recommend you attend for the whole weekend for maximum fun. But if you can't make all of it, the highlight of the weekend will be our free community dinner event on the Saturday night. Don't miss it!

We can't wait to see you in Augusta!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2251f9c9-43f0-476a-b1c0-c796c203ec38" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;West Coast Oz Geocaching has hosted 10 WAGB Events, this is Number 11 (this includes the very first event held by Felix and Geofriends).

This AL celebrates these events and provides an opportunity for cachers to learn a little about the history of some of WA’s awesome WAGB events.

The questions are multiple choice and are not difficult.

The AL is located at the site where the next WAGB event is to be hosted by the West Oz Committee will be held  - 'WAGB 2024'. 

Maybe take some time to check out the fabulous facilities, tourist hotspots and the incredible history of an early WA Settlement.

I hope to see you here at 
WAGB 2024.
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-34.314833" lon="115.156167">
  <ele>41.0</ele>
  <time>2024-09-05T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBZKEd-04</name>
  <desc>WAGOESBIGS4W023</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7161a18e-8eea-4635-af7f-d0cd0f32ea74</url>
  <urlname>WA GOES BIG : S4 WAGB 2023 Narrogin by pood</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918720" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WA GOES BIG : S4 WAGB 2023 Narrogin</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>pood</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">pood</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WA GOES BIG&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;WAGB 2023 Narrogin&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7161a18e-8eea-4635-af7f-d0cd0f32ea74"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7161a18e-8eea-4635-af7f-d0cd0f32ea74&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;WAGB celebrated its anniversary in Narrogin. What anniversary was it?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/bc785173-5f8e-4bb8-ab45-1400d6165057" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A jam packed weekend of fun at Narrogin for WAGB 2023.

GCA3KN0

West Oz Geocaching welcomed all geocachers and community members interested in Geocaching to our 10th anniversary of our WA Goes Big event.

This year we were in Narrogin, located 192 kilometres southeast of Perth in Western Australia's stunning Wheatbelt region.

WAGB is an annual festival of Geocaching held at a different locations around Western Australia. We had put on a range of free activites for the community suitable for beginners through to more experienced geocachers that will keep you entertained. And the best bit is that it's free to attend!

If it's your first time, we recommended you attend for the whole weekend for maximum fun. But if you can't make all of it, the highlight of the weekend was our Sunday Night Free Community Dinner event. Hope you didn’t miss it!

Did we see you in Narrogin?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2251f9c9-43f0-476a-b1c0-c796c203ec38" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;West Coast Oz Geocaching has hosted 10 WAGB Events, this is Number 11 (this includes the very first event held by Felix and Geofriends).

This AL celebrates these events and provides an opportunity for cachers to learn a little about the history of some of WA’s awesome WAGB events.

The questions are multiple choice and are not difficult.

The AL is located at the site where the next WAGB event is to be hosted by the West Oz Committee will be held  - 'WAGB 2024'. 

Maybe take some time to check out the fabulous facilities, tourist hotspots and the incredible history of an early WA Settlement.

I hope to see you here at 
WAGB 2024.
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
