   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WA GOES BIG&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;WA Goes BIG in 2017 Rockingham &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7161a18e-8eea-4635-af7f-d0cd0f32ea74"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7161a18e-8eea-4635-af7f-d0cd0f32ea74&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What was the Animal featured on the WAGB 2017 Geocoin?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/61b3511b-38ff-4e66-90c7-f95e137ad42c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;WA Goes BIG in 2017 
GC6TD11
Gary Holland Community Centre
19 Kent St, Rockingham WA
9 - 10 September 2017

We had 125 teams attend WA Goes BIG in 2013, followed by 128 teams at WA Goes BIG in 2015 (BUT a lot more people!), and then a whopping 183 teams at WA Goes BIG in 2016. So of course we were planning on it being as BIG, if not BIGGER!
This event was attended by plenty of locals and a few more interstate visitors.

There were brilliant gadget caches for geocachers to try their hand at, the geocaching shop was well supported.
There was a race that had you going to a variety of locations around the Rockingham LGA, within a reasonable time frame, wonder how many people can remember this?
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2251f9c9-43f0-476a-b1c0-c796c203ec38" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;West Coast Oz Geocaching has hosted 10 WAGB Events, this is Number 11 (this includes the very first event held by Felix and Geofriends).

This AL celebrates these events and provides an opportunity for cachers to learn a little about the history of some of WA’s awesome WAGB events.

The questions are multiple choice and are not difficult.

The AL is located at the site where the next WAGB event is to be hosted by the West Oz Committee will be held  - 'WAGB 2024'. 

Maybe take some time to check out the fabulous facilities, tourist hotspots and the incredible history of an early WA Settlement.

I hope to see you here at 
WAGB 2024.
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
