   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WA GOES BIG&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;WA GOES BIG 2013&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7161a18e-8eea-4635-af7f-d0cd0f32ea74"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7161a18e-8eea-4635-af7f-d0cd0f32ea74&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What town was the first WA goes BIG Event held in?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d7408cfd-2881-4982-9caa-a19fb79b560d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;WA goes BIG in 2013

GC45X55

This Event was held on the 
Weekend of 27-28th July.
At the Busselton Youth &amp; Community Centre, Cnr High Street &amp; Bussell Hwy BUSSELTON

Registration was at  10.00am Saturday 27th July.

The aim of this weekend was to share tips and tricks with likeminded GeoCachers.

Typically this time of year in the South West can be pretty wet, so a hall was been booked for some games and information sessions for everyone to join in. (Schedule was updated in months to come)

This is a FREE event although you were REQUIRED to wear your teams NAME TAG to access the event.

It was be great to see most of us were able to wear the Geocaching T-Shirt released last year by AlliedOz. Here is a picture of the T-Shirt Okay T-Shirt orders were closed and the orders were finalised.

FUN/ FUN/ FUN
GeoCaching Games
GeoCaching Information Sessions
Beginner FAQ’s and Question Sessions
Time to chat and catch up with Geo Friends
Searching/Finding techniques
Puzzle solving Techniques/ Tips

It was a great weekend of fun, catching up with like minded geocachers.

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2251f9c9-43f0-476a-b1c0-c796c203ec38" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;West Coast Oz Geocaching has hosted 10 WAGB Events, this is Number 11 (this includes the very first event held by Felix and Geofriends).

