   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WA GOES BIG&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;WA Goes BIG in 2016&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7161a18e-8eea-4635-af7f-d0cd0f32ea74"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7161a18e-8eea-4635-af7f-d0cd0f32ea74&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What was the name of the Geocache created by Valoforce for the WAGB event at Fairbridge?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/caa4bf4a-fd94-4678-b88d-055f367c9e68" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fairbridge Village
NORTH PINJARRA

GC5YAGP


WA Day Weekend
4th - 5th June, 2016

The aim of this weekend was to socialise with like-minded geocachers, sharing all of our tips, tricks and stories.

Over the course of the weekend, we were all be able to meet up with old friends and make lots of new friends too.

This time of year can be pretty wet, but being geocachers, we won't be letting a little bit of water dampen our spirits. But just to be sure, the main hall and meeting rooms were booked for some of the games and information sessions that were being scheduled over the weekend.
Well, you needed to plan to be there for starters.

We had 125 teams attend WA Goes BIG in 2013, followed by 128 teams at WA Goes BIG in 2015 (BUT a lot more people!). So of course we were planning on it being as BIG, if not BIGGER.

FYI: Having to work is not an acceptable reason for not coming. You just have to plan some leave time OR swap days off if you work weekends or shiftwork. So once you have minor detail organized, you then need to do a couple more things.

What to do next:

Your “Will Attend” log should include and the total number of people from each team attending. THE MORE, THE MERRIER!! Truth be told, by hosting the event closer to Perth, we were hoping to at least double (triple??) the number of teams attending.
Fairbridge has a number of heritage-listed cottages, with about 350 beds available.The smaller cottages had already been booked, but there was lots of room left, you could have shared a cottage with other geocachers over the duration of the event. 
Camping facilities were also available,

We highly recommended that you do try and stay overnight and enjoy the social scene after hours. food was available onsite too, so you should not have to venture too far from the festivities to feed your hungry hordes.

A brilliant cache was created for this event by ValoForce, replicating the historical church that is located on site.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2251f9c9-43f0-476a-b1c0-c796c203ec38" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;West Coast Oz Geocaching has hosted 10 WAGB Events, this is Number 11 (this includes the very first event held by Felix and Geofriends).

This AL celebrates these events and provides an opportunity for cachers to learn a little about the history of some of WA’s awesome WAGB events.

The questions are multiple choice and are not difficult.

The AL is located at the site where the next WAGB event is to be hosted by the West Oz Committee will be held  - 'WAGB 2024'. 

Maybe take some time to check out the fabulous facilities, tourist hotspots and the incredible history of an early WA Settlement.

I hope to see you here at 
WAGB 2024.
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
