 <wpt lat="-31.969383" lon="116.058733">
  <ele>283.0</ele>
  <time>2024-09-08T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBUWvZ-03</name>
  <desc>KalamundaARTWA3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/aec90b74-e1b2-4b94-8c52-d34f4524922c</url>
  <urlname>Kalamunda ARTWALK : S3 Zig Zag Train Station by fratra</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476915764" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Kalamunda ARTWALK : S3 Zig Zag Train Station</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>fratra</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">fratra</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Kalamunda ARTWALK&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Zig Zag Train Station&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/aec90b74-e1b2-4b94-8c52-d34f4524922c"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/aec90b74-e1b2-4b94-8c52-d34f4524922c&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the Artist?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5e330352-f153-4514-a2b2-f515265158a1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This steel wall sculpture faces the Railway Road side of the 
History Village and was commissioned by the Kalamunda 
and Districts Historical Society as signage for the Village. 
The number 118 refers to the number on the steam train in 
the History Village.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/146ebc3e-34cb-40f0-9813-24586f45d722" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Kalamunda ArtWalk takes you past public artworks within the Kalamunda Town Centre, with extensions to the Kalamunda Community Centre and the City of Kalamunda administration building. It begins at the Perth Hills Kalamunda Visitor Centre on Railway Road.

The ArtWalk brochure can be collected at the Visitor Centre, 50 Railway Road, Kalamunda or downloaded online. The Centre is open 7 days a week, 9am to 4pm during the week, and 10am to 4pm on weekends and most public holidays.

All stages can be accessed for free and are available 24/7.

There is a bonus cache (GCAXNGH) that can be located using information in the Journal.
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.969267" lon="116.059117">
