  <name>LB7ozt-03</name>
  <desc>HomeOfFootball3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1513cc67-dd91-458b-ad70-d415a2fe69f4</url>
  <urlname>The Home of Football : S3 Sandover Medal Walk by Cirrus_WA</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918201" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>The Home of Football : S3 Sandover Medal Walk</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Cirrus_WA</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Cirrus_WA</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;The Home of Football&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Sandover Medal Walk&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1513cc67-dd91-458b-ad70-d415a2fe69f4"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1513cc67-dd91-458b-ad70-d415a2fe69f4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Who were the joint inaugural winners of the Sandover Medal?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2ea33878-cb96-4c27-8346-d9e62021c840" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Sandover Medal Walk at Subiaco Oval is a commemorative pathway honoring the winners of the prestigious Sandover Medal, awarded annually to the best and fairest player in the Western Australian Football League (WAFL). The walk features plaques embedded in the ground, each bearing the name of a Sandover Medal recipient, celebrating their achievements and contributions to WAFL history.

Located near the preserved playing surface of the oval, the Sandover Medal Walk serves as a tribute to the rich football legacy of Subiaco Oval, connecting fans and visitors with the storied history of the WAFL and its top players. It remains a lasting feature of the site following the redevelopment of the oval area.

The walk runs in an anti-clockwise direction, as a nod to the direction the players took their warm up laps on Subiaco Oval.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/df723db2-d3d4-40aa-ba44-1c78a10e77c6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;For over 100 years Subiaco Oval was the home of football in Western Australia.

Established in 1908, it served as the home ground for the Subiaco Football Club and later became the main venue for Australian Football League (AFL) matches in Western Australia.

The oval was initially a modest facility but underwent multiple redevelopments over the years to increase its capacity and improve its amenities. By the time it was fully developed, Subiaco Oval could accommodate over 43,000 spectators, making it the largest stadium in Western Australia.

It hosted many memorable AFL games, including home matches for the West Coast Eagles (from their inception in 1987) and Fremantle Dockers (from 1995). The oval also hosted other sports like rugby, cricket, and soccer, as well as concerts by international artists.

In 2018, Subiaco Oval was officially closed following the opening of the new Perth Stadium, which took over as the primary venue for major sports events in Perth. Following its closure, the oval was partially demolished, but the playing surface and some of its heritage features were preserved as part of a redevelopment plan to integrate the site into the new Bob Hawke College and surrounding community areas.

Subiaco Oval holds a special place in the hearts of Western Australians, symbolizing over a century of local and national sporting achievements.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
