  <name>LB7ozt-04</name>
  <desc>HomeOfFootball4</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1513cc67-dd91-458b-ad70-d415a2fe69f4</url>
  <urlname>The Home of Football : S4 Dockers Race by Cirrus_WA</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918203" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>The Home of Football : S4 Dockers Race</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Cirrus_WA</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Cirrus_WA</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;The Home of Football&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Dockers Race&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1513cc67-dd91-458b-ad70-d415a2fe69f4"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1513cc67-dd91-458b-ad70-d415a2fe69f4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;This bench is dedicated to the amount of tears shed over what? (5 words as written, including punctuation)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b5a23764-d2f4-4a13-90a3-180e0b9b7874" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Located beneath the two-tier stand at Subiaco Oval were the changing rooms for the Fremantle Dockers, the umpires, and the away teams. The two-tier stand, constructed in 1981, was a major part of the stadium’s infrastructure and retained its original bench-style seating for over 35 years, right up until the ground closed in 2017.

These distinctive wooden benches were an iconic feature of Subiaco Oval, used by generations of fans who attended AFL games, concerts, and other events. After the stadium's closure, the benches took on new life. While some remain intact nearby as a reminder of the stadium’s legacy, others—part of a collection of 322 benches—were either repurposed as seating around the preserved oval or auctioned off to fans and collectors.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/df723db2-d3d4-40aa-ba44-1c78a10e77c6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;For over 100 years Subiaco Oval was the home of football in Western Australia.

Established in 1908, it served as the home ground for the Subiaco Football Club and later became the main venue for Australian Football League (AFL) matches in Western Australia.

The oval was initially a modest facility but underwent multiple redevelopments over the years to increase its capacity and improve its amenities. By the time it was fully developed, Subiaco Oval could accommodate over 43,000 spectators, making it the largest stadium in Western Australia.

It hosted many memorable AFL games, including home matches for the West Coast Eagles (from their inception in 1987) and Fremantle Dockers (from 1995). The oval also hosted other sports like rugby, cricket, and soccer, as well as concerts by international artists.

In 2018, Subiaco Oval was officially closed following the opening of the new Perth Stadium, which took over as the primary venue for major sports events in Perth. Following its closure, the oval was partially demolished, but the playing surface and some of its heritage features were preserved as part of a redevelopment plan to integrate the site into the new Bob Hawke College and surrounding community areas.

Subiaco Oval holds a special place in the hearts of Western Australians, symbolizing over a century of local and national sporting achievements.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-34.926117" lon="117.2877">
