  <time>2024-10-19T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBTNCU-05</name>
  <desc>HarewoodForest5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/798602c9-7976-4e1d-b1bf-89d262d721a4</url>
  <urlname>Harewood Forest Walk Trail : S5 Lost Dreams by richlink</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918195" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Harewood Forest Walk Trail : S5 Lost Dreams</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>richlink</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">richlink</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Harewood Forest Walk Trail&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Lost Dreams&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/798602c9-7976-4e1d-b1bf-89d262d721a4"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/798602c9-7976-4e1d-b1bf-89d262d721a4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What percentage of settlers left the Group Settlement scheme?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9e501f10-5270-4895-9eed-be8e7d68c73f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Settlers were allocated land by a ballot system. They began clearing the forest with axes and fire.
Many British immigrants were without the skills needed to farm in these southern forests and living conditions were primitive.
By 1930, many settlers had walked off their allotments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/95b8cddc-dbe0-4bbe-970f-a5bcfda09104" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Logged of all large timber in the late 1800's, Harewood Forest has recovered and is today a great example of regrowth karri forest.
Now you can walk among the tall karris and the whispery fronds of the karri oak with their lush undergrowth of tassel flower and karri hazel. Small birds such as re-winged fairy-wrens and white-breasted robins' flit through the under-storey while purple-crowned lorikeets chatter loudly in the tree tops when the karri is in bloom.

Well defined circuit trail that takes around 1 hour to complete. Dogs are welcome but must be on a lead.

Mobile reception can be sketchy so ensure you have opened the LAB adventure before setting off!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-34.926233" lon="117.288467">
