   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Harewood Forest Walk Trail&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Slow hard work&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/798602c9-7976-4e1d-b1bf-89d262d721a4"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/798602c9-7976-4e1d-b1bf-89d262d721a4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What type of saw was used to cut the timber down? (one word)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/201560ed-8241-430c-a1c1-87bd98ab9e0a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;To fell these giants, two men stood opposite each other on narrow 'spring boards' jammed into the trunk, two metres above the ground.
When they had chopped a third of the way through one side, they moved to the back and used a saw until the tree fell.
Once on the ground the men again used the saw to 'dock' the log into lengths that the bullock or horse drawn whims could handle.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/95b8cddc-dbe0-4bbe-970f-a5bcfda09104" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Logged of all large timber in the late 1800's, Harewood Forest has recovered and is today a great example of regrowth karri forest.
Now you can walk among the tall karris and the whispery fronds of the karri oak with their lush undergrowth of tassel flower and karri hazel. Small birds such as re-winged fairy-wrens and white-breasted robins' flit through the under-storey while purple-crowned lorikeets chatter loudly in the tree tops when the karri is in bloom.

Well defined circuit trail that takes around 1 hour to complete. Dogs are welcome but must be on a lead.

Mobile reception can be sketchy so ensure you have opened the LAB adventure before setting off!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
