   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Harewood Forest Walk Trail&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Big Business&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/798602c9-7976-4e1d-b1bf-89d262d721a4"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/798602c9-7976-4e1d-b1bf-89d262d721a4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;After how many years of intensive logging had most of the useful timber been used? (digit)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/74d6c44f-ae3f-491c-9038-70610c94dc4e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;At their peak the Timber and Trading Company operated three mills in the Denmark area, employing up to 750 people. They dispatched two train loads of sawn karri timber each day to Albany.
From Albany the timber was shipped all over the world.
One of the largest orders was for karri beams to be used as street paving in London. 
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/95b8cddc-dbe0-4bbe-970f-a5bcfda09104" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Logged of all large timber in the late 1800's, Harewood Forest has recovered and is today a great example of regrowth karri forest.
Now you can walk among the tall karris and the whispery fronds of the karri oak with their lush undergrowth of tassel flower and karri hazel. Small birds such as re-winged fairy-wrens and white-breasted robins' flit through the under-storey while purple-crowned lorikeets chatter loudly in the tree tops when the karri is in bloom.

Well defined circuit trail that takes around 1 hour to complete. Dogs are welcome but must be on a lead.

Mobile reception can be sketchy so ensure you have opened the LAB adventure before setting off!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
