 <wpt lat="-31.972783" lon="116.058633">
  <ele>293.0</ele>
  <time>2024-11-02T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBqeSV-03</name>
  <desc>KalamundaARTWAS</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bdd85cc5-4c27-4c82-bc31-5242056eb8d5</url>
  <urlname>Kalamunda ARTWALK II : S3 Western Quoll, Honey Possum, Blue banded bee by fratra</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918221" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Kalamunda ARTWALK II : S3 Western Quoll, Honey Possum, Blue banded bee</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>fratra</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">fratra</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Kalamunda ARTWALK II&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Western Quoll, Honey Possum, Blue banded bee&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bdd85cc5-4c27-4c82-bc31-5242056eb8d5"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bdd85cc5-4c27-4c82-bc31-5242056eb8d5&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many marsupial toes can you see in the mural?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/fee48e6a-68ab-436a-91c2-1a76563e26c3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Artist: Melski McVee
Make your way safely through the carpark and along Mead 
Street to Central Mall to see the third mural on the external 
wall of the Kalamunda Central Shopping Centre. It features 
the Western Quoll, Honey Possum, Blue banded bee and 
Banksia flowers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7e0c1cb3-e1b2-4f92-b1b9-4a177c1cfd16" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Kalamunda ArtWalk takes you past public artworks within the Kalamunda Town Centre, with extensions to the Kalamunda Community Centre and the City of Kalamunda administration building. It begins at the Perth Hills Kalamunda Visitor Centre on Railway Road.

The ArtWalk brochure can be collected at the Visitor Centre, 50 Railway Road, Kalamunda or downloaded online. The Centre is open 7 days a week, 9am to 4pm during the week, and 10am to 4pm on weekends and most public holidays.

All stages can be accessed for free and are available 24/7.

There is a bonus cache (GCAXNGH) that can be located using information in the Journal.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.972267" lon="116.058133">
  <ele>287.0</ele>
  <time>2024-11-02T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBqeSV-05</name>
  <desc>KalamundaARTWAP</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bdd85cc5-4c27-4c82-bc31-5242056eb8d5</url>
  <urlname>Kalamunda ARTWALK II : S5 Pioneer Women’s Sculpture by fratra</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918225" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Kalamunda ARTWALK II : S5 Pioneer Women’s Sculpture</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>fratra</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">fratra</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Kalamunda ARTWALK II&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Pioneer Women’s Sculpture&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bdd85cc5-4c27-4c82-bc31-5242056eb8d5"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bdd85cc5-4c27-4c82-bc31-5242056eb8d5&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How tall does this statue stand? (two words)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/79755f98-d676-4766-a389-711128eac68f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Artists: Julie Parsons and Alison Cameron-Brown
Commissioned for the Centenary of Women’s Suffrage, 
this sculpture recognises and celebrates the important 
role women have played in Western Australia’s history. It 
represents women as ‘pillars in the community’ symbolised 
by a bronze sculpture of a woman at the top inserted into a 
concrete base of figurative relief.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7e0c1cb3-e1b2-4f92-b1b9-4a177c1cfd16" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Kalamunda ArtWalk takes you past public artworks within the Kalamunda Town Centre, with extensions to the Kalamunda Community Centre and the City of Kalamunda administration building. It begins at the Perth Hills Kalamunda Visitor Centre on Railway Road.

The ArtWalk brochure can be collected at the Visitor Centre, 50 Railway Road, Kalamunda or downloaded online. The Centre is open 7 days a week, 9am to 4pm during the week, and 10am to 4pm on weekends and most public holidays.

All stages can be accessed for free and are available 24/7.

There is a bonus cache (GCAXNGH) that can be located using information in the Journal.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.973183" lon="116.059717">
  <ele>296.0</ele>
  <time>2024-11-02T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBqeSV-02</name>
  <desc>KalamundaARTWAI</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bdd85cc5-4c27-4c82-bc31-5242056eb8d5</url>
  <urlname>Kalamunda ARTWALK II : S2 Long Necked Turtle by fratra</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918219" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Kalamunda ARTWALK II : S2 Long Necked Turtle</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>fratra</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">fratra</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Kalamunda ARTWALK II&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Long Necked Turtle &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bdd85cc5-4c27-4c82-bc31-5242056eb8d5"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bdd85cc5-4c27-4c82-bc31-5242056eb8d5&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many Long Necked Turtles can you see in the mural? (both walls)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b67b4cb6-79d1-4a31-9ac5-d0e5b5c2d6ca" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Artist: Melski McVee
Across from the Northern Terminus of the Bibbulmun 
Track, on Railway Road, and along the pathway from the 
red letterbox, are colourful murals on two external walls of 
the Kalamunda Central Shopping Centre. The Red Tailed Black Cockatoo faces Railway 
Road and The Long Necked Turtle faces Mead Street. They both feature fauna 
and flora native to our area.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7e0c1cb3-e1b2-4f92-b1b9-4a177c1cfd16" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Kalamunda ArtWalk takes you past public artworks within the Kalamunda Town Centre, with extensions to the Kalamunda Community Centre and the City of Kalamunda administration building. It begins at the Perth Hills Kalamunda Visitor Centre on Railway Road.

The ArtWalk brochure can be collected at the Visitor Centre, 50 Railway Road, Kalamunda or downloaded online. The Centre is open 7 days a week, 9am to 4pm during the week, and 10am to 4pm on weekends and most public holidays.

All stages can be accessed for free and are available 24/7.

There is a bonus cache (GCAXNGH) that can be located using information in the Journal.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
