   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Kalamunda ARTWALK II&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Horse and whim&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bdd85cc5-4c27-4c82-bc31-5242056eb8d5"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bdd85cc5-4c27-4c82-bc31-5242056eb8d5&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many wooden pins hold the tail in place?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7a436eda-1f44-42f2-8ac4-8a473477dfde" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Artist: Nicholas Compton
This large wooden work reflects the early logging history 
of the district and is carved from a single log of wandoo, a local native tree.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7e0c1cb3-e1b2-4f92-b1b9-4a177c1cfd16" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Kalamunda ArtWalk takes you past public artworks within the Kalamunda Town Centre, with extensions to the Kalamunda Community Centre and the City of Kalamunda administration building. It begins at the Perth Hills Kalamunda Visitor Centre on Railway Road.

The ArtWalk brochure can be collected at the Visitor Centre, 50 Railway Road, Kalamunda or downloaded online. The Centre is open 7 days a week, 9am to 4pm during the week, and 10am to 4pm on weekends and most public holidays.

All stages can be accessed for free and are available 24/7.

There is a bonus cache (GCAXNGH) that can be located using information in the Journal.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
