   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Harvey Bound &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Wattle Babies&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ff613d83-102d-451d-8e50-d7fa9244d075"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ff613d83-102d-451d-8e50-d7fa9244d075&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What do Wattle Babies use for boats? (2 words)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/825879a0-132f-4f80-9f21-56a392f59022" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The sign with the story of the Wattle Babies should not be hard to find behind the 'stables' at the start of the river walk.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9a1def16-8732-4dfa-9551-a162fcc60280" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; Welcome to James Stirling Place in beautiful Harvey, WA. The standout feature of this location- Stirling Cottage- is a replica 1850's timber cottage that has been home to WA's First Governor, Sir James Stirling, as well as many pioneering families including that of 'Snugglepot and Cuddlepie' creator, May Gibbs.
This adventure lab takes you on a leisurely stroll along the river walk pathway surrounding the immaculate Heritage Gardens of the cottage and introduces (or reacquaints) you with some of the wonderful, quirky characters May Gibbs created in her award-winning children's stories.
We hope you have fun and perhaps take some time to visit the abundance of other attractions in and around this delightful township.

&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
