   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Harvey Bound &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Prince Dande Lion&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ff613d83-102d-451d-8e50-d7fa9244d075"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ff613d83-102d-451d-8e50-d7fa9244d075&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What was the occupation of Old Bill in this story?  (8 letters)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e004f96b-ca87-4952-8aa1-ccdc846babad" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This sign at the end of this river walk (or the start depending on your choice of direction) depicts the hero of May Gibbs' final book. The signage content makes for interesting reading.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9a1def16-8732-4dfa-9551-a162fcc60280" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; Welcome to James Stirling Place in beautiful Harvey, WA. The standout feature of this location- Stirling Cottage- is a replica 1850's timber cottage that has been home to WA's First Governor, Sir James Stirling, as well as many pioneering families including that of 'Snugglepot and Cuddlepie' creator, May Gibbs.
This adventure lab takes you on a leisurely stroll along the river walk pathway surrounding the immaculate Heritage Gardens of the cottage and introduces (or reacquaints) you with some of the wonderful, quirky characters May Gibbs created in her award-winning children's stories.
We hope you have fun and perhaps take some time to visit the abundance of other attractions in and around this delightful township.

&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
