   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Harvey Bound &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Chucklebud and Wunkydoo&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ff613d83-102d-451d-8e50-d7fa9244d075"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ff613d83-102d-451d-8e50-d7fa9244d075&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What kind of creature is Mr Wackasmack?  A...&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/71335424-5fbb-443e-95c2-109e9de786fa" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;You know the drill- find the sign with the same title as this location! So, if you are standing in front of the sign referring to these unusually-named characters, all is well. Just as well you are not going to be asked to count the gumnut babies in this illustration!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9a1def16-8732-4dfa-9551-a162fcc60280" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; Welcome to James Stirling Place in beautiful Harvey, WA. The standout feature of this location- Stirling Cottage- is a replica 1850's timber cottage that has been home to WA's First Governor, Sir James Stirling, as well as many pioneering families including that of 'Snugglepot and Cuddlepie' creator, May Gibbs.
This adventure lab takes you on a leisurely stroll along the river walk pathway surrounding the immaculate Heritage Gardens of the cottage and introduces (or reacquaints) you with some of the wonderful, quirky characters May Gibbs created in her award-winning children's stories.
We hope you have fun and perhaps take some time to visit the abundance of other attractions in and around this delightful township.

&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
