   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;East Perth Gasworks&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Steel Magnolia&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/829f2b33-494b-4c2f-a164-fc04a0d3cba1"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/829f2b33-494b-4c2f-a164-fc04a0d3cba1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What do the sculptures symbolise?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2ff23c0f-09df-4532-b7db-6fcd73ee6c6c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This location features three sculptures by Jon Denaro. The sculptures are made from industrial ‘junk’ salvaged from the old Perth Gasworks.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/feec1c9c-746e-42fa-afe0-b8e8e46fcb32" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This lab will explore the history of Mardalup Park, formerly the East Perth Gasworks. After completing the lab, a bonus final cache can be accessed using the journal entries.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.05315" lon="115.7573">
  <ele>37.0</ele>
  <time>2024-11-17T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBKGki-03</name>
  <desc>MonumentHillS3H</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3a984bcd-9bc6-4c61-9fb7-0b76801cdeda</url>
  <urlname>Monument Hill : S3 HMAS Parramatta II by crabzy11</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1057" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Monument Hill : S3 HMAS Parramatta II</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>crabzy11</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">crabzy11</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Monument Hill&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;HMAS Parramatta II&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3a984bcd-9bc6-4c61-9fb7-0b76801cdeda"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3a984bcd-9bc6-4c61-9fb7-0b76801cdeda&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;"Greater love has no man than this, that a man lay down his life for his _______”&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c0aad923-58c4-43b1-b690-e47e1d1fe09b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;IN MEMORY OF THE OFFICERS AND MEN OF
HMAS PARRAMATTA (II)
WHICH SAILED FROM THE PORT OF FREMANTLE ON
29 JUNE 1940
AND WAS SUNK IN WATERS OFF TOBRUK ON
27 NOVEMBER 1941
WITH THE LOSS OF 138 LIVES.
24 SURVIVED.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0b98045d-e559-4769-aee0-528f588cd182" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Monument Hill has been a popular lookout over Fremantle since the early days of British colonisation. in the second half of the 19th century, an obelisk au the hills summit provided a tig point to navigators and surveyors. The Hill was then known as Obelisk Hill.

Early in the 20th century the place was made a park and continued as a lookout and beauty spot popular among locals and visitors alike. To commemorate the losses of the 1914-1918 war, the City of Fremantle erected the Fallen Sailors' &amp; Soldiers Memorial in 1928.

The layout of plantings and parkland was established in the 1930s. More memorials were erected after the
1939-45 war. Monument Hill continues to be used for memorial services, as a lookout and for recreation.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.052467" lon="115.75725">
  <ele>52.0</ele>
  <time>2024-11-17T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBKGki-05</name>
  <desc>MonumentHillS5V</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3a984bcd-9bc6-4c61-9fb7-0b76801cdeda</url>
  <urlname>Monument Hill : S5 Vietnam Navy Memorial by crabzy11</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1059" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Monument Hill : S5 Vietnam Navy Memorial</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>crabzy11</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">crabzy11</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Monument Hill&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Vietnam Navy Memorial&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3a984bcd-9bc6-4c61-9fb7-0b76801cdeda"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3a984bcd-9bc6-4c61-9fb7-0b76801cdeda&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;On the side of the memorial what ship is listed above the HMAS Sydney? (One word)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8cf3d192-bbd0-409c-a95b-7e3ffff7b7ad" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The monument is a sandstone and grey granite block which commemorates the Royal Australian Navy's role in the Vietnam War.

The Royal Australian Navy`s role in the Vietnam War is sometimes overlooked by comparison with the Army`s larger numerical involvement. As well as serving in ships deployed to Vietnam naval personnel served in clearance diving teams, the Navy helicopter flight, in logistic support roles and in medical teams. Australian destroyers sailed nearly 400,000 miles in the course of the war and fired more than 100,000 rounds of ammunition. The converted aircraft carrier HMAS SYDNEY carried about 16,000 Australian troops as the famed `Vung Tau Ferry`. Australian Clearance Divers carried out several thousand ship searches looking for bombs and other explosive devices. A total of eight officers and sailors of the RAN were killed and nearly 50 injured in the 10 years of our Navy`s involvement in hostilities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0b98045d-e559-4769-aee0-528f588cd182" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Monument Hill has been a popular lookout over Fremantle since the early days of British colonisation. in the second half of the 19th century, an obelisk au the hills summit provided a tig point to navigators and surveyors. The Hill was then known as Obelisk Hill.

Early in the 20th century the place was made a park and continued as a lookout and beauty spot popular among locals and visitors alike. To commemorate the losses of the 1914-1918 war, the City of Fremantle erected the Fallen Sailors' &amp; Soldiers Memorial in 1928.

The layout of plantings and parkland was established in the 1930s. More memorials were erected after the
1939-45 war. Monument Hill continues to be used for memorial services, as a lookout and for recreation.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.052483" lon="115.756867">
