   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Monument Hill&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Fallen sailors &amp; soldiers memorial&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3a984bcd-9bc6-4c61-9fb7-0b76801cdeda"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3a984bcd-9bc6-4c61-9fb7-0b76801cdeda&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;There is a plaque under the fallen soldiers and sailors memorial sign, the title is “____ of Fremantle” (one word)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6fa1e55e-f2fd-44e2-a216-b4b061dbdce6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;"THE MEMORIAL IS THE FIRST AUSTRALIAN OBJECT THAT WILL MEET THE EYES OF TRAVELLERS COMING FROM THE WESTWARD AND IT WILL SERVE I FOR ALL TIME AS A DIGNIFIED, SILENT, AND REVERENT REMINDER OF THE STRESS AND STRAIN THROUGH WHICH THE PEOPLES OF THE EMPIRE WERE CALLED UPON TO PASS, AS WELLAS A STANDING MEMORIAL TO THE SONS OF FREMANTLE AND ITS DISTRICTS WHO GAVE ALL THEY HAD, EVEN TO LIFE ITSELF, IN SERVICE OF THEIR COUNTRY."&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0b98045d-e559-4769-aee0-528f588cd182" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Monument Hill has been a popular lookout over Fremantle since the early days of British colonisation. in the second half of the 19th century, an obelisk au the hills summit provided a tig point to navigators and surveyors. The Hill was then known as Obelisk Hill.

Early in the 20th century the place was made a park and continued as a lookout and beauty spot popular among locals and visitors alike. To commemorate the losses of the 1914-1918 war, the City of Fremantle erected the Fallen Sailors' &amp; Soldiers Memorial in 1928.

The layout of plantings and parkland was established in the 1930s. More memorials were erected after the
1939-45 war. Monument Hill continues to be used for memorial services, as a lookout and for recreation.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
