  <name>LBEHni-03</name>
  <desc>GracetownS3Huzz</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/82759dca-2020-447d-8654-35e67b7e09f8</url>
  <urlname>Gracetown  : S3 Huzzas by pood</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918746" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Gracetown  : S3 Huzzas</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>pood</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">pood</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Gracetown &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Huzzas&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/82759dca-2020-447d-8654-35e67b7e09f8"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/82759dca-2020-447d-8654-35e67b7e09f8&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Viewing from the Surfboard Seat at this lookout, how many large permanent waves can be seen?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/41ea4329-9414-4ebe-bedb-b25693584e5d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A Surfers’ Playground

The coastal area around Gracetown is home to some of the region’s most famous surf breaks … a playground for surfers of all skill levels.

Learn to Surf

One of the most well known breaks suitable for those learning to surf is “Huzzas”. Located directly out from the “South Point” car park, Huzzas is a small reef break that rolls in over a shallow, weed covered, rocky ledge not far from the shore.

Groms of all ages cut their teeth learning to surf Huzzas as the wave is usually rolling (not dumping), with a long wall left and right. Plenty of time to get to your feet and learn the art of balance.

Wave size varies throughout the year however is generally considered on the small size.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e84b086a-3b84-4b94-b434-3d548f1fcaf4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Time to unwind and enjoy the waters of Gracetown.
A waterfront seaside holiday town, set on the shores of the Indian Ocean where the Cowaramup Brook meets the Ocean.
The waters here at Gracetown are great for swimming, snorkeling, diving and surfing.
There are safe beaches, great surf breaks, interesting reefs for snorkeling and diving.
There’s also a dedicated shark patrol helicopter that patrols the coastline and safety features to warn swimmers or surfers to get out of the water if there is any imminent danger.

There’s also plenty of fishing off the coastline.

&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
