  <desc>GracetownS4Left</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/82759dca-2020-447d-8654-35e67b7e09f8</url>
  <urlname>Gracetown  : S4 Left Handers Beach by pood</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918748" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Gracetown  : S4 Left Handers Beach</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>pood</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">pood</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Gracetown &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Left Handers Beach&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/82759dca-2020-447d-8654-35e67b7e09f8"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/82759dca-2020-447d-8654-35e67b7e09f8&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The name of the Surfer on the surfboard. Two words.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/30155b30-ee2a-4b26-bdbc-048604ddf590" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Left Handers Beach 
Left Handers is a break on the Ellensbrook coast, but it's accessed from the southern end of Gracetown. Along a dirt track off Salter Drive, past Cobblestones break, you'll need to park and continue on foot. It's a lengthy walk, past Ulus and Noisies to get to Lefties.
Producing a fairly easy wave, especially compared with the next break to the south,
It can get crowded here when the surf is up. Lefties is best in offshore winds from the east and swell from the west southwest, with the best time of year for this break being Autumn.

AN OFF SHORE BREEZE
ACROSS AN EMPTY BEACH
CLEANS A ROLLING SWELL
A QUIET SHORE PERFECT REEFS, THE WAVES CAST THEIR SPELL
WE TRAVEL THE WORLD.

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e84b086a-3b84-4b94-b434-3d548f1fcaf4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Time to unwind and enjoy the waters of Gracetown.
A waterfront seaside holiday town, set on the shores of the Indian Ocean where the Cowaramup Brook meets the Ocean.
The waters here at Gracetown are great for swimming, snorkeling, diving and surfing.
There are safe beaches, great surf breaks, interesting reefs for snorkeling and diving.
There’s also a dedicated shark patrol helicopter that patrols the coastline and safety features to warn swimmers or surfers to get out of the water if there is any imminent danger.

There’s also plenty of fishing off the coastline.

&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
