  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918317" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Bayswater Heritage Buildings : S3 Emberson's Butchers</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>familysteiner</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">familysteiner</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Bayswater Heritage Buildings&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Emberson's Butchers&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/01d023b9-9d1e-418f-af96-0892f47d173c"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/01d023b9-9d1e-418f-af96-0892f47d173c&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The staff slept upstairs in order to receive _____ ______ _____. (Three words)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/bcbecfe7-6951-4b7b-bcba-c5d8afa76a8f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This two storey building was built around 1908 by the ‘Emberson Bros’ in a decorative Victorian style. Emberson began working as a butcher at the McLeish Family Butcher Shop on the other side of King William Street before setting up his own business. Staff would sleep upstairs above the shop. 

The building now houses an Antique Shop.  Look for the plaque at your feet outside the front door of the building.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c152985a-03e2-4f2f-a62d-3e05b7c48485" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Despite the establishment of the Swan River Colony in 1829, Bayswater remained relatively undeveloped (other than land lots for gardening and farming) until the early 1900s. Once the Midland Railway Workshops opened, an influx of workers from the eastern states and Great Britain led to the establishment of many more permanent and substantial structures across the locality including a number of commercial properties along King William Street. 

This Adventure Lab will take you to some of the Heritage-listed locations both in the town centre and close to the Swan River. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.919317" lon="115.9126">
