   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Ellenbrook Line: The Unity of Life&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Ballajura Station&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/39744493-7cb2-44ef-abc1-64bad5ff520c"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/39744493-7cb2-44ef-abc1-64bad5ff520c&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The plaque lists several toolmaking practices depicted in the artwork. What is the Noongar name of the toolmaking practice starting with y?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e10a634f-9b85-47d4-835d-d27c8bd580d5" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Locate the plaque and answer the question. The plaque for Ballajura Station is located in multiple locations throughout the station building including nearby to the stairs outside of the fare paid area.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2c0024d4-3a76-4482-a7f4-efb44f8fb9e1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The skylights across the Ellenbrook train line form a suite of artworks dedicated to revealing the interrelationships of all living things across these areas. Marcia McGuire explored the Noongar social and ecological interdependence for Ellenbrook and Ballajura, while Penelope Forlano focused on the ecological interdependence of the flora and fauna for Whiteman Park, Morley and Noranda.

A bonus final cache will be placed for this lab (GCB14B3). The bonus final will be placed after the opening day due to the high volume of visitors on the opening day.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
