   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Fremantle Markets&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Fremantle Markets : Lane way&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/550f8607-2d66-470c-a4e4-dc04664e9979"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/550f8607-2d66-470c-a4e4-dc04664e9979&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;On the south wall is a street sign, Market Lane.  What is the letter/number combo in the bottom right corner?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d4073b20-35ba-4644-8ec2-0e396c7665b6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Here you'll find another entrance, this one to the fruit and veg markets at the rear of the Fremantle Markets.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f7bacd20-6bb0-401a-ac9b-a8daa7ff29d2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Fremantle Markets is a public market located on the corner of South Terrace and Henderson Street, Fremantle, Western Australia.

Built in 1897, it houses over 150 shops for craftspeople, fashion designers, and merchants in the historic Hall, and fresh food producers, vegetable growers and food retailers in The Yard. It is open on Friday, Saturday, Sunday, as well as most public holidays and is a popular Fremantle tourist destination considered "a Fremantle institution".&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
