   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Fremantle Markets&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Fremantle Markets : Corner Stone&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/550f8607-2d66-470c-a4e4-dc04664e9979"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/550f8607-2d66-470c-a4e4-dc04664e9979&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The stone has the date it was laid, what letter is between the month and the year&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4b1a4565-501d-4cd5-9047-cbf98078e0a0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;At this site you'll find the corner stone to the Markets, laid by the Right Honourable Sir John Forrest in 1987.  It has the answer you need&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f7bacd20-6bb0-401a-ac9b-a8daa7ff29d2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Fremantle Markets is a public market located on the corner of South Terrace and Henderson Street, Fremantle, Western Australia.

Built in 1897, it houses over 150 shops for craftspeople, fashion designers, and merchants in the historic Hall, and fresh food producers, vegetable growers and food retailers in The Yard. It is open on Friday, Saturday, Sunday, as well as most public holidays and is a popular Fremantle tourist destination considered "a Fremantle institution".&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
