   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Lightning Swamp Bushland&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Its not a rat!&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a0ad03f8-4823-430a-9d99-001252b2c1a1"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a0ad03f8-4823-430a-9d99-001252b2c1a1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What miss the word - cannot _ _ _ _ _  like rats can.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6b4b521d-08ac-4f94-8302-ffbac17529cf" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Quenda are one of the few native marsupials that can still be seen in Perth's urban bushland reserves.They are vulnerable to predation by feral foxes and cats and Quenda populations can recover where predators are controlled.

There is a physical bonus cache for you to find once you complete this AL. Take note of the code word in each journal. Once you have all five code words, arrange them in alphabetical order and enter them into the Certitude checker (as one long string of letters, no spaces) on the Adventure Lab Bonus Cache page to receive the coordinates. I hope you enjoy your visit to this area.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a30097d7-183f-4ca0-b978-e1b5f972d3bc" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Lightning Swamp Bushland was first reserved in 1963 as part of the initial edition of the Metropolitan Region Scheme. At the time, the surrounding area was undeveloped. The name comes from the lightning-attracting ironstone in the area. The adjacent suburb of Malaga takes its name from the Aboriginal name for ironstone. Prior to 2008, Lightning Swamp Bushland was only an unofficial name for the reserve, with the official name being "Lot 3003 Crown Reserve 46880", but in 2008, the Geographical Names Committee approved a request by the Cities of Bayswater and Swan to rename the reserve to its current name. 

There is a physical bonus cache for you to find once you complete this AL. Take note of the code word in each journal. Once you have all five code words, arrange them in alphabetical order and enter them into the Certitude checker (as one long string of letters, no spaces) on the Adventure Lab Bonus Cache (GCB1BHD) page to receive the coordinates. I hope you enjoy your visit to this area.

