  <urlname>Lightning Swamp Bushland : S5 Wetland in Lightning Swamp Bushland by sevabo</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918371" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Lightning Swamp Bushland : S5 Wetland in Lightning Swamp Bushland</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>sevabo</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">sevabo</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Lightning Swamp Bushland&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Wetland in Lightning Swamp Bushland&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a0ad03f8-4823-430a-9d99-001252b2c1a1"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a0ad03f8-4823-430a-9d99-001252b2c1a1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Can you see the footpath? how many post on there?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e8fe4467-6724-402c-a116-9bd352295d11" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Lightning Swamp has several main water bodies  lying across the site. These dry over summer.  

The perched wetland in the north east is in good condition. It tends to be damp all year round due to its peaty clay base with poor hydraulic conductivity.  Perched wetlands such as this (i.e. wetlands not connected to the ground water) are relatively rare on the Swan Coastal Plain.

There is a physical bonus cache for you to find once you complete this AL. Take note of the code word in each journal. Once you have all five code words, arrange them in alphabetical order and enter them into the Certitude checker (as one long string of letters, no spaces) on the Adventure Lab Bonus Cache page to receive the coordinates. I hope you enjoy your visit to this area.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a30097d7-183f-4ca0-b978-e1b5f972d3bc" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Lightning Swamp Bushland was first reserved in 1963 as part of the initial edition of the Metropolitan Region Scheme. At the time, the surrounding area was undeveloped. The name comes from the lightning-attracting ironstone in the area. The adjacent suburb of Malaga takes its name from the Aboriginal name for ironstone. Prior to 2008, Lightning Swamp Bushland was only an unofficial name for the reserve, with the official name being "Lot 3003 Crown Reserve 46880", but in 2008, the Geographical Names Committee approved a request by the Cities of Bayswater and Swan to rename the reserve to its current name. 

There is a physical bonus cache for you to find once you complete this AL. Take note of the code word in each journal. Once you have all five code words, arrange them in alphabetical order and enter them into the Certitude checker (as one long string of letters, no spaces) on the Adventure Lab Bonus Cache (GCB1BHD) page to receive the coordinates. I hope you enjoy your visit to this area.

https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lightning_Swamp_Bushland &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
