   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Beaches of William Bay&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Greens Pool&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9497964a-0fde-494a-a9bf-a90d856d208c"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9497964a-0fde-494a-a9bf-a90d856d208c&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What type of rock are the huge boulders?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c2d7b25a-531d-47f6-93ef-e75e504ba4b0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Greens Pool lies on the edge of William Bay National Park and is famous for its large  boulders, green turquoise water and white sandy beach. Boulders surround the pool and protect it from the might of the Southern Ocean.
Beautiful at all times of the year, Greens Pool is especially popular in summer. The calm waters are a great spot to explore for the whole family. You can swim, snorkel and relax on the beach or on the rocks overlooking the water.
Why not go for a snorkel to explore the fascinating seascape and see the many fish and sea creatures that live in the calm waters. Zebra fish, silver drummer, six-spined leatherjackets and mosaic sea stars are just some of the creatures you may encounter.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9f12b897-d81f-44f7-80cb-d1bf2a236ef8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;NO DOGS PERMITTED
Windswept headlands, large rocky outcrops, sheltered bays and beaches. William Bay NP has something for everybody.
The turquoise green waters combined with the stunning coastline attract hordes of visitors. 
Enjoy a swim, fish, snorkel, scuba, surf, swim or walk the bush tracks - there's so much to see and explore. 
During school and public holidays its best to arrive early as parking is limited.

Location of the bonus cache will be revealed on completion of the adventure!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
