   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Yanchep Line Extension&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Yanchep Line - Yanchep Station 2&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5dc6b492-e71f-4229-9a66-97b624e373b3"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5dc6b492-e71f-4229-9a66-97b624e373b3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Which artist created this work?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/70207bd0-1e61-43c3-9d9d-5d7db52df659" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;For this answer you will need to exit the station to the south&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a2f74ef6-443b-4ec3-9b44-ce1accb9cf19" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Since we have lived in the northern Burbs the Joondalup line had a mini extension to Butler and then a bigger extension to Yanchep. This extended the line from Clarkson by over 20km and 4 stations. This little AdLab is to celebrate the extension and its renaming to the Yanchep Line.

You will need to access the stations to get the answers to the questions so please only visit during station opening hours. 

***At the time of writing, Transperth are offering free travel to Smartrider holders until Feb 5th 2025. Sundays are usually free also. Free Smartrider cards are currently available on application - see the transperth website for details.*** There has never been a better time to hop on a train and check out these new offerings. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
