   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Yanchep Line Extension&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Yanchep Line - Yanchep Station 1&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5dc6b492-e71f-4229-9a66-97b624e373b3"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5dc6b492-e71f-4229-9a66-97b624e373b3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is written in the top right corner as you look at the mural? (3 words)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/35c1d479-b904-48f1-9272-8c589a40ceb6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;At platform level you are looking for the artwork on the west side of the tracks&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a2f74ef6-443b-4ec3-9b44-ce1accb9cf19" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Since we have lived in the northern Burbs the Joondalup line had a mini extension to Butler and then a bigger extension to Yanchep. This extended the line from Clarkson by over 20km and 4 stations. This little AdLab is to celebrate the extension and its renaming to the Yanchep Line.

You will need to access the stations to get the answers to the questions so please only visit during station opening hours. 

***At the time of writing, Transperth are offering free travel to Smartrider holders until Feb 5th 2025. Sundays are usually free also. Free Smartrider cards are currently available on application - see the transperth website for details.*** There has never been a better time to hop on a train and check out these new offerings. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
