   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Wetland Walk&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Banjo Frogs&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/6a0dd693-f6d2-4d22-8f10-e6ccc0da40ba"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/6a0dd693-f6d2-4d22-8f10-e6ccc0da40ba&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the Western Banjo Frog also known as?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b74c97bf-2b5a-444c-8fa4-d0f1ac96c0bd" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Western Banjo Frog (Limnodynastes dorsalis) is a common frog that can sustain periods of temporary water supply as it burrows into the ground to seek cool and moist areas. The Banjo Frog grows to about seven centimetres in length and on its back has dark brown blotches and a pale yellow line running down the centre. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/cc3fcebf-4b1f-4c38-81f3-7979ae1d4de1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Piney Lakes Wetland Walk. This area was once part of a larger wetland, but due to climate changes and urbanization, it is now a seasonal dampland.

Walk around the natural wetland and through the paperbark forest. See local plants and
animals including birds, quendas and orchids, and listen out for frog calls! 

The walk is approximately 650m which should take about 30mins. The walk contains sandy trails and uneven ground make it unsuitable for prams or wheelchairs. Dogs and bikes are strictly prohibited from going into the natural wetland area. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
