   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;I Crossed The Nullarbor. &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Madura Road House.&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/362fb28b-826c-4ecd-a601-7f3357468c19"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/362fb28b-826c-4ecd-a601-7f3357468c19&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;On the back of the fuel pump there is a sticker with the transport company's 3 initials what are they?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c0549e58-98b1-4fae-ac3b-3a2da536a9b2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;You have successfully crossed the dip and are starting your way up again.

This is another quirky little stop. It is not open 24 hours but the Adventure Lab stage is available 24hrs.

Here you will find a fuel pump and a vehicle that may have used it. Imaging crossing the Nullarbor in a vehicle like that and having to have your fuel pumped by hand.

We are happy those days are gone.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7e4458f8-42e8-484d-8a59-2f5f96e6dfa7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;We enjoy each crossing either East or West and have also enjoyed the different AD Labs placed to break up the drive.
So we thought we would place one to help others enjoy this fantastic drive.
We see many people purchase "I Crossed the Nullarbor" stickers but here is your chance to get an "I crossed the Nullarbor" Post Card.
Each location we checked had at least 3 bars of Telstra service but not sure about other carriers.

We did use 2 points at roughly the same locations as the Nullarbor Links AL as we forgot there were 2 of them and only checked the WA side before creating this one. We have added a note to the completion page so no one forgets.
We hope you enjoy your visits to different popular stops.
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
