   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;I Crossed The Nullarbor. &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Nullarbor Road House&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/362fb28b-826c-4ecd-a601-7f3357468c19"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/362fb28b-826c-4ecd-a601-7f3357468c19&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;1.  What is the second last word on the sign 2. What is on the end of the whales nose? (leave space between words)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f8488bbb-afb3-425e-96af-7ac07201c8b9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Most travellers stop here some for fuel some for a stretch of the legs.

We stopped to add another stage to this Adventure Lab.

There is plenty to see here with the Old Service station, the great mural and of course the Blue Whale.

At the Whale there is a sign where you will find some of the information.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7e4458f8-42e8-484d-8a59-2f5f96e6dfa7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;We enjoy each crossing either East or West and have also enjoyed the different AD Labs placed to break up the drive.
So we thought we would place one to help others enjoy this fantastic drive.
We see many people purchase "I Crossed the Nullarbor" stickers but here is your chance to get an "I crossed the Nullarbor" Post Card.
Each location we checked had at least 3 bars of Telstra service but not sure about other carriers.

We did use 2 points at roughly the same locations as the Nullarbor Links AL as we forgot there were 2 of them and only checked the WA side before creating this one. We have added a note to the completion page so no one forgets.
We hope you enjoy your visits to different popular stops.
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
