   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;I Crossed The Nullarbor. &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Yalata Remembers&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/362fb28b-826c-4ecd-a601-7f3357468c19"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/362fb28b-826c-4ecd-a601-7f3357468c19&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;On one of the plaques on the base of the 3 structures you will find this answer. What did the Yatala Road House  begin it's life as?  (2 words)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/86fb8c02-ef81-4fcc-8267-e50bfba2a01c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Here you will be standing in front of some metal information boards.
The centre board has some interesting but sad history about the Atomic testing and the local residents.

We recommend you spend a moment here and feel one woman's story about the Atomic tests.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7e4458f8-42e8-484d-8a59-2f5f96e6dfa7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;We enjoy each crossing either East or West and have also enjoyed the different AD Labs placed to break up the drive.
So we thought we would place one to help others enjoy this fantastic drive.
We see many people purchase "I Crossed the Nullarbor" stickers but here is your chance to get an "I crossed the Nullarbor" Post Card.
Each location we checked had at least 3 bars of Telstra service but not sure about other carriers.

We did use 2 points at roughly the same locations as the Nullarbor Links AL as we forgot there were 2 of them and only checked the WA side before creating this one. We have added a note to the completion page so no one forgets.
We hope you enjoy your visits to different popular stops.
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
