   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Six Seasons&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Birak&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9f789354-18ec-46b9-9d1d-ed66378255b2"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9f789354-18ec-46b9-9d1d-ed66378255b2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;They would burn the country in ? patterns.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9c4e17b3-8df8-4b8a-87a0-c5395fe229c1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;December &amp; January

Birak season sees the rains ease up and the warm weather really start to take hold. The afternoons are cooled by the sea breezes that abound from the southwest. This was the fire season, a time to burn the country.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/995cf9a9-d1c3-40cb-b161-abed3224971f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The local Nyoongar Aboriginal people living in spiritual harmony with the land travelled back and forth across the coastal plain according to their six seasons. With the change of these seasons their food resources changed as well. Places of fresh water bear special significance, not only for animal and plant communities, but also to the Nyoongar's spiritual connection to 'Boodja' (Earth Mother)

Take a walk and explore the seasons.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.7521" lon="115.793817">
  <ele>21.0</ele>
  <time>2025-02-02T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBHHrd-01</name>
  <desc>HeritageWallS1W</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a4d4eb03-0015-4dc0-9cbf-bd3de2cf4f20</url>
  <urlname>Heritage Wall : S1 Wanneroo Agricultural Show by SpatialRiq</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-802" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Heritage Wall : S1 Wanneroo Agricultural Show</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>SpatialRiq</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">SpatialRiq</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Heritage Wall&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Wanneroo Agricultural Show&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a4d4eb03-0015-4dc0-9cbf-bd3de2cf4f20"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a4d4eb03-0015-4dc0-9cbf-bd3de2cf4f20&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many beams in the picture is the horse jumping over?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ff0e7aec-f53e-4013-a1e7-21e6be0baaa2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Wanneroo Agricultural society and their volunteers have played an important role in the development of the Wanneroo district. The show first held in April 1909 became an important annual social event where local families could meet and display their produce, livestock and craft. Some one hundred years on the show still brings the community together to show case the many aspects of modern day life in the wanneroo area.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/bed97ab0-d89b-4fd5-a3dd-54a08eaa4d47" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Rotary park was developed by the Rotary club of Waneroo in cooperation with the Shire of Wanneroo on 10th November 1979.

The Heritage Wall is a community peoject to celebrate the centenary of federation and was unveiled 9th September 2001.
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
