   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Heritage Wall&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Industry and Commerce&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a4d4eb03-0015-4dc0-9cbf-bd3de2cf4f20"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a4d4eb03-0015-4dc0-9cbf-bd3de2cf4f20&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What number is on the roof of the race car?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/bf9d4154-d7bb-4321-ab22-9278506102c3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;From primary production and humble beginnings, the city of Wanneroo now offers a wide variety of primary and secondary industries as well as commercial financial government agencies and services.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/bed97ab0-d89b-4fd5-a3dd-54a08eaa4d47" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Rotary park was developed by the Rotary club of Waneroo in cooperation with the Shire of Wanneroo on 10th November 1979.

