 <wpt lat="-35.025683" lon="117.897083">
  <ele>152.0</ele>
  <time>2025-02-02T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBJ8Ma-01</name>
  <desc>ANZACMemoria110</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f0c3fdb0-8900-4662-b70e-cb286e4b6e0c</url>
  <urlname>ANZAC Memorial : S1 The 10th Light Horse Regiment by MummaBear5</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918532" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>ANZAC Memorial : S1 The 10th Light Horse Regiment</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>MummaBear5</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">MummaBear5</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;ANZAC Memorial&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The 10th Light Horse Regiment&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f0c3fdb0-8900-4662-b70e-cb286e4b6e0c"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f0c3fdb0-8900-4662-b70e-cb286e4b6e0c&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;In what year did the 10th Light Horse Regiment disband?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/cbed753e-6fd3-4983-b0c7-202d75b98cb4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
The 10th Light Horse Regiment was the only regiment of mounted
infantry recruited in Western Australia during World War I
Raised in October 1914, the regiment formed part of the 3rd Light
Horse Brigade and served at Gallipoli as infantry in the Australian and
New Zealand Army Corps
The regiment participated in the disastrous charge at the Nek on 7
August 1915.Their courageous actions were immortalised in Peter
Weir's film, Gallipoli. At the end of August the survivors took part in
the fight for Hill 60, where Second Lieutenant Hugo Throssell earned
the Victoria Cross.
After Gallipoli the regiment served in the Middle East as part of the
ANZAC Mounted Division and. later the Australian Mounted Division
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0198e668-c06c-497d-ab67-220af0f041fe" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Enjoy an informative walk at the ANZAC Memorial, the site of the first Dawn Service.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.9524" lon="115.784733">
  <ele>16.0</ele>
  <time>2025-02-08T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LB6wQJ-05</name>
  <desc>WASportsVenues5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cf865ebe-2e5a-448a-bb62-82715ec2a2cc</url>
  <urlname>WA Sports Venues : S5 WAIS by J2V</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918493" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WA Sports Venues : S5 WAIS</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>J2V</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">J2V</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WA Sports Venues&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;WAIS&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cf865ebe-2e5a-448a-bb62-82715ec2a2cc"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cf865ebe-2e5a-448a-bb62-82715ec2a2cc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Outside the WAIS building there are three rows of wooden posts. How many posts in the shortest row?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/42ef52ed-f1df-4089-a848-386d5266d2f4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In 2015, the WA Institute of Sport moved from the front of the HPC complex to the current location. It is a hi-tech facility for high performance testing and training, athlete recovery and rehabilitation. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6c9238ae-200c-4c14-9bb3-3be0e4166fb6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This adventure takes you around some of the State sports venues in Mt Claremont. The five stops are at Bendat Basketball Centre, WA Athletics Stadium, Perth High Performance Centre, WA Institute of Sport and an unusual memorial in the bush. 

You can drive between the locations or take a walk. For an added challenge, find the path through the bush that links the basketball centre to the oval (and the WAIS building). After completing the adventure there is a bonus traditional geocache to fine nearby.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.948483" lon="115.785717">
  <ele>10.0</ele>
  <time>2025-02-08T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LB6wQJ-04</name>
  <desc>WASportsVenues4</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cf865ebe-2e5a-448a-bb62-82715ec2a2cc</url>
  <urlname>WA Sports Venues : S4 Bendat Basketball Centre by J2V</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918501" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WA Sports Venues : S4 Bendat Basketball Centre</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>J2V</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">J2V</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WA Sports Venues&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Bendat Basketball Centre&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cf865ebe-2e5a-448a-bb62-82715ec2a2cc"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cf865ebe-2e5a-448a-bb62-82715ec2a2cc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many tall grey masts are there outside the building?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/cac4f4a1-b54e-4afd-a071-9e01c4f3a308" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The basketball centre opened in 2010 and replaced the old Perry Lakes basketball stadium. It is the home of local NBL team the Perth Wildcats and caters for community basketball, netball, volleyball and badminton. A prominent architectural feature is the masts and cables on the outside of the building.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6c9238ae-200c-4c14-9bb3-3be0e4166fb6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This adventure takes you around some of the State sports venues in Mt Claremont. The five stops are at Bendat Basketball Centre, WA Athletics Stadium, Perth High Performance Centre, WA Institute of Sport and an unusual memorial in the bush. 

You can drive between the locations or take a walk. For an added challenge, find the path through the bush that links the basketball centre to the oval (and the WAIS building). After completing the adventure there is a bonus traditional geocache to fine nearby.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.9493" lon="115.784117">
  <ele>22.0</ele>
  <time>2025-02-08T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LB6wQJ-03</name>
  <desc>WASportsVenues3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cf865ebe-2e5a-448a-bb62-82715ec2a2cc</url>
  <urlname>WA Sports Venues : S3 Memorial arch by J2V</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918499" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WA Sports Venues : S3 Memorial arch</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>J2V</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">J2V</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WA Sports Venues&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Memorial arch&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cf865ebe-2e5a-448a-bb62-82715ec2a2cc"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cf865ebe-2e5a-448a-bb62-82715ec2a2cc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;On the smaller post, what does the word Koora mean in English (two words)?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7b2c5b9a-e2c2-436a-bb49-650503c91685" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This memorial arch in Noongar language at the edge of the bush is a bit of a mystery. It is located away from the nearby buildings, does not have an interpretative sign and is not part of a marked walk.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6c9238ae-200c-4c14-9bb3-3be0e4166fb6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This adventure takes you around some of the State sports venues in Mt Claremont. The five stops are at Bendat Basketball Centre, WA Athletics Stadium, Perth High Performance Centre, WA Institute of Sport and an unusual memorial in the bush. 

You can drive between the locations or take a walk. For an added challenge, find the path through the bush that links the basketball centre to the oval (and the WAIS building). After completing the adventure there is a bonus traditional geocache to fine nearby.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.952583" lon="115.78125">
  <ele>18.0</ele>
