   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Cockburn Memorial Walk&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;North Borneo&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bc5b718a-92a7-4c2e-b83d-5f492f7ac708"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bc5b718a-92a7-4c2e-b83d-5f492f7ac708&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many Australian soldiers were killed in action in the final assault in Borneo?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ab170447-007c-4141-905f-e9a634777fc6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;North Borneo was the location of the final Australian led assault against the Japanese in the Second World War. Australians landed and attacked the stronghold of North Borneo in May 1945. With the Japanese facing total defeat, they fought tenaciously, often launching suicide attacks on Australian Forces. Much of the fighting was at close quarters, with hand-to-hand combat in the thick steaming jungle.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/009c0441-3e95-4e68-ad10-2f810fb4e0cc" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Cockburn's Memorial Walk is set along Veterans Avenue close to Cockburn Arc Sporting Arena.
The walk consists of 36 informative plinths located on both sides of Veteran Avenue.
The plinths are dedicated to a particular conflict or theatre of war in which Australian Forces fought.

Take the time to learn a little bit of our military history as you walk along Veterans Avenue. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
