   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Cockburn Memorial Walk&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Fear of invasion and the enemy within &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bc5b718a-92a7-4c2e-b83d-5f492f7ac708"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bc5b718a-92a7-4c2e-b83d-5f492f7ac708&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;In what year did the men of the Returned Services League Hamilton Hill subbranch form the Volunteer Defence Corps (VDC)?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a5240c64-56dd-4c12-90b6-88a25fd937ae" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Located outside the main entry of Cockburn Arc is an informative plinth about the history of Cockburn preparing for invasion and the fear of war that gripped the locals.
 &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/009c0441-3e95-4e68-ad10-2f810fb4e0cc" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Cockburn's Memorial Walk is set along Veterans Avenue close to Cockburn Arc Sporting Arena.
The walk consists of 36 informative plinths located on both sides of Veteran Avenue.
The plinths are dedicated to a particular conflict or theatre of war in which Australian Forces fought.

Take the time to learn a little bit of our military history as you walk along Veterans Avenue. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
