  <desc>KarrathasArtwo5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3750a827-d411-443c-8ac0-1f30cd3809e3</url>
  <urlname>Karratha’s Artwork : S5 Energy by dimor</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918541" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Karratha’s Artwork : S5 Energy</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>dimor</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">dimor</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Karratha’s Artwork&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Energy&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3750a827-d411-443c-8ac0-1f30cd3809e3"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3750a827-d411-443c-8ac0-1f30cd3809e3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The name mentioned on line three (full name)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/54bfe4fa-ebf1-4faa-9877-118657008101" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;ENERGEIA

The successive stages in the flow of energy through the biological microcosm.

The artists are Joan Walsh-Smith and Charles Smith

It was installed in November 2012 as part of the Dampier Highway Streetscape upgrade project.

Parking is available not to far from the rock that contains the required information &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/604f02ae-3076-43d4-a494-25bc6a5b5532" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Driving and walking around town I’ve come across different forms of art.
This AdLab is featuring three along Dampier Highway that you can’t miss, one on Tank Hill and the other in a little park that is very easy to miss.

Karratha is the first city in the North West region of Western Australia.
Karratha was named after a pastoral station in the area and was established in 1968 to accommodate the processing and exploration workforce of the Hamersley Iron mining company and, in the 1980s the petroleum and liquified natural gas operations of the North West Shelf Venture.

On the first of July 2014 Karratha became a city. It covers an area of fifteen thousand square kilometres and has a population of around 20,000.
Karratha has the expected facilities of a major regional area with shopping centres, health campus and medical services, both public and private schools, airport, restaurants and cafes, hotels/motels and an arts precinct.

The weather here is divine most of the year except when the humidity is unbearable and when cyclones come through (mostly Nov - Mar). Plenty of warm sunny weather to enjoy with the laid back lifestyle ?? &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
