   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Karratha’s Artwork&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Follow the Arrows&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3750a827-d411-443c-8ac0-1f30cd3809e3"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3750a827-d411-443c-8ac0-1f30cd3809e3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the artwork&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6ec57827-3936-4099-b5cf-d6bf290b19ef" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is one of the Dampier Highway artworks/sculptures that you can’t miss.

A navigational landmark for a remarkable land.
The artist is Rick Vermeer and was installed in November 2012 as part of the Dampier Highway Streetscape upgrade project.

Please park on the side street, Shimmon Place and make your way to the rock&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/604f02ae-3076-43d4-a494-25bc6a5b5532" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Driving and walking around town I’ve come across different forms of art.
