  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/91681382-4532-4138-9269-394c51328bdb</url>
  <urlname>[L] Footsteps in time : S3 Discovery of Gold - 1885-95 by Kyzabra</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918575" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>[L] Footsteps in time : S3 Discovery of Gold - 1885-95</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Kyzabra</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Kyzabra</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Footsteps in time&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Discovery of Gold - 1885-95&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/91681382-4532-4138-9269-394c51328bdb"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/91681382-4532-4138-9269-394c51328bdb&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What type of hat is he wearing ?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/307b8e4a-5a91-4491-9b26-ce779849cd83" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The gold boom came to WA. Money to be had.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/40b91d62-e11a-4ade-b2eb-6a839b43f6eb" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;NOTE : If your GPS signal is not working here, I have put large geo-fences in. Start at the man, furthest from the road.

The sculpture group commemorates the 175th anniversary of Western Australia and symbolises the business people who have built this thriving CBD
The five men are: the Dutch from the 17th century, who first explored the region; Anglo-Celtic (the English), who colonised the Swan River Settlement, now Perth; the gold rush days of the mid to late 19th century, which brought money and people to Western Australia; the post Second World War days, when the state again experienced a large influx of people; and last, but certainly not least, the busy and important business man of the early 21st century.
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
