   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Footsteps in time&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Post WW2 European Immigration 1945-55&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/91681382-4532-4138-9269-394c51328bdb"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/91681382-4532-4138-9269-394c51328bdb&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many buttons in total on both the jacket and vest (add together)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e0ee6b7a-7651-4d66-9160-3c0c6383f355" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Settlement was going full steam ahead during this period.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/40b91d62-e11a-4ade-b2eb-6a839b43f6eb" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;NOTE : If your GPS signal is not working here, I have put large geo-fences in. Start at the man, furthest from the road.

The sculpture group commemorates the 175th anniversary of Western Australia and symbolises the business people who have built this thriving CBD
The five men are: the Dutch from the 17th century, who first explored the region; Anglo-Celtic (the English), who colonised the Swan River Settlement, now Perth; the gold rush days of the mid to late 19th century, which brought money and people to Western Australia; the post Second World War days, when the state again experienced a large influx of people; and last, but certainly not least, the busy and important business man of the early 21st century.
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
