   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Timed Stops on the 915&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Fremantle &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1e7df1ce-a3b2-4306-bf9a-eaebd772501a"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1e7df1ce-a3b2-4306-bf9a-eaebd772501a&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What line can you transfer for here?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4159724e-730e-42bb-89c1-f8a39d1e9c75" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to Fremantle, where you will start the epic journey or finishing the wonderful adventure on the 915. You can transfer for the Fremantle line here, also the other high frequency routes such as 910.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/54f60cc4-75cd-4e8c-a61e-455f23fb6068" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Timed stops on the 915. An introduction to the Perth’s high frequency routes. The reason for creating this ad-lab  is to admire how wonderful it is to have a high frequency route run along here, beautiful communities along the way from Bull Creek to Fremantle. Its road design with bike lanes is pretty cool with a small median in the middle. Great!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
