 <wpt lat="-32.042433" lon="115.973133">
  <ele>9.0</ele>
  <time>2025-03-17T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBJhqP-01</name>
  <desc>WalkThroughT863</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/990f3c4f-5be2-48a8-9c85-5e89ab59d41d</url>
  <urlname>A Walk through Time in Kenwick Pioneer Cemetery : S1 Clue 1: 1863- First Public Land by Paskersfind</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918629" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>A Walk through Time in Kenwick Pioneer Cemetery : S1 Clue 1: 1863- First Public Land</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Paskersfind</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Paskersfind</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;A Walk through Time in Kenwick Pioneer Cemetery&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Clue 1: 1863- First Public Land&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/990f3c4f-5be2-48a8-9c85-5e89ab59d41d"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/990f3c4f-5be2-48a8-9c85-5e89ab59d41d&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Find the word on the plaque with a meaning similar to the word  AREA. [6 letters]&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b0e74b95-8e89-4db9-b489-146bdcde503a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The first clue requires seekers to proceed along the clearly defined path through the cemetery until you arrive at a large rock describing the original intended purpose of this land. A plaque acknowledges the generosity of local residents whose efforts and donations contributed to the growth and development of the area. The answer is one of the words written somewhere on the plaque.  &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/418feb75-b387-410e-bdca-56af8416dda4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is not a ghost story. Dylan and Kitty definitely do not believe in ghosts but are still reluctant to pass the cemetery gates as this memorial to the pioneers is rumoured to be haunted by a headless rider. Yikes!  However, they need to find crucial information in order to solve a mystery puzzle left by their granddad inside an old book they discovered on the musty, dusty bookshelf in his long abandoned home.  They need help and this is where you come into play as determined and dauntless adlabers.

The clues they found take them on a walk through time up the central cemetery path that features large granite rocks standing like timeless sentinels guarding this local history. Find the path, take the walk and work out the required five words prerequisite to solving the puzzle.

If you so desire, solve the puzzle and find the hidden cache so that these kids can relax get back to renovating the home.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.0424" lon="115.97305">
  <ele>9.0</ele>
  <time>2025-03-17T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBJhqP-02</name>
  <desc>WalkThroughT900</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/990f3c4f-5be2-48a8-9c85-5e89ab59d41d</url>
  <urlname>A Walk through Time in Kenwick Pioneer Cemetery : S2 Clue 2: 1865 - 1900 First Public Buildings by Paskersfind</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918631" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>A Walk through Time in Kenwick Pioneer Cemetery : S2 Clue 2: 1865 - 1900 First Public Buildings</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Paskersfind</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Paskersfind</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;A Walk through Time in Kenwick Pioneer Cemetery&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Clue 2: 1865 - 1900 First Public Buildings&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/990f3c4f-5be2-48a8-9c85-5e89ab59d41d"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/990f3c4f-5be2-48a8-9c85-5e89ab59d41d&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Find the word on the plaque that can be commonly found in front of these other words: Media, Security, Science  [6 letters] &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/40d66342-278c-4d7e-bcf8-980cf492d421" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The next clue takes you further along the path. Another large rock holds information about the number and variety of public buildings that once adorned this site and illustrates the importance of such amenities to a growing community. The clue requires you to closely examine the plaque and find another key word to solve the puzzle.

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/418feb75-b387-410e-bdca-56af8416dda4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is not a ghost story. Dylan and Kitty definitely do not believe in ghosts but are still reluctant to pass the cemetery gates as this memorial to the pioneers is rumoured to be haunted by a headless rider. Yikes!  However, they need to find crucial information in order to solve a mystery puzzle left by their granddad inside an old book they discovered on the musty, dusty bookshelf in his long abandoned home.  They need help and this is where you come into play as determined and dauntless adlabers.

The clues they found take them on a walk through time up the central cemetery path that features large granite rocks standing like timeless sentinels guarding this local history. Find the path, take the walk and work out the required five words prerequisite to solving the puzzle.

If you so desire, solve the puzzle and find the hidden cache so that these kids can relax get back to renovating the home.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.0423" lon="115.973133">
  <ele>9.0</ele>
  <time>2025-03-17T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBJhqP-03</name>
  <desc>WalkThroughT870</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/990f3c4f-5be2-48a8-9c85-5e89ab59d41d</url>
  <urlname>A Walk through Time in Kenwick Pioneer Cemetery : S3 Clue 3: 1870- First Local Government by Paskersfind</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918633" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>A Walk through Time in Kenwick Pioneer Cemetery : S3 Clue 3: 1870- First Local Government</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Paskersfind</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Paskersfind</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;A Walk through Time in Kenwick Pioneer Cemetery&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Clue 3: 1870- First Local Government&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/990f3c4f-5be2-48a8-9c85-5e89ab59d41d"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/990f3c4f-5be2-48a8-9c85-5e89ab59d41d&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Find the word on the plaque that is an anagram of  "ITEM"  [4 letters]&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/dda0f5cc-b992-4ca6-8866-12f3ebb6e85e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;As you continue to walk through time along the path, you will arrive at another large rock which lists the members of the first local government "Roads Board" as they were once known.  The next clue suggests another word able to be found somewhere on this plaque. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/418feb75-b387-410e-bdca-56af8416dda4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is not a ghost story. Dylan and Kitty definitely do not believe in ghosts but are still reluctant to pass the cemetery gates as this memorial to the pioneers is rumoured to be haunted by a headless rider. Yikes!  However, they need to find crucial information in order to solve a mystery puzzle left by their granddad inside an old book they discovered on the musty, dusty bookshelf in his long abandoned home.  They need help and this is where you come into play as determined and dauntless adlabers.

The clues they found take them on a walk through time up the central cemetery path that features large granite rocks standing like timeless sentinels guarding this local history. Find the path, take the walk and work out the required five words prerequisite to solving the puzzle.

If you so desire, solve the puzzle and find the hidden cache so that these kids can relax get back to renovating the home.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
