   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;A Walk through Time in Kenwick Pioneer Cemetery&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Clue 5: 1900 - The End of an Era&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/990f3c4f-5be2-48a8-9c85-5e89ab59d41d"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/990f3c4f-5be2-48a8-9c85-5e89ab59d41d&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Find the  word on the plaque that is opposite of "BOUGHT" [4 letters]                                                                  &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4fb76233-110d-4d7f-b6bb-39704073a71f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;As you reach the end of the gravel pathway, the final large rock stands majestically and laments the end of an era and the end of your walk through time. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/418feb75-b387-410e-bdca-56af8416dda4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is not a ghost story. Dylan and Kitty definitely do not believe in ghosts but are still reluctant to pass the cemetery gates as this memorial to the pioneers is rumoured to be haunted by a headless rider. Yikes!  However, they need to find crucial information in order to solve a mystery puzzle left by their granddad inside an old book they discovered on the musty, dusty bookshelf in his long abandoned home.  They need help and this is where you come into play as determined and dauntless adlabers.

The clues they found take them on a walk through time up the central cemetery path that features large granite rocks standing like timeless sentinels guarding this local history. Find the path, take the walk and work out the required five words prerequisite to solving the puzzle.

If you so desire, solve the puzzle and find the hidden cache so that these kids can relax get back to renovating the home.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
