   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Chancellor Park - Seasons&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;October / November&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/658abece-e318-43aa-a7e4-20e9fd5bbf96"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/658abece-e318-43aa-a7e4-20e9fd5bbf96&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;During the Kambarang season longer ...&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/900b88e9-a722-4f50-a01a-f9acc0cada3f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;October / November is Kambarang season!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/257404ae-b3fc-45e9-87fd-0b147300d46f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Chancellor Park serves to conserve the regions native vegetation and local biodiversity. This 24 hectare park provides a valuable habitat for many plants and animals.

In the Southwest of Australia, the Noongar seasonal calendar includes six different seasons in a yearly cycle.  These are Birak, Bunuru, Djeran, Makuru, Djilba and Kambarang.  Each of the six seasons represents and explains the seasonal changes we see annually.

This walk will take you to information on each of the season.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
