  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/77a6ca57-da0c-445e-a0b6-455c666d73a2</url>
  <urlname>Axford Park : S4 Mount Hawthorn War Memorial by Jack_Cheng</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918681" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Axford Park : S4 Mount Hawthorn War Memorial</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Jack_Cheng</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Jack_Cheng</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Axford Park&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Mount Hawthorn War Memorial&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/77a6ca57-da0c-445e-a0b6-455c666d73a2"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/77a6ca57-da0c-445e-a0b6-455c666d73a2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;When was Thomas Axford awarded the Victoria Cross?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/716dafaa-f3c1-409c-8a4a-707b655e88aa" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The War Memorial commemorates those who have served in the various conflicts in which Australia has been involved.

On the 13th April 2015, two plaques were unveiled on the memorial to commemorate the centenary of ANZAC. One plaque commemorates City of Vincent residents who served in World War One while the other commemorates Thomas Axford who was awarded the Victoria Cross for conspicuous bravery during World War One and after whom the park is named.

Source: https://monumentaustralia.org.au/themes/conflict/multiple/display/93339-mount-hawthorn-war-memorial&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2e2eda4e-aaf0-4e68-8ba7-b672802dcc31" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Axford Park is at the north end of Oxford Street. It is a piece of  quite land between the Mount Hawthorn Hawaiian's Mezz and  Oxford Street business precinct. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
