   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Axford Park&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Plaque&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/77a6ca57-da0c-445e-a0b6-455c666d73a2"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/77a6ca57-da0c-445e-a0b6-455c666d73a2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Which street did Thomas Axford live?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5da22f15-e50a-4418-89d6-ffeb81161438" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The name of Axford Park is not mis-spelled of Oxford. It is to remember a person who lived nearby.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2e2eda4e-aaf0-4e68-8ba7-b672802dcc31" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Axford Park is at the north end of Oxford Street. It is a piece of  quite land between the Mount Hawthorn Hawaiian's Mezz and  Oxford Street business precinct. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
