 <wpt lat="-32.053117" lon="115.740817">
  <ele>1.0</ele>
  <time>2025-05-25T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBH7ZR-04</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa014</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/dfc54184-8622-46d7-b5e0-287e85178253</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #010 : S4 Whats happened in Perth by neva2old</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1371" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #010 : S4 Whats happened in Perth</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>neva2old</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">neva2old</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #010&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Whats happened in Perth&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/dfc54184-8622-46d7-b5e0-287e85178253"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/dfc54184-8622-46d7-b5e0-287e85178253&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name for where the money is made in Perth?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f87c8f23-7c23-4579-a426-c56de978ddd3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Perth was founded by Captain James Stirling in 1829 as the administrative centre of the Swan River Colony. The city is situated on the traditional lands of the Whadjuk Noongar people, where Aboriginal Australians have lived for at least 48,000 years. Perth was named after the city of Perth in Scotland.[6] Initially established as a free settlement, the colony accepted transported convicts from 1850 to supply labour for public works and construction. Perth was proclaimed as a city by Queen Victoria in 1856.
Perth hosted the Commonwealth Games in 1962
Perth is also known for being the most Isolated capital city in the world&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/15fa4bb5-6e43-4bed-832c-d2155620ecd6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.0514" lon="115.74075">
  <ele>2.0</ele>
  <time>2025-05-25T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBpPPR-01</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa00M</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/be0c66e6-529c-458b-afce-c98190d341bb</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #005 : S1 A Moral Agent for Rottnest by cravo10</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918690" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #005 : S1 A Moral Agent for Rottnest</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>cravo10</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">cravo10</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #005&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;A Moral Agent for Rottnest &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/be0c66e6-529c-458b-afce-c98190d341bb"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/be0c66e6-529c-458b-afce-c98190d341bb&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;In what Year was he sent? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/dfebfdbe-f664-4540-94bc-9b01bf872c77" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Mr Francis Armstrong was sent to Rottnest Island as a Storekeeper and Moral Agent with the task to 'improve the habits and morals of the prisoners'. For accommodation, Armstrong
partially built his own cottage, but resided in it only for a short period. The cottage then became the home of Captain Back, the first Pilot of Rottnest's newly established Pilot Service.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/17b1a746-34b2-4c7f-8ac4-919cca9372ac" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

If you travel over to Rottnest you can take many guided tours and learn about the history of the place. 
close to the ferry terminal is some of the oldest buildings on the Island and this question set is taken from the information on the buildings. The image within each question is a reference to where all the volunteers meet to start the guided tours.  

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.051383" lon="115.740683">
  <ele>2.0</ele>
  <time>2025-05-25T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBpPPR-02</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa00e</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/be0c66e6-529c-458b-afce-c98190d341bb</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #005 : S2 A second Home for the Superintendent by cravo10</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918692" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #005 : S2 A second Home for the Superintendent</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>cravo10</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">cravo10</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #005&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;A second Home for the Superintendent &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/be0c66e6-529c-458b-afce-c98190d341bb"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/be0c66e6-529c-458b-afce-c98190d341bb&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;This cottage was built in what year? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e5907898-d2dd-4e02-a403-c4513b8ef730" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Superintendent Vincent, after his first home was taken over by the Governor for use as a summer residence. Following Vincent's retirement in 1867, the cottage accommodated the Island's Store Keeper, the Colonial Secretary, and the Officer-in-Charge during World War I. It later became the Island Manager's house and derives its name from this period.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/17b1a746-34b2-4c7f-8ac4-919cca9372ac" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

If you travel over to Rottnest you can take many guided tours and learn about the history of the place. 
close to the ferry terminal is some of the oldest buildings on the Island and this question set is taken from the information on the buildings. The image within each question is a reference to where all the volunteers meet to start the guided tours.  

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.05135" lon="115.740617">
  <ele>1.0</ele>
  <time>2025-05-25T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBpPPR-03</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa00r</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/be0c66e6-529c-458b-afce-c98190d341bb</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #005 : S3 Quarters for the Prison Guards by cravo10</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918694" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #005 : S3 Quarters for the Prison Guards</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>cravo10</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">cravo10</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #005&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Quarters for the Prison Guards &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/be0c66e6-529c-458b-afce-c98190d341bb"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/be0c66e6-529c-458b-afce-c98190d341bb&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;In what year was this building Built &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f0d111ce-2a8f-4eac-a2eb-f957e5acd736" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This building originally served as the military barracks and accommodated the soldiers who guarded the Aboriginal prison. When a new prison was built in 1864, the guards were replaced by resident prison warders. To accommodate them and their families, the Barracks building was converted into two cottages. A final extension in 1898 created a third cottage to house the Island's school teacher.
The&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/17b1a746-34b2-4c7f-8ac4-919cca9372ac" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

If you travel over to Rottnest you can take many guided tours and learn about the history of the place. 
close to the ferry terminal is some of the oldest buildings on the Island and this question set is taken from the information on the buildings. The image within each question is a reference to where all the volunteers meet to start the guided tours.  

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
