   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #010&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Whats up North of Western Australia&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/dfc54184-8622-46d7-b5e0-287e85178253"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/dfc54184-8622-46d7-b5e0-287e85178253&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The ocean around Port Hedland is also home to what Fauna?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9f2c9c50-89b1-4913-b928-1a2667a5ec52" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Port of Hedland lies on the northwestern coast in the Pilbara region of Western Australia and boasts of being the largest bulk export facility in the world, mainly dealing with shipments of iron ore. Other commodities handled at the port include ammonium, fuel oils, lithium, project cargo, breakbulk like cement, Roro, conventional cargo, salt, sulphuric acid, copper, chromite and livestock.

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/15fa4bb5-6e43-4bed-832c-d2155620ecd6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.051317" lon="115.740583">
  <ele>2.0</ele>
  <time>2025-05-25T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBpPPR-04</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa00L</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/be0c66e6-529c-458b-afce-c98190d341bb</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #005 : S4 A Lucrative Business by cravo10</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918696" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #005 : S4 A Lucrative Business</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>cravo10</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">cravo10</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #005&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;A Lucrative Business &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/be0c66e6-529c-458b-afce-c98190d341bb"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/be0c66e6-529c-458b-afce-c98190d341bb&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How Many Salt lakes? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/326c928c-5427-48c6-9605-cd36a08f7d7d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Rottnest Island has ? salt lakes, each with a salt content four to six times greater than that of sea water. The two shallowest lakes dry up every summer and expose a thick crust of rock salt that is easily collected. For many years Rottnest was the only source of salt in Western Australia, and this building was used to store the salt before it was shipped to the mainland.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/17b1a746-34b2-4c7f-8ac4-919cca9372ac" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

If you travel over to Rottnest you can take many guided tours and learn about the history of the place. 
close to the ferry terminal is some of the oldest buildings on the Island and this question set is taken from the information on the buildings. The image within each question is a reference to where all the volunteers meet to start the guided tours.  

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
