   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #005&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Rottnest voluntary guides association&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/be0c66e6-529c-458b-afce-c98190d341bb"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/be0c66e6-529c-458b-afce-c98190d341bb&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;In what year did the association start &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/685474e5-3f7a-4eb3-8261-536cf27826db" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Established to promote an increased awareness and appreciation of the natural environment and historical significance of Rottnest Island:
?- Daily Tours &amp; Information Services
- ??Extra Holiday Activities
??- Special Request Tours for Schools, Corporate and Social Groups&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/17b1a746-34b2-4c7f-8ac4-919cca9372ac" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

If you travel over to Rottnest you can take many guided tours and learn about the history of the place. 
close to the ferry terminal is some of the oldest buildings on the Island and this question set is taken from the information on the buildings. The image within each question is a reference to where all the volunteers meet to start the guided tours.  

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
