   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #001&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Quokka facts 5&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/53450e84-8aa1-4283-a32c-961e253fa42c"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/53450e84-8aa1-4283-a32c-961e253fa42c&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Where else on mainland Western Australia are quokkas found?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a7ce2a40-2c75-4dae-8d63-15aa1cff784d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art - Please join in by contacting WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d944e45d-11a0-4e99-b9b5-0cd5a4f8522d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows you to solve all the AdLabs from the docks from the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal. 
