 <wpt lat="-32.051283" lon="115.740317">
  <ele>1.0</ele>
  <time>2025-05-25T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LB5h1h-02</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa00t</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/07893820-f6f4-49be-b63b-56707407500a</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #006 : S2 Project APE by Leg5</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918706" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #006 : S2 Project APE</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Leg5</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Leg5</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #006&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Project APE&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/07893820-f6f4-49be-b63b-56707407500a"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/07893820-f6f4-49be-b63b-56707407500a&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many APE caches were hidden in Australia?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e10839d6-814d-475a-a170-9749c5063da2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Also known as Ape caches, these are a special type of traditional cache that were hidden in conjunction with 20th Century Fox and Groundspeak to promote the 2001 remake of Planet of the Apes. There were 14 APE geocaches placed around the world and each one contained a prop from the film. As of 2023, only 2 APE caches are still active with one near Seattle, Washington ('Tunnel of Light', GC1169) and the other in Brazil ('Southern Bowl', GCC67). &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/668fd45f-bcf0-4d8a-9e69-a0f259cd0073" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
