   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #024&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Netball&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/df84ea67-fd3a-4119-8bb4-24691e566263"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/df84ea67-fd3a-4119-8bb4-24691e566263&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the WA women's Netball team?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/eb2bdfe9-a8d9-4760-8cc6-cc434c3a021a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Netball is another sport that our Kids have grown up playing in both school and weekend sport.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0e324823-2b50-47b8-a7e6-c980b83ee445" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.


To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com

