   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #016&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Shell Beach&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/459e1a0c-90ec-4bdd-9c44-794b98a674b9"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/459e1a0c-90ec-4bdd-9c44-794b98a674b9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Where is this special beach located?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a21fe739-fe6c-4ab4-ad9c-7f1bedc17df1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ever been to a beach with no sand? Well this one true to its name is covered in teeny little shells. The contrast of the bleached shells on a sunny day gives the water the most beautiful aqua blue colour.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7bc2299a-0e5f-4115-bfb3-5da757968c47" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka
off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs
to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry
Terminal.

