   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #016&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Cable Beach&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/459e1a0c-90ec-4bdd-9c44-794b98a674b9"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/459e1a0c-90ec-4bdd-9c44-794b98a674b9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Where is this popular beach located?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/714ad2af-d0ac-4662-b87e-0d4424d3ef2b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Magnificent sunsets, warm waters and a 22km stretch of white sand makes this beach an international tourist favourite.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7bc2299a-0e5f-4115-bfb3-5da757968c47" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka
off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs
to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry
Terminal.

This Adventure Lab is themed on the beautiful beaches of WA&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
