 <wpt lat="-32.0524" lon="115.74085">
  <ele>2.0</ele>
  <time>2025-05-26T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBCv5C-01</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa027</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d918570b-3b7b-4a91-bc60-95620a86add5</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #027 : S1 Weird Place Names - Dog Swamp by chickenhawk07</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918719" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #027 : S1 Weird Place Names - Dog Swamp</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>chickenhawk07</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">chickenhawk07</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #027&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Weird Place Names - Dog Swamp&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d918570b-3b7b-4a91-bc60-95620a86add5"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d918570b-3b7b-4a91-bc60-95620a86add5&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the Noongar name for Dog?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/944233cd-3484-4cb2-b26f-92d978cc25e1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Information on the naming of Dog Swamp is scarce. Not being a detective, the swamp is located in Yokine, the aboriginal word for Dog, which was so named because of the high concentration of Dingos that lived in the area.

Some interesting historical facts about Dog Swamp, it was once the location of a mythical theme park called the Land of Make Believe and was also the home of one of Perth's very first Hungry Jacks stores which opened in 1971. My guess, they were one and the same thing. Also unconfirmed, but the opening of Hungry Jacks coincided with the demise of the Dingo population in the area.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/454e2a1a-eaa0-4856-86e1-ef11f2d79bd2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.05125" lon="115.740817">
