   <groundspeak:owner id="">Deefa71</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #068&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;WA's Most Influential Musicians #6 - John Butler &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/72e39781-a3bb-49bc-b272-4dbf47dc75a4"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/72e39781-a3bb-49bc-b272-4dbf47dc75a4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Where did John Butler live in the US before moving to Fremantle as a 10 year old?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0b9876c9-cdcc-45b1-9b15-3aae4f1dbeb9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;John Butler/John Butler Trio:

Fremantle has had no shortage of dreadlocked hippies playing guitar, but American emigree John Butler beat everyone to the punch with his amazing guitar work, politically charged lyrics, powerful live shows and fierce independence (forming Jarrah Records with fellow Perth folkies the Waifs). He formed the reggae-roots-rock band John Butler Trio in 1998 with Jason McGann on drums, and Gavin Shoesmith. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7feaac35-913b-4fa1-877a-206244e75af7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
