   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #073&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Alaska, USA&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/47501866-f346-4767-aae1-f63cc101d2d5"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/47501866-f346-4767-aae1-f63cc101d2d5&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the best known animal in Alaska USA?  &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2bca46ad-29e8-4442-be61-17ac7f75a9c0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Alaska is famous for its vast and wild landscapes, abundant wildlife, and natural resources. Specifically, it's known for its glaciers, national parks, the Northern Lights, the Midnight Sun, the Iditarod race, the gold rush, the fishing industry, and its rich cultural heritage

Nickname: The Last Frontier
Motto: North to the Future
Anthem: Alaska's Flag&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e791f5ae-326e-4057-b010-24a34f98f646" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
