   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #073&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Utah, USA&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/47501866-f346-4767-aae1-f63cc101d2d5"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/47501866-f346-4767-aae1-f63cc101d2d5&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the state bird?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d6b5362e-bdc5-4180-985c-c58750891d37" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Utah is renowned for its stunning natural beauty, particularly its national parks, ski resorts, and unique landscapes.  Utah boasts five national parks ("The Mighty Five"): Arches, Bryce Canyon, Canyonlands, Capitol Reef, and Zion. These parks are known for their iconic rock formations, canyons, and diverse landscapes.   

Skiing: The Wasatch Range near Salt Lake City is a popular destination for skiing, offering abundant snowfall.  

Utah's landscape includes desert regions, red rocks, mountains, and lakes, making it a visually stunning state. 

Bonneville Salt Flats:
This vast flat plain offers unique scenery and is known for its speed record attempts. 

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e791f5ae-326e-4057-b010-24a34f98f646" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.051233" lon="115.7408">
  <ele>4.0</ele>
