  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/72e39781-a3bb-49bc-b272-4dbf47dc75a4</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #068 : S2 WA's Most Influential Musicians #7 - Eurogliders by Deefa71</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1399" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #068 : S2 WA's Most Influential Musicians #7 - Eurogliders</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Deefa71</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Deefa71</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #068&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;WA's Most Influential Musicians #7 - Eurogliders&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/72e39781-a3bb-49bc-b272-4dbf47dc75a4"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/72e39781-a3bb-49bc-b272-4dbf47dc75a4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;In 2024, Eurogliders were nominated for an ARIA for "Best Use of an Australian Recording in a...?"&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d6cea3be-323c-4ccb-86f4-a69add2ba790" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Eurogliders:

Eurogliders are a band formed in 1980 in Perth which included Grace Knight on vocals, Bernie Lynch on guitar and vocals, and Amanda Vincent on keyboards. In 1984, Eurogliders released an Australian top ten album, This Island which spawned their No. 2 hit single, "Heaven (Must Be There)" which also peaked at No. 21 on the United States Billboard charts and appeared on the Hot 100. Another Australian top ten album, Absolutely  followed in 1985, which provided two further local top ten singles, "We Will Together" and "Can't Wait to See You". 

Eurogliders disbanded in 1989, with Knight having a successful career as a jazz singer. Australian rock music historian Ian McFarlane described Eurogliders as "the accessible face of post-punk new wave music. The band's sophisticated brand of pop was traditional in its structure, but displayed the decidedly 'modern veneer' (hip clothes, heavy use of synthesiser)".&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7feaac35-913b-4fa1-877a-206244e75af7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
