   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #077&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt; Lets all have pun time 5&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/2f614776-caaf-4cf8-9601-35d46a4b16d9"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/2f614776-caaf-4cf8-9601-35d46a4b16d9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What animal was mentioned in the first Pun?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d185fd5b-34a4-402b-a59b-ad342a9d9148" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Why couldn’t the pony sing in the choir? He was a little horse.

Did you hear about the woman who loved making archery supplies? Every day she went to work, she quivered with joy!

The past, the present and the future all walk into a bar. It was tense.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e7ef68b0-63bf-48e4-81d3-e6395f142be5" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com

&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
