   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #002&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Rottnest Snorkel Trail&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/be6a3008-4f22-4f59-918c-f22daf5951be"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/be6a3008-4f22-4f59-918c-f22daf5951be&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What dangerous marine animals can be found on Rottnest Island?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b68148b3-4a6d-4bf5-a5cd-f95208b4cfe7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Henrietta Rocks is a striking snorkelling site featuring the historic shipwreck of Shark. The wreck provides an underwater playground for the abundant sea life. Making it an exciting experience for new and experienced snorkelers&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/36366556-3028-42d0-966c-12be5d9526e6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab Art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth.There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com

Every time we have Pommie visitors its a must to take them to Rottnest Island where there is so much to do for all age groups. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.050983" lon="115.740683">
  <ele>5.0</ele>
