   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #002&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Rottnest Snorkel Trail&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/be6a3008-4f22-4f59-918c-f22daf5951be"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/be6a3008-4f22-4f59-918c-f22daf5951be&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the warm current that Rottnest Island lies in the path of?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a4530e4f-3c0a-40fd-9d13-be15421a65bc" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Little Parakeet Bay is a quiet, secluded location ideal for snorkellers looking for a peaceful experience. The coral gardens here are stunning. You’re likely to spot charming little, blue-scaled fish, graceful starfish and the occasional stingray.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/36366556-3028-42d0-966c-12be5d9526e6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab Art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth.There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com

Every time we have Pommie visitors its a must to take them to Rottnest Island where there is so much to do for all age groups. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
