  <name>LBPSgS-04</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa06I</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/72e39781-a3bb-49bc-b272-4dbf47dc75a4</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #068 : S4 WA's Most Influential Musicians #9 - The Waifs by Deefa71</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918715" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #068 : S4 WA's Most Influential Musicians #9 - The Waifs</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Deefa71</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Deefa71</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #068&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;WA's Most Influential Musicians #9 - The Waifs&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/72e39781-a3bb-49bc-b272-4dbf47dc75a4"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/72e39781-a3bb-49bc-b272-4dbf47dc75a4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Which American singer-songwriter did The Waifs support on his 2003 tour of Australia? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/61aeffa0-ef02-44d9-90d6-14b401397de8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Waifs:

Forming in Albany, The Waifs are a folk rock band acclaimed for their contribution to Australian music. 
The group was formed by sisters Donna Simpson and Vikki Thorn, who previously toured Australia in a Kombi van, meeting Josh Cunningham in Broome after a gig, who would complete the trio. 

From biker bars to local pubs, The Waifs won the hearts of Australians on smaller scales before reaching national success. In June of 2002, The Waifs, John Butler and their common manager Phil Stevens founded independent label Jarrah Records, set up to spread both musicians’ material over North America.

In the same year 'London Still' from breakthrough album Up All Night was released and became a defining song for the band. Simpson captures themes of longing and homesickness, missing the familiar landscapes of Western Australia while touring Europe and living abroad.  &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7feaac35-913b-4fa1-877a-206244e75af7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
