   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #067&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Fremantle Rainbow Containers 4&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b1764857-f9e0-417d-88ed-b8547cc46165"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b1764857-f9e0-417d-88ed-b8547cc46165&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many sea containers make this sculpture&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/25a25784-da31-44b2-a292-a91de48561fd" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is the iconic Rainbow Sea Containers of Fremantle.
There are great views of the river and the port from this magnificent piece of art.
I hope you can learn a little more of its creation and that it brings a smile to your face like it does to mine  &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ae78c498-d2db-429b-8624-2353d90e0427" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on
WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
