  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1f721226-f9ba-4865-b784-2153b4c506cf</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #026 : S1 Boorloo by Kyzabra</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918806" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #026 : S1 Boorloo</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Kyzabra</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Kyzabra</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #026&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Boorloo&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1f721226-f9ba-4865-b784-2153b4c506cf"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1f721226-f9ba-4865-b784-2153b4c506cf&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What do we know Boorloo as  ?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1f37c046-d2ef-4a44-9163-aed4206b6a0b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Australia’s capital cities have ancient origins that predate European settlement. Indigenous cultures and languages thrived across the continent, each leaving their own mark on the landscape. By exploring the traditional names of these cities, we can acknowledge the enduring connection of Aboriginal peoples to the land and appreciate the rich heritage they bring to the nation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e6dc6d8d-e092-4b30-9c83-b3752bf3e420" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com

This AdLab is themed around traditional place names.

Using traditional place names is truth-telling in action. It's a step towards acknowledging First Nations sovereignty.
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
