   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #25&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Origins&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/6ec79758-0d38-40b2-a914-c76eb10b6969"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/6ec79758-0d38-40b2-a914-c76eb10b6969&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;In which Australian town was the bakery located?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5540a7d4-688d-4610-aaf3-607b5def3f00" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In 1847, Scottish immigrant William Arnott opened a bakery&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1fba07c6-627f-4198-b01f-1a2981365340" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.


To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com

In this adventure, you'll learn the origins of Arnotts Biscuits.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
