</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.0528" lon="115.739483">
  <ele>1.0</ele>
  <time>2025-05-27T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBPYxN-05</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa05S</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5a7a2cbb-3361-4a2d-a051-5afbc4e975a8</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #051 : S5 Cooling by atCatpacity</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918912" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #051 : S5 Cooling</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>atCatpacity</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">atCatpacity</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #051&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Cooling &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5a7a2cbb-3361-4a2d-a051-5afbc4e975a8"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5a7a2cbb-3361-4a2d-a051-5afbc4e975a8&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Which season is represented by the colour green as it is the time of the year where the cooler weather begins?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4cc34d9e-94d1-4001-b618-83470b4b4c8f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; April-May

This season sees a break in the really hot weather. A key indicator of the change of season is the cool nights that bring a dewy presence in the early mornings.

The winds will also change, especially in their intensity, with light breezes generally swinging from southerly directions.  Many flying ants can be seen cruising around in the light winds.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ed272129-11bc-4aef-97af-984fd14fa53e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com

There are six Noongar seasons in Western Australia’s South West region, which are indicated by changes in local plants and animals. 

Each of the AdLab stages refers to one of the seasons. The final season is Djilba (August-September). This season is represented by the colour pink as it symbolises growth of wildflowers and plants.
This is the start of the massive flowering explosion that happens in the South West. Beginning with the yellow flowering plants such as the acacias.

Djilba is a transitional time of the year, with some very cold and clear days combining with warmer,rainy and windy days mixing with the occasional sunny day or two.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
