   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #066&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Original SWAG&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/861f80e7-2f1a-4ffb-b666-d4ce86b746ad"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/861f80e7-2f1a-4ffb-b666-d4ce86b746ad&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Which of these was SWAG in the first geocache &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/dbec9276-6343-4f7e-8e65-f7314f5318e3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;"Stuff We All Get." Trade items left in caches by geocachers. This adventure lab highlights some of the swag left in the first geocache by Dave Ulmer all the way back in 2000!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/489efdfa-aa6c-44b6-a99a-f7f22a89015b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

