  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa05A</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/06053490-966c-4ce8-9658-fbb0767ae966</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #050 : S5 WA's Most Influential Bands #5 - Tame Impala by familysteiner</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918946" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #050 : S5 WA's Most Influential Bands #5 - Tame Impala</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>familysteiner</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">familysteiner</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #050&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;WA's Most Influential Bands #5 - Tame Impala&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/06053490-966c-4ce8-9658-fbb0767ae966"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/06053490-966c-4ce8-9658-fbb0767ae966&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many STUDIO albums have Tame Impala released? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/de515cf0-5605-409c-b67b-fb9373617e92" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Tame Impala:

Tame Impala is the psychedelic music project of Australian singer and multi-instrumentalist Kevin Parker. Parker grew up in a musical household and dedicated himself to learning guitar and drums at early age, partially to escape the pressure of family life. His school friend Dominic Simper shared his love of music, especially the psychedelic sounds of the late '60s and they became fixtures on the underground Perth scene. Jay Watson joined them on drums and they changed their name to Tame Impala. The trio formed the live band, but Parker mostly took care of recording duties himself, crafting trippy, woozy psychedelic pop in his bedroom. He posted some songs on MySpace and they quickly became a phenomenon. As a touring act, Tame Impala consists of Parker, Simper and Watson, together with Cam Avery (bass guitar, vocals, synthesiser), and Julien Barbagallo (drums, vocals). 

Kevin Parker came up with the name of the band as a reflection of the music's theme. He felt the name encapsulated a balance between untamed creativity and refined artistry.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/96e4dd22-88de-469f-9ebe-be6ea9dd42f8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
