   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #050&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;WA's Most Influential Bands #3 - Jebediah&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/06053490-966c-4ce8-9658-fbb0767ae966"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/06053490-966c-4ce8-9658-fbb0767ae966&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Jebediah's lead singer Kevin Mitchell is also known as ____ ____?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ce1c2e4c-2a3c-4564-ae8c-83196b6b1e88" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Jebediah:

Jebediah are an Australian alternative rock band formed in 1994. After winning the National Campus Band Competition, the group were brought to national attention when their 1996 single "Jerks of Attention" received heavy airplay on Australian alternative radio station Triple J – which was followed by their breakthrough debut album, Slightly Odway in 1997.

The band released four studio albums by 2004: three entered the top ten on the ARIA Albums Chart; their second album, Of Someday Shambles (3 October 2000), is the highest charting at number two.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/96e4dd22-88de-469f-9ebe-be6ea9dd42f8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
