   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #050&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;WA's Most Influential Bands #4 - Birds of Tokyo&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/06053490-966c-4ce8-9658-fbb0767ae966"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/06053490-966c-4ce8-9658-fbb0767ae966&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;In what year did Birds of Tokyo win an ARIA for "Most Popular Australian Artist"?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/325f25b7-5a8a-48c9-867b-eb086551e72c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Formed in Perth in the early 2000’s, Birds of Tokyo have grown from independent roots to become one of Australia’s most popular contemporary rock bands. Since their 2008 breakthrough Universes, all five of the group’s albums have reached the ARIA top 3 including two #1 hits. Classic songs like “Good Lord”, “Plans”, “Lanterns”, “Two Of Us”, “Brace” and “Unbreakable” have all been top 10 airplay hits and more than seventy of their tracks have featured on Triple J, making them one of the National Youth Broadcaster’s three most played artists of this millennium.  The band has also won the APRA Award for “Most Performed Rock/Alternative Work” on a record setting six separate occasions. Epic live shows have always been at the core of their appeal&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/96e4dd22-88de-469f-9ebe-be6ea9dd42f8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.052783" lon="115.739267">
