 <wpt lat="-32.05295" lon="115.739217">
  <ele>1.0</ele>
  <time>2025-05-26T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBcfBz-01</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa05W</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/06053490-966c-4ce8-9658-fbb0767ae966</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #050 : S1 WA's Most Influential Bands #1 - The Scientists by familysteiner</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918938" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #050 : S1 WA's Most Influential Bands #1 - The Scientists</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>familysteiner</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">familysteiner</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #050&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;WA's Most Influential Bands #1 - The Scientists&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/06053490-966c-4ce8-9658-fbb0767ae966"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/06053490-966c-4ce8-9658-fbb0767ae966&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of The Scientists drummer (who also played with Hoodoo Gurus and Beasts of Bourbon) who passed away in 2025? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/472a9532-9498-44db-9a19-f99066cf8635" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Scientists

Originating in the late '70s, The Scientists were crucial pioneers of Perth's punk and alternative rock scenes. Incorporating elements of garage, swamp, and post-punk, they carved out their own niche in the Australian music landscape. Their raw, gritty sound can be heard on tracks like "Swampland" and "Last Night," exemplifying the groundbreaking influence they've had on countless bands that followed in their wake.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/96e4dd22-88de-469f-9ebe-be6ea9dd42f8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.05295" lon="115.739233">
  <ele>1.0</ele>
