  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #050 : S2 WA's Most Influential Bands #2 - The Triffids by familysteiner</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918940" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #050 : S2 WA's Most Influential Bands #2 - The Triffids</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>familysteiner</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">familysteiner</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #050&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;WA's Most Influential Bands #2 - The Triffids&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/06053490-966c-4ce8-9658-fbb0767ae966"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/06053490-966c-4ce8-9658-fbb0767ae966&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;In which year were The Triffids inducted into the ARIA Hall of Fame?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/59d96866-86fd-4730-938c-7e6901eac203" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Triffids:

The Triffids were an alternative rock and pop band, formed in 1978 with David McComb as singer-songwriter, guitarist, bass guitarist and keyboardist.They achieved some success in Australia, but greater success in the UK and Scandinavia in the 1980s before disbanding in 1989.

According to music historian Ian McFarlane, "The Triffids remain one of Australia's best-loved, post-punk groups ... McComb ... infused his melancholy songs with stark yet beautiful and uniquely Australian imagery. Few songwriters managed to capture the feeling of isolation and fatalistic sense of despair of the Australian countryside". &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/96e4dd22-88de-469f-9ebe-be6ea9dd42f8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
