   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokkaAdLab Art #053&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Big Lollipop&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/188a86ff-0595-4ab0-a35e-7fd2965f1150"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/188a86ff-0595-4ab0-a35e-7fd2965f1150&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What colour combination is the lollipop?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0e2bd6a4-20cb-4a0f-9db2-c3312ced2140" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The owners of Yummylicious Candy Shack built this rainbow giant to attract tourist to Ravensthorpe in 2019. It is the largest free-standing lollipop in the world. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a15b7fa4-c68f-4263-9af9-a3839e3f49fd" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
