   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokkaAdLab Art #053&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Big Western Rock Lobster &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/188a86ff-0595-4ab0-a35e-7fd2965f1150"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/188a86ff-0595-4ab0-a35e-7fd2965f1150&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What colour is the Rock Lobster?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ab4edce2-6c78-4cff-8c36-71f3e0a8e54b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Situated between Jurien Bay and Geraldton, The Big Western Rock Lobster in Dongara is a sight to behold. An ode to Dongaras reputation as "the Rock Lobster capital of Australia", the big red crustacean has many visitors stopping by.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a15b7fa4-c68f-4263-9af9-a3839e3f49fd" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
