   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokkaAdLab Art #053&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Big Tractor&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/188a86ff-0595-4ab0-a35e-7fd2965f1150"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/188a86ff-0595-4ab0-a35e-7fd2965f1150&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What colour is the tractor?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/dbc2c4e7-37a0-476a-bf33-f8b2a8aaedf3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Found in Carnamah, the tractor is a monument to WAs agriculture and manufacturing heritage. It is a five-times, orange replica of the Chamberlain 40K, which was the first tractor manufactured in WA in 1949.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a15b7fa4-c68f-4263-9af9-a3839e3f49fd" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.05195" lon="115.739067">
  <ele>14.0</ele>
  <time>2025-05-30T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBVRyX-05</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLab25</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b29dfbd1-890f-4f29-b9ab-38234dacd0d7</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #22 : S5 Quokka Colony on the Mainland by pood</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1492" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #22 : S5 Quokka Colony on the Mainland</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>pood</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">pood</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #22&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Quokka Colony on the Mainland &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b29dfbd1-890f-4f29-b9ab-38234dacd0d7"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b29dfbd1-890f-4f29-b9ab-38234dacd0d7&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Not many mountain ranges have a quokka colony, where is this quokka colony located?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b4d80d16-742b-4838-bc21-7efca726462f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A new quokka population has been discovered in the Perth Hills by local charity, Bibbul Ngarma Aboriginal Association Inc (BNAA).

The quokkas were discovered through the BoorYul-Bah-Bilya program – a recent initiative that aims to address declining river health through creation of a new type of community catchment plan.

This is the first time that quokkas have been photographed by the general public in the Perth Hills and is an important finding for conservation of the species. While known to occur in isolated locations in the Darling Range, quokkas are rarely seen by the wider community. Their exact location will remain confidential and the best place to see quokkas is still on Wadjemup-Rottnest Island.

Quokkas are best known on Wadjemup-Rottnest Island although small groups live in the forests of Noongar Boodja on the mainland.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d875d50d-1b5f-45c2-a690-11efe6ee8232" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.0527" lon="115.739083">
  <ele>1.0</ele>
  <time>2025-05-27T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBWHNq-01</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa05P</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d813470f-d2b7-4ff9-9482-f41e6cf236e4</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #055 - Pommie Adventures in Aus : S1 A whale of a time down south by RegPlate</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1468" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #055 - Pommie Adventures in Aus : S1 A whale of a time down south</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>RegPlate</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">RegPlate</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #055 - Pommie Adventures in Aus&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;A whale of a time down south&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d813470f-d2b7-4ff9-9482-f41e6cf236e4"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d813470f-d2b7-4ff9-9482-f41e6cf236e4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;But where are we?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/bee7c3d2-0f3b-42b0-9dd8-55d69163d7a0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;We, Mrs RegPlate &amp; I, flew to this town and had a relaxed sightseeing drive back to Perth meeting up with the Aussie family en route. We stayed in a motel almost on the beach, enjoyed the local shops &amp; restaurants and watched the sunsets.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e9a25770-161f-49fc-81aa-998143705f25" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

Hi all, my daughter &amp; family emigrated to WA Australia many years ago and we have been visiting regularly to see our grandaughters growing up.
This AdLab covers some places we have visited, well known landmarks and features in Western Australia. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
