   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #055 - Pommie Adventures in Aus&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Hillarys Boat Harbour&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d813470f-d2b7-4ff9-9482-f41e6cf236e4"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d813470f-d2b7-4ff9-9482-f41e6cf236e4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the group of rocks just west of the Harbour breakwater?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e051093b-d70e-4061-b56e-1047af7f3152" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Hillarys Boat Harbour was the first major marina complex north of Perth. Construction commenced in September 1985 and was officially opened in January 1988.
Lots to do here including swim, eat, drink, eat ice cream or just enjoy the environment people watching.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e9a25770-161f-49fc-81aa-998143705f25" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

