   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #056&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;WA Science Hall of Fame &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c6690439-3add-44b0-9671-2ee4ddfb87ed"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c6690439-3add-44b0-9671-2ee4ddfb87ed&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What years was Professor Donna Cross OAM inducted into the Hall of Fame.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d10e8bf8-5a17-43e4-8e37-e5acdf2ba6ae" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Born in Western Australia, Professor Donna Cross OAM has spent most of her 40-year career working within the State. She is recognised as Australia’s leading bullying prevention expert and one of the world’s most respected researchers into bullying and cyber bullying. Donna Cross is currently Emeritus Professor and Senior Honorary Fellow at The University of Western Australia, and Chief Behavioural Advisor to the New South Wales Government.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d54eb30e-8c28-47f9-8fdd-df7f841ab9ea" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
