   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #012&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Bush tucker 1&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1772127d-25a0-47b7-ad02-1fb53d7199d1"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1772127d-25a0-47b7-ad02-1fb53d7199d1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The witchetty grub is the lavae of what?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d2ec54cf-e0ad-4342-8177-09767b9434c1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art - Please join in by contacting WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com 
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4f571e27-8a1e-4d45-ba30-a57bf0ba4770" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
