   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #47&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Home of the America’s Cup no more&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bb9dbc7c-c98c-43e5-a443-a6510b14c8ae"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bb9dbc7c-c98c-43e5-a443-a6510b14c8ae&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Who was at the helm of Kookaburra Iii?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c741f752-57ae-473f-b7a3-e618b2b6a803" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Louis Vuitton Cup was held in 1987 to detetmine the challenger and US yacht Stars and Stripes 87 won the right to challenge. 
Four syndicates competed for the right to defend and Kevin Parry’s Kookaburra III beat Alan Bond’s Syndicate’s Australia IV 5-nil.
The races for the defence were held in February 1987. The US Stars and Stripes beat Kookaburra III 4-nil. The America’s Cup left Australian shores but left a lot of memories if an exciting time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3915f6f9-65e0-430f-b3f0-26a63d0ce971" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WA Quokka AdLab Art series which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth.
There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
