  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0b4437a3-da91-48fa-8ca8-c9cfc0093695</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #41 : S3 First Bands by megawat60</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1579" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #41 : S3 First Bands</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>megawat60</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">megawat60</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #41&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;First Bands&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0b4437a3-da91-48fa-8ca8-c9cfc0093695"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0b4437a3-da91-48fa-8ca8-c9cfc0093695&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What was the most successful of his first bands?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a679cfd7-bd3d-4a14-874d-e46e95b2a15d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Scott's vocals were inspired by his idol, Little Richard  After working as a postman, bartender and truck packer, Scott started his first band, The Spektors, in 1964 as drummer and occasional lead singer.  In 1966, they merged with another local band, the Winstons, and formed The Valentines, in which Scott was co-lead singer with Vince Lovegrove.  The Valentines recorded several songs written by George Young of The Easybeats. "Every Day I Have to Cry" (a song originally written and sung by Arthur Alexander) made the local record chart.  In 1970, after gaining a place on the National Top 30 with their single "Juliette", The Valentines disbanded due to artistic differences after a much-publicised drug scandal.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/00af1bc3-dabe-47e1-a8dd-dfde7061dba3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

In the world of Rock n Roll probably one of the best know names is Ronald Belford "Bon" Scott, so continuing my AdLabs for this Quokka Art, who better to feature than the man himself!
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
