  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLab43</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bb9dbc7c-c98c-43e5-a443-a6510b14c8ae</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #47 : S3 Home of the Anerica’s Cup: Celebrations by m4yb</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918828" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #47 : S3 Home of the Anerica’s Cup: Celebrations</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>m4yb</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">m4yb</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #47&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Home of the Anerica’s Cup: Celebrations&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bb9dbc7c-c98c-43e5-a443-a6510b14c8ae"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bb9dbc7c-c98c-43e5-a443-a6510b14c8ae&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Who was Australia’s Prime Minister in September 1983?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d7a3b633-764c-4322-8d3b-27ac1673d95c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;There was much celebrating in Australia when news came that the Anerica’s Cup was on its way here after 132 years of US dominance.
In the early hours of the 27th September 1983, the then Prime Minister of Australia uttered the famous words: "Any boss who sacks anyone today for not turning up is a bum".&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3915f6f9-65e0-430f-b3f0-26a63d0ce971" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WA Quokka AdLab Art series which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth.
There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.052883" lon="115.738917">
  <ele>1.0</ele>
  <time>2025-05-30T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBxRVg-04</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLab4H</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bb9dbc7c-c98c-43e5-a443-a6510b14c8ae</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #47 : S4 Home of the America’s Cup: the 1987 Defence by m4yb</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918830" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #47 : S4 Home of the America’s Cup: the 1987 Defence</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>m4yb</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">m4yb</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #47&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Home of the America’s Cup: the 1987 Defence&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bb9dbc7c-c98c-43e5-a443-a6510b14c8ae"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bb9dbc7c-c98c-43e5-a443-a6510b14c8ae&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What was the name of the defending yacht club in 1987?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e113103e-5e6c-4728-8359-9b477e60711f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Plans were put into place for the defence of the America’s Cup in 1987. Gages Road off Fremantle was chosen for the races and Challenger Harbour was built. 
13 syndicates from 6 countries challenged and 4 australian syndicates competed to defend, with a total of 25 boats.
Frementle was a busy thriving place with tourists, reporters as well as yacht crews and supporters.
The WA State Government even issued special Home of the America’s Cup car registration places.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3915f6f9-65e0-430f-b3f0-26a63d0ce971" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WA Quokka AdLab Art series which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth.
There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.052183" lon="115.738717">
  <ele>1.0</ele>
