   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #064&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;WA Mines - Frog's Leg&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0dd302a4-dbea-4800-9f13-883fb38579d0"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0dd302a4-dbea-4800-9f13-883fb38579d0&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the mine?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a2926b06-55d9-4485-a1f4-d7e6d7776bf4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Frog's Leg Gold Mine is a gold mine located 19 km west of Kalgoorlie, the gold deposit at Frog's Leg was discovered in 1999 and mining originally occurred in an open pit operation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/46ba9607-c3b6-4517-ac16-ba42b524fea3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal. To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com 

Western Australia is home to numerous mine sites, some with rather peculiar names. These names often reflect the area's history, the people who discovered them, or simply a touch of imagination.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
