   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #064&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;WA Mines - Granny Smith&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0dd302a4-dbea-4800-9f13-883fb38579d0"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0dd302a4-dbea-4800-9f13-883fb38579d0&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the mine?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/fdd9e7b4-7fb7-40aa-b261-668099ad2990" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Granny Smith Gold Mine is a gold mine 21 kilometres south of Laverton, near Mount Weld. The gold deposit was discovered in 1979 by Canadian prospector Ray Lovi Smith and named after his wife Laurende.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/46ba9607-c3b6-4517-ac16-ba42b524fea3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal. To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com 

Western Australia is home to numerous mine sites, some with rather peculiar names. These names often reflect the area's history, the people who discovered them, or simply a touch of imagination.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
