   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #064&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;WA Mines - White Foil&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0dd302a4-dbea-4800-9f13-883fb38579d0"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0dd302a4-dbea-4800-9f13-883fb38579d0&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the mine?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6d67b71d-f4b3-44d5-833b-53a1f2d2b03b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The White Foil Gold Mine is a gold mine 23 km south-west of Kalgoorlie, the deposit was discovered in 1996.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/46ba9607-c3b6-4517-ac16-ba42b524fea3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal. To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com 

