   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #063&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Mountains&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/88b248a6-b78b-4089-b480-73b188d92210"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/88b248a6-b78b-4089-b480-73b188d92210&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the highest mountain in WA?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5ced945c-68f9-4efc-b742-94f7e5330d3f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;While one of world’s most productive regions for digging holes into the ground (supplying iron ore, gold, diamonds, bauxite, and more), there are also a whopping 3624 named mountains in Western Australia.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/79f52816-70e6-4713-9929-b5327d247bd3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
