   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #063&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Rivers&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/88b248a6-b78b-4089-b480-73b188d92210"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/88b248a6-b78b-4089-b480-73b188d92210&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the longest river in WA?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/fb4f54ea-5a5d-4b69-b51e-f41735c749a8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;There are 208 major waterways in Western Australia with a combined length of more than 25000km (15,534mi). Forty-eight have been identified as 'wild rivers' due to their near pristine condition.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/79f52816-70e6-4713-9929-b5327d247bd3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
