   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #063&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Cliffs&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/88b248a6-b78b-4089-b480-73b188d92210"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/88b248a6-b78b-4089-b480-73b188d92210&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the westernmost point of mainland WA?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/170a2967-30b0-408e-98d1-09c02ff3185c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Western Australia has the longest coastline of all Australian states and is home to the longest fringing reef in the world – the pristine Ningaloo Reef – and to the oldest life forms on earth, the stromatolites of Shark Bay. Alongside the stunning beaches there are spectacular, coloured cliffs, with the Zuytdorp Cliffs in the north west soaring to 250m (820ft) above sea level.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/79f52816-70e6-4713-9929-b5327d247bd3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
