 <wpt lat="-32.0522" lon="115.738667">
  <ele>1.0</ele>
  <time>2025-05-29T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBNeFj-01</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa02J</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c660ff50-2779-4e41-9a91-7d89a41a084e</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #021 : S1 John Butler Trio by megawat60</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918854" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #021 : S1 John Butler Trio</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>megawat60</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">megawat60</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #021&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;John Butler Trio&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c660ff50-2779-4e41-9a91-7d89a41a084e"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c660ff50-2779-4e41-9a91-7d89a41a084e&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year did John Butler Trio start?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b57a6c8c-31de-4ac1-8d54-d4075f79233d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;John Charles Wiltshire-Butler (born 1 April 1975), professionally known as John Butler, is an American-Australian singer, songwriter, and music producer. He is best known for his time as the eponymous frontman of the John Butler Trio, a roots and jam band that formed in Perth Fremantle, Western Australia.  My connection with him is he's the same age as my eldest son and they used to skateboard together a lot in and around the Fremantle area with heaps of guys.

John started playing the guitar after his grandmother gave him a 1930's Dobro styled guitar, which belonged to his deceased grandfather.  He started busking at the Fremantle Markets, a popular tourist spot in Fremantle that operated every Friday, Saturday and Sunday and still do to this day.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1b0b66cb-4c08-4ac4-9310-a772f797f827" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.
This AdLab hopefully will celebrate some of the wonderful musicians and bands of Perth and Western Australia.  As the most isolated city in the world, WA certainly punches way above its weight in turning out some great and original bands.  I have picked 5 that resonated with me during my early days in Perth, having arrived in the late 70’s from Sydney.  All this information was from my memory or mostly stolen off Wikipedia!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.052033" lon="115.73865">
  <ele>1.0</ele>
