  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c660ff50-2779-4e41-9a91-7d89a41a084e</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #021 : S3 The Jets by megawat60</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918858" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #021 : S3 The Jets</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>megawat60</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">megawat60</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #021&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Jets&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c660ff50-2779-4e41-9a91-7d89a41a084e"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c660ff50-2779-4e41-9a91-7d89a41a084e&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year did this band form?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e8fe543c-b93b-4d46-b7e6-82d1ce335417" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The JETS story - a young man with the idea of a band playing good rock n and roll set out to shake up West Australia's live music scene. That, they did. In 1979 Peter Dean or “Deany “as everyone calls him, left the band he was in as lead vocalist and bass player and began to plan a trip around Australia in the coaster camper bus he and his girlfriend, Janie (later became his wife) had bought and then come back to Perth and start a band playing good hard rock in the vein of Led Zeppelin, Deep Purple, AC/DC etc.
I had some weird connection with this band, or more importantly their production crew.  I borrowed their front of house console every Sunday night from the Generator a huge pub barn in Morely for a much more sedate show on Monday evening at the Old Melbourne Hotel in Perth city with a 11 piece jazz fusion band called Manteca. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1b0b66cb-4c08-4ac4-9310-a772f797f827" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.
This AdLab hopefully will celebrate some of the wonderful musicians and bands of Perth and Western Australia.  As the most isolated city in the world, WA certainly punches way above its weight in turning out some great and original bands.  I have picked 5 that resonated with me during my early days in Perth, having arrived in the late 70’s from Sydney.  All this information was from my memory or mostly stolen off Wikipedia!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
