   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #044&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;West Coast Blues ‘n’ Roots Festival 2014&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/38790d87-1054-4d88-a5e0-2c7e88f1b9c3"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/38790d87-1054-4d88-a5e0-2c7e88f1b9c3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Which artist headlined the festival in 2014?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f69fdfb3-2985-4b0d-89de-98a90f876271" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The West Coast Blues 'n' Roots Festival was an annual music festival held in Fremantle, Western Australia from 2005 - 2015. It attracted and featured many talented blues and roots performers, both international and local acts. 
Fremantle was the perfect setting for such an event, known for its thriving arts and entertainment culture. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/81ea4a92-968d-4150-a6e1-fce0b46fbbf3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.
 
To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
