   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #061&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;WA's floral emblem&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/35c5c2ce-4a7f-4afc-890c-cb615c5579d6"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/35c5c2ce-4a7f-4afc-890c-cb615c5579d6&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is WA's flower emblem?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/cbdee36f-7e7c-415b-b83f-d845638cbdbb" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Western Australia has many distinctive and unique plants and flowers.  The State's floral emblem is an example of this, being the best known of its type.  It is only found naturally in Western Australia and can be spotted in many areas of remnant bushland near Perth.  It is also common in the sandy coastal plains of the State’s south-west.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ca56feb7-d1e9-48e1-a6fd-dbb425dba7e3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.


To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
