   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #061&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;WA's bird emblem&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/35c5c2ce-4a7f-4afc-890c-cb615c5579d6"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/35c5c2ce-4a7f-4afc-890c-cb615c5579d6&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is WA's bird emblem?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0af8afc9-8b14-4335-b0af-bee03d965835" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Western Australia's bird emblem is found in wetlands throughout Australia, but it has a special association with the State, occurring in the ancestral stories of the Noongar people.

Flocks of these birds encountered by Dutch and English explorers led to a significant geographical feature in Western Australia being named after them.

Images of the bird can be found on historical and current government documents, bank notes, postage stamps and other publications.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ca56feb7-d1e9-48e1-a6fd-dbb425dba7e3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.


To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
