   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #035&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Northam&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/fbaa44ed-3e88-4c1d-81a1-1ca854f0cb36"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/fbaa44ed-3e88-4c1d-81a1-1ca854f0cb36&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What majestic creature featured in 2019?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d132e7ab-3a01-431b-9525-3f8df127673e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Each year the organising committee take us to a different location in WA for WAGoesBIG. Amongst the merchandise on offer are some beautifully designed coins featuring local flora and fauna.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/93427b03-83cc-4729-956f-9feace4b0fb6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab Art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth.There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com

Western Australia has not yet managed to muster sufficient numbers to be awarded a Mega Event. However we do hold an annual WAGoesBIG Event which has earned the reputation for being well organised, great fun and extremely friendly......you really should GO!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
