   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #061&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;WA's marine animal emblem&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/35c5c2ce-4a7f-4afc-890c-cb615c5579d6"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/35c5c2ce-4a7f-4afc-890c-cb615c5579d6&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is WA's marine animal emblem?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/16b7bb7f-7a14-4516-b1c5-c0adb773f240" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Western Australia's marine animal emblem originated approximately 60 million years ago.  It is a large fish specially camouflaged in its environment due to its markings, which are unique to each individual.

The species can be found in tropical and warm oceans across the equator and are a significant tourist attraction in Western Australia during Autumn and Winter, with the State being one of the best places in the world to encounter them.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ca56feb7-d1e9-48e1-a6fd-dbb425dba7e3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.


To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
