   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #061&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;WA's fossil emblem&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/35c5c2ce-4a7f-4afc-890c-cb615c5579d6"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/35c5c2ce-4a7f-4afc-890c-cb615c5579d6&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is WA's fossil emblem?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8571de90-6e40-4253-84c0-7d0e10a2e579" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Western Australia's fossil emblem is named after a prehistoric formation in the State's far north.  Shales in the area have revealed well preserved skeletons of the creature that from over 300 million years ago.  Some fossils are best preserved of their type in the world.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ca56feb7-d1e9-48e1-a6fd-dbb425dba7e3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.


To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
