 <wpt lat="-32.052467" lon="115.738267">
  <ele>1.0</ele>
  <time>2025-05-26T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBEB6J-01</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa01Y</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b76d406f-87c1-437d-9fdf-ddace6c028d4</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #019 : S1 C Y O'Connor by Rach2</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918754" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #019 : S1 C Y O'Connor</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Rach2</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Rach2</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #019&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;C Y O'Connor &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b76d406f-87c1-437d-9fdf-ddace6c028d4"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b76d406f-87c1-437d-9fdf-ddace6c028d4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year was Fremantle Harbour completed? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c07ac6b3-ef2f-4994-ad25-895494130dd3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Charles Yelverton O'Connor, CMG (11 January 1843 – 10 March 1902), was an Irish engineer who is best known for his work in Western Australia, especially the construction of Fremantle Harbour, thought to be impossible, and the Goldfields Water Supply Scheme. 
The construction of Fremantle Harbour was probably O'Connor's greatest personal triumph, as his proposal to build the harbour within the entrance to the Swan River was contrary to previous expert advice that this was impracticable and that the construction would require constant dredging. Work commenced in 1892 in removing a limestone bar and sand shoals at the mouth of the Swan River and was successfully completed in 1903. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/73b523d5-5ee5-40cb-ae62-0fb6a05dd917" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.
The section of the AdLab is based around Fremantle Prison and some of its famous inmates. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.052417" lon="115.738217">
  <ele>3.0</ele>
  <time>2025-05-26T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBEB6J-03</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa01F</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b76d406f-87c1-437d-9fdf-ddace6c028d4</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #019 : S3 Fremantle Prison by Rach2</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918758" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #019 : S3 Fremantle Prison</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Rach2</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Rach2</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #019&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Fremantle Prison &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b76d406f-87c1-437d-9fdf-ddace6c028d4"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b76d406f-87c1-437d-9fdf-ddace6c028d4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Who designed Fremantle Prison &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/bd0a841d-b34f-4559-8d3c-e0ea96de1534" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fremantle Prison was originally known as the Convict Establishment. It was constructed in the 19th Century and remained in use until 1991. The gatehouse and associated entry complex was constructed between 1854 and 1855 using convict labour. It was designed by Royal Engineer and Comptroller General Edmund Henderson, and constructed out of limestone. The Prison is now a World Heritage Site. 
Famous inmates include Bon Scott (AC/DC), Brendan Abbott (The Postcard Bandit).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/73b523d5-5ee5-40cb-ae62-0fb6a05dd917" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.
The section of the AdLab is based around Fremantle Prison and some of its famous inmates. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
