 <wpt lat="-32.052867" lon="115.738233">
  <ele>1.0</ele>
  <time>2025-05-30T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBJv1S-05</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa03S</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/fbaa44ed-3e88-4c1d-81a1-1ca854f0cb36</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #035 : S5 Narrogin by pommieparkin2</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918840" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #035 : S5 Narrogin</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>pommieparkin2</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">pommieparkin2</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #035&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Narrogin&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/fbaa44ed-3e88-4c1d-81a1-1ca854f0cb36"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/fbaa44ed-3e88-4c1d-81a1-1ca854f0cb36&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many creatures are depicted on the back of the coin?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6a260cbf-99f6-4ff1-a05c-a405977f0958" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;2023 was a pretty special year as it was the 10th anniversary of WAGoesBIG and the organising committee pulled out all the stops to make a truly memorable Event.
The Creature for the year was the Rainbow Serpent and it was depicted in stunning artwork on our commemorative shirts and coins.
I will take this opportunity to thank all committee members 'past and present' for making all of the tremendous work they do for WestOz Geocaching and I also urge anyone who has not yet attended a WAGoesBIG Event to give it a go!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/93427b03-83cc-4729-956f-9feace4b0fb6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab Art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth.There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com

Western Australia has not yet managed to muster sufficient numbers to be awarded a Mega Event. However we do hold an annual WAGoesBIG Event which has earned the reputation for being well organised, great fun and extremely friendly......you really should GO!&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.0529" lon="115.738217">
  <ele>1.0</ele>
