 <wpt lat="-32.052383" lon="115.738133">
  <ele>5.0</ele>
  <time>2025-05-26T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBEB6J-04</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa01J</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b76d406f-87c1-437d-9fdf-ddace6c028d4</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #019 : S4 John Boyle O'Reilly by Rach2</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918760" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #019 : S4 John Boyle O'Reilly</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Rach2</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Rach2</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #019&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;John Boyle O'Reilly &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b76d406f-87c1-437d-9fdf-ddace6c028d4"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b76d406f-87c1-437d-9fdf-ddace6c028d4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What road did JB O'Reilly work on?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/88d9f0b9-dbbe-4783-ab94-75eda7ada1e9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;J B O'Reilly arrived in Fremantle on 9 January 1868, and was admitted to the Convict Establishment (now Fremantle Prison), but after a month he was transferred to Bunbury. He was assigned to a party of convicts tasked with building the Bunbury–Busselton road. With the aid of locals he escaped and sailed to America on a whaling ship. 
In 1879 he wrote a novel about another famous Fremantle escapee, Moondyne.
The novel is loosely based on the life of the Western Australian convict escapee and bushranger Moondyne Joe. It is believed to be the first ever fictional novel set in Western Australia.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/73b523d5-5ee5-40cb-ae62-0fb6a05dd917" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.
The section of the AdLab is based around Fremantle Prison and some of its famous inmates. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.052333" lon="115.738083">
  <ele>5.0</ele>
  <time>2025-05-26T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBEB6J-05</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa01u</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b76d406f-87c1-437d-9fdf-ddace6c028d4</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #019 : S5 Luxury Accommodation by Rach2</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918762" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #019 : S5 Luxury Accommodation</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Rach2</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Rach2</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #019&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Luxury Accommodation &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b76d406f-87c1-437d-9fdf-ddace6c028d4"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b76d406f-87c1-437d-9fdf-ddace6c028d4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The main cell was designed to hold how many men? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/924601be-9520-4824-9890-c8ba6665159d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Conditions in Fremantle Prison during convict times were harsh. The main cell was designed to hold 1,000 men. Their toilet was a bucket, and prisoners had to empty them everyday. The bed was a hammock that was removed during the day. The cells measured 2.1 x 1.2 metres. 
Each cell initially had a basin connected to running water, the smells coming up the pipes led to their removal by the 1860s. The cells were eventually enlarged and in the 1920s they finally got electricity. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/73b523d5-5ee5-40cb-ae62-0fb6a05dd917" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.
The section of the AdLab is based around Fremantle Prison and some of its famous inmates. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.052917" lon="115.7381">
  <ele>1.0</ele>
