  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5342fab6-b981-481f-88c2-6023eb2746ff</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #18 : S5 Goldfields Water Supply Scheme by m4yb</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1551" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #18 : S5 Goldfields Water Supply Scheme</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>m4yb</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">m4yb</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #18&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Goldfields Water Supply Scheme&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5342fab6-b981-481f-88c2-6023eb2746ff"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5342fab6-b981-481f-88c2-6023eb2746ff&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;In what year did CY O’ Connor die?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c8b86274-4a91-4829-b283-0e7cdb0f224b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;As gold was found East of Perth in the late 1800’s, the population exploded in the barren and dry areas around Southern Cross and Coolgardie, causing much hardship and deaths through water shortages.
In 1896 WA State Premier John Forrest raised a £2.5 million loan to build a dam east of Perth, a pipeline and pumping stations to take water to the Goldfields.  
CY O’Connor was appointed to supervise the Scheme. However, he encountered much criticism and accusations of corruption from State MP’s and the press.  
CY O’Connor took his own life at Robb Jetty South of Fremantle but the engineering achievements he left as his legacies live on.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f2d481c7-9643-4925-918d-6fdee6301914" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcometo the WAQuokka AlLab Art series which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth.
There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
