   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #18&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Fremantle Harbour&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5342fab6-b981-481f-88c2-6023eb2746ff"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5342fab6-b981-481f-88c2-6023eb2746ff&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name if the first ocean- going steamer to berth inside Fremantle Harbour?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b9f61cf5-c582-43c6-bddc-04d965e10005" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; Until CY O’Connor’s appointment, Fremantle Harbour was not accessible to larger ships. Under his direction, a limestone bar and sandy shoals at the mouth of the Swan River were removed and in 1897, the first ocean going steamer berthed at what is now Victoria Quay.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f2d481c7-9643-4925-918d-6fdee6301914" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcometo the WAQuokka AlLab Art series which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth.
There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
