   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #032&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Soutern Right Whales&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d4cb9158-78fb-41a3-8979-868e0cbcf2fb"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d4cb9158-78fb-41a3-8979-868e0cbcf2fb&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What does the Southern Right Whale eat?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1eb85f4a-7a5f-4c85-9ee9-c7e4fe5cf973" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Several species of animals migrate past Western Australia, including whales, birds and other marine life.

Soutern Right Whales are Baleen Whales and sieve Plankton through their mouths.  They travel behind Rottnest as the ocean is rich in plankton there.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ec0b28c8-fa05-4883-9075-c86effbb437e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka
off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs
to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry
Terminal.
To join this project, please contact the project Admins on
WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
