   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #032&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;West Australian Salmon&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d4cb9158-78fb-41a3-8979-868e0cbcf2fb"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d4cb9158-78fb-41a3-8979-868e0cbcf2fb&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is a group of salmon (fish)  called?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/fa995142-1fa8-4b13-87e2-2a85d8103ebd" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Several species of animals migrate past Western Australia, including whales, birds and other marine life.

The West Australian Salmon moves from the south coast of Western Australia for the summer months to above Perth waters in the winter months.



