  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/04018f99-f74c-4b70-8c60-75a756924fa5</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #087 : S1 Orchids of WA by Lumpyjrb</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918755" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #087 : S1 Orchids of WA</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Lumpyjrb</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Lumpyjrb</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #087&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Orchids of WA&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/04018f99-f74c-4b70-8c60-75a756924fa5"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/04018f99-f74c-4b70-8c60-75a756924fa5&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many species of Orchid can be found in WA?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0f3bfb78-bbd3-429a-b2c8-a1014250f275" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; Western Australia is home to a diverse range of orchid species due to the state's varied climate and habitats. These orchids are primarily terrestrial  (they grow in the ground) with the exception of some epiphytes (they grow on other plants) found in the northern, tropical regions. Many Western Australian orchids have unique adaptations. They were first studied by Archibald Menzies in 1791&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/191bff51-c256-4c38-83e0-2fd688482d13" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on
WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com

In this ad Lab we will be looking at Western Australia's orchids.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
