   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #072&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Waardong&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5a107d7b-610f-449e-a066-f6d674944ea8"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5a107d7b-610f-449e-a066-f6d674944ea8&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What bird is this?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c3710adc-a518-4849-b101-32fb6a455b9f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This bird has an all black glossy plumage, with a purple-blue greenish sheen.

An omnivorous and opportunistic feeder, the this bird eats a wide variety of plant and animal material, from fruits and seeds to lizards, chicks of other bird species, and small mammals; they will also scour waste bins and disposal sites for human food waste

To the Noongar people, this bird was Waardar, "the Watcher" and was wily and unpredictable. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/544562d7-6c50-42f9-8d90-c18678cf7ed6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
