  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918825" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #072 : S5 Ngolak</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>atCatpacity</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">atCatpacity</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #072&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Ngolak&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5a107d7b-610f-449e-a066-f6d674944ea8"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5a107d7b-610f-449e-a066-f6d674944ea8&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What bird is this?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/62966b2d-50c7-4c37-bb37-39fcebe0b656" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This bird's plumage is mostly greyish black, and it has prominent white cheek patches and a white tail band. They nest in hollows situated high in trees with fairly large diameters, generally Eucalyptus.

They communicate by auditory and visual displays.The voice is generally noisy with several calls; loudest and most frequent is a wailing "wy-lah" which is uttered by both sexes and often heard before the birds themselves are seen. 

This bird is an endangered species, due to habitat lost to land clearing and development.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/544562d7-6c50-42f9-8d90-c18678cf7ed6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
