   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #099&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;BIG PRAWN - Exmouth WA&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/2ba2f8e7-331c-4fab-b57e-ed76f222efd0"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/2ba2f8e7-331c-4fab-b57e-ed76f222efd0&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Whom was the artist?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/904223f6-e37a-4c42-b3e8-ce2961491de2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Exmouth's Big Prawn is a 7-meter-tall, 2,000 kg sculpture of a Western King Prawn, located on Murat Road in Exmouth, Western Australia. It was built by local resident Brian Paskins in 2004 and is a tribute to the local prawning industry. 

Key Facts:
Size: 7 meters tall and weighs 2,000 kg.
Location: Murat Road, Exmouth, Western Australia.
Material: Fibreglass over a steel core.
Purpose: A tribute to the local prawning industry, particularly the Western King Prawn.
History: Initially commissioned by MG Kailis and donated to the Shire of Exmouth by the Kailis family.
Material: Fibreglass over a steel core.
Purpose: A tribute to the local prawning industry, particularly the Western King Prawn.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e44a9fc8-cf07-4dcc-a66c-beee2a460849" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka
off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs
to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry
Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on
WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com

This adventure is about Notable WA "Big Things&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
