   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #099&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;BIG EMU - Nannup WA&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/2ba2f8e7-331c-4fab-b57e-ed76f222efd0"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/2ba2f8e7-331c-4fab-b57e-ed76f222efd0&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the Emu made from?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/52406bfc-3de8-4a47-b513-eb2dc0e2a6cc" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Nannup has a 3-meter tall Emu, part of a "Living with Emus" project aimed at raising awareness about road safety and wildlife collisions. This project involved local students and artist Lewis Horne. The sculpture is located at the main trailhead for the Tank 7 Mountain Bike Park

In addition to the sculpture, Nannup has also been experiencing a significant influx of emus in recent years. These emus have been known to wander through town and even visit residents' gardens

Local students from Nannup District High School were involved in the design and creation of the sculpture, learning about car parts, crash dynamics, and repurposing materials.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e44a9fc8-cf07-4dcc-a66c-beee2a460849" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka
off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs
to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry
Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on
WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com

This adventure is about Notable WA "Big Things&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
