   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #072&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Djiti-Djiti&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5a107d7b-610f-449e-a066-f6d674944ea8"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5a107d7b-610f-449e-a066-f6d674944ea8&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What bird is this?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/26021c77-dd83-403e-a9d3-c955c6fa6040" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This bird is the largest of the Australian fantails with a distinctive white 'eyebrow'. The name stems from the constant sideways wagging of the tail. This species is very vocal, and has a variety of calls, including the well-known "chittit-chittit-chittit".&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/544562d7-6c50-42f9-8d90-c18678cf7ed6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
