   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #096&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Fremantle Dockers - Brownlow Medal&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/2d4e616f-4c5f-45cc-ac60-92f899a9e8c9"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/2d4e616f-4c5f-45cc-ac60-92f899a9e8c9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Which Fremantle Docker player has won 2x Brownlow Medals?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0ce8fddb-03f9-41b2-b559-c5e4c0ee0b3b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Brownlow Medal is the AFL’s most prestigious individual award, given each year to the league’s “best and fairest” player during the home-and-away season. Umpires award votes after each game, and the player with the highest total wins. It’s a symbol of both elite performance and sportsmanship.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8a0f0e76-ecb5-404e-a992-d914e80f0ceb" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka
off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs
to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
