   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #096&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Fremantle Dockers - Home Ground&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/2d4e616f-4c5f-45cc-ac60-92f899a9e8c9"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/2d4e616f-4c5f-45cc-ac60-92f899a9e8c9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Where do Fremantle Dockers play their home games?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/df27a4c8-18e5-40c0-ac59-dab24db75507" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Fremantle Dockers were established in 1994 and joined the AFL in 1995 as the league’s second Western Australian team. Based in the historic port city of Fremantle, the club embraced a strong local identity with purple as its signature colour. Early years were marked by struggles on the field, but the team gradually built competitiveness, culminating in their first finals appearance in 2003. The Dockers reached their first and only Grand Final in 2013, losing to Hawthorn. Over the years, Fremantle has developed a passionate fanbase and continues to aim for its first AFL premiership.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8a0f0e76-ecb5-404e-a992-d914e80f0ceb" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka
off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs
to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
