  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/26579967-cdc9-4ac3-896a-32cc1cffd89a</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #007 : S5 Stage 5 - Lake Clifton by JKJK20</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918753" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #007 : S5 Stage 5 - Lake Clifton</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>JKJK20</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">JKJK20</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #007&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Stage 5 - Lake Clifton&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/26579967-cdc9-4ac3-896a-32cc1cffd89a"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/26579967-cdc9-4ac3-896a-32cc1cffd89a&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Why are the thrombolites in Lake Clifton important?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/af734e1b-35ac-436f-b3de-cd80b58cff2f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; Location: Near Mandurah, WA

Lake Clifton is home to thrombolites — ancient, rock-like living structures made by tiny microbes. These are similar to some of the earliest life forms on Earth, dating back billions of years. You can see them close to shore from a wooden boardwalk, especially when the lake level is low.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7205d174-5558-4b79-ab98-b3f740519b03" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka
off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs
to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry
Terminal.
To join this project, please contact the project Admins on
WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.051117" lon="115.740667">
