  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/8ae704c0-e5c4-42ee-adda-4fc79f8e0e60</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #097 : S1 Rottnest Island Marine Sanctuary Zones by Meme28</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918765" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #097 : S1 Rottnest Island Marine Sanctuary Zones</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Meme28</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Meme28</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #097&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Rottnest Island Marine Sanctuary Zones&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/8ae704c0-e5c4-42ee-adda-4fc79f8e0e60"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/8ae704c0-e5c4-42ee-adda-4fc79f8e0e60&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many Marine sanctuary zones does Rottnest Island have?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b5d19d0a-18ec-4499-98af-f2001ed56ce4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Due to the warm Leeuwin Current that passes along Wadjemup’s western coast, there’s a variety of flourishing sea life to be found. But this does not mean they are available for fishing.

Five Marine Sanctuary Zones have been established around the island to help conserve the pristine environment above and below the waves, where fishing is completely prohibited in some sanctuary zones.

Any fishing, spear-fishing, or collecting of marine plant life is strictly prohibited unless otherwise noted. 
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5d8f415a-095a-4433-9ed6-c3c9a05a51e8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.0512" lon="115.740667">
  <ele>4.0</ele>
  <time>2025-06-01T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBvLqv-02</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa09W</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/8ae704c0-e5c4-42ee-adda-4fc79f8e0e60</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #097 : S2 Western Australia State Fish by Meme28</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918767" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #097 : S2 Western Australia State Fish</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Meme28</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Meme28</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #097&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Western Australia State Fish&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/8ae704c0-e5c4-42ee-adda-4fc79f8e0e60"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/8ae704c0-e5c4-42ee-adda-4fc79f8e0e60&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the State Fish of Western Australia?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0f1fe0b8-6edf-4e26-81dc-434a2edd0da6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Growing up, many of us participated in beach fishing. It was a more affordable holiday alternative for families, who could camp along the stunning Western Australian coastline, soak up the sun, and swim all day—often for free.

Some of the most popular fish to catch around Perth include herring, skippy, whiting, bream, and flathead. The ultimate goal is to land the larger species in WA—such as mulloway, tailor, salmon, dhufish, and barramundi—and avoid having a "one that got away" moment.

Another favourite pastime is to swim with marine life, especially up North such as Monkey Mia, Kalbarri, Exmouth and Ningaloo.

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5d8f415a-095a-4433-9ed6-c3c9a05a51e8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.051167" lon="115.740667">
  <ele>4.0</ele>
  <time>2025-06-01T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBvLqv-03</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa09n</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/8ae704c0-e5c4-42ee-adda-4fc79f8e0e60</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #097 : S3 Fremantle Fish Market by Meme28</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918769" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #097 : S3 Fremantle Fish Market</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Meme28</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Meme28</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #097&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Fremantle Fish Market &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/8ae704c0-e5c4-42ee-adda-4fc79f8e0e60"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/8ae704c0-e5c4-42ee-adda-4fc79f8e0e60&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;When was the Fremantle Fish Market opened by the State Government?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8de49cb3-88d3-4095-a8a3-5984d2473050" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The State government built a fish market in Fremantle in 1908. It was run by the Fremantle Council to make money and resulted in disadvantaging the fishers who frequently went on strike against the low auction prices. 

Towards the end of the 19th century and start of the 20th century, Italian and Greek immigrants settling in Fremantle helped develop the budding commercial fishing industry. It was these fishermen that formed the Fremantle Fishermen’s Co-operative in 1947, effectively marketing their catch of products such as lobsters and finfish and ensuring a viable financial future for their families.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5d8f415a-095a-4433-9ed6-c3c9a05a51e8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
