  <time>2025-06-01T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBvLqv-05</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa09i</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/8ae704c0-e5c4-42ee-adda-4fc79f8e0e60</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #097 : S5 Rottnest Fishing by Meme28</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918773" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #097 : S5 Rottnest Fishing</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Meme28</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Meme28</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #097&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Rottnest Fishing&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/8ae704c0-e5c4-42ee-adda-4fc79f8e0e60"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/8ae704c0-e5c4-42ee-adda-4fc79f8e0e60&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the largest fish caught off Rottnest?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c0f6b97e-dcbe-4a21-9731-3afd0c618002" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Although there are five sanctuary zones around Rottnest, anglers can still fish in certain areas from the beach or a boat.

On February 8 2025, angler Koby Duncan hooked a 79.6kg (175.48 pound) Cobia twelve nautical miles from Perth, Western Australia on the south side of Rottnest Island.

On the deck, the fish measured 203 cm (about 80 inches) total length. Its widest girth was 104 cm (about 41 inches). This smashed the world record that has stood for 40 years - IGFA all-tackle world record was caught in 1985 at Shark Bay off northwest Australia by Peter Goulding.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5d8f415a-095a-4433-9ed6-c3c9a05a51e8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
