 <wpt lat="-32.0513" lon="115.740567">
  <ele>2.0</ele>
  <time>2025-06-01T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LB9nGi-01</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa093</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ad80918f-e77e-415c-8618-ff3669676f2e</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #093 : S1 Great Southern by dimor</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918775" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #093 : S1 Great Southern</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>dimor</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">dimor</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #093&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Great Southern&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ad80918f-e77e-415c-8618-ff3669676f2e"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ad80918f-e77e-415c-8618-ff3669676f2e&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;In Albany there is a famous ‘animal’ rock. What is it called?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/82084b0b-c6dd-4968-b0d3-4f04cbe47014" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Great Southern Region.
It is around 39,000km2.
Farming of livestock- sheep, cattle and crops, along with wool all dominate the local economy.

There is a lot to see and do in the region that makes it a worthy area to spend some time. From the historical port city of Albany with its gorgeous old buildings and the forts area on Mt Clarence to the Stirling Ranges which is the only place in WA that receives regular snowfalls.
There are many towns in the region that all have something to keep you busy. Some have wineries, painted silos, old buildings and that good old country charm. Fishing and surfing are popular in the coastal areas&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8b1ad59a-0838-4269-a950-24737da48890" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.
o To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
——————————————
Regions of WA #2

Quokka #88 is Regions of WA #1

Western Australia is a vast,  diverse and beautiful State. Within our state border we have 10 regions, this AdLab will feature the final five (5).
The first five (5) are my favourites - Pilbara, Wheatbelt, Gascoyne, Kimberley and Midwest.
Nothing beats a road trip to the outer metro regions

