   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #093&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;South West&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ad80918f-e77e-415c-8618-ff3669676f2e"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ad80918f-e77e-415c-8618-ff3669676f2e&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How big is the Wellington Dam mural?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d68704c9-4c1d-47a4-9f85-e3be470967ee" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to WA’s South West Region.
This region is only 24,000km2 and has 12 Local Government Areas, but isn’t the smallest region in WA.
Mining, agriculture, timber and viticulture are major industries are in the region.
It’s only a hop, step and jump from Perth, well a little more than that but it is a very popular tourist/holiday destination.
Areas within the region are famous for tall trees, wineries, waterfalls, beaches, surfing, fishing, caves and relaxation. Along with animals there is seasonal wildflowers that are unique to the area.
Not to forget Wellington Dam, the second largest dam in WA and is State Heritage listed. Plenty of camping available around the dam.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8b1ad59a-0838-4269-a950-24737da48890" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.
o To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
——————————————
