   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #093&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Goldfields - Esperance&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ad80918f-e77e-415c-8618-ff3669676f2e"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ad80918f-e77e-415c-8618-ff3669676f2e&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;On the Eyre Highway is a famous stretch of road. What is it called?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b9d3d37d-c29b-4677-9244-cf5c358affe4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Goldfields - Esperance region.
This region is our largest at a whopping 955,000+km2.
Its covers our south east coastline through to the South Australian border incorporating some of the Nullabor Plain.

Mining of gold and nickel are the primary mineral resources in the goldfields area while agriculture with wheat, canola and barley. Then also sheep and cattle grazing along with fishing and aquaculture.

Kalgoorlie - Boulder has a rich gold history and many lovely old buildings.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8b1ad59a-0838-4269-a950-24737da48890" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.
o To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
