   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #093&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Peel&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ad80918f-e77e-415c-8618-ff3669676f2e"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ad80918f-e77e-415c-8618-ff3669676f2e&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;There is a large fish statue on the bank of the Hotham River. What type of fish is it?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5a95166b-152d-4ae7-9109-00181a3d592d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Peel region.
It has an area of around 6,650km2 and borders the Perth metro area. 
It reaches from the coast to inland rural areas.
Mining and mineral processing dominate the region with agriculture and equine industry being important too.
Peel is a sort after area to live as has coastal, farming, native forests, estuaries, dams and escarpments. Mandurah is the most populated area and being a city has everything you need.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8b1ad59a-0838-4269-a950-24737da48890" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.
