   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #093&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Perth&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ad80918f-e77e-415c-8618-ff3669676f2e"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ad80918f-e77e-415c-8618-ff3669676f2e&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The Fremantle Markets were established in what year?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5977ef7a-f2a3-4de1-b6c6-f2af5220678d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Perth region.
This region is where our States capital city is located on the Swan River. 
Its area is over 6,000kms. It extends from the coast to the hills.
The metro region comprises of five (5) subregions and 30 local government areas.
Within this region Fremantle would have to be my favourite with its history and historical buildings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8b1ad59a-0838-4269-a950-24737da48890" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.
