   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #072&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Koolbardi&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5a107d7b-610f-449e-a066-f6d674944ea8"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5a107d7b-610f-449e-a066-f6d674944ea8&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What bird is this?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/43777462-1d5c-4877-bc99-6bc47b04bb66" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is a black and white bird, described as one of Australia's most accomplished songbirds. In spring, some males become aggressive, swooping and attacking anyone who comes near their nest.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/544562d7-6c50-42f9-8d90-c18678cf7ed6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

