   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #007&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Stage 4 - Lake Cave&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/26579967-cdc9-4ac3-896a-32cc1cffd89a"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/26579967-cdc9-4ac3-896a-32cc1cffd89a&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What makes Lake Cave special inside?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f202e151-6247-4b93-a032-2cd48b1acfa3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; Location: Margaret River region, WA

Lake Cave is a beautiful underground cave with a calm, crystal-clear lake inside. It’s the only cave in WA with a permanent lake. One of its most famous features is a hanging crystal "table" — a rock formation that looks like it's floating above the water. The reflections on the water make the cave feel magical.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7205d174-5558-4b79-ab98-b3f740519b03" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka
off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs
to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry
Terminal.
To join this project, please contact the project Admins on
WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
