 <wpt lat="-32.051083" lon="115.740383">
  <ele>3.0</ele>
  <time>2025-05-31T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LB3hce-01</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa08P</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/baa1dfa5-64aa-4e83-ba3e-4006b529d1cc</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #088 : S1 Pilbara by dimor</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918797" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #088 : S1 Pilbara</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>dimor</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">dimor</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #088&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Pilbara&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/baa1dfa5-64aa-4e83-ba3e-4006b529d1cc"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/baa1dfa5-64aa-4e83-ba3e-4006b529d1cc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What town in the Pilbara is the famous Red Dog statue located?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/63567c0c-c3c2-4984-b159-92ee479a1a52" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the region of iron ore mining and big trucks, long trains and huge ships.
Also Perth, Peel, South West and other regions get their natural gas from, the gas you have in your home.
It is the second biggest region in WA at a whopping 
507,896km2. It extends from the coast to the state border.
There is more to the Pilbara than iron ore, there is ancient rock art, lovely weather (though very hot and humid in summer), national parks with magnificent gorges, a ghost town, and a laid back casual lifestyle.
What’s not to love ?? 

Note: The above image is from the Government of Western Australia Infrastructure Western Australia website&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b33cf88e-ef97-47b2-b029-ad2cbacbcf55" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.
o To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
  - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - 
Western Australia is a vast,  diverse and beautiful State. Within our state border we have 10 regions, this AdLab will feature my five (5) favourites.
The other five (5) are Great Southern, South West, Goldfields - Esperance, Peel and Perth&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
