   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #088&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Wheatbelt&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/baa1dfa5-64aa-4e83-ba3e-4006b529d1cc"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/baa1dfa5-64aa-4e83-ba3e-4006b529d1cc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Which town in the Wheatbelt has the Tin Horse Highway&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7a27bbea-1c51-4c37-aa40-e3ccdb85bcd2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Wheatbelt is our wheat and mainly sheep agricultural region.
It has an area of 154, 862km2 and a large number of local government areas, a huge 42, which means the region is made up of many towns. From the coast to around the middle of the state.
There is a lot to see and do in this region. There are plenty of rock formations, little cute towns with lovely little museums, hot air ballooning, sky diving, 4wd tracks, fishing and lots more. Get out there and see for yourself.
It’s my favourite region to go camping in but gets very cold in winter.

Note: The above image is from the Government of Western Australia Infrastructure Western Australia website&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b33cf88e-ef97-47b2-b029-ad2cbacbcf55" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.
