   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #088&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Gascoyne&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/baa1dfa5-64aa-4e83-ba3e-4006b529d1cc"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/baa1dfa5-64aa-4e83-ba3e-4006b529d1cc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What town in the Gascoyne area is famous for swimming with whale sharks&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9fe2cc7d-a7b5-445b-bbb0-ad8e1b7ffe8e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Gascoyne region is a major  area for Western Australia’s horticulture - bananas, mangoes, table grapes and tomatoes to name a few, and fishing - prawns, scallops, fish and more.
Salt and gypsum are also mined in this region.
The region has an area of 137,938km2. It has about 600km of coastline and extends inland for around 500km.

There is so much to see and do in the region from the World Heritage Sites of Ningaloo Reef and Shark Bay, Mount Augustus which is twice the size of Ulu?u, national parks and more. Let’s not forget the very enjoyable weather. It is a great region to take a holiday to.

Note: The above image is from the Government of Western Australia Infrastructure Western Australia website&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b33cf88e-ef97-47b2-b029-ad2cbacbcf55" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.
