   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #088&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Kimberley&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/baa1dfa5-64aa-4e83-ba3e-4006b529d1cc"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/baa1dfa5-64aa-4e83-ba3e-4006b529d1cc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What animals are famous on Cable Beach&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2fbdea74-518b-4812-9c4c-25744c923693" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Kimberley, Western Australia’s most northern region.
This region is 424,517kms in size which is three times the size of England, twice the size of Victoria, and is bordered by coastline, Northern Territory and the Pilbara region.
Mining, construction, tourism, retail, agriculture and pearling are the major industries of the Kimberley region.
The Kimberley consists of ancient mountains ranges, World Heritage Site, king tides, national parks, the famous Gibb River Road, dinosaur footprints and a pristine beach making it a region with plenty to see and do.
It has a tropical monsoon climate with a wet season and cyclones

Note: The above image is from the Government of Western Australia Infrastructure Western Australia website&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b33cf88e-ef97-47b2-b029-ad2cbacbcf55" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.
