   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #088&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Mid West&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/baa1dfa5-64aa-4e83-ba3e-4006b529d1cc"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/baa1dfa5-64aa-4e83-ba3e-4006b529d1cc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Sandstone has a famous rock formation. What is it called?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0a0db1d1-7de5-4ddb-92fd-4184c20b603d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Midwest region of Western Australia..
This region has part of our two major highways heading north, the Great Northern Highway and the North West Coast Highway.
It has an area of around 285,500 km2.
The coastal area is mainly agricultural and fishing while inland is dominated by mining of gold, iron ore, nickel and other minerals. There is a Square Kilometre Array (SKA) and the WA Space Centre making it an area of space science.
You can see old townsites with historical buildings, meteorite crater, HMAS Sydney Memorial, swimming beaches, the big tractor, wildflowers and much more. This region is worthy of a visit.

Note: The above image is from the Government of Western Australia Infrastructure Western Australia website&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b33cf88e-ef97-47b2-b029-ad2cbacbcf55" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.
