   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #071&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Norfolk Hotel Carving &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/65dc793a-8aaf-4175-81a7-53e90db1229c"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/65dc793a-8aaf-4175-81a7-53e90db1229c&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Before entering politics Dorothy was part of what profession? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1ac365a3-9f1c-4bba-8ba5-3707c6dd7611" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A unique portrait of the first woman member of the Australian Senate (1943). The artwork is carved into the side of the Norfolk Hotel building using construction tools.

Dame Dorothy Margaret Tangney DBE (13 March 1907 – 3 June 1985) was an Australian politician. She was a member of the Australian Labor Party (ALP) and served as a Senator for Western Australia from 1943 to 1968. She was the first woman elected to the Senate and one of the first two women elected to federal parliament, along with Enid Lyons&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7a027cb5-953b-4bcb-aa16-94006b15712d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.  This series will take you on a quick tour of some of my fav public Art installations in Fremantle. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
