   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #007&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Stage 3 - Lake Ballard&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/26579967-cdc9-4ac3-896a-32cc1cffd89a"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/26579967-cdc9-4ac3-896a-32cc1cffd89a&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What makes Lake Ballard different from other salt lakes?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f219bd1e-5d66-46e0-8011-cda495d9475c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; Location: Goldfields region, WA

Lake Ballard is a huge salt lake in the outback that becomes a wide, flat white plain when it dries out. But what really makes it special is the 51 metal sculptures placed all across the salt by artist Antony Gormley. This outdoor art installation is called "Inside Australia", and the lake looks especially magical at sunrise and sunset.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7205d174-5558-4b79-ab98-b3f740519b03" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka
off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs
to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry
Terminal.
To join this project, please contact the project Admins on
WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
