  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa07n</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/65dc793a-8aaf-4175-81a7-53e90db1229c</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #071 : S3 Bon Scott - Fishing Boat Harbour by The Machman</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918811" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #071 : S3 Bon Scott - Fishing Boat Harbour</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>The Machman</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">The Machman</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #071&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Bon Scott - Fishing Boat Harbour&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/65dc793a-8aaf-4175-81a7-53e90db1229c"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/65dc793a-8aaf-4175-81a7-53e90db1229c&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;In 1979 AC/DC released a song called “Highway to ……..”?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6be9d9d6-bb3a-431b-8888-8f1a3febfa60" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ronald Belford Scott, or Bon Scott the was born in Scotland, but came to Fremantle with his parents. 
He was a troubled young man, who died in London in 1980, at the age of 33. His ashes are in the Fremantle Cemetery. 
A bronze statue of Bon was unveiled near the harbour in October 2008, sculpted by Greg James.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7a027cb5-953b-4bcb-aa16-94006b15712d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.  This series will take you on a quick tour of some of my fav public Art installations in Fremantle. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.050967" lon="115.7401">
  <ele>2.0</ele>
  <time>2025-06-02T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBThjT-02</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa07D</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/65dc793a-8aaf-4175-81a7-53e90db1229c</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #071 : S2 Dingo Flour by The Machman</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918809" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #071 : S2 Dingo Flour</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>The Machman</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">The Machman</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #071&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Dingo Flour&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/65dc793a-8aaf-4175-81a7-53e90db1229c"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/65dc793a-8aaf-4175-81a7-53e90db1229c&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The dingo logo was originally painted by artist Les Nash in 1940. How much was he paid to complete the work? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/60870157-3b02-49e5-a733-4b8411c5bfb4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Dingo Flour sign is a stylised silhouetted dingo in red on the side of a historic and heritage-listed working flour mill in North Fremantle, Western Australia.

The mill is in a complex known as the Great Southern Roller Flour Mills Limited. On the site (which dates from 1922) are silos, an office and laboratory and other buildings. There was a second Dingo Flour mill in Narrogin from 1903 to late October 1912, when a new company was formed to take over from the Co-operative company.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7a027cb5-953b-4bcb-aa16-94006b15712d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.  This series will take you on a quick tour of some of my fav public Art installations in Fremantle. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.05105" lon="115.74">
  <ele>1.0</ele>
