   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #023&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Fremantle Prison &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/034e1012-bfa7-4062-9365-3fc82b458a4b"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/034e1012-bfa7-4062-9365-3fc82b458a4b&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year did the Fremantle Prison close? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4392f1cb-bb98-4cb3-8414-66c081aecb95" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fremantle Prison, sometimes referred to as Fremantle Gaol or Fremantle Jail, is a former Australian prison and World Heritage Site in Fremantle, Western Australia. The site includes the prison cellblocks, gatehouse, perimeter walls, cottages, and tunnels. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e623438e-fd44-4ad6-b804-36293b09b351" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on the stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal. 

To join this project, please contact the project admins at WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
