 <wpt lat="-32.0526" lon="115.738917">
  <ele>1.0</ele>
  <time>2025-06-01T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBrD1H-05</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLab5W</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/6aefa9f5-402e-4323-98e6-98e589f12709</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #57 : S5 Western Ringtail Possum The Threatened Species by ringtailposs</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918948" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #57 : S5 Western Ringtail Possum The Threatened Species</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>ringtailposs</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">ringtailposs</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #57&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Western Ringtail Possum The Threatened Species&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/6aefa9f5-402e-4323-98e6-98e589f12709"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/6aefa9f5-402e-4323-98e6-98e589f12709&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What colour is the tip of a Western Ringtail Possums tail&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ae150af4-13ce-465f-b5e0-9e8df782f783" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Western Ringtail possum is a threatened species, their numbers are declining and the spread of the species is dewindling at an alarming rate. 
People who live with possums, will tell you different because we live with them every day. They can be a nuisence ,when they eat your garden or get in your roof or pee on everthing and annoy the dogs. People who live in heavily populated areas of possums will either love them or hate them, personally i love them, ive raised about 300 and released them in areas away from Busselton to populate other pockets.
Not only do they have to deal with enviromental changes and loss of trees and land they become prey to dogs cats humans, birds of prey and rats . Human feeding is also not helpful ,as most of the public have no knowledge of feeding the possums so the feed fruit ,which upsets their gut flora. It also brings the animal to the ground , thos opens them up to predation. Or other injuries can  be severe burns fron shed roof tops or uncovered bbq, electrocution for biting wiring.
A baby possum in care will need hand feeding every 2 to 4 hours with specific milk. They will then be weaned to natural foids this could take up to nine months.
Volunteers not only put up their time but most time the buy formular and cages from their own pocket. So put your hands together for the volunteers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b6e82859-eca9-4e67-84b3-bb622d92c854" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - Which intendsto form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth.
There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved between Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.
This ones about another of our beautiful marsupials, the Western Ringtail Possum. Some will tell you its a load of baloney and absolutly detest them but then theres others whom see them as the endangered species that they are ,and how beautiful they actually are. Most of us that do see them this way have had the pleasure of hand raising one ,two or 300. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
