   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #59&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Stage 2&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/644764ce-8780-4faf-9530-225730724bfb"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/644764ce-8780-4faf-9530-225730724bfb&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What ecological role does the Quenda play in its environment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e30977ec-0547-4e47-a92d-c1f2eae938eb" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Quokka is an iconic Australian marsupial here is a multiple choice question about another Q named Australian marsupial. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5cb82be2-a1b8-4b54-8534-0f01d3f3e85f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome too the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.
 
To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
