 <wpt lat="-32.052033" lon="115.74105">
  <ele>2.0</ele>
  <time>2025-06-04T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LB8cLK-05</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa08F</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1698ad06-2bfc-440e-95d2-782515120d7d</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #085 : S5 WA Feeding the World by Cirrus_WA</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1437" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #085 : S5 WA Feeding the World</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Cirrus_WA</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Cirrus_WA</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #085&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;WA Feeding the World&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1698ad06-2bfc-440e-95d2-782515120d7d"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1698ad06-2bfc-440e-95d2-782515120d7d&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the major Wheat growing region in Western Australia?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4b9dd2c7-26bd-4411-b63d-06f2802bbf11" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Western Australia is a major exporter of wheat, producing around half of Australia’s total wheat output. The state’s wheat is primarily grown in the Wheatbelt region, where vast, dry plains and advanced farming techniques support high yields. WA’s wheat is known for its high quality and is exported mainly to Asia and the Middle East, where it is used for bread, noodles, and other staple foods. Wheat exports are a key part of the state’s agricultural economy, contributing significantly to rural employment and regional development.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b67fdb39-c30a-4037-bc56-d9129f0f20e7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.


To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com


This Adventure aims to highlight some of exports that Western Australia shares with the world.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.051967" lon="115.74095">
  <ele>2.0</ele>
  <time>2025-06-04T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LB8cLK-02</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa08n</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1698ad06-2bfc-440e-95d2-782515120d7d</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #085 : S2 WA Powering the World by Cirrus_WA</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1434" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #085 : S2 WA Powering the World</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Cirrus_WA</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Cirrus_WA</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #085&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;WA Powering the World&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1698ad06-2bfc-440e-95d2-782515120d7d"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1698ad06-2bfc-440e-95d2-782515120d7d&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What continent does Western Australia ship the majority of its LNG to?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ba7016cd-cf9b-479e-b64d-c93ede89cfd8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Western Australia is a major global exporter of liquefied natural gas (LNG), with large-scale projects such as Gorgon, Wheatstone, and North West Shelf driving production. The state’s LNG is primarily sourced from offshore gas fields and processed at advanced coastal facilities before being shipped to key markets in Asia, including Japan, China, and South Korea. LNG exports play a crucial role in Western Australia’s economy, contributing significantly to state revenue and supporting thousands of jobs in engineering, operations, and logistics. The sector also positions WA as a key player in the global energy transition due to LNG’s lower carbon footprint compared to coal and oil.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b67fdb39-c30a-4037-bc56-d9129f0f20e7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.


To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com


This Adventure aims to highlight some of exports that Western Australia shares with the world.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
