 <wpt lat="-32.051983" lon="115.740983">
  <ele>2.0</ele>
  <time>2025-06-04T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LB8cLK-03</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa08D</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1698ad06-2bfc-440e-95d2-782515120d7d</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #085 : S3 WA Dazzling the World by Cirrus_WA</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1435" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #085 : S3 WA Dazzling the World</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Cirrus_WA</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Cirrus_WA</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #085&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;WA Dazzling the World&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1698ad06-2bfc-440e-95d2-782515120d7d"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1698ad06-2bfc-440e-95d2-782515120d7d&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the chemical symbol for Gold?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ccbe1ba9-57d4-4e9e-b63e-b4d1348fffe2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Western Australia is Australia’s largest producer and exporter of gold, with operations concentrated in regions like the Goldfields-Esperance and Pilbara. The state’s gold is extracted from both open-pit and underground mines, then refined and exported primarily to Asia and Europe, where it is used in jewelry, electronics, and as a financial asset. Gold exports are a vital part of WA’s economy, contributing billions in export revenue and supporting a wide range of jobs in mining, refining, and transport. The sector also benefits from strong global demand, especially during times of economic uncertainty when gold is seen as a safe-haven investment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b67fdb39-c30a-4037-bc56-d9129f0f20e7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.


To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com


This Adventure aims to highlight some of exports that Western Australia shares with the world.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.052" lon="115.741017">
  <ele>2.0</ele>
  <time>2025-06-04T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LB8cLK-04</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa107</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1698ad06-2bfc-440e-95d2-782515120d7d</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #085 : S4 WA Charging the World by Cirrus_WA</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1436" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #085 : S4 WA Charging the World</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Cirrus_WA</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Cirrus_WA</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #085&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;WA Charging the World&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1698ad06-2bfc-440e-95d2-782515120d7d"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1698ad06-2bfc-440e-95d2-782515120d7d&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Lithium is the what largest export from Western Australia?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/23aa240a-1f2f-4c0f-85e5-5611b90eea23" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Western Australia is emerging as a global powerhouse in the export of lithium and rare earth minerals, driven by the growing demand for clean energy technologies and electric vehicles. The state hosts some of the world’s richest lithium deposits, particularly in the Greenbushes and Pilgangoora regions, and is a key supplier of spodumene concentrate, a primary lithium source. WA also produces rare earth elements like neodymium and praseodymium, essential for high-performance magnets used in wind turbines and EV motors. These exports are rapidly increasing in value, positioning Western Australia as a critical player in the global shift toward sustainable energy and advanced manufacturing.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b67fdb39-c30a-4037-bc56-d9129f0f20e7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.


To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com


This Adventure aims to highlight some of exports that Western Australia shares with the world.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.05195" lon="115.7409">
  <ele>2.0</ele>
  <time>2025-06-04T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LB8cLK-01</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa08l</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1698ad06-2bfc-440e-95d2-782515120d7d</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #085 : S1 WA Building the World by Cirrus_WA</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1433" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #085 : S1 WA Building the World</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Cirrus_WA</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Cirrus_WA</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #085&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;WA Building the World&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1698ad06-2bfc-440e-95d2-782515120d7d"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1698ad06-2bfc-440e-95d2-782515120d7d&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the number one export from Western Australia&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e159194a-f7d3-4ba8-abb2-cb89caf055cb" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Western Australia is the world’s leading exporter of iron ore, supplying over half of the global demand. The state’s vast reserves, particularly in the Pilbara region, are mined by major companies. Iron ore is primarily shipped to China, Japan, and South Korea, where it is used in steel production. 
This export is the backbone of Western Australia’s economy, generating billions in revenue annually and supporting thousands of jobs across mining, transport, and port operations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b67fdb39-c30a-4037-bc56-d9129f0f20e7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.


To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com


This Adventure aims to highlight some of exports that Western Australia shares with the world.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
