   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #100&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Timber By Rail&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b4a08bbc-4bd8-4504-a994-ab3f3be58f00"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b4a08bbc-4bd8-4504-a994-ab3f3be58f00&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year was the last shipment of timber delivered to Rockingham for export overseas?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e829f647-570f-459a-b616-b4366fb11a5b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Jarrahdale and Dwellingup timber mills provided large quantities of timber for overseas export. A railway line was built to deliver the timber to Rockingham for shipment overseas. 
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e871336a-ecef-43a2-a284-02737accb5ac" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.
 
To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
