   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #100&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Public Passenger Train&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b4a08bbc-4bd8-4504-a994-ab3f3be58f00"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b4a08bbc-4bd8-4504-a994-ab3f3be58f00&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Which towns did the train travel between?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1948ab19-76b1-4592-bc83-a8d2f3425f3e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The transportation of lead and copper to the port lead to the first regular passenger train to run in WA on December 19, 1876. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e871336a-ecef-43a2-a284-02737accb5ac" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.
 
To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
