   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #100&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Intrastate Train Travel&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b4a08bbc-4bd8-4504-a994-ab3f3be58f00"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b4a08bbc-4bd8-4504-a994-ab3f3be58f00&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the train used on this line?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1ef3af99-c044-4b42-a906-dcd862726456" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;TransWA provides a daily service from East Perth to Kalgoorlie and Kalgoorlie to Perth stopping at towns along the way when required. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e871336a-ecef-43a2-a284-02737accb5ac" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.
 
To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
