  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918893" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #094 : S5 Surf’s Up - Smith’s Beach</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>geogypsys</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">geogypsys</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #094&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Surf’s Up - Smith’s Beach&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/13c0ff43-633d-47d3-8ff3-9d4b7f54aefc"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/13c0ff43-633d-47d3-8ff3-9d4b7f54aefc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Before heading out for a Surf, the Best thing to do is?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d121b10a-fe16-42c3-95ad-24ee9c51f616" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Surf’s Up at Smith’s Beach ???   ???
100 kilometres of coastline and over 75 surf breaks can make finding safe, suitable surf challenging. The exposed coastline and unpredictable conditions mean there are very few surf breaks across the region suitable for beginners.

BEFORE HEADING OUT
Be sure to always observe the limits of your own capabilities. It’s best to watch the ocean for at least 15 minutes before entering the water and always chat to a local if in doubt.

SMITHS BEACH, YALLINGUP
A sometimes slabby right-hand reef break that needs a fairly large swell and high tide to really get going. 
On smaller days, it can be great for groms and beginners. The beach is patrolled in the summer months , and the reef is only 50 meters from shore. Easy to find, take Smiths Beach Road and park in the car park at the end.

In surfing, a "grom" refers to a young surfer, often under 16, who is just starting out or developing their skills. The term is a shortened version of "grommet" and has a similar meaning to "nipper" or "gremmie". While originally used for surfers, the term has also expanded to include young participants in other extreme sports like skateboarding, snowboarding, and skiing.

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e47e11c5-8c6e-4bce-8bf2-59a4eacca2d0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;o Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.
 
To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
