   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #098&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;North&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f269c9ad-7b81-4d7b-a3d7-2aaa5b3b4b02"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f269c9ad-7b81-4d7b-a3d7-2aaa5b3b4b02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the Furthest Town to the North of the State?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e42692eb-aa8c-4be7-a895-957827f3bf21" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Western Australia is the Biggest State in Australia, encompassing nearly a third of the continent, and its capital, Perth, is the most isolated major city in the world, with no other capital city closer than 2,200 km.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/91421fe8-3995-40a6-9ad7-bd231f28e8ca" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

