  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/13c0ff43-633d-47d3-8ff3-9d4b7f54aefc</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #094 : S1 Surf’s Up - 3 Bears by geogypsys</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918885" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #094 : S1 Surf’s Up - 3 Bears</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>geogypsys</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">geogypsys</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #094&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Surf’s Up - 3 Bears&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/13c0ff43-633d-47d3-8ff3-9d4b7f54aefc"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/13c0ff43-633d-47d3-8ff3-9d4b7f54aefc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What type of board would you recommend to take to 3 Bears Surf Break?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5fe32199-626a-44bf-9f9f-4a001e5b493d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Surf’s Up at Three Bears 
3 Bears is a popular surf break located south of Sugarloaf Rock, in the Capes region of Western Australia, known for its reef breaks. It's accessed by 4WD tracks and features three main breaks: Mamas, Papas, and Babys. These breaks offer a variety of wave types, catering to different conditions and surfer skill levels, according to Mondo.surf. 
Break Details:
Mamas: A nice left tube and wall, with rights also possible, best on mid to small swells.
Papas: Considered an average wave compared to Mamas and Babys.
Babys: A good peak on small swells, with the left slightly longer and performing well when the swell reaches 6 feet, offering long rides and great tubes. 
Conditions and Accessibility:
Accessibility:
Requires a 4x4 vehicle to access via 4WD tracks, says www.geosurf.com.au. 
Best Conditions:
Southwest swells and east to northeast winds are ideal for the breaks.
Difficulty:
Considered a spot for experienced surfers due to the conditions and the need for 4WD access.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e47e11c5-8c6e-4bce-8bf2-59a4eacca2d0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;o Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.
 
To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
