   <groundspeak:owner id="">geogypsys</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #094&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Surf’s Up - Yallingup - Rabbits &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/13c0ff43-633d-47d3-8ff3-9d4b7f54aefc"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/13c0ff43-633d-47d3-8ff3-9d4b7f54aefc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Rabbits is a favourite surf location of a local Pro Surfer?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d775f6c5-d34d-49ae-a572-b675901ee951" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Surf’s Up at Rabbits, Yallingup.
Yallingup is renown for its reef break off the southern end of the beach, locally know as Car Park. Depending on the size it hold lefts and right in a low swell, developing into a long left with bigger swell. There are also the beach and reef breaks accessible from the northern car park.
Where is the rabbit surf spot in Yallingup?
Just north of Yallingup Beach is Rabbit Hill, where there is a carpark and lookout over the beach. This surf break is famous as one of professional surfer Taj Burrow's favourite spots, and it features a heavy, challenging wave.
 It's an unpatrolled beach and conditions can change quickly.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e47e11c5-8c6e-4bce-8bf2-59a4eacca2d0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;o Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.
 
To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
