   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #094&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Surf’s Up - Preverly &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/13c0ff43-633d-47d3-8ff3-9d4b7f54aefc"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/13c0ff43-633d-47d3-8ff3-9d4b7f54aefc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What type of classic waves do these professional surfers battle?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/16f31fc2-486d-414b-befe-e1ac2cc014b6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Surf’s Up at Surfers Point, Preverly.

Keep your eyes on the ocean as the best professional surfers on the planet battle raw swells, big barrels and shallow ledges in the Margaret River Pro, held in May each year. Set against Margaret River’s spectacular coastline, this iconic surf competition challenges even the most seasoned professionals.

With more than 75 major surfing breaks, Margaret River’s rugged coast has earned a world-class reputation as a destination for consistent big waves. The Margaret River Pro has been part of the World Surf League (WSL) Championship Tour since 2014, with the world’s elite male and female Championship Tour surfers taking on some of the most demanding and powerful surf on the planet. Come for the festival vibes and to get up close to your surfing idols at this mobile event which transforms Surfers Point into an atmospheric event hub. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e47e11c5-8c6e-4bce-8bf2-59a4eacca2d0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;o Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.
 
To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.0513" lon="115.740583">
  <ele>2.0</ele>
  <time>2025-06-03T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBjKEz-04</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa09H</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/13c0ff43-633d-47d3-8ff3-9d4b7f54aefc</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #094 : S4 Surf’s Up - Huzzas by geogypsys</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918891" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #094 : S4 Surf’s Up - Huzzas</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>geogypsys</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">geogypsys</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #094&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Surf’s Up - Huzzas &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/13c0ff43-633d-47d3-8ff3-9d4b7f54aefc"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/13c0ff43-633d-47d3-8ff3-9d4b7f54aefc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;A Grom is a…?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0fdf1e69-a62e-4b5c-9328-665059fcd154" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Surf’s Up in the Surfers’ Playground at Hazzas  ???   ???

The coastal area around Gracetown is home to some of the region’s most famous surf breaks … a playground for surfers of all skill levels.

Learning to Surf

One of the most well known breaks suitable for those learning to surf is “Huzzas”. Located directly out from the “South Point” car park, Huzzas is a small reef break that rolls in over a shallow, weed covered, rocky ledge not far from the shore.

Groms of all ages cut their teeth learning to surf Huzzas as the wave is usually rolling (not dumping), with a long wall left and right. Plenty of time to get to your feet and learn the art of balance.

Wave size varies throughout the year however is generally considered on the small size.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e47e11c5-8c6e-4bce-8bf2-59a4eacca2d0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;o Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.
 
To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
