 <wpt lat="-32.053133" lon="115.738967">
  <ele>1.0</ele>
  <time>2025-06-04T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBJfTC-05</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa10Q</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/13708d96-7fb5-4a10-bb4f-2e0b3a335152</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #103 : S5 Quokkas by ws_cachers</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1412" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #103 : S5 Quokkas</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>ws_cachers</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">ws_cachers</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #103&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Quokkas&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/13708d96-7fb5-4a10-bb4f-2e0b3a335152"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/13708d96-7fb5-4a10-bb4f-2e0b3a335152&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Western Australia is Home to the World’s Happiest Animal, the Quokka!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/acda6f77-be64-46ca-9a6b-a6be613d6885" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Playful, adorable, friendly, and cute as a button, quokkas have recently won the title of the happiest animals on earth.  But, while quokkas are undeniably cheerful, they are gravely endangered, with less than 15,000 left in the world.  Native to Western Australia, most of these fluffy creatures live on Rottnest Island, a short boat ride from Perth.

What makes quokkas so lovable is their contagious, photo-ready smiles.  In fact, they are the ultimate selfie gods taking social media by storm with trending quokka selfies.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6b4ee582-6e6e-4db5-ac8c-d6e7eee85dd7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.052867" lon="115.73895">
  <ele>1.0</ele>
  <time>2025-06-05T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBzZL2-05</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa10m</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/03a0c9c8-f42b-4e9a-a9cf-e8c1b2d19428</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #109 : S5 What's in a name? by chrishere</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918853" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #109 : S5 What's in a name?</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>chrishere</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">chrishere</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #109&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;What's in a name?&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/03a0c9c8-f42b-4e9a-a9cf-e8c1b2d19428"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/03a0c9c8-f42b-4e9a-a9cf-e8c1b2d19428&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Which planet was named after the Roman god of the sea?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/af8413dc-1115-4022-8134-9c3a43185da6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;All of the planets, except for Earth, were named after Greek and Roman gods and goddesses. Jupiter, Saturn, Mars, Venus and Mercury were given their names thousands of years ago. The other planets were not discovered until much later, after telescopes were invented. The tradition of naming the planets after Greek and Roman gods and goddesses was carried on for the other planets discovered as well.

(Image credits: Kaiser Science and Space.com)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4e3e243e-5860-481e-86a9-7686ba28c313" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal. 

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com

This Adventure Lab is located in the southern part of Western Australia which has low humidity levels and virtually no air pollution, creating pristine night skies and the ideal location for stargazing.  In this Adveture Lab we have a quick look at a couple of our neighbours in the Solar System.
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.053133" lon="115.73885">
