  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa10L</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/13708d96-7fb5-4a10-bb4f-2e0b3a335152</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #103 : S2 Lucky Bay by ws_cachers</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1409" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #103 : S2 Lucky Bay</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>ws_cachers</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">ws_cachers</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #103&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Lucky Bay&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/13708d96-7fb5-4a10-bb4f-2e0b3a335152"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/13708d96-7fb5-4a10-bb4f-2e0b3a335152&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Luck Bay is Australia's Whitest Beach&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e733c881-e04f-4db8-9c74-a45c89d4ab92" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Western Australia is home to Lucky Bay, the country’s whitest beach.  And, that’s not an exaggeration or an ad slogan.  It’s been scientifically proven.  Twice.  We really think this is of the most fun fact about Western Australia.  Or, maybe funny facts, considering they have to prove it twice!

The whiteness of the sand has something to do with the size and composition of the dunes.  Sand samples from Lucky Bay show the finest grains of milky-colored quartz minus any impurities.  Unbelievably, Lucky Bay is only one of many beaches in this area that are so white. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6b4ee582-6e6e-4db5-ac8c-d6e7eee85dd7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
