   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #109&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Our Galaxy&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/03a0c9c8-f42b-4e9a-a9cf-e8c1b2d19428"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/03a0c9c8-f42b-4e9a-a9cf-e8c1b2d19428&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the galaxy in which we live?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/dad3ec4a-e3c5-4172-a1e9-f233192e244e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Our solar system is located in a spiral galaxy with two major arms, and two minor arms.  Our Sun is in a small, partial arm of our galaxy called the Orion Arm, or Orion Spur, between the Sagittarius and Perseus arms.   Our solar system orbits the center of the galaxy at about 828,000km/hour; and takes about 230 million years to complete one orbit around the galactic center.

(Image credits: NASA)
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4e3e243e-5860-481e-86a9-7686ba28c313" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal. 

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com

This Adventure Lab is located in the southern part of Western Australia which has low humidity levels and virtually no air pollution, creating pristine night skies and the ideal location for stargazing.  In this Adveture Lab we have a quick look at a couple of our neighbours in the Solar System.
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
