   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #109&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Rocky gas, with a touch of ice&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/03a0c9c8-f42b-4e9a-a9cf-e8c1b2d19428"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/03a0c9c8-f42b-4e9a-a9cf-e8c1b2d19428&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Of the four gas planets, which are the two largest?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8bc6213d-65c5-4492-9dfc-f36051e95b1e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In terms of composition, the planets in our solar system are categorised into rock (terrestrial), ice and gas.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4e3e243e-5860-481e-86a9-7686ba28c313" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal. 

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com

This Adventure Lab is located in the southern part of Western Australia which has low humidity levels and virtually no air pollution, creating pristine night skies and the ideal location for stargazing.  In this Adveture Lab we have a quick look at a couple of our neighbours in the Solar System.
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
