   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #103&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Western Australia is Huge&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/13708d96-7fb5-4a10-bb4f-2e0b3a335152"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/13708d96-7fb5-4a10-bb4f-2e0b3a335152&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Western Australia 10 times bigger than the United Kingdom?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/24f496f7-e80f-4933-be51-8a3d28e4dc50" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Western Australia is Australia’s largest state, with a total land area of 2,527,013 square kilometres (975,685 sq. mi).

Would you believe that Western Australia is 10 times larger than the United Kingdom?  Compared to US states, Western Australia is about one-and-a-half times the size of Alaska and about three-and-a-half times the size of Texas.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6b4ee582-6e6e-4db5-ac8c-d6e7eee85dd7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
