 <wpt lat="-32.0522" lon="115.73875">
  <ele>1.0</ele>
  <time>2025-06-03T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBjDtw-01</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa06p</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cd919853-e9e3-4aec-9723-3d2dd1992f84</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #065 : S1 Swamps on stamps by WA K Team</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1523" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #065 : S1 Swamps on stamps</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>WA K Team</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">WA K Team</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #065&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Swamps on stamps&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cd919853-e9e3-4aec-9723-3d2dd1992f84"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cd919853-e9e3-4aec-9723-3d2dd1992f84&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What was the denomination for the famous inverted swan stamp?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/92b0dcfa-38f8-4495-a197-4c764b4a6b92" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Western Australia, aka The Swan River Colony established its postal service soon after settlment in 1829.  In December of that year, Fremantle's harbourmaster was appointed the first postmaster. 
The colony issued its first postage stamp on 1 August 1854. In keeping with its early title as the Swan River Colony the black swan was chosen to be featured on its stamps and the 1d black was the first issue.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9d97a8a5-760a-4abc-bf42-cde9646d96d8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

This AdLab explores "The Postal History of Western Australia' - ie WA post &amp; stamps prior to federation.
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
