   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #065&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Queen Victoria&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cd919853-e9e3-4aec-9723-3d2dd1992f84"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cd919853-e9e3-4aec-9723-3d2dd1992f84&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What was the highest Value stamps issued depicting Queen Victoria?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/55720af5-3ab7-4b14-885f-075232a407b3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;WA resisted the pressure to issue a postage stamp depicting the ruling monarch until 1900. It finally issued high value stamps with the bust of Queen Victoria in 1902 which were used until Australian stamps were issued in 1913. Unfortunately Queen Victoria died in 1901 so WA never had postage stamps in use depicting a living Monarch.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9d97a8a5-760a-4abc-bf42-cde9646d96d8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

This AdLab explores "The Postal History of Western Australia' - ie WA post &amp; stamps prior to federation.
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.05285" lon="115.73875">
