   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #107&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Perth's Tall Buildings - QV1&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/fe304deb-7b07-4465-a6c9-c89eee63b1cb"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/fe304deb-7b07-4465-a6c9-c89eee63b1cb&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many floors in the building?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9f0dcb45-6e44-4abd-8893-4abf814dc1e1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;QV1 is a 40-storey modernist skyscraper, completed in 1991, the 163-metre building is the fourth-tallest building in Perth, after Central Park, Brookfield Place and 108 St Georges Terrace.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/080c6895-e4d0-4673-89de-434f8c4b1196" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
