   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #106&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Moral Compass - Compassion&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1f37cafa-ae2d-4520-b4ff-26f58b289c9b"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1f37cafa-ae2d-4520-b4ff-26f58b289c9b&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the moral lesson for this stage?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9a1c5887-05cd-4aca-9bad-94782d9ecded" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Compassion is a feeling of sympathy and concern for the suffering or misfortune of another, coupled with a strong desire to alleviate that suffering.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/24b3a78d-6654-45b4-896f-952a12cb5676" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
