   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #106&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Moral Compass - Respect&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1f37cafa-ae2d-4520-b4ff-26f58b289c9b"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1f37cafa-ae2d-4520-b4ff-26f58b289c9b&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the moral lesson for this stage?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/bc217eba-cdb2-40b9-8b97-28dbef81dfb8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Respect is showing regard and consideration for others and their views, even if you don't agree with them. It's about valuing someone for who they are and treating them with courtesy and care.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/24b3a78d-6654-45b4-896f-952a12cb5676" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
