  <name>LBuo51-01</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa06h</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/62a9f3d6-096f-465d-93dd-fa3b6d0be15a</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #062 : S1 Shades of Fremantle: North Fremantle by Lachlan1.77</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918915" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #062 : S1 Shades of Fremantle: North Fremantle</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Lachlan1.77</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Lachlan1.77</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #062&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Shades of Fremantle: North Fremantle&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/62a9f3d6-096f-465d-93dd-fa3b6d0be15a"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/62a9f3d6-096f-465d-93dd-fa3b6d0be15a&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Which suburb is located to the north of Fremantle?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8431939d-5bc2-478c-8700-64d69bb72d43" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;North Fremantle is a unique and diverse suburb in Perth, Western Australia, ideally situated on a peninsula. To its west lies the Indian Ocean, offering pristine beaches like Leighton Beach and Port Beach, famous for their strong "Fremantle Doctor" sea breeze, making them perfect for wind and kite surfing. To its east, the suburb is bordered by the tranquil Swan River and the bustling Fremantle Inner Harbour, Western Australia's main port.

Historically an industrial area, North Fremantle has undergone significant modernisation. While it retains some of its original working-class charm and the iconic Dingo Flour Mill, recent developments at Leighton Beach, Rocky Bay, and Northbank have introduced a more upscale, manicured atmosphere with luxury waterfront homes.

Residents enjoy a relaxed coastal lifestyle combined with a vibrant community spirit. The suburb boasts a growing array of locally-owned cafes, restaurants, and bars, particularly along Stirling Highway, contributing to its dynamic culinary scene. Excellent public transport, including a train station, connects North Fremantle to both Fremantle city centre and Perth's CBD. This blend of industrial heritage, natural beauty, and contemporary amenities makes North Fremantle a highly desirable place to live for a diverse demographic.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9cb94bfb-8343-463e-8a15-1202e656787c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
