  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918919" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #062 : S3 Shades of Fremantle: East Fremantle</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Lachlan1.77</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Lachlan1.77</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #062&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Shades of Fremantle: East Fremantle&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/62a9f3d6-096f-465d-93dd-fa3b6d0be15a"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/62a9f3d6-096f-465d-93dd-fa3b6d0be15a&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What suburb is located to the east of Fremantle?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7b3967ef-b81e-46b7-b518-1619090ab2a8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;East Fremantle, affectionately known as "East Freo," is an affluent and picturesque suburb of Perth, Western Australia, located about 13 km southwest of the central business district. Bounded by the serene Swan River to its north and west, it offers a tranquil riverside lifestyle with many properties boasting expansive water views.

Primarily residential, East Fremantle is celebrated for its commitment to preserving its rich history and heritage. The suburb features a captivating blend of architectural styles, from charming workers' cottages dating back to the late 1800s gold rush to more stately homes and contemporary designs. The Town of East Fremantle has actively encouraged the retention of its heritage homes and tree-lined streetscapes, resisting extensive infill development.

Life in East Fremantle is characterised by a strong sense of community and an outdoor-oriented way of life. The suburb provides abundant green spaces, parks, and scenic river foreshore paths, perfect for walking, cycling, and various recreational activities. It's home to elite sporting clubs, including the East Fremantle Yacht Club and the East Fremantle Football Club.

The vibrant George Street precinct is a popular hub, offering a delightful array of boutique retail, cafes, restaurants, and bars. Other well-loved establishments like The Left Bank also provide fantastic dining experiences with beautiful river views. East Fremantle balances its quiet, residential charm with convenient access to the bustling Fremantle city centre, just a few kilometres away. This unique combination of history, natural beauty, and modern amenities makes East Fremantle a highly desirable place to live.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9cb94bfb-8343-463e-8a15-1202e656787c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
