 <wpt lat="-32.05245" lon="115.738333">
  <ele>1.0</ele>
  <time>2025-06-05T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBuo51-04</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa125</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/62a9f3d6-096f-465d-93dd-fa3b6d0be15a</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #062 : S4 Shades of Fremantle: Fremantle by Lachlan1.77</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918921" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #062 : S4 Shades of Fremantle: Fremantle</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Lachlan1.77</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Lachlan1.77</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #062&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Shades of Fremantle: Fremantle&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/62a9f3d6-096f-465d-93dd-fa3b6d0be15a"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/62a9f3d6-096f-465d-93dd-fa3b6d0be15a&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Which suburb to located south of North Fremantle, west of East Fremantle and north of South Fremantle?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/78ea8785-4f27-4e94-8f1e-bafa64a17fb9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fremantle, affectionately known as "Freo," is a historic port city and vibrant suburb in Western Australia, located at the mouth of the Swan River, approximately 18 km southwest of Perth's CBD. Settled in 1829, it boasts a rich history evident in its well-preserved Victorian and Edwardian streetscapes, convict-era architecture, and maritime heritage.

Today, Fremantle is a thriving hub known for its bohemian spirit and a dynamic arts and culinary scene. The famous "Cappuccino Strip" on South Terrace is a popular spot for al fresco dining, while the Fishing Boat Harbour offers fresh seafood and microbreweries. The Fremantle Markets, established in 1897, remain a beloved institution with over 150 diverse stalls.

Beyond its cultural offerings, Fremantle provides a relaxed coastal lifestyle with easy access to beaches like Bathers Beach and the Swan River. It's also home to significant landmarks like the Fremantle Prison (a UNESCO World Heritage site), the Western Australian Maritime Museum, and the Shipwreck Galleries.

Fremantle's unique blend of history, culture, and coastal charm makes it a popular destination for both residents and tourists, offering a lively and eclectic atmosphere with something for everyone.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9cb94bfb-8343-463e-8a15-1202e656787c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.05245" lon="115.7383">
  <ele>1.0</ele>
  <time>2025-06-05T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBuo51-05</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa126</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/62a9f3d6-096f-465d-93dd-fa3b6d0be15a</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #062 : S5 Shades of Fremantle: West Fremantle by Lachlan1.77</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918923" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #062 : S5 Shades of Fremantle: West Fremantle</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Lachlan1.77</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Lachlan1.77</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #062&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Shades of Fremantle: West Fremantle&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/62a9f3d6-096f-465d-93dd-fa3b6d0be15a"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/62a9f3d6-096f-465d-93dd-fa3b6d0be15a&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Is West Fremantle a real suburb?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e9ad777b-d9c4-4562-a340-5730d9a1af33" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;West Fremantle is a hypothetical, vibrant coastal suburb of Perth, Western Australia, nestled directly on the Indian Ocean coastline, immediately west of the established Fremantle city centre. Unlike its historic neighbours, West Fremantle is a more recent development, having emerged from a reimagined former industrial foreshore and reclaimed land, transforming into a sleek, modern, and highly sought-after residential and leisure destination.

This imagined suburb is characterised by striking contemporary architecture, with high-rise apartments and luxury townhouses designed to maximise the breathtaking ocean views. Its streetscapes are meticulously planned, featuring wide boulevards, public art installations, and extensive green spaces that seamlessly blend with the coastal environment.

West Fremantle's allure lies in its direct and unparalleled access to the ocean. Imagine expansive, pristine beaches – perhaps named "Sunset Sands" or "Ocean Vista Beach" – perfect for swimming, surfing, and enjoying Perth's iconic sunsets. A lively, state-of-the-art marina would be a central feature, accommodating recreational boats and offering various water sports activities.

The commercial heart of West Fremantle would be a chic, pedestrian-friendly precinct brimming with high-end boutiques, gourmet restaurants, sophisticated bars, and art galleries, catering to a discerning clientele. Large, modern public parks and foreshore promenades would provide ample space for recreation and community events.

While lacking the deep historical roots of its 'Freo' counterparts, West Fremantle would cultivate its own identity as a beacon of modern coastal living. It would attract a demographic of young professionals, affluent families, and retirees seeking a luxurious, convenient, and visually stunning lifestyle directly on the Indian Ocean. Its proximity to Fremantle's cultural attractions, combined with its unique contemporary appeal, would make "West Freo" a hypothetical jewel in Perth'&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9cb94bfb-8343-463e-8a15-1202e656787c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
