   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #014&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Emergency Services - Fire Brigade &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/731825ae-3aad-4891-9bfd-e36533ea89a7"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/731825ae-3aad-4891-9bfd-e36533ea89a7&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year did the first fire brigade commence service in WA?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/52673f26-d107-4b6d-8345-7aa0dcec496a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Department of Fire and Emergency Services (DFES) provides the state fire brigade services in Western Australia (WA). The history of this emergency service can be traced back to the early years of the Swan River Colony. As the colony's population began to grow, residents started requesting that the authorities of the colonial government begin providing community services. One of the first services to be established was a fire brigade.
Today DFES is responsible for the management, training and funding of career and volunteer Services that include

- Career Fire and Rescue Service
- Bushfire Service 
- State Emergency Service 
- Volunteer Fire and Emergency Services 
- Volunteer Fire and Rescue Service 
- Marine Rescue Service 
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9d89ab20-f34b-41d6-8118-b3c0cfb39dfb" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
