  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918929" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #014 : S3 Emergency Services - Police</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>I C Nothing</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">I C Nothing</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #014&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Emergency Services - Police &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/731825ae-3aad-4891-9bfd-e36533ea89a7"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/731825ae-3aad-4891-9bfd-e36533ea89a7&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The Police Force in Western Australia was formally established in ?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ea0a957b-94cf-4b55-97fd-90f1974cf561" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Western Australia Police Force, colloquially WAPF, provides police services throughout the state of Western Australia.  Western Australia's police force started with 15 peace-keeping constables working part time and paid for services they performed on behalf of the Courts and local Justices in 1829.
Their responsibility was to maintain public order in Perth and Fremantle colonies.

In 1840, the first full-time constable for Perth was appointed. On 11 May 1849, the colony's Legislative Council passed a Police Ordinance which outlined police powers and responsibilities. On 5 March 1853, the Western Australian Colonial Secretary, W.A. Stanford, signed a notice published in the Government Gazette, formally establishing the Police Force as a "united, structured body".

By 1861, the Police Force consisted of around 75 commissioned officers. 
Today the WAPF has around 10,000 police employees.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9d89ab20-f34b-41d6-8118-b3c0cfb39dfb" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
