 <wpt lat="-32.053217" lon="115.73775">
  <ele>1.0</ele>
  <time>2025-06-02T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBqA2d-04</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa117</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/731825ae-3aad-4891-9bfd-e36533ea89a7</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #014 : S4 Emergency Service - SES by I C Nothing</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918931" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #014 : S4 Emergency Service - SES</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>I C Nothing</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">I C Nothing</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #014&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Emergency Service - SES&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/731825ae-3aad-4891-9bfd-e36533ea89a7"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/731825ae-3aad-4891-9bfd-e36533ea89a7&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;In what year was the State Emergency Service established?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/199f5b11-d620-4ae0-be72-5f17b207a4f3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The State Emergency Service began as a civil defence organisation but evolved into an emergency response to combat civil disasters including fires, floods, cyclones, railway and aircraft accidents, explosions and locating lost civilians.

When the SES was originally was established, it came under the responsibility of the Commissioner of Police and for many years remained a department within the Police Force until 1999. In 1999 the Fire and Emergency Service Authority (FESA) was established which brought together the SES and Fire emergency services under one authority.

SES is a volunteer emergency service with many members providing the community with countless hours of service.  SES Volunteers are easily recognised by their orange overalls with the letters “State Emergency Service” emblazoned on the back when providing rescues and ensuring the public's safety.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9d89ab20-f34b-41d6-8118-b3c0cfb39dfb" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
