   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #101&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Tallest Tree &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/12cba197-dfa2-433c-830e-b841ce0ffc13"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/12cba197-dfa2-433c-830e-b841ce0ffc13&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How high can a Karri tree grow?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5c1ec312-f68a-43b8-aef0-7ac2e012896c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Also known as Eucalyptus diversicolor, Karri is a tall forest tree endemic to Western Australia. It usually grows between 10 to 60 metres but can reach as high as 90 metres. You can find some of the tallest Karri Trees in the timber town of Pemberton.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/667dc5c3-5fa9-4675-a5d4-44ea6f7788f4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
