   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #102&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Stage One - Fremantle Arts Centre&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5f44b592-9006-48a7-898f-917c1e03b3c1"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5f44b592-9006-48a7-898f-917c1e03b3c1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year was the Fremantle Arts Centre built?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c309c66f-7ef9-4994-bfd3-a48bb368f732" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fremantle's most haunted places  

Fremantle Arts Centre History:
The building was originally a lunatic asylum and later a poor house, orphanage, and midwifery school. It was known for overcrowded, prison-like conditions and mistreatment of patients. 
Reports:
Visitors have reported feeling cold spots, witnessing strange lights, and seeing apparitions. Some have even reported being touched by phantom lips or having the feeling of being pushed down stairs. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0ff39bf4-4d8e-416d-93d9-9ed5881ed321" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka
off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs
to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry
Terminal.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
