  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #102 : S3 Stage Three - Roundhouse by JKJK20</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1425" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #102 : S3 Stage Three - Roundhouse</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>JKJK20</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">JKJK20</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #102&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Stage Three - Roundhouse&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5f44b592-9006-48a7-898f-917c1e03b3c1"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5f44b592-9006-48a7-898f-917c1e03b3c1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What did the executioner do to John Gavin prior to his hanging?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4900e4fa-673d-42fd-b148-40a71769de60" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fremantle's most haunted places  
Historical Significance:
The Roundhouse is the oldest public building in Western Australia and was used as a prison for colonial and indigenous prisoners. 
Execution of John Gavin:
The execution of John Gavin, a young boy, at the front of the Roundhouse in 1831 adds to the building's eerie atmosphere. John was the first person legally executed in WA. 
Numerous Stories:
Local clairvoyants and others have reported various paranormal figures haunting the Roundhouse, including John Gavin's spirit, whom many believe was innocent of the crime he was charged with : the murder of an 18 year old farmer, George Pollard. Many more ghostly stories surround the Roundhouse. Multiple women claim to have sighted a man in tattered rags, sporting a big, bushy beard and wild hair in one particular cell. He is typically described as climbing up the walls. Others have claimed to hear ghostly voices, seen strange lights and even full bodies apparitions around the Fremantle Roundhouse.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0ff39bf4-4d8e-416d-93d9-9ed5881ed321" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka
off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs
to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry
Terminal.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.053417" lon="115.73945">
