   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #049&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Perth People - Model&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5b950398-cfe4-4480-a8a8-839f76a333f4"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5b950398-cfe4-4480-a8a8-839f76a333f4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Who is this blowing up a storm?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/62daaff0-669f-4889-aa4a-a18b888a45be" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This female is an Australian model and actress.Born in Perth, Western Australia, she won a model contest when she was 18 in her home town. In 1999 she was cast in a series of commercials for the Italian branch of telecommunications company Vodafone. This led to wide exposure in both Italy and her homeland Australia, and she appeared in Vodafone advertising until 2006. She has also appeared in Italian movies and television shows, and as an actress, she played Fatma in Russell Crowe's The Water Diviner (2014) and Valkyrie in George Miller's Mad Max: Fury Road (2015).

In 2005 she became the national ambassador for "Kids Help Line" and in 2009 she was appointed the first official "National Ambassador" for "The Red Cross".&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1f72b1c1-e16c-4b12-8c7d-5756dd2e4954" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
