   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #102&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Stage Five - Fremantle Cemetery&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5f44b592-9006-48a7-898f-917c1e03b3c1"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5f44b592-9006-48a7-898f-917c1e03b3c1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year was the first burial at Fremantle Cemetery?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6129f365-dec1-48b3-9842-1c255a096338" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fremantle's most haunted places  
Fremantle Cemetery is known for paranormal activity and is considered one of Perth's most haunted places. Stories and accounts of ghostly occurrences have been reported over the years. One notable example is a reported sighting of a hand rising from a grave, which startled mourners. The cemetery's history, including the burial of notable figures and murderers, may contribute to these claims. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0ff39bf4-4d8e-416d-93d9-9ed5881ed321" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka
off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs
to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry
Terminal.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
