   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #049&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Perth People - Sportsman&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5b950398-cfe4-4480-a8a8-839f76a333f4"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5b950398-cfe4-4480-a8a8-839f76a333f4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Who is this Perth born thrill seeker?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0b467606-9280-4d5c-b5be-2dd362226839" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This male is an Australian racing driver, who most recently competed in Formula One from 2011 to 2024. He won eight Formula One Grands Prix across 14 seasons.

Born and raised in Perth to Italian-Australian parents, he began competitive kart racing aged nine. Graduating to junior formulae in 2005, he debuted in his regional Formula Ford championship. He won his first title at the 2008 Formula Renault 2.0 West European Cup with SG Formula, before winning the 2009 British Formula 3 Championship with Carlin. He then progressed to Formula Renault 3.5, finishing runner-up to Mikhail Aleshin by two points in his rookie season. He made his Formula One debut at the 2011 British Grand Prix with HRT as part of the Red Bull Junior Team, replacing Narain Karthikeyan for the remainder of the 2011 season. He earned a full-time drive with Toro Rosso in 2012 and competed in two seasons for them alongside Jean-Éric Vergne, scoring several points finishes in each.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1f72b1c1-e16c-4b12-8c7d-5756dd2e4954" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
