   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #108&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;It's a Gold Mine&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ece5ba8b-3732-4395-8044-41239cc446f3"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ece5ba8b-3732-4395-8044-41239cc446f3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Which gold mine is the deepest in Western Australia?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a3fe1908-c90d-4f75-b19e-6bb3dcef8c3d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;While images of old-timers panning for gold spring to mind, the majority of the world’s gold is hard rock mined using open pit or underground tunnels to recover the gold straight from the rock where it was once formed. Both types of mine are common in Western Australia, although the open Super Pit in Kalgoorlie’s ‘Golden Mile’ is perhaps the most well-known. The mine has been in operation since 1893 and has so far produced around 58million ounces of gold (with a value in excess of $300bn).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/cc132de7-e532-45ec-b47f-fa8d76f9d138" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.052817" lon="115.73885">
