   <groundspeak:placed_by>Barco</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Barco</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #108&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Any Old Iron&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ece5ba8b-3732-4395-8044-41239cc446f3"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ece5ba8b-3732-4395-8044-41239cc446f3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the estimated annual value of the iron ore that WA produces?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ddbc10bc-9b9e-4902-949f-7af519f4704f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;While not as glamorous, Western Australia is the largest iron ore supplier in the world, accounting for 98.9% of total Australian production, and 38% of the global supply (followed by Brazil at 18%). The top 5 mines in WA have an annual output of over 300million tonnes, with WA as a whole producing 840million tonnes annually. In order to move this massive bulk for export the mining companies have built a number of private heavy-haul rail networks, with the BHP Iron Ore Train operating along a 426kms route from Mount Newman to Port Hedland holding the record for being the longest train in the world (the train is 7.3kms (4.5mi) long!). 
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/cc132de7-e532-45ec-b47f-fa8d76f9d138" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
