   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #060&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Lets go for a walk.&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/df38bcaa-39aa-4ef6-bc74-f37d686e38da"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/df38bcaa-39aa-4ef6-bc74-f37d686e38da&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The Porongurups are home to which popular walk trail which provides excellent viewing when reaching the top?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d02ef0fd-27f3-4687-9fce-f8a49d49fe48" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Great Southern Region has many popular National Parks with established walking trails. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e72c31a9-c5f3-4f9f-8a98-b464d1b5e873" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com 
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
