   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #060&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Two Peoples Bay National Park&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/df38bcaa-39aa-4ef6-bc74-f37d686e38da"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/df38bcaa-39aa-4ef6-bc74-f37d686e38da&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The famous Quokka can also be found in the Two Peoples Bay National Park (True or False).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f0f89ff7-6d90-43a9-9fdf-6254cbe6e508" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Two Peoples Bay is a picturesque location close to Albany. It is well worth a visit and you can fish, relax, spot whales and even have a BBQ on the provided facilities. 

Here is the Quokka related question:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e72c31a9-c5f3-4f9f-8a98-b464d1b5e873" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com 
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
