   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #060&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Whale, ho!&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/df38bcaa-39aa-4ef6-bc74-f37d686e38da"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/df38bcaa-39aa-4ef6-bc74-f37d686e38da&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year did whaling operations officially end in Albany?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/cd5317ac-1c60-4d21-b5bb-ce423329abfe" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Albany region is well visited by various species of whale and the Albany Whaling Station was the last operating station in Australia. Whaling was Albany’s oldest industry and was established
by British, French and American whalers well before official settlement took place.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e72c31a9-c5f3-4f9f-8a98-b464d1b5e873" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com 
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
