   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #038&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Rottnest 2&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/34aec70f-3b90-4a08-bcbc-2f74f0931e2a"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/34aec70f-3b90-4a08-bcbc-2f74f0931e2a&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What Nationality was the explorer that named the island Rottnest?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/23eb012c-cf12-4ae8-91ca-635c04e0cc5a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;If you time it right you may see the ferry arriving or departing to Rottnest Island.
This Adventure lab has 5 questions about Rottnest island which can be answered without visiting the island.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3dbe1574-bd05-4ab8-995c-35b6b0f2521a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
