   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #015&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Avon Descent Facts 1&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/84d10b76-7342-4a2d-92f5-f05f4f13d201"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/84d10b76-7342-4a2d-92f5-f05f4f13d201&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Who was my Mixed Double Kayak race partner in 2000 when we came 2nd in this class.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/de605258-0606-4c04-a8cb-e9fe90875d1f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;My geocaching name is burns345 - the 345 representing my kayak race number for 11 of my 13 completed Descents.
I went in my first Avon Descent in 1984 completing only the first day from Northern to Cobbler Pool. (I only had about 3 months of training and no white water experience)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a68ed505-4730-4ed2-b905-c6cae3a3f1cc" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 300mtr geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest  Ferry Terminal
To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
