   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #015&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Avon Descent Facts 4&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/84d10b76-7342-4a2d-92f5-f05f4f13d201"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/84d10b76-7342-4a2d-92f5-f05f4f13d201&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What suburb does the Avon Descent finish in.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a9fe8035-8fa7-4dd4-9d0c-8019030f98fc" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Day 1 presents challengers with obstacles like the formidable Williamson Weir and the intricate maze of the Ti Trees. After an eventful first day of racing, participants rest at the Cobbler Pool campsite, situated 20 kilometers west of Toodyay.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a68ed505-4730-4ed2-b905-c6cae3a3f1cc" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 300mtr geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest  Ferry Terminal
To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
