   <groundspeak:placed_by>burns345</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">burns345</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #015&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Avon Descent Facts 5&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/84d10b76-7342-4a2d-92f5-f05f4f13d201"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/84d10b76-7342-4a2d-92f5-f05f4f13d201&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What Kayak Club doe the Descent pass by on day 2.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/24b550d9-fd51-43fb-af8a-06a06306405c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Day 2 of the race extends over an exhilarating 72 kilometers, offering participants a series of challenges within the valley. This section includes some major white water obstacles, such as Supershoot, Emu Falls, Championship Rapids, and Bells Rapids. The rush of navigating through the valley eventually gives way to a 30-kilometer stretch of flat water, guiding the participants towards Bayswater.
While the victors triumphantly cross the Finish Line, the true achievement lies in merely completing the course.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a68ed505-4730-4ed2-b905-c6cae3a3f1cc" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 300mtr geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest  Ferry Terminal
To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.047183" lon="115.952317">
  <ele>14.0</ele>
  <time>2025-06-16T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBa17s-04</name>
  <desc>ThornlieCockbu4</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a0c57ea5-8b75-400a-b8ed-e04ef18e2c2e</url>
  <urlname>Thornlie-Cockburn Link : S4 Thornlie by InternalLights</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-983" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Thornlie-Cockburn Link : S4 Thornlie</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>InternalLights</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">InternalLights</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Thornlie-Cockburn Link&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Thornlie &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a0c57ea5-8b75-400a-b8ed-e04ef18e2c2e"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a0c57ea5-8b75-400a-b8ed-e04ef18e2c2e&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What stand does route 216 depart from? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/106d1e28-2e73-426b-83fa-ffa2d9fb9411" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Thornlie Station opened in 2005 and went through significant upgrades to make it a ‘through station’.

The upgrades gave the station a fresh and contemporary new look with platform extensions, and a new concourse with lift, stairs and roof cover.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2154cef3-fe4a-4fdc-8506-2cec735488d9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Thornlie-Cockburn Link will be Perth’s first east-west cross line connection, making travel more flexible while providing a higher level of public transport service to Perth’s south-eastern suburbs.

Connecting the Mandurah and Armadale-Thornlie lines will open new opportunities for longer-term developments around the new Nicholson Road and Ranford Road stations.

The Thornlie-Cockburn Link will support growth and accessibility across the south-eastern suburbs by providing direct access to employment and recreation opportunities while supporting about 1,680 jobs through the new stations and upgrades to the existing Thornlie, Cockburn Central and Stadium stations.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.061933" lon="115.93515">
  <ele>20.0</ele>
