  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a0c57ea5-8b75-400a-b8ed-e04ef18e2c2e</url>
  <urlname>Thornlie-Cockburn Link : S3 Nicholson Road by InternalLights</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-982" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Thornlie-Cockburn Link : S3 Nicholson Road</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>InternalLights</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">InternalLights</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Thornlie-Cockburn Link&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Nicholson Road&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a0c57ea5-8b75-400a-b8ed-e04ef18e2c2e"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a0c57ea5-8b75-400a-b8ed-e04ef18e2c2e&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Using the plaque for the art work outside, as green symbolizes rebirth, red represents?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/dad50fc8-056a-498a-b0d3-dfb75f74bfeb" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The new Nicholson Road Station will be about 26 minutes from Perth by train and will support future long-term development in and around Canning Vale.

Users will access the station from a new shared path along Canna Drive or the shared path from the Nicholson Road underpass. Vehicle access will be through an upgraded Tulloch Way and Panama Street. 

The Noongar place name for Nicholson Road is Waitj-biddi and the narrative is ‘The emu tracks’.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2154cef3-fe4a-4fdc-8506-2cec735488d9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Thornlie-Cockburn Link will be Perth’s first east-west cross line connection, making travel more flexible while providing a higher level of public transport service to Perth’s south-eastern suburbs.

Connecting the Mandurah and Armadale-Thornlie lines will open new opportunities for longer-term developments around the new Nicholson Road and Ranford Road stations.

The Thornlie-Cockburn Link will support growth and accessibility across the south-eastern suburbs by providing direct access to employment and recreation opportunities while supporting about 1,680 jobs through the new stations and upgrades to the existing Thornlie, Cockburn Central and Stadium stations.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.075967" lon="115.897133">
