  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #054   : S3 Gracetown cliff collapse, 27 September 1996 by Chookman8</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476918971" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #054   : S3 Gracetown cliff collapse, 27 September 1996</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Chookman8</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Chookman8</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #054  &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Gracetown cliff collapse, 27 September 1996&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ecb13a2a-adf2-412e-acde-d1f8ae20ae07"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ecb13a2a-adf2-412e-acde-d1f8ae20ae07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many tonnes of rubble fell?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/db7b1855-d5a1-46f8-8abb-ab90d6044956" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The collapse of a cliff face during a surfing event at Gracetown sent shock waves through the South West and WA.

Nine people lost their lives at Huzza’s Beach when the limestone cliff and overhang suddenly collapsed during a school surfing carnival. In the days leading up to the collapse, the area had been drenched with heavy rainfall, which soaked into the rock.

On the day, local primary school children from Margaret River and Cowaramup were competing at the surfing carnival. It was the last day of school and conditions were not great, being cold and rainy.

Looking for cover, some of the children, parents and teachers had been sheltering at the base of the cliff under a three-metre rock overhang. As the cliff gave way, around 2000 tonnes of rubble fell on to the beach, killing five adults and four children.

Local emergency services raced to the scene to join the many already looking for survivors. Rescue efforts continued through the night and into the next morning. A memorial commemorating the victims now stands above the site of the collapse.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5eaa658d-5150-44de-9f47-b6ce249b4180" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;?	Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
