   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab #110&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Dragon Boat Racing WA  &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a65bb605-2d99-4e6c-9a1d-b3aed5768218"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a65bb605-2d99-4e6c-9a1d-b3aed5768218&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Dragon Boat Racing has reprentation in how many countries?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6ed603dd-2c2d-4c60-9dc0-44c6d0fada0a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Dragon Boat Racing is one of the worlds most popular sports, with representations in over 35 countries. It is the fastest growing water sport in Australia. 
Dragon Boat Racing is a fun, accessible and competitive sport for all ages who are reasonably fit, a team player and enjoy being on the water. 
Regattas are held on multi lane courses at Champion Lakes in Armadale or safe estuaries and inlets such as Leschenault Inlet in Bunbury. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4258cacb-3cb0-4313-a133-335944e2ce5c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
