   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab #110&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Dragon Boat Racing - Boats&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a65bb605-2d99-4e6c-9a1d-b3aed5768218"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a65bb605-2d99-4e6c-9a1d-b3aed5768218&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The boats are just over how many metres?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/295039d8-7c10-4458-928d-193d81a0d712" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The fibreglass boats are just over 12m long (40 ft), weigh about 255kg and holds a crew of 22 - 20 paddlers sitting side by side on 10 benches, as well as a sweep who steers the boat and a drummer who beats a large drum at the bow. 
Dragon boats are brightly painted and are decorated with a dragon head and tail for race events. 
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4258cacb-3cb0-4313-a133-335944e2ce5c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
