   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab #110&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Dragon Boat Racing - positions&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a65bb605-2d99-4e6c-9a1d-b3aed5768218"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a65bb605-2d99-4e6c-9a1d-b3aed5768218&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The person on the back of the boat is called a … ?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b4e6b928-332c-4847-b594-f3eec321bbf2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Dragon boat team consists of the following:
Sweep: stands at the back with the oar, sets the path and is responsible for the safe operation of the boat.
Drummer: sits on the front of the boat, takes the cadence or beat pace from the strokes and relays calls. 
The paddlers are broken into three sections:
Strokes and Pacers: strokes set the rate according to the sweep or drummers call, the pacers support the strokes and set the pace for the boat.
The Engine Room: these are the stronger paddlers.
The Back 6: help propel the boat with powerful thrusts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4258cacb-3cb0-4313-a133-335944e2ce5c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
