   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab #110&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Dragon Boat Racing - commands&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a65bb605-2d99-4e6c-9a1d-b3aed5768218"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a65bb605-2d99-4e6c-9a1d-b3aed5768218&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the command for reversing the boat?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/55d170ba-128d-4113-b02c-9a3ffd80524d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;These are the most common terms used in racing:
Attention please - race command in a start situation. 
Paddles up - paddles forward and above the water, ready to take a stroke.
Go - command to start paddling.
Let it run - paddles in the relaxed position, parallel over the water, pointed at 90 degrees to the side of the boat.
Check the boat (Stop) - bring the boat to a full stop and holding it steady in place.
Paddles behind - paddles placed in a backwards position for paddling backwards.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4258cacb-3cb0-4313-a133-335944e2ce5c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
