   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #076&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Ford in Australia&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/59a8c712-5721-4133-a14a-83c06a9cc6c3"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/59a8c712-5721-4133-a14a-83c06a9cc6c3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Who won Bathurst in a MK1 Cortina&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/20ab5a75-b32f-428b-b1f8-e83c2cf226aa" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Ford Motor Company of Australia started in the 1900s thru to 2016, when the last Ford vehicle rolled off the production line @ Broadmeadows in Victoria

The Ford Cortina models mk1 and mk2, were produced from 1961 -1972 .It included the 2 door and 4 door sedan. The mk2 was also made as a bread van/Ute version. In 1963 Bob Jane won Bathurst in a mk1 GT, the first of 3 consecutive wins for Ford
We also own a MK2 Cortina so this is the start of our love for Cortinas we have had many of the newer models as well.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/33ad5cf7-3901-4fbc-84a8-236d58a9d1f2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Quokka AdLab series- which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on the stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
