  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/59a8c712-5721-4133-a14a-83c06a9cc6c3</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #076 : S4 The XE Falcon by Falcon351</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1475" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #076 : S4 The XE Falcon</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Falcon351</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Falcon351</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #076&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The XE Falcon&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/59a8c712-5721-4133-a14a-83c06a9cc6c3"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/59a8c712-5721-4133-a14a-83c06a9cc6c3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year was the last V8 model Falcon made?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ab36f523-37b4-4beb-baa7-f92412c89389" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The XE Falcon was produced between 1981 and 1985.
Officially launched in 1982 the model was freshened up from its predecessor the XD Falcon.
The ESP Falcon was launched with the model not being a GT. The ESP Falcon was produced in 1982 it was the last of the Falcon V8s. During 1982 Ford regained total market leadership for the first time in 29 years. There were a total of 1601 ESP Falcons made.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/33ad5cf7-3901-4fbc-84a8-236d58a9d1f2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Quokka AdLab series- which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on the stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.05145" lon="115.740867">
  <ele>2.0</ele>
  <time>2025-06-24T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBgQuV-05</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa196</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/59a8c712-5721-4133-a14a-83c06a9cc6c3</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #076 : S5 The last of the Falcons by Falcon351</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1476" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #076 : S5 The last of the Falcons</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Falcon351</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Falcon351</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #076&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The last of the Falcons&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/59a8c712-5721-4133-a14a-83c06a9cc6c3"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/59a8c712-5721-4133-a14a-83c06a9cc6c3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many vehicles were produced @ the Broadmeadows assembly plant ?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/dde8375d-398c-46a1-89c1-7526cd17658b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Upon the release of the BA and BF Falcon in the early 2000s the V8 was reintroduced as the XR8.
In 2016 the Falcon XR6  and XR8 Falcon Sprint models were released ,these were a non GT model but very potent in Fords history. 
The final Falcon off the production line at Broadmeadows assembly plant was a blue XR6 sedan. The assembly plant had produced 4,396 628 vehicles.
The most mass produced vehicle in Australian motoring history is the Ford Falcon.
We love our cortinas and Falcons so we thought we would give you some history 
We have owned MK2, TC ,TD and TE Cortinas and XE351 Falcon(x police car)XB Falcon panel van,AU Falcon station wagon and 2utes, BA Falcon sedan and Ute.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/33ad5cf7-3901-4fbc-84a8-236d58a9d1f2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Quokka AdLab series- which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on the stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.051267" lon="115.740833">
  <ele>3.0</ele>
  <time>2025-06-27T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBpK3v-01</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa197</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5e5028b6-5b09-4770-a899-2fd811acd773</url>
  <urlname>WA Quokka AdLab Art #074 : S1 01 - The Fremantle Traffic Bridges by Team Red Roo</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1502" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WA Quokka AdLab Art #074 : S1 01 - The Fremantle Traffic Bridges</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Team Red Roo</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Team Red Roo</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WA Quokka AdLab Art #074&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;01 - The Fremantle Traffic Bridges&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5e5028b6-5b09-4770-a899-2fd811acd773"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5e5028b6-5b09-4770-a899-2fd811acd773&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year was Stirling Bridge opened&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/27543240-929d-4e63-8c1a-3f2fa27de364" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This traffic system consists of two bridges - the first being the Fremantle Traffic Bridge which was opened in 1866 and linked Queen Victoria Street in Fremantle to North Fremantle. It was determined that this bridge should be replaced, and work is due to begin in early 2026 with construction expected to take about 12 months. Stirling Bridge (the second bridge) joins East Fremantle to North Fremantle and was opened in 1974 and will take all of the traffic while the first bridge is closed. 

Great views of both bridges can be made by following the road on the south side of the river. 
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/df3ac083-3eac-43e5-85f5-4706261a8cb9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Like many major cities around the world, Perth is situated on a river with it's population and business centers being on both sides of the river. For business and the general public to access quickly it requires bridges across the river at various points and a road system to cope with the traffic levels. 
This Lab introduces you to five of the main bridge systems across the Swan and Canning Rivers several of which are tourist attractions. 

&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.051283" lon="115.740867">
  <ele>3.0</ele>
  <time>2025-06-27T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBpK3v-02</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa198</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5e5028b6-5b09-4770-a899-2fd811acd773</url>
  <urlname>WA Quokka AdLab Art #074 : S2 02 - The Narrows Bridge by Team Red Roo</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1503" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WA Quokka AdLab Art #074 : S2 02 - The Narrows Bridge</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Team Red Roo</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Team Red Roo</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WA Quokka AdLab Art #074&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;02 - The Narrows Bridge&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5e5028b6-5b09-4770-a899-2fd811acd773"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5e5028b6-5b09-4770-a899-2fd811acd773&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year was the first bridge across the Narrows opened&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/bb8ddc78-f209-4711-ab8b-e2c4216856c4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Narrows Bridge consists of two road bridges across the Canning River, the first of which was opened in 1959 - up to that point the closest way across the river and into Perth City was via the Causeway. The second road bridge was finished in 2001 and the rail link (between the two bridges) was opened in 2005. In 1959 the Kwinana Freeway only extended south as far as Canning Bridge.`

Great views of the Narrows Bridges (and their interchanges) can be made from the War Memorial in Kings Park which also has views of Perth City, the Causeway Bridges &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/df3ac083-3eac-43e5-85f5-4706261a8cb9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Like many major cities around the world, Perth is situated on a river with it's population and business centers being on both sides of the river. For business and the general public to access quickly it requires bridges across the river at various points and a road system to cope with the traffic levels. 
This Lab introduces you to five of the main bridge systems across the Swan and Canning Rivers several of which are tourist attractions. 

&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.051317" lon="115.740883">
  <ele>3.0</ele>
  <time>2025-06-27T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBpK3v-03</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa199</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5e5028b6-5b09-4770-a899-2fd811acd773</url>
  <urlname>WA Quokka AdLab Art #074 : S3 03 - The Causeway / Boorloo Bridges by Team Red Roo</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1504" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
