   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #043&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Jewel Cave&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9b58ce02-7869-4e6f-a798-02744b023a76"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9b58ce02-7869-4e6f-a798-02744b023a76&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Who discovered Jewel Cave in 1957?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c3f04fce-c211-413b-b2dc-83110834c072" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Jewel Cave is a magical experience, a dazzling visual display of some of nature's finest and most meticulous work.

It is the largest show cave in Western Australia with three immense chambers. You are immediately awed by the magnitude of the first chamber, which is also home to one of the longest straw stalactites found in any cave in Australia.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/378568d3-abe1-413c-a381-19d06c1b18a6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
