 <wpt lat="-32.053133" lon="115.739083">
  <ele>1.0</ele>
  <time>2025-06-25T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBMNiJ-04</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa04m</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e74fd4ec-7436-4d98-8834-0350424c6533</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #042 : S4 AC/DC - Its all in the Name by TeamBarritts</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1854" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #042 : S4 AC/DC - Its all in the Name</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>TeamBarritts</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">TeamBarritts</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #042&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;AC/DC - Its all in the Name&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e74fd4ec-7436-4d98-8834-0350424c6533"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e74fd4ec-7436-4d98-8834-0350424c6533&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What does AC DC really stand for?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/492fb471-afe9-4981-8f49-b55b80f77865" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Upon formation, Malcolm and Angus developed the band's name after their sister Margaret pointed out the symbol "AC/DC" on the AC adapter of her sewing machine.  The brothers felt that this name symbolised the band's raw energy and the power-driven performances of their music.  It is pronounced one letter at a time, though the band are colloquially known as Acca Dacca in Australia.  

The AC/DC band name is stylised with a lightning bolt separating the AC from DC and has been used on all studio albums, except the international version of Dirty Deeds Done Dirt Cheap. Their logo was designed by American typographer Gerard Huerta in 1977 and first appeared on Let There Be Rock. 
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8c77808a-e155-4a0a-9943-ec47db603507" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which forms a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
