   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #042&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;AC/DC - Albums&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e74fd4ec-7436-4d98-8834-0350424c6533"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e74fd4ec-7436-4d98-8834-0350424c6533&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Which album was the biggest selling release for AC/DC?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/232d2572-bc7c-47fa-b0d0-b4746c92aa8a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;AC/DC have released 18 studio albums, two soundtrack albums, three live albums, one extended play, 57 singles, 11 video albums, 52 music videos and two box sets.

Although many AC/DC singles have been released, the band refused to issue any greatest hits albums. 
 Who Made Who, which served as the soundtrack to Stephen King's film Maximum Overdrive, Iron Man 2 and the band's various live recordings are the closest they have issued to such a compilation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8c77808a-e155-4a0a-9943-ec47db603507" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which forms a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.0531" lon="115.73915">
  <ele>1.0</ele>
  <time>2025-06-25T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBPi8K-01</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa04v</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9b58ce02-7869-4e6f-a798-02744b023a76</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #043 : S1 Mammoth Cave by BJA3</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1831" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #043 : S1 Mammoth Cave</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>BJA3</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">BJA3</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #043&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Mammoth Cave&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9b58ce02-7869-4e6f-a798-02744b023a76"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/9b58ce02-7869-4e6f-a798-02744b023a76&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;When was the cave first explored by Europeans?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/88953910-5a1b-415f-8fc7-7a66b7815f57" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Nestled within the stunning karri and marri forest, Mammoth Cave is a site of incredible natural and historical significance. Once home to ancient fossils of Australia’s megafauna—giant animals that roamed the Earth before their extinction around 46,000 years ago—the cave offers a fascinating glimpse into the past. 

Self-guided audio tours, available in English, French, German, Malay, and Mandarin, allow you to explore at your own pace while learning about the cave’s fascinating history and natural features.

A gently sloping boardwalk and stairs guide you through the cave, where you’ll encounter crystal stalactites, stalagmites, and a seasonal stream that flows through the cave during late winter and early spring.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/378568d3-abe1-413c-a381-19d06c1b18a6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
