   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #089&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Noone wants to be called a ratbag.....&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/317a7a01-6e9f-4977-a8bc-b2a84cc244c2"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/317a7a01-6e9f-4977-a8bc-b2a84cc244c2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Who was not a member of the "Rat Pack"&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/aecce739-f153-4099-b2ff-b5d6ca28da5a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Rottnest Island, often colloquially referred to as "Rotto", is a 19-square-kilometre island off the coast of Western Australia, located 18 kilometers west of Fremantle.
The traditional Noongar name for the island is Wadjemup, which means "place across the water where the spirits are". Human artefacts have been found on the island dating back at least 30,000 years.
The island was first documented by Willem de Vlamingh in 1696, who called it 't Eylandt 't Rottenest (literally 'Rats' Nest Island') after the quokka population. 
This Ad lab is "Rat" themed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ace139a7-c2b0-4800-8deb-277f2e1ef237" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka
off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs
to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry
Terminal.
To join this project, please contact the project Admins on
WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
