   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #048&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Stirling Range National Park&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/24c0957c-9ecd-48a6-b80f-b330e29477b9"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/24c0957c-9ecd-48a6-b80f-b330e29477b9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Which of these orchids is found in the Stirling Range?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d3081ae0-9c27-42f0-b883-fde7d703b48a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Stirling Range is one of Western Australia’s most important biodiversity hotspots. Home to over 1,500 plant species — many found nowhere else — the park bursts into colour during wildflower season. It's one of the best places to spot rare orchids like the Queen of Sheba Orchid, which blooms in burnt bushland.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/57699da9-98a1-4550-9272-4ffbf1c50c94" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.


To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com

This AdLab celebrates fascinating features of plant biodiversity. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
