   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #048&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Fitzgerald River National Park&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/24c0957c-9ecd-48a6-b80f-b330e29477b9"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/24c0957c-9ecd-48a6-b80f-b330e29477b9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;This park is known for over 1,800 plant species. Which rare WA plant is found here?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3c695693-f632-41af-8475-5de0af47577c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This park is a floral wonderland and one of the most botanically significant in Australia. It’s home to over 1,800 plant species — including many that don’t grow anywhere else on Earth. You’ll find colourful wildflowers like the striking Qualup Bell, and rare species hidden in coastal heathlands and rocky slopes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/57699da9-98a1-4550-9272-4ffbf1c50c94" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.


To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com

This AdLab celebrates fascinating features of plant biodiversity. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
