   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #048&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Kalbarri National Park&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/24c0957c-9ecd-48a6-b80f-b330e29477b9"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/24c0957c-9ecd-48a6-b80f-b330e29477b9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Which plant with striking flowers blooms in Kalbarri in spring? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/42b26013-000b-4fa8-9767-9c0efeae432e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Famous for its dramatic red gorges and coastal cliffs, Kalbarri National Park is also a hotspot for wildflowers. From late winter to spring, the landscape transforms with over 1,000 blooming species. Look out for the Kalbarri Catspaw, a vivid yellow and red flower that thrives in sandy soils.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/57699da9-98a1-4550-9272-4ffbf1c50c94" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.


To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com

This AdLab celebrates fascinating features of plant biodiversity. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
