   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #048&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Lesueur National Park&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/24c0957c-9ecd-48a6-b80f-b330e29477b9"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/24c0957c-9ecd-48a6-b80f-b330e29477b9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Lesueur is a biodiversity hotspot. What’s a unique feature of its flora?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2c05227c-0041-4e68-a314-5c84844a92e4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Lesueur is a biodiversity gem on WA’s Coral Coast, home to over 900 plant species packed into a small area — many found nowhere else. It’s especially famous for its wildflowers in spring, including orchids, wattles, and the bright pink Verticordia. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/57699da9-98a1-4550-9272-4ffbf1c50c94" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.


To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com

This AdLab celebrates fascinating features of plant biodiversity. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
