   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #020&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;John Curtin&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3dce4f37-4ff8-47a6-bbea-488c43e48fb9"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3dce4f37-4ff8-47a6-bbea-488c43e48fb9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Which electorate did John Curtin represent?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a0b1655a-2373-4ecb-bba4-aa200b14e7af" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;John Curtin became Prime Minister two months before the attack of Pearl Harbour.  Due to his inspiring national leadership during the Second World War he is considered to be one of Australia's greatest ever Prime Ministers. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0f42b880-ed35-471e-b0c2-002711ea8456" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com

In this Adventure Lab you will discover a few of the iconic bronze statues and their history in the Fremantle City Centre.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.05295" lon="115.73845">
