  <name>LBPjJP-05</name>
  <desc>WAQuokkaAdLa187</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7b75c005-3b03-45f0-b5ba-4a60d0d78581</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #037 : S5 The Pink and Rainbow Lakes, Esperance by sazpazza</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1746" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #037 : S5 The Pink and Rainbow Lakes, Esperance</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>sazpazza</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">sazpazza</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #037&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Pink and Rainbow Lakes, Esperance&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7b75c005-3b03-45f0-b5ba-4a60d0d78581"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7b75c005-3b03-45f0-b5ba-4a60d0d78581&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What was Pink Lake previously called&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9af46b06-cb6e-4889-9218-9445453624d4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;These incredible lakes are not only pink, but at different times of the year they change colour and can be anything from yellow, red, brown, or blue, giving them the accurate name of the Rainbow Lakes.

The lakes are on private land so the only way to see them is from the air, making this an expensive, but unforgettable option for a pink lake experience.

Pink Lake Esperance is another Pink Lake in Esperance.

However, be forewarned that this “pink lake” is no longer pink.  Pink Lake (previously Lake Spencer) is a salt lake located in the Goldfields region near Esperance. Historically this lake was pink, but as of 2023 the lake has not been pink for over 16 years.  Many visitors are disappointed upon arriving and finding out this pink lake Western Australia is indeed, not pink.  They are working on a new signage for the lake that explains why it is no longer pink.  However, many internet photos mistakingly refer to Pink Lake Esperance when in fact it is photos of Lake Hillier.

So why is Pink Lake no longer pink?  Well, the full answer is very complex.  The short answer is that the lake has lost its pink hue due to changes in salinity levels of the lake caused by human activity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0a2f565e-9d3e-4f26-b6d6-8a6a97258d9f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.052233" lon="115.738317">
