   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #020&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Air Commodore Sir Hughie Idwal Edwards &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3dce4f37-4ff8-47a6-bbea-488c43e48fb9"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3dce4f37-4ff8-47a6-bbea-488c43e48fb9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Looking at the statue of Sir Hughie Edwards, what was his main job in the Australian Defence Force?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/094586a0-68ed-43bf-96a4-6ca5375939d2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Sir Hughie Edwards is an Australian Hero.  He was the first airman to win the Distinguished Flying Cross, Distinguished Service Order and the Victoria Cross in the Second World War.  After a successful career in the Australian Defence Force Sir Hughie went on to become a Governor of Western Australia and has a ward named after him 'The Hugh Edwards Ward' at Hollywood Hospital.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0f42b880-ed35-471e-b0c2-002711ea8456" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com

In this Adventure Lab you will discover a few of the iconic bronze statues and their history in the Fremantle City Centre.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
