  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7b75c005-3b03-45f0-b5ba-4a60d0d78581</url>
  <urlname>WAQuokka AdLab Art #037 : S3 Pink Lake Hillier, Middle Island by sazpazza</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1744" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #037 : S3 Pink Lake Hillier, Middle Island</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>sazpazza</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">sazpazza</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #037&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Pink Lake Hillier, Middle Island&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7b75c005-3b03-45f0-b5ba-4a60d0d78581"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7b75c005-3b03-45f0-b5ba-4a60d0d78581&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Why do kids love this pink lake?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d53f66b2-8580-41b4-9d02-094ae6da547f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Located on Middle Island in the Recherche Archipelago, Lake Hillier is one of Australia’s most famous pink lakes.  It’s vibrant pink colour can be seen year-round, meaning that no one will be disappointed when visiting!

The pink color of Lake Hillier is entirely natural.  It comes from 10 species of bacteria, some archaea, and several species of Dunaliella Algae.  They are all pink in color giving the lake its vibrant hue.

Kids will love that this 600 m-long lake is shaped like a footprint.  A scenic flight is the best way to appreciate this lake’s beauty, offering a bird’s eye view of the contrasting pink lake and the sea.

If you’re staying in Esperance, the lake is just 70km away “as the crow flies” (haha – from there you have to fly or take a boat).  However, if you’re in the Perth area, it’s a long 8-hour drive away.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0a2f565e-9d3e-4f26-b6d6-8a6a97258d9f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
