  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1745" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka AdLab Art #037 : S4 Pink Lake of Quairading</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>sazpazza</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">sazpazza</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #037&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Pink Lake of Quairading&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7b75c005-3b03-45f0-b5ba-4a60d0d78581"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7b75c005-3b03-45f0-b5ba-4a60d0d78581&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Why is Wave Rock near Quairading Pink Lake called Wave Rock?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d526c42e-95b3-4026-9669-478609946350" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Quairading Pink Lake Western Australia is a lesser-known but equally stunning pink lake in the Wheatbelt region of Western Australia.  The lake turns a gorgeous shades of pink during the warmer months, with one dark pink side and one pale pink side, with a road running right through it!

Located near the town of Quairading, the lake offers a serene and peaceful atmosphere for families seeking an off-the-beaten-path adventure.

The local area is beautiful and the character- filled town of Quairading is a lovely place to take a wander. Most people visiting the lake do so on their way to Wave Rock from Perth as a welcome mid-journey break.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0a2f565e-9d3e-4f26-b6d6-8a6a97258d9f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
