   <groundspeak:owner id="">Kapelula</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #020&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Bon Scott&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3dce4f37-4ff8-47a6-bbea-488c43e48fb9"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3dce4f37-4ff8-47a6-bbea-488c43e48fb9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Here are a few famous AC/DC songs.  Which did Bon Scott co-write?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/14f23373-48f9-4840-94cd-9362c345af2d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ronald Belford (Bon) Scott was the front man of the internationally recognised band AC/DC which he joined in 1974.  He wrote and co-wrote the lyrics for some of the most popular AC/DC songs.  Bon was rated as number one in a list of the Greatest Frontmen of all time in the July 2004 issue of Classic Rock.



&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0f42b880-ed35-471e-b0c2-002711ea8456" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com

In this Adventure Lab you will discover a few of the iconic bronze statues and their history in the Fremantle City Centre.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
