   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Roley Pool Reserve - Boardwalk Trail&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;A Shelter for Information&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/35be7d2b-cbbf-4ef3-8447-70e332241d3b"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/35be7d2b-cbbf-4ef3-8447-70e332241d3b&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Noongar "Ngalla Djarigarro" translates to the English  _____  _________?  (2 words)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/cb175f9f-13b5-4d84-aee5-9bbc13c8f2ef" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Here's everything you may or may not want to know about Roley Pool and the trails.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c4b21827-121a-4284-8366-a72e02925533" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Roley Pool Reserve is a little hidden gem in the Perth Hills. Follow the trail along the Canning River  through the steep sided Canning Valley and if you're lucky, you may spot a 'Native Otter', Quenda or Brushtail Possum in the unspoilt bushland. The core of this Reserve is Roley Pool itself which was the original Roleystone swimming hole. Winter is the perfect time to take the short stroll from Soldiers Road lower carpark, past the Information Shelter to complete the Adlab or, for those up for it, continue on to Nature's spa and the end of the trail.
There is a bonus cache attached to this lab.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
