   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Roley Pool Reserve - Boardwalk Trail&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;A Shelter for Picnics&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/35be7d2b-cbbf-4ef3-8447-70e332241d3b"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/35be7d2b-cbbf-4ef3-8447-70e332241d3b&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many metres off the main path is the Roley Pool South picnic area?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1ac2f959-b166-4d50-8fce-03ce9001bd72" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A short detour off the main trail and you will find yourself in a quiet spot nearby the stream. The shelter is a bit worse for wear but it does harbour a cache (at time of publication). &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c4b21827-121a-4284-8366-a72e02925533" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Roley Pool Reserve is a little hidden gem in the Perth Hills. Follow the trail along the Canning River  through the steep sided Canning Valley and if you're lucky, you may spot a 'Native Otter', Quenda or Brushtail Possum in the unspoilt bushland. The core of this Reserve is Roley Pool itself which was the original Roleystone swimming hole. Winter is the perfect time to take the short stroll from Soldiers Road lower carpark, past the Information Shelter to complete the Adlab or, for those up for it, continue on to Nature's spa and the end of the trail.
There is a bonus cache attached to this lab.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
