   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Roley Pool Reserve - Boardwalk Trail&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;It's in the Pipeline&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/35be7d2b-cbbf-4ef3-8447-70e332241d3b"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/35be7d2b-cbbf-4ef3-8447-70e332241d3b&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;These QR codes invite you to view a map of the walking trails and learn about the _________  ___________ ? (2 words)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f0734248-e7fc-4307-84cf-3a62684ded96" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This heritage pipeline was once used to transport water from nearby Canning Dam to Roleystone. More details can be downloaded from the QR codes on the nearby sign post.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c4b21827-121a-4284-8366-a72e02925533" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Roley Pool Reserve is a little hidden gem in the Perth Hills. Follow the trail along the Canning River  through the steep sided Canning Valley and if you're lucky, you may spot a 'Native Otter', Quenda or Brushtail Possum in the unspoilt bushland. The core of this Reserve is Roley Pool itself which was the original Roleystone swimming hole. Winter is the perfect time to take the short stroll from Soldiers Road lower carpark, past the Information Shelter to complete the Adlab or, for those up for it, continue on to Nature's spa and the end of the trail.
There is a bonus cache attached to this lab.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
