   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Roley Pool Reserve - Boardwalk Trail&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Rest for the not so wicked!&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/35be7d2b-cbbf-4ef3-8447-70e332241d3b"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/35be7d2b-cbbf-4ef3-8447-70e332241d3b&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many bolts hold the wooden planks to the seat'the s metal frame? (number)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8b798a03-ac47-437c-9ba5-a3de98d05c05" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This seat may provide a welcome rest for those whose energy is spent or for those needing a break before continuing to Nature's Spa further along the trail. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c4b21827-121a-4284-8366-a72e02925533" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Roley Pool Reserve is a little hidden gem in the Perth Hills. Follow the trail along the Canning River  through the steep sided Canning Valley and if you're lucky, you may spot a 'Native Otter', Quenda or Brushtail Possum in the unspoilt bushland. The core of this Reserve is Roley Pool itself which was the original Roleystone swimming hole. Winter is the perfect time to take the short stroll from Soldiers Road lower carpark, past the Information Shelter to complete the Adlab or, for those up for it, continue on to Nature's spa and the end of the trail.
There is a bonus cache attached to this lab.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
