  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1663" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka Adlab #028 : S3 Lyndon Station</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>ebenie</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">ebenie</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka Adlab #028&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Lyndon Station&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/05150a41-7e21-4703-979c-01629ee0f8b4"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/05150a41-7e21-4703-979c-01629ee0f8b4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What type of mine is being operated here&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e9a5ecc8-7d4e-4a0f-9390-962ef9ef3a58" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Lyndon Station is a pastoral lease located in the Gascoyne region.  Approximately 920 kms from Perth 
This station mainly runs cattle to that roam the roads in region.  Part of this track is known as the Wool Wagon Way  from  Mullewa to Exmouth via Lyndon Minnie road where this pic was taken. 
It also has an open cut mine working on the station region.
This windmill is still very operational with cattle yards at the side of it.  Whilst leaving the cattle were roaming in. 
This part of track from the Junction to North west Coastal Hwy was about 230 km and only I car past by. Didn’t even glance our way so be prepared if out travelling this great country&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b51a0bf9-96a5-4dc8-9e7d-cf0f5dd5cfbf" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.051917" lon="115.740283">
  <ele>1.0</ele>
