  <urlname>WAQuokka Adlab #028 : S4 The Murchison and yesterday’s relics by ebenie</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-1664" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>WAQuokka Adlab #028 : S4 The Murchison and yesterday’s relics</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>ebenie</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">ebenie</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka Adlab #028&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Murchison and yesterday’s relics&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/05150a41-7e21-4703-979c-01629ee0f8b4"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/05150a41-7e21-4703-979c-01629ee0f8b4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the main event held here twice a year &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/fad4337f-0a8f-44e2-bd5c-bbc5e0273930" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to a shire with a town.  The Murchison was a major gold rush area in the 1890’s and was known as the ‘whitewater capital’ this owing to many rivers everywhere joint this region and flows in the Murchison and out to sea in Kalbarri.  It has a big network of stations and is supported for tourists with Fuel 24 hr service.  Roadhouse and up to great standard accommodations.   Motel and caravan park 
The road from Mullewa, Geraldton and Gascoyne Junction are all unsealed but up to high standards.
This region is quick big for the local community of stations and a great hub for get togethers &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b51a0bf9-96a5-4dc8-9e7d-cf0f5dd5cfbf" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.05185" lon="115.740217">
