   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka Adlab #028&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Regans Ford &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/05150a41-7e21-4703-979c-01629ee0f8b4"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/05150a41-7e21-4703-979c-01629ee0f8b4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How far is Regans Ford from Perth&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ee506a60-13f6-4b4c-b983-c1509c70d9a9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;My last pic stands so tall here and was once known as the Windmill roadhouse.
It is located at the edge of the road just north of Perth and is housing a caravan park at the back of it. It lays within the Dandaragin shire.
Regans Ford is name after Edward Regan - a shepherd in the area.   
A site for Co-operative Bulk Handling facility for canola, wheat and other cereal crops.
This roadhouse is a shed at the rear which was built by Highline sheds and possibly the patio roof over the front of brick building shed was erected late 1980/1990. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b51a0bf9-96a5-4dc8-9e7d-cf0f5dd5cfbf" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.053133" lon="115.73875">
  <ele>1.0</ele>
