   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #040&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Etmylin&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e247ea17-2884-4cd0-a895-5cb94449fa26"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e247ea17-2884-4cd0-a895-5cb94449fa26&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Etmylin is a stop for the Hotham Valley Railway. What was the sidings main purpose for the railway?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f17dad6a-8301-47d4-a610-91d035780514" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Etmylin is a beautiful spot to visit either by train, vehicle or as a part of the Bibbulmun Track. There is a scenic walk trail to explore and lots of blue wrens can be seen frequenting the area. Beware of train movements here on weekends and school holidays.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/dce8047e-8208-4ecf-856d-6ffb56ed31a3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
