   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #039&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Our Fave Places in WA - Bunker Bay&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a2c6432d-a028-4959-b56a-16e13ab76dc9"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a2c6432d-a028-4959-b56a-16e13ab76dc9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;When is the best time to see whales in Bunker Bay&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/dc809010-d6d4-4e15-b017-7fcaa249d7d9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Three hours south of Perth is Bunker Bay.  It is a sheltered bay, one of the few north facing beaches in WA protected by the rocky outcrops of Cape Naturaliste.  It is pristine with pure white sand and gently lapping waves.  It is perfect for swimming, snorkelling and fishing and whale watching.

Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art - Please join in by contacting WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9e7fcfd4-1f93-433b-8214-caeafb5bfe30" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
