   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #039&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Our Fave Places in WA - New Norcia&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a2c6432d-a028-4959-b56a-16e13ab76dc9"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a2c6432d-a028-4959-b56a-16e13ab76dc9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Who was New Norcia named after?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c625856d-35a2-479f-83f8-3397da171f4b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This town has had many purposes.  Founded in 1847 by Spanish Benedictine Monks, it has been a mission, a monastery, an education provider and is now a spiritual place of retreat and a tourist must visit.  It has a working farm and a historic bakery.
Located approximately 2 hours north of Perth, there is magnificent architecture, cultural and historic heritage, art galleries, a museum, a visitor information centre and local produce, wine and olive oil for purchase.
This unique town is really a ‘town like no other’.


Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art - Please join in by contacting WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com 
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9e7fcfd4-1f93-433b-8214-caeafb5bfe30" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
