   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #104&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Filmed in WA - Rams&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/04f5c01d-df5c-48ef-9f16-2b5307b4bbd2"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/04f5c01d-df5c-48ef-9f16-2b5307b4bbd2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year was this movie released?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/de5df867-cb81-480e-b97a-240abd51058c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Two estranged brothers must set aside their differences when a rare and lethal illness threatens their respective flocks of sheep in Western Australia.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ef3a3144-75bf-4b53-8a85-6713b1387a8f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
