   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #104&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Filmed in WA - Hotel Coolgardie &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/04f5c01d-df5c-48ef-9f16-2b5307b4bbd2"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/04f5c01d-df5c-48ef-9f16-2b5307b4bbd2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What year was this movie released?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f8bc989c-7e88-43ff-b0a6-7cbde9ecb7ed" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Finnish travellers Lina and Steph arrive in Coolgardie, Australia eager for an authentic Outback experience. The local men are also eager, because every three months a new pair of female backpackers come to work at the town's only bar.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ef3a3144-75bf-4b53-8a85-6713b1387a8f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

