   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;WAQuokka AdLab Art #080&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;WAQuokka Adlab Geoart&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a32394d9-7c58-42ff-938e-0a8216ba46cb"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a32394d9-7c58-42ff-938e-0a8216ba46cb&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;110 adventure labs make up the WAQuokka geoart&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b4ece252-406e-4924-9041-121a28aabfd6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The WA Quokka Geoart&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d114842f-5e2b-4230-ba0a-740cb8b79b7b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the WAQuokka AdLab art series - which intends to form a giant quokka off the coast of Perth. There is a 500m geofence on stages which allows the AdLabs to be solved from between the Fremantle Maritime Museum and the Rottnest Ferry Terminal.

To join this project, please contact the project Admins on WAQuokkaAdLab@gmail.com
