  <name>LBf3db1501</name>
  <desc>WhistlerWalk111</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/90591efc-8a80-4354-8a75-4903bcf3db15</url>
  <urlname>Whistler Walk 1 : S1 Sheoak by Chwiliwr</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-461" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Whistler Walk 1 : S1 Sheoak</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Chwiliwr</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Chwiliwr</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Whistler Walk 1&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Sheoak&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/90591efc-8a80-4354-8a75-4903bcf3db15"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/90591efc-8a80-4354-8a75-4903bcf3db15&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the scientific name on the plaque? (two words)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a8bd833f-3311-417f-8a81-15e6cbdff3a6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Sheoak has thick fibrous bark and spreading branches and grows to 15 metres tall.

It occurs on the lateritic soils on the Darling Range and in sand on the Coastal Plain and extends from Jurien Bay southwards to Mt Manypeaks.

(Image by unknown)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/59d90e7c-b537-43d0-9122-5a9586cd4423" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Whistler Walk is a loop trail through the northern area of Bungendore Park in the Wungong Regional Park.

Take a walk beneath Jarrah, Marri, Casuarina and Banksia trees. Enjoy the whistles and calls of the park’s diverse birdlife and the beautiful blossoms.

The one-directional loop trail is well sign posted with boot cleaning stations along the trail to help prevent the spread of Phtytophthora Dieback.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.171336" lon="116.039514">
  <ele>244.0</ele>
