  <desc>WhistlerWalk225</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/87481f83-00bd-4caf-a0ce-acfba093c64d</url>
  <urlname>Whistler Walk 2 : S5 Marri by inspicio</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-460" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Whistler Walk 2 : S5 Marri</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>inspicio</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">inspicio</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Whistler Walk 2&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Marri&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/87481f83-00bd-4caf-a0ce-acfba093c64d"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/87481f83-00bd-4caf-a0ce-acfba093c64d&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the last word of the third paragraph on the plaque?  Do not include the apostrophes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4a5c2e73-3cbd-4f8a-b08d-884fc8b797cc" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Marri grows to a similar size to Jarrah.  Like the Jarrah, the bark is rough, but grows in grey-brown rectangular patches whereas the bark of the Jarrah is stringy.

This attractive tree grows to 40 metres tall with creamy masses of flowers in summer and autumn: pink flowered variants also occur.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d882a320-f213-4ab6-a991-3204b9d9ec16" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Whistler Walk is a loop trail through the northern area of Bungendore Park in the Wungong Regional Park.

Take a walk beneath Jarrah, Marri, Casuarina and Banksia trees. Enjoy the whistles and calls of the park’s diverse birdlife and the beautiful blossoms.

The one-directional loop trail is well sign posted with boot cleaning stations along the trail to help prevent the spread of Phtytophthora Dieback.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.172072" lon="116.038967">
  <ele>251.0</ele>
