   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Whistler Walk 1&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Gravel Wattle&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/90591efc-8a80-4354-8a75-4903bcf3db15"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/90591efc-8a80-4354-8a75-4903bcf3db15&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The wattle grows on laterite gravels of the Darling Scarp from ???  (Three words.)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/93974009-0d8f-427d-88c1-84ae68933260" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This wattle is an erect, spreading shrub growing about 0.5m to 1m tall and is soft without any spines.  The branches are covered with dense hairs and leaves are dark, shiny green on top with paler below.

The Acacia blooms in spring with pale yellow flowers that are rounded about 10cm across. When mature the seed pod is dark brown, flattened and has brown eliptical seeds.

(Image by unknown)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/59d90e7c-b537-43d0-9122-5a9586cd4423" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Whistler Walk is a loop trail through the northern area of Bungendore Park in the Wungong Regional Park.

Take a walk beneath Jarrah, Marri, Casuarina and Banksia trees. Enjoy the whistles and calls of the park’s diverse birdlife and the beautiful blossoms.

The one-directional loop trail is well sign posted with boot cleaning stations along the trail to help prevent the spread of Phtytophthora Dieback.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
