  <desc>YarloopHistory3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3dc60093-f51d-4fb1-aac6-cc2ec13c8844</url>
  <urlname>Yarloop History : S3 Station Street by dezzabills</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-2037" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Yarloop History : S3 Station Street</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>dezzabills</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">dezzabills</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Yarloop History&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Station Street&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3dc60093-f51d-4fb1-aac6-cc2ec13c8844"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3dc60093-f51d-4fb1-aac6-cc2ec13c8844&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Yarloop was developed either side of the Government Railway. Who controlled what was built on the east side?t side?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2a91a503-75f3-47fb-93c8-e2e51af93a2d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Station Street in Yarloop was once the central business district of the town, featuring the police station, post office, and a hotel opposite the railway station. The area was significant for government services, with the police station initially serving both Yarloop and Harvey. The name Yarloop itself is thought to originate from the local Bindjareb people language. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/dbf5b27d-dbb7-4008-a6b6-896088bd3660" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Yarloop, established in 1894, is a town with a rich history rooted in the timber industry. Originally a timber milling town, it became known for its steam workshops which housed machinery for the timber industry. The name is thought to be derived from the local Bindjareb Aboriginal language, though an alternative theory suggests it comes from the term "yard loop" related to the railway. The town was significantly impacted by the 2016 bushfires, which destroyed many buildings, including the historic workshops. Efforts are underway to preserve its heritage.

This Adventure Lab is only a small portion of the Yarloop Heritage Trail.
more information can be obtained here:
 https://trailswa.com.au/trails/trail/yarloop-heritage-walk-trail&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
