   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.958833" lon="115.90015">
  <ele>27.0</ele>
  <time>2025-08-12T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBc884405</name>
  <desc>YarloopHistory5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3dc60093-f51d-4fb1-aac6-cc2ec13c8844</url>
  <urlname>Yarloop History : S5 Yarloop Workshops by dezzabills</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="-2039" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Yarloop History : S5 Yarloop Workshops</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>dezzabills</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">dezzabills</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Yarloop History&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Yarloop Workshops&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3dc60093-f51d-4fb1-aac6-cc2ec13c8844"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/3dc60093-f51d-4fb1-aac6-cc2ec13c8844&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What was maintained in the workshops?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8d31f3ba-824d-4a8f-b1ee-96d881715a46" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Yarloop Workshops, established in 1901, were a railway and timber mill machinery workshop that played a vital role in the timber industry of Western Australia. Initially built by the Millar brothers to service their timber mills, they expanded to become a central hub for maintaining the company's extensive railway and milling equipment. The workshops were known for their skilled workforce and for manufacturing many of the parts needed for their operations. The site was significantly impacted by Cyclone Alby in 1978, leading to its closure and eventual sale. The workshops were also severely damaged by the 2016 Yarloop bushfire, but have since been the focus of restoration efforts&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/dbf5b27d-dbb7-4008-a6b6-896088bd3660" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Yarloop, established in 1894, is a town with a rich history rooted in the timber industry. Originally a timber milling town, it became known for its steam workshops which housed machinery for the timber industry. The name is thought to be derived from the local Bindjareb Aboriginal language, though an alternative theory suggests it comes from the term "yard loop" related to the railway. The town was significantly impacted by the 2016 bushfires, which destroyed many buildings, including the historic workshops. Efforts are underway to preserve its heritage.

This Adventure Lab is only a small portion of the Yarloop Heritage Trail.
more information can be obtained here:
 https://trailswa.com.au/trails/trail/yarloop-heritage-walk-trail&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
