   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Crooked Brook 2&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Rough Honey Myrtle&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/607647da-4e98-4890-9090-c631ae4f5470"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/607647da-4e98-4890-9090-c631ae4f5470&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the colour of the flowers?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0f1ea80e-4c7d-478e-83dd-786013d13ada" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A member of the myrtle family.  It grows to 0.5 metre and has purple flowers from September to December.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/afc8c4cc-df96-4079-8026-52ad9e306d7e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Crooked Brook 2

Crooked Brook Forrest is a project conceived, built and managed by The Crooked Brook Forrest Community Group, volunteers who, for the most part live locally.

The project came into being in 1994 with a vision of creating a "forest for all people" with a particular focus on providing facilities for the elderly and those with a disability.

Crooked Brook Forest Group welcomes you and invites you to explore this magnificent jarrah forest.

Wildflower Walk
Moderate walking
A 3km, moderate walking circuit through Crooked Brook Forest’s magnificent wildflower display. The higher section is an undulating forest walk to a beautiful lookout over the Crooked Brook valley and into Bunbury, while the lower section offers an easier walk. The lower section is also used by cyclists following the Munda Biddi Trail.

This adventure takes you around the northern portion of the Wildflower Walk Circuit from the lookout back to where the trail begins.

Take note of the clues at each stage to find the Bonus Cache.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
