   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Crooked Brook 2&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Pineapple Lily&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/607647da-4e98-4890-9090-c631ae4f5470"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/607647da-4e98-4890-9090-c631ae4f5470&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the scientific name on the plaque? (2 words)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/540e0dbd-4743-4157-815e-4ce271433347" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Grows in damp places in the Southwest's high rainfall forests.  It is similar to the grass tree but its trunk is much thinner and the leaves very obviously pineapple-like in appearance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/afc8c4cc-df96-4079-8026-52ad9e306d7e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Crooked Brook 2

