 <wpt lat="-30.762867" lon="121.460167">
  <ele>362.0</ele>
  <time>2025-08-30T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LB9167301</name>
  <desc>KokodaTrailS1Ko</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e901b100-58da-4935-9caa-31d4e8e91673</url>
  <urlname>Kokoda Trail : S1 Kokoda Trail - Uberi by Barrikon</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99000210" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Kokoda Trail : S1 Kokoda Trail - Uberi</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Barrikon</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Barrikon</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Kokoda Trail&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Kokoda Trail - Uberi&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e901b100-58da-4935-9caa-31d4e8e91673"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e901b100-58da-4935-9caa-31d4e8e91673&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many steps make up the Golden Staircase?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f131c7d4-d4ef-43c1-ba33-c4a2c622a2c6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;UBERI

Uberi village was the site of the first staging camp on the Kokoda Track.

After leaving Ilolo the Track was fairly easy going for some five or six  kilometres before it plunged down mountain sides through dense forest to the valley of the upper reaches of the Goldie River.

The Track then followed the river until it climbed a steep slope to the village of Uberi.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4d6858a4-e96b-497b-bd08-84a262856860" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Kokoda Trail is a tribute to the service men and women of 1939 - 1945

It is a reminder of courageous efforts of the people who served Australia during World War II, especially those from the Goldfields.



This Lab is part of the Kokoda Trail Caches.

5 Physical Caches that tie in with these 5 Adventure Lab caches to result in 1 Bonus cache (GCB7TVK)

Ensure you take note of the Letter and Number you receive upon completing each stage, to complete the bonus cache.
 

This series is best suited for a bicycle, E-Scooter or on foot. There are sections of both sealed and unsealed paths however the unsealed sections are very compact and very easily traversed. It is approximately 5kms return of flat terrain. 

Double Gees are prevalent so wear suitable shoes

It is suggested to park near the listed coordinates and complete the series from here. There are toilets, drinking water, caravan parking, 72hr camping and even coffee at most times.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
