   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Kokoda Trail&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Kokoda Trail - Kokoda&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e901b100-58da-4935-9caa-31d4e8e91673"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e901b100-58da-4935-9caa-31d4e8e91673&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;L G Mellet wrote a poem about Kokoda. It was dedicated to his uncle with the service Number WX (5 digits)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/06873cde-868a-42bc-804a-fcbffbb577d3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;KOKODA

A village in the Yodda or Mambare valley on the northern side of the Owen Stanley Ranges, Kokoda gave its name to the foot pad – ‘the track’ which wound up the hills and across the mountains towards Port Moresby.

The small Kokoda plateau, with an altitude of 1,200 feet, protruded into the valley from the main mountain range.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4d6858a4-e96b-497b-bd08-84a262856860" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Kokoda Trail is a tribute to the service men and women of 1939 - 1945

It is a reminder of courageous efforts of the people who served Australia during World War II, especially those from the Goldfields.



This Lab is part of the Kokoda Trail Caches.

5 Physical Caches that tie in with these 5 Adventure Lab caches to result in 1 Bonus cache (GCB7TVK)

Ensure you take note of the Letter and Number you receive upon completing each stage, to complete the bonus cache.
 

This series is best suited for a bicycle, E-Scooter or on foot. There are sections of both sealed and unsealed paths however the unsealed sections are very compact and very easily traversed. It is approximately 5kms return of flat terrain. 

Double Gees are prevalent so wear suitable shoes

It is suggested to park near the listed coordinates and complete the series from here. There are toilets, drinking water, caravan parking, 72hr camping and even coffee at most times.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.103717" lon="115.998483">
