   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Wrights Lake - Champion Lakes&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Dragon Boat Club&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/eb2ff215-10c1-45a4-844c-021ee15d8cd2"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/eb2ff215-10c1-45a4-844c-021ee15d8cd2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the number on the electrical cabinet? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f2e89af9-a90a-483e-a641-16b5e5fcdfa4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The dragon boat comprises of 20 paddlers, a sweep who steers the boat and a drummer who keeps everyone in time. 
Ages range from 12 - 84 who participate in all divisions; Juniors, premiers and seniors, ladies, men and mixed teams as well as cancer survivors and supporters.
The regatta season begins in October and are held monthly through to the state championships in March each year. 
National Championships are held here each 7 years.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/97f243f0-989c-4a11-8524-4e2ef5d8f03a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Wrights Lake in Kelmscott was named for an early settler Charles Wright, who received the land grant in the 1830’s. The lake was originally a natural drainage line and timber reserve.
The lake and it’s surrounding parkland were developed into an aquatic facility with an international rowing course, with the master plan endorsed in 2000 and completed after the Tonkin Highway extension in 2005. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
