   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Wrights Lake - Champion Lakes&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Champion Lakes - Joe Saunders&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/eb2ff215-10c1-45a4-844c-021ee15d8cd2"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/eb2ff215-10c1-45a4-844c-021ee15d8cd2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The land was vested in council … as written &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/67071b07-73da-42b2-9b6a-15211d37b19c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Joe Saunders 1928-1987
A pig farmer, Joe is remembered for his achievements in rowing. 
He stroked the winning Aquinas College Head of the River Eight in 1946, coached the Western Australian Kings Cup crews and was an Australian selector for men’s rowing teams. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/97f243f0-989c-4a11-8524-4e2ef5d8f03a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Wrights Lake in Kelmscott was named for an early settler Charles Wright, who received the land grant in the 1830’s. The lake was originally a natural drainage line and timber reserve.
The lake and it’s surrounding parkland were developed into an aquatic facility with an international rowing course, with the master plan endorsed in 2000 and completed after the Tonkin Highway extension in 2005. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.899733" lon="115.971617">
