   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Watering holes in Guildford&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Copper and Oak liquor Merchants &lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f246ece8-a9c4-4171-8d45-47b8898daa23"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/f246ece8-a9c4-4171-8d45-47b8898daa23&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Radius: 100m&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Stages: 4&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kind of question: single&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Find on stand alone plaque. In what year did Samuel Baker move his business to the corner of Meadow and Swan st?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5b90955f-fe8c-4347-9af4-e1fbcc1bd9e3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Since 2022 Coper and Oak   Guildford has operated from a historic building with a long standing liquor background. Located at the start of the Swan Valley. It has the original stone cellar still used for storing wine. 
In 1851, Samuel Baker owned 6 buildings here, at the corner of Meadow and Swan St, in partnership with Thomas Gull. Only one of the original buildings remain. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/cc7adf02-64b6-4ff1-a61a-4558773d2023" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This adventure lab will take you around the town of Guildford, close to the Swan Valley and Midland. 
It features 4 historic hotels and 1 liquor merchant. Well known for their craft beers and a variety of cuisines. 
Guilford is well known for its historic colonial architecture, it was established in 1929 on the Swan River. Serving as the first inland port. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
