  <urlname>Sun-kissed Shorelines  - Mandurah Beaches : S1 Silver Sands Beach by hunterzed</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="1476919054" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Sun-kissed Shorelines  - Mandurah Beaches : S1 Silver Sands Beach</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>hunterzed</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">hunterzed</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Sun-kissed Shorelines  - Mandurah Beaches&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Silver Sands Beach&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/dd9d5216-417d-4cd1-8d9a-d290835bd3cb"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/dd9d5216-417d-4cd1-8d9a-d290835bd3cb&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Radius: 20m&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kind of question: single&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;In which month of 1921 did the Leviathan become grounded on the Mandurah bar? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f676152a-397f-4670-ae10-4917bd1d18e5" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to Silver Sands Beach! 
Find your own spot along this very long stretch of shoreline divided by the odd seawall along the way.  Silver Sands Beach is perfect for swimming and surfers can catch a wave at 4th Groyne. 

Amenities include undercover picnic tables which are dotted around the small reserve as well as toilets nearby. 
 
Find the plaque about the Mandurah Wreck Trail to answer the following question. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7c08a902-ed77-4de7-9396-d0f58e9f80f5" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Mandurah's beaches have a lot to offer with a good variety of choice depending on what you are looking to experience.. 

There are relaxed family-friendly spots; surf breaks for those looking for a little more adventure; and calm, scenic bays; all with their own natural beauty. 

Other activities include walking, swimming, snorkelling or simply soaking up the scenic waterside views. 

Whatever your fancy, no trip to Mandurah should go without visiting at least one of these picturesque locations along the coast. I hope you enjoy! And remember to stay safe in the sun and surf ??  &amp;zwj;?? 

**Take note of a letter clue at each completed location to spell out a word associated with the theme of the AdLab to help complete the bonus cache  &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
