  <name>LB4CGK4</name>
  <desc>SunkissedShore4</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/dd9d5216-417d-4cd1-8d9a-d290835bd3cb</url>
  <urlname>Sun-kissed Shorelines  - Mandurah Beaches : S4 Little Mermaid Beach by hunterzed</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99002459" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Sun-kissed Shorelines  - Mandurah Beaches : S4 Little Mermaid Beach</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>hunterzed</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">hunterzed</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Sun-kissed Shorelines  - Mandurah Beaches&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Little Mermaid Beach&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/dd9d5216-417d-4cd1-8d9a-d290835bd3cb"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/dd9d5216-417d-4cd1-8d9a-d290835bd3cb&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Radius: 20m&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kind of question: single&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Take a seat on one of the log bench seats. What does the mosaic spell out underfoot? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/03a77963-c9db-4425-a59d-a7df617b537a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;If you are looking for somewhere less crowded with a high chance of seeing dolphins, then Little Mermaid Beach at Stingray Point is the perfect spot to relax and enjoy the tranquility. 
Although not a typical sandy beach and not suitable for swimming, it has an amazing gigantic fig tree nearby, lawn area with a walking path to enjoy the estuary views. You'll witness boats passing by and the odd person fishing off the jetty. Keep an eye out for dolphins and many other marine wildlife. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7c08a902-ed77-4de7-9396-d0f58e9f80f5" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Mandurah's beaches have a lot to offer with a good variety of choice depending on what you are looking to experience.. 

There are relaxed family-friendly spots; surf breaks for those looking for a little more adventure; and calm, scenic bays; all with their own natural beauty. 

Other activities include walking, swimming, snorkelling or simply soaking up the scenic waterside views. 

Whatever your fancy, no trip to Mandurah should go without visiting at least one of these picturesque locations along the coast. I hope you enjoy! And remember to stay safe in the sun and surf ??  &amp;zwj;?? 

**Take note of a letter clue at each completed location to spell out a word associated with the theme of the AdLab to help complete the bonus cache  &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
