 <wpt lat="-32.531883" lon="115.714817">
  <ele>4.0</ele>
  <time>2025-09-26T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LB4CCM1</name>
  <desc>MandurahWarMem1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5976675f-4c37-4e93-8716-a38ecfb1993f</url>
  <urlname>Mandurah War Memorial  : S1 The New Memorial by Boyzrule5</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99002431" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Mandurah War Memorial  : S1 The New Memorial</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Boyzrule5</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Boyzrule5</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Mandurah War Memorial &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The New Memorial&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5976675f-4c37-4e93-8716-a38ecfb1993f"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5976675f-4c37-4e93-8716-a38ecfb1993f&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Radius: 20m&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kind of question: single&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;'I crouched in a ……. trench on that hell of exposed beaches' what is the missing word?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c8c12828-e46f-406e-87fe-d37ffb33aaae" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A committee was formed in 2004; a design prepared and a tender appointed to construct the memorial. A deadline of mid-April 2005 in readiness for the dedication and consecration ceremony prior to ANZAC Day. 
The memorial was designed by Hames Sharley Architects and built by Pindan Constructions and the City of Manudurah. Work began on Tuesday 14 September 2004 with the official launch on Monday 18 April 2005. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6852750b-7733-4bb6-b95d-6bbcd1362033" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This adventure lab is based at the latest War Memorial. The first was located on the western bank of the estuary, opposite the town on Mary Street and Old Coast Road. In 1997 major road works impacted the site. The original structure was removed and remodelled and installed at the City of Mandurah RSL sun-branch on the corner of ANZAC Place and Third Avenue Mandurah. 

Ref: https://www.mandurah.wa.gov.au/explore/arts-and-culture/war-memorial&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.531933" lon="115.7146">
  <time>2025-09-26T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LB4CCM2</name>
  <desc>MandurahWarMem2</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5976675f-4c37-4e93-8716-a38ecfb1993f</url>
  <urlname>Mandurah War Memorial  : S2 The Memorial Design by Boyzrule5</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99002432" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Mandurah War Memorial  : S2 The Memorial Design</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Boyzrule5</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Boyzrule5</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Mandurah War Memorial &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Memorial Design&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5976675f-4c37-4e93-8716-a38ecfb1993f"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5976675f-4c37-4e93-8716-a38ecfb1993f&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Radius: 20m&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kind of question: single&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What years are listed for the Vietnam War?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f48c229f-41fd-4184-b861-05e1be1664b5" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The poem 'At the Going Down of the Sun' formed the inspiration for Hames Sharley design. The poem is etched in its entirety on selected individual pillars throughout the site. 
The design uses large white pillars of various heights straddling a small rise with the axis of the row lying along the line of the sun's rays on ANZAC Day. At dawn on ANZAC Day the rising sun will light up the columns and create a temporary guiding light to the highest peak of the memorial which be further enhanced by the line of dark shadows cast along the axis. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6852750b-7733-4bb6-b95d-6bbcd1362033" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This adventure lab is based at the latest War Memorial. The first was located on the western bank of the estuary, opposite the town on Mary Street and Old Coast Road. In 1997 major road works impacted the site. The original structure was removed and remodelled and installed at the City of Mandurah RSL sun-branch on the corner of ANZAC Place and Third Avenue Mandurah. 

Ref: https://www.mandurah.wa.gov.au/explore/arts-and-culture/war-memorial&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.531983" lon="115.714517">
  <ele>6.0</ele>
  <time>2025-09-26T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LB4CCM3</name>
  <desc>MandurahWarMem3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5976675f-4c37-4e93-8716-a38ecfb1993f</url>
  <urlname>Mandurah War Memorial  : S3 Remembrance Stone by Boyzrule5</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99002433" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Mandurah War Memorial  : S3 Remembrance Stone</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Boyzrule5</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Boyzrule5</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Mandurah War Memorial &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Remembrance Stone&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5976675f-4c37-4e93-8716-a38ecfb1993f"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5976675f-4c37-4e93-8716-a38ecfb1993f&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Radius: 20m&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kind of question: single&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What are the last three words on the plaque on the right?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c4ce1c9f-90f2-44d0-8a27-c950d674d2e0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The memorial includes a remembrance stone carved from black granite. Listed in it are the conflicts involving Australian service men and women. 
Water flowing through the monument and into the estuary echoes the lapping of the tide at ANZAC Cove. 
The pillars recreate the physical journey and emotional tension of the of the soldiers who courageously stormed the beaches and rose from the trenches to face the conflict that confronted them. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6852750b-7733-4bb6-b95d-6bbcd1362033" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This adventure lab is based at the latest War Memorial. The first was located on the western bank of the estuary, opposite the town on Mary Street and Old Coast Road. In 1997 major road works impacted the site. The original structure was removed and remodelled and installed at the City of Mandurah RSL sun-branch on the corner of ANZAC Place and Third Avenue Mandurah. 

Ref: https://www.mandurah.wa.gov.au/explore/arts-and-culture/war-memorial&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.532233" lon="115.714267">
  <ele>5.0</ele>
