  <desc>MandurahWarMem5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5976675f-4c37-4e93-8716-a38ecfb1993f</url>
  <urlname>Mandurah War Memorial  : S5 Ceremonial Space by Boyzrule5</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="99002435" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Mandurah War Memorial  : S5 Ceremonial Space</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Boyzrule5</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Boyzrule5</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Mandurah War Memorial &lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Ceremonial Space&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5976675f-4c37-4e93-8716-a38ecfb1993f"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5976675f-4c37-4e93-8716-a38ecfb1993f&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Radius: 20m&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kind of question: single&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Which number anniversary does this plaque commemorate?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/da466915-4557-4492-b20a-37708f353c8e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Annual ceremonies held at the memorial represent the convergence of the living with the spirit of the fallen. In its use as a ceremonial space, the Memorial includes a list of the theatres of war in which Australian Service men and women were involved, elevated platforms for flags, speakers, wreath laying and room for a 50 strong choir. At the centre is a black stone plinth, set in water and surrounded by a concrete platform. This is used by the catafalque party to stand during services. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6852750b-7733-4bb6-b95d-6bbcd1362033" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This adventure lab is based at the latest War Memorial. The first was located on the western bank of the estuary, opposite the town on Mary Street and Old Coast Road. In 1997 major road works impacted the site. The original structure was removed and remodelled and installed at the City of Mandurah RSL sun-branch on the corner of ANZAC Place and Third Avenue Mandurah. 

Ref: https://www.mandurah.wa.gov.au/explore/arts-and-culture/war-memorial&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
