   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;The Geocaching Museum of Cache Types&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Gallery 6: EarthCache&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a152d441-6107-4f08-a423-4956b1288a71"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a152d441-6107-4f08-a423-4956b1288a71&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Radius: 100m&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kind of question: single&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What science do EarthCaches usually focus on?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/23ae19a1-8cc0-47a7-9f23-a3f545377ef3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;EarthCaches teach geology at real-world sites instead of having containers.
WA Examples:
Countless Cockles at Shell Beach in Shark Bay.
Cape Peron in Rockingham Lakes Regional Park.
Bunbury Basalt in the South West.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d6ae80bb-6eae-4499-a423-f98a37cf219b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Geocaching Museum! Across ten galleries, you'll learn about the different cache types that geocachers can hide or find. Each gallery features an example from Western Australia, connecting global cache types with local flavor. After each exhibit, you'll answer a quick question to test your knowledge.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
