   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;The Geocaching Museum of Cache Types&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Gallery 7: Virtual Cache&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a152d441-6107-4f08-a423-4956b1288a71"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a152d441-6107-4f08-a423-4956b1288a71&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Radius: 100m&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kind of question: single&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Do Virtual Caches have physical containers? (Yes/No)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/58d4f03a-3d71-4794-a289-c085189d6ae3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Virtuals have no physical container. Instead, you answer a question or submit a photo at the location.

WA Example: WA's Virtuals highlight lighthouses, statues, heritage buildings, and coastal lookouts—perfect spots to showcase without containers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d6ae80bb-6eae-4499-a423-f98a37cf219b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Geocaching Museum! Across ten galleries, you'll learn about the different cache types that geocachers can hide or find. Each gallery features an example from Western Australia, connecting global cache types with local flavor. After each exhibit, you'll answer a quick question to test your knowledge.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
