   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;The Geocaching Museum of Cache Types&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Gallery 10: Adventure Lab&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a152d441-6107-4f08-a423-4956b1288a71"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a152d441-6107-4f08-a423-4956b1288a71&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Radius: 100m&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kind of question: single&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What type of cache experience are you doing right now?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/bb04dd86-5033-4497-8566-9a69f25f1bc0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This final gallery is the one you're exploring right now.

Adventure Labs are app-based experiences guiding you through stories, places, and discoveries. They don't require a physical container.

WA Example: Adventure Labs in WA highlight Aboriginal heritage, urban street art, and lighthouses—perfect places where a container might not work.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d6ae80bb-6eae-4499-a423-f98a37cf219b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Geocaching Museum! Across ten galleries, you'll learn about the different cache types that geocachers can hide or find. Each gallery features an example from Western Australia, connecting global cache types with local flavor. After each exhibit, you'll answer a quick question to test your knowledge.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
