   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Geocaching Muesum Adventure Lab&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Gallery 1: Traditional Cache&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/668319d0-fa9b-40a0-8c2e-c8bc1c557771"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/668319d0-fa9b-40a0-8c2e-c8bc1c557771&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Radius: 200m&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kind of question: multiple choice&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What must you sign inside a Traditional Cache?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c7019e26-d92e-4a94-9ac7-fe83b58b99e6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Step into the first gallery—the foundation of geocaching.

Traditional Caches are the original form of geocaching: go to the listed coordinates, find the container, sign the logbook.

Perth suburbs and regional WA are full of Traditionals, from sneaky nanos to ammo cans in the bush. They're the bread-and-butter of caching here.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b1d01425-2f5c-430d-9ec8-61bcf97c9cfc" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Geocaching Museum! Across ten galleries, you'll learn about the different cache types that geocachers can hide or find. Each gallery features an example from Western Australia, connecting global cache types with local flavour. After each exhibit, you'll answer a quick question to test your knowledge.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
