   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Geocaching Muesum Adventure Lab&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Gallery 3: Multi-Cache&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/668319d0-fa9b-40a0-8c2e-c8bc1c557771"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/668319d0-fa9b-40a0-8c2e-c8bc1c557771&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Radius: 200m&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kind of question: multiple choice&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the minimum number of stages a Multi-Cache must have?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/fd141ce7-a308-456c-8527-6d2a7710d61a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Follow the trail through this multi-stage gallery.

Multi-Caches require visiting two or more locations, with clues leading you to the final.

WA Example: WA hills walks often feature Multis—one stage might be a lookout, the next a plaque, then the final hidden nearby.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b1d01425-2f5c-430d-9ec8-61bcf97c9cfc" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Geocaching Museum! Across ten galleries, you'll learn about the different cache types that geocachers can hide or find. Each gallery features an example from Western Australia, connecting global cache types with local flavour. After each exhibit, you'll answer a quick question to test your knowledge.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
