   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Geocaching Muesum Adventure Lab&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Gallery 4: Event Cache&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/668319d0-fa9b-40a0-8c2e-c8bc1c557771"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/668319d0-fa9b-40a0-8c2e-c8bc1c557771&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Radius: 200m&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kind of question: multiple choice&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What type of cache involves meeting in person?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/834af0b5-e32f-4f70-9e9e-6f30b5389be9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The museum opens into a gathering hall.

Event Caches are about people meeting to share the game.

WA Example: Perth and WA towns regularly host coffee meetups, park picnics, and even special holiday gatherings where geocachers swap stories.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b1d01425-2f5c-430d-9ec8-61bcf97c9cfc" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Geocaching Museum! Across ten galleries, you'll learn about the different cache types that geocachers can hide or find. Each gallery features an example from Western Australia, connecting global cache types with local flavour. After each exhibit, you'll answer a quick question to test your knowledge.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
