   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;h3&gt;Geocaching Muesum Adventure Lab&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Gallery 5: CITO (Cache In Trash Out)&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/668319d0-fa9b-40a0-8c2e-c8bc1c557771"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/668319d0-fa9b-40a0-8c2e-c8bc1c557771&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Radius: 200m&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kind of question: multiple choice&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What does the "I" in CITO stand for?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b5679665-6d3e-4387-838f-ca0cc464f128" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the environmental wing of the museum.

CITO events focus on conservation—collecting rubbish, planting trees, or restoring parks.

WA Example: Many CITOs in Perth and regional WA have cleaned up riverbanks, beaches, and trails—giving back to the environment while caching.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Descriptions&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b1d01425-2f5c-430d-9ec8-61bcf97c9cfc" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Geocaching Museum! Across ten galleries, you'll learn about the different cache types that geocachers can hide or find. Each gallery features an example from Western Australia, connecting global cache types with local flavour. After each exhibit, you'll answer a quick question to test your knowledge.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
