   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Dolphins @ Koombana Bay &lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Type of Dolphin&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c0de3730-100d-4fb9-ab71-3e0bdbb54a24" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c0de3730-100d-4fb9-ab71-3e0bdbb54a24&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 20m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    multiple choice
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What type of dolphins call Koombana Bay home.&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ac9a7272-d1e2-4873-abdd-e77881f6aad7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Hopefully today while you are completing this Adventure Lab you get to see some of the beautiful dolphins that frequent Koombana Bay&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/500d5d94-d04b-46e4-b211-f025332e49aa" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Koombana Bay is not just home to the Dolphin Discovery Centre, it&amp;#039;s also one of the best spots for seeing dolphins from the shore in the South West. It&amp;#039;s common to spot dolphins swimming and playing in the calm, sheltered waters of the bay. Visitors can often see the dolphins up close, as they venture close to the shoreline.

This Adventure Lab is dedicated to facts about the dolphins of Koombana Bay&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
