   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Westonia, a town steeped in history&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Westonia Cemetery &lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d5babed6-bda5-4e4e-a0c7-3675ebaeda2d" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d5babed6-bda5-4e4e-a0c7-3675ebaeda2d&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 100m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The first burial in the cemetery dates back to which year?&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/045d7cc8-b8c1-4bd2-b475-c9fe04ae96ff" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;The Westonia Cemetery was established around the early 1900s, with its first burial in the early 1900’s. The cemetery&amp;#039;s history is marked by events like a large number of deaths from the 1919 influenza pandemic and other mining-related diseases, and its reopening in 1977 with the addition of a niche wall in 1998. The Shire of Westonia maintains the cemetery, which is located on Wolfram Street, and is responsible for managing burial and cremated remains services&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/afcf55ae-3183-46a1-adf9-c7e1384c61bf" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Westonia is a town full of accessible history. Located just off the Great Eastern Highway North East of Perth. 

The town is proud of its heritage. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
