                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Westonia, a town steeped in history&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Ambulance and Fire Station &lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d5babed6-bda5-4e4e-a0c7-3675ebaeda2d" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/d5babed6-bda5-4e4e-a0c7-3675ebaeda2d&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 100m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    multiple choice
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;A fire brigade was established in which year?&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/311a594e-2143-4929-9dd6-9fa66f3b94fd" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Westonia relies on the Department of Fire and Emergency Services (DFES) (DFES) and St John Ambulance for emergency services, with its historical presence influenced by the larger WA gold rush era and the statewide development of volunteer services. While specific historical records for Westonia are limited in the provided search snippets, the region follows the general Western Australian pattern of volunteer brigades forming in response to population growth and the need for community support during the late 19th and early 20th centuries, with a transition to modern, state-coordinated services. &lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/afcf55ae-3183-46a1-adf9-c7e1384c61bf" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Westonia is a town full of accessible history. Located just off the Great Eastern Highway North East of Perth. 

The town is proud of its heritage. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
