   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Monkey Mia &lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Super Sea Grass&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/db824175-8f45-4cc2-b4ad-becd5dcecddd" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/db824175-8f45-4cc2-b4ad-becd5dcecddd&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 40m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    multiple choice
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Dugongs (Wuthuga) eat up to how many Kgs of seagrass per day?&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/587bafba-65ef-4003-b992-b67da0ef94f2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Look for the sign on sea grass to find the answer you are looking for&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/080fdec1-a252-410c-83fe-d5a2dd51799c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Welcome to the wonderful Monkey Mia. Famous for its almost daily visiting bottlenose Dolphins. 
With crystal clear waters, amazing sunrise and sunsets Monkey Mia is a marine park like no other. Laze on the beach, kayak amongst the turtles, dugongs and other sea life. Go for a cruise on a catamaran - the choice is yours. 
A tourist hot spot with accommodation available in the nearby resort or pitch up a tent or park up your van at the camp site, you might even get a friendly visit from an emu. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
