                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Lake Goollelal Boardwalk&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Viewing Platform&lt;/h4&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background:#990000;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;"&gt;
        linear
    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c88315b5-6eb2-4338-ae09-624913d00fe4" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c88315b5-6eb2-4338-ae09-624913d00fe4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 25m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many frogs are there in total?&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9d791c91-c9c7-4e56-b1eb-e3afd1f58759" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;There are three wooden seats in this area, two near the coordinates and one at the end of the lookout.  Take a seat, sit quietly and enjoy the wildlife and the view for a while. 
Keep your eyes open, can you see the frogs?  You may have to search for a while to see them all.
  &lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/6d2a9f01-7fc0-40a6-a0f2-ed8e44a54042" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;The Goollelal Boardwalk is a new 380-meter walkway featuring two viewing platforms that extend over Lake Goollelal in Yellagonga Regional Park. Now complete, the boardwalk is part of the Yellagonga Regional Park Improvement Project and offers improved accessibility to the lake&amp;#039;s biodiversity and historic sites, including the former Luisini Winery. The area is also undergoing development with new amenities, including a café and playground, to enhance nature-based tourism and community engagement. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
