  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cfb0219a-fee5-4492-a67c-d236997e6565</url>
  <urlname>Wanneroo Heritage Artwork : S3 Looking West by FelixII</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="9663606" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Wanneroo Heritage Artwork : S3 Looking West</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>FelixII</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">FelixII</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Wanneroo Heritage Artwork&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Looking West&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cfb0219a-fee5-4492-a67c-d236997e6565" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cfb0219a-fee5-4492-a67c-d236997e6565&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 20m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What&amp;#039;s in the net? &lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9b9ed8e6-b910-42ae-b89e-cb32f6be63ea" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;This roundabout was quite controversial when it was first built. Can you guess why? Yep the bollards!

The sculpture in the middle is constructed from cast steel, granite and stainless steel, and depicts a figure striding out atop a granite base with fishing net on one side and a rake on the other. Jon Tarry created the figure, facing west into the wind off the sea, like a sheet of cloth in the wind. The figure welcomes visitors to Wanneroo and pays homage to the City’s market gardening and fishing heritage. The rake symbolises gardening, growth and cultivation. The net similarly indicates the theme of harvest and life.&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/02809708-7164-44e0-b816-533a7fae1177" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;A short tour of Artwork in the City of Wanneroo.  Share in some local history.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
