   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Wanneroo Heritage Artwork&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Schooling in Wanneroo&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cfb0219a-fee5-4492-a67c-d236997e6565" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cfb0219a-fee5-4492-a67c-d236997e6565&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 20m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;7 word phrase at the bottom of the alphabet&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/846c6ba6-d3bc-44cb-93a5-9470abd26935" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Ahh the trusty blackboard, don&amp;#039;t see too many of them around anymore having been mostly replaced by whiteboards.  Remember the chalk breaking, or having the duster thrown at you? The terrible sound of fingernails screeching down the board. This artwork even had a geocache once upon a time. Imagine trying to find that with the constant stream of muggles in this area.

See if you remember your A B C&amp;#039;s and times tables.&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/02809708-7164-44e0-b816-533a7fae1177" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;A short tour of Artwork in the City of Wanneroo.  Share in some local history.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.749917" lon="115.801867">
  <ele>43.0</ele>
  <time>2025-10-26T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBP8GH-1</name>
  <desc>WannerooHerita1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cfb0219a-fee5-4492-a67c-d236997e6565</url>
  <urlname>Wanneroo Heritage Artwork : S1 Original Wanneroo Townsite Northern Boundary by FelixII</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="9663604" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Wanneroo Heritage Artwork : S1 Original Wanneroo Townsite Northern Boundary</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>FelixII</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">FelixII</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Wanneroo Heritage Artwork&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Original Wanneroo Townsite Northern Boundary&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cfb0219a-fee5-4492-a67c-d236997e6565" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/cfb0219a-fee5-4492-a67c-d236997e6565&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 20m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;On the power pole near GZ, What is the sequence of numbers and letters on the barcode &lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/28d95204-fc27-4b2c-8b41-7abd3cf67c4f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;This point represents the original northern boundary of the Wanneroo townsite established in 1907 at the 16-mile peg of Wanneroo Road. Until the late 1970s, addresses along Wanneroo Road were
given using the closest mile peg to the location. So a property’s address would be given, for example, as the ’13-mile’ or ’19-mile‘. 

Imagine travelling here up the old Wanneroo Block Road. Quite a journey back in 1907
&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
