  <groundspeak:cache id="9667903" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>York Tiny Doors : S4 Town Hall</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Dobenaire</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Dobenaire</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;York Tiny Doors&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Town Hall&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/8bd030ed-c9a5-4a32-8f96-5e691457fb4a" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/8bd030ed-c9a5-4a32-8f96-5e691457fb4a&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 20m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    multiple choice
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Fairies love to dance in ....?&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ac8bce4f-1aa7-424b-88c3-d916bbf8132b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;You never know where our tiny doors turn up! Come into the court yard and you will find this one.&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/37ef8419-f724-466f-ba8e-3738ed9d5c5f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Welcome to the wonderful world of Fairy Doors. York has an assortment of tiny doors hidden throughout the town but you will need to look carefully as they are not always easy to find. This adventure lab will take you to just 5 of them - I wonder how many others you discover along the way? &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.888817" lon="116.768133">
  <ele>183.0</ele>
  <time>2025-11-07T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBPCZY-1</name>
  <desc>AmanaTragedyS1T</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e59b18fc-ada1-44cf-b85b-c199634c5da8</url>
  <urlname>Amana Tragedy : S1 The Plane by Geotrakka</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="9667894" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Amana Tragedy : S1 The Plane</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Geotrakka</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Geotrakka</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Amana Tragedy&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;The Plane&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e59b18fc-ada1-44cf-b85b-c199634c5da8" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e59b18fc-ada1-44cf-b85b-c199634c5da8&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 20m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many windows are on the side of the plane?&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0edb4497-6032-4cad-a047-12a2d4416f4b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;All questions can be answered from the same location.
You are looking for the model plane sculpture.&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/db97a764-66b0-4547-8605-26075fa38bf1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Australias worst peacetime air disaster was Australian National Airways VH-ANA which resulted in 29 fatalities. The flight left with 24 passengers heading from Perth on an 8 hour flight to Adelaide in June 1950. Only 22 minutes after take off and 56km east of Perth Airport the Douglas DC-4 Skymaster crashed 19 kms east of York into thick forest. Local farmers heard the low flying plane and the explosion and raced to the rescue. There was one sole survivor found walking around in a daze and badly burnt. The rescuers walked him out through the thick bushland 3 kms by stretcher until the ambulance could reach them. Sadly he died 5 days later in RPH. A total of 29 people - 5 crew and 24 passengers lost their lives.

After the shire rejected two proposals to build a memorial to honour the crash, Settlers House took it upon themselves with the help of residents to establish this monument and hold a ceremony made possible entirely by volunteer work.

The boulder you are looking at is from the Inkpens property the plane crashed on, hauled into town by tractor through community effort. The sculptors donated their art work, the plaques were donated by the Pilots son, the space containing the rose garden was donated by a York resident.

On 18 Oct 2025 - 75 years after the Amana went down, York has unveiled its own memorial of the AMANA disaster 

This memorial is not just in respect for the lives lost that night in June 1950, it is also to honour the brave responders that risked their lives to head to the burning plane and finally to show that the love and kindness of a small town can make things happen when you all work together. True community spirit ??&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
