   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Toapin Weir&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Kunzea pulchella&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5dba02ef-2904-4d10-927e-394f251bca26" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5dba02ef-2904-4d10-927e-394f251bca26&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 100m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    multiple choice
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How wide does it grow?&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/98cca159-2560-49f1-9ae8-68649654a65f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Kunzea pulchella is also known as the "Granite Bottlebrush". It is a shrub that can growto 3-4 metres high and 6 metres wide. It produces red and white/cream flowers from Juneto November. It is usually found in skeletal sand or clay soils and is associated with granite outcrops and slopes.&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0933b13c-784f-4f68-a8cf-a139985bfaa3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;This is a quick lab at Toapin Weir&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
