    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 100m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    multiple choice
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How high can they grow?&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f8eb3981-b0a3-4fa4-8622-bad3f8159615" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Diplolaena velutinais a spreading shrub that can growto 2 - 2.5 metres high. It produces yellow-green/red-orangeflowers from February/Mayto November. It is found in sandysoils, and within granite outcrops, rocks and hills.&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/0933b13c-784f-4f68-a8cf-a139985bfaa3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
