   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Robinson Reserve 1&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;How Moovellous!&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/21a92acb-3782-4cfa-aeeb-d67855415058" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/21a92acb-3782-4cfa-aeeb-d67855415058&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 20m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What are the names of the cow and her calf? (3 words: ______ and _____)&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/409da13a-f393-4277-8037-8534bd6c0069" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Udderly beautiful artwork!

Created by Artist Mehdi Rasulle in 2019. Made from re-enforced concrete with steel frames, the cows took around 3 months to create and weigh about 800kg. 
Celebrating the importance of Robinson Reserve to the local community, these sculptures remind us of the rich agricultural history of Tuart Hill. The Holstein cow and her calf are a tribute to William Edward Robinson (1880 - 1932) who set up a dairy farm here in 1905
Their names, chosen by the community, recall the market gardens that the area became renowned for. These gentle animals rest here to welcome visitors to this beautiful public space.&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e2780fae-7e0a-4896-9486-1543dd086d5f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Robinson Reserve is a seven-hectare reserve, adjacent to the Osborne Community Hub. It is bound by Royal, Park and Waterloo Streets in Tuart Hill. The reserve is classified as a district open space and provides valuable sporting and recreational opportunities for the community. It is home to the Osborne Agricultural Society and Osborne Park Cricket Club.
At the reserve you will find a playground, shelters, BBQ, public toilets, picnic tables, skate area, basketball half-court, cricket nets and an accessible path network circulating the park.
The reserve is named after William Edward Robinson (1880-1932), a well known dairyman in the area. He established his dairy in 1905.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
