   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Meandering through The Pines. &lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Picnic time &lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ac4f0275-7cbc-4198-9c8a-2b1fa191621d" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/ac4f0275-7cbc-4198-9c8a-2b1fa191621d&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 20m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many bbq’s are under each shelter. One word. &lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c3fe0a6f-ce15-44df-96f8-171cc076d50f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Enjoy some time out relaxing with family and friends at the newly installed bbq and picnic areas. &lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/774844d9-afea-475c-8744-022cdc1505e3" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Gnangara pine plantation. 
A lovely open space to walk your dog along the trails, enjoy the fresh air or have a picnic at the newly installed bbq’s. 
Brief history:  The planting of pines began in the 1920s, chosen to grow on poor sandy soils in the Mediterranean region which was believed to be similar to local conditions.  Due to development of the area it is no longer feasible to replanting but it serves as a popular recreational spot. 
More history can be found on 
the information boards in the park. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
