    &lt;p&gt;Welcome to the Gnangara pine plantation. 
A lovely open space to walk your dog along the trails, enjoy the fresh air or have a picnic at the newly installed bbq’s. 
Brief history:  The planting of pines began in the 1920s, chosen to grow on poor sandy soils in the Mediterranean region which was believed to be similar to local conditions.  Due to development of the area it is no longer feasible to replanting but it serves as a popular recreational spot. 
More history can be found on 
the information boards in the park. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
