   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Kokoda/Vietnam Trail&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Vietnam War - A Historical View&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e901b100-58da-4935-9caa-31d4e8e91673" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e901b100-58da-4935-9caa-31d4e8e91673&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 25m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Possibly bonus:
            &lt;a href="https://coord.info/GCB7TVK" target="_blank"&gt;GCB7TVK&lt;/a&gt;        &lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The chemical, Agent Orange, went by what acronym? &lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/513f4bc8-415e-444e-a112-afda2a26f6f0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;The Vietnam War was a divisive war. Fought in the jungles of Vietnam but also in the Parliaments of involved countries. 

The civil war between North and South Vietnam, drew in countries from across the globe resulting in Australian troops being brought in, initially as observers and later fighting on the front line.

As the war progressed, dirty tactics were deployed including the dropping of Agent Orange, a herbicide that stripped the jungles of the foliage but also had horrific effects on the humans exposed.

The memorial here recognises those who lost their lives fighting in this war.  
&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b769644e-1977-45e3-8754-f9eb55873a00" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;***IMPORTANT UPDATE***
As of October 2025 the council is currently removing, refreshing and updating the information boards so this series has been altered to work without the information boards. 

The Kokoda Trail is a tribute to the service men and women of 1939 - 1945

It is a reminder of courageous efforts of the people who served Australia during World War II, especially those from the Goldfields.

The Vietnam War efforts of local community members are also recognised and remembered in this park.

This Lab is part of the Kokoda Trail Caches.

5 Physical Caches that tie in with these 5 Adventure Lab caches to result in 1 Bonus cache (&amp;lt;a href="https://coord.info/GCB7TVK" target="_blank"&amp;gt;GCB7TVK&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt;)

Ensure you take note of the Letter and Number you receive upon completing each stage, to complete the bonus cache.
 

This series is best suited for a bicycle, E-Scooter or on foot. There are sections of both sealed and unsealed paths however the unsealed sections are very compact and very easily traversed. It is approximately 5kms return of flat terrain. 

Double Gees are prevalent so wear suitable shoes

It is suggested to park near the listed coordinates and complete the series from here. There are toilets, drinking water, caravan parking, 72hr camping and even coffee at most times.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
