                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Keeping Prendwick Green&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Water for the Community Garden&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/529dfb5b-fb52-4eb4-aca2-2935a1097c05" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/529dfb5b-fb52-4eb4-aca2-2935a1097c05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 20m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    multiple choice
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many white orchids are illustrated on this tank?&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/23511c39-efd0-489b-a649-02ce89984788" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Local gardening enthusiasts spend some of their leisure time tending their various plants in the local community garden. Through the fence, a colourfully decorated rainwater tank is evidence of the use of this water source for the garden.&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/91bad608-2509-4999-af63-9401f51d37a1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;The warmer months are a wonderful time to get out in the increasingly abundant sunshine and go for a walk around a well-tended suburban park. Despite record winter rains, summer is on its way and alternative sources of water must be found for plants and animals alike. During your walk, discover five sources of one of our most precious resources that is used to keep this area green.  

&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
