  <desc>GarveyParkS5Art</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bdf06e18-4011-4525-8842-5f7b89e3bb86</url>
  <urlname>Garvey Park : S5 Art studio? by Puzzzzler</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="9688856" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Garvey Park : S5 Art studio?</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Puzzzzler</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Puzzzzler</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Garvey Park&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Art studio?&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bdf06e18-4011-4525-8842-5f7b89e3bb86" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bdf06e18-4011-4525-8842-5f7b89e3bb86&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 20m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What kind of Studio was this building used for?&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4381ea0d-ac30-429f-b09f-eef376cc9ee9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;I believe this building was originally the Kiosk in Garvey park. It also was once leased as an Art studio. The new Kiosk is situated next to the Kayak club. &lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2cf8b825-5313-43eb-b96f-49684f12ca5b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Garvey Park is a lovely place to walk or have a picnic, with a playground for kids and undercover BBQ’s. A lovely grassed area right on the Swan River. Great place to walk your dog or swim in the river. Lots of parking with public toilets ( behind the kiosk). 
This adventure lab is just a short stroll around the area to take in the views and facilities. 
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.921917" lon="115.94295">
  <ele>12.0</ele>
  <time>2025-12-27T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBQ3T0-1</name>
  <desc>GarveyParkS1ABi</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bdf06e18-4011-4525-8842-5f7b89e3bb86</url>
  <urlname>Garvey Park : S1 A bit of history by Puzzzzler</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="9688852" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Garvey Park : S1 A bit of history</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Puzzzzler</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Puzzzzler</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Garvey Park&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;A bit of history&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bdf06e18-4011-4525-8842-5f7b89e3bb86" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/bdf06e18-4011-4525-8842-5f7b89e3bb86&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 20m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;In what year was the upgraded version operated until? (Answer on plaque)&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/64adf51a-e82e-41b7-8e6f-5e52801fb0c9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;In the early part of the century they used to draw clay from the Swan River to supply clay to the local brickworks and potteries, this closed in the mid 1970s. 
What we have now is a lovely grassed playground and picnic area. 
&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2cf8b825-5313-43eb-b96f-49684f12ca5b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Garvey Park is a lovely place to walk or have a picnic, with a playground for kids and undercover BBQ’s. A lovely grassed area right on the Swan River. Great place to walk your dog or swim in the river. Lots of parking with public toilets ( behind the kiosk). 
This adventure lab is just a short stroll around the area to take in the views and facilities. 
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.921767" lon="115.94205">
