   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;BYOM 10 AdLab Art #06&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Reptiles - Crocodiles&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/167c997c-918c-4e16-b2a3-92d17de0fa53" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/167c997c-918c-4e16-b2a3-92d17de0fa53&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 500m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Possibly bonus:
            &lt;a href="https://coord.info/GCBER3Q" target="_blank"&gt;GCBER3Q&lt;/a&gt;        &lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    multiple choice
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Who was the famous Crocodile man from Australia ?&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c1cf5e9d-30be-4d2f-88c0-2c4ee83dc0c9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Crocodiles are large, predatory, semi-aquatic reptiles known for their powerful jaws, armored skin, and long tails, belonging to the order Crocodilia, which also includes alligators, caimans, and gharials. As reptiles, they are cold-blooded (ectothermic) and regulate their body temperature by basking in the sun or resting in the shade, and they are the closest living relatives to birds. They live in tropical regions across Africa, Asia, the Americas, and Australia, inhabiting freshwater and saltwater environments. &lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/58fb7056-095b-4803-8649-90af5bf4f8f5" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Welcome to the BYOM 10 AdLab art series. What is BYOM 10? Bring Your Own Marshmallows (BYOM) is a series of events hosted by the Fellowship of the Trail, usually at a campground in regional WA. To celebrate our 10th event this year at Eaglestone Rock, (&amp;lt;a href="https://coord.info/GCBER3Q" target="_blank"&amp;gt;GCBER3Q&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt;), we&amp;#039;ve put together a little geoart for all to enjoy. All the stages have multiple choice answers and a 500 meter geofence to hopefully minimise the limited cell coverage.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
