   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;BYOM 10 AdLab Art #09&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Australian Native Animals - Koalas&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5ff5da38-65e0-4c5a-9d5c-f35591799697" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/5ff5da38-65e0-4c5a-9d5c-f35591799697&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 500m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Possibly bonus:
            &lt;a href="https://coord.info/GCBER3Q" target="_blank"&gt;GCBER3Q&lt;/a&gt;        &lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    multiple choice
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;A close relation to the Koala is ?&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3c6ec85a-b73d-45ca-bd93-675d81c4769e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;The koala (Phascolarctos cinereus) is an iconic, tree-dwelling marsupial native to Australia, known for its large head, fluffy ears, and prominent black nose, but it is not a bear. It is an herbivore that feeds almost exclusively on eucalyptus leaves, getting most of its water from them, and is known for sleeping up to 18 hours a day. Koalas are classified as Vulnerable or Endangered in many parts of Australia due to threats like habitat loss, disease, and climate change. &lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4cc005bd-fe28-40e2-9ebe-cc3fcae7bf9e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Welcome to the BYOM 10 AdLab art series. What is BYOM 10? Bring Your Own Marshmallows (BYOM) is a series of events hosted by the Fellowship of the Trail, usually at a campground in regional WA. To celebrate our 10th event this year at Eaglestone Rock, (&amp;lt;a href="https://coord.info/GCBER3Q" target="_blank"&amp;gt;GCBER3Q&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt;), we&amp;#039;ve put together a little geoart for all to enjoy. All the stages have multiple choice answers and a 500 meter geofence to hopefully minimise the limited cell coverage.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
