                    multiple choice
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;So Burswood/Crown just hit 40 years old in Dec25, how many of the original day 1 employees made it to 40 years? &lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/df98a2d7-4402-44b5-a79e-02343892e976" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;When Burswood Island Casino (now Crown Perth) opened on December 30, 1985, it employed around 1000 staff; its current employee numbers sit around 5,000. making it Western Australia&amp;#039;s largest single-site employer and has been for several decades.&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/495f602a-da3d-46fb-ad8c-60b9084c8309" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Crown Casino Perth has now been around for 40 years, and there should be a few interesting facts by now. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-32.168117" lon="115.978017">
