 <wpt lat="-31.9309" lon="115.859183">
  <ele>35.0</ele>
  <time>2026-02-11T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBQN5J-1</name>
  <desc>NorthPerthHeri1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b2844e9f-1136-4866-aacd-08282acd3d0e</url>
  <urlname>North Perth Heritage Buildings : S1 Rosemount Hotel by familysteiner</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="9705548" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>North Perth Heritage Buildings : S1 Rosemount Hotel</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>familysteiner</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">familysteiner</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;North Perth Heritage Buildings&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Rosemount Hotel&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b2844e9f-1136-4866-aacd-08282acd3d0e" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/b2844e9f-1136-4866-aacd-08282acd3d0e&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 20m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Looking towards the hotel from the footpath, how many steps up are on the RIGHT HAND SIDE? (Word)&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ca2d171f-bdbc-4fb1-a220-0d9e381ff867" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Constructed in 1902 during the Gold Rush years, the Rosemount Hotel (known locally as the "Rosie") has operated as a continuous hotel since its inception, later evolving into a premier mid-size live music venue. The building&amp;#039;s architecture reflects typical turn-of-the-century design with a public bar on the ground floor and accommodation above. It was significantly renovated in the Art Deco style during the late 1930s. From the 1980s, the venue cemented its reputation in the local community as a cornerstone of Perth&amp;#039;s live music scene, hosting a diverse range of local and touring bands&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4ca77558-4821-4026-870a-224310403b71" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;North Perth developed from low-lying seasonal wetlands significant to the Whadjuk Noongar people into farmland and market gardens in the mid-19th century before rapid residential growth during the WA gold boom of the 1890s. Land was subdivided under enticing names like Toorak and Woodville around 1895–1901, and the area was officially named North Perth in 1901; its early civic infrastructure included the North Perth Primary School (opened 1899), North Perth Town Hall (1902/1910), churches, shops and pubs, aided by tram connections to the city. North Perth briefly operated as its own municipality from 1901 until amalgamation into the City of Perth in 1914, and continued expansion between the world wars brought local businesses and community facilities. Post-World War II migration diversified the population, with European and later Asian communities contributing to its cultural tapestry, and today the suburb is appreciated for its heritage architecture, village-style streets and close-in urban living.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
