    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;In what year did the Canning Jarrah Timber Co. lease the land &lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/feca6215-da7c-4d11-8a66-900dc448d78a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Gathering information while walking in the park&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/572b9cff-5054-41d4-a6ed-bf17830894e0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;DARDANUP is a quaint little town just 15 mins South East of Bunbury . With a fabulous little bakery and being gateway to Ferguson Valley and Gnomesville , it is both a commuter town to Bunbury and a destination in its own right. The Eunice Fowler Park runs along side the township and has the old railway line running through it .&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
