  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/fb90ac35-d27a-4472-bbed-82a175980994</url>
  <urlname>JC-Wilson Park Precinct : S5 Basketball Court by Jack_Cheng</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="9716688" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>JC-Wilson Park Precinct : S5 Basketball Court</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Jack_Cheng</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Jack_Cheng</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;JC-Wilson Park Precinct&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Basketball Court&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/fb90ac35-d27a-4472-bbed-82a175980994" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/fb90ac35-d27a-4472-bbed-82a175980994&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 30m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;How many total points are marked on the wall? &lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/18e4e49e-f007-4766-a19e-ea0f22eb1b89" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Basketball court is next to the netball courts and playground. &lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/cbba45ca-18ff-44c7-9e4d-922338997f5d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Wilson Park Precinct is located within the country of the Whadjuk Noongar People, and includes the registered Aboriginal heritage site, Rivervale Camp (DPLH 3717). Recorded during a broad survey of Aboriginal areas of significance in 1985, the place is identified as an Aboriginal camp that was occupied between 1910 and 1920.

As part of the initial concept design process, a Heritage Report was initiated including engagement with the Whadjuk Working Group and Traditional Owner representatives. This was followed by lodgment of a Section 18 Notice (under Aboriginal Heritage Act 1972) with the Department of Planning, Lands and Heritage, where Conditions of Consent were granted for the site.

Consultation and engagement with Traditional Owners and the local aboriginal community have continued for each stage of the project, guiding the design elements, themes and protocol for development of each zone.

[Credit: https://connect.belmont.wa.gov.au/wilson-park-precinct]&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.963689" lon="115.914922">
  <ele>21.0</ele>
  <time>2026-03-08T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBR1QT-3</name>
  <desc>JCWilsonParkPr3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/fb90ac35-d27a-4472-bbed-82a175980994</url>
  <urlname>JC-Wilson Park Precinct : S3 Netball Courts by Jack_Cheng</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="9716686" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>JC-Wilson Park Precinct : S3 Netball Courts</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Jack_Cheng</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Jack_Cheng</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;JC-Wilson Park Precinct&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Netball Courts&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/fb90ac35-d27a-4472-bbed-82a175980994" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/fb90ac35-d27a-4472-bbed-82a175980994&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 30m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Who was the Deputy Mayor at the official opening?&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3cdc0768-31a3-4df1-b626-dca1f02f876f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;The Wilson Park Netball Facility was approximately 40 years old and has reached the end of its useful life causing potential slip, trip and fall hazards. The facility no longer mees the needs or standards for its primary user, the Belmont Netball Association, nor the wider community’s expectations.

The City’s contractor, MG Group Pty Ltd commenced on site on 21 September 2022, with works including:

removal and replacement of the existing pavement and installation of a new acrylic surface;
removal of existing lighting towers and installation of new energy efficient LED lighting;
multi-purpose court and hit up wall to enable wider community use for other physical activity options;
minor landscaping and fencing.&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/cbba45ca-18ff-44c7-9e4d-922338997f5d" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Wilson Park Precinct is located within the country of the Whadjuk Noongar People, and includes the registered Aboriginal heritage site, Rivervale Camp (DPLH 3717). Recorded during a broad survey of Aboriginal areas of significance in 1985, the place is identified as an Aboriginal camp that was occupied between 1910 and 1920.

As part of the initial concept design process, a Heritage Report was initiated including engagement with the Whadjuk Working Group and Traditional Owner representatives. This was followed by lodgment of a Section 18 Notice (under Aboriginal Heritage Act 1972) with the Department of Planning, Lands and Heritage, where Conditions of Consent were granted for the site.

Consultation and engagement with Traditional Owners and the local aboriginal community have continued for each stage of the project, guiding the design elements, themes and protocol for development of each zone.

[Credit: https://connect.belmont.wa.gov.au/wilson-park-precinct]&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-31.963453" lon="115.915073">
