 <wpt lat="-33.643933" lon="115.344583">
  <ele>2.0</ele>
  <time>2026-04-10T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBRCG1-2</name>
  <desc>OperationGamer2</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c7a05190-46d0-48e3-8156-f37797112e5c</url>
  <urlname>Operation Gamer ~ Busselton’s Monopoly Board Game : S2 The Busselton Jetty Huts by pood</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="9727015" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Operation Gamer ~ Busselton’s Monopoly Board Game : S2 The Busselton Jetty Huts</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>pood</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">pood</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Operation Gamer ~ Busselton’s Monopoly Board Game&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;The Busselton Jetty Huts&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c7a05190-46d0-48e3-8156-f37797112e5c" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c7a05190-46d0-48e3-8156-f37797112e5c&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 30m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What are the 4 word written on the lower part of the Train Exit and Entry sign?&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e3439d69-deec-4f6d-bfd2-6c795e35e60f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;The Busselton Jetty Huts were built in the year 2000. They were designed to resemble the original, historic swim huts from the early 1900’s that were previously destroyed by storms and fire.
Their purpose now is to house the Jetty Interpretive Centre and the start of the Jetty Train ride which goes out to the Underwater Obsevatory at the end of the Jetty. There is another Train Station here, the Roy Morris Platform, there are always Railway Stations on the Monopoly Game Board.&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/961a15bf-a5ce-4f0b-aceb-32354e25c29f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Worldwide Operation Cache Hide. 
If you hide it, they will come!
This Year’s Theme is “OPERATION Gamer"

Board Games, Video Games, Card Games, Sports,
anything that has to do with game competition 
is the subject of this current project.


This AdLab covers some nostalgic sites in Busselton that may be found on a Monopoly Board Game. 
Each site will reveal a code which you will need to use to unfold the coordinates for the Final Letterbox Cache.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-33.644267" lon="115.344917">
  <ele>5.0</ele>
  <time>2026-04-10T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBRCG1-4</name>
  <desc>OperationGamer4</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c7a05190-46d0-48e3-8156-f37797112e5c</url>
  <urlname>Operation Gamer ~ Busselton’s Monopoly Board Game : S4 Utilities in Monopoly by pood</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="9727017" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Operation Gamer ~ Busselton’s Monopoly Board Game : S4 Utilities in Monopoly</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>pood</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">pood</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Operation Gamer ~ Busselton’s Monopoly Board Game&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Utilities in Monopoly&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c7a05190-46d0-48e3-8156-f37797112e5c" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c7a05190-46d0-48e3-8156-f37797112e5c&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 30m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What are the surnames of the 2 tradesmen who rebuilt the crane?&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/58477b9a-91ff-4fed-921c-aca2e48f950a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;There were many different Utilities used in the good old days in the historical Port of Busselton. 
From the trains that serviced the ships, to the cranes that lifted the heavy supplies on and off these very early sailing ships, to the steam vessels of the later years of the shipping industry. &lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/961a15bf-a5ce-4f0b-aceb-32354e25c29f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Worldwide Operation Cache Hide. 
If you hide it, they will come!
