   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Operation Gamer ~ Busselton’s Monopoly Board Game&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Trains,  Planes and Automobiles&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c7a05190-46d0-48e3-8156-f37797112e5c" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c7a05190-46d0-48e3-8156-f37797112e5c&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 30m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What is the name of the oldest surviving Australian made Locomotive?&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8db2d954-b649-46e9-97e5-041953326948" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Travelling around the Monopoly Board Game one uses tokens to show where you land and secure your place in the game, there are cars, the ships, planes, and on the Aussie version there’s the old Holden Ute, a surfboard, a koala, the trusty farm Kelpie, a jar of Vegemite, even a pair of thongs. 
At this spot you will see through the massive windows the only surviving Australian made locomotive.&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/961a15bf-a5ce-4f0b-aceb-32354e25c29f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Worldwide Operation Cache Hide. 
If you hide it, they will come!
