   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Operation Gamer ~ Busselton’s Monopoly Board Game&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Busselton Train Station&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c7a05190-46d0-48e3-8156-f37797112e5c" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c7a05190-46d0-48e3-8156-f37797112e5c&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 30m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The Train Station has been shifted several times, it was originally located in what street?&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f7d77b48-538c-4baa-a8fd-95e46476bec7" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;The Busselton Railway Station is an integral pat of the local Busselton History.
It was built in 1894 and served the community with trains going out to the Jetty receiving and sending goods internationally, a big part of the fishing and jarrah industries. &lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/961a15bf-a5ce-4f0b-aceb-32354e25c29f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
