   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Operation Gamer ~ Busselton’s Monopoly Board Game&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Go Straight to Jail&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c7a05190-46d0-48e3-8156-f37797112e5c" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/c7a05190-46d0-48e3-8156-f37797112e5c&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 30m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;During the Colonial era, this heritage listed building contained the most important public buildings in the district. What did they provide? &lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/5d6ea6c2-85fe-4f6a-83b1-b167669076ca" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;There’s always a direct route to Jail on the Monoploy Board Game. 
Luckily for some, an opportunity may arise with a Chance or Community Card where you may have a Get Out of Jail Free card.
At this location you will be visiting the old Courthouse, Police Station and Goal.&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/961a15bf-a5ce-4f0b-aceb-32354e25c29f" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
