  <name>LBREV9-2</name>
  <desc>FallenSoldiers2</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1e0a2310-e76b-4c18-9ff8-09313cee6b63</url>
  <urlname>Fallen Soldiers Memorial  : S2 Grand Opening by Barnzy12</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="9729255" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Fallen Soldiers Memorial  : S2 Grand Opening</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Barnzy12</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Barnzy12</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Fallen Soldiers Memorial &lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Grand Opening&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1e0a2310-e76b-4c18-9ff8-09313cee6b63" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1e0a2310-e76b-4c18-9ff8-09313cee6b63&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 20m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Who unveiled the memorial? Last name only&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/31bfc95f-9bb1-4785-8b50-e117266dd395" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;The Katanning War Memorial was erected on the corner of Prosser Oval in 1921. The area was then known as the Recreation Ground. The Memorial was paid for by public subscription and there was great controversy about where it should be placed in town. When erected the soldier was facing the street and looking over the town. It was changed in the 1980&amp;#039;s with the development of the area as Prosser Park.&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1f9f64ad-76b6-43ec-a8fe-5138eeb88038" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;The monument commemorates those who died in service or were killed in action in World Wars One and Two.  The monument is of a statue of a soldier on top of a large plinth on a three-tiered base.

It was erected by public subscription and unveiled on ANZAC Day 1921 originally to commemorate those from World War One whose names are inscribed on a brass plaque. The names of those from World War Two were added in 1950.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-33.687717" lon="117.556217">
  <ele>313.0</ele>
  <time>2026-04-17T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBREV9-3</name>
  <desc>FallenSoldiers3</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1e0a2310-e76b-4c18-9ff8-09313cee6b63</url>
  <urlname>Fallen Soldiers Memorial  : S3 Korea &amp; Vietnam by Barnzy12</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="9729256" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Fallen Soldiers Memorial  : S3 Korea &amp; Vietnam</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Barnzy12</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Barnzy12</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Fallen Soldiers Memorial &lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Korea &amp;amp; Vietnam&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1e0a2310-e76b-4c18-9ff8-09313cee6b63" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1e0a2310-e76b-4c18-9ff8-09313cee6b63&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 20m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;On the Korean memorial stone, what are the last four words?&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1e3c0dd5-4dcf-4daf-8463-02ddebc4a877" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;A dozen designs were received for the Fallen Soldiers&amp;#039; Memorial at Katanning, which was thrown open to competition. The accepted design was that of a marble figure of a soldier, 6ft. high, upon a granite base, 13ft. high, the cost erected at Katanning being £750. In addition to that first cost, has to be added the bronze name plates and the carving of the inscription, and also the architect&amp;#039;s fee for supervision. These items are expected to bring the cost to £900, of which about half has been collected.&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1f9f64ad-76b6-43ec-a8fe-5138eeb88038" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;The monument commemorates those who died in service or were killed in action in World Wars One and Two.  The monument is of a statue of a soldier on top of a large plinth on a three-tiered base.

It was erected by public subscription and unveiled on ANZAC Day 1921 originally to commemorate those from World War One whose names are inscribed on a brass plaque. The names of those from World War Two were added in 1950.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
