 <wpt lat="-33.687783" lon="117.556167">
  <time>2026-04-17T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBREV9-1</name>
  <desc>FallenSoldiers1</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1e0a2310-e76b-4c18-9ff8-09313cee6b63</url>
  <urlname>Fallen Soldiers Memorial  : S1 Soldier by Barnzy12</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="9729254" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Fallen Soldiers Memorial  : S1 Soldier</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Barnzy12</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Barnzy12</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Fallen Soldiers Memorial &lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Soldier&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1e0a2310-e76b-4c18-9ff8-09313cee6b63" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1e0a2310-e76b-4c18-9ff8-09313cee6b63&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 20m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;There is a small plaque on the plinth (low down). The memorial was erected by public ________&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/911f3cb5-41d6-43d2-8e82-47992ac8135c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;The Katanning Fallen Soldiers Memorial, located in Prosser Park on Carew and Cliff Street, is a significant heritage monument featuring a life-size marble soldier on a granite plinth, unveiled in 1921 to honor local WWI and WWII casualties. The site, which underwent a major refurbishment in 2024–2025, also features a preserved WWI German-made Ottoman field gun&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1f9f64ad-76b6-43ec-a8fe-5138eeb88038" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;The monument commemorates those who died in service or were killed in action in World Wars One and Two.  The monument is of a statue of a soldier on top of a large plinth on a three-tiered base.

It was erected by public subscription and unveiled on ANZAC Day 1921 originally to commemorate those from World War One whose names are inscribed on a brass plaque. The names of those from World War Two were added in 1950.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-33.68775" lon="117.556267">
  <ele>313.0</ele>
  <time>2026-04-17T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBREV9-5</name>
  <desc>FallenSoldiers5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1e0a2310-e76b-4c18-9ff8-09313cee6b63</url>
  <urlname>Fallen Soldiers Memorial  : S5 Krupp Gun by Barnzy12</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="9729258" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Fallen Soldiers Memorial  : S5 Krupp Gun</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Barnzy12</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Barnzy12</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Fallen Soldiers Memorial &lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Krupp Gun&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1e0a2310-e76b-4c18-9ff8-09313cee6b63" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1e0a2310-e76b-4c18-9ff8-09313cee6b63&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 20m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The gun was captured by the Australian light horse in what year?&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1edb2be4-d19c-4bee-b4a3-10086f7727b1" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;This field gun was captured by the Australian Light Horse in Palestine in 1918. Along with other captured equipment, it became what were known as "war trophies."
• At the conclusion of the war, these trophies were shipped back to Australia and distributed among the nation&amp;#039;s many cities and towns.
• The State War Trophy Committee advised that war trophies were to be allocated based on local population size. As a result, Katanning was initially designated to receive a trench mortar. However, following protests from the town arguing that it deserved a more significant trophy, the Committee revised its decision and advised that Katanning would receive a field gun, provided it was formally requested
• The field gun arrived in time for the official unveiling of the Fallen Soldiers Memorial.&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/1f9f64ad-76b6-43ec-a8fe-5138eeb88038" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;The monument commemorates those who died in service or were killed in action in World Wars One and Two.  The monument is of a statue of a soldier on top of a large plinth on a three-tiered base.

It was erected by public subscription and unveiled on ANZAC Day 1921 originally to commemorate those from World War One whose names are inscribed on a brass plaque. The names of those from World War Two were added in 1950.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
