 <wpt lat="-33.67915" lon="117.557183">
  <ele>321.0</ele>
  <time>2026-04-20T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBRHAJ-5</name>
  <desc>KatanningHisto5</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e192b975-a5e3-486f-b4ab-976c6aadacca</url>
  <urlname>Katanning History : S5 Old Winery Ruins by monkeywand</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="9731654" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Katanning History : S5 Old Winery Ruins</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>monkeywand</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">monkeywand</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Katanning History&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Old Winery Ruins&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e192b975-a5e3-486f-b4ab-976c6aadacca" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e192b975-a5e3-486f-b4ab-976c6aadacca&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 20m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    multiple choice
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Called the Piesse Winery Ruins, what does the remaining structure look like?&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/084b30be-2435-4d4e-82e7-e214d886a604" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;The original winery was erected in 1904 using bricks from the Piesse brickworks. A brick distillery with a basement cellar was added in 1910 and this is the only remaining structure. The tower housed four water tanks. The place was abandoned in 1923 but reopened in 1935 as a butter factory. It was again abandoned in 1942. &lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/436aad31-0d35-472b-afed-92e8da76e4ac" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;KAAT-NYINY is a local Noongar word meaning the head sits here. It comes from the Dreamtime story of Mulka, a giant man whose body parts are embedded in country throughout the Great Southern Region.

Katanning was the junction of three Aboriginal tribal grounds long before European settlement. The first Europeans to explore the Katanning area were Governor James Stirling and Surveyor General John Septimus Roe who travelled through the area in 1835 en route from Perth to Albany.  

Katanning is located in the Upper Great Southern and is at the heart of one of the most productive agricultural regions in Western Australia.
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-33.681617" lon="117.555817">
