   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Lancelin- A Water Paradise (2)&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Jetty- Memorial&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e38f93af-6fd7-4cc1-9a4c-ff634eb7e3f7" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/e38f93af-6fd7-4cc1-9a4c-ff634eb7e3f7&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 20m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;This location was known as the " __  ________"&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/4b53d743-9cb4-457b-8e5d-630207143102" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;A short stroll out along the main branch of the jetty on a sunny day can be very refreshing but perhaps not so in winter. Nevertheless, on the right hand side of this jetty  are are some upright wooden beams, one of which has a small and somewhat rusted plaque dedicated to a local fisherman, John Oostdam. &lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/938fe1a2-5130-4120-90e1-c655bce3f723" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;This Adventure Lab continues the tour around Lancelin that began in the Welcome to Lancelin (1).&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
