   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;BYOM 10 AdLab Art #11&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Get to know the FOTT #2&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7f325672-6832-4409-b0b1-7febe457e1b5" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/7f325672-6832-4409-b0b1-7febe457e1b5&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 500m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Possibly bonus:
            &lt;a href="https://coord.info/GCBER3Q" target="_blank"&gt;GCBER3Q&lt;/a&gt;        &lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    multiple choice
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Still on animals, SmplyR3dd hyas an aversion to a bug. Which one ?&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f222f8ae-24f2-417e-b24b-02902e4857f6" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Here&amp;#039;s something you may or may not have known about the FOTT&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/25e563ce-62d1-4362-865c-8c504f1ef2eb" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Welcome to the BYOM 10 AdLab art series. What is BYOM 10? Bring Your Own Marshmallows (BYOM) is a series of events hosted by the Fellowship of the Trail, usually at a campground in regional WA. To celebrate our 10th event this year at Eaglestone Rock, (&amp;lt;a href="https://coord.info/GCBER3Q" target="_blank"&amp;gt;GCBER3Q&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt;), we&amp;#039;ve put together a little geoart for all to enjoy. All the stages have multiple choice answers and a 500 meter geofence to hopefully minimise the limited cell coverage.

Each stage of this lab will be one of the locations of the BYOM camping trips so far. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
