  <urlname>Brookton History : S4 St Mark's Anglican Church by Lachlan1.77</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache Found</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="9738260" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Brookton History : S4 St Mark's Anglican Church</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>Lachlan1.77</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">Lachlan1.77</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country>Australia</groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Brookton History&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;St Mark&amp;#039;s Anglican Church&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/2421b65f-780f-441d-b3fe-faee2871a90a" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/2421b65f-780f-441d-b3fe-faee2871a90a&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 50m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Possibly bonus:
            &lt;a href="https://coord.info/GCBPKMC" target="_blank"&gt;GCBPKMC&lt;/a&gt;        &lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Who is recognised on the plaque? (two words)&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c558042b-a2d2-46a0-87b7-5d75b760efd9" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;St Mark’s Anglican Church was the first church in Brookton. 

Samuel Williams and his wife helped establish and remained active in the Anglican church, the first church in Brookton. Prior to that, Rev Frederick Lynch who began his service at Gilgering in 1858, had confirmed members of the Seabrook family and Samuel Williams in 1865. Rev Lynch took regular services at Brookton House for John Seabrook prior to the church being established in Brookton. In 1886, Rev Groser was made Canon and in 1907 the rural Dean. He assisted in raising funds for the Brookton Church together with many prominent Brookton families, actually arranging the finance for Brookton. In 1912, Brookton parish separated from Beverley. Mothers Union was formed in 1925, and evolved into the Ladies Guild in 1926/27. The body of the church was consecrated in 1895.

The transept was added in 1918; the Entry Porch in 1924; the Vestry Meeting Room in 1985. Conversation works, on a large scale, have been undertaken in recent years. The Rectory was built in 1908 and demolished in 1987 as the house was beyond economical repair. In 1973, the Guild opened an Op Shop that contributed funds to the Vestry meeting room addition in 1985.&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/34d4685e-9608-4b8b-abc1-0b3f47595a41" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;This Adventure Lab will take you on a brief tour of Brookton, including some sights that might not have been on your radar when in town. 

There is a bonus final cache available using the clues collected in this cache. Details of the bonus final cache can be found on the listing. The GC code for the bonus final cache is &amp;lt;a href="https://coord.info/GCBPKMC" target="_blank"&amp;gt;GCBPKMC&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
