                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Creery Wetlands Reserve&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Entry Lookout&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1a6a4bf1-962a-40fc-be75-e4140a7e541b" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1a6a4bf1-962a-40fc-be75-e4140a7e541b&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 30m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Please leave your ? here, your ? at home&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d21a84ee-9413-4291-9f0e-5a80079d2f56" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Here you find the main entrance to the reserve. And a speculative lookout and boardwalk.&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/ef17fcfe-fa25-41c4-b7c1-10a4764d896a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Creery Wetlands Wander

Welcome to the beautiful Creery Wetlands Nature Reserve, one of Mandurah’s hidden natural treasures. This peaceful walk will take you through a unique wetland environment where boardwalks, bird hides, viewing platforms and winding trails showcase the incredible wildlife that calls this reserve home.

Located on the edge of the Peel Inlet, Creery Wetlands protects an important habitat for waterbirds, including migratory shorebirds that travel thousands of kilometres between Australia and the Northern Hemisphere each year. Keep your eyes open for pelicans, black swans, ospreys, egrets and many other species that frequent the wetlands. You may even spot a quenda or kangaroo amongst the surrounding vegetation. (Trails WA?)

As you make your way through this Adventure Lab, you’ll visit several points of interest that highlight the natural beauty, wildlife and fascinating features of the reserve. Take your time, enjoy the scenery, and don’t forget to bring your camera and binoculars.

The terrain is mostly flat and suitable for most walkers, but mosquitoes can be active during warmer months, so insect repellent is recommended. Please stay on designated paths, respect the wildlife, and leave the wetlands exactly as you found them for others to enjoy. (Birdingplaces.eu?)

Enjoy your adventure through one of Mandurah’s most rewarding birdwatching and nature-walking destinations!

Answers and lower case and no spaces.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
