                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;“Bart” The Giant Ram of Wagin&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Giant Ram Adjacent &lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/56bd3648-7b4d-4c86-abee-08aa54dda076" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/56bd3648-7b4d-4c86-abee-08aa54dda076&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 20m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    multiple choice
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What town in South Australia is home to the Big Farmer statue&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/bc6a3474-78e7-4f4d-813c-44a66501e2bb" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Australia theoretically grew and became economically viable off the sheeps back .  However, in order to be so successful there was a requirement for good quality farming and farmers too. In South Australia there is a town that has a Big Farmer dedication statue .&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/01422e00-578b-4063-9743-1cecb295e370" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;GIANT RAM - WAGIN WA 
The Giant Ram is one of Wagin&amp;#039;s major attractions, the Giant Ram affectionately known as Bart was built in Wagin and was put in place in May 1985. This means Bart is over 40 years old.

Bart the Giant Ram is part of the the network of Big Things across Australia&amp;#039;s rural and regional areas, although unlike many of the country&amp;#039;s whimsical giants, this ram is anatomically correct.

Thousands of tourists visit the Giant Ram  throughout the year which is located in the Wetlands Park of Wagin.
&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
