 <wpt lat="-32.010367" lon="115.879183">
  <ele>7.0</ele>
  <time>2026-08-04T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBTXMV-1</name>
  <desc>BigRingsGBRS1St</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0570c79f-e8db-4c4a-92fb-74d02a3e33a1</url>
  <urlname>Big Rings @ GBR : S1 Stop A. Near the blue canopy (playground) by mjdv99</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="9772330" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Big Rings @ GBR : S1 Stop A. Near the blue canopy (playground)</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>mjdv99</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">mjdv99</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Big Rings @ GBR&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Stop A. Near the blue canopy (playground)&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0570c79f-e8db-4c4a-92fb-74d02a3e33a1" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/0570c79f-e8db-4c4a-92fb-74d02a3e33a1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 20m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;In numerals&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/319eebd1-b419-4f0e-ba51-53d9347d56f8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;This is the nearest ring to Lake Gillon, a serene urban wetland supporting a variety of waterbirds, the Southwestern Snake-Necked Turtle (only found in WA) as well as land dwelling birds. Here you will see a single ring with the same number of reflective strips to be seen on both sides because they are the same strips that wrap around. How many can you see from the side closest to the nearest path?&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d6ea1410-634b-420d-be51-7347cab208c8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Anne Neil&amp;#039;s public art appears throughout WA including seven big steel rings in George Burnett Reserve, Manning. Installed in 2006, they represent the themes of motion and bicycling in response to the dedicated bike paths in this reserve at that time. The rings have reflective strips at the top which represent reflective road markings, and the design on each ring is different.

Your task is to count the number of reflective strips seen on the solo and twin rings as seen from the waypoints on the inner path.

You can start from any point but Stop A is an ideal starting point for those with a wheelchair/mobility aid/stroller noting that disabled parking and access is at the far eastern end of the main carpark. Stop A to E is 500m via the path.

Parking: Some marked bays in Gillon St with the main carpark at The George Burnett Leisure Centre (enter from Manning Rd, any direction). 

Bus: 34 (Gillon St) and 920 (Manning Rd)&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
