    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;In numerals&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/3054aecd-2319-42bc-b545-b764b74b13a2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;The bike jump and pump track can be seen near this delightful duo with reflective strips on both sides, but each ring is different. How many total can you see from the inner path (the path where the rings are leaning towards the path)?&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/d6ea1410-634b-420d-be51-7347cab208c8" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Anne Neil&amp;#039;s public art appears throughout WA including seven big steel rings in George Burnett Reserve, Manning. Installed in 2006, they represent the themes of motion and bicycling in response to the dedicated bike paths in this reserve at that time. The rings have reflective strips at the top which represent reflective road markings, and the design on each ring is different.

Your task is to count the number of reflective strips seen on the solo and twin rings as seen from the waypoints on the inner path.

You can start from any point but Stop A is an ideal starting point for those with a wheelchair/mobility aid/stroller noting that disabled parking and access is at the far eastern end of the main carpark. Stop A to E is 500m via the path.

Parking: Some marked bays in Gillon St with the main carpark at The George Burnett Leisure Centre (enter from Manning Rd, any direction). 

Bus: 34 (Gillon St) and 920 (Manning Rd)&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
