  <desc>WoodanillingH35</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1cfe4d21-9bb5-41fd-86d0-6e7b904ed939</url>
  <urlname>Woodanilling History Walk 3 : S5 Woodanilling Hotel by EGB2020</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="9769949" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Woodanilling History Walk 3 : S5 Woodanilling Hotel</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>EGB2020</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">EGB2020</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Woodanilling History Walk 3&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Woodanilling Hotel&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1cfe4d21-9bb5-41fd-86d0-6e7b904ed939" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1cfe4d21-9bb5-41fd-86d0-6e7b904ed939&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 20m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    multiple choice
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Total outlay for the building was &lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/b8cfa030-c417-43ba-98eb-7f7626396441" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;The hotel that Chapman and Firth built in 1908 has indeed been a credit to the district - but it was not the first such premises in Woodanilling. The industrious Elijah Bell had opened the original hotel on the block immediately north of this building in 1900.&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e5e44ba2-346f-4bd9-9c0b-7f446a0c851c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Opened in 2008, the Woodanilling Heritage Walk consists of 13 panels on a short walk around the townsite. There are old black and white photos on each panel together with stories about Woodanilling’s people and places. Heritage Walk guides are available at the Shire office.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-33.561783" lon="117.433">
  <ele>290.0</ele>
  <time>2026-07-19T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBTV5X-1</name>
  <desc>WoodanillingH31</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1cfe4d21-9bb5-41fd-86d0-6e7b904ed939</url>
  <urlname>Woodanilling History Walk 3 : S1 Sport and Recreation by EGB2020</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="9769945" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Woodanilling History Walk 3 : S1 Sport and Recreation</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>EGB2020</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">EGB2020</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Woodanilling History Walk 3&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Sport and Recreation&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1cfe4d21-9bb5-41fd-86d0-6e7b904ed939" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1cfe4d21-9bb5-41fd-86d0-6e7b904ed939&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 20m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;In what year did the trotting club setup in town?&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/04ad426e-f659-4a15-b2d0-03cc56df1d4c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;As is the case in most small rural towns, sport has played a major part in the lives of Woodanilling residents in the last hundred years. The recreation grounds, some 300 metres north of here, hosted cricket and football matches as early as
1907.&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e5e44ba2-346f-4bd9-9c0b-7f446a0c851c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Opened in 2008, the Woodanilling Heritage Walk consists of 13 panels on a short walk around the townsite. There are old black and white photos on each panel together with stories about Woodanilling’s people and places. Heritage Walk guides are available at the Shire office.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
 <wpt lat="-33.562417" lon="117.431967">
  <ele>287.0</ele>
  <time>2026-07-19T08:00:00Z</time>
  <name>LBTV5X-3</name>
  <desc>WoodanillingH33</desc>
  <url>https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1cfe4d21-9bb5-41fd-86d0-6e7b904ed939</url>
  <urlname>Woodanilling History Walk 3 : S3 National Bank by EGB2020</urlname>
  <sym>Geocache</sym>
  <type>Geocache|Lab Cache</type>
  <groundspeak:cache id="9769947" available="True" archived="False" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1">
   <groundspeak:name>Woodanilling History Walk 3 : S3 National Bank</groundspeak:name>
   <groundspeak:placed_by>EGB2020</groundspeak:placed_by>
   <groundspeak:owner id="">EGB2020</groundspeak:owner>
   <groundspeak:type>Lab Cache</groundspeak:type>
   <groundspeak:container>Virtual</groundspeak:container>
   <groundspeak:attributes>
   </groundspeak:attributes>
   <groundspeak:difficulty>1</groundspeak:difficulty>
   <groundspeak:terrain>1</groundspeak:terrain>
   <groundspeak:country></groundspeak:country>
   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Woodanilling History Walk 3&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;National Bank&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1cfe4d21-9bb5-41fd-86d0-6e7b904ed939" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/1cfe4d21-9bb5-41fd-86d0-6e7b904ed939&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 20m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;The bank reopened as a receiving office in what year?&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/a58b31a4-f1c8-4795-a68a-d2a56641b7e4" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;After 3 years of local agitation the W.A. Bank (latet Bank of NSW) established a branch in Woodanilling in 1908, However, it closed during the Great War (due to a shortage of manpower) and the National Bank opened a branch here on this site op 27 May 1912.&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/e5e44ba2-346f-4bd9-9c0b-7f446a0c851c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Opened in 2008, the Woodanilling Heritage Walk consists of 13 panels on a short walk around the townsite. There are old black and white photos on each panel together with stories about Woodanilling’s people and places. Heritage Walk guides are available at the Shire office.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
