   <groundspeak:state>Western Australia</groundspeak:state>
   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;RSL Memorial Rose Garden&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Gun&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a146bb0d-a2ce-46a6-a114-58f284024d24" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/a146bb0d-a2ce-46a6-a114-58f284024d24&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 20m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    multiple choice
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What emblem is on the butt of the gun? &lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/f6a34350-6cf9-4989-80a7-a248ad6b824a" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;During the First World War the principle long arms issued to Australian Forces were the Short Magazine Lee Enfield No 1 Mk III (SMLE No 1 Mk III)  and the Short magazine Lee Enfield No 1 Mk III* (SMLE No 1 Mk III*). The difference between the two marks was that the SMLE No 1 Mk III had a magazine cut-off which was abolished on the SMLE No 1 Mk III*.&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/7cae4ccb-5866-4404-884b-1d9038526ae2" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;A rose garden commemorating those who served in World War One and the signing of the Armistice on the 11th November 1989. &lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
