   <groundspeak:short_description html="True"> </groundspeak:short_description>
   <groundspeak:long_description html="True">
                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;Elizabeth Baillie Park&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Rotunda Maternity Hospital&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/848b1295-ff1d-4f7c-b1ed-ee1e526cd664" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/848b1295-ff1d-4f7c-b1ed-ee1e526cd664&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 20m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;Rotunda Hospital was built how many years before King Edward Memorial Hospital for Women?&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/8d0887d4-61c8-48a0-864f-1d66bc32579b" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;This location will bring you to an information sign containing the information you need to answer the question.&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/c30d90fe-5479-4c14-a2b1-c891253faf7c" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Elizabeth Baillie Park is a large leafy park, packed with new amenities. The Park leads to Baillie Hill and the heritage-listed Elizabeth Baillie House.

From February 2025 to March 2026, the Town delivered an $8.1 million upgrade of the park, adding a range of new community facilities with a strong focus on accessibility and supporting people with disabilities.

It contains many points of interest that reference the history of the site.

There are also some good geocaches to be found within the park and surrounds, don’t forget to grab those on your way around the park.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
