                                                                                                                                        &lt;h3&gt;AGWA Rooftop sculpture scavenger&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;h4&gt;Two forms in echelon&lt;/h4&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/666795e5-6d95-40e8-a066-e7838f507a45" target="_blank"&gt;https://labs.geocaching.com/goto/666795e5-6d95-40e8-a066-e7838f507a45&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Radius: 200m&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;Stages: 5&lt;/p&gt;


    &lt;p&gt;Kind of question:
                    single
            &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Question:&lt;br /&gt;What country did Barbara Hepworth work?&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Waypoint Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/9ced6689-f7a7-4aa6-b496-d2528e48e7dc" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;All answers can be found on sculptures or their plaques which are located in a garden bed behind or near.&lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;h5&gt;Adventure Lab Description&lt;/h5&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gsmediadata.blob.core.windows.net/mediacontainer/2dc23f7f-d677-4e55-b1c8-23d507d97c9e" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Welcome to this ADLAB, this is scavenger hunt, all gps points are central.
At each lab spot youll be given a question and its up to you to go and find the answer.
AGWA is open10am-5pm, Daily.
Closed Tuesdays, Good Friday and Christmas Day

Here is a little blurb about the AGWA rooftop sculpture walk.

Welcome to the Gallery’s Rooftop – bringing art and entertainment together against Perth’s beautiful city skyline.

Designed by Perth-based firm TAG Architects and Sydney firm fjmt, AGWA’s Rooftop is the largest, commercially-available rooftop venue in Perth, accommodating up to 500 people.

The AGWA Rooftop features an open-air sculpture walk featuring works from the State Art Collection, an internal gallery space for exhibitions and events, and two outdoor multi-purpose spaces with brilliant city, hill and museum views.

The centrepiece of the rooftop is a new 34-metre-long contemporary Aboriginal art piece by Minang/Wardandi/Bibbulmun artist Christopher Pease, commissioned for the State Art Collection and funded by the Foundation through the TomorrowFund.&lt;/p&gt;</groundspeak:long_description>
    <groundspeak:encoded_hints></groundspeak:encoded_hints>
   <groundspeak:logs>
  </groundspeak:logs>
   <groundspeak:travelbugs>
   </groundspeak:travelbugs>
</groundspeak:cache>
</wpt>
